ve in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/strains.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":157,\"content\":\"  e.need = 'scalpel';\"},{\"line_number\":199,\"content\":\"      e.need = 'scalpel';\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"07d4a937-dcdb-46fd-9e54-8357b84d1933"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_29","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Legato sync is confirmed. Now writing all operation files.\n\nDesigning bot-completable operations with clear phases. Broken Glass will use a 240-second timer at 72 BPM. The clean phase targets a gel zone rectangle of roughly 1.2 by 0.5 meters.\n\nThe glass phase will use four shards that spawn pools on removal. The bot needs to track the last removed shard's position for the `at: 'lastRemoved'` spawn target.\n\nEach shard will spawn a pool at its home position when removed, not at the tray. The dip phase must require an explicit done flag because vitals drop to 75 and would otherwise auto-complete without the syringe.\n\nThe dip phase will rely solely on a `stabilized` flag for completion. To prevent the global flag from triggering premature auto-completion, a local `dipDone` flag scoped to the dip phase itself will be set only when the syringe is actually used during that phase.\n\nThe dip phase will reset `flags.stabilized` to false at its start. This prevents leftover flags from triggering premature completion.\n\nThe hidden shard phase will use a scanner and forceps to reveal and clear it. The stitch phase will place two wounds with six and eight gates respectively. The gel zone will be finished last.\n\nPhase 2 pools spawn immediately when each shard is trayed, including the hidden one. Phase 2 completes once all shards and their pools are cleared. Phase 4 handles the hidden shard alone.\n\nThe simulation order runs tools first, then beats, then strains, then phase advancement.\n\nGrowth Spurt will use two sites: skin then bowel. The first phase opens with gel and an incision, completed by clearing both. The second phase bleeds from two bleeders; clamps stay until the end, so completion will rely on a flag or custom condition rather than requiring all clamps to be off.\n\nGrowth Spurt phase 2 will use a `controlled` completion flag requiring all bleeders clamped and no live pools. Phase 3 adds five nodule sites, one hidden. Phase 4 embeds a three-tether tumor and trays it. Phase 5 crashes vitals to thirty, drains, ruptures a twelve-gate wound, and triggers hush if composure is one hundred. Phase 6 unclamps, sutures the incision, and finishes with gel.\n\nThe bot will press use for one frame on the beat to clamp bleeders. This requires exporting the onBeat trigger so the bot can replicate the beat math. Adagio will follow the same structure. The bot design is now being drafted with a memory buffer and reaction delay.\n\nThe bot must not consume the simulation's random number generator. Using `sim.rng()` would break determinism because it advances the shared RNG and alters the simulation state. Instead, the bot should use a separate seeded random source drawn from its memory buffer. This ensures identical inputs across runs when the seed is fixed.\n\nThe bot will use a separate seeded random generator per seat, stored in its memory buffer. This keeps simulation determinism intact because the shared RNG advances identically across runs when the bot is called the same way. The memory helper now initializes each seat with a local RNG, a command queue, a raster cache, and state flags.\n\nThe defibrillator sequence will move the seat to the center of the site and hold use until charge reaches roughly 1.2 before releasing. The bot must read this charge from `sim.state` rather than private fields, since the plan restricts `botInput` to the exported state.\n\nThe exported state will include seat charge, arrest clock, entity needs, gate positions, incision points, and hidden flags. IV position constants are acceptable imports from field.js because they are not simulation state. The bot will inject an IV when vitals drop below forty and the syringe cooldown is zero. It will press the special action once when composure reaches one hundred while vitals remain under fifty-five.\n\nThe bot will scan state.entities for unclamped bleeders and clamp them on the beat. Gel zone coverage rectangles, incision points, gate positions, and embed parameters are missing from export state, so a `job` object will be added to each entity to expose these fields.\n\nThe bot will avoid pathing to hidden entity coordinates until the entity is marked. It will emit siteDelta commands when moving between sites. Movement will use a stickToward helper that slows down as the seat nears its target, but it cannot access tuning parameters from state.\n\nThe bot will read live tuning parameters from `exportState`. This lets it scale stick magnitude with tip speed and other live rules.\n\nThe `approach` helper now computes movement magnitude from distance and tuning parameters. It accelerates until 0.18 meters from the target, then holds near tip speed. The bot will also need a tool set.\n\nThe bot will select the needed tool each frame. Gel rastering will step through rows and columns over the zone rectangle. Cutting will target the point at `along` on the polyline, moving slowly with use held. Suturing will visit each gate while holding use, then flick or alternate after the last. Pulling will move along the axis at speed 0.9 when embedded, or return to the tray to release otherwise. Laser use will be held steady on the target.\n\nThe scanner raster will sweep rows from y = -0.7 to 0.7 in steps of 0.4 across x = -1.1 to 1.1 at speed 0.45 so dwell accumulates. The bot will keep rastering until no hidden unmarked entities remain on the site.\n\nFor clamping bleeders, the bot will calculate beat duration and remaining time until the next beat, then press use for one frame when the seat is within 0.08 meters and the beat window is under 0.12 seconds.\n\nThe defibrillator will release use and steady once charge reaches 1.15. The bot will hold the IV syringe for 0.6 seconds and press special for one frame. Decisions will be delayed by 15 frames to create sloppiness, with small noise added to stick commands. Cheat mode is handled by attract, not the bot. Multi-seat bots will pick unclaimed targets to avoid stacking.\n\nA `claim` function will let each seat track which entity it is working on. Idle seats emit empty commands and sit still. The export state will include charge and job details. Op files will be written compactly, with initial parScore set to 10000 for all seats. Op1 covers gel, forceps, suction, syringe, scanner, and suture; Op2 covers scalpel, clamp, laser, and hush.\n\nOp3 is adagio, Op4 covers staccato and tremolo, Op5 covers sforzando and legato, Op6 adds defib, crescendo, and fermata, and Op7 is coda. GR repeats all strains. Hush is added to Op2 and defib to Op6. A shared `gatesAlong` helper in `ops/helpers.js` will generate gate coordinates for the op files.\n\nThe `gatesAlong` helper now alternates gate heights by parity. All nine op files will be written next, keeping phases short enough for the bot to finish while still requiring travel. Grand rounds will use a compressed timeline: open at 0, adagio and staccato at 50, legato and crescendo at 100, fermata at 150, and close at 185 seconds.\n\nThe original grand-round schedule closes at 4:15, which cannot finish before the 75% window. I will try the plan times first and compress only if the test fails. Threats will spawn on schedule while wounds are already present from the start.\n\nThe grand-round wave schedule is being compressed to 0, 45, 90, 130, and 165 seconds so the round finishes around two hundred seconds. This keeps the win condition inside the seventy-five percent window. Player counts scale with seat count; four players spawn twenty-five incisions and ten shards. Each seat must still complete its own assigned task.\n\nThe 45–75% window applies to the standard single-player bot for each operation and grand round. Four players will run in parallel, so the total workload scales with seat count but each seat still has fewer tasks. The final wave gate remains the hard finisher, bounding all seats together.\n\nThe last wave is now scheduled for 160 seconds so the close phase finishes around 210 seconds, keeping the single-player run inside the seventy percent window. The four-player case is easier because each seat handles only a quarter of the workload. Idle seats still count down their timers and do not fail; they simply sit still. The final patient phase has no timer and no failure condition; it only requires clamping one bleeder and then performing the arrest defibrillator sequence.\n\nPatient busts will be simple parameter objects. Music IDs will follow the or-calm and or-tense naming pattern. The last patient phase will have a scripted length so the bot can finish it without a time window. During lockFail vitals still dip but the timer continues and syringe use remains active.\n\nPhase 5 of Op2 will force vitals to 35 and drain them at three per second. A `scriptDrain` flag will be added to the phase system so the simulator applies continuous damage each frame. The bot will set this flag when entering the phase and clear it once suturing finishes. The damage source must be treated as timed so hush can slow it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4f2a0d44-4dd2-4f0d-be75-644cfc916003-53","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js","old_string":"if (a.forceGift) this.forceGift = a.forceGift;","new_string":"if (a.forceGift) this.forceGift = a.forceGift;\n    if (a.scriptDrain != null) this.scriptDrain = a.scriptDrain;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4f2a0d44-4dd2-4f0d-be75-644cfc916003-54","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js","old_string":"this.sinceProgress +