{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_60","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Growth and other entities are stuck in the open phase with both gel and incision.\n\nScore 0 means no cuts or gels were completed. The bot appears to be stuck painting gel indefinitely, possibly because gel distance outranks incision priority. Broken glass scored 8947 because it only required gel.\n\nIncision priority is higher than gel, so distance is not the cause. The bot is likely stuck on the incision cut and never reaches the start point, which would explain the zero score and zero misses.\n\nSteering or aim assist might be pulling the bot off course. A debug script will print the first 30 decisions and seat positions for growth-spurt.\n\nThe last-patient case advanced to one-shock but never completed it. Vitals stayed at 15 because the arrest clock never ticked without a fermata. The bot ran for over four thousand seconds with noFail and noTimer enabled. It may be sending special gifts every frame due to high composure while vitals sit below fifty, which could block the shock command. The decision order is being checked.\n\nThe arrest flag is confirmed to be exported and set correctly, so the shock command should execute. The investigation is now shifting to the defib step logic, specifically how `seat.steady` and `seat.use` are evaluated when `stepDefib` checks for a valid hold.\n\nThe defib hold logic checks out. `seat.steady` and `seat.use` are set before `stepDefib`, so the hold should register. The charge state is exported correctly, so a stale charge value is not the issue. The queue delay logic was also verified and works properly with zero delay.\n\nThe input merge logic preserves the steady and use flags, so the defib hold should register. The arrest flag is unlikely to be missing from cached state. The next step is to debug the last-patient case after its clamp phase.\n\nIncision points are confirmed exported correctly. The zero score on growth persisted for the full 330 seconds. A wrapped debug script will log state.arrest and frame data after the phase change without modifying the bot code.\n\nThe bot may be stuck at the incision start point. It could be holding use without advancing along the line, which would explain the zero score and zero misses. I will log its positions to verify whether it is actually moving.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a11479ad-461e-44e3-b0eb-dd0fef8ebbaa-70","name":"write","input":{"content":"import { Sim } from '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js';\nimport { botInput } from '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js';\n\nconst sim = new Sim({ op: 'growth-spurt', seed: 1, physics: false });\nfor (let i = 0; i < 400; i++) {\n  const frame = botInput(sim, { id: 0 }, {});\n  if (i % 30 === 0) {\n    const s = sim.state;\n    const me = s.seats[0];\n    const kinds = s.entities.map((e) => `${e.kind}${e.started ? '*' : ''}${e.along != null ? '@' + e.along : ''}`).join(' ');\n    console.log(i, 'pos', me.x.toFixed(2), me.y.toFixed(2), 'tool', frame.tool, 'use', frame.use, 'stick', (frame.x || 0).toFixed(2), (frame.y || 0).toFixed(2), kinds);\n  }\n  sim.input(0, frame);\n  sim.step();\n}\nconsole.log('phase', sim.phase?.id, 'score', sim.score, 'miss', sim.misses);\n","file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/dbg.mjs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":676,"output_tokens":1844,"cache_read_input_tokens":174592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d4d86b7