1\\n180 pos 0.05 -0.00 tool scalpel use 1 stick 0.45 -0.01 gelZone incision*@0.754\\n210 pos 0.28 -0.01 tool scalpel use 1 stick 0.44 -0.01 gelZone incision*@0.977\\n240 pos 0.50 -0.01 tool scalpel use 1 stick 0.44 -0.01 gelZone incision*@1.201\\n270 pos 0.67 -0.02 tool scalpel use 1 stick 0.00 0.00 gelZone incision*@1.374\\n300 pos 0.67 -0.02 tool scalpel use 1 stick 0.00 0.00 gelZone incision*@1.374\\n330 pos 0.67 -0.02 tool scalpel use 1 stick 0.00 0.00 gelZone incision*@1.374\\n360 pos 0.67 -0.02 tool scalpel use 1 stick 0.00 0.00 gelZone incision*@1.374\\n390 pos 0.67 -0.02 tool scalpel use 1 stick 0.00 0.00 gelZone incision*@1.374\\nphase open score 0 miss 0\\n(node:4121497) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/dbg.mjs\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Log the bot's first seconds on Growth Spurt\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-fa32144f-b272-4d90-b0e3-2707526dad44-71.log\",\"total_bytes\":1573}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"0ae5af11-dec2-41c8-9e1b-b774e58b5bf2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_62","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The incision along stops at 1.374. The bot sits at the end with use 1, but the cut never finishes.\n\nThe line is actually 1.4006 units long, not 1.4. The bot stops at 1.374, which is only 0.006 short of the finish threshold. It also lands 0.03 units before the final point. Steering halts when distance drops below 0.028.\n\nThe target clamps to the endpoint, yet the bot logs zero stick output at step 270. The distance to that point is 0.03, which should still exceed the 0.028 threshold. This suggests the target may not actually be the endpoint.\n\nThe seat sits at x=0.67, just 0.03 units from the line end. The target is the endpoint, yet the bot logs zero stick output. The distance to that target is 0.03, which should exceed the 0.028 threshold and trigger movement. This contradiction remains unresolved.\n\nThe bot's position is rounded to 0.674, making the true distance to the target 0.026. That falls below the 0.028 stop threshold, so it halts. The along value also never reaches the end because the tip stops 0.026 short. The fix is to creep until the entity disappears, widen the finish threshold, or aim past the endpoint with a smaller stop radius.\n\nThe fix is to keep the bot creeping toward the endpoint until the entity disappears, and to reduce the cut stop radius from 0.028 to 0.01. The finish threshold will be raised to `len - 0.01` so the tip can actually reach the final point.\n\nThe stop radius will be lowered to 0.012 globally. This is safe for grabs because the grab radius is 0.1 and the settle distance is 0.04. The finish threshold will also be raised to `len - 0.04` so the bot counts as finished while very close to the endpoint.\n\nThe stop radius will be set to 0.015 and the finish threshold to `len - 0.035`. Circle cuts are closed loops, so the same 0.02 shortfall could trap them at the start.\n\nExposition finished successfully. Coda adagio and holes worked, but legato links were never cut due to a swipe bug. Grand rounds died at 108 seconds from vitals because bleeders and strains overlapped. Growth scored zero because it stalled on the final 0.03 of its incision; fixing the end-of-cut should unlock all remaining phases.\n\nThe swipe bug will be debugged after the cut fix, since growth will reach tumor tethers using the same swipe. The last-patient shock failure will be checked separately in parallel. The shock logic appears sound: arrest holds vitals at 15, the gift check runs after arrest, and a non-perfect release only decrements the clock while keeping arrest active.\n\nThe shock window should open at 1.16, well inside the 1.05–1.35 range, so a missed release is unexpected. The steady flag may not be passed correctly. I will add debug logging to trace the last-patient shock.\n\nA manual trace of the last-patient shock shows the charge should hit 1.166 after 70 frames, landing inside the 0.15 release window and triggering a perfect release with no arrest. Since the logic appears sound, the bot may be stuck on the bleeder and never sending the shock command.\n\nThe bot ran for over four thousand seconds in the one-shock phase, yet the shock never fired. The charge may have climbed above 1.35 and triggered an automatic release, or the arrest state might not be clearing as expected.\n\nA cache bug is the likely cause of the infinite weak-shock loop. The root state only refreshes when `root.tick` changes, so stale charge values may prevent the bot from hitting the release window.\n\nThe cache refreshes correctly on every frame because the tick increments each step. Rounding of charge values is also not the issue, so the stale-state theory does not explain the missed shock.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7c4d0154-4b19-4eb5-a3b3-9e19d437dc08-72","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js","old_string":"  if (e.along >= e.len - 0.02) finishCut(sim, seat, e, tol);","new_string":"  if (e.along >= e.len - 0.04) finishCut(sim, seat, e, tol);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7c4d0154-4b19-4eb5-a3b3-9e19d437dc08-73","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  if (d < 0.028) return { source: 'stick', x: 0, y: 0, use: 0, steady };","new_string":"  if (d < 0.012) return { source: 'stick', x: 0, y: 0, use: 0, steady };"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7c4d0154-4b19-4eb5-a3b3-9e19d437dc08-74","name":"write","input":{"content":"import { Sim } from '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js';\nimport { botInput } from '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js';\n\nconst sim = new Sim({ op: 'last-patient', seed: 1, physics: false });\nlet logged = 0;\nfor (let i = 0; i < 8000 && !sim.over; i++) {\n  const frame = botInput(sim, { id: 0 }, {});\n  if (sim.phase?.id === 'one-shock' && logged < 40 && i % 15 === 0) {\n    const s = sim.state;\n    console.log(i, 'arrest', JSON.stringify(s.arrest), 'charge', s.seats[0].charge, 'comp', s.seats[0].composure, 'vit', s.vitals.toFixed(1), 'frame', JSON.stringify(frame));\n    logged++;\n  }\n  sim.input(0, frame);\n  sim.step();\n}\nconsole.log('over', sim.over, 'complete', sim.complete, 'phase', sim.phase?.id, 'arrests', sim.arrestsSurvived, 't', sim.time.toFixed(1));\n","file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231