:\\\"stick\\\",\\\"x\\\":0,\\\"y\\\":0,\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"suction\\\"}\\n615 arrest null charge 0 comp 10 vit 45.0 frame {\\\"source\\\":\\\"stick\\\",\\\"x\\\":0,\\\"y\\\":0,\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"suction\\\"}\\n630 arrest null charge 0 comp 10 vit 45.0 frame {\\\"source\\\":\\\"stick\\\",\\\"x\\\":0,\\\"y\\\":0,\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"suction\\\"}\\n645 arrest null charge 0 comp 10 vit 45.0 frame {\\\"source\\\":\\\"stick\\\",\\\"x\\\":0,\\\"y\\\":0,\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"suction\\\"}\\n660 arrest null charge 0 comp 10 vit 45.0 frame {\\\"source\\\":\\\"stick\\\",\\\"x\\\":0,\\\"y\\\":0,\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"suction\\\"}\\n675 arrest null charge 0 comp 10 vit 45.0 frame {\\\"source\\\":\\\"stick\\\",\\\"x\\\":0,\\\"y\\\":0,\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"suction\\\"}\\n690 arrest null charge 0 comp 10 vit 45.0 frame {\\\"source\\\":\\\"stick\\\",\\\"x\\\":0,\\\"y\\\":0,\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"suction\\\"}\\nover false complete false phase one-shock arrests 1 t 133.3\\n(node:4123257) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/dbg2.mjs\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Trace defibrillator inputs on Last Patient\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-81011f57-df28-4793-b4bb-3db8b4d01b77-75.log\",\"total_bytes\":6444}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"1383e3f6-d721-419c-aaa3-ddd937388452"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_64","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The shock worked, but the phase did not complete. The done state is `{ arrests: 1 }` rather than `{ arrests: 2 }`.\n\nThe completion check should have passed when `arrestsSurvived` equals `d.arrests`. The phase still remains stuck in one-shock, so the cause is unclear.\n\nThe bleeder is still clamped. The final phase logic requires all clamps to be off before it can succeed or complete.\n\nThe bot never unclamps the bleeder because its objective is \"Start the heart,\" which does not begin with \"Close.\" The `flags.closing` flag remains false, so the bot never triggers unclamping. The final phase requires all clamps off, but the bot cannot see that requirement.\n\nThe simplest fix is to unclamp any remaining clamped bleeders on the final phase when no other work remains. This is safe because success on the last phase requires all clamps to be off. The bot needs to know which phase is last, so `phaseCount` or a `lastPhase` flag should be exported.\n\nThe `lastPhase` flag will be set when the current phase index reaches the final phase. The bot will unclamp any remaining clamped bleeders on that phase only if no other work remains. This prevents the bleeder from draining during the shock, since the arrest holds vitals at 15.\n\nThe unclamp check runs after the shock. Candidates are empty during the arrest, so the phase completes once the bleeder is released. On non-final phases, clamped bleeders are not a valid idle target because those phases already advanced past them.\n\nThe last-phase unclamp idea fails for GR because the single phase is also the final one. Unclamping during idle moments before the finale would kill the patient.\n\nThe better fix is to change completePhase so the last phase does not automatically require all clamps off when the phase data already specifies the done conditions.\n\nThe bot will unclamp after the shock because arrest handling runs first. The objective should be \"Close the night\" or \"Close her heart\" so the bot recognizes unclamping as a valid task. This satisfies the final phase requirement without adding an automatic allClampsOff check.\n\nThe existing bot unclamp logic already handles the last patient once the objective starts with \"Close\". The automatic allClampsOff check in completePhase is redundant but harmless. For GR, the objective does not start with \"Close\", so the auto check only applies after other done conditions pass.\n\nThe automatic allClampsOff check never fires early because phaseCleared returns false before 165. The closing flag is still false then, so completePhase is skipped entirely. After 165 the flag is set but wounds remain, so phaseCleared stays false and the auto check never triggers.\n\nThe grand rounds done state already includes `allClampsOff: true`, so the phase cannot complete while clamps remain. The bot will unclamp once the closing flag is set at 165 and no other work remains. For the last patient, the objective will be changed to \"Close the night\" so the bot unclamps after the shock.\n\nThe coda phase also blocks completion because its objective is \"Bring her back,\" which does not start with \"Close.\" The bot will unclamp whenever the last phase's done conditions require all clamps off. A `needUnclamp` flag will be exported by the simulation so the bot can recognize this requirement.\n\nThe `needUnclamp` flag will be set inside `completePhase` when the phase data originally requires all clamps off. The bot will check this flag alongside the closing flag to unclamp bleeders on the final phase.\n\nThe bot will unclamp when the objective starts with \"Close\", `flags.closing` is true, or `flags.needUnclamp` is set. The simulation sets that flag and replaces the phase done state with `allClampsOff` inside `completePhase`. This prevents early unclamping during grand rounds because `phaseCleared` only returns true once the closing flag and all other conditions are met.\n\nThe `needUnclamp` flag will be wired into `completePhase` and the bot's unclamp check. The last patient objective change may be unnecessary if this flag works.\n\nGrowth and legato are stuck on links after the cut fix. A smoke test will show how far they progress. Coda development is also stuck on links, so swipe behavior needs inspection after smoke.\n\nGrand rounds vitals are still dying.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-772c9d9c-a107-42e1-8d4a-0fe5ba0a8356-76","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js","old_string":"      if (this.entities.some((e) => e.alive && e.kind === 'bleeder' && e.clamped)) {\n        this.bark('clampReminder');\n        this.phase.done = { ...(this.phase.done || {}), allClampsOff: true };\n        return;\n      }","new_string":"      if (this.entities.some((e) => e.alive && e.kind === 'bleeder' && e.clamped)) {\n        this.bark('clampReminder');\n        this.flags.needUnclamp = true;\n        this.phase.done = { ...(this.phase.done || {}), allClampsOff: true };\n        return;\n      }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-772c9d9c-a107-42e1-8d4a-0fe5ba0a8356-77","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  const closing = /^close\\b/i.test(state.objective || '') || !!state.flags?.closing;","new_string":"  const closing = /^close\\b/i.test(state.objective || '') || !!state.flags?.closing || !!state.flags?.needUnclamp;"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2135,"output_tokens":2505,"cache_read_input_tokens":181248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_t