{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_69","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reattach is 8 beats. Each cut-to-tray should be under 6 seconds.\n\nChain trip plus cut and return totals about 3.5 seconds, well under the 6.9-second limit. StepLegato reattach uses beat counts, so slow trips may trigger recuts but should still make progress if the average stays below eight beats. Wrong-link healing might clip neighbors if swipes are off-center, though spacing is tight. Moving legato chains to x = 0.85 shortens the ferry; the far end at 1.3 could sit outside the drape, but y should stay near zero.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c29f58cc-3851-4579-8d97-bb54e1e8040d-85","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/smoke.mjs\"","description":"Re-play all operations after link and scan fixes"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5092,"output_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":190336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"2c306a06-76fb-4244-9e88-551eec1f9226"}
