01,114,64,104,101,97,114,116,10,103,114,97,110,100,45,114,111,117,110,100,115,32,32,32,70,65,73,76,58,118,105,116,97,108,115,32,112,104,61,114,111,117,110,100,115,32,116,61,49,49,57,46,49,32,102,114,97,99,61,48,46,51,57,55,32,118,109,105,110,61,45,48,46,48,32,109,105,115,115,61,48,32,115,99,111,114,101,61,49,55,49,49,55,32,114,97,110,107,61,45,32,119,97,108,108,61,49,56,54,32,108,101,102,116,61,98,108,101,101,100,101,114,64,98,111,119,101,108,99,44,98,108,101,101,100,101,114,64,104,101,97,114,116,99,44,115,99,114,97,116,99,104,64,116,114,97,121,44,115,99,114,97,116,99,104,64,116,114,97,121,44,108,101,103,97,116,111,64,98,111,119,101,108,44,108,105,110,107,64,98,111,119,101,108,44,99,114,101,115,99,101,110,100,111,64,104,101,97,114,116,44,102,101,101,100,101,114,64,104,101,97,114,116,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\nbroken-glass   OK ph=finish t=103.5 frac=0.431 vmin=75.0 miss=0 score=8949 rank=S wall=125 left=\\ngrowth-spurt   FAIL:time ph=close t=335.7 frac=1.017 vmin=46.5 miss=0 score=6040 rank=- wall=269 left=bleeder@bowelc,bleeder@bowelc\\nadagio         FAIL:vitals ph=grande t=112.9 frac=0.342 vmin=-0.0 miss=0 score=8298 rank=- wall=275 left=scratch@tray,scratch@tray,scratch@tray,scratch@tray,bleeder@tray,pool@tray,bleeder@tray,pool@tray\\nstaccato       OK ph=close t=116.3 frac=0.323 vmin=69.5 miss=0 score=16789 rank=S wall=158 left=\\nlegato         FAIL:time ph=repair t=360.0 frac=1.000 vmin=38.6 miss=1 score=1717791 rank=- wall=521 left=bleeder@brainc,bleeder@brainc,bleeder@brainc,bleeder@brain\\nfermata        FAIL:time ph=ring t=420.0 frac=1.000 vmin=70.8 miss=0 score=2063 rank=- wall=176 left=crescendo@heart\\ncoda           FAIL:time ph=recap t=575.7 frac=1.010 vmin=48.0 miss=0 score=19061 rank=- wall=491 left=bleeder@heartc,bleeder@lungc,bleeder@lungc,bleeder@lungc,crescendo@aorta,circleCut@aorta\\nlast-patient   OK ph=one-shock t=6.5 frac=0.163 vmin=15.0 miss=0 score=2973 rank=- wall=9 left=bleeder@heart\\ngrand-rounds   FAIL:vitals ph=rounds t=119.1 frac=0.397 vmin=-0.0 miss=0 score=17117 rank=- wall=186 left=bleeder@bowelc,bleeder@heartc,scratch@tray,scratch@tray,legato@bowel,link@bowel,crescendo@heart,feeder@heart\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/smoke.mjs\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Re-play all operations after link and scan fixes\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-c29f58cc-3851-4579-8d97-bb54e1e8040d-85.log\",\"total_bytes\":1327}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"3d96d033-3d7c-44ad-b557-0382657edb79"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_70","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Staccato is working, but the fraction value is zero.\n\nLegato reached repair with working chains. The phase stalled with four bleeders and one unclamped. The timer ran out. The score exploded to 1.7 million points. This indicates a bug in grading or scoring logic.\n\nThe score of 1.7 million points implies an award is granted every single frame. Normal operations cannot produce that many points in a 360-second phase. The cause may be an infinite loop or a laser repeatedly hitting an object that respawns each frame.\n\nThe score averages roughly 80 points per step. That equals about one CLEAN award every other frame. The cause may be a runaway suture or gel timer. Auto-tie respawns are ruled out. I will inspect the scoring code after further fixes.\n\nGrowth still fails at the same point with identical scores. The close phase is too long for the remaining time, so the bot cannot unclamp the last two bleeders before the timer expires. I will debug when the close phase begins.\n\nGel and wound tasks are already finished. Only clamped bleeders remain. The bot should unclamp them instantly if it is near them. The close phase may be stuck because the alt key fails to register during the unclamp pulse. I need to check exactly when the close phase begins.\n\nThe close phase likely begins at t=20. The unclamp pulse is broken. The bot sends alt true for one frame. The bleeder unclamps. Then the bot immediately reclamps it because the priority 90 clamp candidate rule fires. This creates an oscillation loop. The close phase never finishes.\n\nThe phase should complete the same step that unclamps a bleeder, before the next bot frame reclamps it. If two bleeders remain clamped, allClampsOff fails and the phase stalls.\n\nThe oscillation bug is confirmed. Unclamping a bleeder makes it a high-priority clamp target, so the bot reclamps it immediately and loops forever.\n\nThe fix is to skip unclamped bleeders in the candidate list while the close phase is active. This lets the bot unclamp the remaining clamped bleeders without getting stuck in a loop.\n\nThe fix is now implemented in the candidates function. During the close phase, unclamped bleeders are skipped so the bot cannot reclamp them. This lets the phase complete in the same step as the last unclamp. The growth close objective does not require pools to be cleared.\n\nAdagio grande died from vitals. The bot could not keep up with the bleeders and scratches. Total damage is 4.5 per second. I will shorten the fight and let the bot hush to recover.\n\nAdagio grande killed the bot at 112 seconds, after roughly 90 seconds of earlier phases. The operation fraction is 0.342. A \"scratch@tray\" site is odd because gel kills objects and forceps only grabs grabbable items. This suggests a bug or onRemoved logic is incorrectly setting the site to tray.\n\nI will reduce grande HP to 80 so the core laser finishes quickly. I will also cap bleeders at three instead of four, since grande spawns one every even bar. The bot should survive if it clamps them and then hushes.\n\nThe bot may be stuck forcepsing the adagio before it dies, or gel may be failing to finish on moving scratches. I will time-box a debug of grande or reduce its spawns and HP first. Fermata ring now only lists crescendo@heart, not circleCut, scoring 2063.\n\nThe crescendo may be alive because the circle cut was never applied. The bot cannot extract it, so the phase cannot complete. The stepCrescendo logic only marks an entity grabbable when a matching circleCut is already dead.\n\nThe circle cut should be grabbable because the entity remains in the simulation with alive set to false. The bot still does not grab it. The circle may never have spawned or died. The crescendo stays unexposed and the phase stalls.\n\nThe bot may be failing to pull the grabbable circle cut because of axis or embedded-pull angle issues. The entity should still exist in the simulation with alive set to false, so the find logic ought to locate it.\n\nThe circle cut is on the heart site. The pull axis and tolerance look correct, and the embedded path clears the clamp. The grabbable flag is exported. A sudden realization about the cause has just struck.\n\nThe bot should grab the grabbable circle cut, but it may be tearing and resetting instead. Pull speed and angle look correct, so the cause is unclear.\n\nThe adagio core laser deals 90 damage per second. At 150 HP the bot needs about 1.67 seconds of core hits to kill grande. The core beam fires on beats zero, three, and seven of every four-beat cycle.\n\nAt 80 BPM the adagio core laser should kill grande in about one bar. The bot still died from vitals. It may not be close enough to fire because the adagio moves and the bot is too slow or busy with higher-priority tasks. Core laser has priority 93, which beats bleeders at 90 and scratches at 82. The core flag is exported correctly.\n\nThe adagio's movement is too slow to cause a one-frame tracking lag. The bot should stay on it. Core laser flickers every beat, so the bot may chase and miss the window while returning from distant gel tasks. Adagio spawns only three finite scratches.\n\nThe bot should camp on the adagio after gelling. The grande run died of vitals at 113 seconds because bleeders and scratches drained faster than the syringe could heal. Clamping stops that drain.\n\nThe bot's death spiral is caused by the syringe task outranking clamping. When vitals drop below 40, it runs to the IV instead of clamping bleeders. Bleeders drain during the trip. The fix prioritizes unclamped bleeders over the syringe unless vitals are critically low. Gift will be offered when composure is high.\n\nAdagio grande bleeders will be capped at two instead of three. Fermata circle will be debugged after the smoke test. Legato repair is delayed because reattaching chains takes too long; moving the spawn closer to the tray and reducing jerk bleeders should fix the timeout and the score explosion from repeated sever-and-reheal cycles.\n\nLegato repair is too slow. Two chains need roughly 36 seconds, which is shorter than the 162-second target, so I will pad it with a larger gel or longer scanner. Staccato still needs about 50 more seconds. Growth is at 100% because the close phase is wasted on the unclamp oscillation.\n\nAdagio grande HP is being raised to 120 so the bot can kill it in one core window even with sloppy tracking. Coda recap is stuck on the circle cut, just like fermata.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0b0dff66-050d-4c7f-8939-a7b34a7a19e2-86","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"    if (e.kind === 'bleeder' && !e.clamped) { job = 'clamp'; prio = 90; }","new_string":"    if (e.kind === 'bleeder' && !e.clamped) {\n      const closing = /^close\\b/i.test(state.objective || '') || state.flags?.closing || state.flags?.needUnclamp;\n      if (!closing) { job = 'clamp'; prio = 90; }\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0b0dff66-050d-4c7f-8939-a7b34a7a19e2-87","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  if (state.vitals < 40 && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0) return syringeAt(me, IV.x, IV.y, tuning, opts);","new_string":"  const bleeding = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'bleeder' && !e.clamped);\n  if (state.vitals < 40 && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22)) {\n    return syringeAt(me, IV.x, IV.y, tuning, opts);\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0b0dff66-050d-4c7f-8939-a7b34a7a19e2-88","name":"search_replace