,39,115,102,111,114,122,97,110,100,111,68,117,114,97,116,105,111,110,39,93,32,125,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":11,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/config/tuning.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":12,\"content\":\"  laserDps: 30,\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"  drainMult: 1,\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"  stabilizerHeal: 15,\"},{\"line_number\":28,\"content\":\"  hushTimeScale: 0.25,\"},{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"  laserDps: [10, 80],\"},{\"line_number\":50,\"content\":\"  drainMult: [0, 3],\"},{\"line_number\":53,\"content\":\"  stabilizerHeal: [5, 30],\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"  hushTimeScale: [0.05, 0.7],\"},{\"line_number\":70,\"content\":\"  { id: 'tools', label: 'Tools', keys: ['scalpelTol', 'pullTol', 'suctionRate', 'gelRadius', 'stitchGateR', 'laserDps', 'laserBurn', 'scannerRadius', 'clampWindow', 'defibWindow'] },\"},{\"line_number\":71,\"content\":\"  { id: 'patient', label: 'Patient', keys: ['drainMult', 'timerMult', 'tempoPressure', 'stabilizerHeal', 'stabilizerCooldown', 'missLimit'] },\"},{\"line_number\":73,\"content\":\"  { id: 'gifts', label: 'Gifts', keys: ['composureGain', 'hushDuration', 'hushTimeScale', 'sforzandoStun', 'sforzandoDamage', 'sforzandoToolMult', 'sforzandoDuration'] },\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"9e378df7-7940-4798-9d1d-c62aed22052c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_82","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Crescendo problem analysis shows that afterSpawn spawns four feeders and immediately sets armed to true.\n\nstepCrescendo respawns missing feeders on beats divisible by 16. The bot can kill all four feeders before respawn if it stays focused, since four feeders take roughly 5.3 seconds to destroy and beat 16 occurs at 10.9 seconds. However, crescendo grows continuously while the bot is busy, expanding from 0.2 to 1.0 over about ten seconds.\n\nFortissimo at size 1 deals 20 damage and spawns two bleeders, resetting the size to 0.6. The drain rate is roughly 4 vitals per second at size 0.5, totaling about 30–40 over ten seconds. The score of 2063 suggests the bot scored around seven flawless laser kills, likely because it killed three feeders before beat 16 respawned them, creating an endless loop.\n\nThe design intent is to kill all feeders, expose the membrane, cut a circle, and extract the tumor. Feeders should not respawn infinitely once progress begins. The bot needs roughly eight to ten seconds to clear four feeders. Respawn at beat 16 may fire while the bot is still killing them if the phase starts near a multiple of 16. There is also a bug: the respawn check uses `live` captured at the start of the step alongside the beat condition.\n\nThe exact step order between strains and tools determines the bug. If strains run before tools, the beat 16 respawn check sees the old `live` array and spawns new feeders while one is still alive. This prevents exposure on the same step that kills the last feeder.\n\nThe bot should expose the membrane on the step after the last feeder dies, provided it kills all four before the next respawn beat. The total kill time is roughly eight to ten seconds, which fits comfortably inside the eleven-second window.\n\nBleeder clamping is the critical bottleneck. The bot prioritizes clamping bleeders over feeders, so it misses the window to kill all four before the next respawn. Fortissimo spawns bleeders that drain vitals if left unclamped. The bot is trapped in a loop of killing feeders, triggering fortissimo, clamping bleeders, and respawning until the timer expires.\n\nThe 2063-point total likely reflects the open phase, where gel and incision may have scored around 2000. The ring phase probably added almost nothing because the bot was repeatedly interrupted before it could kill feeders.\n\nThe coda export shows the circle cut and crescendo are both alive, confirming the bot exposed the membrane and spawned the circle. It failed to finish the circle cut. Fermata only exported crescendo, so the circle was likely cut but extraction failed or was omitted. A dead circle is not exported.\n\nThe 2063-point score is too low for a completed circle cut plus feeder kills. The timer expired exactly at 420 seconds, suggesting the bot barely reached the end or never spawned the circle. A debug script will log crescendo state every two seconds during the fermata ring to verify exposure, size, feeder count, and vitals.\n\nAdagio grande likely drains vitals to zero because its large damage outpaces the bot's clamping. A focused debug script will trace this instead of guessing. The full scope is massive: view, story, audio, shell, multi-player, tests, and build remain after ops pass.\n\nThe circle cut polyline is closed, so its last point matches the first. The finish condition requires reaching 72 percent of the path length while staying within 0.06 units of that endpoint. Because the end is also the start, the bot can satisfy the distance requirement early even before completing the full loop.\n\nA bug in the circle-cut projection logic may prevent the bot from finishing. Because the polyline is closed, the along parameter can jump near the start point and stall, making it impossible to reach the 72 percent threshold. The target point calculation might also fail on the 