b\\\":false,\\\"holder\\\":null,\\\"circ\\\":null,\\\"bleed\\\":\\\"cc\\\"}\\n{\\\"t\\\":332.9,\\\"pt\\\":278,\\\"v\\\":46.5,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"forceps\\\",\\\"sx\\\":-0.32,\\\"sy\\\":0.15,\\\"site\\\":\\\"skin\\\",\\\"feed\\\":0,\\\"exp\\\":false,\\\"size\\\":null,\\\"grab\\\":false,\\\"holder\\\":null,\\\"circ\\\":null,\\\"bleed\\\":\\\"cc\\\"}\\n{\\\"t\\\":334.9,\\\"pt\\\":280,\\\"v\\\":46.5,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"forceps\\\",\\\"sx\\\":-0.32,\\\"sy\\\":0.15,\\\"site\\\":\\\"skin\\\",\\\"feed\\\":0,\\\"exp\\\":false,\\\"size\\\":null,\\\"grab\\\":false,\\\"holder\\\":null,\\\"circ\\\":null,\\\"bleed\\\":\\\"cc\\\"}\\nEND false time close 335.7 steps 20140\\n(node:4142615) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/dbg-ring.mjs\\\" growth-spurt close\",\"truncated\":true,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Trace growth-spurt close phase\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-8786845a-6fd5-432a-8461-04fdad79ba81-39.log\",\"total_bytes\":23662}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"21ee6bd3-fa84-48d8-b5d4-dd2b97726f42"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_92","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two bugs were found. Crescendo extraction cuts the circle instantly.\n\nThe second bug is that `stepCrescendo` resets `embedded` to true every frame. This overrides the pull check and keeps the circle stuck in the embedded state.\n\nThe bot pulls the circle upward forever because it never becomes free. The fix is to set `embedded` and `grabbable` only once, not every frame.\n\nThe fix uses an `if (e.embed == null)` guard so `embedded` and `embed` are only set once. The pull reached 0.911, which exceeds the 0.35 threshold, but the next frame's strain step immediately reset `embedded` to true. That is why the circle never popped free.\n\nThe simulation step order is the culprit. If strains run after tools, the exported state still shows `embedded` as true, so the bot keeps pulling upward forever. Once the reset bug is fixed, the bot should successfully carry the circle to the tray.\n\nA second bug is that `unclamp` does not switch the bot to the correct bleeder site. The bot remains stuck on the skin at (-0.32, 0.15) while the bleeders are actually at the bowel sites. The gel and suture steps finished around point 22, but the forceps never moved to the proper location.\n\nThe bot is only 0.042 units away from the skin site, so it thinks it is close enough to press alt. But `nearestKind` requires the same site, and no bleeder exists on the skin, so the action does nothing and the bot pulses forever.\n\nThe fix is to make `unclamp` switch the bot's site before acting. It should steer to the target site first, since it is called directly rather than through `actOn`.\n\nThe `unclamp` fix now sets `f.site = idx` and passes state from `decide`. I still need to verify that the site input is actually applied.\n\nThe circle cut finishes instantly because the closed ring triggers an `atEnd` or projection jump. It was already done by point 8, just two seconds after the laser.\n\nThe circle cut finishing instantly is not a bug. At 0.48 force units per second the bot can cut roughly 0.96 length in two seconds, so reaching the finish threshold near the start point is realistic. The stall is still caused by the embedded reset.\n\nAdagio grande death will be traced after the extraction and unclamp fixes are applied, since those same bugs also affect coda and growth.\n\nFermata eyes likely suffer from the same embedded reset bug. `stepFermata` sets `embedded = true` every frame while the grabbable condition holds, which would prevent the item from ever becoming free.\n\nFermata eyes are not affected by the embedded reset bug. The stage change to 'between' happens only once, so `embedded` is set exactly once and never overwritten.\n\nThe reset bug is isolated to crescendo's else branch, which runs every frame.\n\nAdagio grande death is not caused by the embedded reset bug. The adagio code only sets grabbable when health drops to zero, so it never overwrites that state.\n\nThe growth unclamp site bug is confirmed. The bot freezes because it is within 0.05 units of the target and never steers; it only pulses alt. Once the site switch is fixed, the bot should move properly.\n\nThe circle cut's atEnd threshold may be too generous, but fermata finished the ring legitimately, so no change is needed unless tests fail.\n\nThe bot will unclamp on the correct site immediately after the site switch.\n\nOnce unclamp works, growth close will finish too fast. It currently starts at t=54.9 and gel ends at t=76. That is only 23% of the 330-second operation. The target is 45-75% completion. More work must be added after the fix to pad the operation time.\n\nI will pad individual operations with extra gel, sutures, and nodules rather than slowing the bot globally. Broken-glass currently finishes at 43% of its time band; adding about eight more seconds should push it to roughly 130 seconds. Growth close needs substantial extra work to reach the 45–75% target. Adagio grande died at 99 seconds.\n\nStaccato and legato are also too short at roughly 32% and 18% of their time bands. Fermata may total about 36% once the stuck ring is fixed. Coda and grand-rounds remain unmeasured. I will fix the two bugs first, re-smoke, then pad the operations to reach the 45–75% target.\n\nThe crescendo fix now sets `e.revealed = true` before marking the circle grabbable. This prevents the embedded state from being overwritten on the next frame. The bot will then be able to pull the circle free instead of pulsing forever.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-98d65ecb-fea8-4955-9ee4-1fab0a374078-40","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"f\\.site|cmd\\.site|assignSite|siteDelta","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-98d65ecb-fea8-4955-9ee4-1fab0a374078-41","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js","offset":143,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":17361,"output_tokens":2835,"cache_read_input_tokens":85632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"2c1d08ad-1137-4038-acbe-1c1efe54e299"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-98d65ecb-fea8-4955-9ee4-1fab0a374078-40","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,47,65,108,105,118,101,32,105,110,32,67,111,109,109,111,110,32,84,105,109,101,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,32,67,101,110,116,101,114,58,32,83,101,99,111,110,100,32,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,47,115,114,99,47,115,105,109,47,115,105,109,46,106,115,10,54,57,52,58,32,32,32,32,116,104,105,115,46,97,115,115,105,103,110,83,105,116,101,40,115,101,97,116,44,32,115,105,116,101,115,91,105,110,100,101,120,93,46,105,100,41,59,10,55,48,49,58,32,32,32,32,116,104,105,115,46,97,115,115,105,103,110,83,105,116,101,40,115,101,97,116,44,32,115,105,116,101,115,91,110,101,120,116,93,46,105,100,41,59,10,55,48,52,58,32,32,97,115,115,105,103,110,83,105,116,101,40,115,101,97,116,44,32,105,100,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":3,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":694,\"content\":\"    this.assignSite(seat, sites[index].id);\"},{\"line_number\":701,\"content\":\"    this.assignSite(seat, sites[next].id);\"},{\"line_number\":704,\"content\":\"  assignSite(seat, id) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-98d65ecb-fea8-4955-9ee4-1fab0a374078-41","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"143→export function stepTools(sim, dt) {\\n  for (const seat of sim.seats) {\\n    if (seat.out) continue;\\n    const f = seat.cmd;\\n    if (f.tool && f.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = f.tool;\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'tool', seat: seat.id, tool: seat.tool });\\n150→    }\\n    const use = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, f.use || 0));\\n    seat.use = use;\\n    seat.steady = !!f.steady;\\n    if (rising(seat, 'swap')) sim.swapLead(seat);\\n    if (Number.isInteger(f.site)) sim.setSite(seat, f.site);\\n    if (f.siteDelta) sim.nudgeSite(seat, f.siteDelta);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'special')) tryGift(sim, seat);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'alt')) doAlt(sim, seat);\\n    stepSyringe(sim, seat, dt);\\n160→    stepDefib(sim, seat, dt);\\n    const power = toolPower(sim);\\n    if (sim.hushPhase !== 'inhale') {\\n      switch (seat.tool) {\\n        case 'scalpel': stepScalpel(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'forceps': stepForceps(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'suction': stepSuction(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'gel': stepGel(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'suture': stepSuture(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'laser': stepLaser(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n170→        case 'scanner': stepScanner(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'clamp': stepClamp(sim, seat, use); break;\\n        default: break;\",\"content_concise\":\"143→export function stepTools(sim, dt) {\\n  for (const seat of sim.seats) {\\n    if (seat.out) continue;\\n    const f = seat.cmd;\\n    if (f.tool && f.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = f.tool;\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'tool', seat: seat.id, tool: seat.tool });\\n150→    }\\n    const use = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, f.use || 0));\\n    seat.use = use;\\n    seat.steady = !!f.steady;\\n    if (rising(seat, 'swap')) sim.swapLead(seat);\\n    if (Number.isInteger(f.site)) sim.setSite(seat, f.site);\\n    if (f.siteDelta) sim.nudgeSite(seat, f.siteDelta);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'special')) tryGift(sim, seat);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'alt')) doAlt(sim, seat);\\n    stepSyringe(sim, seat, dt);\\n160→    stepDefib(sim, seat, dt);\\n    const power = toolPower(sim);\\n    if (sim.hushPhase !== 'inhale') {\\n      switch (seat.tool) {\\n        case 'scalpel': stepScalpel(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'forceps': stepForceps(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'suction': stepSuction(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'gel': stepGel(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'suture': stepSuture(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'laser': stepLaser(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n170→        case 'scanner': stepScanner(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'clamp': stepClamp(sim, seat, use); break;\\n        default: break;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js\",\"offset\":143,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"export function stepTools(sim, dt) {\\n  for (const seat of sim.seats) {\\n    if (seat.out) continue;\\n    const f = seat.cmd;\\n    if (f.tool && f.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = f.tool;\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'tool', seat: seat.id, tool: seat.tool });\\n    }\\n    const use = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, f.use || 0));\\n    seat.use = use;\\n    seat.steady = !!f.steady;\\n    if (rising(seat, 'swap')) sim.swapLead(seat);\\n    if (Number.isInteger(f.site)) sim.setSite(seat, f.site);\\n    if (f.siteDelta) sim.nudgeSite(seat, f.siteDelta);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'special')) tryGift(sim, seat);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'alt')) doAlt(sim, seat);\\n    stepSyringe(sim, seat, dt);\\n    stepDefib(sim, seat, dt);\\n    const power = toolPower(sim);\\n    if (sim.hushPhase !== 'inhale') {\\n      switch (seat.tool) {\\n        case 'scalpel': stepScalpel(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'forceps': stepForceps(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'suction': stepSuction(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'gel': stepGel(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'suture': stepSuture(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'laser': stepLaser(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'scanner': stepScanner(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'clamp': stepClamp(sim, seat, use); break;\\n        default: break;\\n\",\"total_lines\":789}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"c52e32a7-d795-4ca0-9859-76d72cd9be22"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_93","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"setSite is called when f.site is an integer.\n\nactOn and unclamp both need to set f.site. Site switching will catch stuck bots before distance checks. I'll fix both bugs and trace adagio grande death. The circle cut may finish too early because atEnd is loose and the last point equals the first.\n\nThe circle cut finishes in about two seconds, which is plausible for a small circle. Tray position clears the ceiling clamp. Crescendo should be added to the variance grade list so extraction can achieve FLAWLESS.\n\nGrowth time will be about 80 seconds after the fix. I'll pad the content once all operation times are known.\n\nAdagio spawns with axis 90, unlike the horizontal tumor. killLaser sets grabbable but may not handle embedding correctly. I'm adding decorate adagio to trace this.\n\nAdagio dies from vitals during the fight, not extraction. It is grabbed and carried to the tray immediately because it has no embedded state. I will trace this after confirming the fix.\n\nTutorial fermata needs nine arrests before becoming grabbable. The tutorial sets its health to zero and triggers stage attack and beginArrest.\n\nTutorial fermata clears after one arrest, not nine. The needed:9 threshold prevents the eye from becoming grabbable until nine arrests are reached. The next phase wipe targets 'fermata'. In arrest2, two arrests survive while the eye is still alive but not grabbable. Arrest3 needs only one arrest and has 80 health.\n\nArrest3 clears after three arrests and requires extraction. The axis 90 pull is safe because embed 0.45 leaves room to y=0.95. A speed-zero start of a pull frame should be fine. I am checking whether crescendo's embedded flag resets every frame and prevents the pull from completing.\n\nStrains run after tools, so setting embedded once lets tools clear it and keeps it cleared. The unclamp site switch must check the projected site before distance when the bot is near the wrong site. Growth gel is already dead by the time unclamp starts; the bot is stuck because the tool becomes forceps and stays there.\n\nThe decide function's unclamp call is the only other direct path that skips site checks. Adagio's leftover scratch@tray is puzzling because gel kills scratches without moving them to the tray, and scratches are not grabbable.\n\nAdagio's leftover scratch@tray might come from an overTray release or a site change to tray. The bot may also be treating non-grabbable scratches as grabbable. Adagio still dies from vitals, so the grande trace is deferred until after the extraction fix.\n\nI will pad the operations with valid surgical content rather than dummy waits. The PLAN outlines will guide what to add. Broken-glass needs 41 seconds more, growth 118, staccato 100, and legato 150.\n\nFermata, adagio, coda, and GR each need roughly 100 seconds of padding. Gel zones are too fast to fill the gap alone; the bot moves at 0.58 speed and a single zone takes about 13 seconds. Sutures add only a few seconds. The bot is very fast, so I will either add many zones or slow specific actions.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c983cee-7157-4544-b390-4f6cb0d2fadc-42","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/strains.js","old_string":"    const cut = sim.entities.find((c) => c.kind === 'circleCut' && c.site === e.site && !c.alive);\n    if (cut) {\n      e.grabbable = true;\n      e.need = 'forceps';\n      e.embedded = true;\n      e.embed = e.embed || 0.35;\n      e.axis = 90;\n    }","new_string":"    const cut = sim.entities.find((c) => c.kind === 'circleCut' && c.site === e.site && !c.alive);\n    if (cut && !e.revealed) {\n      e.revealed = true;\n      e.grabbable = true;\n      e.need = 'forceps';\n      e.embedded = true;\n      e.embed = e.embed || 0.35;\n      e.axis = 90;\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c983cee-7157-4544-b390-4f6cb0d2fadc-43","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"function unclamp(me, e, mem, tuning, opts) {\n  const d = Math.hypot(me.x - e.x, me.y - e.y);\n  if (d > 0.05) {","new_string":"function unclamp(me, e, mem, tuning, opts, state) {\n  if (e.site && state && e.site !== me.site && e.site !== 'tray') {\n    const idx = state.sites.indexOf(e.site);\n    const f = steer(me, e.x, e.y, 0.6, tuning, opts);\n    if (idx >= 0) f.site = idx;\n    f.use = 0;\n    f.alt = false;\n    return f;\n  }\n  const d = Math.hypot(me.x - e.x, me.y - e.y);\n  if (d > 0.05) {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c983cee-7157-4544-b390-4f6cb0d2fadc-44","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"      return unclamp(me, clamped, mem, tuning, opts);","new_string":"      return unclamp(me, clamped, mem, tuning, opts, state);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c983cee-7157-4544-b390-4f6cb0d2fadc-45","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js","old_string":"    if (e.kind === 'shard' || e.kind === 'tumor' || e.kind === 'adagio' || e.kind === 'coda' || e.kind === 'ring' || e.kind === 'link' || e.kind === 'fermata') {","new_string":"    if (e.kind === 'shard' || e.kind === 'tumor' || e.kind === 'adagio' || e.kind === 'coda' || e.kind === 'ring' || e.kind === 'link' || e.kind === 