{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_95","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Growth-spurt is now OK at 23.\n\nFermata now fails on arrest1 instead of ring. Extraction worked but the tutorial arrest did not clear, so the shock on the tutorial fermata is broken. Coda remains stuck on recap with circleCut alive and crescendo.\n\nCoda's circle may be unfinished because the bot is distracted or site aorta blocks it. Adagio grande and GR still fail. The fermata tutorial eye might still count as alive despite zero HP.\n\nThe tutorial flag is exported correctly, so the bot should shock the fermata eye. The arrest logic appears sound, which means the tutorial fermata failure likely has a different cause.\n\nThe tutorial fermata should enter arrest immediately because it spawns with stage 'attack'. A lingering arrest from the previous phase is unlikely. The cause of the 400-second shock failure remains unclear.\n\nThe tutorial fermata eye has zero HP, so the shock cannot be weakened. The bot charges steadily and releases the shock at the correct time. The arrest failure is not caused by weak damage.\n\nThe tutorial fermata failure is not caused by the arrest clock expiring. The bot failed on time, which means the clock never reached zero. This suggests the tutorial arrest either never started, the clock is not decrementing, or the shocks are failing to register.\n\nA perfect shock would clear the tutorial arrest and advance the phase. The bot may be using weak shocks that subtract only 2 from the clock while it drains at 1 per second, keeping the clock above zero indefinitely.\n\nThe tutorial fermata likely never enters arrest because the phase wipe kills it before the spawn action can create it. The simulation runs all spawn actions before any begin actions, so the wipe executes first and the fermata never reaches stage 'attack'.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0e8c300e-79f7-403d-814d-fa8f061814e7-47","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"wipe|begin:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0e8c300e-79f7-403d-814d-fa8f061814e7-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js","offset":310,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":761,"output_tokens":1427,"cache_read_input_tokens":110976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"22cf327d-332c-4a86-a160-1ca53c14cd1f"}
