{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_97","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The crescendo is still present. The circleCut remains active.\n\nThe coda circle never finished. Fermata's circle completed in about two seconds. The bot likely spent the entire recap on a higher-priority task and only spawned the circle near the end. Alternatively, a bug may prevent cutting while busy. The leftover items are clamped bleeders on heart and lung, crescendo@aorta, and circleCut@aorta. No feeders remain.\n\nThe bot may be stuck cutting the coda circle. No other infinite job exists. The circle is priority 60, but the cut itself might never finish.\n\nFermata's circle finished very quickly, possibly due to a bug that instant-completes the cut. The `atEnd` check requires `along >= 0.72*len`, but `projectPoly` may pick the nearest segment on a closed loop, causing `along` to stay small and never reach the threshold.\n\nThe coda circle never finished because the bot was occupied with other tasks. Fermata's circle completed successfully, so the cut logic itself works. The leftover clamped bleeders on heart and lung are from the development phase and do not block progress.\n\nThe recap timer was 570 seconds but the run lasted 575. Development likely consumed most of that time. Crescendo began with only about 70 seconds left. The leftover circle is alive because the bot died on the timer while cutting it, not because it was stuck forever.\n\nI will log coda phase entry times with a quick script. Adagio grande has zero vitals because overlapping strains drain too fast. The fermata wipe fix will let arrest1 proceed, so I need to trace adagio and coda phase times and verify the rest of fermata completes. GR dies at 116 seconds before closing at 165; vitals hit zero from simultaneous threats. I will make GR survivable by lowering drain, reducing concurrent threats, and prioritizing survival.\n\nThe test requires one player to finish between 135 and 225 seconds. The death at 116 seconds occurs during the legato and crescendo wave before fermata begins. Vitals collapse from crescendo drain, adagio scratches, bleeders, and legato jerks. The bot prioritizes unclamped bleeders at 90, notes at 88, adagio core at 93, and feeders at 77. Crescendo drain is passive. If the bot fights adagio instead of killing feeders, crescendo kills it. GR switches sites globally with a 12-point site penalty.\n\nThe bot prioritizes local bleeders over distant crescendo feeders because the site penalty drops the feeder score to about 65. This causes the bot to ignore the global crescendo drain while clearing local work, which kills it. The plan compresses GR waves as a deviation, so the content must still be clearable.\n\nThe bot should interrupt routine tasks to kill crescendo feeders when vitals fall below 60 or the circle exceeds half size. Spreading the waves would break the time window, so that is not viable. The death at 116 seconds occurs during the 90-second wave.\n\nAdagio grande spawns only three scratches and three bleeders, so those jobs are finite. Staccato notes are also finite. The bot should reach crescendo feeders before the timer expires. Its death at 116 seconds is therefore not caused by ignoring distant feeders; it is caused by spending too long on local adagio and note work.\n\nCrescendo feeders should outrank almost all other jobs when the parent crescendo is unexposed. The bot should treat them as priority 94, since each feeder drains one point per second while crescendo drains four to six per second. Killing four feeders takes roughly eight seconds, which should be enough if the bot starts immediately. Adagio laser only hits the core on beats three and four, so its effective damage is about ten seconds of real time plus scratch damage.\n\nAdagio grande's death is a separate issue. I will trace it with a compact phase-time logger and a grande sampler.\n\nThe coda recap arrest is resolved. The fermata spawned after crescendo removal has nine needed hits, so it will not become grabbable. The bot lasered the eye to sixty health during the arrest, which satisfies the shock requirement.\n\nThe coda recap is the first arrest, so `arrestsSurvived` starts at zero and increments once during shock. The last-stop phase already shows two completed arrests. After the wipe fix, fermata arrest phases should proceed normally, though arrest3 still requires an extract.\n\nIf the coda circle remains unfinished, I will check it after applying both the wipe fix and the feeder priority change. To ensure the recap has enough time, I may shorten earlier coda phases by lowering health or removing links. The target finish time is 342 seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-368131b4-5306-4ad7-a73e-d8185f092ff5-51","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js","old_string":"    this.objective = phase.objective || '';\n    for (const spec of phase.spawn || []) this.spawnList(spec);\n    for (const act of phase.begin || []) this.act(act);","new_string":"    this.objective = phase.objective || '';\n    for (const act of phase.begin || []) if (act.wipe) this.act(act);\n    for (const spec of phase.spawn || []) this.spawnList(spec);\n    for (const act of phase.begin || []) if (!act.wipe) this.act(act);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-368131b4-5306-4ad7-a73e-d8185f092ff5-52","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/dbg-phases.mjs","content":"import { Sim } from '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js';\nimport { botInput } from '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js';\n\nconst id = process.argv[2] || 'adagio';\nconst watch = process.argv[3] || '';\nconst sim = new Sim({ op: id, seed: 1, difficulty: 'resident', physics: false });\nlet phase = '';\nlet last = -1;\nlet n = 0;\nwhile (!sim.over && n < 80000) {\n  for (const s of sim.state.seats) sim.input(s.id, botInput(sim, { id: s.id }, {}));\n  sim.step();\n  n += 1;\n  if (sim.phase?.id !== phase) {\n    phase = sim.phase?.id || '';\n    console.log('PHASE', phase, 't', sim.time.toFixed(1), 'v', sim.vitals.toFixed(1), 'score', sim.score);\n    last = -1;\n  }\n  if (watch && phase !== watch) continue;\n  const sec = Math.floor(sim.phaseTime);\n  if (sec === last || sec % 2 !== 0) continue;\n  last = sec;\n  const ad = sim.entities.find((e) => e.alive && e.kind === 'adagio');\n  const cres = sim.entities.find((e) => e.alive && e.kind === 'crescendo');\n  const circ = sim.entities.find((e) => e.alive && e.kind === 'circleCut');\n  const seat = sim.seats[0];\n  const kinds = {};\n  for (const e of sim.entities) if (e.alive && !e.tray) kinds[e.kind] = (kinds[e.kind] || 0) + 1;\n  console.log(JSON.stringify({\n    pt: sec, v: +sim.vitals.toFixed(1), tool: seat.tool, site: seat.site,\n    hp: ad ? +ad.hp.toFixed(0) : null,\n    core: ad?.core || false,\n    csize: cres ? +cres.size.toFixed(2) : null,\n    cexp: cres?.exposed || false,\n    along: circ ? +(circ.along || 0).toFixed(2) : null,\n    openB: sim.entities.filter((e) => e.alive && e.kind === 'bleeder' && !e.clamped).length,\n    kinds,\n  }));\n}\nconsole.log('END', sim.complete, sim.failed, phase, sim.time.toFixed(1), 'vmin', sim.vitalsMin.toFixed(1), 'score', sim.score);\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3431,"output_tokens":2994,"cache_read_input_tokens":115200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":nu