{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7537a339-a65f-4926-8ea2-e4fba84358d4-63","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"750→    return this._spawn(spec);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// The class method spawn above is replaced by the implementation that also builds children.\\nSim.prototype._spawn = Sim.prototype.spawn;\\n\\nconst rawSpawn = function spawn(spec) {\\n  if (spec.ifMissing) {\\n    const site = spec.site || this.activeSite;\\n760→    if (this.entities.some((e) => e.alive && e.kind === spec.kind && e.site === site)) return null;\\n  }\\n  const site = spec.site || this.activeSite;\\n  const at = spec.at || [0, 0];\\n  const e = {\\n    id: this.nextId++, kind: spec.kind, site, x: at[0], y: at[1],\\n    alive: true, hidden: !!spec.hidden, marked: !spec.hidden, strain: spec.strain || null,\\n  };\\n  Object.assign(e, this.decorate(spec, e));\\n  if (spec.strain) e.strain = spec.strain;\\n770→  this.entities.push(e);\\n  this.afterSpawn(e);\\n  return e;\\n};\\nSim.prototype.spawn = rawSpawn;\\n\\nSim.prototype.exportState = function exportState() {\\n  const num = (n) => (typeof n === 'number' ? Math.round(n * 1000) / 1000 : n);\\n  return {\\n    tick: this.tick,\",\"content_concise\":\"750→    return this._spawn(spec);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// The class method spawn above is replaced by the implementation that also builds children.\\nSim.prototype._spawn = Sim.prototype.spawn;\\n\\nconst rawSpawn = function spawn(spec) {\\n  if (spec.ifMissing) {\\n    const site = spec.site || this.activeSite;\\n760→    if (this.entities.some((e) => e.alive && e.kind === spec.kind && e.site === site)) return null;\\n  }\\n  const site = spec.site || this.activeSite;\\n  const at = spec.at || [0, 0];\\n  const e = {\\n    id: this.nextId++, kind: spec.kind, site, x: at[0], y: at[1],\\n    alive: true, hidden: !!spec.hidden, marked: !spec.hidden, strain: spec.strain || null,\\n  };\\n  Object.assign(e, this.decorate(spec, e));\\n  if (spec.strain) e.strain = spec.strain;\\n770→  this.entities.push(e);\\n  this.afterSpawn(e);\\n  return e;\\n};\\nSim.prototype.spawn = rawSpawn;\\n\\nSim.prototype.exportState = function exportState() {\\n  const num = (n) => (typeof n === 'number' ? Math.round(n * 1000) / 1000 : n);\\n  return {\\n    tick: this.tick,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js\",\"offset\":750,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"    return this._spawn(spec);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// The class method spawn above is replaced by the implementation that also builds children.\\nSim.prototype._spawn = Sim.prototype.spawn;\\n\\nconst rawSpawn = function spawn(spec) {\\n  if (spec.ifMissing) {\\n    const site = spec.site || this.activeSite;\\n    if (this.entities.some((e) => e.alive && e.kind === spec.kind && e.site === site)) return null;\\n  }\\n  const site = spec.site || this.activeSite;\\n  const at = spec.at || [0, 0];\\n  const e = {\\n    id: this.nextId++, kind: spec.kind, site, x: at[0], y: at[1],\\n    alive: true, hidden: !!spec.hidden, marked: !spec.hidden, strain: spec.strain || null,\\n  };\\n  Object.assign(e, this.decorate(spec, e));\\n  if (spec.strain) e.strain = spec.strain;\\n  this.entities.push(e);\\n  this.afterSpawn(e);\\n  return e;\\n};\\nSim.prototype.spawn = rawSpawn;\\n\\nSim.prototype.exportState = function exportState() {\\n  const num = (n) => (typeof n === 'number' ? Math.round(n * 1000) / 1000 : n);\\n  return {\\n    tick: this.tick,\\n\",\"total_lines\":856}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"bb4a9922-a49a-46f2-b9ff-5ea391cdf722"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_105","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Decorate sets points for circleCut.\n\nAdding a debug probe to inspect the bot cut at recap when the circle is closed and started. The bug likely stems from cutPoly behaving differently for bot versus simulation: on fermata the circle completes instantly near the line, but on coda feeders are killed and the bot switches to scalpel while along stays 0.\n\nThe bot is stationary with zero speed and no nick. It holds the scalpel because it is at the target point within 0.032. The simulation should have set started, but the bot remains in the !started hold branch.\n\nThe bot may have a stale started flag from a prior along of 0. The target point is 0.12 along the curve, but the tolerance is only 0.055. This creates a chicken-and-egg problem: the bot stops because it thinks it has reached the target, yet the simulation never advances along because the tip distance exceeds the tolerance.\n\nThe bot never leaves the hold branch, so it never advances along. The simulation must not be setting started true because the tip is not within 0.08 of points[0] while use is above 0.5.\n\nThe bot may stop at 0.012 from the target point, but the steer function returns early when magnitude drops below 0.13 before reaching 0.032. The resulting distance could exceed the 0.08 tolerance.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-34ec05a7-4095-46df-b222-8f40437f8e02-64","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/dbg-circle.mjs","content":"import { Sim } from '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js';\nimport { botInput } from '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js';\n\nconst sim = new Sim({ op: 'coda', seed: 1, difficulty: 'resident', physics: false });\nlet n = 0;\nlet logged = 0;\nwhile (!sim.over && n < 20000 && logged < 8) {\n  for (const s of sim.state.seats) sim.input(s.id, botInput(sim, { id: s.id }, {}));\n  sim.step();\n  n += 1;\n  if (sim.phase?.id !== 'recap' || sim.phaseTime < 15) continue;\n  if (n % 30 !== 0) continue;\n  const c = sim.entities.find((e) => e.kind === 'circleCut' && e.alive);\n  const seat = sim.seats[0];\n  const p0 = c?.points?.[0];\n  const d0 = p0 ? Math.hypot(seat.x - p0[0], seat.y - p0[1]) : null;\n  console.log(JSON.stringify({\n    pt: +sim.phaseTime.toFixed(2),\n    seat: [+seat.x.toFixed(3), +seat.y.toFixed(3)],\n    tool: seat.tool, use: +seat.use.toFixed(2), spd: +seat.speed.toFixed(3),\n    started: c?.started, along: c?.along, len: c?.len, done: c?.done,\n    nPts: c?.points?.length, p0, d0: d0 == null ? null : +d0.toFixed(3),\n    cx: c?.x, cy: c?.y,\n  }));\n  logged += 1;\n}\nconsole.log('stop', sim.phase?.id, sim.time.toFixed(1));\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":503,"output_tokens":1661,"cache_read_input_tokens":147584,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"7e0f4c1e-7170-4399-b507-bb51fe510881"}
