{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_107","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bot is stuck at x=0.111, y=0.\n\nThe bot is holding a scalpel but not using it. It is not steering toward p0 because the distance to the start is 0.109, which exceeds the 0.012 threshold for stopping. The target point or navigation logic appears to be misaligned.\n\nThe bot may be targeting a point near x=0.111 rather than p0 at 0.22. It might be inside cutPoly but failing to read the 13 points from state, or it could be using the wrong entity reference.\n\nThe 0.13 magnitude threshold is not the cause, since the required speed is roughly 0.46 and well above it. The bot may be bypassing cutPoly entirely, or stuck in a swipe-phase steering loop.\n\nThe site-switch frame is not the cause. The circle entity center is at (0, 0.02), and the seat is at (0.111, 0.02), so the distance is 0.111 and the bot should not be stopped there.\n\nThe bot may have stopped because its approach speed dropped below the magnitude threshold while near the center. I will log the actual bot frame and the candidate job to verify the target. I also need to check whether `e.started` is undefined versus false, and confirm the correct circle cut is being targeted.\n\nThe bot is emitting a zero-speed stop frame with the scalpel tool. I am now checking whether `state.started` is incorrectly true while `sim.started` is false, which would make cutPoly target a point along the circle instead of p0. The first point on that path is at (0.22, 0.02), matching the start position.\n\nThe 0.12-point target along the circle path is not at (0.111, 0.02). The seat position is exactly halfway between the center and p0, which does not match any known feeder or entity coordinate.\n\nI will add a temporary debug log in bot.js to inspect the stuck frame and candidates. I plan to trigger it during the coda recap phase when phase time exceeds 15 seconds, then remove it. I am also re-examining the steer function.\n\nThe steer function returns a stop when distance is under 0.012 or magnitude under 0.13, and goTool forces use to zero. This confirms the bot is frozen in a stop loop every frame.\n\nThe circle points are stored directly on the entity object, not through JSON serialization, so the bot should see them correctly.\n\nIf state.started were true while the seat is at 0.111, pointAlong would target roughly 0.111 rather than p0 at 0.22. The seat position does not match that path target, so this scenario is ruled out.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9e9aee22-5aea-4e53-bfe6-efbdf97dc2f0-66","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/dbg-circle.mjs","old_string":"  for (const s of sim.state.seats) sim.input(s.id, botInput(sim, { id: s.id }, {}));\n  sim.step();","new_string":"  let frame = null;\n  for (const s of sim.state.seats) {\n    frame = botInput(sim, { id: s.id }, {});\n    sim.input(s.id, frame);\n  }\n  sim.step();"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":910,"output_tokens":1846,"cache_read_input_tokens":149760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"433b5251-66c5-4321-a58d-01f1caae20ac"}
