1,101,100,101,114,64,98,111,119,101,108,99,44,98,108,101,101,100,101,114,64,104,101,97,114,116,99,44,99,114,101,115,99,101,110,100,111,64,104,101,97,114,116,44,102,101,101,100,101,114,64,104,101,97,114,116,44,102,101,101,100,101,114,64,104,101,97,114,116,44,102,101,101,100,101,114,64,104,101,97,114,116,44,102,101,101,100,101,114,64,104,101,97,114,116,44,98,108,101,101,100,101,114,64,98,111,119,101,108,99,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\nbroken-glass   OK ph=finish t=103.5 frac=0.431 vmin=75.0 miss=0 score=8949 rank=S wall=258 left=\\ngrowth-spurt   OK ph=close t=76.9 frac=0.233 vmin=45.7 miss=0 score=9747 rank=S wall=210 left=bleeder@bowel,bleeder@bowel\\nadagio         OK ph=close t=97.8 frac=0.296 vmin=39.5 miss=0 score=10215 rank=S wall=181 left=\\nstaccato       OK ph=close t=116.3 frac=0.323 vmin=69.5 miss=0 score=16789 rank=S wall=214 left=\\nlegato         OK ph=repair t=65.6 frac=0.182 vmin=98.5 miss=0 score=27332 rank=S wall=204 left=bleeder@brain,bleeder@brain,bleeder@brain,bleeder@brain\\nfermata        OK ph=close t=59.4 frac=0.141 vmin=68.3 miss=0 score=11961 rank=A wall=123 left=bleeder@heart\\ncoda           FAIL:vitals ph=conductor t=82.0 frac=0.144 vmin=-1.5 miss=0 score=24138 rank=- wall=277 left=bleeder@heartc,bleeder@lungc,bleeder@lungc,bleeder@lungc,fermata@aorta,coda@heart,baton@heart,baton@heart\\nlast-patient   OK ph=one-shock t=3.6 frac=0.090 vmin=100.0 miss=0 score=4208 rank=- wall=10 left=bleeder@heart\\ngrand-rounds   FAIL:vitals ph=rounds t=110.3 frac=0.368 vmin=-0.1 miss=0 score=15317 rank=- wall=199 left=bleeder@bowelc,bleeder@heartc,crescendo@heart,feeder@heart,feeder@heart,feeder@heart,feeder@heart,bleeder@bowelc\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/smoke.mjs\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Re-smoke ops after circle guide and tray fixes\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-033fe23a-097b-4125-ab0b-a943dc64118c-80.log\",\"total_bytes\":1217}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"1d3c649a-def7-49bd-bc5d-ddab04bd9fcb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_116","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All story operations except the coda are complete.\n\nGR still dies. All remaining story segments need significant time increases. Broken-glass needs 30–50 seconds. Growth needs 80–140 seconds. Adagio needs 50–140 seconds. Staccato needs 45–150 seconds. Legato needs 100–190 seconds. Fermata needs 130–250 seconds. The coda conductor kills GR at 82 seconds. The last-patient segment is fine.\n\nThe coda boss is too lethal for the bot's laser windows. The bot beams batons at priority 96 whenever a baton has health, and it can laser during the wind-up beat. Blocking downbeat damage should be possible, yet the bot still dies.\n\nScratches and accumulated chip damage likely contribute to the coda death. The plan is to make the coda and GR survivable first, then pad all remaining operations by increasing their work load rather than adding fake delays.\n\nA single gel zone takes roughly ten seconds. Adding about twelve zones would close the gap for fermata, but that is a large data change.\n\nA global slowdown would make broken-glass too slow. The better approach is to lower each operation's timer so the same clear time falls inside the target band. For broken-glass, a timer of 170 gives a 60.9% fraction. Growth needs a timer around 128 for a 60% band. I will check PLAN.md for the exact target durations.\n\nLowering operation timers to match the bot's speed would make the band a human-friendly target. A slower player might then time out.\n\nThe bot is the intended calibration standard for a competent player. Its speed reflects insufficient work in the operations, not a timer problem. The plan calls for more work or a slower bot. A global slowdown of roughly 2.2x would fix the timing band.\n\nA single global slowdown multiplier cannot fix the timing band. Broken-glass would clear at 95% of its timer, which is too slow. Fermata and legato would still sit outside the target range.\n\nThe better approach is to tune each operation's timer individually. Short operations need longer budgets. Long-budget operations can be shortened slightly. This is a one-line data change per operation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd0628f1-3113-4271-b739-955cc469d2d3-81","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"timer:|5:30|7:00|minutes|Broken Glass","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd0628f1-3113-4271-b739-955cc469d2d3-82","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/ops/broken-glass.js","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd0628f1-3113-4271-b739-955cc469d2d3-83","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md","offset":280,"limit":70}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":735,"output_tokens":1616,"cache_read_input_tokens":161280,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"90b00e30-90d2-48c9-8045-da003e43e037"}
