{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_123","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Feeder priority 95 broke fermata and adagio close. Beam pulse and fortissimo bleeders likely conflict with feeder prioritization. The adagio timeout may be caused by beam pulse slowing the laser.\n\nAdagio close timed out at 330 seconds, far slower than the previous 97-second finish. GR is stable at exactly 60% with vmin 43.5. Fermata dies at the ring after 31 seconds despite feeder priority 95; fortissimo bleeders at 90 may be overriding the laser feeders.\n\nBeam pulse every 4.6 seconds may be breaking the feeder race, causing feeders to respawn endlessly and fortissimo to drain them. Adagio close failure likely stems from arriving too late at the close point.\n\nThe beam pulse should be reverted. It hurts more than it helps. Fermata previously cleared the ring with feeder priority 77, so raising it to 95 is likely the real cause of the failure.\n\nFeeder priority 95 ignores fortissimo bleeders, so fermata dies from their drain. GR succeeds at the same priority because its bleeders are harmless. The beam pulse should be reverted, but feeder priority 95 is too dangerous for fermata.\n\nConditional feeder priority is being considered: 95 only when vitals exceed 60%, otherwise clamping bleeders first. A fixed priority of 88 is also being tested. This would outrank scratches and notes while still losing to fortissimo bleeders, potentially saving GR from ignoring feeders during other tasks.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The laser pulse and feeder priority are fighting the ring and the close. I’ll drop the pulse and let bleeders outrank feeders again."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7b902c1a-dc15-4dde-b755-320b5c180c9c-95","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"function beam(me, e, tuning, opts, mem) {\n  mem.beamT = (mem.beamT || 0) + 1 / 60;\n  if (mem.beamT > 4.6) {\n    if (mem.beamT > 4.85) mem.beamT = 0;\n    return hold('laser', 0);\n  }\n  const d = Math.hypot(me.x - e.x, me.y - e.y);","new_string":"function beam(me, e, tuning, opts) {\n  const d = Math.hypot(me.x - e.x, me.y - e.y);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7b902c1a-dc15-4dde-b755-320b5c180c9c-96","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  if (job === 'beam') return beam(me, e, tuning, opts, mem);","new_string":"  if (job === 'beam') return beam(me, e, tuning, opts);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7b902c1a-dc15-4dde-b755-320b5c180c9c-97","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"    if (eye && !state.arrest.tutorial) return beam(me, eye, tuning, opts, mem);","new_string":"    if (eye && !state.arrest.tutorial) return beam(me, eye, tuning, opts);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7b902c1a-dc15-4dde-b755-320b5c180c9c-98","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"    else if (e.kind === 'feeder') { job = 'beam'; prio = 95; }","new_string":"    else if (e.kind === 'feeder') { job = 'beam'; prio = state.vitals < 55 ? 86 : 94; }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":511,"output_tokens":1591,"cache_read_input_tokens":176896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa5