.07,\\\"site\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"cs\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"bats\\\":[15,0],\\\"notes\\\":1,\\\"spores\\\":7,\\\"scratches\\\":5}\\n{\\\"pt\\\":14.5,\\\"v\\\":17.3,\\\"hp\\\":263,\\\"open\\\":false,\\\"seen\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"laser\\\",\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"vent\\\":0,\\\"sx\\\":-0.12,\\\"sy\\\":0.07,\\\"site\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"cs\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"bats\\\":[15,0],\\\"notes\\\":1,\\\"spores\\\":7,\\\"scratches\\\":5}\\n{\\\"pt\\\":15,\\\"v\\\":13.2,\\\"hp\\\":263,\\\"open\\\":true,\\\"seen\\\":true,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"laser\\\",\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"vent\\\":0,\\\"sx\\\":-0.17,\\\"sy\\\":0.06,\\\"site\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"cs\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"bats\\\":[15,15],\\\"notes\\\":0,\\\"spores\\\":8,\\\"scratches\\\":5}\\n{\\\"pt\\\":15.5,\\\"v\\\":11,\\\"hp\\\":263,\\\"open\\\":true,\\\"seen\\\":true,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"laser\\\",\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"vent\\\":0,\\\"sx\\\":0.24,\\\"sy\\\":0.1,\\\"site\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"cs\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"bats\\\":[15,15],\\\"notes\\\":0,\\\"spores\\\":8,\\\"scratches\\\":5}\\n{\\\"pt\\\":16,\\\"v\\\":8.8,\\\"hp\\\":263,\\\"open\\\":false,\\\"seen\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"laser\\\",\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"vent\\\":0,\\\"sx\\\":0.8,\\\"sy\\\":0.19,\\\"site\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"cs\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"bats\\\":[15,15],\\\"notes\\\":1,\\\"spores\\\":8,\\\"scratches\\\":5}\\n{\\\"pt\\\":16.5,\\\"v\\\":0,\\\"hp\\\":263,\\\"open\\\":false,\\\"seen\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"laser\\\",\\\"use\\\":0,\\\"vent\\\":0,\\\"sx\\\":0.96,\\\"sy\\\":0.21,\\\"site\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"cs\\\":\\\"heart\\\",\\\"bats\\\":[15,15],\\\"notes\\\":0,\\\"spores\\\":9,\\\"scratches\\\":6}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/dbg-coda.mjs\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Half-second trace of the coda conductor\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-b64d97de-33e7-46e6-9e1c-299aa77023d5-101.log\",\"total_bytes\":6239}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d4daef01-aa79-4c6c-a34f-a0bc07df9048"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_127","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The core opens briefly, visible for roughly one second in the samples.\n\nThe bot is trapped at the IV, never reaching the boss. Vitals stay below 40 from spores and scratches; healing only lasts until the next drain. Baton HP resets to 15 every downbeat, so both bats are rarely killed before the slam.\n\nDownbeat is blocked whenever any baton has zero HP. Notes spawn on beat 3 regardless.\n\nSpores drain 0.3 per second and never expire. The bot ignores them while laser-hunting batons, so vitals collapse. Notes should be grabbed before they burst, with priority above batons except during wind-up. The bot must gel spores and scratches during coda instead of laser-hunting the entire time.\n\nBaton targets are now restricted to the wind-up phase. A new coda wait job will keep the bot camped on the core during open windows, and it will only leave for critical heals or wind-up batons.\n\nCamping priority is 70, below notes at 88 and spores at 82. The bot will clear those first before settling on the core. Syringing at 40 vitals pulls the bot away for several seconds and misses core windows; stabilizing vitals by clearing spores is the real fix. Notes spawn two beats after their birth, so nearby camping should catch them.\n\nA coda-camping bot can reach a note in about 0.5 seconds, well under its two-beat lifespan. Spores are instantly killed on contact. If the bot starts moving before the wind-up ends, it can still kill a baton in roughly 0.5 seconds; missing is acceptable as long as spores do not stack.\n\nThe bot needs to reach the baton before beat 4 starts. The travel time is roughly 0.3 seconds, leaving only about 0.35 seconds of laser. That may not kill a baton with 15 HP in one beat. The plan says 0.5 seconds should suffice, so the baton HP might need to drop to 8.\n\nAt 30 damage per second, a 0.5-second laser deals exactly 15 damage. If the bot is late by even 0.3 seconds, it only does 10 damage and the baton survives. The next bar its HP resets to 15, so that partial progress is wasted. The plan requires laser during this exact wind-up, and the ring telegraphs one beat early as designed.\n\nThe bot cannot pre-position on the baton because windup is only true during beat 4. I will keep the one-beat telegraph and lower baton HP to 9. A late arrival can then kill it in roughly 0.3 seconds, giving the bot a tuning concession.\n\nPre-positioning on the baton is impossible because the bot only sees the windup flag. Extending the telegraph to two beats would break the design. Camping closer to a baton is too complex. The better fix is to stop resetting baton HP every bar and let damage accumulate across the wind-up instead.\n\nBaton HP is set to 10. A late arrival can still kill it in about 0.63 seconds, fitting one beat.\n\nCoda camp wait priority is raised to 60 so notes and spores are cleared first. The baton laser stays at 96 during wind-up and the core at 97.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b2584697-b90a-4512-9dc7-d42aa79bbd3c-102","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"kind: 'baton'|a\\.hp = 15|hp: 15","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3019,"output_tokens":2158,"cache_read_input_tokens":182144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"5bcb0c9a-e869-4d0b-a48a-996017b07703"}
