{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_138","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"VitalsSet 88 did not resolve the issue. The character still dies at 118, and the coda remains stuck on the heart without moving.\n\nScratch priority 84 was tested and failed. The successful run used 82. Raising it to 90 also caused death.\n\nThe successful run started at vitals 48, which triggered Hush and slowed the boss by fourfold. With vitalsSet 88, the threshold is no longer met and Hush never fires. The boss attacks at full speed, overwhelming the character.\n\nThe real problem is the minimum vitals dip during hush. Even with Hush active, the lowest recorded point was 4.2. The character recovered afterward but never stayed above 35. To keep vmin above 35, I need to reduce incoming damage or increase healing. Cheating by flooring or locking vitals is not an option.\n\nThe bot syringes whenever vitals fall below 40. Hush only triggers if vitals are below 50 and composure is at least 100. Because the bot always stays under 40, it never reaches the 50-point threshold for Hush. The boss attacks at full speed while the character is constantly running to the IV.\n\nThe fix is to check the gift before the syringe. This lets Hush trigger immediately when vitals drop below 50 and composure reaches 100. The successful run likely survived because Hush fired while vitals were between 40 and 50. Composure may already be at 100 from prior scoring.\n\nThe successful run started at 48.7 vitals, so the gift fires before the syringe check and Hush should trigger immediately if composure is at 100. The dip to 4 occurred during or after that Hush, because the gift lasts seven seconds at quarter speed before the boss returns to full damage.\n\nHush only lasts seven seconds, so the boss returns to full damage and the character crashes. Re-triggering Hush once composure refills is possible but may not be enough.\n\nA better fix is reducing coda damage. The plan calls for spawning a note every bar, but those notes become spores that drain vitals. If the bot grabs them, no spore accumulates. The log shows spores did pile up, which means the grabs failed. Notes at priority 88 should outrank camp at 64, so the bot ought to catch them.\n\nThe bot is likely too busy with scratches to catch notes before they burst. Notes last only about 1.3 seconds, so the bot misses them when it is on the other side of the field or holding a baton.\n\nRaising note priority to 96 would let the bot grab them before they expire. This would stop spores from accumulating and reduce damage.\n\nExtending note lifetime would be a rules change. The timing works out: beat 3 spawns the note, beat 4 is windup where the bot is on a baton, and beat 1 is downbeat or core.\n\nThe note bursts during beat 4 because the bot is on a baton for the entire two-beat window. Extending its lifetime to four beats would give the bot time to grab it after the wind-up. However, the plan explicitly requires staccato notes to burst quickly, and changing the global lifetime would alter staccato difficulty and op timing.\n\nA targeted fix is to give coda notes a longer fuse. The stepNote logic already checks `e.life`, so spawning coda notes with `life: 4` would let the bot grab them after the baton wind-up. This avoids changing the global staccato rule while still reducing spore damage.\n\nMissed downbeats are the real source of early scratches. If those gel at priority 84 between windups, they will not stack to seven. The successful run stacked because the bot was syringing constantly; with notes no longer becoming spores, drain drops and syringing becomes less urgent, leaving more time for gelling and core hits.\n\nThe plan is to extend note lifetime to four beats for coda cues only, and either remove vitalsSet so Hush can trigger naturally or force an initial Hush by setting composure to 100 and vitals to 49.\n\nThe plan is to remove vitalsSet so Hush can trigger naturally, extend note lifetime to four beats for coda cues only, and keep baton cleanup on extract. Scratch priority will stay at 84. If the minimum vitals still drops too low, a vitalsSet of 45 would force the hush band.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c3aad83a-7584-4efc-88d2-b81be80eb540-119","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/ops/coda.js","old_string":"      tools: ['laser', 'forceps', 'gel', 'clamp'],\n      begin: [{ vitalsSet: 88 }],\n      spawn: [{ kind: 'coda', site: 'heart', at: [0, 0.02], hp: 300 }],","new_string":"      tools: ['laser', 'forceps', 'gel', 'clamp'],\n      spawn: [{ kind: 'coda', site: 'heart', at: [0, 0.02], hp: 300 }],"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c3aad83a-7584-4efc-88d2-b81be80eb540-120","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/strains.js","old_string":"      sim.spawn({ kind: 'note', site: e.site, at: [e.x + 0.2, e.y], born: sim.beat.count });","new_string":"      sim.spawn({ kind: 'note', site: e.site, at: [e.x + 0.2, e.y], born: sim.beat.count, life: 5 });"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c3aad83a-7584-4efc-88d2-b81be80eb540-121","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/strains.js","old_string":"  const age = sim.beat.count - (e.born || sim.beat.count);\n  if (age >= 2) {","new_string":"  const age = sim.beat.count - (e.born || sim.beat.count);\n  if (age >= (e.life || 2)) {"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":384,"output_tokens":2531,"cache_