{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_141","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Coda has completed. The minimum value is 16.9, below the threshold of 35, and the fraction is zero.\n\nStaccato reverted to original numbers. The score matches the early run and is stable.\n\nThe 16.9 minimum during the Coda arrest hold is puzzling. Either real damage drops vitals after the arrest, or the vitalsMin skip is failing.\n\nThe 15 minimum likely comes from a prior arrest. The first hold saved pre-hold vitals, so the restored value was already 15.\n\nThe 16.9 minimum likely comes from the conductor fight, not the arrest hold. The hold is skipped, so the fight itself drops vitals to 16.9.\n\nI will raise healing or add an earlier syringe buffer during Coda when vitals fall below 55 and the core is still closed.\n\nThe 16.9 minimum matches the drain math exactly: 40 minus 24 points lost over four seconds of damage equals 16. The bot syringes at 40, but the drain continues during the IV trip.\n\nI will either gel the drains before leaving, syringe earlier, or raise the buffer to 58 so the trip lands near 34.\n\nThe syringe threshold will be 58 whenever a scratch, spore, or coda is alive, and 40 otherwise. This keeps quiet operations unchanged while ensuring boss fights heal before the hole. Adagio also has scratches, so starting at 58 there may slow the op slightly but will raise the minimum vitals margin.\n\nGrowth crash is safe at 45.7 minimum vitals. The Coda phase is at 29% of the target and needs roughly 170 seconds of padding. I will add gel zones after reviewing shape.js and nearby phases to build a shared helper.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f0b14d42-2229-4486-97af-366202d5228a-124","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/