{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_145","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The adagio timeout is caused by healAt 58 triggering on scratches. This creates constant IV trips during the entire fight and exhausts the close phase.\n\nNarrowing `hot` to living coda only. Coda needs healAt 64 to land at 38 instead of 32.5. Earlier trips may shift drain timing and add time.\n\nCoda only needs 5 to 40 seconds of extra time. The current 103.5s is just under the 108s threshold. A small raise should be safe. I am weighing gel or suture work for the remaining ops. I also need a padding strategy for all operations.\n\nGrowth needs 121 seconds. Adagio needs 100. Staccato needs 100. Legato needs 150. Fermata needs 193. Coda needs about 90 more seconds.\n\nGel or suture work should be placed in closing phases after the boss, not during active combat. Growth is already at 0.596 and needs no padding. I am reviewing all operations to identify suitable close-phase gel or suture spots. One gel zone takes roughly 8–12 seconds; a default gel paint takes about 26 seconds.\n\nFive to eight large gel zones could add roughly 130 seconds, but the bot may only paint one zone per phase. Suture timing is still unknown; it likely takes 6–12 seconds. Gel rectangles must also fall inside the drape ellipse.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c53e28c1-3efd-4b50-888b-5d60000aead7-8","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"gelZone|function gel|job === 'gel'|paint","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c53e28c1-3efd-4b50-888b-5d60000aead7-9","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/s