32,112,104,97,115,101,59,32,117,110,108,111,99,107,32,101,118,101,114,121,116,104,105,110,103,59,32,112,108,97,121,32,97,110,121,32,115,116,111,114,121,32,115,99,101,110,101,46,10,54,52,52,58,45,32,67,111,109,112,108,101,116,101,32,111,98,106,101,99,116,105,118,101,59,32,99,111,109,112,108,101,116,101,32,112,104,97,115,101,59,32,119,105,110,32,111,112,101,114,97,116,105,111,110,59,32,102,97,105,108,32,111,112,101,114,97,116,105,111,110,59,32,102,111,114,99,101,32,97,110,121,32,114,97,110,107,32,114,101,112,111,114,116,46,10,54,52,53,58,45,32,71,111,100,32,109,111,100,101,32,40,108,111,99,107,32,118,105,116,97,108,115,41,59,32,102,114,101,101,122,101,32,116,105,109,101,114,59,32,105,110,102,105,110,105,116,101,32,67,111,109,112,111,115,117,114,101,59,32,105,110,102,105,110,105,116,101,32,99,108,97,109,112,115,46,10,54,54,51,58,124,32,124,32,96,103,101,108,82,97,100,105,117,115,96,32,124,32,48,46,49,54,32,124,32,48,46,48,56,226,128,147,48,46,51,32,124,32,71,101,108,32,98,114,117,115,104,32,40,102,117,41,32,124,10,54,55,49,58,124,32,124,32,96,116,105,109,101,114,77,117,108,116,96,32,124,32,49,32,124,32,48,46,53,226,128,147,50,32,124,32,65,108,108,32,116,105,109,101,114,115,32,124,10,55,50,52,58,124,32,96,115,96,32,124,32,104,111,115,116,32,226,134,146,32,97,108,108,32,124,32,117,110,114,101,108,105,97,98,108,101,32,124,32,49,48,47,115,32,124,32,84,105,99,107,44,32,98,101,97,116,44,32,118,105,116,97,108,115,44,32,116,105,109,101,114,44,32,116,105,112,115,44,32,109,111,118,105,110,103,32,101,110,116,105,116,105,101,115,46,32,42,42,77,97,120,32,49,44,49,48,48,32,98,121,116,101,115,42,42,58,32,108,97,114,103,101,114,32,117,110,114,101,108,105,97,98,108,101,32,109,101,115,115,97,103,101,115,32,102,114,97,103,109,101,110,116,32,97,110,100,32,97,114,101,32,108,111,115,116,32,119,104,111,108,101,32,124,10,55,50,54,58,124,32,96,101,96,32,124,32,104,111,115,116,32,226,134,146,32,97,108,108,32,124,32,114,101,108,105,97,98,108,101,32,124,32,117,112,32,116,111,32,53,47,115,32,124,32,66,97,116,99,104,101,100,32,101,118,101,110,116,115,58,32,103,114,97,100,101,115,44,32,112,111,112,115,44,32,98,97,114,107,115,44,32,112,104,97,115,101,32,99,104,97,110,103,101,115,32,124,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":40,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"4. **One more try.** Hard, but never a spike: checkpoints per phase, an honest assist, tuning verified by a bot (§17).\"},{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"| Tool rhythm: drain, gel, laser, forceps, suture, scalpel, syringe, defibrillator | Keep the genre's vocabulary. Add the **clamp** (beat-timed) and a **scanner**. Make the rules ours (§4) |\"},{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"| Difficulty spikes | Per-phase checkpoints, Bea's Notes assist, bot-verified timers (§3.8, §17) |\"},{\"line_number\":129,\"content\":\"`bpm = op.bpm + tempoPressure × (1 - vitals/100)`, smoothed over 1 s. A phase accumulator advances by `dt × timeScale × bpm/60`. Every wrap fires a `beat` event; 4 beats make a bar. The event drives tissue squeeze, ECG spike, HUD pulse, strain actions and rumble. The music follows the same `bpm` and aligns its quarter notes to `beat` (§11). Hush slows it; Fermata stops it.\"},{\"line_number\":166,\"content\":\"- **The Hush (Ren):** a 0.4 s held breath with everything frozen, then for `hushDuration` seconds, strains, drains, timers and the beat run at `hushTimeScale` while your tip and tools run at full speed. An ink-wash expands from the tip: sumi-e monochrome, with red the only color left. Music low-passes down to almost nothing; only the slow heartbeat remains.\"},{\"line_number\":183,\"content\":\"**Checkpoints:** every phase is a checkpoint. Failing offers *Retry phase*, *Restart operation*, *Quit*. Retrying a phase restores vitals to at least 60, the timer to at least 90 s, and the score to the checkpoint's. Phases must be self-contained: a phase's `spawn` lists everything it needs, so `skipTo(phase)` works for retry, dev mode and attract mode alike. Use `ifMissing: true` for what an earlier phase normally leaves behind, such as clamps.\"},{\"line_number\":185,\"content\":\"**Bea's Notes (assist):** after failing the same phase twice, Bea offers her notebook: 30% more time, 30% less drain, rank capped at B. It's optional, stated honestly, and shown on the report.\"},{\"line_number\":232,\"content\":\"- **Gel.** Hold Use: paints a coverage grid (cell 0.04 fu) within `gelRadius`. A zone completes at 90%. Scratches heal when coated for 1 s. Spores clear on contact. Nest holes seal after 1 s. Grade against the zone's par time.\"},{\"line_number\":249,\"content\":\"| **Staccato** | *staccato (adj.): short, sharp, detached. Like her prognosis.* | Tiny black note-heads with flags popping out of holes | Holes spawn notes on off-beats. A note lives 2 beats, then bursts into a spore patch (-2 vitals, then 0.3 vitals/s until gelled). Hidden nests need the Scanner | Laser tap (0.25 s) or Forceps pinch (0.2 s). Gel 1 s (or 3 stitches) seals a nest | Pizzicato on the off-beats |\"},{\"line_number\":262,\"content\":\"### Op 1: Broken Glass (Chapter 1, Ren). Forearm. Timer 4:00, 72 bpm\"},{\"line_number\":265,\"content\":\"1. **Clean:** one gel zone (1.2 × 0.5).\"},{\"line_number\":270,\"content\":\"6. **Finish:** gel zone over the stitches.\"},{\"line_number\":275,\"content\":\"1. **Open:** gel zone, one long incision (1.4 fu). Ink wipe to the bowel site.\"},{\"line_number\":280,\"content\":\"6. **Close:** take clamps off, close incision (10 gates), gel.\"},{\"line_number\":284,\"content\":\"1. **Open:** gel, short incision.\"},{\"line_number\":289,\"content\":\"6. **Close:** clamps off, suture 2 lesions, gel.\"},{\"line_number\":293,\"content\":\"1. **Open:** gel, incision.\"},{\"line_number\":298,\"content\":\"6. **Close:** suture, gel.\"},{\"line_number\":307,\"content\":\"5. **Repair:** suture the vessel (tight gates), clamps off, gel.\"},{\"line_number\":311,\"content\":\"1. **Consult,** then **open:** long incision, gel.\"},{\"line_number\":317,\"content\":\"7. **Close:** clamps off, suture, gel.\"},{\"line_number\":329,\"content\":\"### Last Patient (Chapter 4 ending, Ren). Heart. No HUD, no timer, can't fail\"},{\"line_number\":336,\"content\":\"1. **0:00, Open up:** 2 incisions (liver), 4 shards (bowel), gel zones, 2 bleeders.\"},{\"line_number\":340,\"content\":\"5. **4:15, Close:** wounds everywhere. Done before the timer: win.\"},{\"line_number\":368,\"content\":\"**Bea's barks.** Write 60 or so short in-operation lines keyed by event, each with an expression: `start, nextPhase, toolHint(tool), idle, vitalsLow, vitalsCritical, miss, streak, bleeding, overflow, clampReminder, strainIntro(strain), hushReady, timerLow, success, fail`. A taste:\"},{\"line_number\":375,\"content\":\"- `timerLow`: \\\"Clock, child.\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":483,\"content\":\"| Blood / gel / laser / suture thread | `#C4142F` / `#7CF2C9` / `#FF3B6B` / `#2B6CFF` |\"},{\"line_number\":515,\"content\":\"**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends). For a 1024² canvas on that plane, field to canvas is `cx = (x + 1.8) / 3.6 × 1024`, `cy = (1.25 - y) / 2.5 × 1024`.\"},{\"line_number\":572,\"content\":\"| Face (driven by code, not clips) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression redraws |\"},{\"line_number\":573,\"content\":\"| Instruments | Scalpel press, forceps pinch, suction throb, gel squeeze, needle stitch, laser recoil, scanner sweep, clamp ratchet, syringe plunge, paddles slide-in, charge, slam |\"},{\"line_number\":598,\"content\":\"| OR base | Pulsing minor-key bass that tightens as bpm rises; layers enter with phases |\"},{\"line_number\":607,\"content\":\"Heartbeat double thump (pitch-dropping sine), ECG beep, flatline tone, scalpel slice (filtered noise sweep), forceps click, pop, glass clink (inharmonic partials), suction gurgle, gel spray, stitch tick, thread zip, laser buzz (pitch follows power), scanner ping, clamp ratchet, syringe hiss, defib whine and thump, strain chitter and screech, scratch tear, stamp thud, UI move/confirm/back, rain, gallery murmur, door, phone ring, alarm. Rain ambience in story scenes outdoors or at windows.\"},{\"line_number\":631,\"content\":\"- **What it is:** the real game, driven by the bot (§15.5) with cheats on: vitals locked, timers frozen, Composure always full, free phase jumps. A corner \\\"DEMO\\\" mark and a pulsing \\\"Press any button\\\".\"},{\"line_number\":643,\"content\":\"- Jump to any operation and phase; unlock everything; play any story scene.\"},{\"line_number\":644,\"content\":\"- Complete objective; complete phase; win operation; fail operation; force any rank report.\"},{\"line_number\":645,\"content\":\"- God mode (lock vitals); freeze timer; infinite Composure; infinite clamps.\"},{\"line_number\":663,\"content\":\"| | `gelRadius` | 0.16 | 0.08–0.3 | Gel brush (fu) |\"},{\"line_number\":671,\"content\":\"| | `timerMult` | 1 | 0.5–2 | All timers |\"},{\"line_number\":724,\"content\":\"| `s` | host → all | unreliable | 10/s | Tick, beat, vitals, timer, tips, moving entities. **Max 1,100 bytes**: larger unreliable messages fragment and are lost whole |\"},{\"line_number\":726,\"content\":\"| `e` | host → all | reliable | up to 5/s | Batched events: grades, pops, barks, phase changes |\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"12162c54-0182-4710-95c0-f1e18fa76e76"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_150","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reviewing the PLAN.md structure to identify tasks that can be completed on this computer.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c19057f4-1f78-446b-add4-bddf7f71ab59-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md","offset":250,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c19057f4-1f78-446b-add4-bddf7f71ab59-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"45%|75%|parScore|Normal bot|minTime|padding|time band","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4031,"output_tokens":234,"cache_read_input_tokens":65024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"dc7781d3-d6b1-4bf1-9d14-70a60024a248"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c19057f4-1f78-446b-add4-bddf7f71ab59-24","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"250→| **Tremolo** | *tremolo (n.): a rapid, nervous trembling. Yours, specifically.* | Pale moth with stave-striped wings, always shivering | Flees at 0.9 fu/s if the tip is within 0.6 fu moving faster than 0.45 fu/s. Scratches 1.5 vitals/s while fleeing. Freezes if you approach slowly | Steady in, Scanner 1 s to pin (3 s), Laser 40 HP. Three pins | Fast high strings |\\n| **Legato** | *legato (adj.): smoothly connected, without a break. It does not want a break.* | Bead chain joined by curved slur ribbons, on Rapier rope joints, head pinned | Must be cut **tail first**; the active link glows. Wrong link: two links re-heal, vitals -4. Cut pieces reattach after 8 beats unless carried to the tray. Every 8 beats it jerks and opens a bleeder | Scalpel sever, then Forceps to tray | Gliding portamento lead |\\n| **Crescendo** | *crescendo (n.): gradually getting louder. She is about to get very loud.* | A hairpin \\\"<\\\" wedge wrapped into a ring that widens | Size grows by `0.02 + 0.015 × live feeders` per second, from 0.2 to 1. Drain `1 + 6 × size` vitals/s. Four feeders (HP 40) regrow every 16 beats. At size 1: **Fortissimo**: -20 vitals, 2 bleeders, size resets to 0.6 | Kill all feeders: the ring shrinks and shows a circular cut line. Scalpel the circle, Forceps it out | One new voice every bar |\\n| **Fermata** | *fermata (n.): hold. Hold until the conductor releases you. The conductor is not coming.* | The fermata sign as a giant eye: an arc and a dot, opening on the heart | Stops the heart: music cuts to silence, ECG flat, 8 s arrest clock, vitals hold at 15. While the heart is stopped the eye is exposed | Laser the eye (HP 60, then 80) during the pause, then Defib before the clock ends. Between arrests: inject 3 sites. Finally Forceps | One held organ chord |\\n| **Coda** | *coda (n.): the tail. The part that ends everything.* | Coda sign (circle and cross) as a core, two long baton arms on Rapier chains, a tailcoat membrane | **Beat 1 Downbeat:** ring telegraphs one beat early; the baton slams, -6 vitals and a scratch, unless you Laser the baton 0.5 s during the wind-up. **Beat 3 Cue:** spawns 2 notes or a small Adagio. **Every 4th bar a rest:** the core opens for 2 beats, Laser ×3. At 66% and 33% of HP 300 it moves to another site and its arms regrow; sever the arms to reach it. At 0: long Forceps pull (embed 0.6) | All of it | All the motifs in counterpoint, with the Dies Irae (§11) on organ |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Operations\\n\\n260→About 40 to 55 minutes in total. Timers are for Normal. **Every operation also has a chart:** patient name, age, job, one personal gag, and a one-line follow-up shown on the report. Phases are data (§15.3).\\n\\n### Op 1: Broken Glass (Chapter 1, Ren). Forearm. Timer 4:00, 72 bpm\\n*Desmond Pell, 52, taxi driver. \\\"Has never once used a turn signal.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Discharged Tuesday. Was seen signaling, once, leaving the car park.\\\"*\\nTeaches: tip, wheel, Gel, Forceps, Suction, Syringe, Scanner, Suture.\\n1. **Clean:** one gel zone (1.2 × 0.5).\\n2. **Pull the glass:** 4 shards (embed 0.18 to 0.3). Each pull leaves a small pool (volume 0.4). Done when shards are on the tray and pools are drained.\\n3. **Vitals dip:** scripted -25. Bea teaches the Syringe. Can't fail here.\\n4. **The missing shard:** Bea: \\\"Count them, child.\\\" Scanner finds a deep shard. Forceps it.\\n5. **Stitch:** two lacerations (6 and 8 gates).\\n270→6. **Finish:** gel zone over the stitches.\\n\\n### Op 2: Growth Spurt (Chapter 1, Ren). Abdomen skin, then bowel. Timer 5:30, 76 bpm\\n*Hana Ito, 38, crane operator. \\\"Lifts forty tons for a living. Fainted at the consent form.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Back on the cranes. Asks after you. Has asked you to stop visiting.\\\"*\\nTeaches: Scalpel, Clamp, Laser, sever, the Hush.\\n1. **Open:** gel zone, one long incision (1.4 fu). Ink wipe to the bowel site.\\n2. **Bleed:** 2 bleeders and rising pools. Clamp and Suction.\\n3. **Nodules:** 5 (HP 30), one hidden. Laser, Scanner.\\n4. **The tumor:** sever 3 tethers. Forceps it out (embed 0.4) and carry it to the tray.\\n5. **The crash:** the tumor twitches on the tray. Vitals forced to 35, drain 3/s, a rupture wound (12 gates) opens, Composure is set to 100. Bea screams. The Hush prompt appears. The moment it fires: silence, ink wash, the first time. Suture the rupture.\\n280→6. **Close:** take clamps off, close incision (10 gates), gel.\\n\\n### Op 3: Adagio (Chapter 2, Ren). Liver. Timer 5:30, 80 bpm\\n*Theodora Lund, 61, cellist, Harbor Orchestra. \\\"Refuses anesthesia until she has finished a sentence about Brahms.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Performed in April. Dedicated the slow movement to 'the nervous one.'\\\"*\\n1. **Open:** gel, short incision.\\n2. **Look closer:** Scanner sweep reveals stave lines and 3 nests. Adagio emerges, with strain card.\\n3. **Adagio:** Laser it down, Forceps it out.\\n4. **Eggs:** 4 hidden (Scanner, Laser HP 20) hatching at bar 16 into small Adagios.\\n5. **Adagio Grande:** HP 150, two tails, opens bleeders. Clamp them.\\n6. **Close:** clamps off, suture 2 lesions, gel.\\n290→\\n### Op 4: Staccato (Chapter 2, Ren). Bowel, then stomach. Timer 6:00, 84 bpm\\n*Ruben Castellano, 47, ferry captain. \\\"Has not missed a crossing in nineteen years. Is asking whether this will take long.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Missed two crossings. Sent flowers to the ferry.\\\"*\\n1. **Open:** gel, incision.\\n2. **Wave 1:** 8 notes from 3 open holes.\\n3. **Find the nests:** Scanner, 4 hidden holes. Seal them.\\n4. **Waves 2 and 3:** 12 and 16 notes, faster.\\n5. **Tremolo:** first appears here. Bea: \\\"Slow hands, child.\\\" Three pins.\\n6. **Close:** suture, gel.\\n\\n300→### Op 5: Legato (Chapter 3, **Ines**). Brain. Timer 6:00, 70 bpm. Consult\\n*Nadia Bloom, 29, school music teacher. \\\"Her class has sent a card signed 'Please do not miss.'\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Back with Class 4. They have sent a second card.\\\"*\\nTeaches: Sforzando, the Consult. Scalpel tolerance ×0.75 throughout: this is a brain.\\n1. **Consult,** then **membrane:** two precise arcs.\\n2. **Legato:** 12 links, tail first. Forceps each piece away.\\n3. **Thrash:** at link 6 it speeds up. Composure set to 100. Ines: \\\"Now you will see how I work.\\\" Sforzando prompt.\\n4. **Second chain:** 8 links with two tails.\\n5. **Repair:** suture the vessel (tight gates), clamps off, gel.\\n\\n### Op 6: Fermata (Chapter 3, Ren, with Ines on comms). Heart. Timer 7:00, 88 bpm. Consult\\n310→*Dr. Augustin Bell, 66, Chief of Surgery. \\\"Has told every surgeon in this hospital to quit smoking. Smokes.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Under arrest. Recovering. Has quit.\\\"*\\n1. **Consult,** then **open:** long incision, gel.\\n2. **Crescendo:** feeders, Fortissimo threat, cut out the ring.\\n3. **First arrest:** the eye opens, silence. Defib tutorial, no Laser needed.\\n4. **Antidote:** 3 injection sites, plus bleeders.\\n5. **Second arrest:** Laser the eye (HP 60), then Defib.\\n6. **Third arrest:** Laser the eye (HP 80), Defib, then Forceps the eye out.\\n7. **Close:** clamps off, suture, gel.\\n\\n### Op 7: Coda (Chapter 4, Ren and Ines). Heart, lung, aorta. Timer 9:30, 92 bpm. Consult\\n320→*Beatrice Okonkwo, 58, Head Nurse. The chart is in her own handwriting: \\\"Do not be dramatic about this.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Discharged herself. Is back in OR 3. Has opinions.\\\"*\\nBea is unconscious, so **Pip reads her notebook aloud** as the in-operation voice. This is the emotional core: every bark is her words in someone else's voice (\\\"'Suction before you can't see.' She underlined that twice.\\\").\\n1. **Exposition (heart):** Adagio and Staccato together.\\n2. **Development (lung, breathing field):** Tremolo and a Legato chain. Bleeders open back at the heart: site-switch alarm, teaching L1/R1.\\n3. **Recapitulation (aorta):** Crescendo, then a Fermata arrest. Every monitor in the hospital audibly falls into time with hers.\\n4. **Coda (moves across all three sites):** the Conductor (§5).\\n5. **Closing:** wounds on all three sites, clamps off.\\n6. **The last stop:** her heart stops, no warning and no hint. Composure refills, and the gift is Ren's Hush whoever was leading. Total silence, one Defib. Then her ECG, alone, and the music returns on the downbeat.\\n\\n### Last Patient (Chapter 4 ending, Ren). Heart. No HUD, no timer, can't fail\\n330→*Dr. Cordelia Voss, 71. Chart: \\\"Deceased,\\\" with a date 17 years ago, crossed out by Ren.*\\nForty seconds. Rain. One clamp, one Defib. Report: no rank, only: \\\"Tonight's patient survived.\\\"\\n\\n### Grand Rounds (co-op, Free Play and hub rounds). Liver, bowel, heart. Timer 5:00\\n*Ngaio Reeve, 55, harbor master. \\\"Ward Zero has only this to say: everyone scrub in.\\\"*\\nEach movement overlaps the last, so a team can split up. Counts scale by `1 + 0.5 × (players - 1)`, strain HP by `1 + 0.25 × (players - 1)`.\\n1. **0:00, Open up:** 2 incisions (liver), 4 shards (bowel), gel zones, 2 bleeders.\\n2. **1:00, Adagio and Staccato:** Adagio on the liver, a nest on the bowel.\\n3. **2:15, Legato and Crescendo:** a chain on the bowel, a ring on the heart.\\n4. **3:30, Fermata:** one arrest. **Any one surgeon's shock counts**; simultaneous shocks earn a bonus. Injection sites at every site.\\n340→5. **4:15, Close:** wounds everywhere. Done before the timer: win.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Story\\n\\nDelivered as short scenes on a 3D stage (§9.5). Cross, Enter, Space or a click advances; hold to fast-forward; Triangle or Tab skips the scene, with a prompt on screen. Write 250 to 350 lines in total, in `src/data/story/`. The beats and must-have lines below are fixed; the rest is yours. Chapter names: **Scrub In**, **First Movement**, **Dissent**, **Coda**.\\n\\n| # | When | Where | Beats and must-have lines |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n350→| S0 | New game | OR 3 at night, empty | An envelope slides under the door. The monitor switches itself on and beeps, in time, with no patient. A silhouette lifts a baton. Title sting. 20 s |\\n| S1 | Before Op 1 | Corridor, OR 3 | Flood traffic has stranded the attending. Ren is all there is. \\\"Thirty-one years in this room, child…\\\" \\\"Then simulate faster.\\\" |\\n| S2 | After Op 1 | Bell's office | Bell's praise and warning: \\\"the best hands… the worst nerves.\\\" |\\n| S3 | Before Op 2 | OR 3 gallery | The board watches. Routine tumor. Ren throws up, apologizes to the bucket |\\n| S4 | After Op 2 | OR 3, tray | Ren: \\\"Everything went quiet.\\\" Bea goes very still: \\\"I have heard of that once.\\\" The tumor twitches on the tray. In rhythm. Sting: \\\"Tumors do not keep time, child.\\\" |\\n| S5 | Before Op 3 | Pip's pathology lab | Envelope: sheet music addressed to \\\"The Surgeon on Call\\\". Pip plays it on a keyboard: \\\"It's a heartbeat…\\\" Ambulance: a cellist |\\n| S6 | After Op 3 | Ward Zero | Sorrento: \\\"Please wash your hands.\\\" REQUIEM, spelled out in full, with a straight face. The Conservatory. Ren is drafted |\\n| S7 | Before Op 4 | Ambulance bay, rain | Second score. A ferry captain |\\n| S8 | After Op 4 | OR 3 | The OR phone rings. A breathy voice: \\\"Bravo, Doctor. You play by ear. How delightful.\\\" Bea drops a full instrument tray. Sting |\\n| S9 | Before Op 5 | Ward Zero, then OR 3 | Ines arrives under guard. \\\"Your hands are excellent. Your diagnosis is a eulogy.\\\" She operates; you play her. First Consult |\\n360→| S10 | After Op 5 | Hospital roof, rain | Ines explains: she studied under the Maestro, who had the Hush. \\\"At the end, Doctor, you cannot turn it off.\\\" \\\"He waits for the silence. I do not wait.\\\" |\\n| S11 | Before Op 6 | Boardroom | Bell collapses mid-aphorism. The envelope's dedication: \\\"For Augustin, who signed.\\\" Consult |\\n| S12 | After Op 6 | Recovery room | Bell confesses: he signed Voss's death certificate after the Ward Zero fire, knowing she lived, and funded St. Alder with her research. \\\"Every heart I mended in this building, I mended with her money.\\\" Bea: \\\"I handed her the knife for eleven years. I would know that silence anywhere.\\\" |\\n| S13 | Before Op 7 | OR 3 | Final envelope. Pip plays it and slows down: \\\"I know this rhythm. It has a murmur. Ms. Okonkwo, you've got a—\\\" Bea, turning, mid-sentence: \\\"Forceps, ch—\\\" She falls. Ines: \\\"You cannot operate. You love her.\\\" Ren: \\\"Then you had better hand me the instruments.\\\" Pip, shaking, picks up the notebook. Consult |\\n| S14 | After Op 7 | Recovery, dawn | Bea wakes. Long silence. \\\"You held the forceps wrong, child.\\\" |\\n| S15 | Then | OR 3 gallery | Voss, conducting behind the glass, falters: her own heart is the first host. Sorrento: \\\"Let her go, Doctor.\\\" Ren: \\\"She's a patient.\\\" Leads into Last Patient |\\n| S16 | After | St. Alder, morning | Patients' cameos. Pip in student-nurse scrubs. Bea, with a cane, watches Ren close a wound and, for the only time in the game: **\\\"Good hands, child.\\\"** Credits roll over attract footage. Post-credits: a new envelope, marked *Opus 2* |\\n\\n**Bea's barks.** Write 60 or so short in-operation lines keyed by event, each with an expression: `start, nextPhase, toolHint(tool), idle, vitalsLow, vitalsCritical, miss, streak, bleeding, overflow, clampReminder, strainIntro(strain), hushReady, timerLow, success, fail`. A taste:\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"250→| **Tremolo** | *tremolo (n.): a rapid, nervous trembling. Yours, specifically.* | Pale moth with stave-striped wings, always shivering | Flees at 0.9 fu/s if the tip is within 0.6 fu moving faster than 0.45 fu/s. Scratches 1.5 vitals/s while fleeing. Freezes if you approach slowly | Steady in, Scanner 1 s to pin (3 s), Laser 40 HP. Three pins | Fast high strings |\\n| **Legato** | *legato (adj.): smoothly connected, without a break. It does not want a break.* | Bead chain joined by curved slur ribbons, on Rapier rope joints, head pinned | Must be cut **tail first**; the active link glows. Wrong link: two links re-heal, vitals -4. Cut pieces reattach after 8 beats unless carried to the tray. Every 8 beats it jerks and opens a bleeder | Scalpel sever, then Forceps to tray | Gliding portamento lead |\\n| **Crescendo** | *crescendo (n.): gradually getting louder. She is about to get very loud.* | A hairpin \\\"<\\\" wedge wrapped into a ring that widens | Size grows by `0.02 + 0.015 × live feeders` per second, from 0.2 to 1. Drain `1 + 6 × size` vitals/s. Four feeders (HP 40) regrow every 16 beats. At size 1: **Fortissimo**: -20 vitals, 2 bleeders, size resets to 0.6 | Kill all feeders: the ring shrinks and shows a circular cut line. Scalpel the circle, Forceps it out | One new voice every bar |\\n| **Fermata** | *fermata (n.): hold. Hold until the conductor releases you. The conductor is not coming.* | The fermata sign as a giant eye: an arc and a dot, opening on the heart | Stops the heart: music cuts to silence, ECG flat, 8 s arrest clock, vitals hold at 15. While the heart is stopped the eye is exposed | Laser the eye (HP 60, then 80) during the pause, then Defib before the clock ends. Between arrests: inject 3 sites. Finally Forceps | One held organ chord |\\n| **Coda** | *coda (n.): the tail. The part that ends everything.* | Coda sign (circle and cross) as a core, two long baton arms on Rapier chains, a tailcoat membrane | **Beat 1 Downbeat:** ring telegraphs one beat early; the baton slams, -6 vitals and a scratch, unless you Laser the baton 0.5 s during the wind-up. **Beat 3 Cue:** spawns 2 notes or a small Adagio. **Every 4th bar a rest:** the core opens for 2 beats, Laser ×3. At 66% and 33% of HP 300 it moves to another site and its arms regrow; sever the arms to reach it. At 0: long Forceps pull (embed 0.6) | All of it | All the motifs in counterpoint, with the Dies Irae (§11) on organ |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Operations\\n\\n260→About 40 to 55 minutes in total. Timers are for Normal. **Every operation also has a chart:** patient name, age, job, one personal gag, and a one-line follow-up shown on the report. Phases are data (§15.3).\\n\\n### Op 1: Broken Glass (Chapter 1, Ren). Forearm. Timer 4:00, 72 bpm\\n*Desmond Pell, 52, taxi driver. \\\"Has never once used a turn signal.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Discharged Tuesday. Was seen signaling, once, leaving the car park.\\\"*\\nTeaches: tip, wheel, Gel, Forceps, Suction, Syringe, Scanner, Suture.\\n1. **Clean:** one gel zone (1.2 × 0.5).\\n2. **Pull the glass:** 4 shards (embed 0.18 to 0.3). Each pull leaves a small pool (volume 0.4). Done when shards are on the tray and pools are drained.\\n3. **Vitals dip:** scripted -25. Bea teaches the Syringe. Can't fail here.\\n4. **The missing shard:** Bea: \\\"Count them, child.\\\" Scanner finds a deep shard. Forceps it.\\n5. **Stitch:** two lacerations (6 and 8 gates).\\n270→6. **Finish:** gel zone over the stitches.\\n\\n### Op 2: Growth Spurt (Chapter 1, Ren). Abdomen skin, then bowel. Timer 5:30, 76 bpm\\n*Hana Ito, 38, crane operator. \\\"Lifts forty tons for a living. Fainted at the consent form.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Back on the cranes. Asks after you. Has asked you to stop visiting.\\\"*\\nTeaches: Scalpel, Clamp, Laser, sever, the Hush.\\n1. **Open:** gel zone, one long incision (1.4 fu). Ink wipe to the bowel site.\\n2. **Bleed:** 2 bleeders and rising pools. Clamp and Suction.\\n3. **Nodules:** 5 (HP 30), one hidden. Laser, Scanner.\\n4. **The tumor:** sever 3 tethers. Forceps it out (embed 0.4) and carry it to the tray.\\n5. **The crash:** the tumor twitches on the tray. Vitals forced to 35, drain 3/s, a rupture wound (12 gates) opens, Composure is set to 100. Bea screams. The Hush prompt appears. The moment it fires: silence, ink wash, the first time. Suture the rupture.\\n280→6. **Close:** take clamps off, close incision (10 gates), gel.\\n\\n### Op 3: Adagio (Chapter 2, Ren). Liver. Timer 5:30, 80 bpm\\n*Theodora Lund, 61, cellist, Harbor Orchestra. \\\"Refuses anesthesia until she has finished a sentence about Brahms.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Performed in April. Dedicated the slow movement to 'the nervous one.'\\\"*\\n1. **Open:** gel, short incision.\\n2. **Look closer:** Scanner sweep reveals stave lines and 3 nests. Adagio emerges, with strain card.\\n3. **Adagio:** Laser it down, Forceps it out.\\n4. **Eggs:** 4 hidden (Scanner, Laser HP 20) hatching at bar 16 into small Adagios.\\n5. **Adagio Grande:** HP 150, two tails, opens bleeders. Clamp them.\\n6. **Close:** clamps off, suture 2 lesions, gel.\\n290→\\n### Op 4: Staccato (Chapter 2, Ren). Bowel, then stomach. Timer 6:00, 84 bpm\\n*Ruben Castellano, 47, ferry captain. \\\"Has not missed a crossing in nineteen years. Is asking whether this will take long.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Missed two crossings. Sent flowers to the ferry.\\\"*\\n1. **Open:** gel, incision.\\n2. **Wave 1:** 8 notes from 3 open holes.\\n3. **Find the nests:** Scanner, 4 hidden holes. Seal them.\\n4. **Waves 2 and 3:** 12 and 16 notes, faster.\\n5. **Tremolo:** first appears here. Bea: \\\"Slow hands, child.\\\" Three pins.\\n6. **Close:** suture, gel.\\n\\n300→### Op 5: Legato (Chapter 3, **Ines**). Brain. Timer 6:00, 70 bpm. Consult\\n*Nadia Bloom, 29, school music teacher. \\\"Her class has sent a card signed 'Please do not miss.'\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Back with Class 4. They have sent a second card.\\\"*\\nTeaches: Sforzando, the Consult. Scalpel tolerance ×0.75 throughout: this is a brain.\\n1. **Consult,** then **membrane:** two precise arcs.\\n2. **Legato:** 12 links, tail first. Forceps each piece away.\\n3. **Thrash:** at link 6 it speeds up. Composure set to 100. Ines: \\\"Now you will see how I work.\\\" Sforzando prompt.\\n4. **Second chain:** 8 links with two tails.\\n5. **Repair:** suture the vessel (tight gates), clamps off, gel.\\n\\n### Op 6: Fermata (Chapter 3, Ren, with Ines on comms). Heart. Timer 7:00, 88 bpm. Consult\\n310→*Dr. Augustin Bell, 66, Chief of Surgery. \\\"Has told every surgeon in this hospital to quit smoking. Smokes.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Under arrest. Recovering. Has quit.\\\"*\\n1. **Consult,** then **open:** long incision, gel.\\n2. **Crescendo:** feeders, Fortissimo threat, cut out the ring.\\n3. **First arrest:** the eye opens, silence. Defib tutorial, no Laser needed.\\n4. **Antidote:** 3 injection sites, plus bleeders.\\n5. **Second arrest:** Laser the eye (HP 60), then Defib.\\n6. **Third arrest:** Laser the eye (HP 80), Defib, then Forceps the eye out.\\n7. **Close:** clamps off, suture, gel.\\n\\n### Op 7: Coda (Chapter 4, Ren and Ines). Heart, lung, aorta. Timer 9:30, 92 bpm. Consult\\n320→*Beatrice Okonkwo, 58, Head Nurse. The chart is in her own handwriting: \\\"Do not be dramatic about this.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Discharged herself. Is back in OR 3. Has opinions.\\\"*\\nBea is unconscious, so **Pip reads her notebook aloud** as the in-operation voice. This is the emotional core: every bark is her words in someone else's voice (\\\"'Suction before you can't see.' She underlined that twice.\\\").\\n1. **Exposition (heart):** Adagio and Staccato together.\\n2. **Development (lung, breathing field):** Tremolo and a Legato chain. Bleeders open back at the heart: site-switch alarm, teaching L1/R1.\\n3. **Recapitulation (aorta):** Crescendo, then a Fermata arrest. Every monitor in the hospital audibly falls into time with hers.\\n4. **Coda (moves across all three sites):** the Conductor (§5).\\n5. **Closing:** wounds on all three sites, clamps off.\\n6. **The last stop:** her heart stops, no warning and no hint. Composure refills, and the gift is Ren's Hush whoever was leading. Total silence, one Defib. Then her ECG, alone, and the music returns on the downbeat.\\n\\n### Last Patient (Chapter 4 ending, Ren). Heart. No HUD, no timer, can't fail\\n330→*Dr. Cordelia Voss, 71. Chart: \\\"Deceased,\\\" with a date 17 years ago, crossed out by Ren.*\\nForty seconds. Rain. One clamp, one Defib. Report: no rank, only: \\\"Tonight's patient survived.\\\"\\n\\n### Grand Rounds (co-op, Free Play and hub rounds). Liver, bowel, heart. Timer 5:00\\n*Ngaio Reeve, 55, harbor master. \\\"Ward Zero has only this to say: everyone scrub in.\\\"*\\nEach movement overlaps the last, so a team can split up. Counts scale by `1 + 0.5 × (players - 1)`, strain HP by `1 + 0.25 × (players - 1)`.\\n1. **0:00, Open up:** 2 incisions (liver), 4 shards (bowel), gel zones, 2 bleeders.\\n2. **1:00, Adagio and Staccato:** Adagio on the liver, a nest on the bowel.\\n3. **2:15, Legato and Crescendo:** a chain on the bowel, a ring on the heart.\\n4. **3:30, Fermata:** one arrest. **Any one surgeon's shock counts**; simultaneous shocks earn a bonus. Injection sites at every site.\\n340→5. **4:15, Close:** wounds everywhere. Done before the timer: win.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Story\\n\\nDelivered as short scenes on a 3D stage (§9.5). Cross, Enter, Space or a click advances; hold to fast-forward; Triangle or Tab skips the scene, with a prompt on screen. Write 250 to 350 lines in total, in `src/data/story/`. The beats and must-have lines below are fixed; the rest is yours. Chapter names: **Scrub In**, **First Movement**, **Dissent**, **Coda**.\\n\\n| # | When | Where | Beats and must-have lines |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n350→| S0 | New game | OR 3 at night, empty | An envelope slides under the door. The monitor switches itself on and beeps, in time, with no patient. A silhouette lifts a baton. Title sting. 20 s |\\n| S1 | Before Op 1 | Corridor, OR 3 | Flood traffic has stranded the attending. Ren is all there is. \\\"Thirty-one years in this room, child…\\\" \\\"Then simulate faster.\\\" |\\n| S2 | After Op 1 | Bell's office | Bell's praise and warning: \\\"the best hands… the worst nerves.\\\" |\\n| S3 | Before Op 2 | OR 3 gallery | The board watches. Routine tumor. Ren throws up, apologizes to the bucket |\\n| S4 | After Op 2 | OR 3, tray | Ren: \\\"Everything went quiet.\\\" Bea goes very still: \\\"I have heard of that once.\\\" The tumor twitches on the tray. In rhythm. Sting: \\\"Tumors do not keep time, child.\\\" |\\n| S5 | Before Op 3 | Pip's pathology lab | Envelope: sheet music addressed to \\\"The Surgeon on Call\\\". Pip plays it on a keyboard: \\\"It's a heartbeat…\\\" Ambulance: a cellist |\\n| S6 | After Op 3 | Ward Zero | Sorrento: \\\"Please wash your hands.\\\" REQUIEM, spelled out in full, with a straight face. The Conservatory. Ren is drafted |\\n| S7 | Before Op 4 | Ambulance bay, rain | Second score. A ferry captain |\\n| S8 | After Op 4 | OR 3 | The OR phone rings. A breathy voice: \\\"Bravo, Doctor. You play by ear. How delightful.\\\" Bea drops a full instrument tray. Sting |\\n| S9 | Before Op 5 | Ward Zero, then OR 3 | Ines arrives under guard. \\\"Your hands are excellent. Your diagnosis is a eulogy.\\\" She operates; you play her. First Consult |\\n360→| S10 | After Op 5 | Hospital roof, rain | Ines explains: she studied under the Maestro, who had the Hush. \\\"At the end, Doctor, you cannot turn it off.\\\" \\\"He waits for the silence. I do not wait.\\\" |\\n| S11 | Before Op 6 | Boardroom | Bell collapses mid-aphorism. The envelope's dedication: \\\"For Augustin, who signed.\\\" Consult |\\n| S12 | After Op 6 | Recovery room | Bell confesses: he signed Voss's death certificate after the Ward Zero fire, knowing she lived, and funded St. Alder with her research. \\\"Every heart I mended in this building, I mended with her money.\\\" Bea: \\\"I handed her the knife for eleven years. I would know that silence anywhere.\\\" |\\n| S13 | Before Op 7 | OR 3 | Final envelope. Pip plays it and slows down: \\\"I know this rhythm. It has a murmur. Ms. Okonkwo, you've got a—\\\" Bea, turning, mid-sentence: \\\"Forceps, ch—\\\" She falls. Ines: \\\"You cannot operate. You love her.\\\" Ren: \\\"Then you had better hand me the instruments.\\\" Pip, shaking, picks up the notebook. Consult |\\n| S14 | After Op 7 | Recovery, dawn | Bea wakes. Long silence. \\\"You held the forceps wrong, child.\\\" |\\n| S15 | Then | OR 3 gallery | Voss, conducting behind the glass, falters: her own heart is the first host. Sorrento: \\\"Let her go, Doctor.\\\" Ren: \\\"She's a patient.\\\" Leads into Last Patient |\\n| S16 | After | St. Alder, morning | Patients' cameos. Pip in student-nurse scrubs. Bea, with a cane, watches Ren close a wound and, for the only time in the game: **\\\"Good hands, child.\\\"** Credits roll over attract footage. Post-credits: a new envelope, marked *Opus 2* |\\n\\n**Bea's barks.** Write 60 or so short in-operation lines keyed by event, each with an expression: `start, nextPhase, toolHint(tool), idle, vitalsLow, vitalsCritical, miss, streak, bleeding, overflow, clampReminder, strainIntro(strain), hushReady, timerLow, success, fail`. A taste:\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":250,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"| **Tremolo** | *tremolo (n.): a rapid, nervous trembling. Yours, specifically.* | Pale moth with stave-striped wings, always shivering | Flees at 0.9 fu/s if the tip is within 0.6 fu moving faster than 0.45 fu/s. Scratches 1.5 vitals/s while fleeing. Freezes if you approach slowly | Steady in, Scanner 1 s to pin (3 s), Laser 40 HP. Three pins | Fast high strings |\\n| **Legato** | *legato (adj.): smoothly connected, without a break. It does not want a break.* | Bead chain joined by curved slur ribbons, on Rapier rope joints, head pinned | Must be cut **tail first**; the active link glows. Wrong link: two links re-heal, vitals -4. Cut pieces reattach after 8 beats unless carried to the tray. Every 8 beats it jerks and opens a bleeder | Scalpel sever, then Forceps to tray | Gliding portamento lead |\\n| **Crescendo** | *crescendo (n.): gradually getting louder. She is about to get very loud.* | A hairpin \\\"<\\\" wedge wrapped into a ring that widens | Size grows by `0.02 + 0.015 × live feeders` per second, from 0.2 to 1. Drain `1 + 6 × size` vitals/s. Four feeders (HP 40) regrow every 16 beats. At size 1: **Fortissimo**: -20 vitals, 2 bleeders, size resets to 0.6 | Kill all feeders: the ring shrinks and shows a circular cut line. Scalpel the circle, Forceps it out | One new voice every bar |\\n| **Fermata** | *fermata (n.): hold. Hold until the conductor releases you. The conductor is not coming.* | The fermata sign as a giant eye: an arc and a dot, opening on the heart | Stops the heart: music cuts to silence, ECG flat, 8 s arrest clock, vitals hold at 15. While the heart is stopped the eye is exposed | Laser the eye (HP 60, then 80) during the pause, then Defib before the clock ends. Between arrests: inject 3 sites. Finally Forceps | One held organ chord |\\n| **Coda** | *coda (n.): the tail. The part that ends everything.* | Coda sign (circle and cross) as a core, two long baton arms on Rapier chains, a tailcoat membrane | **Beat 1 Downbeat:** ring telegraphs one beat early; the baton slams, -6 vitals and a scratch, unless you Laser the baton 0.5 s during the wind-up. **Beat 3 Cue:** spawns 2 notes or a small Adagio. **Every 4th bar a rest:** the core opens for 2 beats, Laser ×3. At 66% and 33% of HP 300 it moves to another site and its arms regrow; sever the arms to reach it. At 0: long Forceps pull (embed 0.6) | All of it | All the motifs in counterpoint, with the Dies Irae (§11) on organ |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Operations\\n\\nAbout 40 to 55 minutes in total. Timers are for Normal. **Every operation also has a chart:** patient name, age, job, one personal gag, and a one-line follow-up shown on the report. Phases are data (§15.3).\\n\\n### Op 1: Broken Glass (Chapter 1, Ren). Forearm. Timer 4:00, 72 bpm\\n*Desmond Pell, 52, taxi driver. \\\"Has never once used a turn signal.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Discharged Tuesday. Was seen signaling, once, leaving the car park.\\\"*\\nTeaches: tip, wheel, Gel, Forceps, Suction, Syringe, Scanner, Suture.\\n1. **Clean:** one gel zone (1.2 × 0.5).\\n2. **Pull the glass:** 4 shards (embed 0.18 to 0.3). Each pull leaves a small pool (volume 0.4). Done when shards are on the tray and pools are drained.\\n3. **Vitals dip:** scripted -25. Bea teaches the Syringe. Can't fail here.\\n4. **The missing shard:** Bea: \\\"Count them, child.\\\" Scanner finds a deep shard. Forceps it.\\n5. **Stitch:** two lacerations (6 and 8 gates).\\n6. **Finish:** gel zone over the stitches.\\n\\n### Op 2: Growth Spurt (Chapter 1, Ren). Abdomen skin, then bowel. Timer 5:30, 76 bpm\\n*Hana Ito, 38, crane operator. \\\"Lifts forty tons for a living. Fainted at the consent form.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Back on the cranes. Asks after you. Has asked you to stop visiting.\\\"*\\nTeaches: Scalpel, Clamp, Laser, sever, the Hush.\\n1. **Open:** gel zone, one long incision (1.4 fu). Ink wipe to the bowel site.\\n2. **Bleed:** 2 bleeders and rising pools. Clamp and Suction.\\n3. **Nodules:** 5 (HP 30), one hidden. Laser, Scanner.\\n4. **The tumor:** sever 3 tethers. Forceps it out (embed 0.4) and carry it to the tray.\\n5. **The crash:** the tumor twitches on the tray. Vitals forced to 35, drain 3/s, a rupture wound (12 gates) opens, Composure is set to 100. Bea screams. The Hush prompt appears. The moment it fires: silence, ink wash, the first time. Suture the rupture.\\n6. **Close:** take clamps off, close incision (10 gates), gel.\\n\\n### Op 3: Adagio (Chapter 2, Ren). Liver. Timer 5:30, 80 bpm\\n*Theodora Lund, 61, cellist, Harbor Orchestra. \\\"Refuses anesthesia until she has finished a sentence about Brahms.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Performed in April. Dedicated the slow movement to 'the nervous one.'\\\"*\\n1. **Open:** gel, short incision.\\n2. **Look closer:** Scanner sweep reveals stave lines and 3 nests. Adagio emerges, with strain card.\\n3. **Adagio:** Laser it down, Forceps it out.\\n4. **Eggs:** 4 hidden (Scanner, Laser HP 20) hatching at bar 16 into small Adagios.\\n5. **Adagio Grande:** HP 150, two tails, opens bleeders. Clamp them.\\n6. **Close:** clamps off, suture 2 lesions, gel.\\n\\n### Op 4: Staccato (Chapter 2, Ren). Bowel, then stomach. Timer 6:00, 84 bpm\\n*Ruben Castellano, 47, ferry captain. \\\"Has not missed a crossing in nineteen years. Is asking whether this will take long.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Missed two crossings. Sent flowers to the ferry.\\\"*\\n1. **Open:** gel, incision.\\n2. **Wave 1:** 8 notes from 3 open holes.\\n3. **Find the nests:** Scanner, 4 hidden holes. Seal them.\\n4. **Waves 2 and 3:** 12 and 16 notes, faster.\\n5. **Tremolo:** first appears here. Bea: \\\"Slow hands, child.\\\" Three pins.\\n6. **Close:** suture, gel.\\n\\n### Op 5: Legato (Chapter 3, **Ines**). Brain. Timer 6:00, 70 bpm. Consult\\n*Nadia Bloom, 29, school music teacher. \\\"Her class has sent a card signed 'Please do not miss.'\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Back with Class 4. They have sent a second card.\\\"*\\nTeaches: Sforzando, the Consult. Scalpel tolerance ×0.75 throughout: this is a brain.\\n1. **Consult,** then **membrane:** two precise arcs.\\n2. **Legato:** 12 links, tail first. Forceps each piece away.\\n3. **Thrash:** at link 6 it speeds up. Composure set to 100. Ines: \\\"Now you will see how I work.\\\" Sforzando prompt.\\n4. **Second chain:** 8 links with two tails.\\n5. **Repair:** suture the vessel (tight gates), clamps off, gel.\\n\\n### Op 6: Fermata (Chapter 3, Ren, with Ines on comms). Heart. Timer 7:00, 88 bpm. Consult\\n*Dr. Augustin Bell, 66, Chief of Surgery. \\\"Has told every surgeon in this hospital to quit smoking. Smokes.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Under arrest. Recovering. Has quit.\\\"*\\n1. **Consult,** then **open:** long incision, gel.\\n2. **Crescendo:** feeders, Fortissimo threat, cut out the ring.\\n3. **First arrest:** the eye opens, silence. Defib tutorial, no Laser needed.\\n4. **Antidote:** 3 injection sites, plus bleeders.\\n5. **Second arrest:** Laser the eye (HP 60), then Defib.\\n6. **Third arrest:** Laser the eye (HP 80), Defib, then Forceps the eye out.\\n7. **Close:** clamps off, suture, gel.\\n\\n### Op 7: Coda (Chapter 4, Ren and Ines). Heart, lung, aorta. Timer 9:30, 92 bpm. Consult\\n*Beatrice Okonkwo, 58, Head Nurse. The chart is in her own handwriting: \\\"Do not be dramatic about this.\\\" Follow-up: \\\"Discharged herself. Is back in OR 3. Has opinions.\\\"*\\nBea is unconscious, so **Pip reads her notebook aloud** as the in-operation voice. This is the emotional core: every bark is her words in someone else's voice (\\\"'Suction before you can't see.' She underlined that twice.\\\").\\n1. **Exposition (heart):** Adagio and Staccato together.\\n2. **Development (lung, breathing field):** Tremolo and a Legato chain. Bleeders open back at the heart: site-switch alarm, teaching L1/R1.\\n3. **Recapitulation (aorta):** Crescendo, then a Fermata arrest. Every monitor in the hospital audibly falls into time with hers.\\n4. **Coda (moves across all three sites):** the Conductor (§5).\\n5. **Closing:** wounds on all three sites, clamps off.\\n6. **The last stop:** her heart stops, no warning and no hint. Composure refills, and the gift is Ren's Hush whoever was leading. Total silence, one Defib. Then her ECG, alone, and the music returns on the downbeat.\\n\\n### Last Patient (Chapter 4 ending, Ren). Heart. No HUD, no timer, can't fail\\n*Dr. Cordelia Voss, 71. Chart: \\\"Deceased,\\\" with a date 17 years ago, crossed out by Ren.*\\nForty seconds. Rain. One clamp, one Defib. Report: no rank, only: \\\"Tonight's patient survived.\\\"\\n\\n### Grand Rounds (co-op, Free Play and hub rounds). Liver, bowel, heart. Timer 5:00\\n*Ngaio Reeve, 55, harbor master. \\\"Ward Zero has only this to say: everyone scrub in.\\\"*\\nEach movement overlaps the last, so a team can split up. Counts scale by `1 + 0.5 × (players - 1)`, strain HP by `1 + 0.25 × (players - 1)`.\\n1. **0:00, Open up:** 2 incisions (liver), 4 shards (bowel), gel zones, 2 bleeders.\\n2. **1:00, Adagio and Staccato:** Adagio on the liver, a nest on the bowel.\\n3. **2:15, Legato and Crescendo:** a chain on the bowel, a ring on the heart.\\n4. **3:30, Fermata:** one arrest. **Any one surgeon's shock counts**; simultaneous shocks earn a bonus. Injection sites at every site.\\n5. **4:15, Close:** wounds everywhere. Done before the timer: win.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Story\\n\\nDelivered as short scenes on a 3D stage (§9.5). Cross, Enter, Space or a click advances; hold to fast-forward; Triangle or Tab skips the scene, with a prompt on screen. Write 250 to 350 lines in total, in `src/data/story/`. The beats and must-have lines below are fixed; the rest is yours. Chapter names: **Scrub In**, **First Movement**, **Dissent**, **Coda**.\\n\\n| # | When | Where | Beats and must-have lines |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| S0 | New game | OR 3 at night, empty | An envelope slides under the door. The monitor switches itself on and beeps, in time, with no patient. A silhouette lifts a baton. Title sting. 20 s |\\n| S1 | Before Op 1 | Corridor, OR 3 | Flood traffic has stranded the attending. Ren is all there is. \\\"Thirty-one years in this room, child…\\\" \\\"Then simulate faster.\\\" |\\n| S2 | After Op 1 | Bell's office | Bell's praise and warning: \\\"the best hands… the worst nerves.\\\" |\\n| S3 | Before Op 2 | OR 3 gallery | The board watches. Routine tumor. Ren throws up, apologizes to the bucket |\\n| S4 | After Op 2 | OR 3, tray | Ren: \\\"Everything went quiet.\\\" Bea goes very still: \\\"I have heard of that once.\\\" The tumor twitches on the tray. In rhythm. Sting: \\\"Tumors do not keep time, child.\\\" |\\n| S5 | Before Op 3 | Pip's pathology lab | Envelope: sheet music addressed to \\\"The Surgeon on Call\\\". Pip plays it on a keyboard: \\\"It's a heartbeat…\\\" Ambulance: a cellist |\\n| S6 | After Op 3 | Ward Zero | Sorrento: \\\"Please wash your hands.\\\" REQUIEM, spelled out in full, with a straight face. The Conservatory. Ren is drafted |\\n| S7 | Before Op 4 | Ambulance bay, rain | Second score. A ferry captain |\\n| S8 | After Op 4 | OR 3 | The OR phone rings. A breathy voice: \\\"Bravo, Doctor. You play by ear. How delightful.\\\" Bea drops a full instrument tray. Sting |\\n| S9 | Before Op 5 | Ward Zero, then OR 3 | Ines arrives under guard. \\\"Your hands are excellent. Your diagnosis is a eulogy.\\\" She operates; you play her. First Consult |\\n| S10 | After Op 5 | Hospital roof, rain | Ines explains: she studied under the Maestro, who had the Hush. \\\"At the end, Doctor, you cannot turn it off.\\\" \\\"He waits for the silence. I do not wait.\\\" |\\n| S11 | Before Op 6 | Boardroom | Bell collapses mid-aphorism. The envelope's dedication: \\\"For Augustin, who signed.\\\" Consult |\\n| S12 | After Op 6 | Recovery room | Bell confesses: he signed Voss's death certificate after the Ward Zero fire, knowing she lived, and funded St. Alder with her research. \\\"Every heart I mended in this building, I mended with her money.\\\" Bea: \\\"I handed her the knife for eleven years. I would know that silence anywhere.\\\" |\\n| S13 | Before Op 7 | OR 3 | Final envelope. Pip plays it and slows down: \\\"I know this rhythm. It has a murmur. Ms. Okonkwo, you've got a—\\\" Bea, turning, mid-sentence: \\\"Forceps, ch—\\\" She falls. Ines: \\\"You cannot operate. You love her.\\\" Ren: \\\"Then you had better hand me the instruments.\\\" Pip, shaking, picks up the notebook. Consult |\\n| S14 | After Op 7 | Recovery, dawn | Bea wakes. Long silence. \\\"You held the forceps wrong, child.\\\" |\\n| S15 | Then | OR 3 gallery | Voss, conducting behind the glass, falters: her own heart is the first host. Sorrento: \\\"Let her go, Doctor.\\\" Ren: \\\"She's a patient.\\\" Leads into Last Patient |\\n| S16 | After | St. Alder, morning | Patients' cameos. Pip in student-nurse scrubs. Bea, with a cane, watches Ren close a wound and, for the only time in the game: **\\\"Good hands, child.\\\"** Credits roll over attract footage. Post-credits: a new envelope, marked *Opus 2* |\\n\\n**Bea's barks.** Write 60 or so short in-operation lines keyed by event, each with an expression: `start, nextPhase, toolHint(tool), idle, vitalsLow, vitalsCritical, miss, streak, bleeding, overflow, clampReminder, strainIntro(strain), hushReady, timerLow, success, fail`. A taste:\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1218}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c19057f4-1f78-446b-add4-bddf7f71ab59-25","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,53,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,47,80,76,65,78,46,109,100,10,49,53,50,58,70,105,110,97,108,32,114,97,110,107,32,99,111,109,112,97,114,101,115,32,116,104,101,32,115,99,111,114,101,32,119,105,116,104,32,116,104,101,32,111,112,101,114,97,116,105,111,110,39,115,32,96,112,97,114,83,99,111,114,101,96,32,40,100,97,116,97,44,32,115,101,116,32,102,114,111,109,32,116,104,101,32,98,111,116,32,105,110,32,194,167,49,55,41,58,10,49,53,55,58,124,32,65,32,124,32,97,116,32,108,101,97,115,116,32,55,53,37,32,124,32,65,116,116,101,110,100,105,110,103,32,124,10,56,52,50,58,32,32,116,105,109,101,114,58,32,50,52,48,44,32,98,112,109,58,32,55,50,44,32,112,97,114,83,99,111,114,101,58,32,54,48,48,48,44,32,109,117,115,105,99,58,32,39,111,114,45