{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_151","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plan specifies distinct phases.\n\nExtra phases or gel zones would violate the spec. The calibration knob is tuning data within existing operations. The bot is too fast and its content does not fill 45% of the timer. The summary forbids lowering PLAN timers, using minTime, or globally slowing the bot. Safe gel or suture should be added inside existing close or gel phases.\n\nThe default gel zone is roughly 26 seconds. The clean phase specifies 1.2 × 0.5, but the current gel() is 1.8 × 0.92. Those dimensions are already oversized versus the plan text. The existing gel zone should be enlarged to match the specified proportions rather than adding extra gel or suture.\n\nstepGel paints non-overlapping gel zones sequentially along one path. The total time per phase is therefore the sum of those paths, capped at roughly 30 seconds. To reach 190 seconds, the bot would need about seven sequential full-field gels.\n\nA layering mechanic could keep the same phase alive by spawning a new gel zone once the previous one is removed. The `on` trigger system already supports this, but chaining them is tricky because `once: true` would not fire again for the same trigger.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-54612983-7b6e-487e-91e0-d283fdfc73ed-26","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"when:|removed|once:|phaseCleared|function fireOn|this\\.on","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4380,"output_tokens":773,"cache_read_input_tokens":68992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"44d385cf-cefa-40c6-9fec-ee4f82b5f708"}
