{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5e4e7cd9-d97d-4ade-ad1d-926dba470d4e-29","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"320→    e.need = e.coreOpen ? 'laser' : (telegraph ? 'laser' : 'wait');\\n    const ratio = e.hp / e.maxHp;\\n    if (!e.moved66 && ratio <= 0.66) {\\n      e.moved66 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    } else if (!e.moved33 && ratio <= 0.33) {\\n      e.moved33 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    }\\n  }\\n330→}\\n\\nfunction moveCoda(sim, e) {\\n  const sites = sim.op.sites.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const i = sites.indexOf(e.site);\\n  e.site = sites[(i + 1) % sites.length];\\n  for (const a of sim.entities) if (a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id) a.alive = false;\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x - 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x + 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.events.push({ type: 'codaMove', site: e.site });\\n340→}\\n\\nfunction stepBleeder(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (e.clamped) {\\n    e.need = 'wait';\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  e.need = 'clamp';\\n  const world = sim.drainScale();\\n  sim.hurt(1 * dt * world, 'bleed');\\n350→  if (!e.pool) {\\n    const pool = sim.spawn({ kind: 'pool', site: e.site, at: [e.x, e.y + 0.05], vol: 0.2, cap: 0.55 });\\n    e.pool = pool.id;\\n  }\\n  const pool = sim.entities.find((p) => p.id === e.pool && p.alive);\\n  if (pool) pool.vol += 0.35 * dt * world;\\n}\\n\\nfunction stepPool(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (e.vol > e.cap) {\\n360→    e.overflowed = true;\\n    e.covers = true;\\n    sim.hurt(0.4 * dt * sim.drainScale(), 'overflow');\\n    for (const g of sim.entities) {\\n      if (g.alive && g.site === e.site && dist(g.x, g.y, e.x, e.y) < 0.2 && g.kind !== 'pool') g.covered = true;\\n    }\\n    if ((sim.overflowBark || 0) <= 0) {\\n      sim.bark('overflow');\\n      sim.overflowBark = 4;\\n    }\",\"content_concise\":\"320→    e.need = e.coreOpen ? 'laser' : (telegraph ? 'laser' : 'wait');\\n    const ratio = e.hp / e.maxHp;\\n    if (!e.moved66 && ratio <= 0.66) {\\n      e.moved66 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    } else if (!e.moved33 && ratio <= 0.33) {\\n      e.moved33 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    }\\n  }\\n330→}\\n\\nfunction moveCoda(sim, e) {\\n  const sites = sim.op.sites.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const i = sites.indexOf(e.site);\\n  e.site = sites[(i + 1) % sites.length];\\n  for (const a of sim.entities) if (a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id) a.alive = false;\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x - 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x + 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.events.push({ type: 'codaMove', site: e.site });\\n340→}\\n\\nfunction stepBleeder(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (e.clamped) {\\n    e.need = 'wait';\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  e.need = 'clamp';\\n  const world = sim.drainScale();\\n  sim.hurt(1 * dt * world, 'bleed');\\n350→  if (!e.pool) {\\n    const pool = sim.spawn({ kind: 'pool', site: e.site, at: [e.x, e.y + 0.05], vol: 0.2, cap: 0.55 });\\n    e.pool = pool.id;\\n  }\\n  const pool = sim.entities.find((p) => p.id === e.pool && p.alive);\\n  if (pool) pool.vol += 0.35 * dt * world;\\n}\\n\\nfunction stepPool(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (e.vol > e.cap) {\\n360→    e.overflowed = true;\\n    e.covers = true;\\n    sim.hurt(0.4 * dt * sim.drainScale(), 'overflow');\\n    for (const g of sim.entities) {\\n      if (g.alive && g.site === e.site && dist(g.x, g.y, e.x, e.y) < 0.2 && g.kind !== 'pool') g.covered = true;\\n    }\\n    if ((sim.overflowBark || 0) <= 0) {\\n      sim.bark('overflow');\\n      sim.overflowBark = 4;\\n    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/strains.js\",\"offset\":320,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    e.need = e.coreOpen ? 'laser' : (telegraph ? 'laser' : 'wait');\\n    const ratio = e.hp / e.maxHp;\\n    if (!e.moved66 && ratio <= 0.66) {\\n      e.moved66 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    } else if (!e.moved33 && ratio <= 0.33) {\\n      e.moved33 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction moveCoda(sim, e) {\\n  const sites = sim.op.sites.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const i = sites.indexOf(e.site);\\n  e.site = sites[(i + 1) % sites.length];\\n  for (const a of sim.entities) if (a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id) a.alive = false;\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x - 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x + 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.events.push({ type: 'codaMove', site: e.site });\\n}\\n\\nfunction stepBleeder(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (e.clamped) {\\n    e.need = 'wait';\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  e.need = 'clamp';\\n  const world = sim.drainScale();\\n  sim.hurt(1 * dt * world, 'bleed');\\n  if (!e.pool) {\\n    const pool = sim.spawn({ kind: 'pool', site: e.site, at: [e.x, e.y + 0.05], vol: 0.2, cap: 0.55 });\\n    e.pool = pool.id;\\n  }\\n  const pool = sim.entities.find((p) => p.id === e.pool && p.alive);\\n  if (pool) pool.vol += 0.35 * dt * world;\\n}\\n\\nfunction stepPool(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (e.vol > e.cap) {\\n    e.overflowed = true;\\n    e.covers = true;\\n    sim.hurt(0.4 * dt * sim.drainScale(), 'overflow');\\n    for (const g of sim.entities) {\\n      if (g.alive && g.site === e.site && dist(g.x, g.y, e.x, e.y) < 0.2 && g.kind !== 'pool') g.covered = true;\\n    }\\n    if ((sim.overflowBark || 0) <= 0) {\\n      sim.bark('overflow');\\n      sim.overflowBark = 4;\\n    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":376}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5e4e7cd9-d97d-4ade-ad1d-926dba470d4e-30","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"540→  hpMult() {\\n    return this.tuning.strainHpMult * this.mods.hp * this.grHp;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Called after an entity is pushed when it needs children. */\\n  afterSpawn(e) {\\n    if (e.kind === 'legato') {\\n      e.links.forEach((l, i) => {\\n        const prev = i === 0 ? { x: l.x, y: l.y + 0.14 } : e.links[i - 1];\\n        this.entities.push({\\n550→          id: this.nextId++, kind: 'link', site: e.site, alive: true,\\n          x: l.x, y: l.y, x1: prev.x, y1: prev.y, x2: l.x, y2: l.y,\\n          index: i, chain: e.id, chainActive: e.active, cut: false, strain: 'legato',\\n        });\\n      });\\n    }\\n    if (e.kind === 'crescendo') {\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n        const child = this.spawn({\\n          kind: 'feeder', site: e.site, parent: e.id,\\n560→          at: [e.x + Math.cos((i / 4) * Math.PI * 2) * 0.28, e.y + Math.sin((i / 4) * Math.PI * 2) * 0.16],\\n          hp: 40,\\n        });\\n        child.parent = e.id;\\n      }\\n      e.armed = true;\\n    }\\n    if (e.kind === 'coda') {\\n      this.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x - 0.28, e.y + 0.05], hp: 9 });\\n      this.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x + 0.28, e.y + 0.05], hp: 9 });\\n570→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  hurt(amount, why) {\\n    if (this.cheats.lockVitals || this.noFail || this.lockFail) return;\\n    if (this.arrest?.holdVitals) {\\n      this.vitals = 15;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    let d = amount * this.tuning.drainMult * this.mods.drain * (this.notes ? 0.7 : 1);\\n580→    const timed = why === 'bleed' || why === 'scratch' || why === 'spore' || why === 'tremolo' || why === 'crescendo' || why === 'overflow';\\n    if (timed) d *= this.drainScale();\\n    if (!d) return;\\n    this.vitals -= d;\\n    if (this.vitals < this.vitalsMin) this.vitalsMin = this.vitals;\\n    if (this.vitals <= 30 && this.vitals > 0) this.bark(this.vitals <= 15 ? 'vitalsCritical' : 'vitalsLow');\\n    if (why === 'bleed' || why === 'overflow') this.bark('bleeding');\\n  }\\n\\n  applyVitalsBounds() {\\n590→    if (!this.arrest?.holdVitals && this.vitals < this.vitalsMin) this.vitalsMin = this.vitals;\\n    if (this.over) return;\\n    if (!this.noFail && !this.lockFail && !this.cheats.lockVitals && this.vitals <= 0) {\\n      this.vitals = 0;\\n      this.fail('vitals');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!this.noFail && !this.lockFail && !this.noTimer && this.timer <= 0) {\\n      this.timer = 0;\\n      this.fail('time');\",\"content_concise\":\"540→  hpMult() {\\n    return this.tuning.strainHpMult * this.mods.hp * this.grHp;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Called after an entity is pushed when it needs children. */\\n  afterSpawn(e) {\\n    if (e.kind === 'legato') {\\n      e.links.forEach((l, i) => {\\n        const prev = i === 0 ? { x: l.x, y: l.y + 0.14 } : e.links[i - 1];\\n        this.entities.push({\\n550→          id: this.nextId++, kind: 'link', site: e.site, alive: true,\\n          x: l.x, y: l.y, x1: prev.x, y1: prev.y, x2: l.x, y2: l.y,\\n          index: i, chain: e.id, chainActive: e.active, cut: false, strain: 'legato',\\n        });\\n      });\\n    }\\n    if (e.kind === 'crescendo') {\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n        const child = this.spawn({\\n          kind: 'feeder', site: e.site, parent: e.id,\\n560→          at: [e.x + Math.cos((i / 4) * Math.PI * 2) * 0.28, e.y + Math.sin((i / 4) * Math.PI * 2) * 0.16],\\n          hp: 40,\\n        });\\n        child.parent = e.id;\\n      }\\n      e.armed = true;\\n    }\\n    if (e.kind === 'coda') {\\n      this.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x - 0.28, e.y + 0.05], hp: 9 });\\n      this.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x + 0.28, e.y + 0.05], hp: 9 });\\n570→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  hurt(amount, why) {\\n    if (this.cheats.lockVitals || this.noFail || this.lockFail) return;\\n    if (this.arrest?.holdVitals) {\\n      this.vitals = 15;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    let d = amount * this.tuning.drainMult * this.mods.drain * (this.notes ? 0.7 : 1);\\n580→    const timed = why === 'bleed' || why === 'scratch' || why === 'spore' || why === 'tremolo' || why === 'crescendo' || why === 'overflow';\\n    if (timed) d *= this.drainScale();\\n    if (!d) return;\\n    this.vitals -= d;\\n    if (this.vitals < this.vitalsMin) this.vitalsMin = this.vitals;\\n    if (this.vitals <= 30 && this.vitals > 0) this.bark(this.vitals <= 15 ? 'vitalsCritical' : 'vitalsLow');\\n    if (why === 'bleed' || why === 'overflow') this.bark('bleeding');\\n  }\\n\\n  applyVitalsBounds() {\\n590→    if (!this.arrest?.holdVitals && this.vitals < this.vitalsMin) this.vitalsMin = this.vitals;\\n    if (this.over) return;\\n    if (!this.noFail && !this.lockFail && !this.cheats.lockVitals && this.vitals <= 0) {\\n      this.vitals = 0;\\n      this.fail('vitals');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!this.noFail && !this.lockFail && !this.noTimer && this.timer <= 0) {\\n      this.timer = 0;\\n      this.fail('time');\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js\",\"offset\":540,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"  hpMult() {\\n    return this.tuning.strainHpMult * this.mods.hp * this.grHp;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Called after an entity is pushed when it needs children. */\\n  afterSpawn(e) {\\n    if (e.kind === 'legato') {\\n      e.links.forEach((l, i) => {\\n        const prev = i === 0 ? { x: l.x, y: l.y + 0.14 } : e.links[i - 1];\\n        this.entities.push({\\n          id: this.nextId++, kind: 'link', site: e.site, alive: true,\\n          x: l.x, y: l.y, x1: prev.x, y1: prev.y, x2: l.x, y2: l.y,\\n          index: i, chain: e.id, chainActive: e.active, cut: false, strain: 'legato',\\n        });\\n      });\\n    }\\n    if (e.kind === 'crescendo') {\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n        const child = this.spawn({\\n          kind: 'feeder', site: e.site, parent: e.id,\\n          at: [e.x + Math.cos((i / 4) * Math.PI * 2) * 0.28, e.y + Math.sin((i / 4) * Math.PI * 2) * 0.16],\\n          hp: 40,\\n        });\\n        child.parent = e.id;\\n      }\\n      e.armed = true;\\n    }\\n    if (e.kind === 'coda') {\\n      this.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x - 0.28, e.y + 0.05], hp: 9 });\\n      this.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x + 0.28, e.y + 0.05], hp: 9 });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  hurt(amount, why) {\\n    if (this.cheats.lockVitals || this.noFail || this.lockFail) return;\\n    if (this.arrest?.holdVitals) {\\n      this.vitals = 15;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    let d = amount * this.tuning.drainMult * this.mods.drain * (this.notes ? 0.7 : 1);\\n    const timed = why === 'bleed' || why === 'scratch' || why === 'spore' || why === 'tremolo' || why === 'crescendo' || why === 'overflow';\\n    if (timed) d *= this.drainScale();\\n    if (!d) return;\\n    this.vitals -= d;\\n    if (this.vitals < this.vitalsMin) this.vitalsMin = this.vitals;\\n    if (this.vitals <= 30 && this.vitals > 0) this.bark(this.vitals <= 15 ? 'vitalsCritical' : 'vitalsLow');\\n    if (why === 'bleed' || why === 'overflow') this.bark('bleeding');\\n  }\\n\\n  applyVitalsBounds() {\\n    if (!this.arrest?.holdVitals && this.vitals < this.vitalsMin) this.vitalsMin = this.vitals;\\n    if (this.over) return;\\n    if (!this.noFail && !this.lockFail && !this.cheats.lockVitals && this.vitals <= 0) {\\n      this.vitals = 0;\\n      this.fail('vitals');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!this.noFail && !this.lockFail && !this.noTimer && this.timer <= 0) {\\n      this.timer = 0;\\n      this.fail('time');\\n\",\"total_lines\":861}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"ac84d87d-124f-425a-9809-e4e5cd5c214e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_155","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Clamped bleeders do not drain. Unclamped bleeders drain at 1/s multiplied by drainScale.\n\ndrainScale rises at low vitals. During close phases the bot unclamps clamped bleeders only when the work list is empty. Bleeders already clamped at close start are safe to pad. Unclamped ones drain continuously and are unsafe. The next step is finding which ops enter close with unclamped bleeders.\n\nGrowth is safe because its bleed phase requires clamped bleeders and close requires all clamps off. Early phases are also safe since no bleeders exist yet and vitals stay high. Coda exposition has adagio drain, so it should not be padded. Development contains bleeders and recap contains crescendo.\n\nConductor is the boss. Its objective does not match the close pattern, so the bot clamps unclamped bleeders at priority 90. Later phases may spawn more bleeders, but conductor tools include clamp.\n\nConductor bleeders stay clamped until the work list empties, so a long closing gel chain is safe. For Coda, I will measure the current time and minimum vitals first. If the total is near 250 seconds with a low enough minimum, I will add one closing gel layer to push it past 256 seconds.\n\nA single chain layer adds roughly 8 seconds. One large extra layer adds about 26 seconds. If the base time drops to 168 seconds, four layers would reach 256 seconds. The current coda at healAt 58 is 251.8 seconds.\n\nNarrowing healAt to living coda only should restore adagio to 97.8 seconds and keep coda near 252 seconds, since conductor keeps the coda alive during that phase. The minimum vitals of 32.5 still require a higher threshold, so I will try 66 for coda-only. Any extra syringe trips would extend coda further and raise vitals.\n\nGrand rounds will remain untouched because it contains no coda entity. The implementation plan is to fix healAt for living coda only at threshold 66, add triggerMet `all` support and a gelChain helper, apply chains to safe phases, smoke test, adjust layer counts, try grande HP 150, then par scores, sloppy bot, and idle bot. Flag names must also be checked for collisions with gameplay flags.\n\nFlag names like `dress1` and `dress2` must be unique per phase within an op. Flags persist across phases on the same Sim, so if two phases in one op both use gelChain with identical flags, the second phase's trigger could fire immediately upon spawning its gel because the first phase's flag is still set.\n\nReconsidering the flag collision concern: even if a phase-level flag persists across phases, the gel chain still behaves correctly. The trigger requiring both `removed` and the flag will not fire at phase start because `removed` is false while gel exists. It only fires once the gel actually dies, so stale flags do not cause premature spawning.\n\nThe trigger evaluation loop runs sequentially. If a phase-level flag is already set from an earlier phase, the second trigger sees `removed` as true before the first trigger spawns its replacement gel. This ordering could break the intended chain sequence.\n\nIf a later trigger checks the chain flag before the earlier trigger spawns its replacement gel, the two triggers can fire on the same death and spawn an extra gel in parallel. To prevent this, gel chains should be limited to one phase per operation, or each phase must use unique flags that start unset.\n\nI will use unique flag prefixes per phase and restrict gel chains to one phase per operation. Only the opening, membrane, or finish phase will chain; coda closing alone will chain, not its exposition. Growth will chain only on open. I also need to verify that `when.all` short-circuit logic does not have an OR bug.\n\nThe `when.all` logic is confirmed correct: it returns true only when every condition in the array is met. A large gel rectangle at (-1.02, -0.42, 0.72, 0.42) was verified to sit inside the ellipse bounds. I will now run a microbenchmark to estimate exact layer timing.\n\nSmoke tests finish in a few seconds, so I can iterate quickly. I will add one layer to broken glass and measure the exact time delta to confirm the 26-second estimate.\n\nBot paint speed is 0.58, but existing gels complete in a single pass so extra passes are unnecessary. A parTime of 160 seconds means ROUGH grades at 160×1.6=256 seconds; since parScore is 92% of the bot’s own score, the rank stays S.\n\nI will set parTime to 40 on the padded gel layers. This keeps the normal bot at FLAWLESS while still allowing the sloppy bot to finish within the 160-second limit. The sloppy test is next.\n\nThe score formula is fine. Shared module state is pre-existing: tests should use one sim at a time or clone the op, since fired flags are mutated on shared phase arrays. gelChain creates fresh trigger objects at module load and stores them on each phase.\n\nI will check shape.js export style and op imports. The healAt fix and `all` support are next. Raising coda healAt to 66 triggers IV earlier than the previous 58 threshold. Damage continues during the walk to IV, so the patient spends more time high and the window is narrower.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b7ba17c-bcba-4063-8209-050d3c5818bd-31","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"syringeCd|syringe","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1750,"output_tokens":3044,"cache_read_input_tokens":80384,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"641a66ee-9427-49d7-b7c5-0286a70d2700"}
