rac=0.444 vmin=65.0 miss=0 score=15767 rank=S wall=255 left=bleeder@heart\\ncoda           OK ph=last-stop t=170.8 frac=0.300 vmin=32.5 miss=0 score=53387 rank=S wall=418 left=bleeder@heart,bleeder@lung,bleeder@lung,bleeder@lung\\nlast-patient   OK ph=one-shock t=3.6 frac=0.090 vmin=100.0 miss=0 score=4208 rank=- wall=3 left=bleeder@heart\\ngrand-rounds   OK ph=rounds t=178.7 frac=0.596 vmin=42.8 miss=0 score=26165 rank=S wall=320 left=bleeder@bowel,bleeder@heart,bleeder@bowel,bleeder@bowel\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/smoke.mjs\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Smoke ops after gel-layer padding\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-c125d19c-0266-444d-8bb1-4d7b918f4579-58.log\",\"total_bytes\":1094}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6d45a8e0-7da6-4f74-970f-74c2dcfbe5d3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_167","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Gel layers took less time than estimated.\n\nBG gel layers are within the 0.45–0.75 band at 0.581 and require no changes. Growth gel layers at 0.503 also satisfy the band but sit below the target of 198 seconds; adding one or two more layers would improve margin, though the current value is acceptable.\n\nI decided not to add another growth gel layer. The seeded bot is deterministic, so 0.503 will remain stable. Adding more layers risks overshoot if the per-layer estimate is wrong.\n\nAdagio and staccato are both safely inside their time bands. Legato is also inside its band but only 13 seconds above the floor, so I will add one layer to push it to 193 seconds and a fraction of 0.536.\n\nLegato will receive two additional gel layers, raising its total to eight and its fraction to 0.586.\n\nFermata is 2.6 seconds short of the band floor at 0.444. Two more layers will bring it to 222 seconds and a fraction of 0.529.\n\nCoda’s healAt 64 did not preserve the 251-second time; it returned to roughly 171 seconds. Its minimum value stayed near 32.5, unlike the healAt 40 run.\n\nThe 251-second coda run was driven by scratch and spore healAts causing constant IV trips, not by the coda being alive. When only coda triggers healAt 64, the bot syringes less often because vitals stay above 64 most of the time. The 32.5 dip is just one bad trip. To reach the 256-second floor, at least five gel layers are needed.\n\nCoda needs ten gel layers to hit the 342-second target, yielding a fraction of 0.614.\n\nThe closing phase clamps bleeders, so placing gel layers there is safe as long as they remain clamped. The bot will not reclamp them during the \"Close every site\" objective.\n\nTen gel layers on closing will not fix the minimum value. The 32.5 dip occurs during the conductor before closing, so raising healAt to 64 did not raise the floor above 32.5. That dip likely comes from a burst that drops vitals faster than the syringe can respond, such as a fortissimo or downbeat hit.\n\nThe 32.5 minimum is a fixed floor that appears regardless of heal threshold, whether healAt is 40 or 58. Extra gel layers only add time without improving the floor. The next step is to identify which attack deals enough fixed damage to land at exactly 32.5.\n\nThe 32.5 minimum likely comes from a single hit that lands at exactly 32.5 regardless of heal threshold. A downbeat strike of -6 would drop vitals from 38.5 to 32.5, or a fortissimo of -20 from 52.5. Another possibility is the bot leaving at healAt 40 and losing 7.5 during travel, which lands at 32.5. The dip may actually occur while the coda is dead—after extraction, when it has zero HP and cannot syringe, so scratches, spores, or bleeders drain during the trip.\n\nAdagio was previously killed by a healAt of 58 that triggered on scratches throughout the entire fight, forcing constant syringes and causing a timeout at 335 seconds with gel still pending. Extra gel padding now lets it finish at 169 seconds with 160 seconds remaining.\n\nRe-enabling healAt 58 for scratches would add roughly 238 seconds of extra syringes to adagio, which combined with the existing 72-second padding would push the total past the 330-second limit. A global scratch healAt is therefore unsafe.\n\nThe better approach is to make the coda-specific healAt conditional: only trigger it when the current operation is coda or when a coda exists in state.\n\nA coda-only healAt of 58 would still leave the minimum at 32.5, matching the 64-coda-only run. The floor is not fixed by leaving earlier at 58. The dip must come from a burst or damage source that ignores the heal threshold.\n\nThe 32.5 minimum might come from a scripted hit rather than travel. I will trace the exact moment it drops by logging vitalsMin changes with phase and reason, since hurt() currently lacks that history.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-71e0acd9-f962-41d1-832d-e27a3c307507-59","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function play","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","-A":25}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1215,"output_tokens":2466,"cache_read_input_tokens":101760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"92417a19-2d98-420f-bd73-390cecc81724"}
