{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_171","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The crash occurs at the start of the conductor.\n\nVitals dropped sharply from 48.7 to 42.73 after the downbeat, then again to 35.99 and 35.15. Spores drain about 2.4 per second while the bot is not healing. The bot is not syringing.\n\nThe syringe is blocked because four bleeders are open. The bot only syringes when vitals are below 22 while bleeders are unclamped.\n\nThe bleeders are likely clamped. Four open bleeders would drain 4 per second, but the observed rate is only about 2.4 per second. The drain is probably just scratches and spores.\n\nThe bot was already below the heal threshold of 64 from the first downbeat. It recovered to a floor of 32.54 after about one second. The syringe may not have registered at all.\n\nCore was only briefly active at the start of the drop, so it did not block syringing for most of the ten-second gap. The bot had no arrest queued, and the syringe is checked before the work list, so nothing higher on the priority list should have interfered.\n\nOne unclamped bleeder could explain the 2.4 per second drain alongside scratches. The bot may be blocked from syringing because it is clamping a development bleeder on the heart while the crescendo fortissimo bleeder sits on the aorta, leaving vitals above 22.\n\nBleeder clamp outranks coda wait, so the bot should prioritize clamping over camping. The objective is to end the conductor, not close it. The bot may be treating an unclamped bleeder as clamped.\n\nIf bleeding blocks the syringe, the bot falls through to the gift check. Hush can then fire when composure reaches 100 and vitals are below 50. That would slow the drain to 0.25x.\n\nRaising the syringe exception threshold from 22 to 38 would let the bot heal while bleeders are open. This could interrupt the dip and land it near 30 instead of 32. The current 22 limit was likely chosen to avoid abandoning clamps.\n\nThe dip from 35.99 to 32.5 is slow scratch drain, not travel damage. The bot was fighting while scratches ticked. Leaving for the IV at 36 would add another eight damage during travel. The better fix is to gel scratches before they stack. At t=75 there are five scratches and one spore.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eb45a4a4-819b-4916-a7df-eb84f6af07f4-63","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function stepScratch|function stepSpore|scratch","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/strains.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1274,"output_tokens":1757,"cache_read_input_tokens":107008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"dc6d8308-5839-4f09-b5ab-48e7d73e3867"}
