eder@lungc,bleeder@lungc,bleeder@lungc,coda@heart,baton@heart,baton@heart,scratch@heart\\nfermata        OK ph=close t=222.4 frac=0.529 vmin=65.0 miss=0 score=17027 rank=S wall=449 left=bleeder@heart\\nlegato         OK ph=repair t=195.0 frac=0.542 vmin=90.8 miss=0 score=29795 rank=S wall=333 left=bleeder@brain,bleeder@brain,bleeder@brain,bleeder@brain\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/smoke.mjs\\\" coda fermata legato\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Smoke coda, fermata, and legato\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-680c4a8a-2eb2-44b3-bf3a-cfffa2959f02-71.log\",\"total_bytes\":478}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"0f2da4d2-baaa-4b8d-9050-e5b587356681"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_178","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Fermata 0.529 is in band with a minimum velocity of 65.\n\nLegato 0.542 is in band with a minimum velocity of 90.8. The Coda died at t=113 because the low healAt prevented syringing and scratches killed it. A middle path is needed: syringe enough to survive but not during windup, or on safe beats when vitals are moderately low. The floor must rise by three points. The coda-only healAt 64 test completed at t=170.8 with a minimum velocity of 32.54.\n\nThe floor dropped to 32.5 because a single downbeat during a syringe trip drained vitals from 34.8 to 32.5 before the heal landed. The previous lows of 35.7 and 34.8 also came from -6 drops during trips. Blocking -6 drops during trips should raise the floor, though trips overlapping beat 4 might still cause drops.\n\nAborting during windup would still let the -6 drop and heal fail, possibly killing the bot. Cheating the mechanic by exempting downbeat damage was rejected. The plan is to reduce downbeat damage from 6 to 3. That would keep vitals at 37.8 instead of 34.8, raising the floor above the required threshold.\n\nA bot-only fix is preferred over changing the downbeat damage for humans. The plan explicitly requires -6, so altering that mechanic is undesirable. Stabilizer heals are not a viable path because the global heal amount affects all operations and the lesson phase. The bot may gel scratches more effectively, which would keep vitals higher and reduce syringe trips. However, healAt 64 triggers trips too frequently, and the cooldown often forces them to start from a low point around 41.\n\nThe bot waits until cooldown expires before traveling to the IV. By then vitals have dropped to 41 and a downbeat is imminent. Traveling during cooldown would let the syringe fire the instant cooldown ends, avoiding that damage.\n\nA pre-positioning strategy is being drafted. When the coda is up, vitals are below healAt, and the syringe is on cooldown, the bot will move toward the IV without using the syringe. This lets the heal fire instantly once cooldown expires, shrinking the downbeat window. The proposed condition checks that the coda is active, vitals are low, and the bot is not bleeding or already critically low.\n\nWalking to the IV during cooldown was rejected because it would miss batons and still risk windup. The real fix is to start the heal earlier, before vitals become critical, so both post-heal and pre-downbeat levels stay above 35.\n\nThe 35.7 dip at 68.0 was also a -6 during a trip. If that is prevented, the floor becomes 35.7, which is just above the required threshold. The next step is to determine what the floor would be if both -6 drops during trips are eliminated.\n\nRe-enabling a full trace with healAt 64 will test the cooldown approach. The 35.7 dip at 68.0 occurred while the bot was already at the IV, confirming that early movement does not prevent the -6 drop. Raising healAt to 50 or 55 is being considered for the coda.\n\nA 0.3-second earlier heal could have avoided the downbeat entirely, leaving the floor at roughly 42 from scratch damage alone. The simulation enforces a 0.5-second syringe hold, so timing is unavoidable. Mechanic changes like reducing downbeat damage when vitals are already low or pausing scratches during downbeats were considered and rejected. The PLAN test requires minimum vitals of at least 35; 32.5 fails while 35.7 passes.\n\nA plan to inject on beat 2 was abandoned. The bot would reach the IV during beat 4 and miss the baton, causing the next downbeat to land. This confirms that starting a trip on beats 2-3 is counterproductive.\n\nA round trip to the IV takes roughly 0.8 seconds, which is longer than beat 4’s 0.6 seconds, so the bot cannot return and kill the baton after syringing. Every syringe sacrifice costs a -6 downbeat, which creates the minimum vitals floor. To keep that floor above 35, vitals must be at least 41 before the hit frame, and the drain during the hit must not drop below 35. The desired sequence is to inject first, then take the downbeat: starting at 42 vitals, injecting raises them to 57, and the subsequent -6 leaves them at 51.\n\nThe current sequence is a downbeat during the approach, then injection. Starting at 42 vitals, that yields a floor of 33. The bot cannot return in time to kill the baton after syringing, so the next downbeat still lands. The -6 damage therefore strikes after the heal completes.\n\nThe floor is the pre-heal vitals, not the post-downbeat value. The death spiral is a missed baton, a -6 downbeat, and another missed baton during the syringe trip. If after healing the bot stays at 50 and only takes one -6 per cycle, it lands at 44. That floor is safe.\n\nThe trace shows the first heal cycle absorbed two downbeats because the trip was slow. The plan is to start a cycle before vitals drop below 50, walk during cooldown so the heal lands instantly, and accept exactly one -6 per cycle.\n\nThe bot will sprint to the IV on beat 2 if vitals are below 50, inject, and return. This kills the baton during beat 4 without taking damage. The next downbeat lands on beat 1, but vitals rise from 45 to 60 before that hit. Core must remain open.\n\nIf vitals are 40 at the start of a trip, the floor is 40. healAt 50 means we start when crossing 50, so we might be at 48. Floor ~48 minus scratch drain during trip. Good.\n\n**The miss is only every other bar** if we only trip when vitals < 50. After heal, vitals are 63, scratches drain them. If drain is 2/s and bar is 2.6s, two bars = 5s = -10, vitals 53. Might not need a trip every bar. When it drops under 50, one trip. The -6 after the trip lands on ~60. Safe.\n\nThe concrete implementation is being drafted. It exports beatInBar and sets healAt to 50 when the coda is active, otherwise 40. An emergency syringe triggers at any time if vitals drop below 28, or below 22 while bleeding. When the coda is up, the bot will either syringe on beats 2 or 3 if vitals are low and the cooldown is ready, or steer toward the IV to pre-position during cooldown.\n\nThe pre-positioning strategy is being refined. Walking to the IV during cooldown on beat 2 may extend into beat 4, so the bot would abort and return to the baton. This is messy but will be tested. Another edge case is whether the syringe can fire on beat 3 if cooldown expires there, even if it slightly overlaps beat 4.\n\nA `mem.healCommit` flag will let the bot finish an already-started syringe hold even if beat 4 arrives mid-hold. If vitals are low, it will complete the injection rather than aborting. On beat 2, it sets the flag and either syringes or steers toward the IV.\n\nThe bot will only commit a syringe on beat 2, not beat 3, to maximize time before beat 4. If the core is open that bar, it blocks the heal and fires the core instead. The `beatInBar` helper must be exported, and `mem.healCommit` should be ignored outside coda.\n\nThe `healCommit` flag will be cleared once vitals reach 58 or the syringe cooldown exceeds 2.4 seconds, ensuring the bot resumes fighting after healing. If the IV is unreachable, the flag persists and the bot keeps attempting the heal.\n\nThe `healCommit` flag must be skipped when bleeding is active and vitals are at or above 22, because hush does not restore health and the bot would stay stuck at the IV. The `syringeCd` field is already exported in state. Fermata, legato, and growth margin will remain unchanged. Coda time padding can be added later once the core fix is stable.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0467fe4e-1a02-426c-9d5e-e0bcf19b95ad-72","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js","old_string":"    beat: this.beat.count,\n    beatPhase: num(this.beat.phase),","new_string":"    beat: this.beat.count,\n    beatInBar: this.beat.count > 0 ? ((this.beat.count - 1) % 4) + 1 : 0,\n    beatPhase: num(this.beat.phase),"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0467fe4e-1a02-426c-9d5e-e0bcf19b95ad-73","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  const bleeding = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'bleeder' && !e.clamped);\n  const coreNow = state.entities.some((e) => (e.kind === 'coda' && e.coreOpen) || (e.kind === 'adagio' && e.hp > 0 && e.core));\n  const codaUp = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'coda' && e.hp > 0);\n  const windup = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'baton' && e.hp > 0 && e.windup);\n  // A syringe trip from the conductor misses the baton wind-up and eats the downbeat.\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 32 : 40;\n  if (!coreNow && !windup && state.vitals < healAt && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22)) {\n    return syringeAt(me, IV.x, IV.y, tuning, opts);\n  }","new_string":"  const bleeding = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'bleeder' && !e.clamped);\n  const coreNow = state.entities.some((e) => (e.kind === 'coda' && e.coreOpen) || (e.kind === 'adagio' && e.hp > 0 && e.core));\n  const codaUp = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'coda' && e.hp > 0);\n  const windup = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'baton' && e.hp > 0 && e.windup);\n  const beat = state.beatInBar || 0;\n  if (mem.healCommit && (state.vitals >= 58 || (me.syringeCd || 0) > 2.4 || !codaUp)) mem.healCommit = false;\n  // Leave for the IV on beat 2 so the shot lands before the next wind-up.\n  // Finishing that shot still costs the following downbeat, so do it from a high vitals.\n  if (codaUp && !coreNow && (mem.healCommit || (beat === 2 && state.vitals < 50)) && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22)) {\n    mem.healCommit = true;\n    if ((me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0) return syringeAt(me, IV.x, IV.y, tuning, opts);\n    return syringeAt(me, IV.x, IV.y, tuning, opts);\n  }\n  const healAt = 40;\n  if (!codaUp && !coreNow && !windup && state.vitals < healAt && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22)) {\n    return syringeAt(me, IV.x, IV.y, tuning, opts);\n  }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":448,"output_tokens":4794,"cache_read_input_tokens":121344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"b68b61a3-ad21-4774-81d3-3a94c3a96179"}
