{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_196","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Coda completed with a value of 47.4, well above the 35 threshold.\n\nThe gel layer time needs to increase by 155–241 seconds. Fourteen layers at roughly 18 seconds each would reach about 353 seconds, still under the 427-second ceiling. Twelve layers are the safer choice, expected to total around 317 seconds.\n\nTwelve layers fit comfortably within the time and fraction targets. They will be added to the closing phase's gel zone, since clamped bleeders do not drain it. The chain keeps a gel alive until the final layer, then unclamps. Twelve entries in an `on` array are harmless.\n\nThe first gel trigger fires when the initial closing gel ends, followed by twelve more layers. The existing 101-second closing time already includes that initial gel, so the extra layers add roughly 216 seconds for a total of about 317.\n\nI will add the layers and smoke coda. A full smoke test will also verify that recent bot changes did not regress non-coda operations. The changes are limited to coda-specific logic: healAt at 40, windup blocking, gift checks, and scratch priority.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8b9fbaf8-2fb3-45b8-82bc-ce85651e242a-99","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/ops/coda.js","old_string":"import { gel, gates, line } from './shape.js';","new_string":"import { gel, gelDress, gates, line } from './shape.js';"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8b9fbaf8-2fb3-45b8-82bc-ce85651e242a-100","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/ops/coda.js","old_string":"       