k=- score=0\\n-- grand rounds seats --\\ngr1              grand-rounds   OK t=178.7 frac=0.596 vmin=42.8 rank=S score=26165\\ngr2              grand-rounds   FAIL:miss t=106.7 frac=0.356 vmin=39.9 rank=- score=16763\\ngr3              grand-rounds   FAIL:miss t=18.6 frac=0.062 vmin=66.8 rank=- score=8568\\ngr4              grand-rounds   FAIL:miss t=103.5 frac=0.345 vmin=39.7 rank=- score=21739\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/bots.mjs\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Run sloppy, idle, and multi-seat bots\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-31af427b-1248-44de-a5cd-6e7efc094be7-125.log\",\"total_bytes\":1878}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"21398eca-bc6a-48af-b670-4003ac29719a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_209","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sloppy fails on misses for growth, legato, coda, and GR.\n\nMisses hit the Easy difficulty cap of 12. Noise and reaction delay cause missed stitches and bad cuts. The last patient fails because idle never ends at frame 6666. It has no timer or fail condition, but the bot never performs clamp or defib.\n\nIdle's FAIL:null at frame 6666 is acceptable because noFail prevents failure. The last patient correctly never fails and never completes without input. Vitals stayed at 100, confirming noFail works.\n\nIdle coda and GR correctly fail on vitals. Other operations fail on time.\n\nGR multi-seat misses are caused by bots interfering. They may nick each other or bump during sutures. The claims-per-tick system should split targets, but scalpel aim and suture gates likely still cause misses.\n\nGR3 hits the miss cap at 18.6 seconds with only eight misses, suggesting a burst of errors at the start with three players. I need to reduce sloppy bot misses without hurting the normal bot. Likely causes are scalpel nicks, sutures torn before the gate clears, and wrong link severing. The sloppy bot uses 0.03 noise on stick output.\n\nThe 0.25-second reaction delay is the main culprit. The bot acts on stale positions, so it often arrives late and overshoots. It may hold use while still outside the 0.3-unit suture gate, which triggers a miss. The ±0.03 stick noise is minor compared to this timing lag.\n\nThe bot's steer already slows near the target using reaction delay, but the use=1 command is still sent 0.25 seconds before arrival. During that interval, earlier travel commands continue moving the tip, so the delayed press can land after the gate has passed.\n\nA fix for the sloppy bot is to wait until the tip is stable near the target before asserting use, or to require very low approach speed. The existing steer already accounts for delay overshoot by using a radius that absorbs lag. At 0.25 seconds of delay and 0.5 speed, overshoot is roughly 0.12 units, which is smaller than the 0.3-unit gate miss radius, so this alone may not explain every suture miss.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3fc75909-d7fa-4c33-96e7-49d8aa492086-126","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"'MISS'","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1011,"output_tokens":1404,"cache_read_input_tokens":166272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"94d0c4ea-ae29-444b-bb97-21b42a34a5ed"}
