{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ffc78788-c4a1-49ad-a337-26d2cc92bab1-133","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"300→    sim.arrest.clock = Math.max(0, sim.arrest.clock - 2);\\n    sim.events.push({ type: 'shock', weak: true, seat: seat.id });\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  sim.arrestsSurvived += 1;\\n  const late = sim.arrest.clock < 2;\\n  const back = sim.arrest.savedVitals;\\n  sim.arrest = null;\\n  if (back != null) sim.vitals = Math.max(sim.vitals, Math.min(100, back));\\n  sim.events.push({ type: 'shock', weak: false, seat: seat.id, late });\\n310→  award(sim, seat, 'FLAWLESS', seat.x, seat.y, 'defib');\\n  seat.stats.Saves += 1;\\n  if (late) seat.lastSecond = true;\\n  sim.shockers = sim.shockers || [];\\n  sim.shockers.push(seat.id);\\n  if (sim.shockers.length >= 2) {\\n    sim.score += 500;\\n    sim.events.push({ type: 'syncShock' });\\n  }\\n}\\n320→\\nfunction stepScalpel(sim, seat, dt, use) {\\n  const cutting = use > 0.5;\\n  const tol = sim.scalpelTol;\\n  let onLine = false;\\n  for (const e of sim.entities) {\\n    if (!e.alive || e.site !== seat.site || e.done) continue;\\n    if (e.kind === 'incision' || e.kind === 'circleCut') onLine = cutPoly(sim, seat, e, dt, cutting, tol) || onLine;\\n    if ((e.kind === 'tether' || e.kind === 'link') && cutting) trySever(sim, seat, e);\\n  }\\n330→  if (cutting && !onLine && seat.speed > 0.15) {\\n    seat.nickT = (seat.nickT || 0) + dt;\\n    if (seat.nickT >= 0.4) {\\n      seat.nickT = 0;\\n      nick(sim, seat, 'bare');\\n    }\\n  } else seat.nickT = 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction cutPoly(sim, seat, e, dt, cutting, tol) {\\n340→  if (!e.len) e.len = polyLen(e.points);\\n  const proj = projectPoly(e.points, seat.x, seat.y);\\n  if (!proj) return false;\\n  const near = proj.d <= tol;\\n  if (!cutting) return near;\",\"content_concise\":\"300→    sim.arrest.clock = Math.max(0, sim.arrest.clock - 2);\\n    sim.events.push({ type: 'shock', weak: true, seat: seat.id });\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  sim.arrestsSurvived += 1;\\n  const late = sim.arrest.clock < 2;\\n  const back = sim.arrest.savedVitals;\\n  sim.arrest = null;\\n  if (back != null) sim.vitals = Math.max(sim.vitals, Math.min(100, back));\\n  sim.events.push({ type: 'shock', weak: false, seat: seat.id, late });\\n310→  award(sim, seat, 'FLAWLESS', seat.x, seat.y, 'defib');\\n  seat.stats.Saves += 1;\\n  if (late) seat.lastSecond = true;\\n  sim.shockers = sim.shockers || [];\\n  sim.shockers.push(seat.id);\\n  if (sim.shockers.length >= 2) {\\n    sim.score += 500;\\n    sim.events.push({ type: 'syncShock' });\\n  }\\n}\\n320→\\nfunction stepScalpel(sim, seat, dt, use) {\\n  const cutting = use > 0.5;\\n  const tol = sim.scalpelTol;\\n  let onLine = false;\\n  for (const e of sim.entities) {\\n    if (!e.alive || e.site !== seat.site || e.done) continue;\\n    if (e.kind === 'incision' || e.kind === 'circleCut') onLine = cutPoly(sim, seat, e, dt, cutting, tol) || onLine;\\n    if ((e.kind === 'tether' || e.kind === 'link') && cutting) trySever(sim, seat, e);\\n  }\\n330→  if (cutting && !onLine && seat.speed > 0.15) {\\n    seat.nickT = (seat.nickT || 0) + dt;\\n    if (seat.nickT >= 0.4) {\\n      seat.nickT = 0;\\n      nick(sim, seat, 'bare');\\n    }\\n  } else seat.nickT = 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction cutPoly(sim, seat, e, dt, cutting, tol) {\\n340→  if (!e.len) e.len = polyLen(e.points);\\n  const proj = projectPoly(e.points, seat.x, seat.y);\\n  if (!proj) return false;\\n  const near = proj.d <= tol;\\n  if (!cutting) return near;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js\",\"offset\":300,\"limit\":45,\"raw_output\":\"    sim.arrest.clock = Math.max(0, sim.arrest.clock - 2);\\n    sim.events.push({ type: 'shock', weak: true, seat: seat.id });\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  sim.arrestsSurvived += 1;\\n  const late = sim.arrest.clock < 2;\\n  const back = sim.arrest.savedVitals;\\n  sim.arrest = null;\\n  if (back != null) sim.vitals = Math.max(sim.vitals, Math.min(100, back));\\n  sim.events.push({ type: 'shock', weak: false, seat: seat.id, late });\\n  award(sim, seat, 'FLAWLESS', seat.x, seat.y, 'defib');\\n  seat.stats.Saves += 1;\\n  if (late) seat.lastSecond = true;\\n  sim.shockers = sim.shockers || [];\\n  sim.shockers.push(seat.id);\\n  if (sim.shockers.length >= 2) {\\n    sim.score += 500;\\n    sim.events.push({ type: 'syncShock' });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction stepScalpel(sim, seat, dt, use) {\\n  const cutting = use > 0.5;\\n  const tol = sim.scalpelTol;\\n  let onLine = false;\\n  for (const e of sim.entities) {\\n    if (!e.alive || e.site !== seat.site || e.done) continue;\\n    if (e.kind === 'incision' || e.kind === 'circleCut') onLine = cutPoly(sim, seat, e, dt, cutting, tol) || onLine;\\n    if ((e.kind === 'tether' || e.kind === 'link') && cutting) trySever(sim, seat, e);\\n  }\\n  if (cutting && !onLine && seat.speed > 0.15) {\\n    seat.nickT = (seat.nickT || 0) + dt;\\n    if (seat.nickT >= 0.4) {\\n      seat.nickT = 0;\\n      nick(sim, seat, 'bare');\\n    }\\n  } else seat.nickT = 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction cutPoly(sim, seat, e, dt, cutting, tol) {\\n  if (!e.len) e.len = polyLen(e.points);\\n  const proj = projectPoly(e.points, seat.x, seat.y);\\n  if (!proj) return false;\\n  const near = proj.d <= tol;\\n  if (!cutting) return near;\\n\",\"total_lines\":792}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"66f00ee4-9c8e-4590-a9f2-5ca70097b84e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_216","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Nicks are 'bare' when the event why is 'bare'. The grade why is always 'nick'.\n\nGrade events only show 'nick'. The event why field reveals whether it is bare or line. Bare nicks happen when a scalpel swipe severs a tether but does not register as onLine, causing cutting with speed above 0.15 for 0.4 seconds.\n\ntrySever never sets onLine. Normal bot swipes finish in 0.08 seconds, so they never trigger bare nicks. The sloppy bot is slower and stays cutting for over 0.4 seconds without touching an incision line, causing a bare nick every 0.4 seconds and resulting in 12 nicks and a failure.\n\nThe fix is to treat cutting a tether or link as onLine. This prevents legitimate sever swipes from being counted as bare nicks.\n\nThe fix can be implemented by setting onLine inside trySever when the scalpel is near a tether or link segment, or by having trySever return whether the seat is near that segment.\n\nThis would prevent multi-bot and GR failures where swipes are delayed or slow. In GR at round 18.6 with three players, the early phase has only two incisions, so bots may nick while splitting targets.\n\nThe third bot may have no incision left to claim if the first two bots already took both. It might then gel instead, which does not nick. All three could still try to cut if claims resolve within a single tick and each botInput independently adds to claims.\n\nClaims reset each tick, so bots should not collide on the same incision. The GR nicks may instead come from a third bot still holding a scalpel while its path crosses an incision, or from two bots' paths intersecting during a cut.\n\ncutPoly nicks once when cutting while not near a line, then returns false. If the scalpel oscillates on and off the line, the nicking flag resets and can trigger again. Multiple bots on one incision do not push each other; they have independent tips. Aim assist might pull them toward the line. Both bots could nick if they leave the same line after cutting it.\n\nA single-player run with the normal controller produces zero misses, so three-player nicks are not caused by normal bot behavior. The GR open phase includes four shards that require forceps, two bleeders that need clamps, and gel as a separate job. A third bot may start cutting an incision while another bot's steer crosses the line with use=1 because both are targeting nearby points. The network/couch setting is disabled by default.\n\nEach seat has its own site, so bots can be on different sites. All three may switch to the liver to cut incisions. If both incisions are claimed, the third bot should gel instead.\n\nA new possibility is that an incision finishes and the bot's scalpel use continues for a moment while it moves to the next target. cutPoly does not count a finished incision as onLine, so the bot could start nickT during that gap. One frame is only 1/60 second, which is below the 0.4-second threshold, unless the bot keeps holding the scalpel.\n\nThe one-frame gap after an incision dies does not accumulate a nick timer, because the timer resets when cutting stops. Claims correctly prevent multiple bots from targeting the same dead incision.\n\nA new possibility is that aim assist pulls the scalpel tip off the line. Each seat is pulled toward its nearest guide, so a bot between two incisions might be pulled toward the wrong one and leave the target line, causing a nick.\n\nThe three-player nick likely comes from one bot being pulled off the line by aim assist while between two incisions. Claims are set sequentially within the tick, so simultaneous targeting is not the cause. The rounds phase may also contain circle cuts or tether swipes that fail to register as onLine.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-877af689-2e46-4317-8724-5981539adb05-134","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/miss.mjs","old_string":"  for (const e of sim.events) {\n    if (e.type === 'grade' && e.grade === 'MISS') {\n      const key = (sim.phase?.id || '') + ':' + e.why;\n      counts[key] = (counts[key] || 0) + 1;\n    }\n  }","new_string":"  for (const e of sim.events) {\n    if (e.type === 'nick') {\n      const key = (sim.phase?.id || '') + ':' + e.why;\n      counts[key] = (counts[key] || 0) + 1;\n      if ((counts[key] || 0) <= 3) {\n        const tools = sim.seats.map((s) => s.tool + (s.use > 0.5 ? '*' : '')).join(',');\n        console.log(' nick', key, 't', sim.time.toFixed(2), 'tools', tools, 'spd', sim.seats.map((s) => s.speed.toFixed(2)).join(','));\n      }\n    }\n  }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":798,"output_tokens":2065,"cache_read_input_tokens":174336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"0e077f83-3f92-4b14-9283-96c51846b6e1"}
