{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_246","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Normal coda results are unchanged.\n\nGR 2-seat results are good. Time is 171.3. Vitals are 49.9. Rank is A. Misses are 5.\n\nRe-smoking 1, 3, and 4 seats to confirm unchanged results. The site-switch only triggers when the eye and bot sit on different sites, so seats already on the fermata site should beam similarly. The beat-3 approach only affects batons, which GR likely lacks.\n\nThe site-switch change could pull people off other work during arrest. GR 1, 3, and 4 still need retesting.\n\nSloppy legato remains broken. Time is 504. Vitals improved to 58.5. Link count stayed at 9. Four bleeders remain. The delayed grab did not fix the reattach issue.\n\nSloppy coda changed from a vitals failure to a time failure at t=850.4. The hush effect fired because the bot survived past t=138 with 38.7 vitals and zero misses. Hush slowed timer depletion, allowing the operation to run longer in wall time before the operation timer expired.\n\nSloppy coda is now a development-phase stall rather than a vitals death. The bot accumulated six links and four bleeders, scoring 64272—well above par—so it would have ranked S if it had finished.\n\nThe grab lead is 0.34 while the forceps radius is only 0.1. This gap likely explains why the legato chain cannot complete.\n\nThe 0.25-second reaction delay is the likely culprit. The bot queues a stationary forceps hold when within 0.34 of the piece, but that frame arrives 0.25 seconds later while the bot is still moving. During that interval the tip may have moved past the 0.1 grab radius, so the delayed press never actually catches the piece.\n\nReconsidering the 0.25-second delay: if the tip moves at roughly one fu per second, it would travel about 0.25 fu during that interval. That would place it near a distance of 0.09, still inside the 0.1 grab radius. The delayed press might actually reach the piece after all. The real cause of the legato stall likely lies elsewhere.\n\nThe delayed hold overshoots the piece. The bot keeps steering for 0.25 seconds after crossing the lead radius, then stops and presses at that new position. That landing point may sit outside the 0.1 grab radius.\n\nThe delayed hold should land exactly at the target if the lead distance equals the tip's travel distance during the reaction delay. The bot continues at its previous steering speed for that interval, so it arrives near zero distance and should still be inside the 0.1 grab radius.\n\nThe bot likely overshoots because steer speed is too high when the tip sits just above the lead radius. The hold then freezes the bot past the grab radius. I need to read steer() and moveSeat to understand the speed logic. Reattach lasts about 6.86 seconds, so the bot should have enough time if it actually presses the piece. Only three of twelve links were trayed.\n\nThe bot may be pressing too early. The delayed hold could fire while the tip is still outside the 0.1 grab radius, causing a hold in empty space that never catches the piece.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Normal coda is unchanged and two-seat Grand Rounds now clears. Sloppy legato and coda still stall on chains, so I’m tracing why the delayed forceps press misses the grab."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-be7b3199-ad64-41a6-a02a-dd4fb1f7c6a0-13","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"forceps|grabRadius|holder|reattach|cutAtBeat","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-be7b3199-ad64-41a6-a02a-dd4fb1f7c6a0-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function steer|function hold|function goTool","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":737,"output_tokens":2117,"cache_read_input_tokens":46592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"f9bc53c9-b12b-45bb-a67e-72d38f477a2d"}
