) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/trace-chain.mjs legato sloppy\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Trace sloppy legato chain events\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-8b648f93-357e-41a7-834e-cce49dfadfb6-27.log\",\"total_bytes\":11201}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"c2c2ff6b-88d1-41be-9bc3-4a3bbd4d3587"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_256","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bot is stuck at position 0.\n\nThe bot froze after choosing suction over a swipe. The active link should have been eligible for swiping, so the priority logic is unclear.\n\nThe suction logic should hold use 1 when distance is small. The log shows use 0.00 and speed 0. The bot is outputting zero velocity frames. Either steer returns zero or another function overrides the command.\n\nThe suction stall is a feedback loop. When distance exceeds 0.05, the bot steers with use 0. If steer returns zero velocity because magnitude is below 0.13, the tip never moves and distance stays above 0.05. The bot keeps repeating the same zero-velocity frame forever.\n\nThe suction job outranks the chain swipe, so the priority logic is wrong. The active link may be missing from candidates because chainActive does not match the expected index. The stuck state shows suction with use 0.\n\nNo link swipe candidate exists. The export state may be missing chainActive on the entity. Link 0 is uncut, so the index check should pass.\n\nThe entity's `cut` flag may be true while the chain link is not, which would block the swipe candidate. The log reads from `chain.links`, so an out-of-sync state could explain why the active link is skipped.\n\nstepLegato may return early and leave link entities with stale chainActive values. The suction stall is a general stick-deadzone bug that freezes the bot when commanded speed drops below the threshold. A one-shot dump of candidates at the stuck frame would reveal why the chain swipe was skipped.\n\nA short script will stop at t=220 to dump every entity’s kind, cut status, index, chainActive, grabbable flag, and the top candidate. The steer deadzone threshold is 0.13.\n\nThe slowdown formula `speed = d / (delay + 0.1)` can produce a magnitude below the 0.13 steer threshold while distance remains above 0.05. Spot then demands closer steering, but steer rejects the command because it is too small to move. This deadlock traps the bot in place.\n\nSteer deadzones at a desired speed of 0.059 or lower. The spot() function requests 0.8 speed when distance exceeds 0.05, but the slowdown radius is only about 0.296, so that request is not slowed down.\n\nThe slowdown formula keeps speed above 0.08 inside the slow zone, so steer should still emit a nonzero command. The real freeze may be that distance is below 0.012, causing steer to return zero before spot() ever checks the target.\n\nThe log shows use 0.00, so spot() must have entered the steer branch and not the early hold. If distance were below 0.012, spot() would have returned use 1 immediately. The contradiction suggests the suction target position used by spot() may differ from the actual position.\n\nDifficulty does not change tipSpeed, so the 0.13 deadzone threshold is unchanged. Noise only adds ±0.03 to position after the frame is built, which cannot zero the command. The logged seat state reflects the simulation’s current state after applying a 0.25-second delayed frame.\n\nThe zero command is not merely delayed. The bot is actively emitting zero-velocity frames now.\n\nA new possibility explains the stuck suction tool: if a frame omits the tool field, the seat retains the previous tool. Because the current frame carries use 0 but no tool change, the seat remains on suction.\n\nThe next step is to identify which function returns a bare zero frame without specifying a tool.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-de0d8768-70e9-4767-80fb-1b8e8c05e53f-28","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","offset":385,"limit":55}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-de0d8768-70e9-4767-80fb-1b8e8c05e53f-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/m