{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_266","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The failure occurs in RECAP, which is the step that follows development.\n\nThe legato chain fix allowed the bot to finish development, but the crescendo phase in recap is now causing the failure. The vitals death at 98 seconds suggests the entire pipeline completed much faster than expected.\n\nThe 98-second timeline suggests development finished very quickly. The crescendo phase likely killed vitals by draining them through growth and bleeders, while feeders remained unexposed. The sloppy bot may be failing to kill feeders fast enough due to reaction delay, unclamped bleeders, or missing hush logic.\n\nThe priority threshold is the root cause. Feeders outrank bleeders only when vitals are at least 55. Once vitals drop below that, bleeders (90) outrank feeders (86). The sloppy bot is too slow to kill feeders before vitals fall, so it clamps bleeders instead. Crescendo keeps growing and the death spiral continues.\n\nReverting the feeder priority split is risky because normal coda minimum vitals are only 47.3, so the bot would drop below 55 during crescendo. Raising the low-priority threshold to 91 would keep feeders outranking bleeders at all times, but that could alter normal behavior.\n\nRaising the feeder priority threshold would alter the normal coda score, which would require recomputing the par. The bot has no dedicated sloppy mode branch, so any fix must be applied globally.\n\nA delay-gated fix is possible because the zero-delay path must remain unchanged. Passing a flag through state to candidates() is hacky, so always setting feeder priority to 94 is the cleaner approach. The next step is to trace normal coda's recap vitals path and verify whether that change alters the normal score.\n\nThe cleaner fix is to pass opts into candidates() and gate feeder priority on reactionDelay. When delay is zero, the priority split stays at 94/86. When delay is positive, feeders always outrank bleeders at 94. This avoids mutating state and keeps the zero-delay path unchanged.\n\nThe priority inversion may not be the only cause. Eight bleeders is a lot, and crescendo spawns one at fortissimo. Pools might come from another source, not nicks. I will trace the sloppy coda recap vitals and update the generic trace to cover development and recap.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-00ebdeca-67c1-4964-8b63-7cdfefbc792b-41","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/strains.js","offset":180,"limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-00ebdeca-67c1-4964-8b63-7cdfefbc792b-42","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"clampsUsed|maxClamp|clampLimit","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2209,"output_tokens":1513,"cache_read_input_tokens":87936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"3b57c18b-089e-4ab5-b68a-96471ccf53c7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-00ebdeca-67c1-4964-8b63-7cdfefbc792b-41","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"180→function stepCrescendo(sim, e, dt, beats) {\\n  const live = sim.entities.filter((f) => f.alive && f.kind === 'feeder' && f.parent === e.id);\\n  if (!e.exposed) {\\n    const growDt = dt * sim.beatScale();\\n    e.size = Math.min(1, e.size + (0.02 + 0.015 * live.length) * growDt);\\n    sim.hurt((1 + 6 * e.size) * growDt, 'crescendo');\\n    if (e.size >= 1) {\\n      e.size = 0.6;\\n      sim.hurt(20, 'fortissimo');\\n      sim.spawn({ kind: 'bleeder', site: e.site, at: [e.x - 0.2, e.y] });\\n190→      sim.spawn({ kind: 'bleeder', site: e.site, at: [e.x + 0.2, e.y] });\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'fortissimo', id: e.id });\\n    }\\n    for (const b of beats) {\\n      if (b.beat % 16 === 0 && live.length < 4) {\\n        const missing = 4 - live.length;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < missing; i++) {\\n          sim.spawn({\\n            kind: 'feeder',\\n            site: e.site,\\n200→            parent: e.id,\\n            at: [e.x + Math.cos(i) * 0.25, e.y + Math.sin(i) * 0.18],\\n            hp: 40,\\n          });\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (live.length === 0 && e.armed) {\\n      e.exposed = true;\\n      e.need = 'scalpel';\\n210→      sim.spawn({\\n        kind: 'circleCut',\\n        site: e.site,\\n        at: [e.x, e.y],\\n        points: circle(e.x, e.y, 0.22),\\n      });\\n    }\\n    e.armed = true;\\n  } else {\\n    e.size = Math.max(0.2, e.size - 0.15 * dt);\\n220→    const cut = sim.entities.find((c) => c.kind === 'circleCut' && c.site === e.site && !c.alive);\\n    if (cut && !e.revealed) {\\n      e.revealed = true;\\n      e.grabbable = true;\\n      e.need = 'forceps';\\n      e.embedded = true;\\n      e.embed = e.embed || 0.35;\\n      e.axis = 90;\\n    }\\n  }\\n230→}\\n\\nfunction circle(x, y, r) {\\n  const pts = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i <= 12; i++) {\\n    const a = (i / 12) * Math.PI * 2;\\n    pts.push([x + Math.cos(a) * r, y + Math.sin(a) * r * 0.7]);\\n  }\\n  return pts;\\n}\\n240→\\nfunction stepFermata(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (!sim.arrest && e.stage === 'attack') {\\n    sim.arrest = {\\n      clock: 8,\\n      tutorial: !!e.tutorial,\\n      stopsBeat: true,\\n      holdVitals: true,\\n      source: e.id,\\n      savedVitals: sim.vitals,\\n250→    };\\n    sim.vitals = Math.min(sim.vitals, 15);\\n    sim.events.push({ type: 'arrest', id: e.id });\\n    e.stage = 'open';\\n  }\\n  if (sim.arrest && sim.arrest.source === e.id) {\\n    const clockScale = sim.hushPhase === 'wash' ? sim.tuning.hushTimeScale : 1;\\n    if (sim.hushPhase !== 'inhale') sim.arrest.clock -= dt * clockScale;\\n    sim.vitals = 15;\\n    if (sim.arrest.clock <= 0 && !sim.noFail && !sim.lockFail) sim.fail('vitals');\\n260→  }\\n  if (!sim.arrest && e.stage === 'open') {\\n    e.stage = 'between';\\n    e.arrests = (e.arrests || 0) + 1;\\n    if (e.arrests >= (e.needed || 1) && e.hp <= 0) {\\n      e.grabbable = true;\\n      e.need = 'forceps';\\n      e.embedded = true;\\n      e.embed = 0.45;\\n      e.axis = 90;\\n270→    }\\n  }\\n  e.eye = true;\\n  e.need = e.hp > 0 && sim.arrest ? 'laser' : e.grabbable ? 'forceps' : 'wait';\\n}\\n\\nfunction stepCoda(sim, e, dt, beats) {\\n  const beatInBar = sim.beat.phase >= 0 ? ((sim.beat.count % 4) || 4) : 1;\\n  // Wind-up is the beat before downbeat: beat 4 telegraphs beat 1.\\n  const telegraph = (sim.beat.count % 4) === 0;\",\"content_concise\":\"180→function stepCrescendo(sim, e, dt, beats) {\\n  const live = sim.entities.filter((f) => f.alive && f.kind === 'feeder' && f.parent === e.id);\\n  if (!e.exposed) {\\n    const growDt = dt * sim.beatScale();\\n    e.size = Math.min(1, e.size + (0.02 + 0.015 * live.length) * growDt);\\n    sim.hurt((1 + 6 * e.size) * growDt, 'crescendo');\\n    if (e.size >= 1) {\\n      e.size = 0.6;\\n      sim.hurt(20, 'fortissimo');\\n      sim.spawn({ kind: 'bleeder', site: e.site, at: [e.x - 0.2, e.y] });\\n190→      sim.spawn({ kind: 'bleeder', site: e.site, at: [e.x + 0.2, e.y] });\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'fortissimo', id: e.id });\\n    }\\n    for (const b of beats) {\\n      if (b.beat % 16 === 0 && live.length < 4) {\\n        const missing = 4 - live.length;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < missing; i++) {\\n          sim.spawn({\\n            kind: 'feeder',\\n            site: e.site,\\n200→            parent: e.id,\\n            at: [e.x + Math.cos(i) * 0.25, e.y + Math.sin(i) * 0.18],\\n            hp: 40,\\n          });\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (live.length === 0 && e.armed) {\\n      e.exposed = true;\\n      e.need = 'scalpel';\\n210→      sim.spawn({\\n        kind: 'circleCut',\\n        site: e.site,\\n        at: [e.x, e.y],\\n        points: circle(e.x, e.y, 0.22),\\n      });\\n    }\\n    e.armed = true;\\n  } else {\\n    e.size = Math.max(0.2, e.size - 0.15 * dt);\\n220→    const cut = sim.entities.find((c) => c.kind === 'circleCut' && c.site === e.site && !c.alive);\\n    if (cut && !e.revealed) {\\n      e.revealed = true;\\n      e.grabbable = true;\\n      e.need = 'forceps';\\n      e.embedded = true;\\n      e.embed = e.embed || 0.35;\\n      e.axis = 90;\\n    }\\n  }\\n230→}\\n\\nfunction circle(x, y, r) {\\n  const pts = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i <= 12; i++) {\\n    const a = (i / 12) * Math.PI * 2;\\n    pts.push([x + Math.cos(a) * r, y + Math.sin(a) * r * 0.7]);\\n  }\\n  return pts;\\n}\\n240→\\nfunction stepFermata(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (!sim.arrest && e.stage === 'attack') {\\n    sim.arrest = {\\n      clock: 8,\\n      tutorial: !!e.tutorial,\\n      stopsBeat: true,\\n      holdVitals: true,\\n      source: e.id,\\n      savedVitals: sim.vitals,\\n250→    };\\n    sim.vitals = Math.min(sim.vitals, 15);\\n    sim.events.push({ type: 'arrest', id: e.id });\\n    e.stage = 'open';\\n  }\\n  if (sim.arrest && sim.arrest.source ==