{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_278","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The laser burn rate is 2 per second with a drain multiplier of 0.\n\nScorch damage is negligible. The bot loses the race because four feeders need about eight seconds to kill, and growth from zero takes roughly ten seconds. Lowering healAt to 8 and speeding up delayed beams should help. Now reviewing the beam() function.\n\nThe crawl at 0.32 speed for the last 0.25 units adds roughly 0.8 seconds, plus a 0.25 second delay before firing. The fix is to approach faster when a reaction delay exists and fire earlier.\n\nThe revised beam logic fires at 0.16 distance with a 0.25 second delay. Approach speed is 0.95 until that point, then drops to 0.7. The laser turns on 0.25 seconds later, closing roughly 0.2 units in that interval. If the bot overshoots by more than 0.05, scorch damage may occur.\n\nA simpler fix may be to keep the crawl but stop syringing. The bot could grow from 0.15 to 0.55 without firing, then become exposed. The trace shows feeders respawned while the bot was still climbing size, so the rate stayed high and two feeders remained alive.\n\nThe bot never kept fewer than two feeders alive for long. Respawn triggers on beat % 16, not a fixed interval from phase start, so the window is short and unpredictable. If a respawn hits while one feeder remains, it instantly restores four, forcing the bot to kill all four within that single window.\n\nThe respawn window is at most 10.4 seconds, but it can be shorter if the beat clock is near a multiple of 16. The trace shows feeders dropping from four to three at t=88, then back to four at t=92 just six seconds later. That rapid cycle suggests the bot was stuck at the IV and not actually killing feeders, so the respawn was simply refilling the pool.\n\nThe 14hp feeder was not killed by the bot. A delayed laser command still queued from before the syringe decision kept firing for 0.25 seconds and damaged it down to 7hp. A beat%16 respawn then added two more feeders, bringing the total back to four.\n\nThe t=86 respawn was only five seconds after the previous one, not ten. The 6hp feeder at that moment was likely damaged by a delayed laser rather than a fresh spawn, so the log is too messy to overfit. I will move on to planning the actual fixes.\n\nThe bot already sticks to a single target once it is low on health. The plan is to lower healAt to 8 and speed up delayed beams, then retest coda sloppy only. The circle cut after expose can wait until fortissimo is cleared.\n\nAt t=90 the bot has size 0.83 and two feeders, so it would drain to about 14 before being exposed. That margin is tight, and a respawn at t=91 would instantly refill the pool to four. The faster delayed beam is therefore the essential fix.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e68d84c7-3f94-46dc-9ceb-585600817de1-57","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  const swelling = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0 ? 22 : 40);","new_string":"  const swelling = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0 ? 8 : 40);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e68d84c7-3f94-46dc-9ceb-585600817de1-58","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"function beam(me, e, tuning, opts) {\n  const d = Math.hypot(me.x - e.x, me.y - e.y);\n  if (d > 0.03) {\n    const f = steer(me, e.x, e.y, d > 0.25 ? 0.9 : 0.32, tuning, opts);\n    return goTool(f, 'laser', d < 0.04 ? 1 : 0);\n  }\n  return hold('laser', 1);\n}","new_string":"function beam(me, e, tuning, opts) {\n  const d = Math.hypot(me.x - e.x, me.y - e.y);\n  const delay = opts.reactionDelay || 0;\n  if (delay > 0) {\n    // Fire on the way in. The queued beam then meets the target instead of starting late.\n    if (d > 0.18) return goTool(steer(me, e.x, e.y, 0.95, tuning, opts), 'laser', 0);\n    if (d > 0.04) return goTool(steer(me, e.x, e.y, 0.7, tuning, opts), 'laser', 1);\n    return hold('laser', 1);\n  }\n  if (d > 0.03) {\n    const f = steer(me, e.x, e.y, d > 0.25 ? 0.9 : 0.32, tuning, opts);\n    return goTool(f, 'laser', d < 0.04 ? 1 : 0);\n  }\n  return hold('laser', 1);\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":277,"output_tokens":2617,"cache_read_input_tokens":105728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"9139193e-fa85-4126-90d4-de94807059fa"}
