{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_285","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reviewing the current state: cd is 0.0, adagio is 0, v=19.7, and not bleeding or coda.\n\nThe syringe check should have fired, but the bot was carrying crescendo with forceps. carry() returns before the syringe check, so the decision never reached it.\n\nThe bot was cutting for roughly two seconds while vitals stayed below 40, so it should have walked to the IV instead. I will add a direct call log to trace the decision.\n\nThe exportState function omits `exposed` from the exported entity. The bot reads this state, so `e.exposed` is undefined. This likely breaks the exposed check and prevents the syringe decision.\n\nThe missing `exposed` field keeps `healAt` at 8 even after the crescendo is exposed. The bot therefore never syringes. It also still thinks it is swelling because that flag is invisible. Exporting `exposed` will fix this.\n\nA workaround using exported `grabbable` and `feeder` entities was considered. The bot would detect swelling by checking for alive feeders while the crescendo is not grabbable. Feeders disappear at the exact moment of expose, so this signal would be unreliable.\n\nThe `grabbable` field is exported, so it can be used as the signal. During the fight feeders exist and keep `healAt` at 8. Once feeders die at t=92, `healAt` jumps to 40 and the bot syringes before cutting the circle. This raises vitals to roughly 35 before the cut, which may help the arrest.\n\nThe `grabbable`-and-feeder check is confirmed as the correct fix. It will be added to the code, and `exposed` will also be exported so the bot reads the true simulation state.\n\nAdding `exposed` to the export will change the state hash, but normal bot behavior is unaffected because the new swelling check is delay-gated and currently false. Simulation outcomes remain identical.\n\nThe coda score should remain unchanged because the bot's delay is zero. Entry vitals may still be low at roughly 35, but the hush gate threshold is now below 62, so the conductor could survive with two syringes.\n\nThe prior timeout at 850 occurred during development, so the hush gate was never actually validated on a live run. The bot will be retested with the corrected export once the fix is applied. A scorch of 111 at the start of recap also stands out as an unusually high early laser damage.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30ea8aa4-4e01-46fd-b647-46d6b6aa7697-65","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js","old_string":"      grabbable: e.grabbable || undefined, fleeing: e.fleeing || undefined,","new_string":"      grabbable: e.grabbable || undefined, exposed: e.exposed || undefined, fleeing: e.fleeing || undefined,"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1213,"output_tokens":1832,"cache_read_input_tokens":114688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"3e2a8c5d-f97d-46e3-838f-7681478a30ae"}
