ort 0 laser 6\\nt 90.2 v 25.6 tool laser use 1.00 spd 0.00 pos 0.14 0.17 size 0.75 exp false cd 0.0 feeds 2 34,3 bleed 0 adagio 0 scorch 137 fort 0 laser 7\\nt 92.2 v 19.7 tool laser use 0.00 spd 0.91 pos 0.26 0.03 size 0.77 exp true cd 0.0 feeds 0  bleed 0 adagio 0 scorch 137 fort 0 laser 9\\nt 94.2 v 34.7 tool laser use 0.00 spd 0.00 pos 1.02 0.22 size 0.47 exp true cd 3.0 feeds 0  bleed 0 adagio 0 scorch 137 fort 0 laser 9\\nt 96.2 v 34.7 tool scalpel use 1.00 spd 0.00 pos 0.19 0.01 size 0.20 exp true cd 0.9 feeds 0  bleed 0 adagio 0 scorch 137 fort 0 laser 9\\nt 98.2 v 34.7 tool forceps use 1.00 spd 1.36 pos 0.71 0.40 size 0.20 exp true cd -0.0 feeds 0  bleed 0 adagio 0 scorch 137 fort 0 laser 9\\nt 100.2 v 15.0 tool laser use 0.00 spd 0.99 pos 0.66 0.11 size - exp undefined cd -0.0 feeds 0  bleed 0 adagio 0 scorch 137 fort 0 laser 9\\nt 102.3 v 15.0 tool laser use 1.00 spd 0.00 pos 0.06 0.05 size - exp undefined cd -0.0 feeds 0  bleed 0 adagio 0 scorch 146 fort 0 laser 9\\nt 104.3 v 15.0 tool laser use 1.00 spd 0.00 pos 0.06 0.05 size - exp undefined cd -0.0 feeds 0  bleed 0 adagio 0 scorch 205 fort 0 laser 9\\nPHASE conductor t 104.5 v 34.7\\nEND vitals t 123.9 v 0.0 {\\\"say\\\":4,\\\"tool\\\":56,\\\"burst\\\":8,\\\"scorch\\\":240,\\\"grade\\\":53,\\\"note\\\":5,\\\"bark\\\":140,\\\"downed\\\":2,\\\"hint\\\":10,\\\"wake\\\":1,\\\"grip\\\":10,\\\"tray\\\":10,\\\"sealed\\\":1,\\\"phase\\\":3,\\\"jerk\\\":12,\\\"clamp\\\":4,\\\"site\\\":64,\\\"pin\\\":4,\\\"lasered\\\":9,\\\"sever\\\":8,\\\"hush\\\":6,\\\"drained\\\":4,\\\"stabilize\\\":2,\\\"cut\\\":1,\\\"pop\\\":1,\\\"arrest\\\":1,\\\"shock\\\":1,\\\"cue\\\":8,\\\"downbeat\\\":7,\\\"fail\\\":1}\\n---\\n{\\\"id\\\":\\\"coda\\\",\\\"seats\\\":1,\\\"mode\\\":\\\"normal\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"failed\\\":null,\\\"t\\\":318.4,\\\"frac\\\":0.559,\\\"vmin\\\":47.3,\\\"rank\\\":\\\"S\\\",\\\"score\\\":37227,\\\"par\\\":34249,\\\"miss\\\":0,\\\"phase\\\":\\\"last-stop\\\",\\\"steps\\\":19102,\\\"kinds\\\":{\\\"bleeder\\\":4}}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"SCRATCH=\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer\\\"\\ncd \\\"$SCRATCH\\\"\\nnode trace-recap.mjs > coda-trace4.txt &\\nnode one.mjs coda 1 normal > coda-normal4.json &\\nwait\\necho DONE\\ntail -20 coda-trace4.txt\\necho '---'\\ncat coda-normal4.json\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Retest coda after exporting exposed\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-b1194009-6fdf-43c5-9964-6bd859b0d63f-66.log\",\"total_bytes\":3774}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"042bb3c9-a178-4107-b70f-018eab57b72f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_287","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Normal coda remains perfect. Sloppy now syringes once at version 19.\n\nThe bot still dies at t=123.9, about 19 seconds into the conductor. It entered at 34.7 with hush but seven downbeats still killed it. Other damage from notes, scratches, and spores was also present. The conductor is the boss. The bot must kill it before downbeats stack. At v=34.7 it is very fragile.\n\nA second syringe before arrest would have helped. The cooldown expired during the cut, but extraction blocked it because forceps-carrying skips syringes. The window was too short.\n\nOnly one heal fits unless it is taken earlier during the fight. A healAt of 28 instead of 8 would let the bot syringe mid-fight at v=28, recover to ~43, finish feeders, and syringe again after expose. Entry would then be ~50+. At healAt=30 it would leave at t=88 when v=31.9.\n\nLeaving before the feeders die would trigger a respawn and fortissimo, so only one heal after expose is viable. Entry at ~35 is the result. The conductor must be survivable from that low health with a delayed hand. Hush fires instantly and lasts seven seconds, but the bot should still kill batons and damage the core. The nineteen-second death is unexplained, so the conductor phase needs tracing.\n\nA two-second trace of the conductor phase will log vitals, hush status, coda and baton health, beat, tool, downbeats, and composure. Downbeats deal -3.6 damage each. Seven downbeats total 25.2 damage. Notes and scratches add further damage. The death at 123.9 sim time occurs because hush slows the beat clock while the wall-clock timer continues.\n\nOnly six hush events occurred, suggesting just one seven-second hush at the start. Composure must rebuild to 100 from zero. The bot likely scored only one flawless action during that brief pause. Afterward it ran at full speed for twelve seconds. Downbeats struck roughly every 2.6 seconds, totaling about four or five hits.\n\nThe coda has 255 health. The core deals about 45 damage per second on average, so it should take roughly eleven seconds to kill if the laser is always active during openings. The bot is still dead after nineteen seconds, meaning the coda is probably still alive and the delay is letting downbeats keep stacking.\n\nA second +15 heal is being explored. The bot would syringe immediately upon exposure at low health, then start the cut. The three-second cooldown expires mid-cut, allowing a second syringe before extraction.\n\nThe cooldown expired at t=98.2 while the bot was already forceps-carrying, so it never had a free moment with cd=0 and empty hands after the first heal. The second syringe was therefore impossible.\n\nThe cooldown expired exactly when the bot grabbed the tool, leaving no gap for a second syringe. Lowering cooldown globally is not an option. The plan is to heal earlier so the first syringe's cooldown expires during the cut with a buffer.\n\nA mid-fight syringe at v=28 would likely lose the feeder race. The trace shows a two-second margin, and a three-second trip risks fortissimo. Leaving at t=88 with size 0.65 and three feeders could grow the bot to 0.85 in three seconds, but feeders might respawn. The next test is healAt = 32.\n\nA failed race at healAt=32 will be reverted. Changing stabilizer rules is not an option. The circle cut itself is the delay, and the cooldown expires as the cut ends. Waiting for the cooldown to expire before cutting is not a reliable strategy.\n\nHealing before the cut does not fix the cooldown window. The circle cut and extraction each take about three seconds, so the first three seconds are spent cutting while the cooldown is active, and the last three seconds are spent extracting with hands full. This leaves no free window for a second syringe.\n\nThe circle cut lasts only about two seconds, so the three-second cooldown expires before the bot can grab the tool. A second syringe during the cut is therefore impossible. The only remaining path is to heal before the expose, letting the cooldown expire while the bot waits for the cut to finish.\n\nA late syringe during the feeder fight is being considered when the last feeders are low and health is below 35. The cooldown would run through the end of the fight and the cut, allowing a second heal after exposure before extraction. A preemptive top-up to 64 at the start of recap was rejected because it is not an emergency. A heuristic rule to heal when a crescendo exists and health is below 55 with no feeders low was also dismissed as too complex.\n\nA new heuristic is being drafted: if the crescendo size is below 0.25, health is under 60, delay is positive, and cooldown is ready, the bot syringes once at the start of the fight. This would raise entry health from roughly 34 to about 49.\n\nThe preemptive trip is only about two seconds, so the crescendo can grow from 0.15 to roughly 0.25 during the heal without hitting the size limit. This makes the early top-up viable. The new logic triggers a preemptive syringe when a crescendo exists with delay active, size below 0.22, and health under 70. The heal threshold also drops to 8 instead of 40 whenever a crescendo is present.\n\nThe preemptive syringe fires at recap start because size is 0.15 and health is 49, raising entry to roughly 64. The fight ends near 34, so the post-expose healAt of 40 triggers again and brings entry back to about 49. This gives arrest a buffer of roughly 49. The rule only activates during recap, not development, and fortissimo resets size to 0.6, which is above the 0.22 threshold.\n\nThe preemptive syringe check runs before candidate selection, so the bot will indeed choose it over continuing to the previous site. Development has no crescendo, so the rule is safe there. I will implement the preemptive heal and run a quick conductor survival test; if entry health near 50 still kills the bot, I will improve conductor combat. Early laser scorch might also be hurting the fight by burning when the core is missed.\n\nThe early-fire beam logic is dangerous for the coda boss. When the core is closed, the laser skips the hit and waits 0.25 seconds before applying burn damage. This means the bot could scorch itself while trying to reach a closed coda core.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e1a9d24f-b556-423c-82a3-b21ce43c183b-67","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  const swelling = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0 ? 8 : 40);\n  if (!coreNow && !(codaUp && windup) && state.vitals < healAt && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22)) {","new_string":"  const swelling = state.entities.find((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\n  const slow = (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0;\n  // One early dose, while the swelling is still small, so the delayed hand can stay on the feeders.\n  const preempt = !!(swelling && slow && (swelling.size || 0) < 0.22 && state.vitals < 70);\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && slow ? 8 : 40);\n  if (!coreNow && !(codaUp && windup) && (preempt || state.vitals < healAt) && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22 || preempt)) {"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1610,"output_tokens":3690,"cache_read_input_tokens":117760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"cd82ad49-c3db-4e88-8739-d70b47abb669"}
