se}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"4018e66c-d0fe-4096-baf9-088e10a188bf"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_291","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A preemptive heal caused a fortissimo, reducing size to zero.\n\nThe bot is stuck in a priority inversion loop. Bleeder clamping has higher priority than circle cutting, so it repeatedly syringes and fails to cut the circle. It cannot clamp the two bleeders because they spawn at positions that make the clamp action ineffective.\n\nThe clamp cap is 4. Development legato jerks already used all four clamps on heart bleeders. Recap fortissimo bleeders cannot be clamped because the limit is reached. The bot keeps trying and fails, so it never cuts the circle.\n\nThe fix adds a guard to the bleeder logic. It checks `state.phaseTools` and `state.clampsUsed` before attempting to clamp. If clamping is unavailable, the bot skips it and prioritizes cutting the circle instead. This also changes delay-0 behavior.\n\nNormal coda recap never fortissimos, so it never attempts to clamp. Normal development finishes before clampsUsed reaches four, and clamp is available in that phase. The new guard only affects the problematic recap state.\n\nNormal coda should be retested to confirm the fix does not alter its timing. The sloppy bot now cuts the circle instead of clamping, but the preemptive syringe still caused the fortissimo.\n\nUnclamped bleeders drain the patient during the circle cut. The preemptive heal should be reverted entirely. It caused the fortissimo. The prior version without it was better.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f534f47b-94d4-46d3-bf75-088fea896440-72","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/strains.js","offset":276,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f534f47b-94d4-46d3-bf75-088fea896440-73","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  const swelling = state.entities.find((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\n  const slow = (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0;\n  // One early dose, while the swelling is still small, so the delayed hand can stay on the feeders.\n  const preempt = !!(swelling && slow && (swelling.size || 0) < 0.22 && state.vitals < 70);\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && slow ? 8 : 40);\n  if (!coreNow && !(codaUp && windup) && (preempt || state.vitals < healAt) && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22 || preempt)) {","new_string":"  const swelling = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0 ? 8 : 40);\n  if (!coreNow && !(codaUp && windup) && state.vitals < healAt && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22)) {"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9571,"output_tokens":1473,"cache_read_input_tokens":123904,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"857ff8dc-240e-4ed1-8d3e-4dc57131c003"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f534f47b-94d4-46d3-bf75-088fea896440-72","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"276→function stepCoda(sim, e, dt, beats) {\\n  const beatInBar = sim.beat.phase >= 0 ? ((sim.beat.count % 4) || 4) : 1;\\n  // Wind-up is the beat before downbeat: beat 4 telegraphs beat 1.\\n  const telegraph = (sim.beat.count % 4) === 0;\\n280→  e.windup = telegraph;\\n  for (const arm of e.arms || []) {\\n    arm.windup = telegraph;\\n    arm.need = telegraph ? 'laser' : 'wait';\\n    if (telegraph && arm.hp == null) arm.hp = 30;\\n  }\\n  for (const b of beats) {\\n    if (b.beatInBar === 1) {\\n      const armsNow = sim.entities.filter((a) => a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id);\\n      const blocked = armsNow.some((a) => a.hp <= 0);\\n290→      if (!blocked) {\\n        sim.hurt(6, 'downbeat');\\n        sim.spawn({ kind: 'scratch', site: e.site, at: [e.x, e.y - 0.1], rate: 0.4 });\\n        sim.events.push({ type: 'downbeat', id: e.id });\\n      }\\n      for (const a of armsNow) a.hp = 9;\\n    }\\n    if (b.beatInBar === 3) {\\n      sim.spawn({ kind: 'note', site: e.site, at: [e.x + 0.2, e.y], born: sim.beat.count, life: 5 });\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'cue', id: e.id });\\n300→    }\\n    if (b.bar % 4 === 0 && b.beatInBar === 1) {\\n      e.coreOpen = true;\\n      e.coreTimer = 3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (e.coreOpen) {\\n    e.coreTimer -= beats.length;\\n    if (e.coreTimer <= 0) e.coreOpen = false;\\n  }\\n310→  const arms = sim.entities.filter((a) => a.alive && a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id);\\n  e.arms = arms;\\n  if (e.hp <= 0 && !e.downed) {\\n    e.downed = true;\\n    e.grabbable = true;\\n    e.embedded = true;\\n    e.embed = 0.6;\\n    e.axis = 90;\\n    e.need = 'forceps';\\n  } else if (e.hp > 0) {\\n320→    e.need = e.coreOpen ? 'laser' : (telegraph ? 'laser' : 'wait');\\n    const ratio = e.hp / e.maxHp;\\n    if (!e.moved66 && ratio <= 0.66) {\\n      e.moved66 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    } else if (!e.moved33 && ratio <= 0.33) {\\n      e.moved33 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    }\\n  }\\n330→}\\n\\nfunction moveCoda(sim, e) {\\n  const sites = sim.op.sites.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const i = sites.indexOf(e.site);\\n  e.site = sites[(i + 1) % sites.length];\\n  for (const a of sim.entities) if (a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id) a.alive = false;\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x - 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x + 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.events.push({ type: 'codaMove', site: e.site });\\n340→}\\n\\nfunction stepBleeder(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (e.clamped) {\\n    e.need = 'wait';\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  e.need = 'clamp';\\n  const world = sim.drainScale();\\n  sim.hurt(1 * dt * world, 'bleed');\\n350→  if (!e.pool) {\\n    const pool = sim.spawn({ kind: 'pool', site: e.site, at: [e.x, e.y + 0.05], vol: 0.2, cap: 0.55 });\\n    e.pool = pool.id;\\n  }\\n  const pool = sim.entities.find((p) => p.id === e.pool && p.alive);\\n  if (pool) pool.vol += 0.35 * dt * world;\",\"content_concise\":\"276→function stepCoda(sim, e, dt, beats) {\\n  const beatInBar = sim.beat.phase >= 0 ? ((sim.beat.count % 4) || 4) : 1;\\n  // Wind-up is the beat before downbeat: beat 4 telegraphs beat 1.\\n  const telegraph = (sim.beat.count % 4) === 0;\\n280→  e.windup = telegraph;\\n  for (const arm of e.arms || []) {\\n    arm.windup = telegraph;\\n    arm.need = telegraph ? 'laser' : 'wait';\\n    if (telegraph && arm.hp == null) arm.hp = 30;\\n  }\\n  for (const b of beats) {\\n    if (b.beatInBar === 1) {\\n      const armsNow = sim.entities.filter((a) => a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id);\\n      const blocked = armsNow.some((a) => a.hp <= 0);\\n290→      if (!blocked) {\\n        sim.hurt(6, 'downbeat');\\n        sim.spawn({ kind: 'scratch', site: e.site, at: [e.x, e.y - 0.1], rate: 0.4 });\\n        sim.events.push({ type: 'downbeat', id: e.id });\\n      }\\n      for (const a of armsNow) a.hp = 9;\\n    }\\n    if (b.beatInBar === 3) {\\n      sim.spawn({ kind: 'note', site: e.site, at: [e.x + 0.2, e.y], born: sim.beat.count, life: 5 });\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'cue', id: e.id });\\n300→    }\\n    if (b.bar % 4 === 0 && b.beatInBar === 1) {\\n      e.coreOpen = true;\\n      e.coreTimer = 3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (e.coreOpen) {\\n    e.coreTimer -= beats.length;\\n    if (e.coreTimer <= 0) e.coreOpen = false;\\n  }\\n310→  const arms = sim.entities.filter((a) => a.alive && a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id);\\n  e.arms = arms;\\n  if (e.hp <= 0 && !e.downed) {\\n    e.downed = true;\\n    e.grabbable = true;\\n    e.embedded = true;\\n    e.embed = 0.6;\\n    e.axis = 90;\\n    e.need = 'forceps';\\n  } else if (e.hp > 0) {\\n320→    e.need = e.coreOpen ? 'laser' : (telegraph ? 'laser' : 'wait');\\n    const ratio = e.hp / e.maxHp;\\n    if (!e.moved66 && ratio <= 0.66) {\\n      e.moved66 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    } else if (!e.moved33 && ratio <= 0.33) {\\n      e.moved33 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    }\\n  }\\n330→}\\n\\nfunction moveCoda(sim, e) {\\n  const sites = sim.op.sites.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const i = sites.indexOf(e.site);\\n  e.site = sites[(i + 1) % sites.length];\\n  for (const a of sim.entities) if (a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id) a.alive = false;\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x - 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x + 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.events.push({ type: 'codaMove', site: e.site });\\n340→}\\n\\nfunction stepBleeder(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (e.clamped) {\\n    e.need = 'wait';\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  e.need = 'clamp';\\n  const world = sim.drainScale();\\n  sim.hurt(1 * dt * world, 'bleed');\\n350→  if (!e.pool) {\\n    const pool = sim.spawn({ kind: 'pool', site: e.site, at: [e.x, e.y + 0.05], vol: 0.2, cap: 0.55 });\\n    e.pool = pool.id;\\n  }\\n  const pool = sim.entities.find((p) => p.id === e.pool && p.alive);\\n  if (pool) pool.vol += 0.35 * dt * world;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/strains.js\",\"offset\":276,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"function stepCoda(sim, e, dt, beats) {\\n  const beatInBar = sim.beat.phase >= 0 ? ((sim.beat.count % 4) || 4) : 1;\\n  // Wind-up is the beat before downbeat: beat 4 telegraphs beat 1.\\n  const telegraph = (sim.beat.count % 4) === 0;\\n  e.windup = telegraph;\\n  for (const arm of e.arms || []) {\\n    arm.windup = telegraph;\\n    arm.need = telegraph ? 'laser' : 'wait';\\n    if (telegraph && arm.hp == null) arm.hp = 30;\\n  }\\n  for (const b of beats) {\\n    if (b.beatInBar === 1) {\\n      const armsNow = sim.entities.filter((a) => a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id);\\n      const blocked = armsNow.some((a) => a.hp <= 0);\\n      if (!blocked) {\\n        sim.hurt(6, 'downbeat');\\n        sim.spawn({ kind: 'scratch', site: e.site, at: [e.x, e.y - 0.1], rate: 0.4 });\\n        sim.events.push({ type: 'downbeat', id: e.id });\\n      }\\n      for (const a of armsNow) a.hp = 9;\\n    }\\n    if (b.beatInBar === 3) {\\n      sim.spawn({ kind: 'note', site: e.site, at: [e.x + 0.2, e.y], born: sim.beat.count, life: 5 });\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'cue', id: e.id });\\n    }\\n    if (b.bar % 4 === 0 && b.beatInBar === 1) {\\n      e.coreOpen = true;\\n      e.coreTimer = 3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (e.coreOpen) {\\n    e.coreTimer -= beats.length;\\n    if (e.coreTimer <= 0) e.coreOpen = false;\\n  }\\n  const arms = sim.entities.filter((a) => a.alive && a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id);\\n  e.arms = arms;\\n  if (e.hp <= 0 && !e.downed) {\\n    e.downed = true;\\n    e.grabbable = true;\\n    e.embedded = true;\\n    e.embed = 0.6;\\n    e.axis = 90;\\n    e.need = 'forceps';\\n  } else if (e.hp > 0) {\\n    e.need = e.coreOpen ? 'laser' : (telegraph ? 'laser' : 'wait');\\n    const ratio = e.hp / e.maxHp;\\n    if (!e.moved66 && ratio <= 0.66) {\\n      e.moved66 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    } else if (!e.moved33 && ratio <= 0.33) {\\n      e.moved33 = true;\\n      moveCoda(sim, e);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction moveCoda(sim, e) {\\n  const sites = sim.op.sites.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const i = sites.indexOf(e.site);\\n  e.site = sites[(i + 1) % sites.length];\\n  for (const a of sim.entities) if (a.kind === 'baton' && a.parent === e.id) a.alive = false;\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x - 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.spawn({ kind: 'baton', site: e.site, parent: e.id, at: [e.x + 0.28, e.y], hp: 9 });\\n  sim.events.push({ type: 'codaMove', site: e.site });\\n}\\n\\nfunction stepBleeder(sim, e, dt) {\\n  if (e.clamped) {\\n    e.need = 'wait';\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  e.need = 'clamp';\\n  const world = sim.drainScale();\\n  sim.hurt(1 * dt * world, 'bleed');\\n  if (!e.pool) {\\n    const pool = sim.spawn({ kind: 'pool', site: e.site, at: [e.x, e.y + 0.05], vol: 0.2, cap: 0.55 });\\n    e.pool = pool.id;\\n  }\\n  const pool = sim.entities.find((p) => p.id === e.pool && p.alive);\\n  if (pool) pool.vol += 0.35 * dt * world;\\n\",\"total_lines\":376}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f534f47b-94d4-46d3-bf75-088fea896440-73","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"  const swelling = state.entities.find((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\\n  const slow = (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0;\\n  // One early dose, while the swelling is still small, so the delayed hand can stay on the feeders.\\n  const preempt = !!(swelling && slow && (swelling.size || 0) < 0.22 && state.vitals < 70);\\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && slow ? 8 : 40);\\n  if (!coreNow && !(codaUp && windup) && (preempt || state.vitals < healAt) && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22 || preempt)) {\",\"new_string\":\"  const swelling = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0 ? 8 : 40);\\n  if (!coreNow && !(codaUp && windup) && state.vitals < healAt && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22)) {\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"  const swelling = state.entities.find((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\\n  const slow = (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0;\\n  // One early dose, while the swelling is still small, so the delayed hand can stay on the feeders.\\n  const preempt = !!(swelling && slow && (swelling.size || 0) < 0.22 && state.vitals < 70);\\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && slow ? 8 : 40);\\n  if (!coreNow && !(codaUp && windup) && (preempt || state.vitals < healAt) && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22 || preempt)) {\",\"old_line\":395,\"new_string\":\"  const swelling = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0 ? 8 : 40);\\n  if (!coreNow && !(codaUp && windup) && state.vitals < healAt && (me.syringeCd || 0) <= 0 && (!bleeding || state.vitals < 22)) {\",\"new_line\":395,\"context_before\":\"  if (codaUp && (me.composure || 0) >= 100 && state.vitals < 62 && !coreNow) {\\n    return { source: 'stick', x: 0, y: 0, use: 0, special: true, tool: me.tool };\\n  }\\n\",\"context_after\":\"    return syringeAt(me, IV.x, IV.y, tuning, opts);\\n  }\\n\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6e5a363a-b7b9-40b0-a90d-f0f1bc9517ed"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_292","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found in the stepCoda telegraph.\n\nThe telegraph logic correctly aligns with beatInBar. Windup occurs on beat 4, and the downbeat follows on beat 1. The bot must kill the baton during the windup beat before the next downbeat.\n\nAt 92 BPM, each beat lasts roughly 0.65 seconds. The bot must reach the target baton during beat 3, travel about 0.3 seconds to a baton 0.28 units away, and begin the windup beam on beat 4.\n\nThe 0.25-second delay means the laser command arrives 0.25 seconds into beat 4. That leaves about 0.4 seconds of beam, which is enough to kill a 9-HP baton.\n\nThe early-fire beam triggers when the bot is within 0.18 units. If it is already on the baton from beat 3, the laser turns on immediately when windup starts.\n\nHowever, the approach frames from beat 3 still occupy the first 0.25 seconds of beat 4. Those frames use zero laser power, so the actual hold begins only after that delay.\n\nThe bot should have enough laser time to kill the baton. It should also prioritize approach over hushing or syringing, and windup beam over notes. The downbeat still fires after seven beats. This suggests killing one baton may trigger the downbeat condition, which then resets both batons to full HP.\n\nThe downbeat resets every baton to full HP on beat 1 regardless of whether it was blocked. The bot must kill a baton each bar during the windup or it will take a downbeat. The sloppy bot misses most bars.\n\nCore opens every 16 bars for three beats when bar % 4 === 0 and beatInBar === 1.\n\nCore and baton priorities do not overlap. Core opens on beat 1, while the baton windup occurs on beat 4.\n\nDuring a core-open window, the bot prioritizes the core at 97 over the baton approach at 93. It stays on the core through beat 3 and beat 4. Because core remains open, it continues shooting the core instead of the baton. This causes the bot to miss the baton and trigger the downbeat.\n\nThe core timer decrements by the number of beats that crossed this frame. It starts at 3 and drops to 2 on the opening beat, then to 1 on the next, and closes when it reaches 0. The core therefore stays open for three beats total.\n\nThe core timer closes at the end of beat 3. The bot reads state after the step, so it sees the core is already closed when beat 3 begins. It can then approach the baton during beat 3 and fire the windup beam on beat 4.\n\nThe sloppy bot syringes immediately after hush because its health drops to about 35. It stays in that state through the downbeats and only fights once it heals to 50.\n\nThe sloppy bot's repeated syringing creates a death spiral. Each downbeat drops its health to about 46. It then leaves to heal again, misses the next baton, and takes another downbeat. This cycle continues until it dies.\n\nThe coda heal threshold of 46 was meant for the normal bot with higher vitals. The sloppy bot enters at only 35 and cannot hush.\n\nA fix is to avoid syringing during coda unless vitals are critically low while batons or core need attention. Another option is to syringe only on beat 2, when the bot is neither approaching nor winding up.\n\nA syringe trip takes about three beats, which overlaps the entire windup. Any healing during the coda therefore misses a baton. The bot should only syringe when vitals are critically low, or use hush instead, since hush does not move the tip.\n\nThe coda heal threshold should be 16 for delayed reactions and 46 for normal ones. The bot can survive the fight from its starting health of 35 by blocking downbeats, laser core, and using hush to slow the first seven seconds. This keeps the fight to roughly fifteen to twenty seconds.\n\nThe sloppy bot will stay on the boss until its health drops below 16. If the fight is won before that point, the syringe trip is safe. Blocking downbeats also limits how many scratches accumulate, since each scratch drains 0.4 health and notes burst for -2 if not cleared.\n\nNote damage is minor. Each note burst costs about 1.2 health, and over seven bars the total is roughly eight points. That is acceptable from a starting health of 35.\n\nThe healAt threshold will be updated to 16 for delayed reactions while the normal threshold stays at 46. The swelling healAt of 8 remains unchanged.\n\nThe bot must not stall on gift-checks during coda. Hush runs first, which resets composure to zero immediately.\n\nNext step is to implement these changes and run the sloppy coda test in one.mjs. If it fails, the conductor logic will be traced briefly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0c5aeca-0ed8-4119-9312-cdc16fa387ac-74","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  const swelling = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\n  const healAt = codaUp ? 46 : (swelling && (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0 ? 8 : 40);","new_string":"  const swelling = state.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'crescendo' && !e.exposed);\n  const slow = (opts.reactionDelay || 0) > 0;\n  // A delayed hand that leaves the conductor for the IV misses the baton and eats the downbeat.\n  const healAt = codaUp ? (slow ? 16 : 46) : (swelling && slow ? 8 : 40);"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2761,"output_tokens":2613,"cache_read_input_tokens":133376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"ee6961ca-4d9c-4588-9d71-3ba898d0ce29"}
