{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_299","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The faster beam killed the patient in recap at t=90.\n\nThe early laser fires before the conductor. It scorches heavily while approaching feeders. The burn rate is 2/s with long off-target time. Previously scorch survived for two seconds. Now the beam fires from within 0.14 distance while still traveling. If the path is long, offT exceeds 0.25 and burns continuously. Vitals hit zero at t=90.6. Recap started at t=79.6 with vitals of 42.6. That is lower than the previous 49.4.\n\nThe tighter beam is too aggressive for general use. Feeders need a beam that does not scorch. I will revert the general beam() delay branch to fire only when closer, and move the aggressive close behavior into a baton-specific function.\n\nThe previous beam fired at 0.18 distance and survived recap. The new one fires at 0.14 from further away and scorches too aggressively. I will restore the old delay branch and add a `beamBaton` function for the committed baton that parks tighter without a long pre-fire.\n\nThe `beamBaton` function will only pre-fire the laser once the distance drops to 0.06 or closer. It steers at 1.1 speed until that point, then holds at 0.8. The 0.25 second delay means the laser starts after the agent has already begun moving toward the target, so it should arrive centered.\n\nSimply holding at 0.06 distance overshoots the target by 0.14. The laser must instead be triggered when the predicted position after the delay equals the target. That requires predicting travel at current speed for 0.25 seconds. Near the target, steering slows the agent, so the exact timing is tricky.\n\nI rejected special-casing the laser use bit to avoid the 0.25 second reaction delay, since that would cheat the sloppy model. Instead, I will pre-fire the laser early when the aim is aligned and the baton can reach within the delay window. The scorch is acceptable for batons because the approach is only 0.28 units long. Feeders still need a gentler beam since their approach is much longer.\n\nThe baton beam will use a high close speed and hold only at d<=0.025. The laser fires only when d<0.07 to avoid scorching from far away. The 0.25 second delay means the laser starts late, which is the 2 HP shortfall. Setting the trigger at d<0.12 would start lasering while the agent is still roughly 0.12 units away.\n\nQueuing the laser use command at d=0.12 and continuing at 0.6 fu/s means the agent arrives at the target exactly when the delayed command executes. The laser turns on at arrival with no pre-fire scorch. The key is to queue the use command early enough so it fires precisely on arrival rather than 0.25 seconds after.\n\nThe 2 HP shortfall matches the wasted 0.25 seconds exactly: 0.25 s × 30 dps = 7.5 HP. The baton beam should trigger use 1 at d < 0.19, which covers the reaction delay and travel distance. The new `beamBaton` function will steer at 1.05 speed for distances over 0.2 and 0.7 otherwise.\n\nThe `beamBaton` function now arms the laser at d < 0.205, which is 0.03 plus the desired speed multiplied by the 0.25 second delay. At 0.7 fu/s the agent travels roughly 0.175 units during that delay, so the laser fires when the tip is near 0.025 distance. The scorch window begins exactly when the delayed command executes.\n\nThe scorch window is small because the laser turns on after most of the gap is closed. The general beam() will be restored to the version that cleared recap, which fires from 0.18 distance at speed 0.7. The faster approach only affects batons and does not impact feeders.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5be87239-951c-4e32-a22a-ec7dc7ca1fad-83","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  if (delay > 0) {\n    // Park inside the 0.05 hit radius. A slower close was stopping on the edge.\n    if (d > 0.1) return goTool(steer(me, e.x, e.y, d > 0.25 ? 1.05 : 0.75, tuning, opts), 'laser', d < 0.14 ? 1 : 0);\n    return hold('laser', 1);\n  }","new_string":"  if (delay > 0) {\n    // Fire on the way in. The queued beam then meets the target instead of starting late.\n    if (d > 0.18) return goTool(steer(me, e.x, e.y, 0.95, tuning, opts), 'laser', 0);\n    if (d > 0.04) return goTool(steer(me, e.x, e.y, 0.7, tuning, opts), 'laser', 1);\n    return hold('laser', 1);\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5be87239-951c-4e32-a22a-ec7dc7ca1fad-84","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"function approach(me, e, tuning, opts) {","new_string":"function beamBaton(me, e, tuning, opts) {\n  const d = Math.hypot(me.x - e.x, me.y - e.y);\n  const delay = opts.reactionDelay || 0;\n  if (d > 0.025) {\n    const want = d > 0.22 ? 1.05 : 0.72;\n    // Arm one reaction early so the beam is already on when the tip arrives.\n    const arm = 0.03 + want * delay;\n    return goTool(steer(me, e.x, e.y, want, tuning, opts), 'laser', d < arm ? 1 : 0);\n  }\n  return hold('laser', 1);\n}\n\nfunction approach(me, e, tuning, opts) {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5be87239-951c-4e32-a22a-ec7dc7ca1fad-85","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"      return actOn(state, me, state.beatInBar === 3 && !bat.windup ? 'approach' : 'beam', bat, mem, tuning, opts);","new_string":"      if (state.beatInBar === 3 && !bat.windup) return approach(me, bat, tuning, opts);\n      return beamBaton(me, bat, tuning, opts);"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":331,"output_tokens":2722,"cache_read_input_tokens":147712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"c9b53ec4-185d-46ce-8944-b18b30775846"}
