{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_304","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Downbeats dropped from 6 to 5 in a similar time. One bar was blocked. Down went to zero for a while then returned to one.\n\nThe first blocked downbeat succeeded. Later attempts failed. Coda HP dropped to 251. Core opened at the end. Vitals are falling. The IV is at position 1.01 when v<16. Damage was applied but not fatal.\n\nHush slowed beats to 0.25, giving about 2.6 seconds per beat and allowing the first downbeat block. After hush ended, full-speed beats returned to 0.65 seconds, which was too fast to finish. The strategy needs more laser time during normal speed. Composure only reached 40 at death, so another hush was impossible.\n\nPoise regenerates at roughly 3 per second. Reaching 100 for another hush would take about 33 seconds, which is too slow.\n\nAt full speed, the laser window is only 0.40 seconds after delay. That should be enough to kill a baton, but the bot is missing it. The laser is only on target for about 0.13 seconds, so most of the window is wasted. The bot is not positioning itself correctly during the downbeat.\n\nThe bot is switching batons every bar. It hits one at t=116.6 then moves to the other at t=118.1. The code resets mem.batonId on beats 1 and 2. It then re-picks the closest baton on beat 3. This causes the target to change each bar.\n\nThe bot probably cannot reach the baton and kill it during the same bar. If mem.batonId is never cleared, the tip stays on one baton permanently. The laser would then be ready for every downbeat, and the same baton could be killed every bar.\n\nThe bot wanders off to other jobs because mem.batonId is cleared on beats 1 and 2. Core opens on those same beats, so the bot misses them. The fix is to keep mem.batonId alive while core is closed, then return to that same baton once core closes. When core is open, the bot should leave for the core via candidates.\n\nThe baton target will be locked whenever the coda is up and the core is closed, not only on beats 3 and 4. Leaving for the core takes about two beats, but the bot can still reach the baton before the next windup. The code change is being drafted.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f4affd8f-4ae6-489b-867c-e60bdd38721a-90","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"slow && codaUp","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","-A":28}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1095,"output_tokens":1455,"cache_read_input_tokens":153856,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"809c5d3e-8d38-4470-a890-72cf5867f5f7"}
