 40.5\\nCORE 110.48 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.25 0.07 hp 240 v 40.5\\nCORE 110.50 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.27 0.07 hp 240 v 40.5\\nCORE 110.52 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.28 0.07 hp 240 v 40.5\\nCORE 110.53 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.29 0.07 hp 240 v 40.5\\nCORE 110.55 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.30 0.07 hp 240 v 40.5\\nCORE 110.57 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.31 0.08 hp 240 v 40.5\\nCORE 110.58 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.32 0.08 hp 240 v 40.5\\nCORE 110.60 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.32 0.08 hp 240 v 40.5\\nCORE 110.62 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.33 0.08 hp 240 v 40.4\\nCORE 110.63 seen false cmd laser 1.00 pos 0.34 0.08 hp 240 v 40.4\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/trace-boss.mjs | rg \\\"^CORE\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Dump the first core-open window frame by frame\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-0974c935-a911-4dd0-af1b-ac5cfd8fd8e7-108.log\",\"total_bytes\":7747}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"df66a958-749e-415c-b75a-ef4de6f32275"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_319","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The core was only open from t=108.\n\nThe core was open for 0.95 seconds total. Damage lasted only 0.15 seconds, dropping HP by 15. The laser overshot the core center and missed after 0.28 seconds, leaving HP stuck at 240 until the core closed.\n\nThe overshoot is caused by reaction delay. The steer command cannot stop the tip in time, so it passes through the core. The hold only activates within 0.03 of the center. To fix this, the robot should slow down proportionally to distance and delay so it stops at the target.\n\nThe existing slowdown logic is too weak. At a distance of 0.2, the code commands speed 0.57, but the robot still executes the previous high-speed command for 0.25 seconds. That covers 0.29 and overshoots past the target.\n\nA constant low speed is not enough. The 0.28-unit gap and 0.95-second window require sprinting, then braking early so the robot stops on the target.\n\nThe fix is to command a stop when the robot is within 0.32 units of the core. The queued stop will arrive after the 0.25-second delay, letting the tip settle on the target instead of overshooting.\n\nThe hold command at 0.32 units away closes the gap by exactly 0.29, stopping the tip at 0.03. The laser turns on with a delayed hold so it fires as the robot arrives. If the hold is issued too early while speed is low, the robot stops short and may miss the opening.\n\nThe 0.32-unit hold threshold is too aggressive. At the start of the opening the robot is already within 0.28 units of the core, so the first decision would be a hold. That would freeze the robot on the baton and prevent it from ever approaching the core. The hold must only trigger once the robot has already begun sprinting toward the target.\n\nThe revised plan uses a two-phase approach. When the robot is more than 0.12 units away, it sprints toward the core so it can queue a hold command before closing the gap. Once the distance drops to 0.12 or less, it holds with the laser on. The queued sprint frames will carry the robot past the 0.12 threshold, but the delayed hold will stop it inside the 0.05 hit radius.\n\nThe 0.12-unit hold threshold overshoots by 0.13 units. The correct brake point is approximately speed times delay, about 0.25 units away. The robot will sprint until it reaches 0.22 units, then queue a hold so the delayed stop lands inside the 0.05 radius.\n\nThe sprint threshold is now 0.2 units, with a speed of 1.05 and the laser held on. The next step is to test this and check the CORE dump HP to see if the robot stops short or overshoots. If the robot still misses, the threshold will be adjusted up or down. Time pressure means running just one iteration. The vitals drain about 1 point per second without downbeats, so each opening must deal roughly 80 damage to keep the fight alive.\n\nThe 16-beat spacing between openings means four attacks would last about 42 seconds. That would drain the robot's vitals to zero unless the damage is mostly scorch from firing the laser while missing the core. The log shows a steady drop of roughly 1.2 points per second during the opening, which matches the off-target laser burn rate.\n\nThe 1-point-per-second drain is not from scorching a dead baton. The beamBaton logic filters out targets with zero health, so it never attacks a dead baton. When both bats are dead, the robot falls through to other jobs instead of firing. This rules out the dead-baton theory for the vitals loss.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-02b3b43a-b619-48aa-b7d7-817618611adc-109","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"function beamCore(me, e, tuning, opts) {\n  const d = Math.hypot(me.x - e.x, me.y - e.y);\n  const delay = opts.reactionDelay || 0;\n  if (d > 0.03) {\n    const want = 1.15;\n    const arm = 0.04 + want * Math.max(delay, 0.05);\n    return goTool(steer(me, e.x, e.y, want, tuning, opts), 'laser', d < arm ? 1 : 0);\n  }\n  return hold('laser', 1);\n}","new_string":"function beamCore(me, e, tuning, opts) {\n  const d = Math.hypot(me.x - e.x, me.y - e.y);\n  const delay = opts.reactionDelay || 0;\n  if (delay > 0) {\n    // Brake early: the queued sprint otherwise carries the tip through the core.\n    if (d > 0.22) return goTool(steer(me, e.x, e.y, 1.05, tuning, opts), 'laser', 1);\n    return hold('laser', 1);\n  }\n  return beam(me, e, tuning, opts);\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3346,"output_tokens":2663,"cache_read_input_tokens":173824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"b72476b5-8858-4168-a308-647e11fe3fc0"}
