195 bar 3 tool laser use 0.00 pos -0.05 0.07 hp 197 open false bats 9,0 down 1 site heart\\nt 121.2 v 23.7 hush null comp 50 beat 198 bar 2 tool laser use 0.00 pos -0.07 0.07 hp 197 open false bats 0,9 down 1 site heart\\nt 122.7 v 21.0 hush null comp 55 beat 202 bar 2 tool laser use 1.00 pos 0.26 0.07 hp 197 open false bats 9,0 down 1 site heart\\nt 124.2 v 18.0 hush null comp 55 beat 205 bar 1 tool laser use 1.00 pos 0.05 0.01 hp 194 open true bats 9,9 down 1 site heart\\nt 125.7 v 11.1 hush null comp 55 beat 209 bar 1 tool laser use 1.00 pos 0.34 0.02 hp 168 open false bats 9,9 down 2 site lung\\nt 127.2 v 7.4 hush null comp 55 beat 212 bar 4 tool laser use 0.00 pos 0.95 0.20 hp 168 open false bats 9,8 down 2 site lung\\nEND vitals t 128.6 v 0.0 down 3\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/trace-boss.mjs | rg \\\"^PHASE|^t |^END\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Summarize conductor after core prelude\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-bbc743c2-eea7-4d8b-bbbf-20f2ebf9c3c1-118.log\",\"total_bytes\":3036}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"374002de-cb57-4b8a-a20f-fdcd7b356595"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_328","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Health dropped from 255 to 197 at timestamp 118.\n\nThe coda moved to the lung at 66% HP. The second opening caused 29 damage. The bot died at timestamp 128.6.\n\nVital loss was 13.9 in six seconds before the coda move, or about 2.3 per second. The move reset batons and forced a site switch while vitals were already low. That combination proved fatal.\n\nThe coda move triggered after about 30 seconds of damage. Entering the move at 30 vitals instead of 11 might have allowed survival. The rapid drop from 31.9 to 18.0 vitals between openings was driven by downbeats and drain.\n\nDrain after the downbeat reached 1.6 per second, far above the expected 0.46 from notes alone. Scratches and scorch could not account for the full loss rate. The death log shows eight spores and three scratches, suggesting spores were a major factor.\n\nSpores drain at 1.44 per second, matching the observed loss rate. Notes spawn on beat three and burst into spores after five beats. The bot camps batons and ignores notes, so they accumulate unchecked. Eight spores create a death spiral. Clearing notes is essential to survive.\n\nThe right baton sits only 0.08 units from the note, just outside the 0.05 hit radius, so laser targeting the baton misses the note entirely. The bot must instead grab or laser the note directly on beat 2 to prevent it from spawning a spore.\n\nBeat 2 is free because beat 4 is windup and beat 1 may be core. The bot will use beam() to kill the nearest note on beat 2 when the core is not immediately needed. This prevents the note from spawning a spore.\n\nExisting spores must also be cleared on beat 2. Preventing new ones alone would leave old spores draining vitals.\n\nThe bot should prioritize killing the nearest note first, then gel one spore. A note is roughly 0.2 units away, so travel plus laser takes about 0.45 seconds. That fits inside a 0.65-second beat if started immediately after the downbeat.\n\nBeat 1 may be free on non-core bars, but starting on beat 2 after the downbeat is safer.\n\nBaton resets occur on beat one, so early damage is needed there. Beat two is the dedicated note-clearing window, and it remains open even when the core prelude bar is active. If no note appears, a single spore gets gelled on beat two; eight existing spores would require faster cleanup. The spore count will be monitored to confirm whether notes stop bursting.\n\nThe note-cleaning check will be inserted after the core prelude guard but before the always-camp baton logic. It only triggers on beat two when the core is closed, and it targets notes on the current site sorted by distance.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-00566620-2a49-4b48-b617-e018b0dc066b-119","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  if (slow && codaUp && !coreNow) {","new_string":"  if (slow && codaUp && !coreNow && state.beatInBar === 2) {\n    const note = state.entities.filter((e) => e.kind === 'note' && e.site === me.site)\n      .sort((a, b) => Math.hypot(a.x - me.x, a.y - me.y) - Math.hypot(b.x - me.x, b.y - me.y))[0];\n    if (note) return beam(me, note, tuning, opts);\n  }\n\n  if (slow && codaUp && !coreNow) {"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1078,"output_tokens":2257,"cache_read_input_tokens":188032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"2ee6c01b-9996-4c21-bcb0-01d0c573bc6e"}
