{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_330","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The result is almost identical at t=128.\n\nNote cleanup had no effect. Eight spores remain. The beat 2 note beam does not prevent bursts. The note likely spawns too late or the laser misses it due to beam delay and travel time.\n\nThe note site matches the player. The beat 2 window is only 0.65 seconds, and prior baton commands likely fill the queue, leaving insufficient time to reach the note before beat 3.\n\nThe note never receives the required 0.25 seconds of laser. Pinch with forceps has a similar timing problem. Aiming between the notes is impossible because they are too close and lack overlap. Extending note life to 8 would give more clearance time, though this adds another deviation from the default.\n\nExtending note life is risky because the normal bot already clears these notes, so the score would not improve. A better approach is to make the sloppy bot interrupt baton camping whenever a note is older than two beats. The problem is that note age is not currently exported in the state. If every note triggers an urgent pop, the bot would miss downbeats and die faster.\n\nThe bot will pop notes on beats 1 and 2 of non-opening bars. This avoids missing downbeats while still giving about 1.3 seconds to reach the note.\n\nThe note sits near the right baton, so clearing it on beats 1 and 2 leaves enough time to kill the batons on beats 3 and 4. Beam will be used to laser the note.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-20b62824-53bd-44ab-a866-98bc483b17f3-121","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  if (slow && codaUp && !coreNow && state.beatInBar === 2) {","new_string":"  if (slow && codaUp && !coreNow && state.b