{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_339","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Seven notes were popped and seven burst. The two groups are equal.\n\nCleanup damage is still lethal. Seven bursts plus seven spores deal enough damage over thirty seconds. Five downbeats were missed, each costing three points and a scratch. Popping notes and blocking downbeats compete for the same beats. A single laser tip cannot fire both at once. Changing the note hit radius would require a simulation change.\n\nA single laser can clear both the baton and a nearby note. The search radius for notes is raised to 0.12, while the baton stays at 0.05. This lets one action hit both targets.\n\nThe baton is closer than the note, so it wins the hit. The note is not popped. Raising the search radius to 0.12 does not solve this.\n\nThe fix is to apply burn damage to every note within 0.12 of the laser tip, while still dealing direct damage to the closest target within 0.05. A tip on the baton at +0.28 reaches the note at +0.20, so the note pops without needing a larger search radius.\n\nThis change might affect the normal bot. It normally pops notes and batons separately. A note that would have burst later could pop earlier during a baton laser. The grade timing and score could shift.\n\nA bot-only alternative is to aim the laser at a point 0.04 toward the note while beaming the baton, placing the tip at 0.24 to hit both targets within 0.05. The normal coda score must be retested to confirm whether the change stays within the allowed band.\n\nOnly the right baton overlaps the note. The left baton sits 0.48 units away, so a tip aimed at it would miss the note entirely.\n\nThe bot will aim at the right baton, offset 0.04 toward the note, while keeping the left baton centered. When distances are similar, it will prefer the positive-x baton. The laser step still selects the nearest target.\n\nThe nearest target wins the laser hit, so a note just 0.001 closer than the baton would be skipped entirely. The cleanest fix is a simulation change: after selecting the primary target in stepLaser, also advance burn on any note within 0.1 units. This lets both targets receive damage without requiring a larger search radius.\n\nThe normal coda score will be checked after the change. If it stays at 37227, no further adjustment is needed. Otherwise the par will be recomputed while keeping the grade in band.\n\nThe implementation adds a side-burn loop inside stepLaser. It scans all notes within 0.1 units of the laser seat and advances their burn timers if they are not the primary hit target. This treats the beam as having a small width so nearby notes still burn even when the hot spot lands on a baton.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-edbae91e-2aec-4c05-be10-e57cc2c61e3d-132","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"  if (slow && codaEnt && !coreNow && (state.beatInBar === 2 || state.beatInBar === 3)) {\n    const note = state.entities.filter((e) => e.kind === 'note' && e.site === me.site)\n      .sort((a, b) => Math.hypot(a.x - me.x, a.y - me.y) - Math.hypot(b.x - me.x, b.y - me.y))[0];\n    if (note) return beam(me, note, tuning, opts);\n    if (state.beatInBar === 2 && codaEnt.site === me.site) {\n      return parkOn(me, { x: (codaEnt.x || 0) + 0.2, y: codaEnt.y || 0 }, tuning, opts);\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (slow && codaUp && !coreNow) {","new_string":"  if (slow && codaUp && !coreNow) {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-edbae91e-2aec-4c05-be10-e57cc2c61e3d-133","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js","old_string":"  seat.offT = 0;\n  if (hit.kind === 'note') {","new_string":"  seat.offT = 0;\n  // A beam on a baton also singes a cue sitting just beside it.\n  for (const note of sim.entities) {\n    if (!note.alive || note.kind !== 'note' || note.site !== seat.site || note === hit) continue;\n    if (dist(seat.x, seat.y, note.x, note.y) > 0.1) continue;\n    note.burnT = (note.burnT || 0) + dt;\n    if (note.burnT >= 0.25) popNote(sim, seat, note);\n  }\n  if (hit.kind === 'note') {"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":341,"output_tokens":2572,"cache_read_input_tokens":198272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"25c13f02-f51c-4bd9-9257-a0fc1621d58a"}
