,99,104,97,115,101,32,116,104,105,115,46,32,84,104,101,32,103,97,109,101,32,109,117,115,116,32,115,104,111,119,32,97,32,102,114,105,101,110,100,108,121,32,110,111,45,103,114,97,112,104,105,99,115,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,32,114,97,116,104,101,114,32,116,104,97,110,32,99,114,97,115,104,46,10,57,52,48,58,35,35,35,32,49,54,46,52,32,82,101,110,100,101,114,101,114,32,98,111,111,116,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":80,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":12,\"content\":\"## 1. The game\"},{\"line_number\":22,\"content\":\"### Pillars\"},{\"line_number\":30,\"content\":\"### What to keep from the source, and what to change\"},{\"line_number\":51,\"content\":\"### Originality rule\"},{\"line_number\":57,\"content\":\"## 2. World, cast and tone\"},{\"line_number\":59,\"content\":\"### 2.1 Setting\"},{\"line_number\":63,\"content\":\"### 2.2 Cast\"},{\"line_number\":75,\"content\":\"| **Dr. Cordelia Voss, \\\"the Maestro\\\"**, 71 | Villain. Founder of St. Alder's cardiac unit, officially dead since a fire 17 years ago | she | Silver hair to the waist, tailcoat over a surgical gown, baton | Breathy, with organ-like harmonics | Musical metaphors, unhurried |\"},{\"line_number\":77,\"content\":\"### 2.3 REQUIEM and the Conservatory\"},{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"### 2.4 Tone rules\"},{\"line_number\":111,\"content\":\"## 3. Core rules\"},{\"line_number\":115,\"content\":\"### 3.1 The field\"},{\"line_number\":121,\"content\":\"### 3.2 The instrument tip\"},{\"line_number\":127,\"content\":\"### 3.3 The beat clock\"},{\"line_number\":131,\"content\":\"### 3.4 Vitals, clock, misses\"},{\"line_number\":137,\"content\":\"### 3.5 Grades and score\"},{\"line_number\":150,\"content\":\"### 3.6 Ranks\"},{\"line_number\":162,\"content\":\"### 3.7 Composure and the two gifts\"},{\"line_number\":171,\"content\":\"### 3.8 Difficulty, checkpoints, assist\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"### 3.9 Consults\"},{\"line_number\":200,\"content\":\"## 4. Tools\"},{\"line_number\":242,\"content\":\"## 5. Strains\"},{\"line_number\":254,\"content\":\"| **Coda** | *coda (n.): the tail. The part that ends everything.* | Coda sign (circle and cross) as a core, two long baton arms on Rapier chains, a tailcoat membrane | **Beat 1 Downbeat:** ring telegraphs one beat early; the baton slams, -6 vitals and a scratch, unless you Laser the baton 0.5 s during the wind-up. **Beat 3 Cue:** spawns 2 notes or a small Adagio. **Every 4th bar a rest:** the core opens for 2 beats, Laser ×3. At 66% and 33% of HP 300 it moves to another site and its arms regrow; sever the arms to reach it. At 0: long Forceps pull (embed 0.6) | All of it | All the motifs in counterpoint, with the Dies Irae (§11) on organ |\"},{\"line_number\":258,\"content\":\"## 6. Operations\"},{\"line_number\":262,\"content\":\"### Op 1: Broken Glass (Chapter 1, Ren). Forearm. Timer 4:00, 72 bpm\"},{\"line_number\":272,\"content\":\"### Op 2: Growth Spurt (Chapter 1, Ren). Abdomen skin, then bowel. Timer 5:30, 76 bpm\"},{\"line_number\":279,\"content\":\"5. **The crash:** the tumor twitches on the tray. Vitals forced to 35, drain 3/s, a rupture wound (12 gates) opens, Composure is set to 100. Bea screams. The Hush prompt appears. The moment it fires: silence, ink wash, the first time. Suture the rupture.\"},{\"line_number\":282,\"content\":\"### Op 3: Adagio (Chapter 2, Ren). Liver. Timer 5:30, 80 bpm\"},{\"line_number\":291,\"content\":\"### Op 4: Staccato (Chapter 2, Ren). Bowel, then stomach. Timer 6:00, 84 bpm\"},{\"line_number\":300,\"content\":\"### Op 5: Legato (Chapter 3, **Ines**). Brain. Timer 6:00, 70 bpm. Consult\"},{\"line_number\":309,\"content\":\"### Op 6: Fermata (Chapter 3, Ren, with Ines on comms). Heart. Timer 7:00, 88 bpm. Consult\"},{\"line_number\":319,\"content\":\"### Op 7: Coda (Chapter 4, Ren and Ines). Heart, lung, aorta. Timer 9:30, 92 bpm. Consult\"},{\"line_number\":329,\"content\":\"### Last Patient (Chapter 4 ending, Ren). Heart. No HUD, no timer, can't fail\"},{\"line_number\":333,\"content\":\"### Grand Rounds (co-op, Free Play and hub rounds). Liver, bowel, heart. Timer 5:00\"},{\"line_number\":344,\"content\":\"## 7. Story\"},{\"line_number\":350,\"content\":\"| S0 | New game | OR 3 at night, empty | An envelope slides under the door. The monitor switches itself on and beeps, in time, with no patient. A silhouette lifts a baton. Title sting. 20 s |\"},{\"line_number\":382,\"content\":\"## 8. Controls and screens\"},{\"line_number\":384,\"content\":\"### 8.1 Operating controls\"},{\"line_number\":409,\"content\":\"### 8.2 Menu controls\"},{\"line_number\":413,\"content\":\"### 8.3 Prompts\"},{\"line_number\":423,\"content\":\"### 8.4 Ten-foot rules (tests can't judge these; check at 1920×1080)\"},{\"line_number\":430,\"content\":\"### 8.5 The operating HUD\"},{\"line_number\":444,\"content\":\"### 8.6 Screens\"},{\"line_number\":469,\"content\":\"## 9. Art direction\"},{\"line_number\":477,\"content\":\"### 9.1 Palette\"},{\"line_number\":488,\"content\":\"### 9.2 The operating view (values verified in the prototype)\"},{\"line_number\":497,\"content\":\"### 9.3 Sites\"},{\"line_number\":511,\"content\":\"| Aorta | One thick tube across the field | `#B52A3E` | Pulse wave down its length |\"},{\"line_number\":519,\"content\":\"### 9.4 Instruments\"},{\"line_number\":527,\"content\":\"### 9.5 Story staging\"},{\"line_number\":535,\"content\":\"### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\"},{\"line_number\":547,\"content\":\"### 9.7 Effects, and the juice list\"},{\"line_number\":565,\"content\":\"## 10. Animation\"},{\"line_number\":582,\"content\":\"## 11. Audio\"},{\"line_number\":590,\"content\":\"### Music\"},{\"line_number\":605,\"content\":\"### Sound effects (all procedural)\"},{\"line_number\":609,\"content\":\"### Voices\"},{\"line_number\":615,\"content\":\"| Ren | 190 Hz | Fast | Light, wavers when nervous |\"},{\"line_number\":628,\"content\":\"## 12. Attract mode\"},{\"line_number\":637,\"content\":\"## 13. Dev mode\"},{\"line_number\":689,\"content\":\"## 14. Multiplayer\"},{\"line_number\":693,\"content\":\"### 14.1 The decision\"},{\"line_number\":706,\"content\":\"### 14.2 Rules that apply in a session (`AIHub.active`)\"},{\"line_number\":714,\"content\":\"### 14.3 Authority and messages (the tested pattern)\"},{\"line_number\":767,\"content\":\"### 14.4 The card\"},{\"line_number\":771,\"content\":\"### 14.5 Couch co-op (on its own)\"},{\"line_number\":775,\"content\":\"### 14.6 Head tags\"},{\"line_number\":790,\"content\":\"### 14.7 What the hub's own check does\"},{\"line_number\":796,\"content\":\"## 15. Architecture\"},{\"line_number\":798,\"content\":\"### 15.1 Layout\"},{\"line_number\":821,\"content\":\"### 15.2 Sim and view\"},{\"line_number\":832,\"content\":\"### 15.3 Operations are data\"},{\"line_number\":863,\"content\":\"### 15.4 Observable state and test hooks\"},{\"line_number\":871,\"content\":\"### 15.5 The bot\"},{\"line_number\":877,\"content\":\"## 16. Verified recipes and traps\"},{\"line_number\":881,\"content\":\"### 16.1 Packages\"},{\"line_number\":891,\"content\":\"### 16.2 The build\"},{\"line_number\":926,\"content\":\"### 16.3 Browser flags for headless WebGPU\"},{\"line_number\":936,\"content\":\"- WebKit via Playwright runs WebGL2 fine. **Headless Firefox refused WebGL2 here** (\\\"AllowWebgl2:false\\\"), with the preferences we tried. Test with Chromium and WebKit, and don't chase this. The game must show a friendly no-graphics screen rather than crash.\"},{\"line_number\":940,\"content\":\"### 16.4 Renderer boot\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-80adcc15-707a-4955-9b52-ce2e89813abc-59","content":"{\"type\":\"ListDir\",\"Content\":{\"content\":\"- /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhig