10,32,116,104,101,115,101,32,114,117,110,115,44,32,115,111,32,97,108,108,111,119,32,102,111,114,32,105,116,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":10,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"| Star-drawing activation of the special was unreliable | The special is one reliable button (mirrored for the left thumb) |\"},{\"line_number\":567,\"content\":\"Use the native system as the base: `AnimationMixer`, `AnimationClip`, keyframe tracks built in code, and `SkinnedMesh` with `Bone` where bodies bend (toon skinning with a mixer is verified on both backends). Don't hand-roll transform tweens where a clip will do; use code only for continuous motion that follows sim values.\"},{\"line_number\":716,\"content\":\"The host's copy runs the only `Sim`, including Rapier. Everyone else renders snapshots. The host's view reads the sim directly; a client reads its decoded state, with entities and other seats interpolated 100 to 150 ms behind. **Your own tip is always local and instant**, and tool sounds and cosmetic trails start locally. Grades and results come from the host.\"},{\"line_number\":722,\"content\":\"| `i` | client → host | unreliable | 12/s | Tip x, y, tool, use, steady, site, sequence number |\"},{\"line_number\":724,\"content\":\"| `s` | host → all | unreliable | 10/s | Tick, beat, vitals, timer, tips, moving entities. **Max 1,100 bytes**: larger unreliable messages fragment and are lost whole |\"},{\"line_number\":725,\"content\":\"| `k` | host → all | reliable | 1/s | Full keyframe, under 16 KB |\"},{\"line_number\":728,\"content\":\"Keep each copy to at most 16 messages/s (the limit is 20, burst 40) with one token-bucket `send()` wrapper that sheds `s` and `i` first. **Any console line starting `[AIHub]` fails the hub's check**, including rate and size warnings, and `finish` called from a non-host. Drop snapshots older than the newest applied. Clients send `i` even when idle, as the harness needs traffic both ways.\"},{\"line_number\":810,\"content\":\"                        tools/*.js, strains/*.js, ops-runner.js, snapshot.js, bot.js\"},{\"line_number\":825,\"content\":\"The view reconciles meshes against `state` by entity id, and turns `events` into particles, paint, sounds and barks. It runs from `sim.state` in solo and couch play, and from decoded snapshots on a hub client: the same code either way. That single decision makes the Node tests, the bot, attract mode, the server copy and co-op all cheap.\"},{\"line_number\":879,\"content\":\"All run here on 2026-11-04: Chromium 153 under Playwright 1.63.0, Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. A skeleton with this stack (a toon scene, Rapier on the host, its own card, snapshots at 10/s with a 1/s keyframe, input at 12/s) passed the hub's harness on WebGPU at 2 players, 4 players on a bad network with one leaving, host-leave and server scenarios. The 4-player run also passed without WebGPU, on the WebGL2 fallback. The skeleton's scene was small: your real game will take longer in these runs, so allow for it.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2cfc6f22-57f0-4ae5-af17-636d87d06f34-67","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,56,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114