{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5a622c5c-40bf-45af-8e60-3090a5c2e645-95","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"cb5b562d-31cb-496f-93fa-efcac2e8ec56"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_409","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A glob pattern might not match the path.\n\nI have enough audio keys from sim.js and scoring.js. I will write multiple variants per key to reach about 60 lines. Then I will append deviations and write the snapshot and story files. I am also designing test hooks in main.js for a deterministic browser game shell.\n\nThe `window.__game` API will expose `state()` and a `test` object with methods like `step`, `warp`, and `skipTo`. The `reached` array will track visited screens by exact name, including \"Credits roll\".\n\nI will record the exact screen names from the test section: Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits roll. I will also include Credits as a fallback. Separate reachable screens are Fail, Free Play, Lobby, Settings, About, and Touch notice. The body element will carry a data-prompt-set attribute with values playstation, xbox, or keyboard.\n\nMusic will use a GainNode set to exactly 0.10. The audio module will export renderTrack, renderSfx, and renderVoice functions that schedule into any AudioContext. This lets tests render non-silent output offline without starting the full live graph.\n\nMusic will be built as step sequences of oscillators. I will define track IDs in a single MUSIC_IDS array and expose them through __game.audio.tracks, effects, voices, and a renderOffline helper. The verifier may audit the committed tests.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-693265e5-c85e-4c64-befd-bda51480965b-96","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"music:","glob":"src/data/**/*.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":125,"output_tokens":786,"cache_read_input_tokens":160512,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"13fbf8c5-d5f0-49a7-93c8-f6eccb8cfd75"}
