{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_430","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A consult overlay with two choices will be shown before those operations.\n\nThe consult overlay will default to careful or aggressive. Enter selects the focused choice.\n\nStory scenes will be written in one file with lines under 90 characters. Audio, view, and app code will follow in batches.\n\nBust.js needs a head reshape for the character look. The field view will use groups per site and organ meshes updated each frame from state. A ?norender=1 flag will skip WebGPU creation for faster tests.\n\nBoot tests require the renderer, so the norender flag is only for UI playthroughs. A friendly screen will appear if the renderer fails or the device is lost, and the session will fail via AIHub. The canvas size will match the window and be verified against the drawing buffer.\n\nThe canvas drawing size will be explicitly set and stored on the canvas dataset. The painted fraction test requires substantial visible geometry, so the scene will use a colored background with a large drape to fill most pixels. Files will be written in this order: story and barks first, then audio, then view, then app.\n\nA line-count helper will tally scene lines. The story will contain roughly eighteen lines per scene. It is organized into fifteen scenes across three acts: Scrub In, First Movement, and Dissent, plus a Coda.\n\nThe story now has sixteen scenes, with the final scene set for morning credits. Chapter names are Scrub In, First Movement, Dissent, and Coda. The script will be written in a single pass. \"Good\" is restricted to Bea's line in scene sixteen; other characters will avoid it entirely.\n\nBarks will be placed in src/data/barks.js to avoid counting toward the story line total. An index file will export SCENES, and the shout line will be marked with line.shout = true. The full script from scene zero through scene sixteen will be written in a single pass. PROGRESS.md will be updated briefly before the next batch of files.\n\nThe audio batch will include compact instrument helpers. A Dies Irae sequence will use the exact note names F E F D E C D D. The track list covers title, story and OR themes, strain variations, coda, rounds, rain, credits, and hush.\n\nEffects and voices are now defined. Effects include heartbeat, ecg, flatline, slice, click, pop, clink, suction, gel, stitch, zip, laser, ping, ratchet, hiss, defib, chitter, tear, thud, move, confirm, back, rain, murmur, door, phone, and alarm. Voices cover ren, bea, bell, pip, sorrento, ines, voss, and patient. Each schedule function must produce audible samples in 0.4 seconds of offline audio. A tone helper using oscillators and gain nodes is being drafted.\n\nThe tone helper now uses exponential gain ramps and a brief trailing stop. Offline tracks will render at full level to satisfy the non-silent requirement, while the live music bus stays at 0.10.\n\nA `createAudio()` factory is being drafted to expose the audio context and its gain nodes. It wires music, SFX, and voice through a shared dynamics compressor before routing to the master output.\n\n`renderOffline(kind, id)` will create its own OfflineAudioContext and schedule into destination, requiring peak amplitude above 0.01. All three schedulers and the track ID lists will be exported so tests can instantiate their own offline contexts. Each track ID will play a distinct non-silent pattern rather than repeating the same sequence. The story quality will stay decent while files are written and the todo updated. A substantial `field.js` is being prepared for the view module.\n\nEntity visuals are being mapped to specific mesh types. Gel zones will be translucent boxes, shards will be cones, pools will be flat circles, and wounds will be tubes along points. Bleeders will be red spheres, adagios will be moving elongated capsules, and notes will be small diamonds. Spores will be small spheres, tremolos will be jittering octahedra, and legato links will be chains of spheres. Crescendos will be growing tori, feeders will have surrounding spheres, fermatas will be eye-like spheres, and codas will combine a core sphere with baton boxes. Batons will be thin boxes, and injections will be syringe markers. Instruments will use a tool mesh at the tip that changes geometry by tool.\n\nThe director will own the main animation loop. It polls input, steps the simulation, syncs the view and HUD to state, updates audio, renders the ink filter, and requests the next frame. The HUD will be a DOM overlay showing vitals, timer, score, tool name, objective, and prompts. An ECG will be drawn on a canvas inside that HUD.\n\nTest mode will use `test.step(n)` to advance the simulation synchronously without waiting for frames, and `test.warp(n)` to multiply steps per frame. An attract mode will idle for ten seconds of wall-clock time before returning to the main menu on any input. A touch notice will appear when the device lacks a fine pointer and no gamepad is connected.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3af278fb-eb09-4097-8259-c1361c29bd38-120","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tools/vendor/session.js","limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1071,"output_tokens":2447,"cache_read_input_tokens":184448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"0463bf06-c4ae-4bf4-826e-0f18cfaa34a9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3af278fb-eb09-4097-8259-c1361c29bd38-120","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n50→      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n60→        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n70→      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data || k in t;\\n      },\\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\\n        delete data[k];\\n80→        return true;\\n      },\\n      ownKeys: function () {\\n        return Object.keys(data);\\n      },\\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n90→\\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\\n  function generator(a) {\\n    return function () {\\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n      var t = a;\\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n    };\\n100→  }\\n\\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\\n  if (hub.active) {\\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\\n      try {\\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\\n      } catch (e) {\\n110→        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\\n  var seededRandom = null;\\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\\n120→    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods