vitalsLow`: \\\"Pressure's falling, child. Stabilizer.\\\"\\n- `miss`: \\\"That was not on the line.\\\" / \\\"I saw that. God saw that.\\\"\\n- `streak`: \\\"…Adequate.\\\" (her highest praise)\\n- `bleeding`: \\\"You are swimming in it. Suction.\\\"\\n- `clampReminder`: \\\"Your clamps are still in. Would you like to sign for them?\\\"\\n- `timerLow`: \\\"Clock, child.\\\"\\n- `fail`: \\\"Call it. Then go and tell the family. No. You. That is the job.\\\"\\n\\n**Lint:** a test fails if any Bea line contains \\\"good\\\" outside S16. In Op 5 Bea still calls the barks and trades shots with Ines. In Op 6 Ines interjects over comms. In Op 7 every bark comes from Pip reading the notebook.\\n\\n380→---\\n\\n## 8. Controls and screens\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":344,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"## 7. Story\\n\\nDelivered as short scenes on a 3D stage (§9.5). Cross, Enter, Space or a click advances; hold to fast-forward; Triangle or Tab skips the scene, with a prompt on screen. Write 250 to 350 lines in total, in `src/data/story/`. The beats and must-have lines below are fixed; the rest is yours. Chapter names: **Scrub In**, **First Movement**, **Dissent**, **Coda**.\\n\\n| # | When | Where | Beats and must-have lines |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| S0 | New game | OR 3 at night, empty | An envelope slides under the door. The monitor switches itself on and beeps, in time, with no patient. A silhouette lifts a baton. Title sting. 20 s |\\n| S1 | Before Op 1 | Corridor, OR 3 | Flood traffic has stranded the attending. Ren is all there is. \\\"Thirty-one years in this room, child…\\\" \\\"Then simulate faster.\\\" |\\n| S2 | After Op 1 | Bell's office | Bell's praise and warning: \\\"the best hands… the worst nerves.\\\" |\\n| S3 | Before Op 2 | OR 3 gallery | The board watches. Routine tumor. Ren throws up, apologizes to the bucket |\\n| S4 | After Op 2 | OR 3, tray | Ren: \\\"Everything went quiet.\\\" Bea goes very still: \\\"I have heard of that once.\\\" The tumor twitches on the tray. In rhythm. Sting: \\\"Tumors do not keep time, child.\\\" |\\n| S5 | Before Op 3 | Pip's pathology lab | Envelope: sheet music addressed to \\\"The Surgeon on Call\\\". Pip plays it on a keyboard: \\\"It's a heartbeat…\\\" Ambulance: a cellist |\\n| S6 | After Op 3 | Ward Zero | Sorrento: \\\"Please wash your hands.\\\" REQUIEM, spelled out in full, with a straight face. The Conservatory. Ren is drafted |\\n| S7 | Before Op 4 | Ambulance bay, rain | Second score. A ferry captain |\\n| S8 | After Op 4 | OR 3 | The OR phone rings. A breathy voice: \\\"Bravo, Doctor. You play by ear. How delightful.\\\" Bea drops a full instrument tray. Sting |\\n| S9 | Before Op 5 | Ward Zero, then OR 3 | Ines arrives under guard. \\\"Your hands are excellent. Your diagnosis is a eulogy.\\\" She operates; you play her. First Consult |\\n| S10 | After Op 5 | Hospital roof, rain | Ines explains: she studied under the Maestro, who had the Hush. \\\"At the end, Doctor, you cannot turn it off.\\\" \\\"He waits for the silence. I do not wait.\\\" |\\n| S11 | Before Op 6 | Boardroom | Bell collapses mid-aphorism. The envelope's dedication: \\\"For Augustin, who signed.\\\" Consult |\\n| S12 | After Op 6 | Recovery room | Bell confesses: he signed Voss's death certificate after the Ward Zero fire, knowing she lived, and funded St. Alder with her research. \\\"Every heart I mended in this building, I mended with her money.\\\" Bea: \\\"I handed her the knife for eleven years. I would know that silence anywhere.\\\" |\\n| S13 | Before Op 7 | OR 3 | Final envelope. Pip plays it and slows down: \\\"I know this rhythm. It has a murmur. Ms. Okonkwo, you've got a—\\\" Bea, turning, mid-sentence: \\\"Forceps, ch—\\\" She falls. Ines: \\\"You cannot operate. You love her.\\\" Ren: \\\"Then you had better hand me the instruments.\\\" Pip, shaking, picks up the notebook. Consult |\\n| S14 | After Op 7 | Recovery, dawn | Bea wakes. Long silence. \\\"You held the forceps wrong, child.\\\" |\\n| S15 | Then | OR 3 gallery | Voss, conducting behind the glass, falters: her own heart is the first host. Sorrento: \\\"Let her go, Doctor.\\\" Ren: \\\"She's a patient.\\\" Leads into Last Patient |\\n| S16 | After | St. Alder, morning | Patients' cameos. Pip in student-nurse scrubs. Bea, with a cane, watches Ren close a wound and, for the only time in the game: **\\\"Good hands, child.\\\"** Credits roll over attract footage. Post-credits: a new envelope, marked *Opus 2* |\\n\\n**Bea's barks.** Write 60 or so short in-operation lines keyed by event, each with an expression: `start, nextPhase, toolHint(tool), idle, vitalsLow, vitalsCritical, miss, streak, bleeding, overflow, clampReminder, strainIntro(strain), hushReady, timerLow, success, fail`. A taste:\\n\\n- `vitalsLow`: \\\"Pressure's falling, child. Stabilizer.\\\"\\n- `miss`: \\\"That was not on the line.\\\" / \\\"I saw that. God saw that.\\\"\\n- `streak`: \\\"…Adequate.\\\" (her highest praise)\\n- `bleeding`: \\\"You are swimming in it. Suction.\\\"\\n- `clampReminder`: \\\"Your clamps are still in. Would you like to sign for them?\\\"\\n- `timerLow`: \\\"Clock, child.\\\"\\n- `fail`: \\\"Call it. Then go and tell the family. No. You. That is the job.\\\"\\n\\n**Lint:** a test fails if any Bea line contains \\\"good\\\" outside S16. In Op 5 Bea still calls the barks and trades shots with Ines. In Op 6 Ines interjects over comms. In Op 7 every bark comes from Pip reading the notebook.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Controls and screens\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1218}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"7ae530d8-04af-45df-adb7-17126fda2a08"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_448","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The S2 must-have line is \"the best hands… the worst nerves.\" The summary used the full sentence without the ellipsis.\n\nI'll grep the story file for must-have phrases. Then I'll write the code. I need to fix S14 in scenes.js. I may add the ellipsis phrase to S2. I also need to create src/data/barks.js, src/data/cast.js, and src/data/sites.js.\n\nThe remaining files span audio, view, input, UI, app logic, and tests. I will write them all now.\n\nI also need to create tests/hub/*.mjs, docs/AUTHORING.md, exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, and the PLAN.md deviations section. The title string \"Alive in Common Time\" must appear only in identity.js; the description must not contain it. Tests will search src/ for tuning IDs, TODOs, Math.random in simulations, and the title string.\n\nThe build template needs a boot div so \"Scrubbing in…\" appears before the module script. The hub harness sets body[data-complete=true], not the game itself. I must confirm window.__game exists before trusting the page.\n\nTouch detection will use matchMedia to detect coarse pointers, matching Playwright device profiles. The attract timer will use wall-clock time and exit on any input after ten seconds of idle. Save data will persist in localStorage so progress survives reloads. Dev mode will be triggered from the pause state.\n\nDev tools will include buttons for sim methods and sliders that mutate tuning. Reset will call resetTuning.\n\nThe test suite must click every dev tool once without error. These include jump to operation and phase, unlock everything, play story scene, complete objective or phase, win or fail, force rank, god mode, freeze timer, infinite composure and clamps, trigger bleeder or spawn strain or arrest or fortissimo or hush or sforzando, time scale, single step, auto surgeon, overlays, and render toggles.\n\nCouch mode will use two pads in one Sim. Each pad maps to a seat, and both seats score independently through sim.seats.\n\nStandard gamepad input mapping is now defined. Right stick axes control aim, left stick axes control tool flick, and buttons map to use, steady, alt, syringe, special, site navigation, pause, and menu. The tool wheel activates via left-stick flick with an 8-sector deflection threshold.\n\nTool wheel angles will use atan2(stickX, -stickY) with 0° at north and clockwise positive. Eight sectors map to scalpel, forceps, suction, gel, suture, laser, scanner, and clamp. Switching requires a deflection past 0.6 and sector stability. Keyboard 1–8 will select tools. WASD or arrows may move the tip when no mouse input is recent.\n\nMouse input will be absolute. The canvas covers the drape, so pointer coordinates map to field space with the center of the canvas at field (0, 0). A simple linear scale converts clientX to fieldX.\n\nMouse Y maps to field space with a vertical flip. The tip-speed test will use either a pad stub or real polling. A full right-stick input for one second must yield tipSpeed within five percent. Aim assist may pull the tip within 0.12 of a guide, so exact speed is not guaranteed. Operation 1’s clean phase uses only the gel zone, which has no guide.\n\nA full right-stick input for one second should move the tip from -1.05 to 0.85, within the x clamp of [-1.55, 1.9]. The browser test will inject this via window.__pads[0].axes or test.input, and test.step will loop over n steps so the game polls the same input each frame.\n\ntest.step will read pad inputs into the simulation and call sim.step each frame. A test.input override on seat 0 takes precedence. R2 analog input maps directly to use value. Left-stick flick deflection above 0.6 triggers tool selection.\n\nThe tool-wheel angles are now fully mapped: northeast is forceps, east is suction, and so on clockwise. Keyboard keys 1 through 8 select scalpel, forceps, suction, gel, suture, laser, scanner, and clamp in that order. Prompts will be gated by a data-prompt-set attribute on the html element, switching between playstation, xbox, keyboard, or mouse. The settings glyph option can force the prompt set to Xbox even when the last device was a pad.\n\nThe settings glyph option only overrides pad prompts to Xbox; keyboard and mouse prompts remain unchanged. Music gain will be exactly 0.10, exposed through state().musicGain. Offline audio scheduling functions are being prepared for browser-only tests, since Node 24 may not support OfflineAudioContext.\n\nThe built page will expose `__game.audio.renderOffline(kind, id)` for browser tests to measure audio peaks. The full track list is now defined: title, story-calm, story-comic, story-tense, story-sad, story-villain, or-calm, or-tense, strain-adagio, strain-staccato, strain-legato, strain-fermata, coda, rounds, rain, credits, and hush.\n\nThe SFX list covers heartbeat, ecg, flatline, scalpel, forceps, pop, glass, suction, gel, stitch, thread, laser, scanner, clamp, syringe, defib, chitter, screech, scratch, stamp, ui-move, ui-confirm, ui-back, rain, murmur, door, phone, and alarm. Voice actors are ren, bea, bell, pip, sorrento, ines, voss, and patient. No audio files are referenced in source code. Fonts will be embedded as woff2 data URLs via esbuild. The hub client script must not contain the banner string `/*! aihub-session`.\n\nSession.js will send absolute input frames as `i` messages and discrete actions as `a` messages. The host applies local input directly, while clients transmit both. Absolute coordinates carry a `source: 'abs'` flag. Discrete actions merge into the command as rising flags. A token bucket limits traffic to 16 per second, dropping `s` and `i` first when overloaded. The hub allows a burst of 40 over 20 seconds. Input rate is capped at 12 per second, status at 10, and keyboard at 1 per second.\n\nThe token bucket will use a two-tier `allow` function: priority 0 drops `s` and `i` first, while priority 1 keeps `a`, `k`, and `e`. JSON string length will be checked to keep messages under caps. The host simulation will tick on a `setTimeout` instead of `requestAnimationFrame`; the view can still render separately.\n\nAIHub.ready() will be called immediately after listener registration, before renderer initialization. The server path skips the view entirely and calls ready right away. If the renderer fails, AIHub.fail is invoked.\n\nThe card event displays the card without auto-answering. The countdown uses AIHub.time() and starts once the value reaches zero or below. The host sends the finish signal only once. Button 8 held suppresses options. Session pause is settings-only; the simulation continues running. No browser APIs such as alert, confirm, prompt, window.open, WebSocket, EventSource, or RTCPeerConnection are used. Graphics failure shows a friendly screen and calls AIHub.fail if a session exists. The title text appears in the DOM on a colored background before WebGL paints.\n\nStandalone boot shows \"Scrubbing in…\" on a teal background before the DOM title appears. The `?test=1` flag exposes the test API. `?norender=1` skips WebGPU initialization for fast tests while keeping the DOM, and boot tests must still verify WebGPU availability. `?webgl=1` forces WebGL mode.\n\nCanvas drawing size must match the requested width and height and fill the window. Progress is saved to localStorage under the key 'aict-save-v1'. The difficulty question appears once in Bea's voice after New Game is selected, before the first chart, using three large buttons for Intern, Resident, and Attending.\n\nThe main menu will hold five items: Story, Free Play, Grand Rounds, Settings, and About. The Story entry opens a sub-screen with Continue and New Game; Continue is disabled when no save exists and New Game is focused. After ten seconds of idle time on the title screen, an attract demo begins that cycles through at least three different operations.\n\nThe attract demo will be driven by a bot that cycles through operations every eight seconds. It enables lockVitals, freezeTimer, and infiniteComposure to showcase each operation visibly. The loop records attractOps in state so tests can verify three distinct operations. A DOM \"DEMO\" label and \"Press any button\" prompt appear during the loop. Any input returns to the main menu without saving.\n\nAfter S16 the Credits screen appears and is skippable. The \"Credits roll\" entry is pushed to reached. Tests can trigger failure via dev mode or by calling sim.hurt on __game.sim, since test.kill is not used. Vitals reaching zero also causes a fail and displays the Fail screen.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a28964fa-3f0b-4512-b51b-81b0328aa40d-29","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"best hands|Good hands|REQUIEM|Recombinant|Forceps, ch|Let her go|metronome|common time","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/story/scenes.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a28964fa-3f0b-4512-b51b-81b0328aa40d-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/snapshot.js","limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a28964fa-3f0b-4512-b51b-81b0328aa40d-31","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"inDrape","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/field.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8530,"output_tokens":4611,"cache_read_input_tokens":85760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e1bd41e5-242d-492c-8846-89689c915dee"}
