{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_451","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test for the last idle patient should cap steps.\n\nThe last patient operation should not fail. I will step for a few seconds and assert it remains active.\n\n120 seconds of simulation should be enough to prove the last idle patient stays active. Other operations fail at their timers within that window.\n\nThe full test suite will run for roughly five minutes. A combined test will measure the largest snapshot during four-seat grand rounds to avoid double-playing. The planned structure covers normal, sloppy easy, and capped idle runs for every operation plus four normal grand rounds.\n\nAll operations will be tested in sloppy mode. They will run sequentially in one Node process.\n\nThe test must use play() and avoid calling botInput outside it.\n\nBrowser tests will boot with WebGPU disabled. The script will navigate through the title, story, difficulty, and chart screens using keyboard input.\n\nWarp 120 should compress each operation to roughly one or two seconds. Headless browsers may throttle animation frames, so the test might step manually in a loop instead.\n\nThe director will step during animation frames when warp is high and the bot is active. It will fall back to setTimeout if the document is hidden. The browser test will loop through screens, calling test.step(8000) directly on operation or attract-wait screens, and pressing keys otherwise.\n\nThe browser test will step in chunks of 3000 frames to stay within Playwright's timeout. It will combine warp with direct test.step calls during operations, using keyboard inputs only for menus.\n\ntest.step will advance the simulation synchronously but must also pump the shell so screen transitions occur. The director's afterStep callback handles the switch to the report screen once sim.over is reached.\n\nI will read the harness to understand its protocol expectations, including hello, ready, card, answer, send, and finish messages.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-017cb7f5-d0bf-4ce1-bd88-2a15d19149f8-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"finish|ready|standings|__hubCheck|hello","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site","glob":"*.js","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-017cb7f5-d0bf-4ce1-bd88-2a15d19149f8-37","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/story/scenes.js","offset":300,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2862,"output_tokens":1602,"cache_read_input_tokens":103168,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"1e6c3382-14aa-428f-9ebc-0f754e75b461"}
