{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_452","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plan is ready. I will now write the files.\n\nI'll patch the story line first. Then I'll write the remaining files in batches. Director.js will be split into ui/screens.js to stay under 800 lines. I've assigned warm colors to each cast member and prepared SVG glyph strings for buttons.\n\nInput polling will read gamepads, keyboard state, and mouse position for each seat. Seat 0 uses keyboard and mouse; seats 1 through 3 use pads. The lobby claims seat 0 for keyboard confirmers. During operations, each seat receives its own device frame. Test input overrides seat 0 until cleared.\n\nWASD will act as an aim stick when keyboard is the active device and no recent mouse movement exists. If both devices are present, the last one used wins for seat 0. During test steps, pad axes will be polled directly to verify full right stick input.\n\nBot input will be skipped when no override is active. Aim assist is disabled during stick tests. The R2 test will set button 7 to 0.62 and verify the seat use value.\n\nI'll verify that tools set seat.use from cmd.use. If not, the test will fail and I'll fix it.\n\nThe left stick flick test will move the stick east to trigger suction. Keys 1 through 8 will dispatch keyboard digits so the tool changes immediately on keydown. The mouse absolute test will move the cursor to a canvas coordinate and step to place the tip near the field point.\n\nMenu items will receive data-action attributes and a click handler so hover moves focus and clicks activate the target. During attract mode, the operation ID will cycle every 2.5 seconds to display three different operations within about eight seconds of wall-clock time. The touch test will use Playwright devices for a Pixel 7 and an iPhone 15.\n\nThe touch test will launch a browser with the Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 Playwright devices. It will verify the controller prompt, tap Settings, wait for attract mode to start after ten seconds, and confirm that a pad press leaves a notice. An init script will simulate a pressed pad button on mobile so the game detects it. I will check whether `any-pointer` is false on mobile during testing.\n\nThe save test will start a new game, reach an operation or finish one, reload the page, and confirm that a continue option appears because localStorage persists.\n\nThe dev mode test will open the pause menu, enter Dev Mode, and cycle through each tool. It will adjust the tipSpeed slider, step the simulation, verify the tuning change, then reset. Because the Dev Mode button is only reachable from Pause, the test must first reach an operation using test.skipTo.\n\nThe couch test will launch a Grand Rounds lobby with two pads. Both players press Cross to start, then move their sticks. The simulation will run bots for both seats so each accumulates a score.\n\nThe graphics boot test will launch Chromium with GPU flags, wait for the WebGPU render backend, confirm no console errors, and verify the screenshot is not blank.\n\nThe graphics boot test will verify the canvas drawing size matches the requested dimensions and is substantially filled. A blank PNG is smaller than a real screenshot, so the test will check that canvas pixels are not all one color. The first frame may take several seconds with software WebGPU, so a sixty-second timeout is set.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d67fc868-243f-4484-bd9a-661b34de0662-38","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^## ","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3323,"output_tokens":1864,"cache_read_input_tokens":105984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d73b784d-70c5-4de8-937d-4830ff3e6943"}
