:[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":332,\"content\":\"    if (a.event === 'arrest') this.beginArrest(a);\"},{\"line_number\":333,\"content\":\"    if (a.event === 'fortissimo') this.events.push({ type: 'fortissimo' });\"},{\"line_number\":348,\"content\":\"  beginArrest(a) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"55cbcacb-871b-4d29-b94c-7531150b2328"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_465","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `beginArrest` method exists and can be called with an empty object.\n\nHush and sforzando will set composure to 100 before triggering their effects. Time scale will use `cheats.timeScale`. A devPaused flag will let the shell pause the simulation except for single-step and test.step. The auto surgeon bot will be enabled. Dev overlays will use `game.devView` flags. Render toggles will adjust ink uniforms when a view exists. Sliders will use range inputs to set `sim.tuning` values and show them, with reset buttons calling `resetTuning`.\n\nSliders will mutate a tuning object that carries over to the next simulation when dev opens from a story pause. Every tuning ID is already read in src/, so test checks remain valid. The renderer will be capable but not excessive. A simple two-bone tube skinned mesh will animate adagio, driven by an AnimationMixer. Rapier cosmetic effects will spawn dynamic balls on pop events.\n\nRAPIER will be initialized once in main and shared with the view. The simulation also calls RAPIER.init, but double initialization is harmless. Norender tests will skip renderer and rapier setup entirely. Node tests use physics:false, while browser operations keep physics:true.\n\nRAPIER.init will run before the first operation so the title screen loads quickly. The renderer initializes on boot because tests check for rendering. Canvas size will use clientWidth and clientHeight with a pixel ratio capped at 2. The drawing buffer will match the requested size.\n\nThe canvas width will equal the requested size multiplied by the device pixel ratio. Tests will verify this by reading pixels from the canvas.\n\nWebGPU canvases cannot be read via 2D getImageData. Playwright screenshots will verify rendering instead. The launch check combines a screenshot with a readPixels attempt. A blank buffer from a started browser is a failure to fix, but a blank readback from a browser that never launched is not.\n\nThe launch script will decode the screenshot PNG to confirm it contains non-background colors. A `game.view.painted` flag will be set after the first successful render, and the script will wait for that flag before taking the screenshot. The title DOM ensures the page is not blank before the GPU frame, but the 3D view must also be substantially filled. If the device is lost, a message will appear.\n\nA friendly no-graphics screen will display a message and a button when WebGPU or WebGL2 is unavailable, with no navigation. The FXAA import path from three/addons/tsl/display/FXAANode.js will be verified at build time. A build plugin will enforce exact three.js resolution. CSS fonts will use woff2 data URLs via esbuild.\n\nThe Bangers font path in src/ui/ui.css resolves correctly via esbuild. The about.json screen will display full content. The exit-interview will be drafted now and updated with real test results afterward, including counts for issues caught, critical bugs, and the most and least helpful tests.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f457e6ca-c7b3-40f0-aa7b-849c6ca03926-56","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/scoring.js","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f457e6ca-c7b3-40f0-aa7b-849c6ca03926-57","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/story/scenes.js","offset":45,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":463,"output_tokens":1438,"cache_read_input_tokens":131328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"50203d89-ab55-4562-a471-084d2de1b52d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f457e6ca-c7b3-40f0-aa7b-849c6ca03926-56","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→export const GRADE_POINTS = Object.freeze({ FLAWLESS: 300, CLEAN: 150, ROUGH: 50, MISS: -100 });\\nexport const GRADE_POISE = Object.freeze({ FLAWLESS: 10, CLEAN: 5, ROUGH: 0, MISS: -10 });\\n\\nconst RANK_ROWS = Object.freeze([\\n  ['S', 0.9, 'Chief of Surgery'],\\n  ['A', 0.75, 'Attending'],\\n  ['B', 0.55, 'Resident'],\\n  ['C', 0.35, 'Intern'],\\n  ['D', -Infinity, 'Malpractice Suit Pending'],\\n10→]);\\n\\nexport function comboMult(combo) {\\n  return Math.min(2, 1 + 0.05 * combo);\\n}\\n\\nexport function rankFor(score, par, cap) {\\n  const ratio = par > 0 ? score / par : (score > 0 ? 1 : 0);\\n  let idx = RANK_ROWS.length - 1;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < RANK_ROWS.length; i++) {\\n20→    if (ratio >= RANK_ROWS[i][1]) { idx = i; break; }\\n  }\\n  if (cap) {\\n    const capIdx = RANK_ROWS.findIndex((r) => r[0] === cap);\\n    if (capIdx >= 0 && idx < capIdx) idx = capIdx;\\n  }\\n  const row = RANK_ROWS[idx];\\n  return { id: row[0], title: row[2], ratio };\\n}\\n\\n30→export function award(sim, seat, grade, x, y, why) {\\n  const base = GRADE_POINTS[grade];\\n  const mult = comboMult(seat.combo);\\n  const points = Math.round(base * mult * sim.mods.score);\\n  sim.score += points;\\n  seat.score += points;\\n  seat.graded = (seat.graded || 0) + 1;\\n  if (grade === 'FLAWLESS' || grade === 'CLEAN') {\\n    seat.clean = (seat.clean || 0) + 1;\\n    seat.combo += 1;\\n40→    if (seat.combo > seat.bestCombo) seat.bestCombo = seat.combo;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→export const GRADE_POINTS = Object.freeze({ FLAWLESS: 300, CLEAN: 150, ROUGH: 50, MISS: -100 });\\nexport const GRADE_POISE = Object.freeze({ FLAWLESS: 10, CLEAN: 5, ROUGH: 0, MISS: -10 });\\n\\nconst RANK_ROWS = Object.freeze([\\n  ['S', 0.9, 'Chief of Surgery'],\\n  ['A', 0.75, 'Attending'],\\n  ['B', 0.55, 'Resident'],\\n  ['C', 0.35, 'Intern'],\\n  ['D', -Infinity, 'Malpractice Suit Pending'],\\n10→]);\\n\\nexport function comboMult(combo) {\\n  return Math.min(2, 1 + 0.05 * combo);\\n}\\n\\nexport function rankFor(score, par, cap) {\\n  const ratio = par > 0 ? score / par : (score > 0 ? 1 : 0);\\n  let idx = RANK_ROWS.length - 1;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < RANK_ROWS.length; i++) {\\n20→    if (ratio >= RANK_ROWS[i][1]) { idx = i; break; }\\n  }\\n  if (cap) {\\n    const capIdx = RANK_ROWS.findIndex((r) => r[0] === cap);\\n    if (capIdx >= 0 && idx < capIdx) idx = capIdx;\\n  }\\n  const row = RANK_ROWS[idx];\\n  return { id: row[0], title: row[2], ratio };\\n}\\n\\n30→export function award(sim, seat, grade, x, y, why) {\\n  const base = GRADE_POINTS[grade];\\n  const mult = comboMult(seat.combo);\\n  const points = Math.round(base * mult * sim.mods.score);\\n  sim.score += points;\\n  seat.score += points;\\n  seat.graded = (seat.graded || 0) + 1;\\n  if (grade === 'FLAWLESS' || grade === 'CLEAN') {\\n    seat.clean = (seat.clean || 0) + 1;\\n    seat.combo += 1;\\n40→    if (seat.combo > seat.bestCombo) seat.bestCombo = seat.combo;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/scoring.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"export const GRADE_POINTS = Object.freeze({ FLAWLESS: 300, CLEAN: 150, ROUGH: 50, MISS: -100 });\\nexport const GRADE_POISE = Object.freeze({ FLAWLESS: 10, CLEAN: 5, ROUGH: 0, MISS: -10 });\\n\\nconst RANK_ROWS = Object.freeze([\\n  ['S', 0.9, 'Chief of Surgery'],\\n  ['A', 0.75, 'Attending'],\\n  ['B', 0.55, 'Resident'],\\n  ['C', 0.35, 'Intern'],\\n  ['D', -Infinity, 'Malpractice Suit Pending'],\\n]);\\n\\nexport function comboMult(combo) {\\n  return Math.min(2, 1 + 0.05 * combo);\\n}\\n\\nexport function rankFor(score, par, cap) {\\n  const ratio = par > 0 ? score / par : (score > 0 ? 1 : 0);\\n  let idx = RANK_ROWS.length - 1;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < RANK_ROWS.length; i++) {\\n    if (ratio >= RANK_ROWS[i][1]) { idx = i; break; }\\n  }\\n  if (cap) {\\n    const capIdx = RANK_ROWS.findIndex((r) => r[0] === cap);\\n    if (capIdx >= 0 && idx < capIdx) idx = capIdx;\\n  }\\n  const row = RANK_ROWS[idx];\\n  return { id: row[0], title: row[2], ratio };\\n}\\n\\nexport function award(sim, seat, grade, x, y, why) {\\n  const base = GRADE_POINTS[grade];\\n  const mult = comboMult(seat.combo);\\n  const points = Math.round(base * mult * sim.mods.score);\\n  sim.score += points;\\n  seat.score += points;\\n  seat.graded = (seat.graded || 0) + 1;\\n  if (grade === 'FLAWLESS' || grade === 'CLEAN') {\\n    seat.clean = (seat.clean || 0) + 1;\\n    seat.combo += 1;\\n    if (seat.combo > seat.bestCombo) seat.bestCombo = seat.combo;\\n\",\"total_lines\":56}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f457e6ca-c7b3-40f0-aa7b-849c6ca03926-57","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"45→      line('bea', 'stern', 'Gloves. Lamp. Eyes on me until I tell you to look at the wound.'),\\n      line('ren', 'steady', 'Yes, ma\\\\'am.'),\\n      line('bea', 'quiet', 'Child. Breathe on the count I give you. Not yours.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n50→  {\\n    id: 'S2', chapter: 'Scrub In', where: \\\"Bell's office\\\", set: 'office', music: 'story-calm',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('bell', 'pleased', 'You have the best hands I have ever seen, Doctor, and the worst nerves.'),\\n      line('ren', 'shy', 'I counted out loud. Bea said that was allowed.'),\\n      line('bell', 'warm', 'Surgery is the art of being wrong slowly enough to fix it.'),\\n      line('bea', 'dry', 'He was wrong twice and said so. I am writing that down as a miracle.'),\\n      line('ren', 'quiet', 'The driver asked if he could keep the glass. I said no.'),\\n      line('bell', 'amused', 'A correct answer. Frame it.'),\\n      line('bea', 'stern', 'Do not frame it. Do not get fond of yourself.'),\\n60→      line('bell', 'serious', 'There is a second case stacking. A boy, a belly, a thing that should not be growing.'),\\n      line('ren', 'nervous', 'Tonight?'),\\n      line('bell', 'calm', 'The flood took the night shift. You are the night shift.'),\\n      line('bea', 'firm', 'He will eat first. Then he will throw up. Then he will scrub.'),\\n      line('ren', 'small', 'I do not always throw up.'),\",\"content_concise\":\"45→      line('bea', 'stern', 'Gloves. Lamp. Eyes on me until I tell you to look at the wound.'),\\n      line('ren', 'steady', 'Yes, ma\\\\'am.'),\\n      line('bea', 'quiet', 'Child. Breathe on the count I give you. Not yours.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n50→  {\\n    id: 'S2', chapter: 'Scrub In', where: \\\"Bell's office\\\", set: 'office', music: 'story-calm',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('bell', 'pleased', 'You have the best hands I have ever seen, Doctor, and the worst nerves.'),\\n      line('ren', 'shy', 'I counted out loud. Bea said that was allowed.'),\\n      line('bell', 'warm', 'Surgery is the art of being wrong slowly enough to fix it.'),\\n      line('bea', 'dry', 'He was wrong twice and said so. I am writing that down as a miracle.'),\\n      line('ren', 'quiet', 'The driver asked if he could keep the glass. I said no.'),\\n      line('bell', 'amused', 'A correct answer. Frame it.'),\\n      line('bea', 'stern', 'Do not frame it. Do not get fond of yourself.'),\\n60→      line('bell', 'serious', 'There is a second case stacking. A boy, a belly, a thing that should not be growing.'),\\n      line('ren', 'nervous', 'Tonight?'),\\n      line('bell', 'calm', 'The flood took the night shift. You are the night shift.'),\\n      line('bea', 'firm', 'He will eat first. Then he will throw up. Then he will scrub.'),\\n      line('ren', 'small', 'I do not always throw up.'),\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/story/scenes.js\",\"offset\":45,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"      line('bea', 'stern', 'Gloves. Lamp. Eyes on me until I tell you to look at the wound.'),\\n      line('ren', 'steady', 'Yes, ma\\\\'am.'),\\n      line('bea', 'quiet', 'Child. Breathe on the count I give you. Not yours.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'S2', chapter: 'Scrub In', where: \\\"Bell's office\\\", set: 'office', music: 'story-calm',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('bell', 'pleased', 'You have the best hands I have ever seen, Doctor, and the worst nerves.'),\\n      line('ren', 'shy', 'I counted out loud. Bea said that was allowed.'),\\n      line('bell', 'warm', 'Surgery is the art of being wrong slowly enough to fix it.'),\\n      line('bea', 'dry', 'He was wrong twice and said so. I am writing that down as a miracle.'),\\n      line('ren', 'quiet', 'The driver asked if he could keep the glass. I said no.'),\\n      line('bell', 'amused', 'A correct answer. Frame it.'),\\n      line('bea', 'stern', 'Do not frame it. Do not get fond of yourself.'),\\n      line('bell', 'serious', 'There is a second case stacking. A boy, a belly, a thing that should not be growing.'),\\n      line('ren', 'nervous', 'Tonight?'),\\n      line('bell', 'calm', 'The flood took the night shift. You are the night shift.'),\\n      line('bea', 'firm', 'He will eat first. Then he will throw up. Then he will scrub.'),\\n      line('ren', 'small', 'I do not always throw up.'),\\n\",\"total_lines\":377}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"bace8da8-6e35-4d21-99a4-e9e24c81f41a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_466","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Adding an ellipsis line after the first bell line.\n\nDrafting the test runner in compact style. The ink filter will be copied verbatim. Tests will run sequentially with one browser at a time, closing between each test to manage memory. Six browser launches are planned for hub tests, each up to 300 seconds. The runner will start after the game builds.\n\nPlaywright will use Chromium with SwiftShader GPU flags. The single HTML test can load via file://, but the hub harness needs an HTTP server because it loads game.html as an iframe. I will copy dist/game.html into tests/hub/site before running hub tests.\n\nI will add a .gitignore. I will verify __game before trusting it. I am writing files in large parallel batches. For the Operation screen, director.js will render the HUD from state each frame by updating existing elements or creating new ones.\n\nThe Operation HUD HTML will contain objective, vitals, timer, score, tool, bark, an ECG canvas, and a wheel. Wheel buttons will be clickable with data-tool attributes. glyphs.js will render prompts by replacing tokens like {use}. The state() method will return the current screen name, operation ID, and phase ID.\n\nThe state() method will also expose vitals, timer, score, rank, BPM, beat count, active site, tool, seat positions with scores and tools, focus ID, prompt set, glyph set, attract mode, dev mode, and render backend.\n\nThe state() method will also expose musicGain, tuning, and reached. Rank will be returned as an id string so tests can verify it directly.\n\nmusicGain will be exactly 0.10, defaulting to that value if the audio context fails. The settings music slider will adjust gain, and tests will verify the default before changing it. The save shape will store storyIndex, a cleared map of operation IDs to rank IDs, and difficulty set to 'resident'.\n\nThe save shape will also store settings, an unlocked flag, and a `st-alder-progress` localStorage key. Attract mode will skip saving. Free play will show cleared or reached operations, with dev mode unlocking all cards and displaying the best rank stamp. The lobby will have four seats, prompt for confirmation to join, and start when seat one is ready.\n\nThe lobby will use a single Start button that stays disabled until at least one seat is joined. A pad or keyboard press on the focused Start button will begin the operation. This avoids a second confirm press from joining a seat also starting the game.\n\nPad confirm presses will join unjoined seats, and re-pressing confirm on a joined seat will activate focus on the Start button. The test sequence will press pad0, then pad1, then press Start or Enter. After starting, pad0 will move tip 0 forward while pad1 moves tip 1 backward to verify independent movement. A bot test will run for several seconds to score both tips.\n\nFail screen tests will skip to an operation, trigger a failure, and verify the Fail screen appears and is recorded in reached. Bea's notes offer button will appear when notes are available. I will add lightweight sim tests for gel coverage and forceps rules rather than reimplementing them.\n\nI will write direct sim tests for core mechanics rather than full operations. These will assert outcomes like vitals dropping to zero, timer expiry, rank titles, and hush slowing the beat. I will also test determinism, snapshot caps during grand rounds, data lint, and bot invariants. Tool tests will use short scripted inputs instead of full ops. A syringe test on a broken-glass dip may be added.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e7f1444-7b4d-4fd6-83fd-ffb547474cd1-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"checkpoint","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2435,"output_tokens":2055,"cache_read_input_tokens":131712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"c487cd9f-ab11-45c3-83fa-31473baeb27c"}
