{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_468","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Patching the story and starting to write files.\n\nWriting audio and data first, then the view and director. Barks will avoid \"good\" in Bea lines. Pip barks can still use those lines since they are not Bea's speech. A separate lint may scan all source files for this rule.\n\nThe streak line will read \"Adequate\". New files must not contain placeholder, stub, TODO, or FIXME. The director will be fully implemented. Session local tips will move instantly with input and send absolute positions for host application. The harness visual is secondary to messages and finish.\n\nSnapshots will be buffered with timestamps and rendered 120ms behind the host. Local seat positions override the host view. The simulation pumps on setTimeout instead of requestAnimationFrame, while the view uses rAF separately when not a server or norender mode. AIHub.ready() runs before view initialization.\n\nGraphics failures will call AIHub.fail to end the session. The card UI screen is named 'card' and is excluded from standalone reached checks. A countdown overlay shows 3-2-1 while time() is negative, and the simulation only starts once time reaches zero or above. Player data comes from info.players.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b73b759d-f847-4966-9e9b-2c90f20a681e-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/rng.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b73b759d-f847-4966-9e9b-2c90f20a681e-61","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tools/vendor/session.js","offset":386,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":349,"output_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":136320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"855c711f-22be-4fbe-b283-e812a95ee247"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b73b759d-f847-4966-9e9b-2c90f20a681e-60","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Mulberry32. The sim never touches Math.random. */\\nexport function makeRng(seed) {\\n  let s = (seed >>> 0) || 1;\\n  const next = () => {\\n    s = (s + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n    let t = s;\\n    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n10→  };\\n  next.int = (n) => Math.floor(next() * n);\\n  next.seed = seed >>> 0;\\n  return next;\\n}\\n\\nexport function hashString(str) {\\n  let h = 2166136261;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {\\n    h ^= str.charCodeAt(i);\\n20→    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return h >>> 0;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Mulberry32. The sim never touches Math.random. */\\nexport function makeRng(seed) {\\n  let s = (seed >>> 0) || 1;\\n  const next = () => {\\n    s = (s + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n    let t = s;\\n    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n10→  };\\n  next.int = (n) => Math.floor(next() * n);\\n  next.seed = seed >>> 0;\\n  return next;\\n}\\n\\nexport function hashString(str) {\\n  let h = 2166136261;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {\\n    h ^= str.charCodeAt(i);\\n20→    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return h >>> 0;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/rng.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/** Mulberry32. The sim never touches Math.random. */\\nexport function makeRng(seed) {\\n  let s = (seed >>> 0) || 1;\\n  const next = () => {\\n    s = (s + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n    let t = s;\\n    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n  };\\n  next.int = (n) => Math.floor(next() * n);\\n  next.seed = seed >>> 0;\\n  return next;\\n}\\n\\nexport function hashString(str) {\\n  let h = 2166136261;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {\\n    h ^= str.charCodeAt(i);\\n    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return h >>> 0;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":23}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b73b759d-f847-4966-9e9b-2c90f20a681e-61","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"386→  /** A seeded random number generator (0 ≤ n < 1), the same sequence on every device for the same label. */\\n  hub.rng = function (label) {\\n    var h = 2166136261;\\n    var s = String(label === undefined ? '' : label);\\n390→    for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n      h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\\n      h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n    }\\n    return generator((hub.seed ^ h) >>> 0);\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\\n  function finite(v) {\\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\\n400→  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\\n   */\\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\\n410→      return null;\\n    }\\n    var copy = {};\\n    for (var key in outcome) {\\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\\n    }\\n    return copy;\\n420→  }\\n\\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\",\"content_concise\":\"386→  /** A seeded random number generator (0 ≤ n < 1), the same sequence on every device for the same label. */\\n  hub.rng = function (label) {\\n    var h = 2166136261;\\n    var s = String(label === undefined ? '' : label);\\n390→    for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n      h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\\n      h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n    }\\n    return generator((hub.seed ^ h) >>> 0);\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\\n  function finite(v) {\\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\\n400→  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\\n   */\\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\\n410→      return null;\\n    }\\n    var copy = {};\\n    for (var key in outcome) {\\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\\n    }\\n    return copy;\\n420→  }\\n\\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\\n    if (!welcomed || 