{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_476","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The folder name contains the title, but it is a directory rather than a source file.\n\nI will write the required files using the Write tool. I plan to generate 60 barks programmatically as data. I will also fix story and rng in parallel with the first writes.\n\nI will export a `lineFor` function to generate bark text by key. I will add four more barks: toolHint, overflow, strainIntro, and hushReady. I will create `src/data/cast.js` to store voice parameters and bust data like skin color, hair color, hair style seed, and clothes color.\n\nI am writing the files now. I am keeping syntax errors out of them. I am adding a `Bucket` class to limit session send rate. It refills tokens over time and blocks sends when empty.\n\nA single reliable message will be queued if needed. The host sim step accumulator will run at 16 ms intervals. The client will send input messages at 12 per second even while idle. The client will maintain a local tip position using simple integration instead of duplicating the host's moveSeat logic. The host remains authoritative for the simulation.\n\nI will send absolute tip coordinates after local integration instead of raw stick values. The host will place the tip directly from those absolute positions. Local and host will match unless aim assist pulls the host's copy.\n\nI will merge input and aim messages into a single command map. Each client's latest stick and use state is stored per ID and applied to the simulation every step.\n\nI will clear one-shot flags like syringe and special after each step. Events will be batched and sent up to five times per second as reliable messages. Keyframes will be generated from the host simulation state, with a size check to avoid oversized packets. The view will decode keyframes and unreliable updates, store the state, and interpolate between snapshots.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6b2efe8-ae6e-48b8-b3d6-4badb120144f-71","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html","offset":390,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1550,"output_tokens":1358,"cache_read_input_tokens":143872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"56cfa08e-403e-46a3-9c1a-162e794db3ac"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b6b2efe8-ae6e-48b8-b3d6-4badb120144f-71","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"390→  return test();\\n}\\n\\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\\n400→  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\\n  const checks = [];\\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\\n    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\\n    renderChecks(checks);\\n    return !!pass;\\n410→  };\\n  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\\n  window.__hubCheck = report;\\n  try {\\n    const state = await newRound();\\n    if (!state) {\\n      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const n = state.n;\\n420→    const m = state.metas;\\n    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\\n    const seats = String(m?.players ?? '').match(/\\\\d+/g)?.map(Number) ?? [];\\n    const [least, most = least] = seats;\\n    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\\n    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\\n\\n    // Every copy: the players, and in a server round the server's copy.\\n    const copies = () => [...(state.status?.players ?? []), ...(state.status?.server ? [state.status.server] : [])];\\n    const helloed = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\\n430→    check('every copy says hello', helloed, copies().filter((p) => !p.hello).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    if (!helloed) return;\\n    const caps = state.coordinator.seats().map((s) => s.caps);\\n    check('hello names protocol 1 and the mode', caps.every((c) => c.v === 1 && modeOf(c.mode) === state.coordinator.mode), JSON.stringify(caps[0]));\\n    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\\n    if (state.cells.some((c) => !c.frame.contentDocument)) {\\n      check('frames reachable for synthetic input', false, 'serve the game from the same origin as this harness');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n440→    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\\n    const loaded = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.ready), 20_000);\\n    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    // A game that shows its own card takes the players' answers on it: Enter is Ready.\\n    if (caps.some((c) => c?.card)) {\\n      const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server);\\n      const sent = await until(() => players.every((c) => c.cardSent), 2000);\\n      for (const cell of players) poke(cell, 'Enter');\\n      const answered = await until(() => players.every((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)), 3000);\\n      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\\n450→    }\\n    releaseRound(state);\\n    const started = await until(() => state.status?.phase !== 'loading', 15_000);\\n    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\\n    if (!started || state.record) return;\\n\\n    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\\n    const arrows = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'a', 'd', 'w', 's'];\\n    const randomly = async (ms) => {\\n      const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n460→      while (performance.now() < end && !state.record) {\\n        for (const cell of state.cells) if (!cell.gone && !cell.server) poke(cell, arrows[Math.floor(Math.random() * arrows.length)]);\\n        await sleep(150);\\n      }\\n    };\\n    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\\n\\n    const mode = state.coordinator.mode;\\n    // Parallel and ghost: every copy runs its own world from the same seeded start. A game\\n    // still tagged race was built to race's contract: no seeded start, and no progress asked.\",\"content_concise\":\"390→  return test();\\n}\\n\\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\\n400→  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\\n  const checks = [];\\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\\n    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\\n    renderChecks(checks);\\n    return !!pass;\\n410→  };\\n  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\\n  window.__hubCheck = report;\\n  try {\\n    const state = await newRound();\\n    if (!state) {\\n      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const n = state.n;\\n420→    const m = state.metas;\\n    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\\n    const seats = String(m?.players ?? '').match(/\\\\d+/g)?.map(Number) ?? [];\\n    const [least, most = least] = seats;\\n    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\\n    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\\n\\n    // Every copy: the players, and in a server round the server's copy.\\n    const copies = () => [...(state.status?.players ?? []), ...(state.status?.server ? [state.status.server] : [])];\\n    const helloed = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\\n430→    check('every copy says hello', helloed, copies().filter((p) => !p.hello).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    if (!helloed) return;\\n    const caps = state.coordinator.seats().map((s) => s.caps);\\n    check('hello names protocol 1 and the mode', caps.every((c) => c.v === 1 && modeOf(c.mode) === state.coordinator.mode), JSON.stringify(caps[0]));\\n    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\\n    if (state.cells.some((c) => !c.frame.contentDocument)) {\\n      check('frames reachable for synthetic input', false, 'serve the game from the same origin as this harness');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n440→    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\\n    const loaded = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.ready), 20_000);\\n    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    // A game that shows its own card takes the players' answers on it: Enter is Ready.\\n    if (caps.some((c) => c?.card)) {\\n      const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server);\\n      const sent = await until(() => players.every((c) => c.cardSent), 2000);\\n      for (const cell of players) poke(cell, 'Enter');\\n      const answered = await until(() => players.every((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)), 3000);\\n      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\\n450→    }\\n    releaseRound(state);\\n    const started = await until(() => state.status?.phase !== 'loading', 15_000);\\n    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\\n    if (!started || state.record) return;\\n\\n    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\\n    const arrows = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'a', 'd', 'w', 's'];\\n    const randomly = async (ms) => {\\n      const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n460→      while (performance.now() < end && !state.record) {\\n        for (const cell of state.cells) if (!cell.gone && !cell.server) poke(cell, arrows[Math.floor(Math.random() * arrows.length)]);\\n        await sleep(150);\\n      }\\n    };\\n    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\\n\\n    const mode = state.coordinator.mode;\\n    // Parallel and ghost: every copy runs its own world from the same seeded start. A game\\n    // still tagged race was built to race's contract: no seeded start, and no progress asked.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html\",\"offset\":390,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  return test();\\n}\\n\\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\\n  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\\n  const checks = [];\\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\\n    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\\n    renderChecks(checks);\\n    return !!pass;\\n  };\\n  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\\n  window.__hubCheck = report;\\n  try {\\n    const state = await newRound();\\n    if (!state) {\\n      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const n = state.n;\\n    const m = state.metas;\\n    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\\n    const seats = String(m?.players ?? '').match(/\\\\d+/g)?.map(Number) ?? [];\\n    const [least, most = least] = seats;\\n    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\\n    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\\n\\n    // Every copy: the players, and in a server round the server's copy.\\n    const copies = () => [...(state.status?.players ?? []), ...(state.status?.server ? [state.status.server] : [])];\\n    const helloed = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\\n    check('every copy says hello', helloed, copies().filter((p) => !p.hello).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    if (!helloed) return;\\n    const caps = state.coordinator.seats().map((s) => s.caps);\\n    check('hello names protocol 1 and the mode', caps.every((c) => c.v === 1 && modeOf(c.mode) === state.coordinator.mode), JSON.stringify(caps[0]));\\n    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\\n    if (state.cells.some((c) => !c.frame.contentDocument)) {\\n      check('frames reachable for synthetic input', false, 'serve the game from the same origin as this harness');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\\n    const loaded = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.ready), 20_000);\\n    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    // A game that shows its own card takes the players' answers on it: Enter is Ready.\\n    if (caps.some((c) => c?.card)) {\\n      const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server);\\n      const sent = await until(() => players.every((c) => c.cardSent), 2000);\\n      for (const cell of players) poke(cell, 'Enter');\\n      const answered = await until(() => players.every((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)), 3000);\\n      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\\n    }\\n    releaseRound(state);\\n    const started = await until(() => state.status?.phase !== 'loading', 15_000);\\n    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\\n    if (!started || state.record) return;\\n\\n    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\\n    const arrows = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'a', 'd', 'w', 's'];\\n    const randomly = async (ms) => {\\n      const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n      while (performance.now() < end && !state.record) {\\n        for (const cell of state.cells) if (!cell.gone && !cell.server) poke(cell, arrows[Math.floor(Math.random() * arrows.length)]);\\n        await sleep(150);\\n      }\\n    };\\n    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\\n\\n    const mode = state.coordinator.mode;\\n    // Parallel and ghost: every copy runs its own world from the same seeded start. A game\\n    // still tagged race was built to race's contract: no seeded start, and no progress asked.\\n\",\"total_lines\":548}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"f1fa095d-1cbe-443b-9aa4-7bd54550def0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_477","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The ready signal must arrive within 20 seconds of the check starting, which occurs after hello.\n\nReady can be called immediately after connect resolves, before the renderer starts. The harness sets cardSent when it sends the card event, not when the game receives it.\n\nThe card UI must call AIHub.answer('ready') on Enter. I'll listen for Enter on the window keydown. The WASD check must also catch 'a' via e.key or e.code, since the harness sends code: key.\n\nCalling answer() during play is safe because it no-ops once goAt is set. The server copy can call ready() and send snapshots without a player view, and Enter is not poked there. If the host leaves and the round voids, the game will stop on the end event instead of finishing.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f9d99c75-d48c-47a4-aaa7-8c4967291c87-72","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html","offset":180,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2770,"output_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":145408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"481d56d8-593f-4a87-a9a3-e71903a266ac"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f9d99c75-d48c-47a4-aaa7-8c4967291c87-72","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"180→\\n  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\\n  current = state;\\n  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\\n\\n  state.coordinator = createRound({\\n    round,\\n    players,\\n    hostKey: 'p0',\\n    serverKey: serverMode ? 'server' : null,\\n190→    mode,\\n    seed,\\n    limitMs,\\n    gate: true,\\n    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\\n    onStatus: (s) => { state.status = s; render(state); },\\n    onEnd: (record) => {\\n      state.record = record;\\n      log(`round ${round} ${record.status}: ${record.reason}${record.standings ? ' — standings ' + JSON.stringify(record.standings) : ''}`);\\n      render(state);\\n200→    },\\n  });\\n  hubEnd.onMessage((from, env) => {\\n    if (env.k !== 'c' || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.m?.type !== 'vis') log(`${from} → hub: ${env.m?.type}${env.m?.type === 'result' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify({ time: env.m.time, score: env.m.score }) : ''}${env.m?.type === 'finish' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify(env.m.standings) : ''}`);\\n    state.coordinator.receive(from, env.m);\\n  });\\n\\n  for (const p of [...players, ...(serverMode ? [{ key: 'server', slot: null, name: 'Server', server: true }] : [])]) {\\n    const color = p.server ? '#8a8a8a' : ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'][p.slot];\\n210→    const frame = document.createElement('iframe');\\n    frame.allow = 'fullscreen; autoplay; gamepad; pointer-lock';\\n    frame.title = p.name;\\n    const label = document.createElement('div');\\n    label.className = 'cell__bar';\\n    label.innerHTML = `<span class=\\\"cell__dot\\\" style=\\\"background:${color}\\\"></span><b></b><span class=\\\"cell__state\\\"></span>`;\\n    label.querySelector('b').textContent = `${p.name} (${p.key})`;\\n    const el = document.createElement('div');\\n    el.className = 'cell';\\n    el.style.borderColor = color;\\n220→    el.append(label, frame);\\n    grid.append(el);\\n\\n    const endpoint = net.endpoint(p.key);\\n    const cell = { ...p, el, label, frame, endpoint, violations: [], instrumented: true, gone: false, progress: [], cardSent: '' };\\n    const post = postTo(frame);\\n    cell.bridge = createBridge({\\n      key: p.key,\\n      round,\\n      coordinator: 'hub',\",\"content_concise\":\"180→\\n  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\\n  current = state;\\n  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\\n\\n  state.coordinator = createRound({\\n    round,\\n    players,\\n    hostKey: 'p0',\\n    serverKey: serverMode ? 'server' : null,\\n190→    mode,\\n    seed,\\n    limitMs,\\n    gate: true,\\n    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\\n    onStatus: (s) => { state.status = s; render(state); },\\n    onEnd: (record) => {\\n      state.record = record;\\n      log(`round ${round} ${record.status}: ${record.reason}${record.standings ? ' — standings ' + JSON.stringify(record.standings) : ''}`);\\n      render(state);\\n200→    },\\n  });\\n  hubEnd.onMessage((from, env) => {\\n    if (env.k !== 'c' || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.m?.type !== 'vis') log(`${from} → hub: ${env.m?.type}${env.m?.type === 'result' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify({ time: env.m.time, score: env.m.score }) : ''}${env.m?.type === 'finish' ? ' ' + JSON.stri