g\"},{\"line_number\":63,\"content\":\"### 2.2 Cast\"},{\"line_number\":77,\"content\":\"### 2.3 REQUIEM and the Conservatory\"},{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"### 2.4 Tone rules\"},{\"line_number\":111,\"content\":\"## 3. Core rules\"},{\"line_number\":115,\"content\":\"### 3.1 The field\"},{\"line_number\":121,\"content\":\"### 3.2 The instrument tip\"},{\"line_number\":127,\"content\":\"### 3.3 The beat clock\"},{\"line_number\":131,\"content\":\"### 3.4 Vitals, clock, misses\"},{\"line_number\":137,\"content\":\"### 3.5 Grades and score\"},{\"line_number\":150,\"content\":\"### 3.6 Ranks\"},{\"line_number\":162,\"content\":\"### 3.7 Composure and the two gifts\"},{\"line_number\":171,\"content\":\"### 3.8 Difficulty, checkpoints, assist\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"### 3.9 Consults\"},{\"line_number\":200,\"content\":\"## 4. Tools\"},{\"line_number\":242,\"content\":\"## 5. Strains\"},{\"line_number\":258,\"content\":\"## 6. Operations\"},{\"line_number\":262,\"content\":\"### Op 1: Broken Glass (Chapter 1, Ren). Forearm. Timer 4:00, 72 bpm\"},{\"line_number\":272,\"content\":\"### Op 2: Growth Spurt (Chapter 1, Ren). Abdomen skin, then bowel. Timer 5:30, 76 bpm\"},{\"line_number\":282,\"content\":\"### Op 3: Adagio (Chapter 2, Ren). Liver. Timer 5:30, 80 bpm\"},{\"line_number\":291,\"content\":\"### Op 4: Staccato (Chapter 2, Ren). Bowel, then stomach. Timer 6:00, 84 bpm\"},{\"line_number\":300,\"content\":\"### Op 5: Legato (Chapter 3, **Ines**). Brain. Timer 6:00, 70 bpm. Consult\"},{\"line_number\":309,\"content\":\"### Op 6: Fermata (Chapter 3, Ren, with Ines on comms). Heart. Timer 7:00, 88 bpm. Consult\"},{\"line_number\":319,\"content\":\"### Op 7: Coda (Chapter 4, Ren and Ines). Heart, lung, aorta. Timer 9:30, 92 bpm. Consult\"},{\"line_number\":329,\"content\":\"### Last Patient (Chapter 4 ending, Ren). Heart. No HUD, no timer, can't fail\"},{\"line_number\":333,\"content\":\"### Grand Rounds (co-op, Free Play and hub rounds). Liver, bowel, heart. Timer 5:00\"},{\"line_number\":344,\"content\":\"## 7. Story\"},{\"line_number\":382,\"content\":\"## 8. Controls and screens\"},{\"line_number\":384,\"content\":\"### 8.1 Operating controls\"},{\"line_number\":409,\"content\":\"### 8.2 Menu controls\"},{\"line_number\":413,\"content\":\"### 8.3 Prompts\"},{\"line_number\":423,\"content\":\"### 8.4 Ten-foot rules (tests can't judge these; check at 1920×1080)\"},{\"line_number\":430,\"content\":\"### 8.5 The operating HUD\"},{\"line_number\":444,\"content\":\"### 8.6 Screens\"},{\"line_number\":469,\"content\":\"## 9. Art direction\"},{\"line_number\":477,\"content\":\"### 9.1 Palette\"},{\"line_number\":488,\"content\":\"### 9.2 The operating view (values verified in the prototype)\"},{\"line_number\":497,\"content\":\"### 9.3 Sites\"},{\"line_number\":519,\"content\":\"### 9.4 Instruments\"},{\"line_number\":527,\"content\":\"### 9.5 Story staging\"},{\"line_number\":535,\"content\":\"### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\"},{\"line_number\":547,\"content\":\"### 9.7 Effects, and the juice list\"},{\"line_number\":565,\"content\":\"## 10. Animation\"},{\"line_number\":582,\"content\":\"## 11. Audio\"},{\"line_number\":590,\"content\":\"### Music\"},{\"line_number\":605,\"content\":\"### Sound effects (all procedural)\"},{\"line_number\":609,\"content\":\"### Voices\"},{\"line_number\":628,\"content\":\"## 12. Attract mode\"},{\"line_number\":637,\"content\":\"## 13. Dev mode\"},{\"line_number\":689,\"content\":\"## 14. Multiplayer\"},{\"line_number\":693,\"content\":\"### 14.1 The decision\"},{\"line_number\":706,\"content\":\"### 14.2 Rules that apply in a session (`AIHub.active`)\"},{\"line_number\":714,\"content\":\"### 14.3 Authority and messages (the tested pattern)\"},{\"line_number\":767,\"content\":\"### 14.4 The card\"},{\"line_number\":771,\"content\":\"### 14.5 Couch co-op (on its own)\"},{\"line_number\":775,\"content\":\"### 14.6 Head tags\"},{\"line_number\":790,\"content\":\"### 14.7 What the hub's own check does\"},{\"line_number\":796,\"content\":\"## 15. Architecture\"},{\"line_number\":798,\"content\":\"### 15.1 Layout\"},{\"line_number\":821,\"content\":\"### 15.2 Sim and view\"},{\"line_number\":832,\"content\":\"### 15.3 Operations are data\"},{\"line_number\":863,\"content\":\"### 15.4 Observable state and test hooks\"},{\"line_number\":871,\"content\":\"### 15.5 The bot\"},{\"line_number\":877,\"content\":\"## 16. Verified recipes and traps\"},{\"line_number\":881,\"content\":\"### 16.1 Packages\"},{\"line_number\":891,\"content\":\"### 16.2 The build\"},{\"line_number\":926,\"content\":\"### 16.3 Browser flags for headless WebGPU\"},{\"line_number\":940,\"content\":\"### 16.4 Renderer boot\"},{\"line_number\":958,\"content\":\"### 16.5 The ink filter (run exactly as written, on both backends)\"},{\"line_number\":1038,\"content\":\"### 16.6 Materials\"},{\"line_number\":1067,\"content\":\"### 16.7 Rapier\"},{\"line_number\":1085,\"content\":\"### 16.8 Pad stub for tests\"},{\"line_number\":1101,\"content\":\"## 17. Testing\"},{\"line_number\":1147,\"content\":\"## 18. Build order\"},{\"line_number\":1167,\"content\":\"## 19. Finishing: About screen, exit interview, catalogue\"},{\"line_number\":1191,\"content\":\"## 20. Brief coverage checklist\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c5b95171-63e2-4ea7-8e40-f38727c5e4f1-5","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-ma