{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_514","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The class has a duplicate spawn method at line 379 and another at line 780.\n\nThe class method at line 754 overwrites the earlier spawn. The public spawn is rawSpawn.\n\nsiteDelta is not edge-triggered in tools.js, so holding a key spams nudges. The director should edge-detect siteDelta and swap before sending them to the sim. Alternatively, nudgeSite could apply the delta every frame since it is idempotent.\n\nnudgeSite cycles through all sites every frame while a key is held, so the director must track previous siteDelta per seat to send nudges only on rising edges. Syringe is hold-based and should remain true while pressed. Special, swap, and alt are rising-edge inputs.\n\nNetwork one-shots merge input and clear after each step. Local inputs replace commands each poll, so one-shots only last for the current frame while a key is held.\n\nEnter triggers full use, not menu confirm. The director must avoid applying keyboard frame use when paused, since the menu handles confirmation in that state.\n\ntest.input(frame) overrides seat 0. test.bot(on, opts) takes over bot control.\n\ntest.warp(n) advances n simulation steps per frame. test.step(n) runs poll, apply input, sim.step, and post-step synchronously. Attract mode requires wall-clock time, so tests will sleep 10 seconds rather than stepping through it. The attract demo will be scripted by switching operations over time using a bot with cheats.\n\nAttract mode will change `state().op` as it visits each operation, letting tests poll the current operation over time. The attract demo also needs to display the exact screen name \"Touch notice\".\n\nThe touch notice screen displays the exact text \"Controller or keyboard required\". It is detected by checking that `(any-pointer: fine)` returns false and no pad input has been seen. A settings button on the notice uses a `data-item` tap. Exiting the notice with a key or pad returns to Title. The detection logic will be verified against Playwright phone tests.\n\nIf `createView` throws, a friendly fallback screen appears. The session only calls `AIHub.fail` when both backends fail.\n\nThe `?norender=1` flag disables WebGPU initialization and uses a pointer camera instead.\n\n`?webgl=1` forces WebGL mode.\n\nDev tools run through `devRun(id)` and hide in the hub. Sliders mutate `sim.tuning`, which resets via `resetTuning`.\n\nSeveral dev commands must survive an operation ending. These include jump, unlock, play scene, complete objective or phase, win, fail, force rank, god mode, freeze timer, infinite composure, infinite clamps, spawn bleeder or strain, beginArrest, fortissimo, hush, sforzando, time scale, single step, auto surgeon, overlays, and ink toggles.\n\nSave data goes to localStorage. It is not stored in the session and is disabled during attract.\n\nSave data stores settings and story progress. Continue uses it and survives reload.\n\nThe story flow is New Game, then a single Bea difficulty question with Intern, Resident, or Attending choices defaulting to Resident. After that comes S0, then each operation follows a fixed sequence: Chart screen, Operation, Report, then after-scene. The final operation ends at S16, followed by skippable credits and the menu.\n\nEach operation maps to two scenes: broken-glass S1/S2, growth S3/S4, adagio S5/S6, staccato S7/S8, legato S9/S10, fermata S11/S12, coda S13/S14, and last-patient S15/S16.\n\nContinue will resume from the next unplayed operation using saved state including story index, seen operations, ranks, difficulty, settings, and unlocked items. The Chart screen preselects the careful consult option so Enter starts the operation immediately.\n\nThe Chart screen places focus on Begin while the consult option defaults to Careful. One Enter press applies the careful consult and starts the operation. The difficulty screen lists Intern, Resident, and Attending, with Resident as the default choice.\n\nThe main menu lists Story, Free Play, Grand Rounds, Settings, and About. If a save exists, the Story item opens a submenu with Continue and New Game; otherwise it starts a new game directly. This keeps the total at five items.\n\nThe menu system enforces exactly one focused item at a time. Focus is tracked by a `focusId` in state and moves via hover. Up and down keys change focus, while confirm activates the selected item.\n\nPad confirm also triggers menu selection. Story text advances one line per confirm edge; Tab or Triangle skips the current scene immediately. Pause opens via Esc or Options, with Resume, Skip Scene, Settings, Dev Mode, and Quit available during story, while sessions only show Settings and keep running. The pause menu also appears automatically when the document becomes hidden outside of sessions.\n\nFail screens list FLATLINE, TIME, and MALPRACTICE. They offer Retry, Restart, Quit, and Notes when due.\n\nReport shows Time, Vitals, Precision, Best Combo, a rank stamp, follow-up, and Continue.\n\nFree Play displays cards for completed operations. It includes Difficulty and Doctor settings. Dev mode unlocks everything.\n\nThe Lobby has four seats. Confirm joins the focused seat. Seat one starts the session when ready.\n\nThe lobby test will inject two stub pads and press their confirm buttons to join seats. The keyboard joins seat zero when no pad is active. A focused Begin item starts the operation once at least one seat has joined.\n\nThe lobby test will use a two-step join-and-start flow. Pads press confirm to join their seats, and the keyboard presses Enter on a focused Begin button to start the operation. During the operation, pads drive both tips independently while the keyboard stays out of seat zero.\n\nBoth seats in a couch grand rounds session will be driven by the test bot so both score. Settings pages cover Audio, Controls, Display, and Q/E. Music gain defaults to 0.10. Glyphs can switch between PlayStation and Xbox; the Xbox prompt appears only when a pad is connected.\n\nThe About screen renders its content from an inline JSON script tag. Tests will verify that the JSON parses and its fields appear on screen.\n\nThe game will read the About content from the inline `#about-data` script tag at runtime. It will not import the JSON file directly, so importer edits update the displayed text without a rebuild.\n\nThe credits roll screen is named \"Credits roll\" and marks the reached state as \"Credits\". It appears after S16 over attract footage and can be skipped. The full list of reached screens includes Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, Credits roll, Credits, Fail, Free Play, Lobby, Settings, About, and Touch notice. The harness sets the `data-complete` attribute; the game must not set it itself. The Title screen needs static DOM text on the teal background so the pre-GPU frame is not blank. The built HTML will contain the title from the identity bundle.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3120f02c-6484-4330-83f5-434edf9b95a3-48","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"infiniteClamps|lockVitals|freezeTimer|timeScale|cheats\\.","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3120f02c-6484-4330-83f5-434edf9b95a3-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js","offset":270,"limit":55}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3120f02c-6484-4330-83f5-434edf9b95a3-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function tryGift|hushPhase|composure","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2407,"output_tokens":3459,"cache_read_input_tokens":109056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"4d62acd0-b746-4181-adb7-9d6a189873fe"}
