112,116,121,32,98,117,102,102,101,114,32,105,115,32,97,32,102,97,105,108,117,114,101,32,116,111,32,102,105,120,46,10,50,51,58,54,46,32,103,97,116,105,110,103,58,32,80,97,114,115,101,32,96,101,120,105,116,45,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,46,106,115,111,110,96,59,32,99,111,110,102,105,114,109,32,116,104,101,32,114,111,111,116,32,72,84,77,76,32,97,110,100,32,100,101,118,45,102,111,108,100,101,114,32,110,97,109,101,115,59,32,99,111,110,102,105,114,109,32,116,104,101,32,99,108,105,101,110,116,32,104,97,115,104,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,97,116,32,116,104,101,32,104,117,98,32,98,97,110,110,101,114,32,115,116,114,105,110,103,32,97,112,112,101,97,114,115,32,111,110,99,101,59,32,99,111,110,102,105,114,109,32,111,119,110,32,115,111,117,114,99,101,32,40,110,111,116,32,116,104,101,32,98,117,110,100,108,101,41,32,104,97,115,32,110,111,32,98,97,110,110,101,100,32,115,111,117,114,99,101,32,110,97,109,101,115,44,32,110,111,32,96,77,97,116,104,46,114,97,110,100,111,109,96,32,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,115,105,109,44,32,97,110,100,32,110,111,32,84,79,68,79,47,70,73,88,77,69,47,112,108,97,99,101,104,111,108,100,101,114,47,115,116,117,98,46,32,82,101,99,111,114,100,32,114,101,115,117,108,116,115,32,105,110,32,96,123,83,67,82,65,84,67,72,125,47,112,97,99,107,97,103,101,46,108,111,103,96,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":3,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"4. gating: Launch the real root HTML twice, from `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1` (bind `127.0.0.1` on an OS-picked port; confirm `window.__game` exists before trusting the page). Use the five flags above. Each run: zero page errors; canvas drawing buffer equals the requested size; painted fraction is high (a blank or speck fails — do not treat a successful blank readback as a missing tool); a driven input (stub pad or mouse) changes the on-screen tip or HUD, visible in a second capture. Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch.log` and rely on steps 1–3; a started browser that returns an empty buffer is a failure to fix.\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"6. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json`; confirm the root HTML and dev-folder names; confirm the client hash and that the hub banner string appears once; confirm own source (not the bundle) has no banned source names, no `Math.random` in the sim, and no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub. Record results in `{SCRATCH}/package.log`.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1add7eb3-6bae-4c4b-beaf-2fabf0e0615d-70","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1185→| Research | What you actually did, plus this plan's: the AI Hub protocol and harness, engine prototypes on this computer, reference pages on the source |\\n\\n**Exit interview file.** Write it exactly as your brief specifies, and check it parses. For the `aiHub` block: `type` Game; `genre` Simulation; `source` Trauma Center: Second Opinion; `series` Trauma Center; `players` 1–4; `controls` \\\"Right stick or mouse to aim, left stick or 1-8 for tools, R2 or left click to use\\\"; `tags` `[\\\"3d\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"sci-fi\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]`. `name`, `tagline` and `description` are yours.\\n\\n---\\n1190→\\n## 20. Brief coverage checklist\\n\\nTick each before you call it done.\\n\\n| Your brief asks for | Where |\\n|---|---|\\n| Genre and perspective chosen to fit the source | §1 |\\n| Title as a playful riff, chosen your brief's way | Yours (top of this plan) |\\n| Research: your choice | The research behind this plan is in §1 and §16; add more if you want, record what you actually did |\\n1200→| Single HTML file, dependencies inlined | §16.2 |\\n| Three.js r180, WebGPU, cel-shaded ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API | §9, §16, §8.1 |\\n| Art: engine base, new art for what makes it feel like the source | §9 |\\n| Animation: native system base, new animations | §10 |\\n| Audio in code only; gibberish voices; music at 10% | §11 |\\n| Online per the hub | §14 |\\n| Dev folder, bundling, shared-machine manners (one or two browsers, own PIDs only, 127.0.0.1 port 0, confirm the page is yours, no global tools install) | §15, §16.3, §17 |\\n| Performance is out of scope: add detail freely | §9 (don't optimize; don't count frames) |\\n| Headless tests, one command, failures and a count, a full scripted playthrough, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | §17 |\\n| Original game inspired by the source; feature-complete, polished vertical slice; infrastructure for building out later | §1, §6, §15.3, `docs/AUTHORING.md` |\\n1210→| Dev mode from pause: standard tools, live sliders, reset | §13 |\\n| Attract mode: 10 s idle, looping, cheats, any input exits | §12 |\\n| Multiplayer in the hub and for the game on its own | §14 |\\n| Narrative tone like the source's | §2.4, §7 |\\n| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover moves focus; prompts follow last input; PlayStation glyphs with Xbox option; no dense screens | §8 |\\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, exact notice text, Settings button, attract runs | §8.6 |\\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §17 packaging test |\\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in chat and on the About/Credits screen | §19 |\\n| Exit interview, parses as JSON | §19 |\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1185→| Research | What you actually did, plus this plan's: the AI Hub protocol and harness, engine prototypes on this computer, reference pages on the source |\\n\\n**Exit interview file.** Write it exactly as your brief specifies, and check it parses. For the `aiHub` block: `type` Game; `genre` Simulation; `source` Trauma Center: Second Opinion; `series` Trauma Center; `players` 1–4; `controls` \\\"Right stick or mouse to aim, left stick or 1-8 for tools, R2 or left click to use\\\"; `tags` `[\\\"3d\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"sci-fi\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]`. `name`, `tagline` and `description` are yours.\\n\\n---\\n1190→\\n## 20. Brief coverage checklist\\n\\nTick each before you call it done.\\n\\n| Your brief asks for | Where |\\n|---|---|\\n| Genre and perspective chosen to fit the source | §1 |\\n| Title as a playful riff, chosen your brief's way | Yours (top of this plan) |\\n| Research: your choice | The research behind this plan is in §1 and §16; add more if you want, record what you actually did |\\n1200→| Single HTML file, dependencies inlined | §16.2 |\\n| Three.js r180, WebGPU, cel-shaded ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API | §9, §16, §8.1 |\\n| Art: engine base, new art for what makes it feel like the source | §9 |\\n| Animation: native system base, new animations | §10 |\\n| Audio in code only; gibberish voices; music at 10% | §11 |\\n| Online per the hub | §14 |\\n| Dev folder, bundling, shared-machine manners (one or two browsers, own PIDs only, 127.0.0.1 port 0, confirm the page is yours, no global tools install) | §15, §16.3, §17 |\\n| Performance is out of scope: add detail freely | §9 (don't optimize; don't count frames) |\\n| Headless tests, one command, failures and a count, a full scripted playthrough, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | §17 |\\n| Original game inspired by the source; feature-complete, polished vertical slice; infrastructure for building out later | §1, §6, §15.3, `docs/AUTHORING.md` |\\n1210→| Dev mode from pause: standard tools, live sliders, reset | §13 |\\n| Attract mode: 10 s idle, looping, cheats, any input exits | §12 |\\n| Multiplayer in the hub and for the game on its own | §14 |\\n| Narrative tone like the source's | §2.4, §7 |\\n| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover moves focus; prompts follow last input; PlayStation glyphs with Xbox option; no dense screens | §8 |\\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, exact notice text, Settings button, attract runs | §8.6 |\\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §17 packaging test |\\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in chat and on the About/Credits screen | §19 |\\n| Exit interview, parses as JSON | §19 |\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1185,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"| Research | What you actually did, plus this plan's: the AI Hub protocol and harness, engine prototypes on this computer, reference pages on the source |\\n\\n**Exit interview file.** Write it exactly as your brief specifies, and check it parses. For the `aiHub` block: `type` Game; `genre` Simulation; `source` Trauma Center: Second Opinion; `series` Trauma Center; `players` 1–4; `controls` \\\"Right stick or mouse to aim, left stick or 1-8 for tools, R2 or left click to use\\\"; `tags` `[\\\"3d\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"sci-fi\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]`. `name`, `tagline` and `description` are yours.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 20. Brief coverage checklist\\n\\nTick each before you call it done.\\n\\n| Your brief asks for | Where |\\n|---|---|\\n| Genre and perspective chosen to fit the source | §1 |\\n| Title as a playful riff, chosen your brief's way | Yours (top of this plan) |\\n| Research: your choice | The research behind this plan is in §1 and §16; add more if you want, record what you actually did |\\n| Single HTML file, dependencies inlined | §16.2 |\\n| Three.js r180, WebGPU, cel-shaded ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API | §9, §16, §8.1 |\\n| Art: engine base, new art for what makes it feel like the source | §9 |\\n| Animation: native system base, new animations | §10 |\\n| Audio in code only; gibberish voices; music at 10% | §11 |\\n| Online per the hub | §14 |\\n| Dev folder, bundling, shared-machine manners (one or two browsers, own PIDs only, 127.0.0.1 port 0, confirm the page is yours, no global tools install) | §15, §16.3, §17 |\\n| Performance is out of scope: add detail freely | §9 (don't optimize; don't count frames) |\\n| Headless tests, one command, failures and a count, a full scripted playthrough, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | §17 |\\n| Original game inspired by the source; feature-complete, polished vertical slice; infrastructure for building out later | §1, §6, §15.3, `docs/AUTHORING.md` |\\n| Dev mode from pause: standard tools, live sliders, reset | §13 |\\n| Attract mode: 10 s idle, looping, cheats, any input exits | §12 |\\n| Multiplayer in the hub and for the game on its own | §14 |\\n| Narrative tone like the source's | §2.4, §7 |\\n| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover moves focus; prompts follow last input; PlayStation glyphs with Xbox option; no dense screens | §8 |\\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, exact notice text, Settings button, attract runs | §8.6 |\\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §17 packaging test |\\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in chat and on the About/Credits screen | §19 |\\n| Exit interview, parses as JSON | §19 |\\n\",\"total_lines\":1218}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"7c19f2bc-21a8-401a-ba16-3ba1dc1b3153"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_528","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading the full verification plan from the goal plan.","signature":"RSGSYdQCvT3H1r0OdrXtqliK9BnWwp6FKOjPL5lJKRNDaNGRwoFbmD8FJt4XzYKMhJJsjfGsOUYxIU8NjHn0Eo+2twmmwrCfAsuubrJ3ekFg9BNvgIg"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1596b9e4-d509-46ab-83b3-19c76b5de2e5-71","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/goal/plan.md","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2092,"output_tokens":117,"cache_read_input_tokens":132992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"965c9f94-e217-47f0-9eba-b13575daa336"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1596b9e4-d509-46ab-83b3-19c76b5de2e5-71","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Plan: Build the surgical-action demo PLAN.md specifies, and hand in every artifact TASK.md and STAGE.md require\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. Hand-in package. The work folder contains `PROGRESS.md`, a parsable `exit-interview.json` beside the game HTML (one object, every TASK.md key filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, `aiHub.type` Game, `aiHub.genre` Simulation, `aiHub.source` `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, `aiHub.series` `Trauma Center`, `aiHub.players` `1–4`, controls and tags as PLAN §19), a dev subfolder named `{Title}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230`, and one root file `{Title}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230.html`. `{Title}` is an original playful riff on the source (50 titles brainstormed, then one picked with a real RNG), shown on the title screen, and stored so no other source file contains that string. The HTML is one self-contained file that runs from `file://` and from `http://127.0.0.1` (scripts and fonts inlined; no external script or font URLs). It includes exactly one unmodified AI Hub session client (SHA-256 equals the released hash for the vendored version), the §14.6 hub meta tags in that exact `name`-then-`content` order and wording (no `hub:webgpu=required`), catalogue tags (`title` split on the dash, description, `theme-color` `#17707A`, inline SVG icon, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` `1–4`, `hub:source` `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`), and an About/Credits screen whose `#about-data` JSON shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback with PLAN §19’s fixed values. The same four blocks are in the finishing chat reply. Own source has no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, or `stub`. A short authoring note explains how to add an operation, a strain, a story scene, and a tuning value.\\n\\n2. Surgical simulation. A headless sim (no renderer, DOM, or audio) steps at fixed 1/60 from seeded RNG only (`Math.random` absent from sim code). It implements the beat clock (`bpm` rises as vitals fall; beat drives tissue, ECG, strains, music tempo); vitals, timer, and miss failures; grades FLAWLESS/CLEAN/ROUGH/MISS, combo, and ranks S/A/B/C/D titled Chief of Surgery / Attending / Resident / Intern / Malpractice Suit Pending (never XS, Bad, Good, or Cool); all eight wheel tools plus syringe and defibrillator with the PLAN §4 rules (including analog use, nicks, tears, clamp-on-beat, defib gold band, clamps off before the end); Hush and Sforzando; Intern/Resident/Attending multipliers; phase checkpoints (retry restores vitals ≥60, timer ≥90s, checkpoint score) and optional Bea’s Notes after two failures of the same phase; consults (careful vs aggressive). Same seed and inputs yield the same state hash twice. At the busiest 4-seat Grand Rounds moment the unreliable snapshot is ≤1100 bytes and the keyframe ≤16 KB. Data lint: every touchable spawn lies inside the drape ellipse, `teaches` covers the eight wheel tools, syringe, defib, both gifts, and all seven strains, and no Bea line contains “good” except the final scene.\\n10→\\n3. Demo content a bot can finish. Playable vertical slice: operations Broken Glass, Growth Spurt, Adagio, Staccato, Legato, Fermata, Coda, Last Patient, and Grand Rounds, with strains Adagio, Staccato, Tremolo, Legato, Crescendo, Fermata, and Coda behaving as in PLAN §5, original cast and setting (Port Calloway, St. Alder, Ward Zero, Ren, Bea, Bell, Pip, Sorrento, Ines, Voss/REQUIEM/the Hush — never Derek Stiles, Angie Thompson, Naomi Kimishima, Caduceus, Delphi, GUILT or its strain names, Healing Touch, star drawing, or Hope Hospital). Story scenes S0–S16, 250–350 lines, must-have lines present, scenes skippable. Phases are data and `skipTo` works. On Normal, a bot that reads only sim state clears each operation (Last Patient only has to complete: no timer, no rank, cannot fail) in 45–75% of that op’s timer, minimum vitals ≥35, rank ≥A; `parScore` is taken from that bot. A sloppy bot (noise and reaction delay) on Easy clears at rank ≥C. No input fails every op except Last Patient. Story order through Last Patient, and Grand Rounds at 1, 2, 3, and 4 seats (counts and strain HP scale as PLAN §6), all complete.\\n\\n4. Playable presentation, input, and shell. The shipped page boots a Three.js r180 scene with cel-shaded/toon materials, the ink/halftone filter, code-built organs, instruments, and strains, and Rapier-backed pulls, on WebGPU under PLAN §16.3’s five flags and on WebGL2 without them, with zero page errors. The render surface’s drawing size equals the requested size and is substantially filled (not a blank or a few pixels). Pad (standard mapping), keyboard, and mouse drive the same screens: tip, eight-way wheel, analog use, hover-moves-focus, prompts follow the last device (`data-prompt-set`; PlayStation glyphs default, Xbox via Settings). All music, effects, and Animalese/Simlish voices are synthesized (no audio files); music-bus gain defaults to 0.10. Touch-only (`(any-pointer: fine)` false and no pad) shows exactly “Controller or keyboard required” plus a tappable Settings button, no touch controls, and attract mode still runs. Attract mode starts after 10 s of wall-clock idle on Title, Main Menu, Free Play, and the touch notice, loops a cheated play of many ops, and any input returns to the previous screen without saving. Dev mode opens from pause (hidden in hub sessions) with the PLAN §13 tools and live sliders (current value, default tick, per-page and global reset) that change the sim immediately. Progress survives reload outside a session. A scripted UI playthrough reaches Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits; Fail, Free Play, Lobby, Settings, About, and the touch notice are reachable. Missing graphics shows a friendly screen instead of crashing.\\n\\n5. Multiplayer, hub and couch. With no hub the page starts the standalone game (`AIHub.active` false, `Math.random` untouched). In a session it uses shared-world, seats 1–4, own card: straight into Grand Rounds (no title, menus, attract, story, dev, or saves); pause is Settings only and the sim keeps running; network only through the hub; host alone runs the sim (including a viewless server copy) on a timer not tied to animation frames; clients render snapshots; the local tip is instant; `finish()` is host-only and reports standings, scores, won, stats, and awards. Couch Grand Rounds: up to four seats on one screen; two pads join, move two tips independently, and both score. The real hub harness passes all of: 2 players; 3 players and 4 players at ~150 ms ±50 ms and 5% loss; host-leave; server copy; and the 4-player case again on WebGL2 — each with `__hubCheck.pass === true` and no console line starting with `[AIHub]`. The standalone harness sequence (Enter, Space, Enter, Space) throws nothing and the shot is not blank.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: Add or update in-repo tests that import the shipped sim (no reimplementation, no mocking the sim, no hardcoded full-state oracles) and assert criterion 2 and 3: each tool and strain rule, determinism by comparing two runs, snapshot byte caps, data lint, banned names, bot Normal/Easy/idle invariants, story order, Grand Rounds at 1–4 seats. Run the one shipped command for the sim suite (PLAN §17: `node tests/run-all.mjs sim`). It must print only failures plus a one-line count and exit 0. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/sim.log`.\\n2. gating: Browser suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs browser`) drives the shipped page, including `?test=1` hooks that call into the real sim, and asserts criterion 4: WebGPU boot with the five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, WebGL2 boot without them, WebKit boot, zero page errors, non-blank shots, pad/mouse/key input (full right stick for 1 s moves the tip by `tipSpeed` ±5%), prompt set and Xbox glyphs, dev-mode slider changes the sim and reset restores defaults, attract at 10 s ±1 s and exit without a save, Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 profiles show the exact touch notice and a working Settings tap, OfflineAudioContext output is non-silent for every track, effect, and voice, music gain 0.10, no audio-file references, save survives reload, About fields and `#about-data` parse, two stub pads score in couch play, UI playthrough `state().reached` contains Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits roll, packaging checks from criterion 1. Exit 0; failures-only output. Save `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n20→3. gating: Hub suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs hub`) copies the built page into the real harness from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` and runs every row in criterion 5 (1280×860, up to 300 s, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, `__hubCheck.pass === true`, no `[AIHub]` console line), plus the on-its-own Enter/Space sequence. Exit 0. Save `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Launch the real root HTML twice, from `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1` (bind `127.0.0.1` on an OS-picked port; confirm `window.__game` exists before trusting the page). Use the five flags above. Each run: zero page errors; canvas drawing buffer equals the requested size; painted fraction is high (a blank or speck fails — do not treat a successful blank readback as a missing tool); a driven input (stub pad or mouse) changes the on-screen tip or HUD, visible in a second capture. Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch.log` and rely on steps 1–3; a started browser that returns an empty buffer is a failure to fix.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, capture Title, Main Menu, a story shout, calm operation, danger, Hush, each strain, Report, Settings, About, the session card, one upright HUD portrait, and one upright cut-in under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Use them only to fix ten-foot type, ink, and overlap; they do not gate if steps 1–4 pass.\\n6. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json`; confirm the root HTML and dev-folder names; confirm the client hash and that the hub banner string appears once; confirm own source (not the bundle) has no banned source names, no `Math.random` in the sim, and no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub. Record results in `{SCRATCH}/package.log`.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, frame-time optimization, or lowering scene detail to chase performance.\\n- Playable post-credits “Opus 2”, online play outside AI Hub, custom names, chat, or emotes.\\n- Touch-screen gameplay controls, a second desktop layout, or Firefox WebGL2 (headless Firefox here has no WebGL2).\\n- Hardware rumble feel, a human listener, real iOS Safari, or a physical DualSense (stub the pad; guard a missing vibration actuator).\\n30→- Source-game IP, star-drawing specials, or the source’s grade names.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nGreenfield work folder (`PLAN.md`, `STAGE.md`, `TASK.md` only). New dev subfolder plus root HTML, `PROGRESS.md`, and `exit-interview.json`. Dependencies installed inside the dev folder: `three@0.180.0`, `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3`, `esbuild@0.28.2`, `playwright@1.63.0`, `@fontsource/bangers`, `@fontsource/barlow-condensed`. Hub `session.js` and harness files downloaded from `michaelcrosato/ai-hub` `lib/hub`. Browsers already on the machine; do not run `playwright install`. Tests and screenshots stay inside the dev folder; command logs copied to `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for rules and content; the layout there is guidance so the sim stays testable, not a reason to reject an equivalent structure. Keep the operation sim pure (JSON state, seeded RNG, fixed 1/60, Rapier in field space) so Node tests and the bot drive it with no browser. Let the view, audio, and DOM reconcile that state or a decoded snapshot, never own the rules. Build operations, strains, and scenes as data. Ship one command that runs sim, then browser, then hub, and prints only failures and a count. Inline the browser bundle so `file://` works. Use the five WebGPU flags from PLAN §16.3, not the shorter set in TASK.md. One browser at a time. Stop only processes this work started, by PID.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Scaffold the dev folder, identity (RNG title), tuning defaults, package, inlined single-file build, vendored hub client, and a test command that prints only failures and a count.\\n40→- [ ] Implement the headless sim: beat, vitals, scoring, tools, gifts, checkpoints, and Op 1; bot clears Op 1; sim tests green.\\n- [ ] Render the operative field (toon, ink, Rapier juice, HUD, pad/mouse/keys) so Op 1 is playable through the report on WebGPU and WebGL2.\\n- [ ] Add remaining tools, Hush, Sforzando, all seven strains, ops 2–7, Last Patient, and Grand Rounds; bot invariants hold.\\n- [ ] Add story scenes, busts, procedural music, effects, and gibberish voices (music gain 0.10).\\n- [ ] Add menus, chart, free play, settings, glyphs, touch notice, save, About, credits, attract mode, and dev mode.\\n- [ ] Add couch co-op and hub session (card, snapshots, host/server rules) until every hub harness run passes.\\n- [ ] Calibrate `parScore`, write the authoring note, fill About and `exit-interview.json`, copy the HTML to the root name, and save sim, browser, hub, and two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md’s shorter WebGPU flags drop the device after the first frame on this machine; PLAN §16.3’s five flags are the ones that draw. A blank readback with those five flags is an app bug, not an excuse to skip the launch check.\\n50→- Software WebGPU is ~260–410 ms/frame and earlyoom kills extra browsers. Hub runs may need the full 300 s budget. Run one browser. If the harness process itself cannot start, capture that log; do not substitute a mocked hub result.\\n- The required HTML and folder names include spaces and a colon (`Trauma Center: Second Opinion`). Keep that literal pattern; Linux allows it.\\n- The released hub-client hash may no longer be the 1.4.0 value in PLAN §16.2 if upstream moved. Hash the vendored file against `RELEASES` in `scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs` and require a match; do not edit the client.\\n- Pad-only audio unlock and real rumble cannot be proven here. Cover synthesis with `OfflineAudioContext` and a missing-actuator guard; say so in Testing Feedback.\\n- Headless Firefox has no WebGL2 here. Do not block on it. WebKit WebGL2 and Chromium WebGPU plus WebGL2 are the bar.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Grand Rounds waves at 45s, 90s, 130s, and 165s (plan: 60, 135, 210, 255) so a one-player finish stays inside 45–75% of the 5:00 timer.\\n- Coda batons are 9 HP so one beat of laser drops an arm; the plan text reads about 0.5 s.\\n- Coda cue notes live 5 beats, and a beam resting on a dropped baton singes a cue within 0.14 without scorching.\\n60→- The grande Adagio has 100 HP, not 150.\\n- Growth Spurt's crash sets vitals to 48 and drains 1/s, not 35 and 3/s.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Plan: Build the surgical-action demo PLAN.md specifies, and hand in every artifact TASK.md and STAGE.md require\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. Hand-in package. The work folder contains `PROGRESS.md`, a parsable `exit-interview.json` beside the game HTML (one object, every TASK.md key filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, `aiHub.type` Game, `aiHub.genre` Simulation, `aiHub.source` `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, `aiHub.series` `Trauma Center`, `aiHub.players` `1–4`, controls and tags as PLAN §19), a dev subfolder named `{Title}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230`, and one root file `{Title}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230.html`. `{Title}` is an original playful riff on the source (50 titles brainstormed, then one picked with a real RNG), shown on the title screen, and stored so no other source file contains that string. The HTML is one self-contained file that runs from `file://` and from `http://127.0.0.1` (scripts and fonts inlined; no external script or font URLs). It includes exactly one unmodified AI Hub session client (SHA-256 equals the released hash for the vendored version), the §14.6 hub meta tags in that exact `name`-then-`content` order and wording (no `hub:webgpu=required`), catalogue tags (`title` split on the dash, description, `theme-color` `#17707A`, inline SVG icon, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` `1–4`, `hub:source` `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`), and an About/Credits screen whose `#about-data` JSON shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback with PLAN §19’s fixed values. The same four blocks are in the finishing chat reply. Own source has no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, or `stub`. A short authoring note explains how to add an operation, a strain, a story scene, and a tuning value.\\n\\n2. Surgical simulation. A headless sim (no renderer, DOM, or audio) steps at fixed 1/60 from seeded RNG only (`Math.random` absent from sim code). It implements the beat clock (`bpm` rises as vitals fall; beat drives tissue, ECG, strains, music tempo); vitals, timer, and miss failures; grades FLAWLESS/CLEAN/ROUGH/MISS, combo, and ranks S/A/B/C/D titled Chief of Surgery / Attending / Resident / Intern / Malpractice Suit Pending (never XS, Bad, Good, or Cool); all eight wheel tools plus syringe and defibrillator with the PLAN §4 rules (including analog use, nicks, tears, clamp-on-beat, defib gold band, clamps off before the end); Hush and Sforzando; Intern/Resident/Attending multipliers; phase checkpoints (retry restores vitals ≥60, timer ≥90s, checkpoint score) and optional Bea’s Notes after two failures of the same phase; consults (careful vs aggressive). Same seed and inputs yield the same state hash twice. At the busiest 4-seat Grand Rounds moment the unreliable snapshot is ≤1100 bytes and the keyframe ≤16 KB. Data lint: every touchable spawn lies inside the drape ellipse, `teaches` covers the eight wheel tools, syringe, defib, both gifts, and all seven strains, and no Bea line contains “good” except the final scene.\\n10→\\n3. Demo content a bot can finish. Playable vertical slice: operations Broken Glass, Growth Spurt, Adagio, Staccato, Legato, Fermata, Coda, Last Patient, and Grand Rounds, with strains Adagio, Staccato, Tremolo, Legato, Crescendo, Fermata, and Coda behaving as in PLAN §5, original cast and setting (Port Calloway, St. Alder, Ward Zero, Ren, Bea, Bell, Pip, Sorrento, Ines, Voss/REQUIEM/the Hush — never Derek Stiles, Angie Thompson, Naomi Kimishima, Caduceus, Delphi, GUILT or its strain names, Healing Touch, star drawing, or Hope Hospital). Story scenes S0–S16, 250–350 lines, must-have lines present, scenes skippable. Phases are data and `skipTo` works. On Normal, a bot that reads only sim state clears each operation (Last Patient only has to complete: no timer, no rank, cannot fail) in 45–75% of that op’s timer, minimum vitals ≥35, rank ≥A; `parScore` is taken from that bot. A sloppy bot (noise and reaction delay) on Easy clears at rank ≥C. No input fails every op except Last Patient. Story order through Last Patient, and Grand Rounds at 1, 2, 3, and 4 seats (counts and strain HP scale as PLAN §6), all complete.\\n\\n4. Playable presentation, input, and shell. The shipped page boots a Three.js r180 scene with cel-shaded/toon materials, the ink/halftone filter, code-built organs, instruments, and strains, and Rapier-backed pulls, on WebGPU under PLAN §16.3’s five flags and on WebGL2 without them, with zero page errors. The render surface’s drawing size equals the requested size and is substantially filled (not a blank or a few pixels). Pad (standard mapping), keyboard, and mouse drive the same screens: tip, eight-way wheel, analog use, hover-moves-focus, prompts follow the last device (`data-prompt-set`; PlayStation glyphs default, Xbox via Settings). All music, effects, and Animalese/Simlish voices are synthesized (no audio files); music-bus gain defaults to 0.10. Touch-only (`(any-pointer: fine)` false and no pad) shows exactly “Controller or keyboard required” plus a tappable Settings button, no touch controls, and attract mode still runs. Attract mode starts after 10 s of wall-clock idle on Title, Main Menu, Free Play, and the touch notice, loops a cheated play of many ops, and any input returns to the previous screen without saving. Dev mode opens from pause (hidden in hub sessions) with the PLAN §13 tools and live sliders (current value, default tick, per-page and global reset) that change the sim immediately. Progress survives reload outside a session. A scripted UI playthrough reaches Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits; Fail, Free Play, Lobby, Settings, About, and the touch notice are reachable. Missing graphics shows a friendly screen instead of crashing.\\n\\n5. Multiplayer, hub and couch. With no hub the page starts the standalone game (`AIHub.active` false, `Math.random` untouched). In a session it uses shared-world, seats 1–4, own card: straight into Grand Rounds (no title, menus, attract, story, dev, or saves); pause is Settings only and the sim keeps running; network only through the hub; host alone runs the sim (including a viewless server copy) on a timer not tied to animation frames; clients render snapshots; the local tip is instant; `finish()` is host-only and reports standings, scores, won, stats, and awards. Couch Grand Rounds: up to four seats on one screen; two pads join, move two tips independently, and both score. The real hub harness passes all of: 2 players; 3 players and 4 players at ~150 ms ±50 ms and 5% loss; host-leave; server copy; and the 4-player case again on WebGL2 — each with `__hubCheck.pass === true` and no console line starting with `[AIHub]`. The standalone harness sequence (Enter, Space, Enter, Space) throws nothing and the shot is not blank.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: Add or update in-repo tests that import the shipped sim (no reimplementation, no mocking the sim, no hardcoded full-state oracles) and assert criterion 2 and 3: each tool and strain rule, determinism by comparing two runs, snapshot byte caps, data lint, banned names, bot Normal/Easy/idle invariants, story order, Grand Rounds at 1–4 seats. Run the one shipped command for the sim suite (PLAN §17: `node tests/run-all.mjs sim`). It must print only failures plus a one-line count and exit 0. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/sim.log`.\\n2. gating: Browser suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs browser`) drives the shipped page, including `?test=1` hooks that call into the real sim, and asserts criterion 4: WebGPU boot with the five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, WebGL2 boot without them, WebKit boot, zero page errors, non-blank shots, pad/mouse/key input (full right stick for 1 s moves the tip by `tipSpeed` ±5%), prompt set and Xbox glyphs, dev-mode slider changes the sim and reset restores defaults, attract at 10 s ±1 s and exit without a save, Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 profiles show the exact touch notice and a working Settings tap, OfflineAudioContext output is non-silent for every track, effect, and voice, music gain 0.10, no audio-file references, save survives reload, About fields and `#about-data` parse, two stub pads score in couch play, UI playthrough `state().reached` contains Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits roll, packaging checks from criterion 1. Exit 0; failures-only output. Save `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n20→3. gating: Hub suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs hub`) copies the built page into the real harness from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` and runs every row in criterion 5 (1280×860, up to 300 s, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, `__hubCheck.pass === true`, no `[AIHub]` console line), plus the on-its-own Enter/Space sequence. Exit 0. Save `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Launch the real root HTML twice, from `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1` (bind `127.0.0.1` on an OS-picked port; confirm `window.__game` exists before trusting the page). Use the five flags above. Each run: zero page errors; canvas drawing buffer equals the requested size; painted fraction is high (a blank or speck fails — do not treat a successful blank readback as a missing tool); a driven input (stub pad or mouse) changes the on-screen tip or HUD, visible in a second capture. Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch.log` and rely on steps 1–3; a started browser that returns an empty buffer is a failure to fix.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, capture Title, Main Menu, a story shout, calm operation, danger, Hush, each strain, Report, Settings, About, the session card, one upright HUD portrait, and one upright cut-in under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Use them only to fix ten-foot type, ink, and overlap; they do not gate if steps 1–4 pass.\\n6. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json`; confirm the root HTML and dev-folder names; confirm the client hash and that the hub banner string appears once; confirm own source (not the bundle) has no banned source names, no `Math.random` in the sim, and no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub. Record results in `{SCRATCH}/package.log`.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, frame-time optimization, or lowering scene detail to chase performance.\\n- Playable post-credits “Opus 2”, online play outside AI Hub, custom names, chat, or emotes.\\n- Touch-screen gameplay controls, a second desktop layout, or Firefox WebGL2 (headless Firefox here has no WebGL2).\\n- Hardware rumble feel, a human listener, real iOS Safari, or a physical DualSense (stub the pad; guard a missing vibration actuator).\\n30→- Source-game IP, star-drawing specials, or the source’s grade names.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nGreenfield work folder (`PLAN.md`, `STAGE.md`, `TASK.md` only). New dev subfolder plus root HTML, `PROGRESS.md`, and `exit-interview.json`. Dependencies installed inside the dev folder: `three@0.180.0`, `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3`, `esbuild@0.28.2`, `playwright@1.63.0`, `@fontsource/bangers`, `@fontsource/barlow-condensed`. Hub `session.js` and harness files downloaded from `michaelcrosato/ai-hub` `lib/hub`. Browsers already on the machine; do not run `playwright install`. Tests and screenshots stay inside the dev folder; command logs copied to `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for rules and content; the layout there is guidance so the sim stays testable, not a reason to reject an equivalent structure. Keep the operation sim pure (JSON state, seeded RNG, fixed 1/60, Rapier in field space) so Node tests and the bot drive it with no browser. Let the view, audio, and DOM reconcile that state or a decoded snapshot, never own the rules. Build operations, strains, and scenes as data. Ship one command that runs sim, then browser, then hub, and prints only failures and a count. Inline the browser bundle so `file://` works. Use the five WebGPU flags from PLAN §16.3, not the shorter set in TASK.md. One browser at a time. Stop only processes this work started, by PID.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Scaffold the dev folder, identity (RNG title), tuning defaults, package, inlined single-file build, vendored hub client, and a test command that prints only failures and a count.\\n40→- [ ] Implement the headless sim: beat, vitals, scoring, tools, gifts, checkpoints, and Op 1; bot clears Op 1; sim tests green.\\n- [ ] Render the operative field (toon, ink, Rapier juice, HUD, pad/mouse/keys) so Op 1 is playable through the report on WebGPU and WebGL2.\\n- [ ] Add remaining tools, Hush, Sforzando, all seven strains, ops 2–7, Last Patient, and Grand Rounds; bot invariants hold.\\n- [ ] Add story scenes, busts, procedural music, effects, and gibberish voices (music gain 0.10).\\n- [ ] Add menus, chart, free play, settings, glyphs, touch notice, save, About, credits, attract mode, and dev mode.\\n- [ ] Add couch co-op and hub session (card, snapshots, host/server rules) until every hub harness run passes.\\n- [ ] Calibrate `parScore`, write the authoring note, fill About and `exit-interview.json`, copy the HTML to the root name, and save sim, browser, hub, and two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md’s shorter WebGPU flags drop the device after the first frame on this machine; PLAN §16.3’s five flags are the ones that draw. A blank readback with those five flags is an app bug, not an excuse to skip the launch check.\\n50→- Software WebGPU is ~260–410 ms/frame and earlyoom kills extra browsers. Hub runs may need the full 300 s budget. Run one browser. If the harness process itself cannot start, capture that log; do not substitute a mocked hub result.\\n- The required HTML and folder names include spaces and a colon (`Trauma Center: Second Opinion`). Keep that literal pattern; Linux allows it.\\n- The released hub-client hash may no longer be the 1.4.0 value in PLAN §16.2 if upstream moved. Hash the vendored file against `RELEASES` in `scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs` and require a match; do not edit the client.\\n- Pad-only audio unlock and real rumble cannot be proven here. Cover synthesis with `OfflineAudioContext` and a missing-actuator guard; say so in Testing Feedback.\\n- Headless Firefox has no WebGL2 here. Do not block on it. WebKit WebGL2 and Chromium WebGPU plus WebGL2 are the bar.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Grand Rounds waves at 45s, 90s, 130s, and 165s (plan: 60, 135, 210, 255) so a one-player finish stays inside 45–75% of the 5:00 timer.\\n- Coda batons are 9 HP so one beat of laser drops an arm; the plan text reads about 0.5 s.\\n- Coda cue notes live 5 beats, and a beam resting on a dropped baton singes a cue within 0.14 without scorching.\\n60→- The grande Adagio has 100 HP, not 150.\\n- Growth Spurt's crash sets vitals to 48 and drains 1/s, not 35 and 3/s.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Plan: Build the surgical-action demo PLAN.md specifies, and hand in every artifact TASK.md and STAGE.md require\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. Hand-in package. The work folder contains `PROGRESS.md`, a parsable `exit-interview.json` beside the game HTML (one object, every TASK.md key filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, `aiHub.type` Game, `aiHub.genre` Simulation, `aiHub.source` `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`, `aiHub.series` `Trauma Center`, `aiHub.players` `1–4`, controls and tags as PLAN §19), a dev subfolder named `{Title}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230`, and one root file `{Title}-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230.html`. `{Title}` is an original playful riff on the source (50 titles brainstormed, then one picked with a real RNG), shown on the title screen, and stored so no other source file contains that string. The HTML is one self-contained file that runs from `file://` and from `http://127.0.0.1` (scripts and fonts inlined; no external script or font URLs). It includes exactly one unmodified AI Hub session client (SHA-256 equals the released hash for the vendored version), the §14.6 hub meta tags in that exact `name`-then-`content` order and wording (no `hub:webgpu=required`), catalogue tags (`title` split on the dash, description, `theme-color` `#17707A`, inline SVG icon, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` `1–4`, `hub:source` `Trauma Center: Second Opinion`), and an About/Credits screen whose `#about-data` JSON shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback with PLAN §19’s fixed values. The same four blocks are in the finishing chat reply. Own source has no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, or `stub`. A short authoring note explains how to add an operation, a strain, a story scene, and a tuning value.\\n\\n2. Surgical simulation. A headless sim (no renderer, DOM, or audio) steps at fixed 1/60 from seeded RNG only (`Math.random` absent from sim code). It implements the beat clock (`bpm` rises as vitals fall; beat drives tissue, ECG, strains, music tempo); vitals, timer, and miss failures; grades FLAWLESS/CLEAN/ROUGH/MISS, combo, and ranks S/A/B/C/D titled Chief of Surgery / Attending / Resident / Intern / Malpractice Suit Pending (never XS, Bad, Good, or Cool); all eight wheel tools plus syringe and defibrillator with the PLAN §4 rules (including analog use, nicks, tears, clamp-on-beat, defib gold band, clamps off before the end); Hush and Sforzando; Intern/Resident/Attending multipliers; phase checkpoints (retry restores vitals ≥60, timer ≥90s, checkpoint score) and optional Bea’s Notes after two failures of the same phase; consults (careful vs aggressive). Same seed and inputs yield the same state hash twice. At the busiest 4-seat Grand Rounds moment the unreliable snapshot is ≤1100 bytes and the keyframe ≤16 KB. Data lint: every touchable spawn lies inside the drape ellipse, `teaches` covers the eight wheel tools, syringe, defib, both gifts, and all seven strains, and no Bea line contains “good” except the final scene.\\n\\n3. Demo content a bot can finish. Playable vertical slice: operations Broken Glass, Growth Spurt, Adagio, Staccato, Legato, Fermata, Coda, Last Patient, and Grand Rounds, with strains Adagio, Staccato, Tremolo, Legato, Crescendo, Fermata, and Coda behaving as in PLAN §5, original cast and setting (Port Calloway, St. Alder, Ward Zero, Ren, Bea, Bell, Pip, Sorrento, Ines, Voss/REQUIEM/the Hush — never Derek Stiles, Angie Thompson, Naomi Kimishima, Caduceus, Delphi, GUILT or its strain names, Healing Touch, star drawing, or Hope Hospital). Story scenes S0–S16, 250–350 lines, must-have lines present, scenes skippable. Phases are data and `skipTo` works. On Normal, a bot that reads only sim state clears each operation (Last Patient only has to complete: no timer, no rank, cannot fail) in 45–75% of that op’s timer, minimum vitals ≥35, rank ≥A; `parScore` is taken from that bot. A sloppy bot (noise and reaction delay) on Easy clears at rank ≥C. No input fails every op except Last Patient. Story order through Last Patient, and Grand Rounds at 1, 2, 3, and 4 seats (counts and strain HP scale as PLAN §6), all complete.\\n\\n4. Playable presentation, input, and shell. The shipped page boots a Three.js r180 scene with cel-shaded/toon materials, the ink/halftone filter, code-built organs, instruments, and strains, and Rapier-backed pulls, on WebGPU under PLAN §16.3’s five flags and on WebGL2 without them, with zero page errors. The render surface’s drawing size equals the requested size and is substantially filled (not a blank or a few pixels). Pad (standard mapping), keyboard, and mouse drive the same screens: tip, eight-way wheel, analog use, hover-moves-focus, prompts follow the last device (`data-prompt-set`; PlayStation glyphs default, Xbox via Settings). All music, effects, and Animalese/Simlish voices are synthesized (no audio files); music-bus gain defaults to 0.10. Touch-only (`(any-pointer: fine)` false and no pad) shows exactly “Controller or keyboard required” plus a tappable Settings button, no touch controls, and attract mode still runs. Attract mode starts after 10 s of wall-clock idle on Title, Main Menu, Free Play, and the touch notice, loops a cheated play of many ops, and any input returns to the previous screen without saving. Dev mode opens from pause (hidden in hub sessions) with the PLAN §13 tools and live sliders (current value, default tick, per-page and global reset) that change the sim immediately. Progress survives reload outside a session. A scripted UI playthrough reaches Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits; Fail, Free Play, Lobby, Settings, About, and the touch notice are reachable. Missing graphics shows a friendly screen instead of crashing.\\n\\n5. Multiplayer, hub and couch. With no hub the page starts the standalone game (`AIHub.active` false, `Math.random` untouched). In a session it uses shared-world, seats 1–4, own card: straight into Grand Rounds (no title, menus, attract, story, dev, or saves); pause is Settings only and the sim keeps running; network only through the hub; host alone runs the sim (including a viewless server copy) on a timer not tied to animation frames; clients render snapshots; the local tip is instant; `finish()` is host-only and reports standings, scores, won, stats, and awards. Couch Grand Rounds: up to four seats on one screen; two pads join, move two tips independently, and both score. The real hub harness passes all of: 2 players; 3 players and 4 players at ~150 ms ±50 ms and 5% loss; host-leave; server copy; and the 4-player case again on WebGL2 — each with `__hubCheck.pass === true` and no console line starting with `[AIHub]`. The standalone harness sequence (Enter, Space, Enter, Space) throws nothing and the shot is not blank.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: Add or update in-repo tests that import the shipped sim (no reimplementation, no mocking the sim, no hardcoded full-state oracles) and assert criterion 2 and 3: each tool and strain rule, determinism by comparing two runs, snapshot byte caps, data lint, banned names, bot Normal/Easy/idle invariants, story order, Grand Rounds at 1–4 seats. Run the one shipped command for the sim suite (PLAN §17: `node tests/run-all.mjs sim`). It must print only failures plus a one-line count and exit 0. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/sim.log`.\\n2. gating: Browser suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs browser`) drives the shipped page, including `?test=1` hooks that call into the real sim, and asserts criterion 4: WebGPU boot with the five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, WebGL2 boot without them, WebKit boot, zero page errors, non-blank shots, pad/mouse/key input (full right stick for 1 s moves the tip by `tipSpeed` ±5%), prompt set and Xbox glyphs, dev-mode slider changes the sim and reset restores defaults, attract at 10 s ±1 s and exit without a save, Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 profiles show the exact touch notice and a working Settings tap, OfflineAudioContext output is non-silent for every track, effect, and voice, music gain 0.10, no audio-file references, save survives reload, About fields and `#about-data` parse, two stub pads score in couch play, UI playthrough `state().reached` contains Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits roll, packaging checks from criterion 1. Exit 0; failures-only output. Save `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n3. gating: Hub suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs hub`) copies the built page into the real harness from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` and runs every row in criterion 5 (1280×860, up to 300 s, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, `__hubCheck.pass === true`, no `[AIHub]` console line), plus the on-its-own Enter/Space sequence. Exit 0. Save `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Launch the real root HTML twice, from `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1` (bind `127.0.0.1` on an OS-picked port; confirm `window.__game` exists before trusting the page). Use the five flags above. Each run: zero page errors; canvas drawing buffer equals the requested size; painted fraction is high (a blank or speck fails — do not treat a successful blank readback as a missing tool); a driven input (stub pad or mouse) changes the on-screen tip or HUD, visible in a second capture. Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch.log` and rely on steps 1–3; a started browser that returns an empty buffer is a failure to fix.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, capture Title, Main Menu, a story shout, calm operation, danger, Hush, each strain, Report, Settings, About, the session card, one upright HUD portrait, and one upright cut-in under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Use them only to fix ten-foot type, ink, and overlap; they do not gate if steps 1–4 pass.\\n6. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json`; confirm the root HTML and dev-folder names; confirm the client hash and that the hub banner string appears once; confirm own source (not the bundle) has no banned source names, no `Math.random` in the sim, and no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub. Record results in `{SCRATCH}/package.log`.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, frame-time optimization, or lowering scene detail to chase performance.\\n- Playable post-credits “Opus 2”, online play outside AI Hub, custom names, chat, or emotes.\\n- Touch-screen gameplay controls, a second desktop layout, or Firefox WebGL2 (headless Firefox here has no WebGL2).\\n- Hardware rumble feel, a human listener, real iOS Safari, or a physical DualSense (stub the pad; guard a missing vibration actuator).\\n- Source-game IP, star-drawing specials, or the source’s grade names.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nGreenfield work folder (`PLAN.md`, `STAGE.md`, `TASK.md` only). New dev subfolder plus root HTML, `PROGRESS.md`, and `exit-interview.json`. Dependencies installed inside the dev folder: `three@0.180.0`, `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3`, `esbuild@0.28.2`, `playwright@1.63.0`, `@fontsource/bangers`, `@fontsource/barlow-condensed`. Hub `session.js` and harness files downloaded from `michaelcrosato/ai-hub` `lib/hub`. Browsers already on the machine; do not run `playwright install`. Tests and screenshots stay inside the dev folder; command logs copied to `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md for rules and content; the layout there is guidance so the sim stays testable, not a reason to reject an equivalent structure. Keep the operation sim pure (JSON state, seeded RNG, fixed 1/60, Rapier in field space) so Node tests and the bot drive it with no browser. Let the view, audio, and DOM reconcile that state or a decoded snapshot, never own the rules. Build operations, strains, and scenes as data. Ship one command that runs sim, then browser, then hub, and prints only failures and a count. Inline the browser bundle so `file://` works. Use the five WebGPU flags from PLAN §16.3, not the shorter set in TASK.md. One browser at a time. Stop only processes this work started, by PID.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Scaffold the dev folder, identity (RNG title), tuning defaults, package, inlined single-file build, vendored hub client, and a test command that prints only failures and a count.\\n- [ ] Implement the headless sim: beat, vitals, scoring, tools, gifts, checkpoints, and Op 1; bot clears Op 1; sim tests green.\\n- [ ] Render the operative field (toon, ink, Rapier juice, HUD, pad/mouse/keys) so Op 1 is playable through the report on WebGPU and WebGL2.\\n- [ ] Add remaining tools, Hush, Sforzando, all seven strains, ops 2–7, Last Patient, and Grand Rounds; bot invariants hold.\\n- [ ] Add story scenes, busts, procedural music, effects, and gibberish voices (music gain 0.10).\\n- [ ] Add menus, chart, free play, settings, glyphs, touch notice, save, About, credits, attract mode, and dev mode.\\n- [ ] Add couch co-op and hub session (card, snapshots, host/server rules) until every hub harness run passes.\\n- [ ] Calibrate `parScore`, write the authoring note, fill About and `exit-interview.json`, copy the HTML to the root name, and save sim, browser, hub, and two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md’s shorter WebGPU flags drop the device after the first frame on this machine; PLAN §16.3’s five flags are the ones that draw. A blank readback with those five flags is an app bug, not an excuse to skip the launch check.\\n- Software WebGPU is ~260–410 ms/frame and earlyoom kills extra browsers. Hub runs may need the full 300 s budget. Run one browser. If the harness process itself cannot start, capture that log; do not substitute a mocked hub result.\\n- The required HTML and folder names include spaces and a colon (`Trauma Center: Second Opinion`). Keep that literal pattern; Linux allows it.\\n- The released hub-client hash may no longer be the 1.4.0 value in PLAN §16.2 if upstream moved. Hash the vendored file against `RELEASES` in `scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs` and require a match; do not edit the client.\\n- Pad-only audio unlock and real rumble cannot be proven here. Cover synthesis with `OfflineAudioContext` and a missing-actuator guard; say so in Testing Feedback.\\n- Headless Firefox has no WebGL2 here. Do not block on it. WebKit WebGL2 and Chromium WebGPU plus WebGL2 are the bar.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Grand Rounds waves at 45s, 90s, 130s, and 165s (plan: 60, 135, 210, 255) so a one-player finish stays inside 45–75% of the 5:00 timer.\\n- Coda batons are 9 HP so one beat of laser drops an arm; the plan text reads about 0.5 s.\\n- Coda cue notes live 5 beats, and a beam resting on a dropped baton singes a cue within 0.14 without scorching.\\n- The grande Adagio has 100 HP, not 150.\\n- Growth Spurt's crash sets vitals to 48 and drains 1/s, not 35 and 3/s.\\n\",\"total_lines\":61}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d0dc4cd5-9767-4776-958c-4ab75799b324"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_529","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a clear picture. I will write the core application files now.\n\nI'll use innerHTML carefully for director HTML rendering and textContent for hub names. I'm avoiding banned words like TODO, FIXME, stub, and placeholder in comments. I'll keep Math.random out of the director to preserve determinism, since only src/sim is required to use LCG.\n\nI'll keep all randomness in src/ to a counter-based LCG. The title string will live only in identity.js so tests can read it from the page.\n\nI'll keep the title string out of tests, docs, PROGRESS.md, and build.mjs. Tests can read it from identity.js or the page header instead.\n\nThe meta description has no quotes. The title tag will use an em dash between the game title and tagline. The icon will be an inline SVG heart.\n\nHub player counts will use an en dash in the catalogue and a hyphen in session-players. The client script will be placed immediately after the charset tag. Both the root game.html and tests/hub/site/game.html will be copies of the built dist file.\n\nThe root game file will be named with the title, version, and timestamp. The director's state model is being designed with screens, focus index, items, overlays, story progress, simulation state, attract mode, input tracking, reached scenes, settings, save data, and developer flags.\n\nThe director state model now includes sessionMode, couchSeats, page index, dialogue hold, bark text, and rankStamp. The title screen uses an invisible \"start\" item to route any confirm key into the main menu. The standalone test sequence must run without errors and produce a non-blank screenshot.\n\nThe title screen will render DOM text immediately, so the initial frame is never blank. The standalone test sequence is designed to avoid double-fires: Space on the title triggers the main menu, Enter confirms Story, and another Space advances the first story line. Input polling uses rising-edge detection with 500ms gaps between keystrokes to ensure clean keyup handling.\n\nAttract mode will swallow the input that exits it, preventing double navigation. The test step function polls input, applies samples, steps the simulation, and renders the DOM. Polling multiple times in a tight loop is safe because only the first step registers a rising edge while the key remains held.\n\nWarp mode will use synchronous test.step loops instead of animation frames, since software GPU frame timing is too slow. The bot logic will feed simulated inputs to each active seat during every step.\n\nAttract mode will advance its operation sequence on wall-clock time rather than simulation time. Because the software WebGPU renderer runs at only about 260 milliseconds per frame, a ten-second test window would translate to roughly forty frames and just sixty milliseconds of simulation. Advancing attract operations by wall-clock time keeps the test timing realistic.\n\nAttract mode will show operations in timed buckets: one operation for the first three seconds, another for the next three, and so on. The simulation will step a few times per frame with bot inputs to keep things moving. When the wall-clock bucket changes, the director will construct a new Sim instance and update the current operation state. The test will record seen operations in an array. Saving will be disabled during attract. Attract can start from the Title, Main Menu, Free Play, or Touch notice screens, but not from Settings, About, Lobby, Pause, Dev, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, or Credits. Exiting attract returns to the screen where it began.\n\nAttract mode will keep the current screen state unchanged while running, so the director returns to the same screen after attract ends. The operation demo will display underneath the existing view. Touch detection at boot will use a CSS media query for fine pointers.\n\nThe boot flow will show the Touch notice when no fine pointer is detected and no pad press has been seen yet. A pad press dismisses that notice and returns to the Title screen. The Touch notice itself will be reachable by tapping the Settings item, which must work via tap, and the back button from Settings will return there. Save data will use the key `st-alder-chart` and store version, difficulty, next operation, cleared scenes, ranks, settings, and unlock status. It will only be written when the player continues from a report or changes settings, never during attract mode or in session.\n\nThe Story screen will serve both the difficulty question and the opening scenes. If the player has cleared operations, the story resumes at the next operation's before scene instead of starting from S0. The chart unlocks only after S0 and S1 are completed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0fcc906a-728c-4aae-a953-d58280277c11-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"opts\\.cheat|cheat","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/bot.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4066,"output_tokens":2343,"cache_read_input_tokens":135040,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"75c88239-8a1d-4ae8-ae5d-7187099ab454"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0fcc906a-728c-4aae-a953-d58280277c11-72","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d65bb8b2-fc14-4a06-8aa1-88d8b8bfd931"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_530","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bot does not implement a cheat feature.\n\nCheats belong to the simulation, not the bot. The real bot will run through all operations in the browser. This should take about ten to thirty seconds. Skipping to the last phase is an alternative.\n\nThe bot will run operations in chunks of two thousand steps. Physics will be disabled to match node speed. The test will check for completion after each chunk. The last patient finishes without a rank. The report screen appears before the credits.\n\nThe credits screen is skippable with confirm or tab. It leads to the main menu.\n\nDev tools will expose commands for jumping, unlocking, scene changes, objectives, ranks, god mode, freezes, bleeder and strain types, music effects, timescale, single steps, auto mode, overlays, and ink toggles. Missing simulations are created on demand. Sliders will bind to simulation tuning keys.\n\nIf no simulation exists, a tuning object will be preserved for the next one. Slider changes mutate the shared tuning object directly, so live behavior updates immediately. Resetting restores the exact default values. The focused control is tracked by its data-item id. The active prompt set comes from input, and the glyph set defaults to \"playstation\" or the current settings.\n\nMusic gain is stored in audio.music.gain.value and exposed through state(). The render backend is view.backend or 'none'. Tuning is the live object. Tips are seat positions. Tool is seat 0. Rank is sim.rank?.id or null. A HUD will appear during operations. Visibility pause triggers when document.hidden is true and no session exists.\n\nCouch scoring will be verified by running the bot for roughly two thousand steps and checking that both seats score above zero. During couch testing, pressing pad buttons switches the device to pad mode, so both pads appear in the seats array and receive input through sim.input. Lobby joining works via confirm edge detection on each pad, marking the seat as joined and starting the begin item. For free play doctor choice, the test will pass ren or ines with a difficulty parameter.\n\nThe simulation doctor will be set after construction when the operation does not fix one, though the test may not verify this. Consult chart defaults to careful; begin uses the consult choice. The director module may reach 1500 to 2000 lines, which is acceptable. Session mode can reuse director exports for UI helpers, since it already owns its own DOM for cards, countdown, HUD, and settings.\n\nThe director will accept a mode parameter to distinguish standalone and session operation. The main entry point will connect to the AI hub, create the director with hub and URL parameters, then either start a session or launch standalone mode. In shared-world sessions, the pump begins immediately because the ready signal is sent before the view initializes.\n\nIn session mode, the game API is attached to window.__game synchronously before bootView runs. The pump starts immediately after handler registration and ready() is called right away. In standalone mode, the director is created and the API exposed in the same way.\n\nHeavy module parsing is acceptable because static imports are evaluated before main runs. The pump will start immediately without waiting for physics initialization; that setup happens inside the pump before the first simulation step.\n\nThe pump will run continuously via setTimeout, calling tick() each frame. BootAsync handles view initialization, physics setup, and simulation creation asynchronously without blocking the loop.\n\nClients send idle input before the simulation exists. The host sends the start signal only after the simulation is ready. The host must not wait for view initialization to begin the simulation, because that would delay the eight-second play window. Physics setup will proceed first, then the simulation is created.\n\nThe simulation and view initialization will run in parallel. The host awaits physics setup before creating the simulation, while the server skips both steps. The pump continues running concurrently. Snapshots begin flowing as soon as the simulation exists, and clients render once both the view and a snapshot are ready.\n\nInput will be read from pads and keys before the view exists. Mouse absolute positioning requires the camera, but stick input works without it.\n\nThe card screen uses DOM elements and appears immediately on session start, before the view loads. A window keydown listener will handle Enter to mark readiness during the card phase, bypassing any menu system that might intercept the event.\n\nTriangle maps to button 3 or the M key. The harness only sends Enter for ready, so additional controls should still be implemented.\n\nThe countdown displays while AIHub.time() is between negative three thousand and zero milliseconds. Once time reaches zero or passes it, the operation begins and the simulation steps forward.\n\nThe simulation will not step before the countdown ends. Clients send idle input only during play, not during the countdown itself.\n\nTo handle unreliable network traffic, keyframes are sent reliably and snapshots carry sequence numbers. If a snapshot arrives out of order or is dropped, the client ignores it. The latest snapshot is applied whenever it is newer than the current state.\n\nInput commands are merged into a per-player map. Each player's latest input overwrites the previous one, and the merged state is applied to the simulation before the step runs.\n\nHost local input overwrites the player's merged command each tick before the simulation step. The merge logic prevents a later absolute message from wiping an idle one. Events are sent reliably as batches at five per second. Snapshots are dropped if they exceed 1100 bytes to avoid fragmentation. The client checks JSON string length against that byte limit.\n\nThe renderer will receive decoded state for its sync call. Audio is active on the host and clients but not the server, and the audio context suspends when the session ends. Pausing during a session only opens the settings overlay; the simulation pump continues running. Session mode disables save and dev menu options. The game API still exposes state during a session, and screen names such as Card or Countdown are acceptable.\n\nThe host will send the final result only once, guarded by a finished flag. Standalone tests verify the exact screen names in the hub list, so those names must match exactly. Optional probe and progress messages are skipped to avoid extra network traffic.\n\nPresent players are sorted by score descending, then grouped into ties by matching scores. If the simulation is not ready when time-up arrives, the host finishes with every player tied at zero and won set to false.\n\nThe server is excluded from the simulation seats. A leave event removes the player from the simulation, and if the host leaves, the client stops without finishing.\n\nMessage handlers must not throw, because the client wraps them in setTimeout and any error becomes a page-level failure. I will run an early browser test to catch Three.js boot errors. Ink rendering and tool mesh cloning may need post-build fixes if they fail on first sync. The touch notice will reuse existing CSS classes.\n\nA minimal boot screen with an ECG line will appear while the view initializes. The canvas, UI, and WebGL fallback div are hidden by default and revealed once boot completes. A friendly no-graphics notice is included for browsers without WebGL.\n\nThe test API and devRun will be exposed whenever the test parameter is present, not just during tests. This makes debugging easier for both manual checks and automated runs.\n\nThe dev tool will step the simulation once even when paused. Auto-surgeon mode sets botOn. Time scale is adjusted via sim.cheats.timeScale. Force rank sets the simulation rank and completion flags directly, then shows the report; it does nothing if already over. Bleeder spawning at the active site tip needs to be verified against decorate handling.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e632b161-90ed-4f9c-af6f-1953ed146e82-73","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/physics.js","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e632b161-90ed-4f9c-af6f-1953ed146e82-74","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/barks.js","offset":90,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2506,"output_tokens":4110,"cache_read_input_tokens":139008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"f6e4d246-8d09-4a11-8f13-eebe0f104419"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e632b161-90ed-4f9c-af6f-1953ed146e82-73","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';\\n\\nlet ready = null;\\n\\nexport function physicsReady() {\\n  ready ??= RAPIER.init();\\n  return ready;\\n}\\n\\n10→/** Flat field: screen x → world x, screen y → world −z, tissue at y = 0. */\\nexport class FieldPhysics {\\n  constructor() {\\n    this.world = new RAPIER.World({ x: 0, y: -9.81, z: 0 });\\n    this.world.timestep = 1 / 60;\\n    this.tips = new Map();\\n    this.bodies = new Map();\\n    this.joints = new Map();\\n  }\\n\\n20→  tip(id, x, y) {\\n    let body = this.tips.get(id);\\n    if (!body) {\\n      body = this.world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased().setTranslation(x, 0.2, -y));\\n      this.tips.set(id, body);\\n    }\\n    body.setNextKinematicTranslation({ x, y: 0.2, z: -y });\\n    return body;\\n  }\\n\\n30→  ensureItem(e) {\\n    let body = this.bodies.get(e.id);\\n    if (body) return body;\\n    body = this.world.createRigidBody(\\n      RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(e.x, 0.15, -e.y).setLinearDamping(2).setAngularDamping(3),\\n    );\\n    this.world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.ball(0.05).setDensity(2), body);\\n    this.bodies.set(e.id, body);\\n    return body;\\n  }\\n40→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';\\n\\nlet ready = null;\\n\\nexport function physicsReady() {\\n  ready ??= RAPIER.init();\\n  return ready;\\n}\\n\\n10→/** Flat field: screen x → world x, screen y → world −z, tissue at y = 0. */\\nexport class FieldPhysics {\\n  constructor() {\\n    this.world = new RAPIER.World({ x: 0, y: -9.81, z: 0 });\\n    this.world.timestep = 1 / 60;\\n    this.tips = new Map();\\n    this.bodies = new Map();\\n    this.joints = new Map();\\n  }\\n\\n20→  tip(id, x, y) {\\n    let body = this.tips.get(id);\\n    if (!body) {\\n      body = this.world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased().setTranslation(x, 0.2, -y));\\n      this.tips.set(id, body);\\n    }\\n    body.setNextKinematicTranslation({ x, y: 0.2, z: -y });\\n    return body;\\n  }\\n\\n30→  ensureItem(e) {\\n    let body = this.bodies.get(e.id);\\n    if (body) return body;\\n    body = this.world.createRigidBody(\\n      RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(e.x, 0.15, -e.y).setLinearDamping(2).setAngularDamping(3),\\n    );\\n    this.world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.ball(0.05).setDensity(2), body);\\n    this.bodies.set(e.id, body);\\n    return body;\\n  }\\n40→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/physics.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"import RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';\\n\\nlet ready = null;\\n\\nexport function physicsReady() {\\n  ready ??= RAPIER.init();\\n  return ready;\\n}\\n\\n/** Flat field: screen x → world x, screen y → world −z, tissue at y = 0. */\\nexport class FieldPhysics {\\n  constructor() {\\n    this.world = new RAPIER.World({ x: 0, y: -9.81, z: 0 });\\n    this.world.timestep = 1 / 60;\\n    this.tips = new Map();\\n    this.bodies = new Map();\\n    this.joints = new Map();\\n  }\\n\\n  tip(id, x, y) {\\n    let body = this.tips.get(id);\\n    if (!body) {\\n      body = this.world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased().setTranslation(x, 0.2, -y));\\n      this.tips.set(id, body);\\n    }\\n    body.setNextKinematicTranslation({ x, y: 0.2, z: -y });\\n    return body;\\n  }\\n\\n  ensureItem(e) {\\n    let body = this.bodies.get(e.id);\\n    if (body) return body;\\n    body = this.world.createRigidBody(\\n      RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(e.x, 0.15, -e.y).setLinearDamping(2).setAngularDamping(3),\\n    );\\n    this.world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.ball(0.05).setDensity(2), body);\\n    this.bodies.set(e.id, body);\\n    return body;\\n  }\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":88}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e632b161-90ed-4f9c-af6f-1953ed146e82-74","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→    adagio: pack('Adagio. It crawls. Burn it, then lift it out.'),\\n    staccato: pack('Staccato. The holes sing. Seal them before the choir arrives.'),\\n    tremolo: pack('Tremolo. It shakes the vessels. Pin it before it spreads.'),\\n    legato: pack('Legato. A chain. Cut the links from the tail, and do not let them kiss.'),\\n    crescendo: pack('Crescendo. Starve the feeders before the bloom.'),\\n    fermata: pack('Fermata. The heart is holding. You shock it back onto the bar.'),\\n    coda: pack('Coda. Two arms, one core. Drop an arm or the downbeat lands.'),\\n  },\\n};\\n\\n100→export function barkText(key, arg, n = 0) {\\n  const row = BARKS[key];\\n  if (!row) return 'Stay with the field.';\\n  if (Array.isArray(row)) return row[Math.abs(n) % row.length].text;\\n  const leaf = (arg && row[arg]) || row.scalpel || row.adagio;\\n  return leaf?.text || 'Stay with the field.';\\n}\\n\\nexport function barkMood(key, arg, n = 0) {\\n  const row = BARKS[key];\\n110→  if (!row) return 'stern';\\n  if (Array.isArray(row)) return row[Math.abs(n) % row.length].mood;\\n  const leaf = (arg && row[arg]) || null;\\n  return leaf?.mood || 'stern';\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"90→    adagio: pack('Adagio. It crawls. Burn it, then lift it out.'),\\n    staccato: pack('Staccato. The holes sing. Seal them before the choir arrives.'),\\n    tremolo: pack('Tremolo. It shakes the vessels. Pin it before it spreads.'),\\n    legato: pack('Legato. A chain. Cut the links from the tail, and do not let them kiss.'),\\n    crescendo: pack('Crescendo. Starve the feeders before the bloom.'),\\n    fermata: pack('Fermata. The heart is holding. You shock it back onto the bar.'),\\n    coda: pack('Coda. Two arms, one core. Drop an arm or the downbeat lands.'),\\n  },\\n};\\n\\n100→export function barkText(key, arg, n = 0) {\\n  const row = BARKS[key];\\n  if (!row) return 'Stay with the field.';\\n  if (Array.isArray(row)) return row[Math.abs(n) % row.length].text;\\n  const leaf = (arg && row[arg]) || row.scalpel || row.adagio;\\n  return leaf?.text || 'Stay with the field.';\\n}\\n\\nexport function barkMood(key, arg, n = 0) {\\n  const row = BARKS[key];\\n110→  if (!row) return 'stern';\\n  if (Array.isArray(row)) return row[Math.abs(n) % row.length].mood;\\n  const leaf = (arg && row[arg]) || null;\\n  return leaf?.mood || 'stern';\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/barks.js\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"    adagio: pack('Adagio. It crawls. Burn it, then lift it out.'),\\n    staccato: pack('Staccato. The holes sing. Seal them before the choir arrives.'),\\n    tremolo: pack('Tremolo. It shakes the vessels. Pin it before it spreads.'),\\n    legato: pack('Legato. A chain. Cut the links from the tail, and do not let them kiss.'),\\n    crescendo: pack('Crescendo. Starve the feeders before the bloom.'),\\n    fermata: pack('Fermata. The heart is holding. You shock it back onto the bar.'),\\n    coda: pack('Coda. Two arms, one core. Drop an arm or the downbeat lands.'),\\n  },\\n};\\n\\nexport function barkText(key, arg, n = 0) {\\n  const row = BARKS[key];\\n  if (!row) return 'Stay with the field.';\\n  if (Array.isArray(row)) return row[Math.abs(n) % row.length].text;\\n  const leaf = (arg && row[arg]) || row.scalpel || row.adagio;\\n  return leaf?.text || 'Stay with the field.';\\n}\\n\\nexport function barkMood(key, arg, n = 0) {\\n  const row = BARKS[key];\\n  if (!row) return 'stern';\\n  if (Array.isArray(row)) return row[Math.abs(n) % row.length].mood;\\n  const leaf = (arg && row[arg]) || null;\\n  return leaf?.mood || 'stern';\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":114}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"ad1b11f3-691b-4627-a94c-a2ad3f5017b7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_531","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether world.free should be added at the end of physics.js.","signature":"86iCsHtM5bNmoBIKnb+xR0XDKUUGwwg37QIY83jSXG/KQeaRs5bcs/8SadrBrtbAQGUnrQkoCMDbZ5Yci+Ficqm9rEqLoaF20ZNMCC5P8QWDnpv8kruEhEM9Ch6WhWBr3TXFie0QYXLtGEb9BxzF"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef256cda-aded-4265-8e17-fcb754efb7ba-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"free\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/physics.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4933,"output_tokens":107,"cache_read_input_tokens":141440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"3dbc9f3c-3cff-4e77-8e63-48fc9ecae084"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ef256cda-aded-4265-8e17-fcb754efb7ba-75","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,47,65,108,105,118,101,32,105,110,32,67,111,109,109,111,110,32,84,105,109,101,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,32,67,101,110,116,101,114,58,32,83,101,99,111,110,100,32,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,47,115,114,99,47,115,105,109,47,112,104,121,115,105,99,115,46,106,115,10,56,53,58,32,32,102,114,101,101,40,41,32,123,10,56,54,58,32,32,32,32,116,104,105,115,46,119,111,114,108,100,46,102,114,101,101,40,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/physics.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"  free() {\"},{\"line_number\":86,\"content\":\"    this.world.free();\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0