{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_532","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed `sim.physics.free()` exists. Now writing all the files.\n\nPlanning the director's HUD ECG draw function and scene lookup by ID. Difficulty screen text will read \"How much do you hate yourself, child?\". Items are Intern, Resident, and Attending with Resident as the default focus. Rank display uses title and id. Report stats include time, vitals, precision, and best combo. Starting a menu structure helper.\n\nCompleted the `setScreen` helper to manage screen state, focus, and reached flags. Started wiring up `applyMenu` to handle attract mode exits and map menu controls from both the sample and seat edges.\n\nThe director's poll function does not expose pad axes, so up and down menu navigation cannot come from the left stick. Menu controls will rely on keyboard edges and pad buttons like confirm, back, and page. Pad-based menu navigation is possible but messy.\n\nAdding up and down menu navigation to pad edges in input.js using d-pad buttons and left stick axes. The director will merge pad0 edges into menu controls so keyboard and pad users can both navigate menus.\n\nCouch lobby joins will use each seat's confirm edge. Pad confirm is Cross during operations and must not trigger menu confirm outside overlays. Pause toggles via pad pause or keyboard back, resuming on back while paused. Enter serves as use during operations and as confirm during menus; both actions cannot fire at once.\n\nStandalone pause will freeze the simulation entirely. During a settings overlay, Enter may still trigger both confirmation and use, which is acceptable. The director will track the last site key to send a siteDelta edge only when the site changes or the sign appears, preventing continuous cycling while held.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-912893b7-905c-4d40-942c-3a610d5f668a-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js","offset":140,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":334,"output_tokens":1107,"cache_read_input_tokens":146304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"249b9de7-b331-4a7d-844a-d62641519128"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-912893b7-905c-4d40-942c-3a610d5f668a-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"140→  return e.hidden && !e.marked;\\n}\\n\\nexport function stepTools(sim, dt) {\\n  for (const seat of sim.seats) {\\n    if (seat.out) continue;\\n    const f = seat.cmd;\\n    if (f.tool && f.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = f.tool;\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'tool', seat: seat.id, tool: seat.tool });\\n150→    }\\n    const use = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, f.use || 0));\\n    seat.use = use;\\n    seat.steady = !!f.steady;\\n    if (rising(seat, 'swap')) sim.swapLead(seat);\\n    if (Number.isInteger(f.site)) sim.setSite(seat, f.site);\\n    if (f.siteDelta) sim.nudgeSite(seat, f.siteDelta);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'special')) tryGift(sim, seat);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'alt')) doAlt(sim, seat);\\n    stepSyringe(sim, seat, dt);\\n160→    stepDefib(sim, seat, dt);\\n    const power = toolPower(sim);\\n    if (sim.hushPhase !== 'inhale') {\\n      switch (seat.tool) {\\n        case 'scalpel': stepScalpel(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'forceps': stepForceps(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'suction': stepSuction(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'gel': stepGel(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'suture': stepSuture(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'laser': stepLaser(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n170→        case 'scanner': stepScanner(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'clamp': stepClamp(sim, seat, use); break;\\n        default: break;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    seat.prev = {\\n      alt: !!f.alt, syringe: !!f.syringe, special: !!f.special, swap: !!f.swap,\\n      use: use > 0.4, steady: !!f.steady,\\n    };\\n  }\",\"content_concise\":\"140→  return e.hidden && !e.marked;\\n}\\n\\nexport function stepTools(sim, dt) {\\n  for (const seat of sim.seats) {\\n    if (seat.out) continue;\\n    const f = seat.cmd;\\n    if (f.tool && f.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = f.tool;\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'tool', seat: seat.id, tool: seat.tool });\\n150→    }\\n    const use = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, f.use || 0));\\n    seat.use = use;\\n    seat.steady = !!f.steady;\\n    if (rising(seat, 'swap')) sim.swapLead(seat);\\n    if (Number.isInteger(f.site)) sim.setSite(seat, f.site);\\n    if (f.siteDelta) sim.nudgeSite(seat, f.siteDelta);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'special')) tryGift(sim, seat);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'alt')) doAlt(sim, seat);\\n    stepSyringe(sim, seat, dt);\\n160→    stepDefib(sim, seat, dt);\\n    const power = toolPower(sim);\\n    if (sim.hushPhase !== 'inhale') {\\n      switch (seat.tool) {\\n        case 'scalpel': stepScalpel(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'forceps': stepForceps(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'suction': stepSuction(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'gel': stepGel(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'suture': stepSuture(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'laser': stepLaser(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n170→        case 'scanner': stepScanner(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'clamp': stepClamp(sim, seat, use); break;\\n        default: break;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    seat.prev = {\\n      alt: !!f.alt, syringe: !!f.syringe, special: !!f.special, swap: !!f.swap,\\n      use: use > 0.4, steady: !!f.steady,\\n    };\\n  }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  return e.hidden && !e.marked;\\n}\\n\\nexport function stepTools(sim, dt) {\\n  for (const seat of sim.seats) {\\n    if (seat.out) continue;\\n    const f = seat.cmd;\\n    if (f.tool && f.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = f.tool;\\n      sim.events.push({ type: 'tool', seat: seat.id, tool: seat.tool });\\n    }\\n    const use = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, f.use || 0));\\n    seat.use = use;\\n    seat.steady = !!f.steady;\\n    if (rising(seat, 'swap')) sim.swapLead(seat);\\n    if (Number.isInteger(f.site)) sim.setSite(seat, f.site);\\n    if (f.siteDelta) sim.nudgeSite(seat, f.siteDelta);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'special')) tryGift(sim, seat);\\n    if (rising(seat, 'alt')) doAlt(sim, seat);\\n    stepSyringe(sim, seat, dt);\\n    stepDefib(sim, seat, dt);\\n    const power = toolPower(sim);\\n    if (sim.hushPhase !== 'inhale') {\\n      switch (seat.tool) {\\n        case 'scalpel': stepScalpel(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'forceps': stepForceps(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'suction': stepSuction(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'gel': stepGel(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'suture': stepSuture(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'laser': stepLaser(sim, seat, dt, use, power); break;\\n        case 'scanner': stepScanner(sim, seat, dt, use); break;\\n        case 'clamp': stepClamp(sim, seat, use); break;\\n        default: break;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    seat.prev = {\\n      alt: !!f.alt, syringe: !!f.syringe, special: !!f.special, swap: !!f.swap,\\n      use: use > 0.4, steady: !!f.steady,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\",\"total_lines\":826}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"77b4a3bc-2348-4cb5-981f-24bfca5242a8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_533","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A null tool value leaves the current state unchanged.\n\nKeyboard and pad inputs correctly set or clear the tool state. Mouse absolute positioning requires pointer-to-field conversion using camera and canvas rect. Hover focus updates the active item class. Click triggers activation and polls for clicked items.\n\nTo prevent double activation, a pending-activation queue will be used. The step function will process each click once after the pointer event fires.\n\nonActivate will trigger actions immediately and clear the click state. step will only poll menu edges for activation, never clicked items. Keyboard confirm will be handled by polling in step rather than inside onKey, preventing double activation with Enter. Clicks may fire without a subsequent step.\n\nClick activation fires immediately in onActivate. Pad confirm requires polling inside step because gamepads lack a dedicated event. Keyboard input uses test.step after keydown.\n\nDuring attract mode, any input exits the screen without navigating menus. A key pressed during attract stays in the keys set until keyup, so step might still detect it as a menu confirm if the latch was false.\n\nA `noteInput` helper will be called at the start of `onKey` and pointer handlers. When attract mode is active, it exits attract and immediately polls the input to prime the menu latch, preventing the same key from triggering a menu activation in the next step.\n\nThe step function will check for attract-mode input at the start of each frame. If any input is detected while attract mode is active, it exits immediately and skips menu navigation entirely.\n\nA 10-second idle timeout will trigger attract mode on title screens when no input occurs. The check runs every frame and inside test.step to catch cases where the browser throttles animation frames. Attract mode also blocks save operations.\n\nAttract mode will cycle through seven operations every 2.5 seconds using a new simulation instance with cheats enabled each time. A `.demo` element will mark the demo state during attract. Free play attract follows the same pattern. I am ready to write the implementation and worker-based simulation tests, including story line counts and banned name checks.\n\nI will add focused behavioral tests for individual mechanics rather than relying solely on bot playthroughs. These include gel zone coverage, rank titles, miss and idle failure checks, determinism hashing, snapshot bytes, skipTo, note timing after two misses, consult timer behavior, difficulty multipliers, GR scaling, and hush effects. I will drive the simulation directly instead of reimplementing it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ab934483-de6d-4ac3-a43b-ade01be97bb2-77","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"must-have|verbatim|I've only ever|Good hands|How much do you hate","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1708,"output_tokens":1404,"cache_read_input_tokens":146560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e0c8fecb-0e73-4588-9081-71d593bf3951"}
