{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_543","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Proceeding to write all source files.\n\nSettled on the module structure. Director will import nothing from session to avoid circular dependencies. Session.js will contain the protocol pump and export attachSession for main to call.\n\nSession.js will export `startSession(app, info)`. It will call the app's methods directly for UI, canvas, audio, input, tuning, view, settings, and rendering.\n\nDefining the app API interface for director to expose. Noted that readLocalFrame overlaps with input polling, but the session pump will call input.poll() directly.\n\nSession.js will own the network handlers, pump, and simulation creation. Director will call `startSession(app, info)` from there. The session pump will be the sole input poller during sessions to prevent edge events from being missed.\n\nDirector will import `runSession` from session.js and call it with the app instance. Session.js will not import director back; it receives the app object directly. During sessions, the session pump will write DOM updates to #ui, replacing director's paint method. Director will skip its rAF polling while in session mode.\n\nRefined the session API. Instead of passing individual app methods, `runSession` will receive a single shared `model` object containing screen, sim, view, netState, and other state fields. Session mutates this model directly, while director reads from it via `director.state()`. This keeps the interface clean and avoids circular imports.\n\nFinalized the shared model fields: screen, sim, view, audio, input, tuning, settings, session state, dev flags, story state, and UI elements. Will write the files now with minimal comments. Also need to fix site organ sync inside the frame loop.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-937e196e-1894-4a01-926a-bbea26c466fe-87","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/field.js","limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":313,"output_tokens":1300,"cache_read_input_tokens":166144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"8c85a6b8-7b64-4f6a-95ae-173e70c3c211"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-937e196e-1894-4a01-926a-bbea26c466fe-87","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→export const DT = 1 / 60;\\nexport const TRAY = { x: 1.62, y: 0.2, hw: 0.28, hh: 0.42 };\\nexport const IV = { x: 1.02, y: 0.22 };\\n\\nexport const clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\nexport const hypot = (x, y) => Math.hypot(x, y);\\n\\nexport function inDrape(x, y) {\\n  return (x / 1.4) ** 2 + (y / 0.85) ** 2 <= 1 + 1e-6;\\n10→}\\n\\nexport function clampTip(x, y) {\\n  return [clamp(x, -1.55, 1.9), clamp(y, -0.95, 0.95)];\\n}\\n\\nexport function overTray(x, y) {\\n  return Math.abs(x - TRAY.x) <= TRAY.hw && Math.abs(y - TRAY.y) <= TRAY.hh;\\n}\\n\\n20→export function dist(ax, ay, bx, by) {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→export const DT = 1 / 60;\\nexport const TRAY = { x: 1.62, y: 0.2, hw: 0.28, hh: 0.42 };\\nexport const IV = { x: 1.02, y: 0.22 };\\n\\nexport const clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\nexport const hypot = (x, y) => Math.hypot(x, y);\\n\\nexport function inDrape(x, y) {\\n  return (x / 1.4) ** 2 + (y / 0.85) ** 2 <= 1 + 1e-6;\\n10→}\\n\\nexport function clampTip(x, y) {\\n  return [clamp(x, -1.55, 1.9), clamp(y, -0.95, 0.95)];\\n}\\n\\nexport function overTray(x, y) {\\n  return Math.abs(x - TRAY.x) <= TRAY.hw && Math.abs(y - TRAY.y) <= TRAY.hh;\\n}\\n\\n20→export function dist(ax, ay, bx, by) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/field.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"export const DT = 1 / 60;\\nexport const TRAY = { x: 1.62, y: 0.2, hw: 0.28, hh: 0.42 };\\nexport const IV = { x: 1.02, y: 0.22 };\\n\\nexport const clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\nexport const hypot = (x, y) => Math.hypot(x, y);\\n\\nexport function inDrape(x, y) {\\n  return (x / 1.4) ** 2 + (y / 0.85) ** 2 <= 1 + 1e-6;\\n}\\n\\nexport function clampTip(x, y) {\\n  return [clamp(x, -1.55, 1.9), clamp(y, -0.95, 0.95)];\\n}\\n\\nexport function overTray(x, y) {\\n  return Math.abs(x - TRAY.x) <= TRAY.hw && Math.abs(y - TRAY.y) <= TRAY.hh;\\n}\\n\\nexport function dist(ax, ay, bx, by) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":71}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"0732c75b-82ea-4687-b555-bc6f125e82a7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_544","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Proceeding to write everything. Adding a small helper for escaping.\n\nAttract ops will run every 2 seconds to show three within the test window. Cheats include lockVitals, freezeTimer, infiniteComposure, and infiniteClamps. The bot will play to keep the demo moving. When attract exits, the simulation will be destroyed and cleared without saving. The touch notice overlay stays visible during attract mode.\n\nThe overlay will paint both the notice and a demo mark. The operation HUD sits behind them. A snapshot function will read state().op from the simulation or network state for testing.\n\nThe snapshot function will also capture phase, vitals, timer, score, rank, BPM, beat, site, tool, seat positions, focus ID, prompt set, and glyph set.\n\nThe snapshot function will also capture attract mode, dev tools, render backend, music gain, tuning, and reached flags. Rank will be returned as a string ID or null.\n\nThe tuning object will be exposed as a live reference so slider changes affect the simulation directly. Tests should move the slider DOM to trigger updates.\n\nA `devRun` method will be added to the API. The test object will only be created when the URL parameter `test=1` is present.\n\nThe main loop will poll menus whenever the screen is not an operation. During operations it will apply input and step the simulation unless paused. Paused state will only poll menus unless a single-step command is active. In attract mode the simulation will step with bot input while cheats remain active.\n\nAttract mode will step the simulation eight times per animation frame to keep motion visible even if rendering is slow. Operations will change on wall-clock intervals. The test.step command will also advance the simulation during attract mode.\n\nThe first paint will poll once to set the prompt set. CSS additions will be appended to ui.css via search_replace. Pad up and down inputs will be added to frameFromPad, with menu navigation using only pad 0 edges when multiple pads are present. The create button will ignore pause state. Pressing H during operations will trigger a bark sound.\n\nThe H key will trigger a bark sound during operations through the `onKey` handler. It will not be added to the keyboard frame structure.\n\nA key repeat guard will be added to the card answer handler so repeated Enter presses do not spam duplicate posts. The director menu will also avoid binding Enter to both the card answer and its own confirm action.\n\nThe card answer will be handled directly in the `onKey` handler rather than relying on the simulation pump. This avoids duplicate posts if both the keyboard and click paths trigger. The key listener is registered at application startup before connection, so Enter presses are captured immediately.\n\nA mutable `game` object will hold the `onKey` handler so it can read the current `cardUp` state. The standalone animation loop will be skipped when a session is active, since the session pump already drives updates.\n\nThe startup sequence will expose the API on `window.__game` before connecting to the hub. If a session is available, it starts there; otherwise it falls back to standalone mode. The boot element will be hidden immediately. A long director script will be written next, with fixes applied as needed. Settings pages will be stored in `model.settings`, including music and effects gain values.\n\nSettings will store voices, glyphs, rumble, aim assist, swap sticks, tip speed, fullscreen, shake, boil, text speed, and difficulty. Aim assist and tip speed will be copied into the tuning object so the simulation reads them live. Fullscreen will use requestFullscreen with a try/catch wrapper.\n\nLine boil will be toggled via `view.setBoil`. Screen shake will respect `model.settings.shake` and pass it to the view. Audio gains will sync whenever settings change. The director script will be written in a compact style.\n\nFail notes will appear as a \"Bea's Notes\" button that calls `acceptNotes` and returns to operation. Forcing a rank will route to the report screen.\n\nDev tools will use buttons with `data-item` attributes such as `dev:jump`, and `devRun` will parse those IDs. Test code can call `__game.devRun('god')` directly without touching the DOM. Tuning sliders will bind to `input` events and write values into `tuning[key]`.\n\nReset page and reset all buttons will use `data-item` attributes. The dev tools page will be dense with rem-based big buttons. Travel tools will appear in pages of four since the operation list is long. Each tool will have a dedicated button so test code can call them directly via `devRun`.\n\nDev tools will include speed controls, step, auto, overlay toggles, and ink effects. They will be grouped into pages of six. `devRun` will also accept an options object for jumping to a specific operation and phase. Slider changes will be tested by dispatching an `input` event directly on the range element.\n\nThe reset-all button will call `resetTuning`. The Dev Mode menu item is hidden during sessions and only appears in standalone mode. Escape is mapped to the back menu edge so it opens pause from the operation screen. During operations, `test.step` checks for the back or pause input to open pause without treating back as a separate action.\n\nThe pause overlay will be drawn on top of the Operation screen, so `state().screen` stays `Operation` and tests continue to see it. The `devOpen` flag will track when dev tools are active. Reaching a settings page or similar menu will mark it in the reached list. The paint function will check overlays before drawing the main screen.\n\nA client-side send rate will be enforced using per-message accumulators. Input events will be sent roughly every 80 milliseconds, state updates every 96 milliseconds, and keystrokes every second. This keeps the client well below the host's maximum of 16 updates per second.\n\nA token bucket will cap client traffic at 16 updates per second with an 8-update burst. Each client sends at most 15 messages, so it stays safely below the host’s 16-message limit. The AIHub bucket allows bursts up to 40, so a single client’s burst of 8 will not exceed it.\n\nAIHub.send will be skipped when tokens are below one to avoid warnings. Input and state updates will use unreliable delivery. Keystrokes, actions, and events will be reliable. Messages will be dropped if they exceed 1100 bytes for state or 16000 bytes for keystrokes. Simulation events will be batched into one message every 200 milliseconds.\n\nEmpty event batches will be skipped. Input messages will carry absolute coordinates, source seat, and sequence numbers so the host can apply them directly. The client will also integrate its own position locally to keep the tip cursor instant, though the host simulation remains authoritative for scoring.\n\nThe host will apply input messages directly to the simulation, so the view reads state instantly. Clients will merge their own seat position into the snapshot before rendering. The site field will be sent as an integer index and applied via `setSite`. Discrete action messages will only fire when a tool modifier is active and will be rate-limited to three per second.\n\nInput messages will merge into the command object without clearing one-shot flags, so the host can set them true and clear them after each step. One-shots will not be included in input messages to avoid accidental resets. The server has no local seat and only receives remote input and action messages.\n\nThe server will not call `sim.input` on its own. The host will write local input directly into the simulation using `AIHub.me`. The view will sync `sim.state` for the host and merge network state with a local tip override for clients. Input messages will only be sent once the countdown reaches zero, though sending them during the countdown is still acceptable.\n\nThe simulation will be created immediately during boot without waiting for the view, since physicsReady is fast and the pump can check for it. A race between pump startup and simulation creation is harmless because the countdown lasts several seconds. If createView throws, the code will catch it, attempt a WebGL fallback, and only fail if that also fails. The webgl parameter will be passed to createView, and norender will not be used in sessions. The scene will stay modest to keep memory usage low with four players.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6aabf070-f3c3-40fd-accc-eae3a72e62a8-88","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html","offset":138,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1625,"output_tokens":4431,"cache_read_input_tokens":166400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"a32df234-ca16-4fce-8a7a-fe90052cf3a2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6aabf070-f3c3-40fd-accc-eae3a72e62a8-88","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"138→/** Wrap what a game must not call in hub mode, where the page can reach it. */\\nfunction instrument(cell) {\\n140→  try {\\n    const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n    for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\\n      const original = win[name];\\n      win[name] = (...args) => {\\n        cell.violations.push(`${name}() called`);\\n        log(`${cell.name}: ${name}() called — not allowed in a session`);\\n        return name === 'confirm' ? false : name === 'prompt' ? null : undefined;\\n      };\\n      void original;\\n150→    }\\n    win.addEventListener('error', (e) => cell.violations.push(`error: ${e.message}`));\\n    win.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => cell.violations.push(`unhandled rejection: ${e.reason?.message || e.reason}`));\\n  } catch {\\n    cell.instrumented = false;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nasync function newRound() {\\n  endCurrent();\\n160→  applyNet();\\n  const game = $('game').value.trim();\\n  if (!game) return null;\\n  if (!gameUrl(game)) {\\n    log(`Not loading ${game}: the harness only plays pages from this site.`);\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(4, Number($('players').value) || 2));\\n  const metas = await metasOf(game);\\n  const mode = modeOf(metas?.mode);\\n170→  const limitMs = params.has('limit') ? Number(params.get('limit')) * 1000 : limitFor(metas?.minutes);\\n  const seed = params.has('seed') ? Number(params.get('seed')) >>> 0 : crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint32Array(1))[0];\\n  const round = ++roundNo;\\n  const players = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, slot) => ({ key: `p${slot}`, slot, name: NAMES[slot] }));\\n  const hubEnd = net.endpoint('hub');\\n  const grid = $('grid');\\n  grid.replaceChildren();\\n  const copies = n + (serverMode ? 1 : 0);\\n  grid.style.gridTemplateColumns = copies > 1 ? '1fr 1fr' : '1fr';\\n  grid.style.gridTemplateRows = `repeat(${Math.ceil(copies / (copies > 1 ? 2 : 1))}, 1fr)`;\\n180→\\n  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\\n  current = state;\\n  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\\n\\n  state.coordinator = createRound({\\n    round,\\n    players,\\n    hostKey: 'p0',\\n    serverKey: serverMode ? 'server' : null,\\n190→    mode,\\n    seed,\\n    limitMs,\\n    gate: true,\\n    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\\n    onStatus: (s) => { state.status = s; render(state); },\\n    onEnd: (record) => {\\n      state.record = record;\\n      log(`round ${round} ${record.status}: ${record.reason}${record.standings ? ' — standings ' + JSON.stringify(record.standings) : ''}`);\\n      render(state);\\n200→    },\\n  });\\n  hubEnd.onMessage((from, env) => {\\n    if (env.k !== 'c' || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.m?.type !== 'vis') log(`${from} → hub: ${env.m?.type}${env.m?.type === 'result' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify({ time: env.m.time, score: env.m.score }) : ''}${env.m?.type === 'finish' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify(env.m.standings) : ''}`);\\n    state.coordinator.receive(from, env.m);\\n  });\\n\\n  for (const p of [...players, ...(serverMode ? [{ key: 'server', slot: null, name: 'Server', server: true }] : [])]) {\\n    const color = p.server ? '#8a8a8a' : ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'][p.slot];\\n210→    const frame = document.createElement('iframe');\\n    frame.allow = 'fullscreen; autoplay; gamepad; pointer-lock';\\n    frame.title = p.name;\\n    const label = document.createElement('div');\\n    label.className = 'cell__bar';\\n    label.innerHTML = `<span class=\\\"cell__dot\\\" style=\\\"background:${color}\\\"></span><b></b><span class=\\\"cell__state\\\"></span>`;\\n    label.querySelector('b').textContent = `${p.name} (${p.key})`;\\n    const el = document.createElement('div');\\n    el.className = 'cell';\\n    el.style.borderColor = color;\\n220→    el.append(label, frame);\\n    grid.append(el);\\n\\n    const endpoint = net.endpoint(p.key);\\n    const cell = { ...p, el, label, frame, endpoint, violations: [], instrumented: true, gone: false, progress: [], cardSent: '' };\\n    const post = postTo(frame);\\n    cell.bridge = createBridge({\\n      key: p.key,\",\"content_concise\":\"138→/** Wrap what a game must not call in hub mode, where the page can reach it. */\\nfunction instrument(cell) {\\n140→  try {\\n    const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n    for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\\n      const original = win[name];\\n      win[name] = (...args) => {\\n        cell.violations.push(`${name}() called`);\\n        log(`${cell.name}: ${name}() called — not allowed in a session`);\\n        return name === 'confirm' ? false : name === 'prompt' ? null : undefined;\\n      };\\n      void original;\\n150→    }\\n    win.addEventListener('error', (e) => cell.violations.push(`error: ${e.message}`));\\n    win.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => cell.violations.push(`unhandled rejection: ${e.reason?.message || e.reason}`));\\n  } catch {\\n    cell.instrumented = false;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nasync function newRound() {\\n  endCurrent();\\n160→  applyNet();\\n  const game = $('game').value.trim();\\n  if (!game) return null;\\n  if (!gameUrl(game)) {\\n    log(`Not loading ${game}: the harness only plays pages from this site.`);\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(4, Number($('players').value) || 2));\\n  const metas = await metasOf(game);\\n  const mode = modeOf(metas?.mode);\\n170→  const limitMs = params.has('limit') ? Number(params.get('limit')) * 1000 : limitFor(metas?.minutes);\\n  const seed = params.has('seed') ? Number(params.get('seed')) >>> 0 : crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint32Array(1))[0];\\n  const round = ++roundNo;\\n  const players = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, slot) => ({ key: `p${slot}`, slot, name: NAMES[slot] }));\\n  const hubEnd = net.endpoint('hub');\\n  const grid = $('grid');\\n  grid.replaceChildren();\\n  const copies = n + (serverMode ? 1 : 0);\\n  grid.style.gridTemplateColumns = copies > 1 ? '1fr 1fr' : '1fr';\\n  grid.style.gridTemplateRows = `repeat(${Math.ceil(copies / (copies > 1 ? 2 : 1))}, 1fr)`;\\n180→\\n  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\\n  current = state;\\n  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\\n\\n  state.coordinator = createRound({\\n    round,\\n    players,\\n    hostKey: 'p0',\\n    serverKey: serverMode ? 'server' : null,\\n190→    mode,\\n    seed,\\n    limitMs,\\n    gate: true,\\n    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\\n    onStatus: (s) => { state.status = s; render(state); },\\n    onEnd: (record) => {\\n      state.record = record;\\n      log(`round ${round} ${record.status}: ${record.reason}${record.standings ? ' — standings ' + JSON.stringify(record.standings) : ''}`);\\n      render(state);\\n200→    },\\n  });\\n  hubEnd.onMessage((from, env) => {\\n    if (env.k !== 'c' || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.m?.type !== 'vis') log(`${from} → hub: ${env.m?.type}${env.m?.type === 'result' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify({ time: env.m.time, score: env.m.score }) : ''}${env.m?.type === 'finish' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify(env.m.standings) : ''}`);\\n    state.coordinator.receive(from, env.m);\\n  });\\n\\n  for (const p of [...players, ...(serverMode ? [{ key: 'server', slot: null, name: 'Server', server: true }] : [])]) {\\n    const color = p.server ? '#8a8a8a' : ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'][p.slot];\\n210→    const frame = document.createElement('iframe');\\n    frame.allow = 'fullscreen; autoplay; gamepad; pointer-lock';\\n    frame.title = p.name;\\n    const label = document.createElement('div');\\n    label.className = 'cell__bar';\\n    label.innerHTML = `<span class=\\\"cell__dot\\\" style=\\\"background:${color}\\\"></span><b></b><span class=\\\"cell__state\\\"></span>`;\\n    label.querySelector('b').textContent = `${p.name} (${p.key})`;\\n    const el = document.createElement('div');\\n    el.className = 'cell';\\n    el.style.borderColor = color;\\n220→    el.append(label, frame);\\n    grid.append(el);\\n\\n    const endpoint = net.endpoint(p.key);\\n    const cell = { ...p, el, label, frame, endpoint, violations: [], instrumented: true, gone: false, progress: [], cardSent: '' };\\n    const post = postTo(frame);\\n    cell.bridge = createBridge({\\n      key: p.key,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html\",\"offset\":138,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"/** Wrap what a game must not call in hub mode, where the page can reach it. */\\nfunction instrument(cell) {\\n  try {\\n    const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n    for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\\n      const original = win[name];\\n      win[name] = (...args) => {\\n        cell.violations.push(`${name}() called`);\\n        log(`${cell.name}: ${name}() called — not allowed in a session`);\\n        return name === 'confirm' ? false : name === 'prompt' ? null : undefined;\\n      };\\n      void original;\\n    }\\n    win.addEventListener('error', (e) => cell.violations.push(`error: ${e.message}`));\\n    win.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => cell.violations.push(`unhandled rejection: ${e.reason?.message || e.reason}`));\\n  } catch {\\n    cell.instrumented = false;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nasync function newRound() {\\n  endCurrent();\\n  applyNet();\\n  const game = $('game').value.trim();\\n  if (!game) return null;\\n  if (!gameUrl(game)) {\\n    log(`Not loading ${game}: the harness only plays pages from this site.`);\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(4, Number($('players').value) || 2));\\n  const metas = await metasOf(game);\\n  const mode = modeOf(metas?.mode);\\n  const limitMs = params.has('limit') ? Number(params.get('limit')) * 1000 : limitFor(metas?.minutes);\\n  const seed = params.has('seed') ? Number(params.get('seed')) >>> 0 : crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint32Array(1))[0];\\n  const round = ++roundNo;\\n  const players = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, slot) => ({ key: `p${slot}`, slot, name: NAMES[slot] }));\\n  const hubEnd = net.endpoint('hub');\\n  const grid = $('grid');\\n  grid.replaceChildren();\\n  const copies = n + (serverMode ? 1 : 0);\\n  grid.style.gridTemplateColumns = copies > 1 ? '1fr 1fr' : '1fr';\\n  grid.style.gridTemplateRows = `repeat(${Math.ceil(copies / (copies > 1 ? 2 : 1))}, 1fr)`;\\n\\n  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\\n  current = state;\\n  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\\n\\n  state.coordinator = createRound({\\n    round,\\n    players,\\n    hostKey: 'p0',\\n    serverKey: serverMode ? 'server' : null,\\n    mode,\\n    seed,\\n    limitMs,\\n    gate: true,\\n    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\\n    onStatus: (s) => { state.status = s; render(state); },\\n    onEnd: (record) => {\\n      state.record = record;\\n      log(`round ${round} ${record.status}: ${record.reason}${record.standings ? ' — standings ' + JSON.stringify(record.standings) : ''}`);\\n      render(state);\\n    },\\n  });\\n  hubEnd.onMessage((from, env) => {\\n    if (env.k !== 'c' || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.m?.type !== 'vis') log(`${from} → hub: ${env.m?.type}${env.m?.type === 'result' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify({ time: env.m.time, score: env.m.score }) : ''}${env.m?.type === 'finish' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify(env.m.standings) : ''}`);\\n    state.coordinator.receive(from, env.m);\\n  });\\n\\n  for (const p of [...players, ...(serverMode ? [{ key: 'server', slot: null, name: 'Server', server: true }] : [])]) {\\n    const color = p.server ? '#8a8a8a' : ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'][p.slot];\\n    const frame = document.createElement('iframe');\\n    frame.allow = 'fullscreen; autoplay; gamepad; pointer-lock';\\n    frame.title = p.name;\\n    const label = document.createElement('div');\\n    label.className = 'cell__bar';\\n    label.innerHTML = `<span class=\\\"cell__dot\\\" style=\\\"background:${color}\\\"></span><b></b><span class=\\\"cell__state\\\"></span>`;\\n    label.querySelector('b').textContent = `${p.name} (${p.key})`;\\n    const el = document.createElement('div');\\n    el.className = 'cell';\\n    el.style.borderColor = color;\\n    el.append(label, frame);\\n    grid.append(el);\\n\\n    const endpoint = net.endpoint(p.key);\\n    const cell = { ...p, el, label, frame, endpoint, violations: [], instrumented: true, gone: false, progress: [], cardSent: '' };\\n    const post = postTo(frame);\\n    cell.bridge = createBridge({\\n      key: p.key,\\n\",\"total_lines\":548}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"46c1f258-f2a7-45fa-a37e-5507b273f9b3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_545","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"An unhandled rejection caused the check to fail.\n\ncreateView and ink errors must be caught. The RAPIER.init warning is acceptable. renderer.init rejections are handled. Playwright background iframes still execute setTimeout. The simulation will not pause on visibility changes because the harness controls visibility events.\n\nMath.random will not be replaced in shared-world mode. The director will be comprehensive and include copying the game to the hub site during build. The root HTML path is resolved using the game title from identity.js.\n\nBuild runs from the dev folder. The root path resolves to the work folder.\n\nI will add .gitignore and write save.js, dev.js, session.js, director.js, main.js, build.mjs, plus CSS and input patches. Tests come last.\n\nDirector logic will advance story screens on held confirmations every three steps, on click activation, and via tab skip or pad edge during story. The difficulty screen is also treated as a story screen.\n\nThe difficulty question and its scenes will both mark the Story screen. The chart screen will be marked when it appears. If a test uses skipTo, it will mark Operation. The playthrough will not use skipTo; it will navigate through menus and bot controls instead.\n\nPlaythrough duration is estimated at roughly 120,000 steps. The browser suite timeout will be ten minutes. Cheats in the simulation freeze the timer but do not reduce step count, so the bot still needs to complete each operation.\n\nThe browser playthrough should take roughly thirty to ninety seconds. Tests will warp and bot through step loops with a maximum limit, and physics will be disabled in test mode. The final patient completes in about two hundred sixteen steps. When the simulation ends, the director will automatically transition to the report or fail screen once, using a shownResult flag. Report continue will advance to the after scene. Model flow callbacks will be implemented.\n\nRank will be saved on the report screen. The director reads game metadata from an `about-data` script tag in the built page. A small patch will be applied to input.js and ui.css.\n\nThe credits page will list backend renderer information alongside the game credits. The about section will be split into five pages: Source, Testing, Engine, Prompt, and Credits. Each page shows its heading and answers in ten-foot font, and the Q and E keys switch between them. All four required headings will be present in the DOM so the test can read them.\n\nPlaywright's text locator defaults to visible elements only, so the four required headings must be visible. The test will check that all headings appear on screen and that #about-data parses correctly.\n\nThe test will read `#ui.textContent()` to capture all about-page text, including hidden sections.\n\nThe about page will use a tab row for the four headings, with only the active page shown. Key source fields like game title and genre will also be displayed.\n\nTesting feedback questions will be answered in the JSON and on the page. The attract mode timeout is set to 10000 ms. The test will check that attract is not active at 9000 ms and is active at 11000 ms, using wall-clock timing from boot.\n\nThe test will record the title screen as the reference time for attract mode. It will wait nine seconds after that point and then check for attract mode.\n\nThe attract timer will be checked inside the animation frame loop so it runs even when the simulation is paused. The test will wait on the title screen without pressing a key, since any input would navigate away from the title.\n\nThe animation frame loop will only call stepOnce when the simulation is not in test mode or when warping. During playthrough, the step function handles all polling, so the frame loop should skip it to avoid consuming keys before the test step runs.\n\nA `rendering` flag will prevent overlapping async `view.render()` calls. The animation frame loop will only call `stepOnce` when the simulation is not in test mode or when warping, ensuring that only `test.step` polls input.\n\nA potential bug was spotted: when test.step(n) runs with n greater than one, only the first step consumes the confirm input, so subsequent steps may miss it.\n\nA test bug was found: Playwright's `keyboard.press` sends keydown and keyup before the step, so the rising edge is missed and the simulation never registers the input. The test should press the key, then call `test.step(1)` to let the simulation poll for it.\n\nA pending-edge fix for the Playwright keypress bug is being drafted. `onKey` will store a pending flag when a keydown arrives, and `stepOnce` will consume it during polling so the rising edge is no longer missed.\n\nThe pending-edge fix is finalized. `stepOnce` will copy any pending keydown into the menu state and immediately clear the flag, so a single step consumes the rising edge. This prevents double-firing if polling also detects the key in the same frame. Pad buttons do not use this mechanism; they fire on their own edges.\n\nMouse clicks and hover events will trigger immediately rather than waiting for the step loop. The pending-edge mechanism is being wired directly into the game object. On the title screen, any keypress will set a pending start flag so the simulation can leave the title even if the test presses the key before polling. If attract mode is active, pressing any key will also swallow it and turn off attract mode.\n\nA `swallowAttract` helper will be called at the start of `onKey`, `onHover`, and `onActivate` to exit attract mode when any input arrives. It clears pending flags, resets the last input timestamp, and paints immediately so the key or pointer event does not trigger navigation.\n\n`lastInput` will only update when real input arrives, not on every poll. A `sampleActive` helper will detect activity from keys, clicks, pad buttons, and pad stick, but ignore sticky hover to prevent attract mode from blocking.\n\n`lastInput` will be updated in `onHover` and `pointerdown` to catch pointer activity. Pad activity will also reset the idle timer inside `stepOnce`. The `poll` function will return whether any pad button or stick was pressed so the frame loop can distinguish idle pads from active ones.\n\nThe director will check navigator.getGamepads directly to detect pad activity and update lastInput. The attract bot will not reset that timestamp. Additional CSS rules for .card, .touch, .row, and .hidden will be appended to ui.css.\n\nThe tuning object will be created once and shared between the simulation and the dev sliders. Sim will store the exact same reference instead of cloning it, so both can mutate the same values directly. All files will be written in a single batch.\n\nThe director will skip its own paint during a session so the session can render its card and HUD directly. A `model.ownsUi` flag will tell the director to yield control. The card screen is not required for standalone mode. A countdown screen will be added, and the playing state will show the Operation screen.\n\nThe pause settings overlay will use `model.sessionSettings` and the pump loop will ignore it. A win is defined as `sim.complete && !sim.failed && sim.vitals > 0`, while a time-up is simply whether the simulation is complete. Scores map each seat ID to its score, and stats are cleaned per ID into an object with string keys.\n\nAwards will be an array of objects with numeric IDs, titles, and details. Standings will be a descending score list grouped by tied scores. Every present player will be included, defined as info.players minus those who left or were seated out.\n\nThe time-up handler will call finish synchronously instead of waiting for the next step. If the operation ends during play, finish(true) fires immediately; if time-up arrives after that, it is ignored. When a client receives an end event because the host left, the pump stops but the simulation does not finish.\n\nThe `leave` handler adds the departing player to a set of left players and calls `sim.leave(id)`. The server will send snapshots bidirectionally so every remaining copy reports both sent and received counts, and it will verify that all copies are present before finalizing.\n\nThe server cell is not marked gone, so it must report both sent and received traffic. After the host leaves and its cell is removed, the remaining players should already have exchanged messages during the first random interval before the removal.\n\nThe host-leave sequence is now fully sequenced. The countdown ends before the random delay begins, so traffic should start before the host leaves. If the host departs before any messages are sent, the round is voided and a record still exists before time-up.\n\nThe simulation boots asynchronously while the card is shown, so it should be ready before the countdown ends and traffic begins. The server has no view, so it starts even faster. An input snapshot will be sent immediately at the first play moment, even if the input value is zero. A local tip will be placed at coordinates -1.05 and 0.62.\n\nA heartbeat send will fire every 120 milliseconds during play if the accumulator stalls, though it is redundant with normal traffic. The JSON size of k was measured at 3038 bytes. The director must avoid using the words stub, placeholder, TODO, FIXME, and any substring containing \"common time\".","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d209116a-a85f-4d1e-a725-8d1e05fc2b69-89","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js","offset":1,"limit":140}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5832,"output_tokens":5447,"cache_read_input_tokens":167936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6ec7602c-67ee-4c94-9323-f04f634b0937"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d209116a-a85f-4d1e-a725-8d1e05fc2b69-89","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { uniform } from 'three/tsl';\\nimport RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';\\nimport { createInk } from './ink.js';\\nimport { toon, wetOrgan, paintCanvas, flipUVs } from './materials.js';\\nimport { fieldToWorld, placeOrCamera, placeStoryCamera, pointerToField } from './camera.js';\\nimport { bustFor } from './bust.js';\\nimport { siteLook } from '../data/sites.js';\\n\\n10→const KIND_COLOR = {\\n  shard: '#d8f4ff', pool: '#8e1d2a', bleeder: '#ff3355', gelZone: '#7dffa0',\\n  incision: '#2a120c', wound: '#6a2030', nodule: '#c46a2a', tumor: '#6a2040',\\n  adagio: '#5a1028', staccato: '#e8d56a', tremolo: '#d06a9a', legato: '#c4a0e8',\\n  crescendo: '#ff8844', fermata: '#88d0ff', coda: '#1a1028', note: '#f5f0e6',\\n  spore: '#9ad06a', scratch: '#6a1420', feeder: '#ffcc66', baton: '#e8e0c8',\\n  link: '#c8b0e0', tether: '#e8d0a0', hole: '#201018', egg: '#f0e6c8', nest: '#304028',\\n  injection: '#d8fff8', clamp: '#c0c8d0',\\n};\\n\\n20→function displace(geo, organ) {\\n  const pos = geo.attributes.position;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < pos.count; i++) {\\n    const x = pos.getX(i);\\n    const y = pos.getY(i);\\n    let h = Math.exp(-(x * x + y * y) * 0.35) * 0.22;\\n    h += Math.sin(x * 6 + organ.length) * 0.015 + Math.sin(y * 9) * 0.012;\\n    if (organ === 'heart') h += Math.exp(-((x - 0.2) ** 2 + y * y) * 2) * 0.12;\\n    if (organ === 'brain') h += Math.sin(x * 14) * Math.cos(y * 12) * 0.03;\\n    if (organ === 'bowel') h += Math.sin(x * 10) * 0.04;\\n30→    pos.setZ(i, h);\\n  }\\n  geo.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\\nfunction makeOrgan(organ) {\\n  const look = siteLook(organ);\\n  const geo = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 64, 44);\\n  geo.rotateX(-Math.PI / 2);\\n  displace(geo, organ);\\n40→  const paint = paintCanvas(look.color);\\n  const beat = uniform(0);\\n  const mat = wetOrgan(paint.tex, beat);\\n  const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\\n  mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  mesh.castShadow = false;\\n  mesh.userData.paint = paint;\\n  mesh.userData.beat = beat;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n50→\\nfunction makeDrape() {\\n  const shape = new THREE.Shape();\\n  shape.moveTo(-2.6, -2.1);\\n  shape.lineTo(2.6, -2.1);\\n  shape.lineTo(2.6, 2.1);\\n  shape.lineTo(-2.6, 2.1);\\n  shape.closePath();\\n  const hole = new THREE.Path();\\n  const steps = 48;\\n60→  for (let i = 0; i <= steps; i++) {\\n    const a = (i / steps) * Math.PI * 2;\\n    const wob = 1 + Math.sin(a * 5) * 0.03;\\n    const x = Math.cos(a) * 1.5 * wob;\\n    const y = Math.sin(a) * 0.95 * wob;\\n    if (i === 0) hole.moveTo(x, y);\\n    else hole.lineTo(x, y);\\n  }\\n  shape.holes.push(hole);\\n  const geo = new THREE.ExtrudeGeometry(shape, { depth: 0.08, bevelEnabled: false });\\n70→  geo.rotateX(-Math.PI / 2);\\n  geo.translate(0, 0.34, 0);\\n  const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, toon({ color: '#17707A' }));\\n  mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nfunction toolMesh(kind) {\\n  const g = new THREE.Group();\\n  const metal = toon({ color: '#d5dde2' });\\n80→  const grip = toon({ color: '#2a3338' });\\n  const add = (geo, mat, x, y, z) => {\\n    const m = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\\n    m.position.set(x, y, z);\\n    m.castShadow = true;\\n    g.add(m);\\n    return m;\\n  };\\n  if (kind === 'forceps') {\\n    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.03, 0.02, 0.28), metal, -0.03, 0, 0.1);\\n90→    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.03, 0.02, 0.28), metal, 0.03, 0, 0.1);\\n  } else if (kind === 'defib') {\\n    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.18, 0.05, 0.12), toon({ color: '#e8eef2' }), -0.2, 0, 0);\\n    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.18, 0.05, 0.12), toon({ color: '#e8eef2' }), 0.2, 0, 0);\\n  } else {\\n    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.04, 0.04, 0.34), kind === 'laser' ? toon({ color: '#e8443a' }) : metal, 0, 0, 0.08);\\n    add(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.035, 0.04, 0.16, 8), grip, 0, 0, -0.12);\\n  }\\n  g.userData.kind = kind;\\n  return g;\\n100→}\\n\\nfunction entityMesh(kind) {\\n  const color = KIND_COLOR[kind] || '#f2f2f2';\\n  let geo;\\n  if (kind === 'baton' || kind === 'link' || kind === 'tether') geo = new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.03, 0.03, 0.4, 6);\\n  else if (kind === 'note') geo = new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.06, 8, 6);\\n  else if (kind === 'gelZone' || kind === 'pool') geo = new THREE.CircleGeometry(0.18, 12);\\n  else geo = new THREE.SphereGeometry(kind === 'coda' || kind === 'crescendo' ? 0.16 : 0.09, 10, 8);\\n  if (geo.attributes && !geo.attributes.normal) geo.computeVertexNormals();\\n110→  const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, toon({ color }));\\n  if (kind === 'gelZone' || kind === 'pool') mesh.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nfunction skinnedAdagio() {\\n  const bones = [new THREE.Bone(), new THREE.Bone()];\\n  bones[0].position.y = 0;\\n  bones[1].position.y = 0.2;\\n  bones[0].add(bones[1]);\\n120→  const geo = new THREE.CapsuleGeometry(0.08, 0.28, 4, 8);\\n  const skinIndex = [];\\n  const skinWeight = [];\\n  const pos = geo.attributes.position;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < pos.count; i++) {\\n    const y = pos.getY(i);\\n    skinIndex.push(y > 0 ? 1 : 0, 0, 0, 0);\\n    skinWeight.push(1, 0, 0, 0);\\n  }\\n  geo.setAttribute('skinIndex', new THREE.Uint16BufferAttribute(skinIndex, 4));\\n130→  geo.setAttribute('skinWeight', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(skinWeight, 4));\\n  const mesh = new THREE.SkinnedMesh(geo, toon({ color: KIND_COLOR.adagio }));\\n  const arm = new THREE.Skeleton(bones);\\n  mesh.add(bones[0]);\\n  mesh.bind(arm);\\n  mesh.userData.bone = bones[1];\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nfunction storyRoom(set) {\\n140→  const g = new THREE.Group();\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { uniform } from 'three/tsl';\\nimport RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';\\nimport { createInk } from './