{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-45b67f02-dc52-4239-9139-8b6244bc82a3-93","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"220→  const portraitGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(0.7, 0.7));\\n  const portrait = new THREE.Mesh(portraitGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\\n  portrait.position.set(0, -0.55, -1.4);\\n  camera.add(portrait);\\n  scene.add(camera);\\n\\n  const cutGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.1, 0.7));\\n  const cutin = new THREE.Mesh(cutGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\\n  cutin.position.set(0.7, 0.25, -1.6);\\n  cutin.rotation.z = -0.12;\\n230→  cutin.visible = false;\\n  camera.add(cutin);\\n\\n  const particles = new THREE.InstancedMesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.03, 5, 4), toon({ color: '#ff4455' }), 48);\\n  particles.count = 0;\\n  or.add(particles);\\n  const dummy = new THREE.Object3D();\\n\\n  const story = new THREE.Group();\\n  story.visible = false;\\n240→  scene.add(story);\\n  let storySet = null;\\n  const busts = { left: null, right: null };\\n\\n  let ink = null;\\n  try {\\n    ink = createInk(renderer, scene, camera);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    renderer.dispose();\\n    throw err;\\n250→  }\\n\\n  let juice = null;\\n  try {\\n    await RAPIER.init();\\n    juice = new RAPIER.World({ x: 0, y: -4, z: 0 });\\n  } catch {\\n    juice = null;\\n  }\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"220→  const portraitGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(0.7, 0.7));\\n  const portrait = new THREE.Mesh(portraitGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\\n  portrait.position.set(0, -0.55, -1.4);\\n  camera.add(portrait);\\n  scene.add(camera);\\n\\n  const cutGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.1, 0.7));\\n  const cutin = new THREE.Mesh(cutGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\\n  cutin.position.set(0.7, 0.25, -1.6);\\n  cutin.rotation.z = -0.12;\\n230→  cutin.visible = false;\\n  camera.add(cutin);\\n\\n  const particles = new THREE.InstancedMesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.03, 5, 4), toon({ color: '#ff4455' }), 48);\\n  particles.count = 0;\\n  or.add(particles);\\n  const dummy = new THREE.Object3D();\\n\\n  const story = new THREE.Group();\\n  story.visible = false;\\n240→  scene.add(story);\\n  let storySet = null;\\n  const busts = { left: null, right: null };\\n\\n  let ink = null;\\n  try {\\n    ink = createInk(renderer, scene, camera);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    renderer.dispose();\\n    throw err;\\n250→  }\\n\\n  let juice = null;\\n  try {\\n    await RAPIER.init();\\n    juice = new RAPIER.World({ x: 0, y: -4, z: 0 });\\n  } catch {\\n    juice = null;\\n  }\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js\",\"offset\":220,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  const portraitGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(0.7, 0.7));\\n  const portrait = new THREE.Mesh(portraitGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\\n  portrait.position.set(0, -0.55, -1.4);\\n  camera.add(portrait);\\n  scene.add(camera);\\n\\n  const cutGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.1, 0.7));\\n  const cutin = new THREE.Mesh(cutGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\\n  cutin.position.set(0.7, 0.25, -1.6);\\n  cutin.rotation.z = -0.12;\\n  cutin.visible = false;\\n  camera.add(cutin);\\n\\n  const particles = new THREE.InstancedMesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.03, 5, 4), toon({ color: '#ff4455' }), 48);\\n  particles.count = 0;\\n  or.add(particles);\\n  const dummy = new THREE.Object3D();\\n\\n  const story = new THREE.Group();\\n  story.visible = false;\\n  scene.add(story);\\n  let storySet = null;\\n  const busts = { left: null, right: null };\\n\\n  let ink = null;\\n  try {\\n    ink = createInk(renderer, scene, camera);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    renderer.dispose();\\n    throw err;\\n  }\\n\\n  let juice = null;\\n  try {\\n    await RAPIER.init();\\n    juice = new RAPIER.World({ x: 0, y: -4, z: 0 });\\n  } catch {\\n    juice = null;\\n  }\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":465}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"dd877520-9a19-49f2-9f78-81e8c6c70dba"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_550","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Starting to write the application code.\n\nPatching ensureTip to use toolMesh(k) instead of clone for tools. This avoids material clone bugs. Writing files now, starting with smaller ones and then the core director/session/main/build modules.\n\nSession input will be handled by the pump polling every 16ms. The host player uses keyboard input via readLocalFrame. Card answers use onKey events instead of polling. Session settings will be processed in the pump when an overlay is open.\n\nThe session pause overlay will use a minimal settings panel with music slider, glyphs toggle, and back. It will handle Q/E and confirm edges through the pump.\n\nThe pump will route session pause through director's paint and menu methods. Session will only handle simulation and network updates. Director will expose paint() and consumeMenu(sample) for this.\n\nSession will receive director's paint, menu consumption, and frame collection as callbacks injected into the model before runSession. The pump will call these directly instead of routing through director methods.\n\nConfirmed no circular imports. The director's startSession will assign paint and other callbacks to the model before calling runSession. runSession will register AIHub handlers, ready, and the pump. The model will hold input, audio, canvas, ui, tuning, params, and settings.\n\nSession.js will be self-contained. Director will inject simulation callbacks and UI methods into the model before runSession. The pump will call model.paint, model.onSim, model.sync, model.readSample, model.localFrames, model.audio, and model.renderCard.\n\nDirector will be written as a single large file of roughly 800 to 1200 lines. Session will be about 400 lines. Sim tests will be written in parallel and run before the browser shell.\n\nDrafting the simulation test suite. Worker.mjs will run individual play() operations in isolated processes. Suite.mjs will spawn workers and run lint, determinism checks, snapshots, and fast idle tests in-process. Determinism tests will hash 200 scripted steps for equality. Snapshot tests will track peak memory usage during bot runs.\n\nDrafting simulation test cases. Data lint will run in the main thread by importing ops and checking inDrape. Banned names and Math.random usage will be verified by reading source files directly. Tests will cover story count, phrases, rankFor titles, skipTo phase transitions, notesOffer after two failures, and consult timer calculations.\n\nDifficulty intern drains 0.6. GR countScale is 2.5 for four players. Tool tests will verify idle failure, syringe healing at IV, and bot coverage of tool mechanics.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-41063c7e-cfc8-4f35-b6e1-501394955226-94","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function stepGel|function stepSyringe|function stepClamp|function stepDefib|function stepLaser","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":595,"output_tokens":1750,"cache_read_input_tokens":182912,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"329bc4a4-fbf2-40c0-a9f1-9d0d5056528c"}
