{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-17c0ba22-4137-41e7-9d7f-0376f0f7d208-99","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"  const tips = new Map();\\n  const entities = new Map();\\n  const tools = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suction', 'gel', 'suture', 'laser', 'scanner', 'clamp', 'syringe', 'defib'];\\n  const toolProto = Object.fromEntries(tools.map((k) => [k, toolMesh(k)]));\",\"new_string\":\"  const tips = new Map();\\n  const entities = new Map();\\n  const tools = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suction', 'gel', 'suture', 'laser', 'scanner', 'clamp', 'syringe', 'defib'];\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"  const tips = new Map();\\n  const entities = new Map();\\n  const tools = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suction', 'gel', 'suture', 'laser', 'scanner', 'clamp', 'syringe', 'defib'];\\n  const toolProto = Object.fromEntries(tools.map((k) => [k, toolMesh(k)]));\",\"old_line\":204,\"new_string\":\"  const tips = new Map();\\n  const entities = new Map();\\n  const tools = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suction', 'gel', 'suture', 'laser', 'scanner', 'clamp', 'syringe', 'defib'];\",\"new_line\":204,\"context_before\":\"  const track = new THREE.KeyframeTrack('.rotation[z]', [0, 1, 2], [0, 0.18, 0]);\\n  mixer.clipAction(new THREE.AnimationClip('swing', 2, [track])).play();\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n  const bustScene = new THREE.Scene();\\n  bustScene.background = new THREE.Color('#10282c');\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"60b524e5-d3a1-4851-b493-7e2ba548db2a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_554","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now writing the major files carefully.\n\nPlanning the director API and key constants. Will write save.js, dev.js, session, and director next.\n\nFleshing out director.js with the core game loop and UI functions. Difficulty levels are intern, resident, and attending. The Bea question screen will present these three options.\n\nDrafting the save.js module. The save object will hold version, difficulty, story position, intro state, cleared scenes, ranks, unlock status, and settings. Loading will read localStorage on boot and write only outside of attract mode or active sessions.\n\nsave.js is now complete with load and write functions. Director will wrap writes with guards. dev.js will hold the runDev helper that mutates model.sim and model directly.\n\ndev.js will catch errors internally so the API never throws. Director assigns model.replaceSim to swap simulations safely. The jump tool needs ALL_OPS and SCENES.\n\nSeven strain names are defined. Rank scoring maps S to 1× par, A to 0.8×, B to 0.6×, C to 0.4×, and D to 0.1×. The director will compute the score, call rankFor, mark the simulation complete, and switch to the Report screen. It also calls completePhase on the active operation when the simulation exists.\n\ndevRun will explicitly switch the screen to Report or Fail when a simulation finishes, then repaint. Spawning a bleeder will be wrapped in a try-catch to avoid crashes if decoration is unsupported. beginArrest will be exposed as a public method. The time-scale cheat cycles between 0.1× and 4× by doubling the current rate.\n\nFleshing out the remaining dev.js cheat commands. Single-step advances the simulation if it is not over. Auto toggles bot mode. Overlays, ink lines, and shadows can be switched on or off. Unlocking sets the save flag to true. Scene cycling will use a director-assigned openScene helper.\n\nAdding a phase-next cheat that advances the simulation to the next operation phase. The op-* commands will replace the active simulation. Aim assist settings will be stored in the shared tuning object and read by the dev overlay sliders, which director paint will render directly. Dev tool buttons will use data-item attributes so activate can route them to runDev.\n\nAdding reset buttons. Session.js will use model state for UI, canvas, audio, input, tuning, settings, paint, syncView, freeSim, reached scenes, screen, and the AIHub global. It will set model.sim, netState, sessionPause, and card. Director paint will render the Card screen, a countdown number, or the operation HUD during sessions.\n\nSession paint will show settings when paused and a message when ended. The Card screen renders HTML directly in director paint. Key presses answer the card when the screen is Card or during a session. The pump polls input to detect pad cross and confirm inputs for card answers.\n\nThe session pump will be the only input poller during card answers, avoiding double polling. It can safely poll every 16 ms without stepping the simulation. Keyboard confirmations for cards will be handled by onKey instead of the pump.\n\nPump will only answer card questions when the pad’s confirm edge is pressed. Keyboard confirmations are handled by onKey alone, preventing double answers.\n\nClicking the Ready or More buttons triggers AIHub answers. The card event handler copies all message fields into model.card and switches to the Card screen.\n\nThe card event carries a single detail object with fields left, paused, starting, ready, asking, and asked. The ready array holds player IDs. The Card screen will build its player list with DOM elements using textContent for names and color borders, appending \"ready\" to any player already confirmed.\n\nThe Card screen will use local copy for its win instructions and controls line. It will display the title GAME_TITLE and show seconds remaining from card.left or AIHub.time(). When AIHub.time() is negative, the director switches to Countdown mode and computes the ceiling of negative time divided by 1000. Once that value reaches zero or goes non-negative, it advances to the operation phase.\n\nThe director will switch to Operation mode and step the simulation once AIHub.time() becomes non-negative. Before that, it stays on Card. The start event sets a flag, and a 3-2-1 countdown runs from -3000 ms down to zero. Audio resumes on first input, and rounds music plays when an operation begins. The server will skip audio and view rendering.\n\nThe server is still a browser page, so it can paint a \"running\" screen without creating a view or playing audio. syncView will only run when a view exists.\n\nFor client network state, applyNet decodes keyframes and drops stale ones by tick. It applies unreliable updates and stashes sound events. If an unreliable update arrives before the first keyframe, it waits until the keyframe arrives.\n\nClients will override their own seat position, tool, and coordinates in the network state before syncing to the view. The host will push simulation state directly. A finish payload helper is being added to session.js. A token bucket rate limiter is being drafted for outgoing messages.\n\nThe token bucket now enforces a 1100-byte cap on unreliable updates and a 16000-byte cap on keyframes. Tokens refill at 16 per second, and the bucket holds up to 8 tokens. Low-priority messages are dropped when tokens are exhausted; high-priority messages like keyframes, audio, and events are also dropped to avoid warnings rather than forcing delivery. A rate schedule using millisecond accumulators is being drafted, along with a commands map and a merge function.\n\nThe merge function initializes each player’s command entry with default absolute coordinates, tool, and use state. It handles incoming input commands by updating position, tool, and use flags, and it processes action commands by toggling syringe, special, alt, swap, and site delta bits.\n\nThe host will feed merged commands into the simulation directly, skipping the local command map. It passes the local frame for its own seat and then steps. The simulation handles both absolute and stick input, so the host can send raw pad data without preintegrating. Clients preintegrate their commands before passing them in.\n\nThe local player is always seat index 0 on their own page, so the host pulls that frame directly from input.poll and passes it to sim.input for AIHub.me. Clients integrate that frame into local coordinates before sending an absolute update.\n\nClient-side stick input is preintegrated before sending. Absolute frames overwrite local coordinates directly. Stick frames scale speed by magnitude and curve, apply steady-factor when held, and clamp position to the tip bounds.\n\nClients send input commands on schedule even when coordinates and tool are unchanged. The host does not send input frames. Action flags are sent only when syringe, special, alt, swap, or siteDelta is active. Each command carries a sequence number. The local site index is sent in the message and updated by frame deltas. The host simulation treats the frame’s site as authoritative. Sending the site every step could trigger setSite every frame and reset cooldowns.\n\nThe site field will be included in every input message. The simulation assigns the site even when it is unchanged, so the network stays chatty but avoids duplicate events.\n\nThe session simulation will use `network: true` so gifts alternate by seat index. Even indices receive Hush and odd indices receive Sforzando, matching the plan's team split. Each seat will keep its own site rather than sharing one with a couch cooldown.\n\nSession mode will use a surgical-team split with each seat holding its own site, though nudgeSite may briefly conflict with the viewed active site. The grand-rounds operation ID is set to \"GR\". Difficulty will be stored as a resident value. Physics initialization must complete before the simulation starts, and any failure there will trigger AIHub.fail. The pump will stop and the audio context will suspend when the session ends.\n\nThe session ends with the message \"The round is over.\" No save occurs. Pressing Escape or pad pause toggles a sessionPause flag and opens the settings menu. The simulation keeps stepping and sending updates while paused. The back button closes settings without toggling pause. A single input edge handles both actions.\n\nThe settings overlay will be shared between session and standalone modes. It will hide the developer menu and quit option during sessions. A `settingsItems()` helper will generate the control list, and the pause menu will consume the menu button for settings pages while still allowing back to close.\n\nThe back button will close the settings overlay when sessionPause is active, and it will toggle pause otherwise. Sliders will use native range input without polling. Both standalone settings and session pause will render through a single `model.overlay = 'settings'` flag. The next step is to write the actual code.\n\nAttract screens will include Title, Main Menu, Free Play, and a Touch notice. A setInterval running every 250 ms will check attract timeouts independently of requestAnimationFrame, ensuring the ten-second idle threshold still fires even if the main thread is blocked.\n\nAttract mode will not start during sessions. The director will suppress Space key scrolling and carefully manage pending keys.\n\nTab will be suppressed with preventDefault to keep browser focus on the page. The body element will receive focus so keyboard events reach the window listeners.\n\nThe hub harness dispatches KeyboardEvents directly on the body or active element, so window listeners catch them during the bubble phase. The key handler checks e.key, which covers both Enter and Space.\n\nTests will be added after a successful build. The pad input path correctly omits keyboard fallbacks, and card input uses onKey. FrameFromPad handles all four pads when stubs exist, though solo mode only reads index zero. Mouse absolute coordinates rely on game.view being captured by createInput, so later updates to the view object remain accessible.\n\nThe input system will use a single `model` object that holds `view`, `screen`, `settings`, and `audio`. `createInput` receives this object directly, so later updates to `model.view` remain accessible. Wheel clicks and mouse wheel events set `model.pendingTool`, which `stepOnce` applies onto the current frame before it is sent.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sim is locked. I’m writing the shell, the hub session, and the build next, then I’ll run the suites against that shipped code."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-88f2fef5-5345-4eec-9f0c-cb8c9d34f13d-100","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/save.js","new_string":"/** Progress and settings. Never called during a session or an attract demo. */\n\nconst KEY = 'st-alder-chart';\n\nexport function emptySave() {\n  return {\n    v: 1,\n    difficulty: 'resident',\n    storyPos: 0,\n    intro: false,\n    cleared: [],\n    ranks: {},\n    unlocked: false,\n    settings: null,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function loadSave() {\n  try {\n    const raw = localStorage.getItem(KEY);\n    if (!raw) return emptySave();\n    const data = JSON.parse(raw);\n    if (!data || data.v !== 1) return emptySave();\n    return { ...emptySave(), ...data, cleared: data.cleared || [], ranks: data.ranks || {} };\n  } catch {\n    return emptySave();\n  }\n}\n\nexport function writeSave(data) {\n  try {\n    localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\n    return true;\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-88f2fef5-5345-4eec-9f0c-cb8c9d34f13d-101","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/dev.js","new_string":"import { ALL_OPS } from '../data/ops/index.js';\nimport { SCENES } from '../data/story/scenes.js';\nimport { rankFor } from '../sim/scoring.js';\nimport { Sim } from '../sim/sim.js';\nimport { resetTuning, TUNING_DEFAULTS } from '../config/tuning.js';\n\nconst STRAINS = ['adagio', 'staccato', 'tremolo', 'legato', 'crescendo', 'fermata', 'coda'];\n\nexport const DEV_IDS = [\n  ...ALL_OPS.map((op) => `op:${op.id}`),\n  'phase-next', 'unlock', 'scene-next',\n  'complete-objective', 'complete-phase', 'win', 'fail',\n  'rank:S', 'rank:A', 'rank:B', 'rank:C', 'rank:D',\n  'god', 'freeze', 'composure', 'clamps',\n  'bleeder', ...STRAINS.map((k) => `strain:${k}`),\n  'arrest', 'fortissimo', 'hush', 'sforzando',\n  'speed', 'step', 'auto',\n  'overlay:grid', 'overlay:targets', 'overlay:beat', 'overlay:input',\n  'ink:lines', 'ink:tone', 'ink:boil', 'ink:shadows',\n  'reset-page', 'reset-all',\n];\n\nfunction fresh(model, opId) {\n  const prev = model.sim;\n  try { prev?.physics?.free?.(); } catch { /* world already freed */ }\n  const sim = new Sim({\n    op: opId,\n    seed: 1,\n    physics: false,\n    tuning: model.tuning,\n    difficulty: model.settings.difficulty || 'resident',\n    players: 1,\n  });\n  model.sim = sim;\n  model.screen = 'Operation';\n  model.overlay = null;\n  model.opId = opId;\n  model.reached?.add('Operation');\n  model.resultShown = false;\n  return sim;\n}\n\nexport function runDev(model, id, arg) {\n  const name = String(id || '');\n  const sim = () => model.sim;\n  const go = (fn) => {\n    try { fn(); } catch { /* a tool on a finished op stays quiet */ }\n  };\n  if (name.startsWith('op:')) {\n    const opId = name.slice(3);\n    go(() => {\n      const simx = fresh(model, opId);\n      if (arg) simx.skipTo(arg);\n    });\n    return true;\n  }\n  if (name === 'jump') {\n    go(() => {\n      const simx = fresh(model, arg?.op || 'broken-glass');\n      if (arg?.phase) simx.skipTo(arg.phase);\n    });\n    return true;\n  }\n  if (name === 'unlock') {\n    model.save.unlocked = true;\n    model.persist?.();\n    return true;\n  }\n  if (name === 'scene-next' || name === 'scene') {\n    const cur = SCENES.findIndex((s) => s.id === (arg || model.sceneId));\n    const next = SCENES[(cur + 1 + SCENES.length) % SCENES.length];\n    model.openScene?.(arg && name === 'scene' ? arg : next.id, () => model.setScreen?.('Main Menu', null));\n    return true;\n  }\n  const live = sim();\n  if (!live) return true;\n  if (name === 'phase-next') {\n    go(() => {\n      const phases = live.op.phases;\n      const i = Math.min(phases.length - 1, live.phaseIndex + 1);\n      live.skipTo(phases[i].id);\n    });\n  } else if (name === 'complete-objective') {\n    go(() => {\n      for (const e of live.entities) e.alive = false;\n      live.vitals = 100;\n      live.flags.stabilized = true;\n      live.arrestsSurvived = 99;\n      if (!live.over) live.completePhase();\n    });\n  } else if (name === 'complete-phase') {\n    go(() => { if (!live.over) live.completePhase(); });\n  } else if (name === 'win') {\n    go(() => { if (!live.over) live.succeed(); });\n  } else if (name === 'fail') {\n    go(() => { if (!live.over) live.fail('vitals'); });\n  } else if (name.startsWith('rank:')) {\n    go(() => {\n      const letter = name.slice(5);\n      const par = live.op.parScore || 1;\n      const ratio = { S: 1, A: 0.8, B: 0.6, C: 0.4, D: 0.1 }[letter] ?? 0.8;\n      live.score = Math.round(par * ratio);\n      live.rank = rankFor(live.score, par, null);\n      live.over = true;\n      live.complete = true;\n      live.failed = null;\n      model.screen = 'Report';\n      model.reached?.add('Report');\n    });\n  } else if (name === 'god') {\n    live.cheats.lockVitals = !live.cheats.lockVitals;\n  } else if (name === 'freeze') {\n    live.cheats.freezeTimer = !live.cheats.freezeTimer;\n  } else if (name === 'composure') {\n    live.cheats.infiniteComposure = !live.cheats.infiniteComposure;\n  } else if (name === 'clamps') {\n    live.cheats.infiniteClamps = !live.cheats.infiniteClamps;\n  } else if (name === 'bleeder') {\n    go(() => {\n      const seat = live.seats[0];\n      live.spawn({ kind: 'bleeder', site: live.activeSite, at: [seat.x, seat.y] });\n    });\n  } else if (name.startsWith('strain:')) {\n    go(() => {\n      const kind = name.slice(7);\n      const seat = live.seats[0];\n      live.spawn({ kind, strain: kind, site: live.activeSite, at: [seat.x, seat.y], hp: 40 });\n    });\n  } else if (name === 'arrest') {\n    go(() => { if (!live.arrest) live.beginArrest({ clock: 8 }); });\n  } else if (name === 'fortissimo') {\n    go(() => live.act({ event: 'fortissimo' }));\n  } else if (name === 'hush') {\n    go(() => {\n      live.hushPhase = 'wash';\n      live.hushT = live.tuning.hushDuration;\n      live.events.push({ type: 'hush', phase: 'wash' });\n    });\n  } else if (name === 'sforzando') {\n    go(() => { live.sforzandoT = live.tuning.sforzandoDuration; });\n  } else if (name === 'speed') {\n    const cur = live.cheats.timeScale || 1;\n    live.cheats.timeScale = cur >= 4 ? 0.1 : Math.round(Math.min(4, cur * 2) * 10) / 10;\n  } else if (name === 'step') {\n    go(() => { if (!live.over) live.step(); });\n  } else if (name === 'auto') {\n    model.botOn = !model.botOn;\n  } else if (name.startsWith('overlay:')) {\n    const key = name.slice(8);\n    model.overlays[key] = !model.overlays[key];\n  } else if (name === 'ink:lines') {\n    const u = model.view?.ink?.u;\n    if (u) u.lineOn.value = u.lineOn.value ? 0 : 1;\n  } else if (name === 'ink:tone') {\n    const u = model.view?.ink?.u;\n    if (u) u.toneOn.value = u.toneOn.value ? 0 : 1;\n  } else if (name === 'ink:boil') {\n    model.view?.setBoil?.(!(model.boilOn === false));\n    model.boilOn = model.boilOn === false;\n  } else if (name === 'ink:shadows') {\n    const map = model.view?.renderer?.shadowMap;\n    if (map) map.enabled = !map.enabled;\n  } else if (name === 'reset-all') {\n    resetTuning(model.tuning);\n  } else if (name === 'reset-page') {\n    const keys = arg || Object.keys(TUNING_DEFAULTS);\n    resetTuning(model.tuning, keys);\n  }\n  if (live.over && live.complete && model.screen === 'Operation') {\n    model.screen = 'Report';\n    model.reached?.add('Report');\n  } else if (live.over && live.failed && model.screen === 'Operation') {\n    model.screen = 'Fail';\n    model.reached?.add('Fail');\n  }\n  model.paint?.();\n  return true;\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":442,"output_tokens":8638,"cache_read_input_tokens":191744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"405bb569-88cb-49d1-8ce5-397ece5646b8"}
