{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_576","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A checkpoint was set in enterPhase at line 312.\n\nConstructor calls enterPhase. I will write build.mjs and a smoke test. I will patch resultShown to prevent double clicks on completing steps. I will add a return in stepOnce when feedSim calls setScreen. I verified ensureDom ran before paint during startStandalone. AudioContext creation is safe.\n\nplayTrack scheduling is safe even if the AudioContext is suspended. esbuild will bundle director, three.js, and rapier for the build. The openScene function is hoisted because model.openScene is assigned before the function keyword.\n\nI will verify the build with a quick esbuild syntax check. The feedSim early return needs a small patch. lobbyHtml returns an SVG string that is inserted into innerHTML. Chart does not include a title string.\n\nThe main menu title is escaped and inserted via innerHTML, then set again with textContent. Duplicate setScreen logic and startSession overwriting paint are harmless. The session pump calls model.paint every frame. Card signals remain stable initially because the card element is null, so no flicker occurs.\n\nCard event updates and bark changes correctly trigger rebuilds. Operation session paint updates numbers via patchLive without rebuilding the whole frame. The host starts in Card mode before the clock reaches zero, then switches to Operation. A bug was found in stepOnce: it returns immediately when the mode is session, which prevents pad confirm on the card.\n\nSession input is handled by the session pump, not stepOnce. The loop never starts during session mode because startSession cancels rAF. A bug was also found: ignoreUntil blocks confirm on the next step within 350ms after attract exit.\n\nThe 350ms ignoreUntil window is intentional. It swallows confirmations immediately after attract exit, including new key presses up to 100ms later, as required by the spec.\n\nI verified that present guards against missing views. A createView failure shows a nogfx notice on the Title screen. WebGPU may work with flags, but the renderer falls back to WebGL2 automatically.\n\nI will write build.mjs exactly as planned, including catalogue tags and copying output to the root and hub site. The build script will check the client banner hash and throw early if it is wrong. I also need to verify that DESCRIPTION and Icon imports contain no quotes, and that CSS does not accidentally include `</style>`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f3aef704-8a59-4256-a72e-33bdb9451676-60","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"</script>","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tools/vendor/session.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f3aef704-8a59-4256-a72e-33bdb9451676-61","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","old_string":"      feedSim(sample);\n      if (model.screen === 'Lobby' && !model.overlay) {","new_string":"      const showedResult = model.resultShown;\n      feedSim(sample);\n      if (model.resultShown && !showedResult) return;\n      if (model.screen === 'Lobby' && !model.overlay) {"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":370,"output_tokens":1515,"cache_read_input_tokens":175360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e631a1a3-2134-4590-b1fb-22133106c651"}
