{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_587","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether the grand rounds teaching material includes tremolo.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d77b93e7-c30e-4e6a-8a6b-1429050691ef-75","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md","offset":344,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d77b93e7-c30e-4e6a-8a6b-1429050691ef-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/field.js","limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d77b93e7-c30e-4e6a-8a6b-1429050691ef-77","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/snapshot.js","offset":100,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2518,"output_tokens":485,"cache_read_input_tokens":184064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"217c9183-98b7-4a03-b043-caeb641eb175"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d77b93e7-c30e-4e6a-8a6b-1429050691ef-75","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"344→## 7. Story\\n\\nDelivered as short scenes on a 3D stage (§9.5). Cross, Enter, Space or a click advances; hold to fast-forward; Triangle or Tab skips the scene, with a prompt on screen. Write 250 to 350 lines in total, in `src/data/story/`. The beats and must-have lines below are fixed; the rest is yours. Chapter names: **Scrub In**, **First Movement**, **Dissent**, **Coda**.\\n\\n| # | When | Where | Beats and must-have lines |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n350→| S0 | New game | OR 3 at night, empty | An envelope slides under the door. The monitor switches itself on and beeps, in time, with no patient. A silhouette lifts a baton. Title sting. 20 s |\\n| S1 | Before Op 1 | Corridor, OR 3 | Flood traffic has stranded the attending. Ren is all there is. \\\"Thirty-one years in this room, child…\\\" \\\"Then simulate faster.\\\" |\\n| S2 | After Op 1 | Bell's office | Bell's praise and warning: \\\"the best hands… the worst nerves.\\\" |\\n| S3 | Before Op 2 | OR 3 gallery | The board watches. Routine tumor. Ren throws up, apologizes to the bucket |\\n| S4 | After Op 2 | OR 3, tray | Ren: \\\"Everything went quiet.\\\" Bea goes very still: \\\"I have heard of that once.\\\" The tumor twitches on the tray. In rhythm. Sting: \\\"Tumors do not keep time, child.\\\" |\\n| S5 | Before Op 3 | Pip's pathology lab | Envelope: sheet music addressed to \\\"The Surgeon on Call\\\". Pip plays it on a keyboard: \\\"It's a heartbeat…\\\" Ambulance: a cellist |\\n| S6 | After Op 3 | Ward Zero | Sorrento: \\\"Please wash your hands.\\\" REQUIEM, spelled out in full, with a straight face. The Conservatory. Ren is drafted |\\n| S7 | Before Op 4 | Ambulance bay, rain | Second score. A ferry captain |\\n| S8 | After Op 4 | OR 3 | The OR phone rings. A breathy voice: \\\"Bravo, Doctor. You play by ear. How delightful.\\\" Bea drops a full instrument tray. Sting |\\n| S9 | Before Op 5 | Ward Zero, then OR 3 | Ines arrives under guard. \\\"Your hands are excellent. Your diagnosis is a eulogy.\\\" She operates; you play her. First Consult |\\n360→| S10 | After Op 5 | Hospital roof, rain | Ines explains: she studied under the Maestro, who had the Hush. \\\"At the end, Doctor, you cannot turn it off.\\\" \\\"He waits for the silence. I do not wait.\\\" |\\n| S11 | Before Op 6 | Boardroom | Bell collapses mid-aphorism. The envelope's dedication: \\\"For Augustin, who signed.\\\" Consult |\\n| S12 | After Op 6 | Recovery room | Bell confesses: he signed Voss's death certificate after the Ward Zero fire, knowing she lived, and funded St. Alder with her research. \\\"Every heart I mended in this building, I mended with her money.\\\" Bea: \\\"I handed her the knife for eleven years. I would know that silence anywhere.\\\" |\\n| S13 | Before Op 7 | OR 3 | Final envelope. Pip plays it and slows down: \\\"I know this rhythm. It has a murmur. Ms. Okonkwo, you've got a—\\\" Bea, turning, mid-sentence: \\\"Forceps, ch—\\\" She falls. Ines: \\\"You cannot operate. You love her.\\\" Ren: \\\"Then you had better hand me the instruments.\\\" Pip, shaking, picks up the notebook. Consult |\\n| S14 | After Op 7 | Recovery, dawn | Bea wakes. Long silence. \\\"You held the forceps wrong, child.\\\" |\\n| S15 | Then | OR 3 gallery | Voss, conducting behind the glass, falters: her own heart is the first host. Sorrento: \\\"Let her go, Doctor.\\\" Ren: \\\"She's a patient.\\\" Leads into Last Patient |\\n| S16 | After | St. Alder, morning | Patients' cameos. Pip in student-nurse scrubs. Bea, with a cane, watches Ren close a wound and, for the only time in the game: **\\\"Good hands, child.\\\"** Credits roll over attract footage. Post-credits: a new envelope, marked *Opus 2* |\\n\\n**Bea's barks.** Write 60 or so short in-operation lines keyed by event, each with an expression: `start, nextPhase, toolHint(tool), idle, vitalsLow, vitalsCritical, miss, streak, bleeding, overflow, clampReminder, strainIntro(strain), hushReady, timerLow, success, fail`. A taste:\\n\\n370→- `vitalsLow`: \\\"Pressure's falling, child. Stabilizer.\\\"\\n- `miss`: \\\"That was not on the line.\\\" / \\\"I saw that. God saw that.\\\"\\n- `streak`: \\\"…Adequate.\\\" (her highest praise)\\n- `bleeding`: \\\"You are swimming in it. Suction.\\\"\\n- `clampReminder`: \\\"Your clamps are still in. Would you like to sign for them?\\\"\\n- `timerLow`: \\\"Clock, child.\\\"\\n- `fail`: \\\"Call it. Then go and tell the family. No. You. That is the job.\\\"\\n\\n**Lint:** a test fails if any Bea line contains \\\"good\\\" outside S16. In Op 5 Bea still calls the barks and trades shots with Ines. In Op 6 Ines interjects over comms. In Op 7 every bark comes from Pip reading the notebook.\\n\\n380→---\\n\\n## 8. Controls and screens\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"344→## 7. Story\\n\\nDelivered as short scenes on a 3D stage (§9.5). Cross, Enter, Space or a click advances; hold to fast-forward; Triangle or Tab skips the scene, with a prompt on screen. Write 250 to 350 lines in total, in `src/data/story/`. The beats and must-have lines below are fixed; the rest is yours. Chapter names: **Scrub In**, **First Movement**, **Dissent**, **Coda**.\\n\\n| # | When | Where | Beats and must-have lines |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n350→| S0 | New game | OR 3 at night, empty | An envelope slides under the door. The monitor switches itself on and beeps, in time, with no patient. A silhouette lifts a baton. Title sting. 20 s |\\n| S1 | Before Op 1 | Corridor, OR 3 | Flood traffic has stranded the attending. Ren is all there is. \\\"Thirty-one years in this room, child…\\\" \\\"Then simulate faster.\\\" |\\n| S2 | After Op 1 | Bell's office | Bell's praise and warning: \\\"the best hands… the worst nerves.\\\" |\\n| S3 | Before Op 2 | OR 3 gallery | The board watches. Routine tumor. Ren throws up, apologizes to the bucket |\\n| S4 | After Op 2 | OR 3, tray | Ren: \\\"Everything went quiet.\\\" Bea goes very still: \\\"I have heard of that once.\\\" The tumor twitches on the tray. In rhythm. Sting: \\\"Tumors do not keep time, child.\\\" |\\n| S5 | Before Op 3 | Pip's pathology lab | Envelope: sheet music addressed to \\\"The Surgeon on Call\\\". Pip plays it on a keyboard: \\\"It's a heartbeat…\\\" Ambulance: a cellist |\\n| S6 | After Op 3 | Ward Zero | Sorrento: \\\"Please wash your hands.\\\" REQUIEM, spelled out in full, with a straight face. The Conservatory. Ren is drafted |\\n| S7 | Before Op 4 | Ambulance bay, rain | Second score. A ferry captain |\\n| S8 | After Op 4 | OR 3 | The OR phone rings. A breathy voice: \\\"Bravo, Doctor. You play by ear. How delightful.\\\" Bea drops a full instrument tray. Sting |\\n| S9 | Before Op 5 | Ward Zero, then OR 3 | Ines arrives under guard. \\\"Your hands are excellent. Your diagnosis is a eulogy.\\\" She operates; you play her. First Consult |\\n360→| S10 | After Op 5 | Hospital roof, rain | Ines explains: she studied under the Maestro, who had the Hush. \\\"At the end, Doctor, you cannot turn it off.\\\" \\\"He waits for the silence. I do not wait.\\\" |\\n| S11 | Before Op 6 | Boardroom | Bell collapses mid-aphorism. The envelope's dedication: \\\"For Augustin, who signed.\\\" Consult |\\n| S12 | After Op 6 | Recovery room | Bell confesses: he signed Voss's death certificate after the Ward Zero fire, knowing she lived, and funded St. Alder with her research. \\\"Every heart I mended in this building, I mended with her money.\\\" Bea: \\\"I handed her the knife for eleven years. I would know that silence anywhere.\\\" |\\n| S13 | Before Op 7 | OR 3 | Final envelope. Pip plays it and slows down: \\\"I know this rhythm. It has a murmur. Ms. Okonkwo, you've got a—\\\" Bea, turning, mid-sentence: \\\"Forceps, ch—\\\" She falls. Ines: \\\"You cannot operate. You love her.\\\" Ren: \\\"Then you had better hand me the instruments.\\\" Pip, shaking, picks up the notebook. Consult |\\n| S14 | After Op 7 | Recovery, dawn | Bea wakes. Long silence. \\\"You held the forceps wrong, child.\\\" |\\n| S15 | Then | OR 3 gallery | Voss, conducting behind the glass, falters: her own heart is the first host. Sorrento: \\\"Let her go, Doctor.\\\" Ren: \\\"She's a patient.\\\" Leads into Last Patient |\\n| S16 | After | St. Alder, morning | Patients' cameos. Pip in student-nurse scrubs. Bea, with a cane, watches Ren close a wound and, for the only time in the game: **\\\"Good hands, child.\\\"** Credits roll over attract footage. Post-credits: a new envelope, marked *Opus 2* |\\n\\n**Bea's barks.** Write 60 or so short in-operation lines keyed by event, each with an expression: `start, nextPhase, toolHint(tool), idle, vitalsLow, vitalsCritical, miss, streak, bleeding, overflow, clampReminder, strainIntro(strain), hushReady, timerLow, success, fail`. A taste:\\n\\n370→- `vitalsLow`: \\\"Pressure's falling, child. Stabilizer.\\\"\\n- `miss`: \\\"That was not on the line.\\\" / \\\"I saw that. God saw that.\\\"\\n- `streak`: \\\"…Adequate.\\\" (her highest praise)\\n- `bleeding`: \\\"You are swimming in it. Suction.\\\"\\n- `clampReminder`: \\\"Your clamps are still in. Would you like to sign for them?\\\"\\n- `timerLow`: \\\"Clock, child.\\\"\\n- `fail`: \\\"Call it. Then go and tell the family. No. You. That is the job.\\\"\\n\\n**Lint:** a test fails if any Bea line contains \\\"good\\\" outside S16. In Op 5 Bea still calls the barks and trades shots with Ines. In Op 6 Ines interjects over comms. In Op 7 every bark comes from Pip reading the notebook.\\n\\n380→---\\n\\n## 8. Controls and screens\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":344,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"## 7. Story\\n\\nDelivered as short scenes on a 3D stage (§9.5). Cross, Enter, Space or a click advances; hold to fast-forward; Triangle or Tab skips the scene, with a prompt on screen. Write 250 to 350 lines in total, in `src/data/story/`. The beats and must-have lines below are fixed; the rest is yours. Chapter names: **Scrub In**, **First Movement**, **Dissent**, **Coda**.\\n\\n| # | When | Where | Beats and must-have lines |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| S0 | New game | OR 3 at night, empty | An envelope slides under the door. The monitor switches itself on and beeps, in time, with no patient. A silhouette lifts a baton. Title sting. 20 s |\\n| S1 | Before Op 1 | Corridor, OR 3 | Flood traffic has stranded the attending. Ren is all there is. \\\"Thirty-one years in this room, child…\\\" \\\"Then simulate faster.\\\" |\\n| S2 | After Op 1 | Bell's office | Bell's praise and warning: \\\"the best hands… the worst nerves.\\\" |\\n| S3 | Before Op 2 | OR 3 gallery | The board watches. Routine tumor. Ren throws up, apologizes to the bucket |\\n| S4 | After Op 2 | OR 3, tray | Ren: \\\"Everything went quiet.\\\" Bea goes very still: \\\"I have heard of that once.\\\" The tumor twitches on the tray. In rhythm. Sting: \\\"Tumors do not keep time, child.\\\" |\\n| S5 | Before Op 3 | Pip's pathology lab | Envelope: sheet music addressed to \\\"The Surgeon on Call\\\". Pip plays it on a keyboard: \\\"It's a heartbeat…\\\" Ambulance: a cellist |\\n| S6 | After Op 3 | Ward Zero | Sorrento: \\\"Please wash your hands.\\\" REQUIEM, spelled out in full, with a straight face. The Conservatory. Ren is drafted |\\n| S7 | Before Op 4 | Ambulance bay, rain | Second score. A ferry captain |\\n| S8 | After Op 4 | OR 3 | The OR phone rings. A breathy voice: \\\"Bravo, Doctor. You play by ear. How delightful.\\\" Bea drops a full instrument tray. Sting |\\n| S9 | Before Op 5 | Ward Zero, then OR 3 | Ines arrives under guard. \\\"Your hands are excellent. Your diagnosis is a eulogy.\\\" She operates; you play her. First Consult |\\n| S10 | After Op 5 | Hospital roof, rain | Ines explains: she studied under the Maestro, who had the Hush. \\\"At the end, Doctor, you cannot turn it off.\\\" \\\"He waits for the silence. I do not wait.\\\" |\\n| S11 | Before Op 6 | Boardroom | Bell collapses mid-aphorism. The envelope's dedication: \\\"For Augustin, who signed.\\\" Consult |\\n| S12 | After Op 6 | Recovery room | Bell confesses: he signed Voss's death certificate after the Ward Zero fire, knowing she lived, and funded St. Alder with her research. \\\"Every heart I mended in this building, I mended with her money.\\\" Bea: \\\"I handed her the knife for eleven years. I would know that silence anywhere.\\\" |\\n| S13 | Before Op 7 | OR 3 | Final envelope. Pip plays it and slows down: \\\"I know this rhythm. It has a murmur. Ms. Okonkwo, you've got a—\\\" Bea, turning, mid-sentence: \\\"Forceps, ch—\\\" She falls. Ines: \\\"You cannot operate. You love her.\\\" Ren: \\\"Then you had better hand me the instruments.\\\" Pip, shaking, picks up the notebook. Consult |\\n| S14 | After Op 7 | Recovery, dawn | Bea wakes. Long silence. \\\"You held the forceps wrong, child.\\\" |\\n| S15 | Then | OR 3 gallery | Voss, conducting behind the glass, falters: her own heart is the first host. Sorrento: \\\"Let her go, Doctor.\\\" Ren: \\\"She's a patient.\\\" Leads into Last Patient |\\n| S16 | After | St. Alder, morning | Patients' cameos. Pip in student-nurse scrubs. Bea, with a cane, watches Ren close a wound and, for the only time in the game: **\\\"Good hands, child.\\\"** Credits roll over attract footage. Post-credits: a new envelope, marked *Opus 2* |\\n\\n**Bea's barks.** Write 60 or so short in-operation lines keyed by event, each with an expression: `start, nextPhase, toolHint(tool), idle, vitalsLow, vitalsCritical, miss, streak, bleeding, overflow, clampReminder, strainIntro(strain), hushReady, timerLow, success, fail`. A taste:\\n\\n- `vitalsLow`: \\\"Pressure's falling, child. Stabilizer.\\\"\\n- `miss`: \\\"That was not on the line.\\\" / \\\"I saw that. God saw that.\\\"\\n- `streak`: \\\"…Adequate.\\\" (her highest praise)\\n- `bleeding`: \\\"You are swimming in it. Suction.\\\"\\n- `clampReminder`: \\\"Your clamps are still in. Would you like to sign for them?\\\"\\n- `timerLow`: \\\"Clock, child.\\\"\\n- `fail`: \\\"Call it. Then go and tell the family. No. You. That is the job.\\\"\\n\\n**Lint:** a test fails if any Bea line contains \\\"good\\\" outside S16. In Op 5 Bea still calls the barks and trades shots with Ines. In Op 6 Ines interjects over comms. In Op 7 every bark comes from Pip reading the notebook.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Controls and screens\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1218}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d77b93e7-c30e-4e6a-8a6b-1429050691ef-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→export const DT = 1 / 60;\\nexport const TRAY = { x: 1.62, y: 0.2, hw: 0.28, hh: 0.42 };\\nexport const IV = { x: 1.02, y: 0.22 };\\n\\nexport const clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\nexport const hypot = (x, y) => Math.hypot(x, y);\\n\\nexport function inDrape(x, y) {\\n  return (x / 1.4) ** 2 + (y / 0.85) ** 2 <= 1 + 1e-6;\\n10→}\\n\\nexport function clampTip(x, y) {\\n  return [clamp(x, -1.55, 1.9), clamp(y, -0.95, 0.95)];\\n}\\n\\nexport function overTray(x, y) {\\n  return Math.abs(x - TRAY.x) <= TRAY.hw && Math.abs(y - TRAY.y) <= TRAY.hh;\\n}\\n\\n20→export function dist(ax, ay, bx, by) {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→export const DT = 1 / 60;\\nexport const TRAY = { x: 1.62, y: 0.2, hw: 0.28, hh: 0.42 };\\nexport const IV = { x: 1.02, y: 0.22 };\\n\\nexport const clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\nexport const hypot = (x, y) => Math.hypot(x, y);\\n\\nexport function inDrape(x, y) {\\n  return (x / 1.4) ** 2 + (y / 0.85) ** 2 <= 1 + 1e-6;\\n10→}\\n\\nexport function clampTip(x, y) {\\n  return [clamp(x, -1.55, 1.9), clamp(y, -0.95, 0.95)];\\n}\\n\\nexport function overTray(x, y) {\\n  return Math.abs(x - TRAY.x) <= TRAY.hw && Math.abs(y - TRAY.y) <= TRAY.hh;\\n}\\n\\n20→export function dist(ax, ay, bx, by) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/field.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"export const DT = 1 / 60;\\nexport const TRAY = { x: 1.62, y: 0.2, hw: 0.28, hh: 0.42 };\\nexport const IV = { x: 1.02, y: 0.22 };\\n\\nexport const clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\nexport const hypot = (x, y) => Math.hypot(x, y);\\n\\nexport function inDrape(x, y) {\\n  return (x / 1.4) ** 2 + (y / 0.85) ** 2 <= 1 + 1e-6;\\n}\\n\\nexport function clampTip(x, y) {\\n  return [clamp(x, -1.55, 1.9), clamp(y, -0.95, 0.95)];\\n}\\n\\nexport function overTray(x, y) {\\n  return Math.abs(x - TRAY.x) <= TRAY.hw && Math.abs(y - TRAY.y) <= TRAY.hh;\\n}\\n\\nexport function dist(ax, ay, bx, by) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":71}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d77b93e7-c30e-4e6a-8a6b-1429050691ef-77","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→    charge: u(row[11] || 0),\\n    name: base.name, gift: base.gift, stats: base.stats || { Cuts: 0, Stitches: 0, Burns: 0, Saves: 0, Accuracy: 100 },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Fields the operative view reads. A decoded snapshot must carry all of them. */\\nexport const VIEW_FIELDS = ['tick', 'op', 'phase', 'vitals', 'timer', 'score', 'bpm', 'beat', 'beatInBar', 'bar', 'site', 'hush', 'arrest', 'seats', 'entities', 'phaseTools', 'sites', 'flags', 'objective'];\\n\\nfunction worldOf(state) {\\n  return {\\n110→    tick: state.tick, op: state.op, phase: state.phase, phaseIndex: state.phaseIndex,\\n    objective: state.objective, vitals: state.vitals, vitalsMin: state.vitalsMin,\\n    timer: state.timer, score: state.score, misses: state.misses, combo: state.combo,\\n    bpm: state.bpm, beat: state.beat, beatInBar: state.beatInBar, beatPhase: state.beatPhase,\\n    bar: state.bar, site: state.site, doctor: state.doctor, hush: state.hush,\\n    arrest: state.arrest, complete: state.complete, failed: state.failed, over: state.over,\\n    rank: state.rank, phaseTools: state.phaseTools, sites: state.sites, flags: state.flags,\\n    notes: state.notes, clampsUsed: state.clampsUsed,\\n  };\\n}\\n120→\\nexport function keyframeOf(sim) {\\n  const state = sim.state || sim;\\n  const msg = {\\n    t: 'k',\\n    w: worldOf(state),\\n    ents: (state.entities || []).map(packEntity),\\n  };\\n  msg.seats = (state.seats || []).map((s) => ({\\n    id: s.id, name: s.name, color: s.color, gift: s.gift, stats: s.stats,\\n130→    x: q(s.x), y: q(s.y), tool: s.tool, use: q(s.use || 0), site: s.site,\\n    composure: q(s.composure || 0), score: s.score || 0, combo: s.combo || 0, out: !!s.out,\\n    charge: q(s.charge || 0),\\n  }));\\n  return msg;\\n}\\n\\nexport function unreliableOf(sim, sinceTick = -1) {\\n  const state = sim.state || sim;\\n  const mv = [];\\n140→  for (const e of state.entities || []) {\\n    const moved = e.kind === 'adagio' || e.kind === 'note' || e.kind === 'spore' || e.kind === 'tremolo'\\n      || e.kind === 'feeder' || e.kind === 'pool' || e.kind === 'crescendo' || e.holder != null\\n      || e.kind === 'baton' || e.kind === 'coda' || e.kind === 'legato' || e.kind === 'link';\\n    if (!moved && e.kind !== 'scratch' && e.kind !== 'bleeder') continue;\\n    mv.push([e.id, q(e.x || 0), q(e.y || 0), e.hp == null ? null : q(e.hp), flagBits(e), e.holder ?? null, q(e.vol || 0), q(e.size || 0), q(e.coverage || 0)]);\\n  }\\n  return {\\n    t: 's',\\n    k: state.tick,\\n150→    since: sinceTick,\\n    v: q(state.vitals),\\n    m: q(state.timer),\\n    sc: state.score,\\n    b: state.beat,\\n    bp: q(state.beatPhase || 0),\\n    bpm: q(state.bpm),\\n    bar: state.bar,\\n    bib: state.beatInBar,\\n    site: state.site,\\n160→    h: state.hush || 0,\\n    ar: state.arrest ? q(state.arrest.clock) : 0,\\n    ph: state.phase,\\n    tips: (state.seats || []).map(packSeat),\\n    mv,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function bytesOf(msg) {\\n  return new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(msg)).length;\\n170→}\\n\\nexport function decodeKeyframe(msg) {\\n  const w = msg.w;\\n  const seats = (msg.seats || []).map((s) => ({\\n    id: s.id, name: s.name, color: s.color, gift: s.gift, stats: s.stats || {},\\n    x: u(s.x), y: u(s.y), tool: s.tool, use: u(s.use), site: s.site,\\n    composure: u(s.composure), score: s.score, combo: s.combo, out: !!s.out, charge: u(s.charge || 0),\\n  }));\\n  return { ...w, seats, entities: (msg.ents || []).map(unpackEntity) };\\n180→}\\n\\n/** Apply an unreliable snapshot onto a decoded keyframe. Drops anything older than the base tick. */\\nexport function applyUnreliable(base, msg) {\\n  if (!base || !msg || msg.t !== 's') return base;\\n  if (base.tick != null && msg.k < base.tick) return base;\\n  const next = {\\n    ...base,\\n    tick: msg.k, vitals: u(msg.v), timer: u(msg.m), score: msg.sc, beat: msg.b,\\n    beatPhase: u(msg.bp), bpm: u(msg.bpm), bar: msg.bar, beatInBar: msg.bib, site: msg.site,\",\"content_concise\":\"100→    charge: u(row[11] || 0),\\n    name: base.name, gift: base.gift, stats: base.stats || { Cuts: 0, Stitches: 0, Burns: 0, Saves: 0, Accuracy: 100 },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Fields the operative view reads. A decoded snapshot must carry all of them. */\\nexport const VIEW_FIELDS = ['tick', 'op', 'phase', 'vitals', 'timer', 'score', 'bpm', 'beat', 'beatInBar', 'bar', 'site', 'hush', 'arrest', 'seats', 'entities', 'phaseTools', 'sites', 'flags', 'objective'];\\n\\nfunction worldOf(state) {\\n  return {\\n110→    tick: state.tick, op: state.op, phase: state.phase, phaseIndex: state.phaseIndex,\\n    objective: state.objective, vitals: state.vitals, vitalsMin: state.vitalsMin,\\n    timer: state.timer, score: state.score, misses: state.misses, combo: state.combo,\\n    bpm: state.bpm, beat: state.beat, beatInBar: state.beatInBar, beatPhase: state.beatPhase,\\n    bar: state.bar, site: state.site