1e-6;\\n}\\n\\nexport function clampTip(x, y) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":71}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e07a0e37-41fb-4055-ae55-6388a3c69875"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_590","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing the simulation worker, linter, and runner.\n\nKeeping browser and hub as functions that run-all calls. Drafting a recursive walk function for spawn lint to find nodes with two numeric coordinates, avoiding cycles and deep function traversal.\n\nTray items may sit outside the spawn ellipse. A quick Node script will verify if any `at` coordinates are invalid. Gel rectangles are not `at` nodes. Tests will be written and run immediately.\n\nPlanning to scan all JavaScript files under src/sim for banned names and the rank XS. The plan requires explicit mechanical tests for beat clock advancement, vitals drain, miss cap, and grades.\n\nA compact rules file will import Sim and verify observable outcomes. Each tool must be driven through sim.input and sim.step without reimplementing logic. The minimum inputs for scoring gels, sutures, and other tools need to be identified first.\n\nThe bot playthrough will serve as the integration test for tools. Smaller unit checks will cover §3 mechanics: tip movement, beat increments, vitals drain, timer countdown, miss and combo tracking, rank boundaries, gift effects, difficulty multipliers, checkpoint floors, and consult careful. §4 tools will be validated by spawning entities and applying input near them for a few seconds to assert progress.\n\nShallow tests may fail if the verifier demands real-path validation without hard-coded values or re-implemented logic. Tool tests will use Sim and bot directly rather than copying game mechanics. Strain tests will spawn entities and verify they exist with health.\n\nskipTo is a valid public test API for reaching phases, but it must not bypass the code path under test. The planned tests are bot invariants, determinism, snapshot roundtrip and size during the GR4 run, data lint, and idle behavior.\n\nDirect mechanic checks will cover tip speed, beat, timer, retry floors, hush versus time, difficulty, rank titles, consult timer, countScale, and notes after two failures. Tool validation will use the broken-glass bot: a completed operation means tools worked, so the test asserts seat.stats such as Stitches > 0. Not every tool has a matching stat.\n\nThe bot test `normal:broken-glass` will assert a completed operation with rank A and a valid time window to prove the tools worked. Extra shallow tests are optional. A tip-speed test is being drafted by moving the stick horizontally for 60 steps and measuring the resulting displacement.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4f98ebe6-8425-4dff-b1b2-563a096f6756-81","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function moveSeat","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/tools.js","-A":35}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1887,"output_tokens":1502,"cache_read_input_tokens":191488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"494d4adf-849f-4067-975a-5fe8d6f0513f"}
