2,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":225,\"content\":\"      this.timer -= dt * ts / Math.max(0.05, this.tuning.timerMult);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"2d11ecc4-dfcb-44da-969a-e930c6e31a3d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_593","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The timer scale is zero because the wash time scale is zero.\n\nTimer drops at 0.25 rate while sim.time advances by dt each step. A 5-second wash phase prevents expiration in one step. advanceGifts decrements hushT without clearing the wash state. Consultation begins with a plain Sim instance.\n\nCareful consultation adds 60 to the timer, raising legato from 360 to 420. Aggressive mode uses a 40-second timer. A checkpoint with low vitals and timer will be used to test retryPhase thresholds.\n\nretryPhase restores vitals to at least 60 and timer to at least 90 after a low checkpoint. countScale is 1 for one player and scales with player count for grand-rounds. Difficulty assertions are next.\n\nEasy difficulty sets drain to 0.6 and timer above 240 seconds. Rank titles are assigned by score ratio against a par of 1000: S for 1000, A for 800, B for 600, C for 400, and D for 0. Two identical simulations will verify determinism.\n\nSnapshot tests will keyframe a simulation, decode the result, and verify every view field. The GR4 worker will track bytes. A miss-limit test forces the failure path by setting misses to the limit before stepping. Vitals failure is also being tested.\n\nVitals failure is confirmed when vitals reach zero. Timer failure is also verified, with vitals checked first so a positive value still allows time to expire. Worker jobs will return a name and an optional fail string. The lint check runs in the main thread and returns a fails array. Story must-haves, Bea, Math.random, banned names, and Drape will each be tested as single tests.\n\nTeaches union and line count will each be single tests. The suite will output only failures. Drape data will be fixed only if it is a real out-of-bounds bug. Browser tests will run one browser at a time, booting WebGPU with flags; the norender menu already works.\n\nBrowser tests will cover boot without norender, WebGL without flags, and WebKit. Input stubs for pad, keys, and mouse will be tested under norender with test=1. Prompts, dev mode, attract mode, touch profiles, audio offline, save reload, about, and couch are also planned. A full playthrough across eight operations is included but may take 30 to 90 seconds. Packaging checks will run in the node runner instead of the browser suite.\n\nPackaging checks will run in the node suite and separately in the browser suite. The title string must appear only in identity.js; it is forbidden from src, tests, docs, tools/build.mjs, PROGRESS, and PLAN.\n\nThe dev folder name may contain the title, but that is not a source file so it is excluded from checks. Director and build.mjs were verified to avoid the literal title string. A full browser playthrough will use norender and test=1 flags, starting from the title screen and advancing through menu and ask states.\n\nThe browser playthrough script will skip story scenes with Tab, then loop through Chart, Operation, Report, and Fail screens until it reaches Credits roll or Main Menu. Chart focus starts on Begin, so Enter advances it.\n\nThe browser playthrough will use the `window.__game.test.bot(true)` API to drive operations in chunks of 4000 steps. A full run may take several minutes depending on step latency. The test will fail immediately if an operation hits a bot failure, recording the operation ID and reason. Guard iterations will prevent infinite retries. The attract mode test begins at the title screen.\n\nThe attract mode test waits for the attract flag to become true within 14 seconds, expecting a 9 to 12 second delay. It then collects operation IDs for 9 seconds and asserts at least three distinct operations were shown. Pressing Enter exits attract mode back to the title screen. The test also checks that localStorage is not written during attract.\n\nAttract mode advances operation IDs every two seconds via requestAnimationFrame even without simulation steps, because checkAttract creates a new simulation each cycle. The save test will use the UI to change the music slider and verify the setting persists after reload.\n\nThe save test will navigate through the settings menu with keyboard down and left to lower the music slider, then reload the page to verify the gain is below 0.1. Each test will start with a fresh localStorage context so prior state does not leak.\n\nThe dev mode test will open the pause menu and navigate to the Dev option. It will then import DEV_IDS from src/app/dev.js and run each dev command in a fresh skipTo context, catching any throws.\n\nThe dev test will use `page.evaluate` to run each `DEV_IDS` command inside a fresh `skipTo('broken-glass', 'clean')` context, catching any throws as page errors. For the slider test, the plan is to drive the range input directly rather than mutating the tuning object, since the slider changes simulation behavior live. The tipSpeed control appears on a tuning page that follows all dev commands, so the test must navigate through several dev subpages.\n\nThe slider test will mutate the tuning object directly via evaluate rather than driving a DOM range input. The test will set tipSpeed to 3.2, verify the change is reflected in the simulation state, then reset it with devRun('reset-all'). The developer questions whether mutating the tuning object from the test counts as using a slider.\n\nThe slider test will now target the actual DOM element. The test will open dev mode and press E until the tipSpeed range input appears, then fill it with 3. This triggers the input event listener to write the setting live. The reset-all button may be on the final tuning page, so both the devRun function and the UI button will be used.\n\nThe couch test will stub a pad input and boot with test=1 and norender, then navigate to grand rounds from the menu.\n\nThe couch test will use two stubbed pads to join the lobby, then start the match with bot mode enabled. After 3000 steps both tips must move independently and both scores must increase.\n\nThe couch test will step the bot for up to 8000 frames if scores are still zero after 3000. The pad stub from the plan will be copied into the test. The touch profile test will run one browser at a time across two devices, checking text and settings taps; if pointer detection fails, it will log matchMedia results and adjust only when the profile is wrong.\n\nThe audio test will render every track offline via `OfflineAudioContext` in the browser. It will import `TRACK_IDS` from source and run one render per track; the total duration is acceptable. Packaging checks will run only in the node suite.\n\nThe hub suite will run one browser at a time with sequential scenarios. It will test five GPU configurations plus one WebGL four-player run. The server will use Node’s http module to serve the tests/hub/site directory.\n\nThe Node server will decode URL paths, guard against directory traversal by requiring the resolved path to stay inside the site directory, and return 403 or 404 for invalid requests. It will serve HTML as text/html, JavaScript as text/javascript, and all other files as application/octet-stream.\n\nThe hub server will listen on a random local port and serve the site directory. The harness URL will pass game.html, auto=1, play=8000, and players=2. The suite will wait for body[data-complete=true] with a 300-second timeout and verify __hubCheck.pass while blocking console [AIHub] output. A standalone check will load game.html directly, simulate two-player input with Enter and Space at 500ms intervals, and assert no page errors, AIHub.active is false, AIHub.seeded is not true, and the screenshot is not blank.\n\nThe smoke test will be expanded to cover the no-test flag path. Without test=1, requestAnimationFrame consumes pending keys instead of test.step. A quick parallel smoke run will verify this behavior.\n\nThe standalone check will use a 2.5-second wait so the title screen is visible before asserting the screenshot is not blank. The client does not replace Math.random, so seeded will remain false. I will now write the simulation files and start that suite while writing the browser suite.\n\nThe worker process will suppress all console output so only the parent reports failures. A sloppy rank helper will accept ranks S through C and reject D or worse. The last patient in a match is skipped for rank checks when it has no rank, such as during idle or normal completion. Grand rounds normal mode will verify all seat counts with fractions. The test will also capture vitalsMin from sim.vitalsMin.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The menu path works. Next I’ll add the sim suite and run it against the shipped operations."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff61ecca-8d5f-455f-a4fa-55caa3384923-84","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/sim/worker.mjs","new_string":"import { parentPort, workerData } from 'node:worker_threads';\nimport { Sim } from '../../src/sim/sim.js';\nimport { play } from '../../src/sim/bot.js';\nimport { getOp } from '../../src/data/ops/index.js';\nimport { bytesOf, keyframeOf, unreliableOf } from '../../src/sim/snapshot.js';\n\nconst RANK = ['S', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D'];\n\nfunction finish(sim, op, mode) {\n  const frac = op.timer ? sim.time / op.timer : 0;\n  const rank = sim.rank?.id || null;\n  return {\n    complete: !!sim.complete,\n    failed: sim.failed,\n    frac,\n    vmin: sim.vitalsMin,\n    score: sim.score,\n    rank,\n    time: sim.time,\n    misses: sim.misses,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction check(sim, op, mode) {\n  const row = finish(sim, op, mode);\n  if (op.noFail) {\n    if (!row.complete || row.failed) return `${mode} ${op.id} did not complete (${row.failed || 'open'}) t=${row.time.toFixed(1)}`;\n    if (row.rank) return `${mode} ${op.id} ranked ${row.rank} with no rank expected`;\n    return null;\n  }\n  if (!row.complete || row.failed) {\n    return `${mode} ${op.id} failed ${row.failed || 'open'} t=${row.time.toFixed(1)} vmin=${row.vmin.toFixed(1)} score=${row.score} rank=${row.rank}`;\n  }\n  if (mode === 'normal') {\n    if (row.frac < 0.45 || row.frac > 0.75) {\n      return `${mode} ${op.id} clear ${row.frac.toFixed(3)} of ${op.timer}s (want 0.45-0.75) score=${row.score} vmin=${row.vmin.toFixed(1)}`;\n    }\n    if (row.vmin < 35) return `${mode} ${op.id} vitalsMin ${row.vmin.toFixed(1)}`;\n    if (row.rank !== 'S' && row.rank !== 'A') return `${mode} ${op.id} rank ${row.rank} score=${row.score}`;\n  }\n  if (mode === 'sloppy') {\n    const idx = RANK.indexOf(row.rank);\n    if (idx < 0 || idx > RANK.indexOf('C')) return `${mode} ${op.id} rank ${row.rank} score=${row.score}`;\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction runPlay(job) {\n  const op = getOp(job.id);\n  const players = job.players || 1;\n  const sim = new Sim({\n    op: job.id,\n    seed: 1,\n    physics: false,\n    difficulty: job.mode === 'sloppy' ? 'easy' : 'resident',\n    players,\n  });\n  const opts = job.mode === 'sloppy' ? { noise: 0.03, reactionDelay: 0.25 } : {};\n  let maxS = 0;\n  let maxK = 0;\n  let maxE = 0;\n  if (job.measure) {\n    let n = 0;\n    while (!sim.over && n < 1e7) {\n      const ids = sim.state.seats.map((s) => s.id);\n      for (const id of ids) {\n        sim.input(id, sim.state && id != null ? null : null);\n      }\n      n += 1;\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n  if (job.measure) {\n    const { botInput } = awaitImport();\n    let n = 0;\n    while (!sim.over && n < 1e7) {\n      for (const id of sim.seats.map((s) => s.id)) sim.input(id, botInput(sim, { id }, opts));\n      sim.step();\n      const sBytes = bytesOf(unreliableOf(sim));\n      const kBytes = bytesOf(keyframeOf(sim));\n      if (sBytes > maxS) maxS = sBytes;\n      if (kBytes > maxK) maxK = kBytes;\n      if (sim.entities.length > maxE) maxE = sim.entities.length;\n      n += 1;\n    }\n  } else {\n    play(sim, opts);\n  }\n  const fail = check(sim, op, job.mode);\n  return { fail, maxS, maxK, maxE, row: finish(sim, op, job.mode) };\n}\n\nfunction awaitImport() {\n  return botInputRef;\n}\n\nconst botInputRef = await import('../../src/sim/bot.js');\n\nfunction runIdle(job) {\n  const op = getOp(job.id);\n  const sim = new Sim({ op: job.id, seed: 1, physics: false, difficulty: 'resident', players: job.players || 1 });\n  const cap = op.noFail ? 6000 : Math.round((op.timer || 40) * 60 + 100);\n  let n = 0;\n  while (!sim.over && n < cap) {\n    sim.step();\n    n += 1;\n  }\n  if (op.noFail) {\n    if (sim.failed) return { fail: `idle ${op.id} failed ${sim.failed} at ${n}` };\n    return { fail: null };\n  }\n  if (!sim.over || !sim.failed) return { fail: `idle ${op.id} still open after ${n} steps` };\n  return { fail: null };\n}\n\nlet result;\ntry {\n  if (workerData.mode === 'idle') result = runIdle(workerData);\n  else {\n    const botInput = botInputRef.botInput;\n    const op = getOp(workerData.id);\n    const sim = new Sim({\n      op: workerData.id,\n      seed: 1,\n      physics: false,\n      difficulty: workerData.mode === 'sloppy' ? 'easy' : 'resident',\n      players: workerData.players || 1,\n    });\n    const opts = workerData.mode === 'sloppy' ? { noise: 0.03, reactionDelay: 0.25 } : {};\n    let maxS = 0;\n    let maxK = 0;\n    let maxE = 0;\n    let n = 0;\n    while (!sim.over && n < 1e7) {\n      for (const seat of sim.seats) {\n        if (!seat.out) sim.input(seat.id, botInput(sim, { id: seat.id }, opts));\n      }\n      sim.step();\n      if (workerData.measure) {\n        maxS = Math.max(maxS, bytesOf(unreliableOf(sim)));\n        maxK = Math.max(maxK, bytesOf(keyframeOf(sim)));\n        maxE = Math.max(maxE, sim.entities.length);\n      }\n      n += 1;\n    }\n    result = { fail: check(sim, op, workerData.mode), maxS, maxK, maxE };\n  }\n} catch (err) {\n  result = { fail: `${workerData.mode} ${workerData.id}: ${err.stack || err.message}` };\n}\n\nparentPort.postMessage(result);\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":575,"output_tokens":6438,"cache_read_input_tokens":195840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"31b1f677-6e52-4961-a022-8489aecf0a94"}
