umber\":275,\"content\":\"  const holding = !!seat.steady && seat.use > 0.5;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"19445f3b-7868-469e-8772-0ee8e59a019d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_621","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Adding `use` to the tips in `state()` so the test can see it.\n\nDirector state builds tips with `use` included. Next is the browser suite, then the hub suite. Browser playthroughs may be slow due to heavy main-thread work per step.\n\nCalling `test.step(500)` in a loop from Node would require 160 round trips and likely take several minutes. A single `page.evaluate` call looping inside the page is preferable, though Playwright's default 30-second timeout may be too short. Pressing keys from within the page also appears difficult.\n\nA concrete browser playthrough pattern is emerging. Keys will be sent from Playwright so real listeners fire. The loop checks the current screen state via `page.evaluate`. It presses Tab for Story, Enter for Chart and Report, and uses a bot for Operation steps. Operation steps are the bulk of the work.\n\nA single `page.evaluate` call looping 400 steps at a time should finish the full playthrough in about three to four minutes. The main overhead is likely audio scheduling and DOM paint each step, though patchLive makes paint cheap after the first update. If tests still time out, tickAudio can be bypassed during test warps without changing production code.\n\nStory scenes are skipped with Tab, one per scene. The fail path test will use skipTo to broken-glass and trigger failure via devRun('fail'). Free play, lobby, settings, about, and touch notice will be tested as separate flows in the same Chromium page to avoid extra launches. The browserTests suite will have a packaging node that runs without a browser, followed by one norender Chromium page that handles the long playthrough.\n\nThe Chromium session will run input tests, dev mode, glyphs and prompt sets, attract mode, and the remaining screens before the long playthrough. This ordering ensures earlier failures are caught even if the full playthrough times out. After the playthrough, the page will reload to verify the save file exists.\n\nTouch tests for Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 require separate contexts because they use device profiles. Audio can run in the first page via renderOffline. WebGL2, WebGPU, WebKit, and standalone rAF boot tests will be sequential and separate from the main Chromium session. Packaging will include a client hash. Screenshots will be validated by checking that PNG size exceeds 8000 bytes to ensure they are non-blank.\n\nBlank teal pages may compress to only 5–20 KB, so a size check alone is unreliable. The plan now favors verifying the screenshot buffer is not a single uniform color, or at least exceeds 15 KB and matches the Title screen state.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ae8c9f15-4fc1-4987-8313-54642134f600-62","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/goal/plan.md","offset":17,"limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ae8c9f15-4fc1-4987-8313-54642134f600-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/config/tuning.js","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":287,"output_tokens":1439,"cache_read_input_tokens":106880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"23da1e0c-b463-47b3-9903-d69d23cd0f7e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ae8c9f15-4fc1-4987-8313-54642134f600-62","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"17→## Verification plan\\n1. gating: Add or update in-repo tests that import the shipped sim (no reimplementation, no mocking the sim, no hardcoded full-state oracles) and assert criterion 2 and 3: each tool and strain rule, determinism by comparing two runs, snapshot byte caps, data lint, banned names, bot Normal/Easy/idle invariants, story order, Grand Rounds at 1–4 seats. Run the one shipped command for the sim suite (PLAN §17: `node tests/run-all.mjs sim`). It must print only failures plus a one-line count and exit 0. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/sim.log`.\\n2. gating: Browser suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs browser`) drives the shipped page, including `?test=1` hooks that call into the real sim, and asserts criterion 4: WebGPU boot with the five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, WebGL2 boot without them, WebKit boot, zero page errors, non-blank shots, pad/mouse/key input (full right stick for 1 s moves the tip by `tipSpeed` ±5%), prompt set and Xbox glyphs, dev-mode slider changes the sim and reset restores defaults, attract at 10 s ±1 s and exit without a save, Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 profiles show the exact touch notice and a working Settings tap, OfflineAudioContext output is non-silent for every track, effect, and voice, music gain 0.10, no audio-file references, save survives reload, About fields and `#about-data` parse, two stub pads score in couch play, UI playthrough `state().reached` contains Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits roll, packaging checks from criterion 1. Exit 0; failures-only output. Save `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n20→3. gating: Hub suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs hub`) copies the built page into the real harness from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` and runs every row in criterion 5 (1280×860, up to 300 s, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, `__hubCheck.pass === true`, no `[AIHub]` console line), plus the on-its-own Enter/Space sequence. Exit 0. Save `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Launch the real root HTML twice, from `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1` (bind `127.0.0.1` on an OS-picked port; confirm `window.__game` exists before trusting the page). Use the five flags above. Each run: zero page errors; canvas drawing buffer equals the requested size; painted fraction is high (a blank or speck fails — do not treat a successful blank readback as a missing tool); a driven input (stub pad or mouse) changes the on-screen tip or HUD, visible in a second capture. Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch.log` and rely on steps 1–3; a started browser that returns an empty buffer is a failure to fix.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, capture Title, Main Menu, a story shout, calm operation, danger, Hush, each strain, Report, Settings, About, the session card, one upright HUD portrait, and one upright cut-in under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Use them only to fix ten-foot type, ink, and overlap; they do not gate if steps 1–4 pass.\\n6. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json`; confirm the root HTML and dev-folder names; confirm the client hash and that the hub banner string appears once; confirm own source (not the bundle) has no banned source names, no `Math.random` in the sim, and no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub. Record results in `{SCRATCH}/package.log`.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, frame-time optimization, or lowering scene detail to chase performance.\\n- Playable post-credits “Opus 2”, online play outside AI Hub, custom names, chat, or emotes.\\n- Touch-screen gameplay controls, a second desktop layout, or Firefox WebGL2 (headless Firefox here has no WebGL2).\\n- Hardware rumble feel, a human listener, real iOS Safari, or a physical DualSense (stub the pad; guard a missing vibration actuator).\\n30→- Source-game IP, star-drawing specials, or the source’s grade names.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"17→## Verification plan\\n1. gating: Add or update in-repo tests that import the shipped sim (no reimplementation, no mocking the sim, no hardcoded full-state oracles) and assert criterion 2 and 3: each tool and strain rule, determinism by comparing two runs, snapshot byte caps, data lint, banned names, bot Normal/Easy/idle invariants, story order, Grand Rounds at 1–4 seats. Run the one shipped command for the sim suite (PLAN §17: `node tests/run-all.mjs sim`). It must print only failures plus a one-line count and exit 0. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/sim.log`.\\n2. gating: Browser suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs browser`) drives the shipped page, including `?test=1` hooks that call into the real sim, and asserts criterion 4: WebGPU boot with the five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, WebGL2 boot without them, WebKit boot, zero page errors, non-blank shots, pad/mouse/key input (full right stick for 1 s moves the tip by `tipSpeed` ±5%), prompt set and Xbox glyphs, dev-mode slider changes the sim and reset restores defaults, attract at 10 s ±1 s and exit without a save, Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 profiles show the exact touch notice and a working Settings tap, OfflineAudioContext output is non-silent for every track, effect, and voice, music gain 0.10, no audio-file references, save survives reload, About fields and `#about-data` parse, two stub pads score in couch play, UI playthrough `state().reached` contains Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits roll, packaging checks from criterion 1. Exit 0; failures-only output. Save `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n20→3. gating: Hub suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs hub`) copies the built page into the real harness from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` and runs every row in criterion 5 (1280×860, up to 300 s, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, `__hubCheck.pass === true`, no `[AIHub]` console line), plus the on-its-own Enter/Space sequence. Exit 0. Save `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Launch the real root HTML twice, from `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1` (bind `127.0.0.1` on an OS-picked port; confirm `window.__game` exists before trusting the page). Use the five flags above. Each run: zero page errors; canvas drawing buffer equals the requested size; painted fraction is high (a blank or speck fails — do not treat a successful blank readback as a missing tool); a driven input (stub pad or mouse) changes the on-screen tip or HUD, visible in a second capture. Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch.log` and rely on steps 1–3; a started browser that returns an empty buffer is a failure to fix.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, capture Title, Main Menu, a story shout, calm operation, danger, Hush, each strain, Report, Settings, About, the session card, one upright HUD portrait, and one upright cut-in under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Use them only to fix ten-foot type, ink, and overlap; they do not gate if steps 1–4 pass.\\n6. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json`; confirm the root HTML and dev-folder names; confirm the client hash and that the hub banner string appears once; confirm own source (not the bundle) has no banned source names, no `Math.random` in the sim, and no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub. Record results in `{SCRATCH}/package.log`.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, frame-time optimization, or lowering scene detail to chase performance.\\n- Playable post-credits “Opus 2”, online play outside AI Hub, custom names, chat, or emotes.\\n- Touch-screen gameplay controls, a second desktop layout, or Firefox WebGL2 (headless Firefox here has no WebGL2).\\n- Hardware rumble feel, a human listener, real iOS Safari, or a physical DualSense (stub the pad; guard a missing vibration actuator).\\n30→- Source-game IP, star-drawing specials, or the source’s grade names.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":17,\"limit\":15,\"raw_output\":\"## Verification plan\\n1. gating: Add or update in-repo tests that import the shipped sim (no reimplementation, no mocking the sim, no hardcoded full-state oracles) and assert criterion 2 and 3: each tool and strain rule, determinism by comparing two runs, snapshot byte caps, data lint, banned names, bot Normal/Easy/idle invariants, story order, Grand Rounds at 1–4 seats. Run the one shipped command for the sim suite (PLAN §17: `node tests/run-all.mjs sim`). It must print only failures plus a one-line count and exit 0. Save the log to `{SCRATCH}/sim.log`.\\n2. gating: Browser suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs browser`) drives the shipped page, including `?test=1` hooks that call into the real sim, and asserts criterion 4: WebGPU boot with the five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, WebGL2 boot without them, WebKit boot, zero page errors, non-blank shots, pad/mouse/key input (full right stick for 1 s moves the tip by `tipSpeed` ±5%), prompt set and Xbox glyphs, dev-mode slider changes the sim and reset restores defaults, attract at 10 s ±1 s and exit without a save, Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 profiles show the exact touch notice and a working Settings tap, OfflineAudioContext output is non-silent for every track, effect, and voice, music gain 0.10, no audio-file references, save survives reload, About fields and `#about-data` parse, two stub pads score in couch play, UI playthrough `state().reached` contains Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report, and Credits roll, packaging checks from criterion 1. Exit 0; failures-only output. Save `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n3. gating: Hub suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs hub`) copies the built page into the real harness from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` and runs every row in criterion 5 (1280×860, up to 300 s, `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]`, `__hubCheck.pass === true`, no `[AIHub]` console line), plus the on-its-own Enter/Space sequence. Exit 0. Save `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Launch the real root HTML twice, from `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1` (bind `127.0.0.1` on an OS-picked port; confirm `window.__game` exists before trusting the page). Use the five flags above. Each run: zero page errors; canvas drawing buffer equals the requested size; painted fraction is high (a blank or speck fails — do not treat a successful blank readback as a missing tool); a driven input (stub pad or mouse) changes the on-screen tip or HUD, visible in a second capture. Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch.log` and rely on steps 1–3; a started browser that returns an empty buffer is a failure to fix.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, capture Title, Main Menu, a story shout, calm operation, danger, Hush, each strain, Report, Settings, About, the session card, one upright HUD portrait, and one upright cut-in under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Use them only to fix ten-foot type, ink, and overlap; they do not gate if steps 1–4 pass.\\n6. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json`; confirm the root HTML and dev-folder names; confirm the client hash and that the hub banner string appears once; confirm own source (not the bundle) has no banned source names, no `Math.random` in the sim, and no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub. Record results in `{SCRATCH}/package.log`.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, frame-time optimization, or lowering scene detail to chase performance.\\n- Playable post-credits “Opus 2”, online play outside AI Hub, custom names, chat, or emotes.\\n- Touch-screen gameplay controls, a second desktop layout, or Firefox WebGL2 (headless Firefox here has no WebGL2).\\n- Hardware rumble feel, a human listener, real iOS Safari, or a physical DualSense (stub the pad; guard a missing vibration actuator).\\n- Source-game IP, star-drawing specials, or the source’s grade names.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":61}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ae8c9f15-4fc1-4987-8313-54642134f600-63","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Live tuning. Sliders mutate the object the sim reads every step. */\\nexport const TUNING_DEFAULTS = Object.freeze({\\n  tipSpeed: 1.9,\\n  stickCurve: 1.7,\\n  aimAssist: 0.35,\\n  steadyFactor: 0.4,\\n  scalpelTol: 0.055,\\n  pullTol: 1.6,\\n  suctionRate: 1.0,\\n10→  gelRadius: 0.16,\\n  stitchGateR: 0.07,\\n  laserDps: 30,\\n  laserBurn: 2,\\n  scannerRadius: 0.3,\\n  clampWindow: 0.18,\\n  defibWindow: 0.30,\\n  drainMult: 1,\\n  timerMult: 1,\\n  tempoPressure: 60,\\n20→  stabilizerHeal: 15,\\n  stabilizerCooldown: 3,\\n  missLimit: 8,\\n  strainHpMult: 1,\\n  strainSpeedMult: 1,\\n  spawnRateMult: 1,\\n  composureGain: 1,\\n  hushDuration: 7,\\n  hushTimeScale: 0.25,\\n  sforzandoStun: 3,\\n30→  sforzandoDamage: 0.25,\\n  sforzandoToolMult: 2,\\n  sforzandoDuration: 6,\\n});\\n\\nexport const TUNING_RANGES = Object.freeze({\\n  tipSpeed: [0.8, 3.5],\\n  stickCurve: [1, 3],\\n  aimAssist: [0, 1],\\n  steadyFactor: [0.2, 0.8],\\n40→  scalpelTol: [0.02, 0.12],\\n  pullTol: [0.6, 3],\\n  suctionRate: [0.3, 3],\\n  gelRadius: [0.08, 0.3],\\n  stitchGateR: [0.03, 0.15],\\n  laserDps: [10, 80],\\n  laserBurn: [0, 6],\\n  scannerRadius: [0.15, 0.5],\\n  clampWindow: [0.06, 0.4],\\n  defibWindow: [0.1, 0.6],\\n50→  drainMult: [0, 3],\\n  timerMult: [0.5, 2],\\n  tempoPressure: [0, 120],\\n  stabilizerHeal: [5, 30],\\n  stabilizerCooldown: [0.5, 8],\\n  missLimit: [3, 20],\\n  strainHpMult: [0.3, 3],\\n  strainSpeedMult: [0.3, 2.5],\\n  spawnRateMult: [0.3, 2.5],\\n  composureGain: [0.2, 3],\\n60→  hushDuration: [2, 15],\\n  hushTimeScale: [0.05, 0.7],\\n  sforzandoStun: [1, 6],\\n  sforzandoDamage: [0.05, 0.6],\\n  sforzandoToolMult: [1.2, 4],\\n  sforzandoDuration: [2, 12],\\n});\\n\\nexport const TUNING_PAGES = Object.freeze([\\n  { id: 'hands', label: 'Hands', keys: ['tipSpeed', 'stickCurve', 'aimAssist', 'steadyFactor'] },\\n70→  { id: 'tools', label: 'Tools', keys: ['scalpelTol', 'pullTol', 'suctionRate', 'gelRadius', 'stitchGateR', 'laserDps', 'laserBurn', 'scannerRadius', 'clampWindow', 'defibWindow'] },\\n  { id: 'patient', label: 'Patient', keys: ['drainMult', 'timerMult', 'tempoPressure', 'stabilizerHeal', 'stabilizerCooldown', 'missLimit'] },\\n  { id: 'strains', label: 'Strains', keys: ['strainHpMult', 'strainSpeedMult', 'spawnRateMult'] },\\n  { id: 'gifts', label: 'Gifts', keys: ['composureGain', 'hushDuration', 'hushTimeScale', 'sforzandoStun', 'sforzandoDamage', 'sforzandoToolMult', 'sforzandoDuration'] },\\n]);\\n\\nexport function createTuning(over) {\\n  return { ...TUNING_DEFAULTS, ...over };\\n}\\n\\n80→/** Copy defaults back onto a live object so holders of the reference see the reset. */\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Live tuning. Sliders mutate the object the sim reads every step. */\\nexport const TUNING_DEFAULTS = Object.freeze({\\n  tipSpeed: 1.9,\\n  stickCurve: 1.7,\\n  aimAssist: 0.35,\\n  steadyFactor: 0.4,\\n  scalpelTol: 0.055,\\n  pullTol: 1.6,\\n  suctionRate: 1.0,\\n10→  gelRadius: 0.16,\\n  stitchGateR: 0.07,\\n  laserDps: 30,\\n  laserBurn: 2,\\n  scannerRadius: 0.3,\\n  clampWindow: 0.18,\\n  defibWindow: 0.30,\\n  drainMult: 1,\\n  timerMult: 1,\\n  tempoPressure: 60,\\n20→  stabilizerHeal: 15,\\n  stabilizerCooldown: 3,\\n  missLimit: 8,\\n  strainHpMult: 1,\\n  strainSpeedMult: 1,\\n  spawnRateMult: 1,\\n  composureGain: 1,\\n  hushDuration: 7,\\n  hushTimeScale: 0.25,\\n  sforzandoStun: 3,\\n30→  sforzandoDamage: 0.25,\\n  sforzandoToolMult: 2,\\n  sforzandoDuration: 6,\\n});\\n\\nexport const TUNING_RANGES = Object.freeze({\\n  tipSpeed: [0.8, 3.5],\\n  stickCurve: [1, 3],\\n  aimAssist: [0, 1],\\n  steadyFactor: [0.2, 0.8],\\n40→  scalpelTol: [0.02, 0.12],\\n  pullTol: [0.6, 3],\\n  suctionRate: [0.3, 3],\\n  gelRadius: [0.08, 0.3],\\n  stitchGateR: [0.03, 0.15],\\n  laserDps: [10, 80],\\n  laserBurn: [0, 6],\\n  scannerRadius: [0.15, 0.5],\\n  clampWindow: [0.06, 0.4],\\n  defibWindow: [0.1, 0.6],\\n50→  drainMult: [0, 3],\\n  timerMult: [0.5, 2],\\n  tempoPressure: [0, 120],\\n  stabilizerHeal: [5, 30],\\n  stabilizerCooldown: [0.5, 8],\\n  missLimit: [3, 20],\\n  strainHpMult: [0.3, 3],\\n  strainSpeedMult: [0.3, 2.5],\\n  spawnRateMult: [0.3, 2.5],\\n  composureGain: [0.2, 3],\\n60→  hushDuration: [2, 15],\\n  hushTimeScale: [0.05, 0.7],\\n  sforzandoStun: [1, 6],\\n  sforzandoDamage: [0.05, 0.6],\\n  sforzandoToolMult: [1.2, 4],\\n  sforzandoDuration: [2, 12],\\n});\\n\\nexport const TUNING_PAGES = Object.freeze([\\n  { id: 'hands', label: 'Hands', keys: ['tipSpeed', 'stickCurve', 'aimAssist', 'steadyFactor'] },\\n70→  { id: 'tools', label: 'Tools', keys: ['scalpelTol', 'pullTol', 'suctionRate', 'gelRadius', 'stitchGateR', 'laserDps', 'laserBurn', 'scannerRadius', 'clampWindow', 'defibWindow'] },\\n  { id: 'patient', label: 'Patient', keys: ['drainMult', 'timerMult', 'tempoPressure', 'stabilizerHeal', 'stabilizerCooldown', 'missLimit'] },\\n  { id: 'strains', label: 'Strains', keys: ['strainHpMult', 'strainSpeedMult', 'spawnRateMult'] },\\n  { id: 'gifts', label: 'Gifts', keys: ['composureGain', 'hushDuration', 'hushTimeScale', 'sforzandoStun', 'sforzandoDamage', 'sforzandoToolMult', 'sforzandoDuration'] },\\n]);\\n\\nexport function createTuning(over) {\\n  return { ...TUNING_DEFAULTS