{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_636","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"cardSent is set when showsCard is true, indicating the ready signal was sent.\n\nThe ready sequence is verified: ready() fires immediately, showsCard becomes true, and cardSent sets on the next tick. The server copy also calls ready(), since every player copy must be ready.\n\nready() is a load signal, not the card answer, so the server can call it immediately without waiting for its view. View initialization on four WebGPU pages may be slow, but ready() does not block. One bug to fix: clear one-shots only after a step.\n\nOld snapshot drops need a tick check on s messages. The host simulation creation already skips view initialization. Physics is enabled in the hub, but RAPIER readiness is awaited before creating a new simulation. WebGPU inside iframes on localhost is secure. Four WebGPU players may exhaust memory; the first five runs use GPU flags, and any crash would fall back to WebGL.\n\nIf four WebGPU iframes crash from memory exhaustion, the test will run in a single browser instead. The scene itself cannot be simplified.\n\nThe `finish` outcome awards only the first-ranked player. If all scores are zero, the lowest-ID player still receives the award.\n\nStats accuracy defaults to 100 when undefined.\n\nWhen simulation seat IDs do not match player IDs, every player scores zero but remains in the standings.\n\nThe hub emits a leave event with an ID.\n\nLeft players are excluded from standings. The harness already omits them.\n\nWhen the last player leaves, the host drops them and the round voids.\n\nIf the host is removed, the host page is destroyed before it can finish. Other clients still receive the end signal and set ended, so they do not finish.\n\nServer mode is confirmed: the server acts as host and runs the simulation, while players are clients. Traffic flows bidirectionally between them. The server receives i messages from other cells and sends s, k, and e responses. WebGL fallback is enabled when the harness passes webgl=1.\n\nThe session is nearly ready. A warning will appear if finish standings are missing. Payloads exceeding 16000 characters are dropped before shipping. Keyframe objects measure about 844 bytes, so they stay well under the 1100-byte unreliable limit. Event messages are small because only type, who, key, and id are kept. The remaining fixes are clearing one-shots after a step and adding tick checks for old snapshot drops.\n\nA bug was found in the host boot logic. If `physicsReady` throws, the current catch block calls `AIHub.fail`, which voids the round even though graphics might still be available. The host should create the simulation with `physics: false` when physics fails, rather than failing the entire session.\n\nThe outer boot catch should only log the error and must not call AIHub.fail. The host already handles graphics failures internally by catching createView errors and falling back to a non-physical simulation, so the outer catch must not override that.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a2fb9468-0465-4601-9bfb-bc68cbc60ad1-87","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"this\\.rng","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1732,"output_tokens":1565,"cache_read_input_tokens":142720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6ae96a83-0b72-4b19-8be7-2e96dca8995f"}
