{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4f76aa34-6268-4398-b920-4e93fc5406ce-92","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→function packSeat(s) {\\n  return [s.id, q(s.x), q(s.y), s.tool, q(s.use || 0), s.site, q(s.composure || 0), s.score || 0, s.combo || 0, s.out ? 1 : 0, s.color || '', q(s.charge || 0)];\\n}\\n\\nfunction unpackSeat(row, prev) {\\n  const base = prev || {};\\n  return {\\n    ...base,\\n    id: row[0], x: u(row[1]), y: u(row[2]), tool: row[3], use: u(row[4]), site: row[5],\\n    composure: u(row[6]), score: row[7], combo: row[8], out: !!row[9], color: row[10] || base.color,\\n100→    charge: u(row[11] || 0),\\n    name: base.name, gift: base.gift, stats: base.stats || { Cuts: 0, Stitches: 0, Burns: 0, Saves: 0, Accuracy: 100 },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Fields the operative view reads. A decoded snapshot must carry all of them. */\\nexport const VIEW_FIELDS = ['tick', 'op', 'phase', 'vitals', 'timer', 'score', 'bpm', 'beat', 'beatInBar', 'bar', 'site', 'hush', 'arrest', 'seats', 'entities', 'phaseTools', 'sites', 'flags', 'objective'];\\n\\nfunction worldOf(state) {\\n  return {\\n110→    tick: state.tick, op: state.op, phase: state.phase, phaseIndex: state.phaseIndex,\\n    objective: state.objective, vitals: state.vitals, vitalsMin: state.vitalsMin,\\n    timer: state.timer, score: state.score, misses: state.misses, combo: state.combo,\\n    bpm: state.bpm, beat: state.beat, beatInBar: state.beatInBar, beatPhase: state.beatPhase,\\n    bar: state.bar, site: state.site, doctor: state.doctor, hush: state.hush,\\n    arrest: state.arrest, complete: state.complete, failed: state.failed, over: state.over,\\n    rank: state.rank, phaseTools: state.phaseTools, sites: state.sites, flags: state.flags,\\n    notes: state.notes, clampsUsed: state.clampsUsed,\\n  };\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"90→function packSeat(s) {\\n  return [s.id, q(s.x), q(s.y), s.tool, q(s.use || 0), s.site, q(s.composure || 0), s.score || 0, s.combo || 0, s.out ? 1 : 0, s.color || '', q(s.charge || 0)];\\n}\\n\\nfunction unpackSeat(row, prev) {\\n  const base = prev || {};\\n  return {\\n    ...base,\\n    id: row[0], x: u(row[1]), y: u(row[2]), tool: row[3], use: u(row[4]), site: row[5],\\n    composure: u(row[6]), score: row[7], combo: row[8], out: !!row[9], color: row[10] || base.color,\\n100→    charge: u(row[11] || 0),\\n    name: base.name, gift: base.gift, stats: base.stats || { Cuts: 0, Stitches: 0, Burns: 0, Saves: 0, Accuracy: 100 },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Fields the operative view reads. A decoded snapshot must carry all of them. */\\nexport const VIEW_FIELDS = ['tick', 'op', 'phase', 'vitals', 'timer', 'score', 'bpm', 'beat', 'beatInBar', 'bar', 'site', 'hush', 'arrest', 'seats', 'entities', 'phaseTools', 'sites', 'flags', 'objective'];\\n\\nfunction worldOf(state) {\\n  return {\\n110→    tick: state.tick, op: state.op, phase: state.phase, phaseIndex: state.phaseIndex,\\n    objective: state.objective, vitals: state.vitals, vitalsMin: state.vitalsMin,\\n    timer: state.timer, score: state.score, misses: state.misses, combo: state.combo,\\n    bpm: state.bpm, beat: state.beat, beatInBar: state.beatInBar, beatPhase: state.beatPhase,\\n    bar: state.bar, site: state.site, doctor: state.doctor, hush: state.hush,\\n    arrest: state.arrest, complete: state.complete, failed: state.failed, over: state.over,\\n    rank: state.rank, phaseTools: state.phaseTools, sites: state.sites, flags: state.flags,\\n    notes: state.notes, clampsUsed: state.clampsUsed,\\n  };\\n}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/snapshot.js\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"function packSeat(s) {\\n  return [s.id, q(s.x), q(s.y), s.tool, q(s.use || 0), s.site, q(s.composure || 0), s.score || 0, s.combo || 0, s.out ? 1 : 0, s.color || '', q(s.charge || 0)];\\n}\\n\\nfunction unpackSeat(row, prev) {\\n  const base = prev || {};\\n  return {\\n    ...base,\\n    id: row[0], x: u(row[1]), y: u(row[2]), tool: row[3], use: u(row[4]), site: row[5],\\n    composure: u(row[6]), score: row[7], combo: row[8], out: !!row[9], color: row[10] || base.color,\\n    charge: u(row[11] || 0),\\n    name: base.name, gift: base.gift, stats: base.stats || { Cuts: 0, Stitches: 0, Burns: 0, Saves: 0, Accuracy: 100 },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Fields the operative view reads. A decoded snapshot must carry all of them. */\\nexport const VIEW_FIELDS = ['tick', 'op', 'phase', 'vitals', 'timer', 'score', 'bpm', 'beat', 'beatInBar', 'bar', 'site', 'hush', 'arrest', 'seats', 'entities', 'phaseTools', 'sites', 'flags', 'objective'];\\n\\nfunction worldOf(state) {\\n  return {\\n    tick: state.tick, op: state.op, phase: state.phase, phaseIndex: state.phaseIndex,\\n    objective: state.objective, vitals: state.vitals, vitalsMin: state.vitalsMin,\\n    timer: state.timer, score: state.score, misses: state.misses, combo: state.combo,\\n    bpm: state.bpm, beat: state.beat, beatInBar: state.beatInBar, beatPhase: state.beatPhase,\\n    bar: state.bar, site: state.site, doctor: state.doctor, hush: state.hush,\\n    arrest: state.arrest, complete: state.complete, failed: state.failed, over: state.over,\\n    rank: state.rank, phaseTools: state.phaseTools, sites: state.sites, flags: state.flags,\\n    notes: state.notes, clampsUsed: state.clampsUsed,\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":210}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"049a9647-9ede-4579-976e-a76a793433ad"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_642","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The session keyframe drop for older ticks is already handled in the handler.\n\nFixing the physics fail bug and one-shot clear next. Will write tests after that. The four WebGPU contexts will stay as-is. Gamepad and key polling in the iframe is fine. DOM rebuilds every 16ms are acceptable because card left changes only once per second. The async render flag prevents overlapping paints, but slow software WebGPU frames may pile up render promises.\n\nOnly one host renders the simulation. The four WebGPU contexts are renderers, not hosts, so the memory risk is acceptable if it crashes. createView safely falls back from WebGPU to WebGL. I will update session.js and write both test suites completely.\n\nThe one-shot clear now uses a stepped flag set inside the 60fps loop. The physics fix checks `physicsReady()` and passes the result to the Sim constructor. The outer AIHub fail wrapper is being removed to avoid double-failing if the inner catch already sets failedGfx.\n\nThe outer catch block will be kept but left empty to prevent unhandled rejections. The director use field also needs a rebuild.\n\nI will rebuild once after all edits, then run the browser suite in the background. The packaging walk skips node_modules and includes only src files. The title check passes because identity.js is the only JavaScript file containing the exact title string.\n\nThe director source imports GAME_TITLE rather than embedding the title string directly. The browser test suite will use a class-like fails array. Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 device names are expected in Playwright 1.63, but the suite will report if they are missing. WebGPU launch arguments must attach to the browser context, not the device.\n\nHeadless Playwright does not need xvfb because DISPLAY is unset. Boot tests will use a 1280x720 viewport. Screenshots will be validated by size and title text presence, since a solid teal page can be very small. Canvas fill verification belongs to the launch check, not the browser suite.\n\nThe browser suite will verify that screenshots are not blank. Launch verification is deferred to two real launches after the suites finish. Canvas resize sizing will be checked during those later tests. The playthrough uses Tab to skip story text and Enter to activate the chart begin button. If the bot does not finish within four minutes, it will report the current screen, operation, and phase. Resident difficulty appears after confirmation.\n\nConsult careful mode uses a longer timer and less drain, so the bot should still finish within 45–75 seconds of the DATA timer. The browser test only checks that the operation completes and reaches its target screens, not the exact completion fraction. A lower rank from reduced scoring is acceptable because the UI playthrough does not verify rank. If vitals fail, the screen becomes Fail.\n\nCareful mode should help vitals. The last-patient bot passed idle and normal simulation tests. The browser suite will collect failures in a `fails` array and continue running other sections in parallel browsers instead of aborting on error. A `check` helper will record each result, and the main function will wrap each test in try-catch to catch unexpected exceptions.\n\nThe scripted test will run inside a single browser with internal try/finally cleanup. It will catch its own exceptions and report them via the check helper so partial results are not lost. A heartbeat log to a scratch file may be added for debugging without polluting stdout.\n\nThe test suite will not write progress to stderr, since the verifier expects only failures and a count. A heartbeat log may be appended to a scratch file instead, but the test code must avoid hardcoding that path.\n\nNo heartbeat log will be written to avoid extra output. The process can be monitored with ps instead.\n\nThe story early return to tick audio is not required for tests.\n\nMenu activation via mouse click calls activate immediately without a step. Hovering sets focus, and clicking the free option follows.\n\nInput tests will start at the title screen, run attract first while lastInput is fresh, exit attract with a key press, then test menus.\n\nThe scripted test will wait 11 seconds in attract mode, then run three operations over roughly six seconds, exit with a key press, and continue through input tests, screens, and playthrough. The attract wait adds about 20 seconds to the total runtime.\n\nA localStorage save check will verify that no save data exists before and after exiting attract mode.\n\nChanging the glyphs setting and reloading will confirm that settings are restored correctly.\n\nThe scripted test will use the `skipTo` test hook to drive an operation before running input tests, since the plan explicitly permits using `?test=1` hooks. The planned session order is: attract on title, exit, empty save snapshot, then input tests. Additional screens to verify include About (four headings and JSON keys), Fail, Free play, and Lobby.\n\nMenu navigation will use real keys rather than skipTo. The scripted test will also cover dev-run from pause, slider, reset, settings glyphs, couch via menu and pads, about, fail via devRun, free play, audio renderOffline, save reload, and a fresh-context playthrough to avoid a save chooser.\n\nThe playthrough will run in a fresh context or after clearing localStorage and reloading, since attract mode is already complete. Touch and GPU tests will run in separate browsers. The devRun hook for each operation ID can be embedded directly in the scripted page. The skipTo test hook must set the screen to Operation so pause works correctly. The pad initialization script must be injected before navigation begins.\n\nThe pad stub script creates two connected DualSense gamepads with empty axes and buttons. It overrides navigator.getGamepads to return them on every poll. The couch join logic detects a button press edge on the first pad to trigger joining.\n\nThe couch join test will press the confirm button on both pads in a single step so both join. After releasing, Enter begins the game.\n\nAfter the couch join press, both pads release their confirm buttons and a keyboard Enter step begins the game. The focus stays on Begin because pad axes are zero and cross is not up. Movement is tested by setting aimAssist to zero, pushing pad 0 forward and pad 1 backward on the Z axis, and stepping for thirty frames. The device becomes pad-based because active pads override keyboard input, and the couch feedSim uses pad frames for joined players.\n\nThe bot-on test will run for 1800 steps after resetting sticks to avoid pad interference, then check scores. If they remain zero, it will step another 3600 frames because GR may need time to spawn scoreable things. Out seats will be verified by checking that player IDs 0 and 1 have a score of zero. The browser bot uses the same code as the Node version, so its scoring behavior is trusted. A note will be added to the session to avoid failing on physics.\n\nOne-shot inputs are cleared only after a step. During session pause, the host skips applying local input but still steps and applies commands from other clients. The host never sends its own input to itself, so it cannot overwrite its own command.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-023805f1-641e-43d6-8912-cd0ff44faae0-93","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function checkStandings|won|standings","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/round.js","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":791,"output_tokens":3366,"cache_read_input_tokens":149632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"bd077f4c-6331-4961-b893-341c430727cb"}
