{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f74c30ec-3846-43d6-803b-cd58fd50849d-96","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"190→  timings = TIMINGS,\\n  gate = false,\\n  serverKey = null,\\n}) {\\n  mode = modeOf(mode);\\n  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\\n  const seats = [...players]\\n    .sort((a, b) => a.slot - b.slot)\\n    .map((p, id) => ({\\n      id,\\n200→      key: p.key,\\n      slot: p.slot,\\n      name: p.name,\\n      color: SLOT_COLORS[p.slot % SLOT_COLORS.length],\\n      hello: false,\\n      ready: false,\\n      out: null,\\n      result: null,\\n      /** The last progress score the hub saw: the result of a player who never reports one. */\\n      progress: null,\\n210→      stats: null,\\n      awards: [],\\n      caps: null,\\n      hidden: null,\\n    }));\\n  const server = serverKey\\n    ? { id: seats.length, key: serverKey, slot: null, name: 'Server', color: null, hello: false, ready: false, out: null, result: null, progress: null, stats: null, awards: [], caps: null, hidden: null }\\n    : null;\\n  /** Every copy in the round: the players, then the server when there is one. */\\n  const copies = server ? [...seats, server] : seats;\\n220→  const byKey = new Map(copies.map((s) => [s.key, s]));\\n  const ids = seats.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const host = server ?? byKey.get(hostKey) ?? seats[0];\\n  const timers = new Set();\\n  const issues = [];\\n  let phase = 'loading';\\n  let goAt = null;\\n  let record = null;\\n  let released = !gate;\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"190→  timings = TIMINGS,\\n  gate = false,\\n  serverKey = null,\\n}) {\\n  mode = modeOf(mode);\\n  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\\n  const seats = [...players]\\n    .sort((a, b) => a.slot - b.slot)\\n    .map((p, id) => ({\\n      id,\\n200→      key: p.key,\\n      slot: p.slot,\\n      name: p.name,\\n      color: SLOT_COLORS[p.slot % SLOT_COLORS.length],\\n      hello: false,\\n      ready: false,\\n      out: null,\\n      result: null,\\n      /** The last progress score the hub saw: the result of a player who never reports one. */\\n      progress: null,\\n210→      stats: null,\\n      awards: [],\\n      caps: null,\\n      hidden: null,\\n    }));\\n  const server = serverKey\\n    ? { id: seats.length, key: serverKey, slot: null, name: 'Server', color: null, hello: false, ready: false, out: null, result: null, progress: null, stats: null, awards: [], caps: null, hidden: null }\\n    : null;\\n  /** Every copy in the round: the players, then the server when there is one. */\\n  const copies = server ? [...seats, server] : seats;\\n220→  const byKey = new Map(copies.map((s) => [s.key, s]));\\n  const ids = seats.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const host = server ?? byKey.get(hostKey) ?? seats[0];\\n  const timers = new Set();\\n  const issues = [];\\n  let phase = 'loading';\\n  let goAt = null;\\n  let record = null;\\n  let released = !gate;\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/round.js\",\"offset\":190,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  timings = TIMINGS,\\n  gate = false,\\n  serverKey = null,\\n}) {\\n  mode = modeOf(mode);\\n  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\\n  const seats = [...players]\\n    .sort((a, b) => a.slot - b.slot)\\n    .map((p, id) => ({\\n      id,\\n      key: p.key,\\n      slot: p.slot,\\n      name: p.name,\\n      color: SLOT_COLORS[p.slot % SLOT_COLORS.length],\\n      hello: false,\\n      ready: false,\\n      out: null,\\n      result: null,\\n      /** The last progress score the hub saw: the result of a player who never reports one. */\\n      progress: null,\\n      stats: null,\\n      awards: [],\\n      caps: null,\\n      hidden: null,\\n    }));\\n  const server = serverKey\\n    ? { id: seats.length, key: serverKey, slot: null, name: 'Server', color: null, hello: false, ready: false, out: null, result: null, progress: null, stats: null, awards: [], caps: null, hidden: null }\\n    : null;\\n  /** Every copy in the round: the players, then the server when there is one. */\\n  const copies = server ? [...seats, server] : seats;\\n  const byKey = new Map(copies.map((s) => [s.key, s]));\\n  const ids = seats.map((s) => s.id);\\n  const host = server ?? byKey.get(hostKey) ?? seats[0];\\n  const timers = new Set();\\n  const issues = [];\\n  let phase = 'loading';\\n  let goAt = null;\\n  let record = null;\\n  let released = !gate;\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":533}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"c47aa17b-b539-4a19-a556-12c96dc3b5a6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_646","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Player IDs run from 0 to n-1. The server ID equals seats.length.\n\nHost logic is sound. The server ID is excluded from player lists but correctly identifies the host. Simulations use only player IDs for inputs and standings. Session physics are fixed. Award titles are short.\n\nWriting browser and hub test suites now. One-shot clearing will be fixed too. A Node HTTP server is being set up for the hub suite.\n\nThe hub test server is complete. It serves files from the tests/hub/site directory. The browser suite will run four scenarios: 2-player, 3-player with network latency and jitter, 4-player with those same settings, and a host-leave scenario.\n\nThe hub suite now includes a server scenario and a 4-player WebGL test. Tests run at 1280x860 with a 300-second timeout. Each run waits for `data-complete=true` and checks that no `[AIHub]` console lines appear. Page errors also fail the test. Only one browser instance runs at a time, closing between scenarios.\n\nThe hub suite is expected to take 10 to 20 minutes total. The harness URL for WebGL tests passes the query string through the game parameter so the searchParams logic preserves it.\n\nThe test harness will verify the iframe loads the correct game page by checking for `__game` and passing traffic checks. The standalone Enter/Space sequence is required in both the hub suite and the browser suite.\n\nThe standalone Enter/Space sequence will be run in the hub suite only. The browser suite covers the remaining criterion 4 items. The standalone test loads the page via file://, waits two and a half seconds, then presses Enter and Space with five hundred millisecond gaps. It waits two seconds after, checks that the screenshot is not blank, verifies AIHub.active is false, and confirms seeded is not true. Chromium will run without GPU flags to force WebGL fallback.\n\nThe standalone Enter/Space sequence is appended to the hub suite as a single browser test. It exercises the real rAF path rather than the smoke test step, pressing Enter to reach the main menu, Space to confirm the story, Enter to confirm the resident, and Space to advance a line. Audio resumes on keypress, and ignoreUntil is not involved.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7cc43876-c0d6-4552-b620-c423083c6b21-97","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"connect: function|hub.connect|type === 'welcome'","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tools/vendor/session.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":519,"output_tokens":1626,"cache_read_input_tokens":156032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"ac42c54a-d6b5-4640-abcd-08f5ad601dcc"}
