       cmd.swap = false;\\n          cmd.siteDelta = 0;\\n        }\\n      }\",\"new_line\":220,\"context_before\":\"      }\\n      for (const [id, cmd] of cmds) model.sim.input(id, cmd);\\n      acc += dt;\\n\",\"context_after\":\"      if (model.sim.over) finish(!!model.sim.complete);\\n      accS += dt * 1000;\\n      accK += dt * 1000;\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6903aa79-cbff-4d5c-8e0c-6d2579b5f1b4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_650","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Older keyframes were already dropped in the handler.\n\nWriting the browser and hub suites as complete files. Session checks will ignore keyframes with ticks below the applied base tick. The keyframe handler will reapply when ticks are equal. Tests will be written next. Importing DEV_IDS from dev.js is acceptable.\n\nThe browser suite will be written carefully. Skipping audio tick before story returns to avoid music stalls. The dev menu page count will be computed by pressing Escape, stepping the game, and navigating down four items to find the tipSpeed readout.\n\nPressing Enter to open the dev menu and stepping the game. The test will press E up to 20 times until the body text contains \"tipSpeed\". ArrowRight will nudge the focused item.\n\nThe dev menu layout is tipSpeed first, then aimAssist third. The test will press E until the page indicator shows the final page and the text contains \"Reset all\", then press Enter to reset.\n\nThe early \"Reset all\" button would reset too early if focus is wrong. The test will call `devRun('reset-all')` directly via evaluate on the final page after nudging. This satisfies the Pause-menu entry requirement and avoids premature resets. Each tool will be set through devRun, and the slider adjusted with keyboard nudges. Reset will be verified by checking restored values.\n\nThe test will loop through every DEV_IDS entry once, calling devRun and catching page errors. Each win or fail path will trigger the broken-glass screen before the operation. Scene-next opens the story and returns. The op object refreshes before each call to avoid state conflicts. Complete-phase on the final phase succeeds the operation.\n\nThe test sequence is now fixed. It begins by skipping to the broken-glass screen, then opens the dev menu, nudges the tipSpeed slider, closes overlays, and measures stick movement over sixty steps. The dx value is compared against tuning.tipSpeed before any reset occurs. Afterward the suite runs all dev tool ids via devRun, followed by the remaining screens.\n\nThe WASD stick test will use aimAssist at zero before nudging tipSpeed to expect 1.9, then retest at the new speed. Pads will be zeroed between tests. The suite file can now be written with an errors array on the page. Playwright keyboard presses work on the focused page, and test.step consumes pending input after evaluate.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5013c0fe-a8b7-4b1c-a3e0-9cda27845fc1-103","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5013c0fe-a8b7-4b1c-a3e0-9cda27845fc1-104","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Math\\.random|\\.mp3|\\.ogg|\\.wav|\\.flac","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2981,"output_tokens":1470,"cache_read_input_tokens":159488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"2dabba85-0b82-4e76-8763-0e0608a6404a"}
