{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_674","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A critical bug was found in the stepOnce function.\n\nThe pause overlay logic appears sound. The focus shifted to stub pads.\n\nThe test stubs always report two connected gamepads. This could cause input.js to treat them as active devices. The pad edge logic might also interfere with focus movement.\n\nThe idle stub pad issue is unlikely to be the cause. The test zeroes pad axes before pressing Escape, so the device should already be keyboard when the pause overlay opens. The next step is to press KeyA and move the mouse.\n\nThe pause overlay opened successfully. ArrowDown presses and Enter were sent, but the developer menu did not appear. The focus may not have started at zero. The stub pad's down edge might also be stuck true every frame.\n\nThe real bug is in the confirm logic. When the pause overlay is active, `model.screen` remains `'Operation'`, so the code ignores the Enter key press. ArrowDown still shifts focus, but Enter does nothing.\n\nThe confirm logic failure explains the missing developer menu, unchanged slider, and failed quit. Hover free fails because the focus never returns to the main menu. ArrowDown still shifts focus while paused on Operation. The page-right logic for overlay pause is also being examined.\n\nThe page-turn and slider-nudge logic is confirmed harmless during pause. The fix is to allow confirm presses to activate the focused item when any overlay is active, even if the screen remains Operation.\n\nThe back button already handles overlays correctly, but confirm does not. The screen check was meant to reserve Enter for tool use during Operation, yet it wrongly blocks menu activation while any overlay is open.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-233bef8d-618b-4e6b-93e6-637998f3e94b-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function currentItems|function activate\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-233bef8d-618b-4e6b-93e6-637998f3e94b-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/input/input.js","offset":100,"limit":180}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2043,"output_tokens":1501,"cache_read_input_tokens":59520,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"b18f3916-17eb-412b-94e6-27594b6281e1"}
