{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_678","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"49 tests passed, covering packaging checks, early scripted checks, touch, and backends.\n\nThe scripted throw occurred before the lobby audio playthrough tests. The fix is in director.js, which must be rebuilt before rerunning the full browser suite because the suite loads the bundled root HTML. Playthrough does not need a pause confirmation since it uses Enter on Chart and Report screens.\n\nVerified that the pause confirmation fix won't break ArrowDown or KeyE behavior. The pending state is set once per keypress and cleared after step, preventing double page turns.\n\nThe slider test logic was also verified. ArrowRight nudges settings correctly. Escape from dev properly toggles the pause overlay and clears it on a second press.\n\nThe second Escape key correctly unpause the game when the overlay is pause. The speed test then increases tipSpeed and sets aimAssist to zero.\n\nThe pad aim test may fail after unpause. The tip could already be near the x clamp of 1.9 from earlier moves, so the next step would only travel about 1.05 instead of the expected 2.035. This would cause the \"slider changes the sim\" check to fail.\n\nThe pad aim test sequence leaves the tip near x ≈ 0.85. The mouse check only requires movement away from the start point, not a specific location.\n\nThe mouse position at 62% width likely places the tip near x ≈ 1.5. The pad aim test should recenter the tip before measuring, since it currently leaves the tip near the right clamp and the subsequent +2.0 step would be fully clamped.\n\nThe pad aim test should start from the left clamp. The tip is currently near x ≈ 0.85, so a +2.035 step would be clamped to 1.9 and yield only 1.05 distance. Moving the tip left first would give it full room to travel.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f2f63c9a-2392-47ac-99aa-89b1eb22bb27-21","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":1520,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f2f63c9a-2392-47ac-99aa-89b1eb22bb27-22","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pointerToField","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2063,"output_tokens":1715,"cache_read_input_tokens":69888,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"5909d27f-7aea-4982-b745-5d74c4f7bd50"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f2f63c9a-2392-47ac-99aa-89b1eb22bb27-21","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1520→      list.append(seat);\\n    }\\n    const secs = document.createElement('p');\\n    secs.className = 'vitals';\\n    if (model.card?.left != null) secs.textContent = String(Math.max(0, Math.ceil(model.card.left)));\\n    const how = document.createElement('p');\\n    how.className = 'note';\\n    how.textContent = 'Aim with the right stick or the mouse. Use with R2 or click. Tools are the left stick or the number keys.';\\n    const menu = document.createElement('div');\\n    menu.className = 'menu';\\n1530→    for (const item of [{ id: 'ready', label: 'Ready' }, { id: 'more', label: 'More Time' }]) {\\n      const b = document.createElement('button');\\n      b.type = 'button';\\n      b.className = 'item';\\n      b.dataset.item = item.id;\\n      b.textContent = item.label;\\n      menu.append(b);\\n    }\\n    wrap.append(h, tag, goal, list, secs, how, menu);\\n    ui.append(wrap);\\n1540→  }\\n\\n  function state() {\\n    const sim = model.sim;\\n    const net = !sim ? model.netState : null;\\n    const seats = sim?.seats || net?.seats || [];\\n    const seat = seats.find((s) => !s.out) || seats[0];\\n    const items = currentItems();\\n    const rank = sim?.rank?.id || (typeof net?.rank === 'string' ? net.rank : net?.rank?.id) || null;\\n    return {\\n1550→      screen: model.screen,\\n      op: sim?.op?.id || net?.op || null,\\n      phase: sim?.phase?.id || net?.phase || null,\\n      vitals: sim ? sim.vitals : (net?.vitals ?? null),\\n      timer: sim ? sim.timer : (net?.timer ?? null),\\n      score: sim ? sim.score : (net?.score ?? 0),\\n      rank,\\n      bpm: sim ? sim.beat.bpm : (net?.bpm ?? null),\\n      beat: sim ? sim.beat.count : (net?.beat ?? 0),\\n      site: sim ? sim.activeSite : (net?.site ?? null),\\n1560→      tool: seat?.tool || null,\\n      tips: seats.map((s) => ({ id: s.id, x: s.x, y: s.y, tool: s.tool, score: s.score || 0, use: s.use || 0 })),\\n      focusId: items[model.focus]?.id || null,\\n      promptSet: model.input?.promptSet || document.documentElement.dataset.promptSet || 'keyboard',\\n      glyphSet: model.settings.glyphs || 'playstation',\\n      attract: !!model.attract.on,\\n      devOpen: model.overlay === 'dev',\\n      renderBackend: model.view?.backend || 'none',\\n      musicGain: model.audio?.music?.gain?.value ?? 0.1,\\n      tuning: model.tuning,\\n1570→      reached: [...model.reached],\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const api = {\\n    state,\\n    audio,\\n    devRun(id, arg) { return runDev(model, id, arg); },\\n  };\\n  if (model.test) {\\n1580→    api.test = {\\n      step(n) {\\n        const count = Math.max(0, n | 0);\\n        for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) stepOnce();\\n      },\\n      warp(n) { model.warp = n | 0; },\\n      input(frame) { model.override = frame || null; },\\n      bot(on, opts) {\\n        model.botOn = !!on;\\n        if (opts) model.botOpts = opts;\\n1590→      },\\n      skipTo(op, phase) {\\n        model.flow = model.flow || 'free';\\n        model.opId = op;\\n        freeSim();\\n        model.sim = new Sim({\\n          op, seed: 1, physics: false, tuning: model.tuning,\\n          difficulty: model.settings.difficulty || 'resident', players: 1,\\n        });\\n        if (phase) model.sim.skipTo(phase);\\n1600→        model.resultShown = false;\\n        model.overlay = null;\\n        setScreen('Operation');\\n      },\\n      hash() { return model.sim ? model.sim.hash() : ''; },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  let raf = 0;\\n  let timer = 0;\\n1610→  function draw() {\\n    if (model.mode === 'session' || !model.view || model.norender || model.painting) return;\\n    model.painting = true;\\n    try {\\n      if (model.sim && (model.attract.on || model.screen === 'Operation')) {\\n        model.view.showOr?.();\\n        model.view.sync(decorateState(model.sim.state), 1 / 60);\\n      } else if (model.screen === 'Story') present();\\n    } catch { /* draw again next frame */ }\\n    const drawn = model.view.render?.();\\n1620→    if (drawn?.then) drawn.then(() => { model.painting = false; }, () => { model.painting = false; });\\n    else model.painting = false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function loop() {\\n    raf = requestAnimationFrame(loop);\\n    if (model.mode === 'session') return;\\n    checkAttract();\\n    if (model.test && !(model.warp > 0)) {\\n      /* scripted steps own the sim */\\n1630→    } else {\\n      const n = model.warp > 0 ? model.warp : 1;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) stepOnce();\\n    }\\n    draw();\\n  }\\n\\n  function wantsTouch() {\\n    const mq = window.matchMedia?.('(any-pointer: fine)');\\n    if (!mq) return false;\",\"content_concise\":\"1520→      list.append(seat);\\n    }\\n    const secs = document.createElement('p');\\n    secs.className = 'vitals';\\n    if (model.card?.left != null) secs.textContent = String(Math.max(0, Math.ceil(model.card.left)));\\n    const how = document.createElement('p');\\n    how.className = 'note';\\n    how.textContent = 'Aim with the right stick or the mouse. Use with R2 or click. Tools are the left stick or the number keys.';\\n    const menu = document.createElement('div');\\n    menu.className = 'menu';\\n1530→    for (const item of [{ id: 'ready', label: 'Ready' }, { id: 'more', label: 'More Time' }]) {\\n      const b = document.createElement('button');\\n      b.type = 'button';\\n      b.className = 'item';\\n      b.dataset.item = item.id;\\n      b.textContent = item.label;\\n      menu.append(b);\\n    }\\n    wrap.append(h, tag, goal, list, secs, how, menu);\\n    ui.append(wrap);\\n1540→  }\\n\\n  function state() {\\n    const sim = model.sim;\\n    const net = !sim ? model.netState : null;\\n    const seats = sim?.seats || net?.seats || [];\\n    const seat = seats.find((s) => !s.out) || seats[0];\\n    const items = currentIte