yboard', (await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.dataset.promptSet)) === 'keyboard', 'set');\\n\\n    const box = await page.locator('#view').boundingBox();\\n    await page.mouse.move(box.x + box.width * 0.62, box.y + box.height * 0.4);\\n    await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.test.step(2));\\n    const mouse = await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state().tips[0]);\\n    check('mouse aims', Math.hypot(mouse.x + 1.05, mouse.y - 0.62) > 0.25, JSON.stringify(mouse));\\n\\n    await press(page, 'Escape');\\n    check('pause from operation', (await page.evaluate(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Dev Mode'))), 'pause items');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) await press(page, 'ArrowDown');\\n    await press(page, 'Enter');\\n    check('dev opens from pause', await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state().devOpen), 'dev');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 24 && !(await page.evaluate(() => document.body.innerText.includes('tipSpeed'))); i++) {\\n      await press(page, 'KeyE');\\n    }\\n    const beforeSpeed = await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state().tuning.tipSpeed);\\n    await press(page, 'ArrowRight');\\n    const afterSpeed = await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state().tuning.tipSpeed);\\n    check('slider changes tuning', afterSpeed > beforeSpeed + 0.05, `${beforeSpeed} -> ${afterSpeed}`);\\n    await press(page, 'Escape');\\n    await press(page, 'Escape');\\n    await page.evaluate(() => { window.__game.state().tuning.aimAssist = 0; });\\n    const sped = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n      window.__pads[0].axes[2] = -1;\\n      window.__pads[0].axes[3] = 0;\\n      window.__game.test.step(90);\\n      const x0 = window.__game.state().tips[0].x;\\n      window.__pads[0].axes[2] = 1;\\n      window.__game.test.step(60);\\n      window.__pads[0].axes[2] = 0;\\n      const st = window.__game.state();\\n      const dx = st.tips[0].x - x0;\\n      return { dx, speed: st.tuning.tipSpeed, x0, x1: st.tips[0].x };\\n    });\\n    check('slider changes the sim', Math.abs(sped.dx - sped.speed) <= Math.abs(sped.speed) * 0.05, JSON.stringify(sped));\\n    await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.devRun('reset-all'));\\n    const restored = await page.evaluate((defaults) => {\\n      const live = window.__game.state().tuning;\\n      return Object.keys(defaults).every((key) => live[key] === defaults[key]);\\n    }, TUNING_DEFAULTS);\\n    check('reset restores defaults', restored, 'tuning');\\n\\n    const toolErrors = await page.evaluate(async (ids) => {\\n      const bad = [];\\n      for (const id of ids) {\\n        try {\\n          window.__game.devRun('op:broken-glass');\\n          window.__game.devRun(id);\\n        } catch (err) {\\n          bad.push(`${id}: ${err.message}`);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      return bad;\\n    }, DEV_IDS);\\n    check('dev tools run', toolErrors.length === 0, toolErrors.join('; '));\\n\\n    await press(page, 'Escape');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) await press(page, 'ArrowDown');\\n    await press(page, 'Enter');\\n    check('quit reaches menu', (await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state().screen)) === 'Main Menu', 'screen');\\n\\n    await page.hover('[data-item=\\\"free\\\"]');\\n    check('hover moves focus', (await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state().focusId)) === 'free', 'focus');\\n    await page.click('[data-item=\\\"free\\\"]');\\n    check('click opens free play', (await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state().screen)) === 'Free Play', 'screen');\\n    await press(page, 'Escape');\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":461}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"a19eef63-fb6b-4e6e-aea4-eaa283d9465f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_700","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The failure shows x remained at 0.\n\nThe tip stayed at 524 after Escape Escape. The overlay may still be blocking, or the keyboard seat may overwrite pad input for mouse devices. I am re-examining poll() and readPad() to find why the pad axes are ignored.\n\nThe pad seat is assigned before the keyboard seat, so the pad input should take precedence. Because dx remains zero, feedSim is likely paused or the stick axes are not registering.\n\nThe first Escape unpauses the game. The second Escape pauses it again. If the game started paused, it ends paused. That explains why pad steps produce no movement.\n\nSmoke tests without the prelude pass, but confirm still fails to open dev. The prelude sequence is now being isolated. A mouse move sets the device to mouse before Escape opens pause, yet ArrowDown should still register. The canvas focus or a hover effect under the cursor may be blocking input. The KeyA press before the mouse is also being examined.\n\nKeyA during play is ignored by onKey, so it does not set pending. The mouse move and Escape sequence works correctly. The focus failure after ArrowDown is now the main puzzle. I will add logging to reproduce the exact prelude and inspect focusId and devOpen state.\n\nI will log focusId, the focused button text, and the active element after each press. I will also check whether ArrowDown is in the pressed keys. The pending state clears every step, so I need to verify if onKey actually ran.\n\nI will inject a capture-phase keydown listener into the page to log every keystroke before the game processes it. This avoids relying on the unexposed `onKey` function and will reveal exactly which keys are intercepted.\n\nI will write a reproduction that skips the attract sequence to save time. If it passes, I will add attract and reload. I am also considering whether Playwright repeats ArrowDown or if the page's preventDefault fails to stop the focused button from changing.\n\nI am checking whether native Enter behavior conflicts with model focus. The game's Enter handler activates model focus via pending, not DOM focus. Native Enter does not fire click or pointerup events, so it cannot interfere with the pending confirm.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6d9afaee-acb1-485d-84bf-49acf3c66d30-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Dev Mode|dev mode|Dev","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1411,"output_tokens":1421,"cache_read_input_tokens":110208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"eb87feaf-3c55-4031-a408-3253113f6076"}
