{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_704","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The reproduction passes with the same prelude.\n\nThe reproduction skipped the attract exit path. The suite fails because it presses Escape directly without calling test.step, and waits for attract to become false.\n\nThe Escape key handler exits attract immediately and sets a 350ms ignore window. The reproduction passed the remaining tests, so the failure likely stems from the reload path. After reload, attract starts after 10 seconds and the interval steps the simulation four times every 250ms.\n\nPending state is cleared after attract exit in both the key handler and exitAttract. The reproduction passed skipTo without attract, so that step is not the culprit. A race with the attract interval is unlikely because the check `if (model.attract.on && model.test)` would prevent stepping once attract is off.\n\nskipTo sets the Operation screen, which is not an idle state that would restart attract. The reproduction passes while the suite fails, so the cause of the difference remains unclear.\n\nThe suite failed at 179 seconds, including a 120-second hover timeout. Earlier checks passed, and the pause text check also passed. The failure occurred at the dev opens step. The reproduction matched that exact tail, so the issue must stem from something that happens before skipTo in the full suite.\n\nThe reproduction omitted the localStorage clear and reload that the suite performs. A stale save might alter the title flow, though this seems unlikely to affect pause confirmation. The full scripted start through the dev check should be included in the reproduction.\n\nThe reproduction likely inherited stale localStorage from the previous failed suite run, while the suite clears storage before starting. Settings like swapSticks, glyphs, or tipSpeed could interfere with keyboard menu navigation.\n\nSettings were ruled out as the cause of the failure. The reproduction will now include the attract sequence, localStorage clear, and reload to match the suite exactly. A potential race condition between the attract interval and exitAttract is also being examined.\n\nThe attract interval and key handler were ruled out as causes. The focus is now shifting to the suite's `keyboard.down('KeyD')` call.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4ebe41ff-9758-42af-b611-e0f01cd0285f-56","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"test","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/main.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4ebe41ff-9758-42af-b611-e0f01cd0285f-57","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"model.test|params.test|searchParams","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":600,"output_tokens":2683,"cache_read_input_tokens":116480,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"c6e7390a-3034-4220-bcc0-890d6b57a0f5"}
