{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-29f53167-83f9-4ec5-ac32-c2fd548f4e34-58","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,47,65,108,105,118,101,32,105,110,32,67,111,109,109,111,110,32,84,105,109,101,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,32,67,101,110,116,101,114,58,32,83,101,99,111,110,100,32,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,47,115,114,99,47,97,112,112,47,100,105,114,101,99,116,111,114,46,106,115,10,49,48,51,58,32,32,32,32,116,101,115,116,58,32,112,97,114,97,109,115,46,103,101,116,40,39,116,101,115,116,39,41,32,61,61,61,32,39,49,39,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":103,\"content\":\"    test: params.get('test') === '1',\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"5272879d-4872-4ecb-8a0f-8a01cd8fb37a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_706","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test is set. I am examining createApp and whether keyboard events on the suite page follow a different code path when the canvas has focus after mouse movement and the attract interval is active.\n\nThe reproduction without the attract path succeeded, so the attract interval is the key difference. I will add it to the smoke test and rerun. I will also check for a potential bug during attract exit.\n\nEscape opens the pause menu correctly. ArrowDown and Enter fail to move focus or confirm. The overlay closes on Enter, so KeyE cannot find tipSpeed.\n\nTwo Escape presses close the pause menu and should unpause the game. The pad still did not move, so the input likely failed to apply or the game paused again immediately. When Enter activates resume, focus remains stuck at resume, preventing ArrowDown from moving it. During operation, ArrowRight sets pending.right because the overlay is null.\n\nArrowRight cannot move the tip because onKey returns early when the overlay is null. The tip speed stays at 1.9. The pad should move after two Escape presses unpause the game, but dx was zero. This means the game remained paused when the pad was measured.\n\nThe second Escape press reopens the pause menu. The pad stays paused and dx remains zero. ArrowDown and Enter are ignored while the overlay is open. Escape still works because it uses the same press() helper.\n\nThe pause menu may have opened from a visibilitychange event rather than the Escape key press. If so, ArrowDown and Enter would be ignored while the overlay is open. The Escape press still succeeded because it closed the overlay. The check passed afterward because Dev Mode text was visible.\n\nArrowDown and Escape share the same input listener, so neither should be swallowed before onKey. The event key and code match correctly. The failure likely lies elsewhere in the pause menu focus logic.\n\nThe reproduction confirmed ArrowDown works after a mouse move. The suite-specific factors—such as the attract interval, reload, storage, and time—appear to be the actual cause of the failure. A stuck key or competing keydown listeners are unlikely because the overlay remains set and the listener uses standard window bubbling.\n\nThe browser is not intercepting ArrowDown to move focus between buttons. The suite's page may be failing to receive the key due to a Playwright timeout or overlay issue. The scripted function cannot be run in isolation because it is not exported.\n\nLocalStorage was ruled out because the suite clears it at startup. The attract interval is also inactive during the operation phase, so it cannot interrupt the arrow presses.\n\nA pointer event from the keyboard press is unlikely. Hovering over a pause menu button does not fire onHover without a pointermove, so focus stays on resume and ArrowDown should still move it. The reproduction with the mouse in the same position succeeded, confirming the attract interval is the actual cause of the failure.\n\nThe attract wait loop and Escape exit are not the cause. The keyboard aim test passed, so key presses work for aiming. Arrow keys fail only in the menu path because onKey returns early while the game is in play.\n\nThe same keydown listener handles both marking the key and the onKey callback, so ArrowDown should fire if the event reaches the window. The reproduction confirms this path works. I ruled out a different HTML file, a service worker, or a race condition where the suite loaded before the build finished.\n\nI will print the tip x coordinate in the reproduction to verify page geometry matches. I will keep the attract interval at its full 10-second duration. The browser configuration is identical between the suite and the smoke test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce7c4b05-c40c-4758-b2c0-149c325f9e1c-59","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/pause-smoke.mjs","old_string":"await page.goto(url.href, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });\nawait page.waitForFunction(() => window.__game?.state?.().screen === 'Title');","new_string":"await page.goto(url.href, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });\nawait page.waitForFunction(() => window.__game && window.__game.state);\nawait page.evaluate(() => localStorage.clear());\nawait page.reload({ waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });\nawait page.waitForFunction(() => window.__game?.state?.().screen === 'Title');\nconst t0 = Date.now();\nawait page.waitForFunction(() => window.__game.state().attract === true, null, { timeout: 13000 });\nconsole.log('attract', Date.now() - t0);\nawait page.waitForTimeout(2000);\nawait page.keyboard.press('Escape');\nawait page.waitForFunction(() => window.__game.state().attract === false, null, { timeout: 3000 });"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":336,"output_tokens":2250,"cache_read_input_tokens":119936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"7d7137a4-9373-4820-b6a8-ad15d3a49a51"}
