re the warning was created)\\nattract 9995\\n{\\\"label\\\":\\\"after mouse\\\",\\\"screen\\\":\\\"Operation\\\",\\\"focus\\\":null,\\\"dev\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"gel\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Disinfect the wound |  | 100 |  | 72 |  | 4:00 |  | 0 |  | scalpel | forceps | suction | gel | suture | laser | scanner | clamp |  | BEA |  | Gel first, child. Everything in a taxi is filthy, and so are you. |  | gel |  |  gift  s\\\"}\\n{\\\"label\\\":\\\"after escape\\\",\\\"screen\\\":\\\"Operation\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"resume\\\",\\\"dev\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"gel\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Paused | Resume | Retry Phase | Restart Operation | Settings | Dev Mode | Quit to Menu\\\"}\\n{\\\"label\\\":\\\"down 0\\\",\\\"screen\\\":\\\"Operation\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"retry\\\",\\\"dev\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"gel\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Paused | Resume | Retry Phase | Restart Operation | Settings | Dev Mode | Quit to Menu\\\"}\\n{\\\"label\\\":\\\"down 1\\\",\\\"screen\\\":\\\"Operation\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"restart\\\",\\\"dev\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"gel\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Paused | Resume | Retry Phase | Restart Operation | Settings | Dev Mode | Quit to Menu\\\"}\\n{\\\"label\\\":\\\"down 2\\\",\\\"screen\\\":\\\"Operation\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"settings\\\",\\\"dev\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"gel\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Paused | Resume | Retry Phase | Restart Operation | Settings | Dev Mode | Quit to Menu\\\"}\\n{\\\"label\\\":\\\"down 3\\\",\\\"screen\\\":\\\"Operation\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"dev\\\",\\\"dev\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"gel\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Paused | Resume | Retry Phase | Restart Operation | Settings | Dev Mode | Quit to Menu\\\"}\\n{\\\"label\\\":\\\"after enter\\\",\\\"screen\\\":\\\"Operation\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"dev\\\",\\\"dev\\\":false,\\\"tool\\\":\\\"gel\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Paused | Resume | Retry Phase | Restart Operation | Settings | Dev Mode | Quit to Menu\\\"}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/pause-smoke.mjs\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Reproduce pause path after attract mode\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/terminal/call-88975d79-0819-4765-9575-b1fac78f13ec-60.log\",\"total_bytes\":1586}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"4a3751b8-8124-4603-9aa9-345dce895cfb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_708","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Focus moves correctly to \"dev\" after attract. Enter does not open it.\n\nThe confirm key is being swallowed by an `ignoreUntil` timer. It was set during attract and may be refreshing on pointer events, blocking Enter from opening dev.\n\nThe 350ms ignoreUntil should have expired long ago, so it is not blocking Enter. The real cause must be elsewhere in the input check.\n\nThe ignoreUntil timer is still active. It blocks Enter but not arrow keys, which explains why focus moves yet confirm fails. The earlier Escape that opened pause must have worked because it triggered a pending pause state rather than a blocked confirm.\n\nThe ignoreUntil timer is still active when Enter is pressed, even though attract exited long ago. It may be getting refreshed by pointer events or set to a much larger value than expected.\n\nThe 350ms ignoreUntil timer likely has not expired yet. The test sequence after attract exit takes only milliseconds to seconds, so the timer is still active when Enter is pressed.\n\nThe test sequence might finish under 350ms. The suite still fails. This suggests the ignoreUntil timer is being refreshed after attract exits. Mouse moves call onPointer. That function updates lastInput and may reset the timer.\n\nThe onPointer function does not refresh ignoreUntil because attract is already off. The entire script after attract exit likely finishes in under 350 milliseconds, so the timer has not expired when Enter is pressed.\n\nThe fix is to make ignoreUntil only swallow the input that exited attract, not a later confirm keypress.\n\nThe 350ms ignoreUntil is a blanket safeguard. It prevents the key that exits attract from also activating the menu. The suite failure is a deterministic test flake on fast machines, where logical steps finish in under 350ms of wall-clock time.\n\nThe 350ms window is meant to suppress the exiting key's own keyup or held confirm, and possibly a still-pressed pad button. It should not swallow a later Enter.\n\nTwo fixes are under consideration. One makes ignoreUntil track the exact key or pad button that exited attract, so later deliberate presses are not swallowed. The other simply adds a 400ms wait after attract in the test.\n\nThe 350ms lockout is intentional game behavior. The real bug is that the lockout is time-based rather than bound to the specific exiting control. A player who taps to exit and then immediately confirms should not have to wait. The correct fix is to make ignoreUntil last only until that exiting key or pad button is released.\n\nThe exiting key never sets pending.confirm, so it cannot navigate even without ignoreUntil. The ignoreUntil timer is therefore unnecessary for the keyboard.press exit path. It only matters if a step runs while that key is still held.\n\nThe ignoreUntil window is necessary to prevent a held exit key from triggering the title menu. If removed, the next step would see the key still down and confirm the title button. The suite releases the key before the next step, so it would not double-fire.\n\nA concrete implementation is being drafted. The `onKey` handler will set `ignoreSticky = true` when attract exits, and a new keydown after all controls are released will clear the lockout.\n\nA `swallowHeld` flag in `stepOnce` is being considered. It would suppress menu activation only while the exit key or pad button is still held, then clear automatically once all controls are released. This avoids the blanket 350ms timer and handles pad exits cleanly.\n\nA `blockMenu` flag is being drafted to replace the blanket 350ms timer. It would be set when attract exits and cleared only after a step sees no held confirm or back button. This would suppress menu activation solely for the exiting keypress rather than swallowing all later inputs.\n\nThe `blockMenu` flag is being implemented in `stepOnce`. It suppresses menu activation while the exit key or pad button is still held, then clears automatically once all controls are released. This prevents the exiting input from double-firing the title menu, and a later Enter press works normally because the lockout is already gone.\n\nA flaw in the `blockMenu` approach was found. If a new key is pressed immediately after the exit key is released, `stepOnce` copies `pending.confirm` to the menu state and clears pending at the start of the step. The subsequent `blockMenu` check then sees that pending confirm and returns early, swallowing the new input before it can activate.\n\nThe `blockMenu` approach is being abandoned because it would swallow a new keypress that arrives immediately after the exit key is released. The revised plan is to snapshot the currently held menu keys when attract exits, then block only those specific edges until they are released. A later keypress will then set pending normally and activate correctly.\n\nThe `blockMenu` logic is being refined. It would suppress menu activation only while the exiting key or pad button is still held, then clear automatically and let unrelated pending inputs through. The test sequence confirms this works: the exit key releases before any step, so a later Enter press sets pending normally.\n\nThe `press()` helper releases the key before `stepOnce` runs, so `held.confirm` is false when the step executes. The `blockMenu` flag therefore clears automatically and lets a later Enter press activate normally.\n\nThe keyboard aim test confirms the fix works. The held key is not a menu button, so blockMenu clears and the step processes aim normally. A later pause Enter still activates even within 350ms.\n\nFor pad exits, the same logic holds. If Cross is held to exit attract, blockMenu suppresses menu activation while that button remains pressed, then clears automatically once the pad input releases.\n\nA mouse click that exits attract is handled by the existing `ignoreUntil` logic. `onPointer` triggers the exit, and `onActivate` sees the timer still active and swallows the click that caused it.\n\nThe blanket 350ms lockout is being removed entirely. For mouse exits, `blockMenu` will be set on `pointerdown`, swallowed by the next `onActivate`, then cleared so later clicks still work. For keyboard exits, the flag will clear automatically on the first step where no confirm or back key is held, since the exit key never sets pending.\n\nThe implementation plan is now concrete. `blockMenu` will replace the blanket `ignoreUntil` timer for all exit paths: keyboard, pointer, and hover. When attract exits, the flag is set and `onActivate` swallows the activating click while clearing it. The existing `stepOnce` attract branch already returns early, so it needs no changes.\n\nThe `blockMenu` guard must not check `menu.confirm` or `menu.back`. If it did, a new keypress that arrives immediately after the exit key is released would still register as a rising edge, be copied to pending, and then swallowed by the hold check. The test suite already releases the exit key before the next step, so `held.confirm` is false when that step runs.\n\nThe test suite confirms the keyboard exit path works correctly. The exit key releases before the next step, so blockMenu clears automatically and a later Enter press activates the menu normally.\n\nA quick second press after exiting attract will also navigate correctly. This is an improvement over the old 350ms window, since the lockout now lasts only until the specific exiting key or pad button is released.\n\nThe blockMenu flag is safe during attract steps. The loop continues for the remaining iterations while the exit button may still be held, but each step sees the flag and returns early.\n\nEscape during operation is treated as pending.pause rather than confirm. Because blockMenu only checks held confirm or back buttons, it clears automatically when Escape is released and does not swallow the pause open.\n\nA pad Cross tap that releases before the next step is safe. The exit fires in the step that sees the edge, blockMenu is set and cleared, and no stray confirm follows.\n\nThe old `ignoreUntil` guard in `stepOnce` will be removed entirely. The new `blockMenu` check will run before menu actions but after the attract exit check.\n\nThe `blockMenu` guard is being placed in `stepOnce` immediately after the attract exit check. It suppresses menu activation only while a confirm, back, or pad button remains held, then clears automatically on the next step. Hover exits are safe because they do not hold any confirm key and do not activate a menu item.\n\nThe `takeClick` helper discards the pointer click without activating anything, so swallowing it in `onActivate` is safe. The existing `ignoreUntil` check in `onActivate` will be replaced by the new `blockMenu` flag.\n\nThe old `ignoreUntil` guard in `onActivate` will be replaced by the new `blockMenu` flag. A mouse click that exits attract during the old 350ms window will still be swallowed once, then the lockout clears. For a keyboard exit, the flag persists until the next step where no confirm or back key is held, so a later Enter press activates normally. The `onKey` handler may also be checked for any remaining `ignoreUntil` logic.\n\nThe pad back button (Circle) is a potential edge input, not a held button. The current `blockMenu` check only looks at held confirm and back keys, so it would miss a pad back press and fail to suppress menu activation during attract exit. The logic needs to account for pad edges as well.\n\nPad back buttons are rising edges, not held keys. The attract branch returns before menu handling, so the same step cannot activate from a pad edge. The next step sees no edge and proceeds normally. blockMenu is therefore only needed for keyboard held keys that would otherwise register as rising edges on the following step.\n\nThe keyboard held key test confirms the fix. `poll()` runs at the start of `stepOnce`, so `menuLatch` updates before the `blockMenu` check. A later step sees no rising edge and does not activate.\n\nThe `blockMenu` check will be inserted in `stepOnce` immediately after the `poll()` call and after any attract exit handling. The hover exit path will also set `blockMenu` instead of using `ignoreUntil`. The old `ignoreUntil` timer field can be removed entirely, since it will no longer be used.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2cb9dd75-942d-444d-8333-e622d62484ff-61","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":100,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2cb9dd75-942d-444d-8333-e622d62484ff-62","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":148,"limit":95}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2cb9dd75-942d-444d-8333-e622d62484ff-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":1178,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":693,"output_tokens":6045,"cache_read_input_tokens":122496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"8dea4f9e-367f-4a91-99ec-5bd82234ef8c"}
