{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_713","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A potential bug was spotted: `onActivate` clears `blockMenu` and returns.\n\nThe `blockMenu` bug is harmless in practice because the suite never clicks. A related issue was spotted: clicking to exit attract mode sets `blockMenu` via `onPointer`, which may conflict with `stepOnce`'s block check and `onActivate`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4356a04c-1554-47fb-900e-07a58fc2ed84-74","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":1188,"limit":22}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":606,"output_tokens":317,"cache_read_input_tokens":134272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d5556c7a-7909-4379-98da-34e17c397c0f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4356a04c-1554-47fb-900e-07a58fc2ed84-74","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1188→      model.pending = {};\\n      const menu = { ...sample.menu };\\n1190→      for (const k of Object.keys(pend)) if (pend[k]) menu[k] = true;\\n      model.input.takeClick();\\n      if (realInput(sample, menu, pend)) model.lastInput = performance.now();\\n      if (model.attract.on && (realInput(sample, menu, pend) || sample.hover)) {\\n        model.blockMenu = true;\\n        exitAttract();\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (model.blockMenu) {\\n        const held = sample.held || {};\\n1200→        const padHeld = sample.seats.some((s) => (s.frame?.use || 0) > 0.2);\\n        if (held.confirm || held.back || padHeld) return;\\n        model.blockMenu = false;\\n      }\\n      if (model.screen === 'Touch notice' && (pend.leaveTouch || sample.seenPad || model.input.seenPad)) {\\n        if (pend.leaveTouch || sample.seats.some((s) => s.edges && Object.values(s.edges).some(Boolean))) {\\n          setScreen('Title');\\n          return;\\n        }\\n      }\",\"content_concise\":\"1188→      model.pending = {};\\n      const menu = { ...sample.menu };\\n1190→      for (const k of Object.keys(pend)) if (pend[k]) menu[k] = true;\\n      model.input.takeClick();\\n      if (realInput(sample, menu, pend)) model.lastInput = performance.now();\\n      if (model.attract.on && (realInput(sample, menu, pend) || sample.hover)) {\\n        model.blockMenu = true;\\n        exitAttract();\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (model.blockMenu) {\\n        const held = sample.held || {};\\n1200→        const padHeld = sample.seats.some((s) => (s.frame?.use || 0) > 0.2);\\n        if (held.confirm || held.back || padHeld) return;\\n        model.blockMenu = false;\\n      }\\n      if (model.screen === 'Touch notice' && (pend.leaveTouch || sample.seenPad || model.input.seenPad)) {\\n        if (pend.leaveTouch || sample.seats.some((s) => s.edges && Object.values(s.edges).some(Boolean))) {\\n          setScreen('Title');\\n          return;\\n        }\\n      }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js\",\"offset\":1188,\"limit\":22,\"raw_output\":\"      model.pending = {};\\n      const menu = { ...sample.menu };\\n      for (const k of Object.keys(pend)) if (pend[k]) menu[k] = true;\\n      model.input.takeClick();\\n      if (realInput(sample, menu, pend)) model.lastInput = performance.now();\\n      if (model.attract.on && (realInput(sample, menu, pend) || sample.hover)) {\\n        model.blockMenu = true;\\n        exitAttract();\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (model.blockMenu) {\\n        const held = sample.held || {};\\n        const padHeld = sample.seats.some((s) => (s.frame?.use || 0) > 0.2);\\n        if (held.confirm || held.back || padHeld) return;\\n        model.blockMenu = false;\\n      }\\n      if (model.screen === 'Touch notice' && (pend.leaveTouch || sample.seenPad || model.input.seenPad)) {\\n        if (pend.leaveTouch || sample.seats.some((s) => s.edges && Object.values(s.edges).some(Boolean))) {\\n          setScreen('Title');\\n          return;\\n        }\\n      }\\n\",\"total_lines\":1704}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d0b853a6-cb40-471e-ab01-6c280492be4b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_714","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found: when blockMenu is active but the exiting key is not held, the menu clears and falls through to process pend and menu for the current step.\n\nThe first step after attract is keyboard aim, not Enter. The attract exit Escape sets blockMenu without setting pending, so the next step is aim. The first stepOnce clears blockMenu because KeyD is not a confirm or back key. Later Enter on pause should work and pass.\n\nConfirmed that the attract exit key cannot leave a stale confirm pending, since its onKey clears pending and returns before setting confirm. Rebuilding and running smoke tests now. Also reviewing the touch test for pad button exits.\n\nThe touch test holds Cross during the 250ms attract exit interval. The button is released before the first step and re-pressed after it.\n\nThe touch test's release step clears blockMenu because padHeld is false. The screen becomes Touch notice, but seenPad remains true from the prior hold. The leaveTouch pending flag is unset, so the step falls through to the seat edge check. The button release produces no rising edge, leaving edges empty.\n\nThe touch test works correctly. The release step keeps the player in Touch notice because no edge fires on release. The second step produces a rising confirm edge and transitions to Title. During the 250ms interval while the button is held, the first step exits attract and returns; the following three steps keep blockMenu active and padHeld true, so the player does not leave Touch notice.\n\nEscape exits attract without opening the main menu. Its onKey returns before setting pending.confirm, and Escape is not a confirm key. Title screen confirm uses any key.\n\nA human tap on Enter that releases before the next step clears blockMenu and leaves no pending input. The player stays on Title until a second press registers.","signature":""