{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_736","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The about change is in the HTML.\n\nThe browser suite should be re-run to match the shipped page. The package check script can run in parallel since it doesn't launch a browser. The launch script will also be prepared. Next, I need to determine what package.log should contain.\n\nPackage.log will record the exit-interview.json parse, root HTML and dev-folder names, client hash, and a single hub banner string. It must also verify that own source lacks banned names, Math.random in the sim, and TODO or FIXME placeholders. Banned names include Derek Stiles, Angie Thompson, Naomi Kimishima, Caduceus, Delphi, GUILT, Healing Touch, Hope Hospital, and Kyriaki.\n\nA Node script in scratch will generate the pass/fail package.log. It will run while the browser suite executes. The title must also be absent from other source files; the browser suite already checks this, and package.log should record it. The launch script will be sequential, running after the browser suite, with five GPU flags and a file:// root HTML using ?test=1 for stepping but no norender.\n\nThe launch script will wait for the game and Title screen to appear. A screenshot will be taken after moving into an operation and shifting the tip so the HUD and field are visible. Canvas dimensions will be compared against client size, and painted pixels counted from the PNG. Python or ImageMagick may decode the compressed image. The browser suite will start now while the package script is written.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c8e99b08-5cdf-4197-b2ef-9f0a99cf3e77-109","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230\" && node tests/run-all.mjs browser > \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/browser.log\" 2>&1; echo EXIT:$? >> \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/browser.log\"","description":"Re-run browser suite on the rebuilt page","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c8e99b08-5cdf-4197-b2ef-9f0a99cf3e77-110","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/package-check.mjs","content":"import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\n\nconst work = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work';\nconst devName = readdirSync(work).find((name) => name.endsWith('-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230') && statSync(path.join(work, name)).isDirectory());\nconst htmlName = readdirSync(work).find((name) => name.endsWith('-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230.html'));\nconst dev = path.join(work, devName);\nconst htmlPath = path.join(work, htmlName);\nconst lines = [];\nconst fail = (msg) => lines.push('FAIL ' + msg);\nconst ok = (msg) => lines.push('OK ' + msg);\n\nconst interview = JSON.parse(readFileSync(path.join(work, 'exit-interview.json'), 'utf8'));\nconst keys = ['sourceInformation', 'testingFeedback', 'engineFeedback', 'promptFeedback', 'aiHub'];\nfor (const key of keys) if (!(key in interview)) fail('exit interview missing ' + key);\nif (interview.sourceInformation.usage !== 'added on import') fail('usage');\nelse ok('usage added on import');\nconst hub = interview.aiHub;\nif (hub.type !== 'Game') fail('type');\nif (hub.genre !== 'Simulation') fail('genre');\nif (hub.source !== 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion') fail('source');\nif (hub.series !== 'Trauma Center') fail('series');\nif (hub.players !== '1–4') fail('players ' + hub.players);\nif (hub.controls !== 'Right stick or mouse to aim, left stick or 1-8 for tools, R2 or left click to use') fail('controls');\nconst tags = ['3d', 'co-op', 'story', 'sci-fi', 'boss fights'];\nif (JSON.stringify(hub.tags) !== JSON.stringify(tags)) fail('tags');\nelse ok('aiHub catalogue fields');\nif (!hub.name || !hub.tagline || !hub.description) fail('name tagline description');\nif (hub.description.includes(hub.name)) fail('description contains the title');\nelse ok('description omits the title');\n\nif (!devName || !htmlName) fail('names missing');\nelse if (devName + '.html' !== htmlName) fail('html name does not match the dev folder');\nelse ok('names ' + htmlName);\n\nconst html = readFileSync(htmlPath, 'utf8');\nconst start = html.indexOf('/*! aihub-session ');\nconst endMark = '})(typeof window !== \\'undefined\\' ? window : globalThis);';\nconst end = html.indexOf(endMark);\nconst slice = html.slice(start, end + endMark.length).replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n');\nconst hash = createHash('sha256').update(slice).digest('hex');\nconst HASH = '529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a';\nif (hash !== HASH) fail('client hash ' + hash);\nelse ok('client hash');\nif (html.split('/*! aihub-session ').length !== 2) fail('banner count');\nelse ok('banner once');\nif (/<script[^>]+src=/i.test(html)) fail('external script');\nelse ok('no external script');\n\nconst bannedWords = ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub'];\nconst bannedNames = ['Derek Stiles', 'Angie Thompson', 'Naomi Kimishima', 'Caduceus', 'Delphi', 'GUILT', 'Healing Touch', 'Hope Hospital', 'Kyriaki', 'Deftera', 'Triti', 'Tetarti', 'Pempti', 'Paraskevi', 'Savato'];\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === 'dist') continue;\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\n    else if (/\\.(js|mjs|json|css|md)$/.test(name)) out.push(p);\n  }\n  return out;\n}\nconst title = hub.name;\nfor (const file of walk(path.join(dev, 'src'))) {\n  const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n  const rel = path.relative(dev, file);\n  if (rel !== 'src/config/identity.js' && text.includes(title)) fail('title in ' + rel);\n  for (const word of bannedWords) if (text.includes(word)) fail(rel + ' ' + word);\n  for (const word of bannedNames) if (text.includes(word)) fail(rel + ' has ' + word);\n  if (rel.startsWith('src/sim') && text.includes('Math.random')) fail('Math.random in ' + rel);\n}\nok('source walk finished');\nconst fails = lines.filter((line) => line.startsWith('FAIL')).length;\nlines.push(fails + ' failed');\nconsole.log(lines.join('\\n'));\nprocess.exit(fails ? 1 : 0);\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":254,"output_tokens":2100,"cache_read_input_tokens":169984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"90240f79-d889-426b-9b9d-17113ec82a12"}
