{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_739","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PIL is unavailable. I will decode PNGs with a minimal implementation or ffmpeg.\n\nPlaywright screenshots and WebGL readPixels are possible but unreliable. A minimal non-interlaced PNG decoder using Node zlib is the most reliable fallback.\n\nffmpeg signalstats and rawvideo extraction are viable alternatives to a custom PNG decoder. I will write the launch script now. It will launch Chromium with five flags at 1280x720, initialize stub pads, navigate to the test URL, wait for the Title screen, and record errors.\n\nThe script will skip to the broken-glass screen and wait for two animation frames. It will read canvas dimensions, move the tip via pad or keyboard, capture a screenshot, and measure painted pixels with ffmpeg rawvideo. A pixel is considered painted if it differs from the corner color beyond a threshold or has high channel variance.\n\nThe painted-pixel threshold is 18 in any channel from the median corner color. A fraction below 0.05 fails the script. Both runs must agree on canvas size, empty errors, high painted fraction, and tip movement. The two runs will execute sequentially in one script.\n\nI will save the two screenshots as launch-1.png and launch-2.png, with both reports in launch.log. Tip movement will use the game's test.input API to override stick input for sixty frames, then read the tip's new x position.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-93903f07-c938-42fa-aef5-acbeebfb6027-113","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":1636,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":280,"output_tokens":1028,"cache_read_input_tokens":173056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}