{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_750","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The SVG glyphs have a \"glyph\" class, but the corresponding CSS is missing.\n\nUnstyled SVGs default to 300×150 pixels, which explains the oversized buttons. I will add CSS to set `.glyph` to 2.4rem with `inline-block` display, and update `.hud-bot .note` to keep the prompt on one line.\n\nThe prompt mixes SVG and text inline. The glyph CSS will align them with the words. I will re-launch to fix the saved screenshots. Then I will rerun the full browser suite because the HTML changed.\n\nThe glyph class is only used in fillPrompt. The prompt will wrap as a single line of small keycaps and words, sitting at the top of the bottom row.\n\nI will set `.hud-bot` to `align-items: flex-end` so the prompt sits at the bottom edge of the wheel. The glyph size is being tightened to 2.2rem with a slight vertical offset. I also need to prevent the note from shrinking and wrapping.\n\nThe prompt may wrap within its flex item. At 2rem font, three glyphs plus words could reach about 40rem wide and exceed the right column. Three short lines should still fit next to the wheel.\n\nThe prompt will be capped at 22rem with right alignment and a tight line height. This keeps the long word \"stabilizer\" from forcing the row to overflow.\n\nThe bottom row is tall enough to fit three lines of 2rem text. The dark rectangle at the bottom center is likely the operating table or drape edge, not a bug.\n\nA 1280×720 screenshot will verify the prompt layout before the browser suite and launches run. PROGRESS will be updated and goal checkboxes flipped once the new launches finish. The temporary helper scripts will be deleted after the logs and images are preserved. The black bar might be an oversized tray mesh, but the view code will not be inspected right now.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-47fe2831-c410-4e1a-bfce-b49303af9b4b-128","name":