{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_783","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The title UI is replaced when the attract sequence starts.\n\nWebGPU boot may exceed the 10-second idle timeout. If attract starts before the page is ready, I'll exit attract to return to the title and capture a screenshot within the remaining window.\n\nThe script waits for WebGPU initialization, checks the attract flag, presses Escape to exit attract, advances the test state, and captures the title screenshot.\n\nEach operation will skip to a target and wait for the next frame. A 2500ms pause between shots should cover rendering time. The browser will close after all screenshots are taken, with errors logged. A portrait close-up can be captured by clipping the bottom center of the page.\n\nFull-page screenshots will be taken as required. If portrait details are hard to see, the image will be inspected with read_file.\n\nThe CSS review shows a font-size failure. The .where class has no rule and inherits 16px at 1080p, which is below the 34px requirement. The .who element is correctly styled at 35px.\n\nThe .where class needs a 2.2rem font-size rule to meet the 34px requirement. The .shout dialogue is already correctly sized at 44px. Timer and score numbers are currently 38.4px, below the 56px target; they will be enlarged to 3.5rem and checked against the objective row for overlap.\n\nThe plan is to capture all screenshots first, then fix obvious type and layout issues. Any CSS changes will require rebuilding the HTML and rerunning the full browser suite. The suite is lengthy: 80 tests across WebGPU, WebKit, and playthrough. Evidence must match the shipped code.\n\nThe verifier audits committed tests and saved evidence, so old browser logs become invalid if the game code changes. Re-running the full suite is the honest path. I am considering whether CSS-only fixes can be verified with a smaller targeted subset.\n\nThe plan specifies `node tests/run-all.mjs browser` as the full command, so any UI change requires running the entire suite. I will grep the director paint code against the CSS to catch missing class definitions like `.where`. The source info pages should avoid dense walls and use short answers per page.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef598268-afb1-4041-87ee-7d23ff6788db-63","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ABOUT_HEADS|function aboutItems|function turnPage","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef598268-afb1-4041-87ee-7d23ff6788db-64","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"class=\\\"[a-z-]+\\\"","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3465,"output_tokens":1557,"cache_read_input_tokens":106752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e426a509-9adf-40b3-9cd9-c30d2c2b5ea6"}
