{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_786","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"setSpeaker is only called for story lines, not operation barks.\n\nThe HUD portrait and story shout both use the same bust render texture, so a face UV error would break both. present() is called from draw during Story screens. I will write the script now, measure overflow, and use WebGL for the session card script to keep it lightweight.\n\nThe built game.html is the harness target. file:// will be used for root HTML with WebGPU support. Paths containing spaces or colons need pathToFileURL conversion. Playwright Chromium arguments and a 180-second timeout will be configured. Disabling animations may not wait for WebGPU readiness, so canvas pixel polling is being considered as an alternative.\n\nA 2-second timeout after state changes will be used, with retries if the title shot is blank. The launch log counted non-background pixels; a similar check will be done here. Playwright screenshots are more reliable than WebGL readPixels for WebGPU canvases. A screenshot file size above 50KB will serve as a sanity check.\n\nA pixel check using Playwright screenshot buffers will count non-dark pixels without extra dependencies. The script will use a press helper that waits for the game step to advance. If the attract screen exits via blockMenu, a second Enter key is required to reach the main menu.\n\nThe script will press Enter twice to exit the title screen if the attract menu blocked it, then capture the main menu. Settings and About are reached by pressing down three and four times respectively, with Escape used to return from settings. Story mode is triggered via devRun('scene', 'S0').\n\nStory mode advances by pressing Enter twelve times, then captures the dialogue text and saves the story-shout image. An `op` helper will skip to operation phases, step the game forward, run optional extras, and take a screenshot. The Danger extra function is being drafted.\n\nThe Danger extra script freezes the game, applies five bleeders, and steps forward in 0.5-second increments until vitals drop below 28 or the screen leaves Operation. The Hush extra simply triggers hush and advances ten test steps.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2c80900-834f-4f58-a21b-8e4ed69c30bf-68","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"succeed\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2c80900-834f-4f58-a21b-8e4ed69c30bf-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/sim/sim.js","offset":620,"limit":45}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":540,"output_tokens":1356,"cache_read_input_tokens":115712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e2bbe4cc-2269-4763-b068-fff3f894398f"}
