{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-47ebc344-9e70-464e-b4e9-b20f194efa84-74","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"110→}\\n\\n/**\\n * For a game tagged parallel or ghost, the seed rides in the address: the client seeds Math.random with it before the game's scripts run.\\n * Only a page of this site is loaded: ?game= comes from the address bar, and a javascript: or another site's\\n * address in an unsandboxed frame would run as this origin, where a signed-in player's session is kept.\\n */\\nconst gameUrl = (game, { tag, seed } = {}) => {\\n  let url;\\n  try {\\n120→    url = new URL(game, location.href);\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n  if (url.origin !== location.origin || !/^https?:$/.test(url.protocol)) return null;\\n  url.searchParams.set('aihub', '1');\\n  if (seedsRandom(tag)) url.searchParams.set('aihub-seed', String(seed >>> 0));\\n  return url.href;\\n};\\n\\n130→function applyNet() {\\n  Object.assign(net.settings, {\\n    latency: Math.max(0, Number($('latency').value) || 0),\\n    jitter: Math.max(0, Number($('jitter').value) || 0),\\n    loss: Math.min(0.5, Math.max(0, (Number($('loss').value) || 0) / 100)),\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Wrap what a game must not call in hub mode, where the page can reach it. */\\nfunction instrument(cell) {\\n140→  try {\\n    const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n    for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\\n      const original = win[name];\\n      win[name] = (...args) => {\\n        cell.violations.push(`${name}() called`);\\n        log(`${cell.name}: ${name}() called — not allowed in a session`);\\n        return name === 'confirm' ? false : name === 'prompt' ? null : undefined;\\n      };\\n      void original;\",\"content_concise\":\"110→}\\n\\n/**\\n * For a game tagged parallel or ghost, the seed rides in the address: the client seeds Math.random with it before the game's scripts run.\\n * Only a page of this site is loaded: ?game= comes from the address bar, and a javascript: or another site's\\n * address in an unsandboxed frame would run as this origin, where a signed-in player's session is kept.\\n */\\nconst gameUrl = (game, { tag, seed } = {}) => {\\n  let url;\\n  try {\\n120→    url = new URL(game, location.href);\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n  if (url.origin !== location.origin || !/^https?:$/.test(url.protocol)) return null;\\n  url.searchParams.set('aihub', '1');\\n  if (seedsRandom(tag)) url.searchParams.set('aihub-seed', String(seed >>> 0));\\n  return url.href;\\n};\\n\\n130→function applyNet() {\\n  Object.assign(net.settings, {\\n    latency: Math.max(0, Number($('latency').value) || 0),\\n    jitter: Math.max(0, Number($('jitter').value) || 0),\\n    loss: Math.min(0.5, Math.max(0, (Number($('loss').value) || 0) / 100)),\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Wrap what a game must not call in hub mode, where the page can reach it. */\\nfunction instrument(cell) {\\n140→  try {\\n    const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n    for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\\n      const original = win[name];\\n      win[name] = (...args) => {\\n        cell.violations.push(`${name}() called`);\\n        log(`${cell.name}: ${name}() called — not allowed in a session`);\\n        return name === 'confirm' ? false : name === 'prompt' ? null : undefined;\\n      };\\n      void original;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html\",\"offset\":110,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"}\\n\\n/**\\n * For a game tagged parallel or ghost, the seed rides in the address: the client seeds Math.random with it before the game's scripts run.\\n * Only a page of this site is loaded: ?game= comes from the address bar, and a javascript: or another site's\\n * address in an unsandboxed frame would run as this origin, where a signed-in player's session is kept.\\n */\\nconst gameUrl = (game, { tag, seed } = {}) => {\\n  let url;\\n  try {\\n    url = new URL(game, location.href);\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n  if (url.origin !== location.origin || !/^https?:$/.test(url.protocol)) return null;\\n  url.searchParams.set('aihub', '1');\\n  if (seedsRandom(tag)) url.searchParams.set('aihub-seed', String(seed >>> 0));\\n  return url.href;\\n};\\n\\nfunction applyNet() {\\n  Object.assign(net.settings, {\\n    latency: Math.max(0, Number($('latency').value) || 0),\\n    jitter: Math.max(0, Number($('jitter').value) || 0),\\n    loss: Math.min(0.5, Math.max(0, (Number($('loss').value) || 0) / 100)),\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Wrap what a game must not call in hub mode, where the page can reach it. */\\nfunction instrument(cell) {\\n  try {\\n    const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n    for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\\n      const original = win[name];\\n      win[name] = (...args) => {\\n        cell.violations.push(`${name}() called`);\\n        log(`${cell.name}: ${name}() called — not allowed in a session`);\\n        return name === 'confirm' ? false : name === 'prompt' ? null : undefined;\\n      };\\n      void original;\\n\",\"total_lines\":548}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"58eca433-5ee2-4ec5-b1b4-b3371c4a4634"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_792","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The URL constructor will preserve the existing `webgl=1` parameter and append `aihub=1`.\n\nThe 10-second splash ends when the harness loads, not when the game boots. I will poll every 500 milliseconds for up to 30 seconds until the screen shows Card, then screenshot immediately.\n\nI will hide the header, sidebar, and cell bar via CSS so the iframe fills the viewport. The viewport is 1920 by 1080. The game uses one player. I confirmed main.js reads the webgl parameter. I am ready to write the script.\n\nEach screenshot will be wrapped in its own try/catch so one failure does not abort the rest. State will be logged to shots/index.json after every shot. The title logo is acceptable in the PNGs because they are evidence files, not source code. The capture script will avoid hardcoding the title since state() does not include it.\n\nI will wait to fix the missing `.where` style until after screenshots. Keyboard presses during operations might trigger pause or confirm actions, but skipTo avoids key input entirely. The planned sequence covers title, main menu, settings, about, story, calm operation, hush, danger, seven strains, report, and finally the session card. This yields seventeen images total.\n\nThe plan calls for two extra upright shots: a HUD portrait and a cut-in. These will be named hud-portrait.png and cut-in.png, and they will be captured at the same moments as the calm operation and story shout.\n\nThe portrait camera position is y=-0.55 and z=-1.4, which places it in the lower canvas behind the HUD bark DOM. I am calculating its NDC visibility against the 34-degree vertical FOV to determine whether a direct screenshot would be occluded.\n\nThe portrait plane is partially clipped by the bottom of the visible frustum. Only its top third remains in view, so the captured image will likely show just the head or hair rather than a full upright portrait.\n\nThe cut-in camera position is y=0.25 and z=-1.6. It sits within the vertical frustum but clips slightly at the top edge. Its right side also clips against the canvas boundary because its width exceeds the visible horizontal span. Only the left-center portion of the cut-in should remain visible.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fe8f4f95-ac5a-48a5-b0ac-37154143a2bf-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function placeOrCamera","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view","glob":"*.js","-A":25}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":577,"output_tokens":1549,"cache_read_input_tokens":121472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"ec65c585-0884-4bee-832e-106de51ebadf"}
