{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_794","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"resize() calls placeStoryCamera when in story mode.\n\nStory camera sits at (0, 0.2, 12.5) with a 30° FOV. Cut-in is parented to the camera at local (0.7, 0.25, -1.6). It moves with the camera and stays in front of the lens. At this distance the cut-in spans the vertical and right edges of the view.\n\nThe cut-in likely still shows a face if the face sits in the left-center of the plane. During OR mode the camera is in world space looking at the table, but children stay in camera local space so the portrait remains in front of the lens regardless. The portrait center sits below the frustum, which suggests a bug. I will capture a screenshot to confirm and then fix positions if needed. I also need to check resize() to see when the portrait is placed.\n\nThe portrait is created once in camera local space. I will write and run the capture script, logging entity counts. If a step fails, it will log the error and retry with fewer steps. The shots directory will be created with fs.mkdirSync. Playwright screenshots of the full page with overflow hidden capture only the viewport. I will check for .shout and .where styles to add. Given 1920 WebGPU slowness, the full capture should take about 3 to 6 minutes.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The 1920×1080 review is the piece PLAN still asks for. I’ll capture those screens from the shipped page and fix type, ink, or overlap if the shots show it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2622230d-88e2-4503-919e-d600d06cb095-77","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"gap","content":"Read goal plan, STAGE, TASK, and current hand-in to find the remaining gap","status":"completed"},{"id":"shots","content":"Capture 1920x1080 screens PLAN asks for and inspect them","status":"in_progress"},{"id":"fix","content":"Fix ten-foot type, ink, or overlap the shots show","status":"pending"},{"id":"verify","content":"Rebuild and re-check anything the fixes change","status":"pending"}],"merge":true}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2622230d-88e2-4503-919e-d600d06cb095-78","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots.mjs","content":"import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\nimport { readFileSync, mkdirSync, writeFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport path from 'node:path';\n\nconst require = createRequire('/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/package.json');\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\n\nconst DEV = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230';\nconst HTML = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230.html';\nconst OUT = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots';\nconst FLAGS = [\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\n  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\n];\n\nmkdirSync(OUT, { recursive: true });\nconst log = [];\nconst say = (line) => { log.push(line); console.log(line); };\n\nfunction serve(root) {\n  const server = createServer((req, res) => {\n    const url = new URL(req.url, 'http://127.0.0.1');\n    const rel = decodeURIComponent(url.pathname);\n    if (rel.includes('..')) { res.writeHead(403); res.end(); return; }\n    const file = path.join(root, rel === '/' ? 'harness.html' : rel);\n    if (!file.startsWith(root)) { res.writeHead(403); res.end(); return; }\n    try {\n      const body = readFileSync(file);\n      const ext = path.extname(file);\n      const type = ext === '.html' ? 'text/html' : ext === '.js' ? 'text/javascript' : 'application/octet-stream';\n      res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': type });\n      res.end(body);\n    } catch {\n      res.writeHead(404); res.end();\n    }\n  });\n  return new Promise((resolve) => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => resolve(server)));\n}\n\nasync function main() {\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: FLAGS });\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\n  page.setDefaultTimeout(180000);\n  const errors = [];\n  page.on('pageerror', (e) => errors.push(String(e)));\n  page.on('console', (msg) => {\n    if (msg.type() === 'error') errors.push(msg.text());\n  });\n\n  const url = pathToFileURL(HTML).href + '?test=1';\n  say('goto ' + url);\n  await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__game && window.__game.state && window.__game.state().renderBackend === 'webgpu', null, { timeout: 180000 });\n  say('booted ' + JSON.stringify(await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state())));\n\n  async function press(key) {\n    await page.keyboard.press(key);\n    await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.test.step(1));\n  }\n  async function state() {\n    return page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state());\n  }\n  async function audit() {\n    return page.evaluate(() => {\n      const vh = innerHeight;\n      const vw = innerWidth;\n      const min = 34 * (vh / 1080);\n      const keyMin = 56 * (vh / 1080);\n      const safe = { l: vw * 0.05, t: vh * 0.05, r: vw * 0.95, b: vh * 0.95 };\n      const rows = [];\n      for (const el of document.querySelectorAll('#ui *')) {\n        const hasText = [...el.childNodes].some((n) => n.nodeType === 3 && n.textContent.trim());\n        if (!hasText) continue;\n        const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();\n        if (r.width < 2 || r.height < 2) continue;\n        const fs = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(el).fontSize);\n        const key = el.classList.contains('vitals') || el.classList.contains('timer') || el.classList.contains('score');\n        const small = fs + 0.6 < (key ? keyMin : min);\n        const clip = r.left < -1 || r.top < -1 || r.right > vw + 1 || r.bottom > vh + 1;\n        const unsafe = r.left < safe.l - 2 || r.top < safe.t - 2 || r.right > safe.r + 2 || r.bottom > safe.b + 2;\n        if (small || clip || unsafe) {\n          rows.push({\n            text: el.textContent.trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').slice(0, 60),\n            fs: Math.round(fs),\n            small, clip, unsafe, key,\n            x: Math.round(r.left), y: Math.round(r.top), w: Math.round(r.width), h: Math.round(r.height),\n          });\n        }\n      }\n      return rows;\n    });\n  }\n  async function shot(name) {\n    await page.evaluate(() => new Promise((resolve) => {\n      let n = 0;\n      const tick = () => { if (++n >= 3) resolve(); else requestAnimationFrame(tick); };\n      requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n    }));\n    await page.waitForTimeout(1800);\n    const st = await state();\n    const issues = await audit();\n    await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(OUT, name), animations: 'disabled' });\n    const bytes = statSync(path.join(OUT, name)).size;\n    say(`${name} screen=${st.screen} phase=${st.phase} vitals=${st.vitals == null ? '' : Math.round(st.vitals)} attract=${st.attract} bytes=${bytes} issues=${issues.length}`);\n    for (const row of issues) say('  ' + JSON.stringify(row));\n    return st;\n  }\n\n  let st = await state();\n  if (st.attract) {\n    say('attract already on, exiting');\n    await press('Enter');\n    await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.test.step(2));\n  }\n  await shot('title.png');\n  await press('Enter');\n  st = await state();\n  if (st.screen === 'Title') await press('Enter');\n  await shot('main-menu.png');\n\n  await press('ArrowDown');\n  await press('ArrowDown');\n  await press('ArrowDown');\n  await press('Enter');\n  await shot('settings.png');\n  await press('Escape');\n  st = await state();\n  say('after settings back ' + st.screen + ' focus ' + st.focusId);\n\n  if (st.screen !== 'Main Menu') {\n    await page.keyboard.press('Escape');\n    await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.test.step(2));\n  }\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) await press('ArrowDown');\n  await press('Enter');\n  await shot('about.png');\n\n  await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.devRun('scene', 'S0'));\n  for (let i = 0; i < 16; i++) {\n    const shout = await page.evaluate(() => !!document.querySelector('.dialogue.shout'));\n    if (shout) break;\n    await press('Enter');\n  }\n  const line = await page.evaluate(() => document.querySelector('.dialogue')?.innerText || '');\n  say('story line ' + line.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').slice(0, 120));\n  await shot('story-shout.png');\n  await shot('cut-in.png');\n\n  async function go(op, phase) {\n    const ok = await page.evaluate(({ op, phase }) => {\n      window.__game.test.skipTo(op, phase);\n      window.__game.test.step(12);\n      return window.__game.state();\n    }, { op, phase });\n    say(`go ${op} ${phase} -> ${ok.screen} ${ok.phase} vitals=${ok.vitals == null ? '' : Math.round(ok.vitals)}`);\n  }\n\n  await go('broken-glass', 'glass');\n  await shot('op-calm.png');\n  await shot('hud-portrait.png');\n\n  await page.evaluate(() => { window.__game.devRun('hush'); window.__game.test.step(8); });\n  await shot('hush.png');\n\n  await go('broken-glass', 'glass');\n  const danger = await page.evaluate(() => {\n    const g = window.__game;\n    g.devRun('freeze');\n    for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) g.devRun('bleeder');\n    let last = g.state();\n    for (let n = 0; n < 50; n++) {\n      g.test.step(20);\n      last = g.state();\n      if (last.vitals < 22 || last.screen !== 'Operation') break;\n    }\n    return { screen: last.screen, vitals: last.vitals, phase: last.phase };\n  });\n  say('danger ' + JSON.stringify(danger));\n  await shot('op-danger.png');\n\n  const strains = [\n    ['strain-adagio.png', 'adagio', 'creature'],\n    ['strain-staccato.png', 'staccato', 'wave1'],\n    ['strain-tremolo.png', 'staccato', 'moths'],\n    ['strain-legato.png', 'legato', 'chain'],\n    ['strain-crescendo.png', 'fermata', 'ring'],\n    ['strain-fermata.png', 'fermata', 'arrest2'],\n    ['strain-coda.png', 'coda', 'conductor'],\n  ];\n  for (const [name, op, phase] of strains) {\n    await go(op, phase);\n    await shot(name);\n  }\n\n  await page.evaluate(() => { window.__game.devRun('win'); window.__game.test.step(2); });\n  await shot('report.png');\n  say('errors ' + errors.length);\n  for (const e of errors.slice(0, 12)) say('ERR ' + e.slice(0, 240));\n\n  await page.close();\n\n  const site = path.join(DEV, 'tests/hub/site');\n  const server = await serve(site);\n  const port = server.address().port;\n  const cardUrl = `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/harness.html?game=${encodeURIComponent('game.html?webgl=1')}&players=1`;\n  say('card ' + cardUrl);\n  const page2 = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\n  page2.setDefaultTimeout(120000);\n  const cardErrors = [];\n  page2.on('pageerror', (e) => cardErrors.push(String(e)));\n  await page2.addInitScript(() => {\n    const style = document.createElement('style');\n    style.textContent = 'header,aside{display:none!important}main{grid-template-columns:1fr!important}#grid{padding:0!important}.cell__bar{display:none!important}';\n    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => document.documentElement.append(style));\n  });\n  await page2.goto(cardUrl, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });\n  const found = await page2.waitForFunction(() => {\n    const frame = document.querySelector('iframe');\n    const game = frame && frame.contentWindow && frame.contentWindow.__game;\n    if (!game || !game.state) return false;\n    return game.state().screen;\n  }, null, { timeout: 90000 }).then(async () => page2.evaluate(() => {\n    const game = document.querySelector('iframe').contentWindow.__game;\n    return game.state().screen;\n  })).catch((err) => 'timeout ' + err.message);\n  say('card screen ' + found);\n  await page2.waitForTimeout(1500);\n  const frame = page2.frames().find((f) => f.url().includes('game.html'));\n  if (frame) {\n    const issues = await frame.evaluate(() => {\n      const vh = innerHeight;\n      const vw = innerWidth;\n      const min = 34 * (vh / 1080);\n      const rows = [];\n      for (const el of document.querySelectorAll('#ui *')) {\n        const hasText = [...el.childNodes].some((n) => n.nodeType === 3 && n.textContent.trim());\n        if (!hasText) continue;\n        const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();\n        if (r.width < 2 || r.height < 2) continue;\n        const fs = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(el).fontSize);\n        if (fs + 0.6 < min || r.bottom > vh + 1 || r.right > vw + 1) {\n          rows.push({ text: el.textContent.trim().slice(0, 50), fs: Math.round(fs), bottom: Math.round(r.bottom), right: Math.round(r.right), vh, vw });\n        }\n      }\n      return { rows, screen: window.__game.state().screen, box: { w: innerWidth, h: innerHeight } };\n    });\n    say('card audit ' + JSON.stringify(issues));\n  }\n  await page2.screenshot({ path: path.join(OUT, 'session-card.png'), animations: 'disabled' });\n  say('session-card bytes ' + statSync(path.join(OUT, 'session-card.png')).size + ' cardErrors ' + cardErrors.length);\n  for (const e of cardErrors.slice(0, 8)) say('CARDERR ' + e.slice(0, 200));\n\n  await browser.close();\n  server.close();\n  writeFileSync(path.join(OUT, 'shots.log'), log.join('\\n') + '\\n');\n  say('done');\n}\n\nmain().catch((err) => {\n  console.error(err);\n  writeFileSync(path.join(OUT, 'shots.log'), log.join('\\n') + '\\n' + err.stack + '\\n');\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":461,"output_tokens":4476,"cache_read_input_tokens":124032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"db13f431-fba4-4d57-b41e-eb63775f30ce"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2622230d-88e2-4503-919e-d600d06cb095-77","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [completed] gap: Read goal plan, STAGE, TASK, and current hand-in to find the remaining gap\\n- [pending] fix: Fix ten-foot type, ink, or overlap the shots show\\n- [pending] verify: Rebuild and re-check anything the fixes change\\n- [in_progress] shots: Capture 1920x1080 screens PLAN asks for and inspect them\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Read goal plan, STAGE, TASK, and current hand-in to find the remaining gap\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Fix ten-foot type, ink, or overlap the shots show\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Rebuild and re-check anything the fixes change\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Capture 1920x1080 screens PLAN asks for and inspect them\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"gap\":{\"content\":\"Read goal plan, STAGE, TASK, and current hand-in to find the remaining gap\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"fix\":{\"content\":\"Fix ten-foot type, ink, or overlap the shots show\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"verify\":{\"content\":\"Rebuild and re-check anything the fixes change\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"shots\":{\"content\":\"Capture 1920x1080 screens PLAN asks for and inspect them\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2622230d-88e2-4503-919e-d600d06cb095-78","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\\nimport { readFileSync, mkdirSync, writeFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\n\\nconst require = createRequire('/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/package.json');\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst DEV = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230';\\nconst HTML = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230.html';\\nconst OUT = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots';\\nconst FLAGS = [\\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\\n];\\n\\nmkdirSync(OUT, { recursive: true });\\nconst log = [];\\nconst say = (line) => { log.push(line); console.log(line); };\\n\\nfunction serve(root) {\\n  const server = createServer((req, res) => {\\n    const url = new URL(req.url, 'http://127.0.0.1');\\n    const rel = decodeURIComponent(url.pathname);\\n    if (rel.includes('..')) { res.writeHead(403); res.end(); return; }\\n    const file = path.join(root, rel === '/' ? 'harness.html' : rel);\\n    if (!file.startsWith(root)) { res.writeHead(403); res.end(); return; }\\n    try {\\n      const body = readFileSync(file);\\n      const ext = path.extname(file);\\n      const type = ext === '.html' ? 'text/html' : ext === '.js' ? 'text/javascript' : 'application/octet-stream';\\n      res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': type });\\n      res.end(body);\\n    } catch {\\n      res.writeHead(404); res.end();\\n    }\\n  });\\n  return new Promise((resolve) => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => resolve(server)));\\n}\\n\\nasync function main() {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: FLAGS });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\\n  page.setDefaultTimeout(180000);\\n  const errors = [];\\n  page.on('pageerror', (e) => errors.push(String(e)));\\n  page.on('console', (msg) => {\\n    if (msg.type() === 'error') errors.push(msg.text());\\n  });\\n\\n  const url = pathToFileURL(HTML).href + '?test=1';\\n  say('goto ' + url);\\n  await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__game && window.__game.state && window.__game.state().renderBackend === 'webgpu', null, { timeout: 180000 });\\n  say('booted ' + JSON.stringify(await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state())));\\n\\n  async function press(key) {\\n    await page.keyboard.press(key);\\n    await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.test.step(1));\\n  }\\n  async function state() {\\n    return page.evaluate(() => window.__game.state());\\n  }\\n  async function audit() {\\n    return page.evaluate(() => {\\n      const vh = innerHeight;\\n      const vw = innerWidth;\\n      const min = 34 * (vh / 1080);\\n      const keyMin = 56 * (vh / 1080);\\n      const safe = { l: vw * 0.05, t: vh * 0.05, r: vw * 0.95, b: vh * 0.95 };\\n      const rows = [];\\n      for (const el of document.querySelectorAll('#ui *')) {\\n        const hasText = [...el.childNodes].some((n) => n.nodeType === 3 && n.textContent.trim());\\n        if (!hasText) continue;\\n        const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();\\n        if (r.width < 2 || r.height < 2) continue;\\n        const fs = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(el).fontSize);\\n        const key = el.classList.contains('vitals') || el.classList.contains('timer') || el.classList.contains('score');\\n        const small = fs + 0.6 < (key ? keyMin : min);\\n        const clip = r.left < -1 || r.top < -1 || r.right > vw + 1 || r.bottom > vh + 1;\\n        const unsafe = r.left < safe.l - 2 || r.top < safe.t - 2 || r.right > safe.r + 2 || r.bottom > safe.b + 2;\\n        if (small || clip || unsafe) {\\n          rows.push({\\n            text: el.textContent.trim().replace(/\\\\s+/g, ' ').slice(0, 60),\\n            fs: Math.round(fs),\\n            small, clip, unsafe, key,\\n            x: Math.round(r.left), y: Math.round(r.top), w: Math.round(r.width), h: Math.round(r.height),\\n          });\\n        }\\n      }\\n      return rows;\\n    });\\n  }\\n  async function shot(name) {\\n    await page.evaluate(() => new Promise((resolve) => {\\n      let n = 0;\\n      const tick = () => { if (++n >= 3) resolve(); else requestAnimationFrame(tick); };\\n      requestAnimationFrame(tick);\\n    }));\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(1800);\\n    const st = await state();\\n    const issues = await audit();\\n    await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(OUT, name), animations: 'disabled' });\\n    const bytes = statSync(path.join(OUT, name)).size;\\n    say(`${name} screen=${st.screen} phase=${st.phase} vitals=${st.vitals == null ? '' : Math.round(st.vitals)} attract=${st.attract} bytes=${bytes} issues=${issues.length}`);\\n    for (const row of issues) say('  ' + JSON.stringify(row));\\n    return st;\\n  }\\n\\n  let st = await state();\\n  if (st.attract) {\\n    say('attract already on, exiting');\\n    await press('Enter');\\n    await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.test.step(2));\\n  }\\n  await shot('title.png');\\n  await press('Enter');\\n  st = await state();\\n  if (st.screen === 'Title') await press('Enter');\\n  await shot('main-menu.png');\\n\\n  await press('ArrowDown');\\n  await press('ArrowDown');\\n  await press('ArrowDown');\\n  await press('Enter');\\n  await shot('settings.png');\\n  await press('Escape');\\n  st = await state();\\n  say('after settings back ' + st.screen + ' focus ' + st.focusId);\\n\\n  if (st.screen !== 'Main Menu') {\\n    await page.keyboard.press('Escape');\\n    await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.test.step(2));\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) await press('ArrowDown');\\n  await press('Enter');\\n  await shot('about.png');\\n\\n  await page.evaluate(() => window.__game.devRun('scene', 'S0'));\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 16; i++) {\\n    const shout = await page.evaluate(() => !!document.querySelector('.dialogue.shout'));\\n    if (shout) break;\\n    await press('Enter');\\n  }\\n  const line = await page.evaluate(() => document.querySelector('.dialogue')?.innerText || '');\\n  say('story line ' + line.replace(/\\\\s+/g, ' ').slice(0, 120));\\n  await shot('story-shout.png');\\n  await shot('cut-in.png');\\n\\n  async function go(op, phase) {\\n    const ok = await page.evaluate(({ op, phase }) => {\\n      window.__game.test.skipTo(op, phase);\\n      window.__game.test.step(12);\\n      return window.__game.state();\\n    }, { op, phase });\\n    say(`go ${op} ${phase} -> ${ok.screen} ${ok.phase} vitals=${ok.vitals == null ? '' : Math.round(ok.vitals)}`);\\n  }\\n\\n  await go('broken-glass', 'glass');\\n  await shot('op-calm.png');\\n  await shot('hud-portrait.png');\\n\\n  await page.evaluate(() => { window.__game.devRun('hush'); window.__game.test.step(8); });\\n  await shot('hush.png');\\n\\n  await go('broken-glass', 'glass');\\n  const danger = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n    const g = window.__game;\\n    g.devRun('freeze');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) g.devRun('bleeder');\\n    let last = g.state();\\n    for (let n = 0; n < 50; n++) {\\n      g.test.step(20);\\n      last = g.state();\\n      if (last.vitals < 22 || last.screen !== 'Operation') break;\\n    }\\n    return { screen: last.screen, vitals: last.vitals, phase: last.phase };\\n  });\\n  say('danger ' + JSON.stringify(danger));\\n  await shot('op-danger.png');\\n\\n  const strains = [\\n    ['strain-adagio.png', 'adagio', 'creature'],\\n    ['strain-staccato.png', 'staccato', 'wave1'],\\n    ['strain-tremolo.png', 'staccato', 'moths'],\\n    ['strain-legato.png', 'legato', 'chain'],\\n    ['strain-crescendo.png', 'fermata', 'ring'],\\n    ['strain-fermata.png', 'fermata', 'arrest2'],\\n    ['strain-coda.png', 'coda', 'conductor'],\\n  ];\\n  for (const [name, op, phase] of strains) {\\n    await go(op, phase);\\n    await shot(name);\\n  }\\n\\n  await page.evaluate(() => { window.__game.devRun('win'); window.__game.test.step(2); });\\n  await shot('report.png');\\n  say('errors ' + errors.length);\\n  for (const e of errors.slice(0, 12)) say('ERR ' + e.slice(0, 240));\\n\\n  await page.close();\\n\\n  const site = path.join(DEV, 'tests/hub/site');\\n  const server = await serve(site);\\n  const port = server.address().port;\\n  const cardUrl = `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/harness.html?game=${encodeURIComponent('game.html?webgl=1')}&players=1`;\\n  say('card ' + cardUrl);\\n  const page2 = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\\n  page2.setDefaultTimeout(120000);\\n  const cardErrors = [];\\n  page2.on('pageerror', (e) => cardErrors.push(String(e)));\\n  await page2.addInitScript(() => {\\n    const style = document.createElement('style');\\n    style.textContent = 'header,aside{display:none!important}main{grid-template-columns:1fr!important}#grid{padding:0!important}.cell__bar{display:none!important}';\\n    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => document.documentElement.append(style));\\n  });\\n  await page2.goto(cardUrl, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });\\n  const found = await page2.waitForFunction(() => {\\n    const frame = document.querySelector('iframe');\\n    const game = frame && frame.contentWindow && frame.contentWindow.__game;\\n    if (!game || !game.state) return false;\\n    return game.state().screen;\\n  }, null, { timeout: 90000 }).then(async () => page2.evaluate(() => {\\n    const game = document.querySelector('iframe').contentWindow.__game;\\n    return game.state().screen;\\n  })).catch((err) => 'timeout ' + err.message);\\n  say('card screen ' + found);\\n  await page2.waitForTimeout(1500);\\n  const frame = page2.frames().find((f) => f.url().includes('game.html'));\\n  if (frame) {\\n    const issues = await frame.evaluate(() => {\\n      const vh = innerHeight;\\n      const vw = innerWidth;\\n      const min = 34 * (vh / 1080);\\n      const rows = [];\\n      for (const el of document.querySelectorAll('#ui *')) {\\n        const hasText = [...el.childNodes].some((n) => n.nodeType === 3 && n.textContent.trim());\\n        if (!hasText) continue;\\n        const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();\\n        if (r.width < 2 || r.height < 2) continue;\\n        const fs = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(el).fontSize);\\n        if (fs + 0.6 < min || r.bottom > vh + 1 || r.right > vw + 1) {\\n          rows.push({ text: el.textContent.trim().slice(0, 50), fs: Math.round(fs), bottom: Math.round(r.bottom), right: Math.round(r.right), vh, vw });\\n        }\\n      }\\n      return { rows, screen: window.__game.state().screen, box: { w: innerWidth, h: innerHeight } };\\n    });\\n    say('card audit ' + JSON.stringify(issues));\\n  }\\n  await page2.screenshot({ path: path.join(OUT, 'session-card.png'), animations: 'disabled' });\\n  say('session-card bytes ' + statSync(path.join(OUT, 'session-card.png')).size + ' cardErrors ' + cardErrors.length);\\n  for (const e of cardErrors.slice(0, 8)) say('CARDERR ' + e.slice(0, 200));\\n\\n  await browser.close();\\n  server.close();\\n  writeFileSync(path.join(OUT, 'shots.log'), log.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n');\\n  say('done');\\n}\\n\\nmain().catch((err) => {\\n  console.error(err);\\n  writeFileSync(path.join(OUT, 'shots.log'), log.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n' + err.stack + '\\\\n');\\n  process.exit(1);\\n});\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots.mjs has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.bui