{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_802","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The command output was truncated. Only the exit code 0 is visible.\n\nTesseract is not installed. PIL imported successfully. The pale dome is a surgical lamp cone at y=2.2 with cream color #f4efe4, positioned between the camera and target.\n\nThe cone at y=2.2 is a small surgical lamp hanging into the frame. It is 1.35 units below the camera, so it should not fill the top of the screen unless it sits very close to the camera frustum.\n\nThe lamp cone is too small to explain the large pale dome. The portrait plane is the more likely source of that shape. I am calculating the camera's local axes to verify this.\n\nThe portrait plane is too low in the frame to explain the top pale dome. The bust render would only create a pale band at the bottom. I will examine the actual pixels to find the true source of the dome.\n\nThe organ plane is too large and would color the entire field pale, not just the top. The lamp cone is still too small. I will inspect the image pixels directly to find the true source of the dome.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-acf9ec04-c4bd-4a49-a54b-8724c3ab1966-93","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/bust.js","offset":150,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-acf9ec04-c4bd-4a49-a54b-8724c3ab1966-94","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/data/sites.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-acf9ec04-c4bd-4a49-a54b-8724c3ab1966-95","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntry:\n    from PIL import Image\nexcept ImportError:\n    import subprocess, sys\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', 'pillow', '-q'])\n    from PIL import Image\np = Path('/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots')\nfor name in ['title.png','main-menu.png','about.png','story-shout.png']:\n    f = p/name\n    if not f.exists():\n        print(name, 'missing'); continue\n    im = Image.open(f).convert('RGB')\n    w,h = im.size\n    print(name, w, h)\n    # sample a grid\n    for gy in range(6):\n        row=[]\n        for gx in range(8):\n            x=int((gx+0.5)*w/8); y=int((gy+0.5)*h/6)\n            row.append('%02x%02x%02x'%im.getpixel((x,y)))\n        print(' ', row)\nPY","description":"Sample screenshot colors on a grid"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3519,"output_tokens":1459,"cache_read_input_tokens":147968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6209cc65-7340-4657-a227-4a54b698e150"}
