0,40,123,32,99,111,108,111,114,58,32,39,35,101,56,101,101,102,50,39,32,125,41,44,32,45,48,46,50,44,32,48,44,32,48,41,59,10,57,51,58,32,32,32,32,97,100,100,40,110,101,119,32,84,72,82,69,69,46,66,111,120,71,101,111,109,101,116,114,121,40,48,46,49,56,44,32,48,46,48,53,44,32,48,46,49,50,41,44,32,116,111,111,110,40,123,32,99,111,108,111,114,58,32,39,35,101,56,101,101,102,50,39,32,125,41,44,32,48,46,50,44,32,48,44,32,48,41,59,10,57,53,58,32,32,32,32,97,100,100,40,110,101,119,32,84,72,82,69,69,46,66,111,120,71,101,111,109,101,116,114,121,40,48,46,48,52,44,32,48,46,48,52,44,32,48,46,51,52,41,44,32,107,105,110,100,32,61,61,61,32,39,108,97,115,101,114,39,32,63,32,116,111,111,110,40,123,32,99,111,108,111,114,58,32,39,35,101,56,52,52,51,97,39,32,125,41,32,58,32,109,101,116,97,108,44,32,48,44,32,48,44,32,48,46,48,56,41,59,10,49,52,50,58,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,102,108,111,111,114,32,61,32,110,101,119,32,84,72,82,69,69,46,77,101,115,104,40,110,101,119,32,84,72,82,69,69,46,66,111,120,71,101,111,109,101,116,114,121,40,49,52,44,32,48,46,50,44,32,56,41,44,32,116,111,111,110,40,123,32,99,111,108,111,114,58,32,39,35,48,101,50,99,51,48,39,32,125,41,41,59,10,49,52,54,58,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,98,97,99,107,32,61,32,110,101,119,32,84,72,82,69,69,46,77,101,115,104,40,110,101,119,32,84,72,82,69,69,46,66,111,120,71,101,111,109,101,116,114,121,40,49,52,44,32,54,44,32,48,46,50,41,44,32,119,97,108,108,41,59,10,49,53,48,58,32,32,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,119,105,110,32,61,32,110,101,119,32,84,72,82,69,69,46,77,101,115,104,40,110,101,119,32,84,72,82,69,69,46,66,111,120,71,101,111,109,101,116,114,121,40,52,44,32,50,44,32,48,46,48,56,41,44,32,116,111,111,110,40,123,32,99,111,108,111,114,58,32,39,35,56,101,99,56,100,56,39,32,125,41,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":8,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":89,\"content\":\"    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.03, 0.02, 0.28), metal, -0.03, 0, 0.1);\"},{\"line_number\":90,\"content\":\"    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.03, 0.02, 0.28), metal, 0.03, 0, 0.1);\"},{\"line_number\":92,\"content\":\"    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.18, 0.05, 0.12), toon({ color: '#e8eef2' }), -0.2, 0, 0);\"},{\"line_number\":93,\"content\":\"    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.18, 0.05, 0.12), toon({ color: '#e8eef2' }), 0.2, 0, 0);\"},{\"line_number\":95,\"content\":\"    add(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.04, 0.04, 0.34), kind === 'laser' ? toon({ color: '#e8443a' }) : metal, 0, 0, 0.08);\"},{\"line_number\":142,\"content\":\"  const floor = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(14, 0.2, 8), toon({ color: '#0e2c30' }));\"},{\"line_number\":146,\"content\":\"  const back = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(14, 6, 0.2), wall);\"},{\"line_number\":150,\"content\":\"    const win = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(4, 2, 0.08), toon({ color: '#8ec8d8' }));\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bd742011-7d16-4dad-b27b-cb1216eb9e09-99","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"488→### 9.2 The operating view (values verified in the prototype)\\n\\n490→- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(34, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at `(0, 3.55, 1.65)`, looking at `(0, 0.1, 0.06)`. For aspect under 16:9, scale the distance by `(16/9)/aspect`.\\n- Subtle life: parallax toward the tip, a 0.2% dolly on each beat, shake on slams, punch-in on Hush, 0.35 s whip between sites.\\n- **Drape:** an extruded teal shape at `y = 0.34` with an irregular elliptical window (radii about 1.5 × 0.95, wavy edge). It hides the field's rectangular edge and instantly reads as surgery.\\n- **Lamp:** visible in title and story. In the OR it's just warm light.\\n- **Lighting:** `HemisphereLight(0xffffff, 0x9aa6b0, 1.5)` and `DirectionalLight(0xfff2de, 1.9)` from upper right, shadow map 2048, `bias -0.0006`, `normalBias 0.03`. Tissue meshes: `receiveShadow` yes, `castShadow` no; otherwise you get wavy acne.\\n- Add a low-vitals lamp flicker, and red `danger` from the ink module.\\n\\n### 9.3 Sites\\n\\nEach site is a `heightAt(x, y)` sum of Gaussian lobes minus creases, plus two layers of fine sine relief (the relief is what breaks highlights into wet glints), a 1024² painted `CanvasTexture`, and an optional vertex motion. Use `PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 280, 200)` with `rotateX(-Math.PI / 2)`, `computeVertexNormals()` after displacement, and `positionNode = positionLocal.add(normalLocal.mul(uBeat.mul(0.03)))` for the squeeze.\\n500→\\n| Site | Height idea | Base colors | Motion and detail |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Forearm | One long ridge | `#E8B48F` skin, gash mesh | Slight tremor |\\n| Abdomen skin | Gentle dome | Skin, iodine-orange swab paint | Breathing |\\n| Bowel | Many tube-like folds | `#E87A8B` | Slow peristalsis |\\n| Liver | Two broad lobes, one crease | `#8E2A3A` | Slight squeeze |\\n| Stomach | One big dome with rugae lines | `#E9967A` | Churn |\\n| Brain | Gyri: sine folds warped by noise | `#E8A9B8`, blue vessels | Nearly still, makes the cuts scary |\\n| Heart | Big muscular dome, coronary ridges | `#C4364F`, branching veins | Strong beat |\\n510→| Lung | Two inflating lobes | `#F0A3A8` | Breath every 4 beats moves targets 0.05 fu |\\n| Aorta | One thick tube across the field | `#B52A3E` | Pulse wave down its length |\\n\\n**Veins:** draw on the canvas with a recursive branching stroke, tapering width (5 lines of code; it looks great in the prototype).\\n**Wet glints** (verified): `emissiveNode` with hard `smoothstep` thresholds on `dot(normalView, H)` for two fixed view-space half-vectors (§16.6). Keep glints under about 8% of the area.\\n**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends). For a 1024² canvas on that plane, field to canvas is `cx = (x + 1.8) / 3.6 × 1024`, `cy = (1.25 - y) / 2.5 × 1024`.\\n**Scanner:** a world-space circle in the site material's `colorNode`, replacing the surface with cyan-on-navy hatching inside `scannerRadius` (verified).\\n**Stave lines:** when a strain is present, five dark lines ink themselves across the organ, drawn on the paint layer, with little note-marks riding them.\\n\\n### 9.4 Instruments\\n520→\\nEach is a small hierarchy of named meshes with `use` animation clips, tilted toward the lower right so it never hides the target, with a springy swing as it moves and a contact shadow. No hands.\\n\\nScalpel, Forceps (two jaws), Suction wand (hose as a tube), Gel nozzle (foam blobs), Needle driver with curved needle and thread, Laser pen (additive beam, ember at the tip), Scanner puck (with a sweeping ring), Clamp (ratcheting jaws, stays on the bleeder), Syringe (plunger moves), Defib paddles (a pair, sliding in from each side).\\n\\nCo-op: each seat's tip has a ring in the seat color and a floating name (DOM, `textContent`).\\n\\n### 9.5 Story staging\\n\\n- 16:9 stage with a bottom dialogue box and name tag in the character's color.\\n530→- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(30, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at about `(0, 0.2, 12.5)`, busts at about x = ±2.1. Slow dolly. Punch-in plus `speedLines` for shouts (§16.5; it looks exactly like manga).\\n- **Five sets** built from boxes and props, inked by the filter: OR 3 and gallery; corridor with rain on the windows; Ward Zero (green tile, pipes); Pip's lab; hospital roof in rain. Bell's office and the boardroom can reuse the corridor shell with new props.\\n- Text types out in sync with gibberish voice (§11). Transitions are an ink-wipe across the screen.\\n- **Cut-ins:** at big moments, a tilted panel with thick white border shows a close-up of a bust and a comic SFX word (\\\"KA-THUMP!\\\", \\\"FLATLINE!\\\"). Panels are 3D planes parented to the camera, textured from a `RenderTarget` of the bust (verified per-frame on both backends), so the ink pass lines them like everything else. **A render target shows upside down on a plain plane unless you flip the plane's UVs** (§16.6).\\n\\n### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\\n\\nBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. This reads as a cartoon anime face in the ink filter. It's a good base, not a finish, so spend time on hair and clothes. In the prototype, narrower shoulders looked like a bobblehead, and simple chin tapers gave either a ball or a point.\",\"content_concise\":\"488→### 9.2 The operating view (values verified in the prototype)\\n\\n490→- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(34, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at `(0, 3.55, 1.65)`, looking at `(0, 0.1, 0.06)`. For aspect under 16:9, scale the distance by `(16/9)/aspect`.\\n- Subtle life: parallax toward the tip, a 0.2% dolly on each beat, shake on slams, punch-in on Hush, 0.35 s whip between sites.\\n- **Drape:** an extruded teal shape at `y = 0.34` with an irregular elliptical window (radii about 1.5 × 0.95, wavy edge). It hides the field's rectangular edge and instantly reads as surgery.\\n- **Lamp:** visible in title and story. In the OR it's just warm light.\\n- **Lighting:** `HemisphereLight(0xffffff, 0x9aa6b0, 1.5)` and `DirectionalLight(0xfff2de, 1.9)` from upper right, shadow map 2048, `bias -0.0006`, `normalBias 0.03`. Tissue meshes: `receiveShadow` yes, `castShadow` no; otherwise you get wavy acne.\\n- Add a low-vitals lamp flicker, and red `danger` from the ink module.\\n\\n### 9.3 Sites\\n\\nEach site is a `heightAt(x, y)` sum of Gaussian lobes minus creases, plus two layers of fine sine relief (the relief is what breaks highlights into wet glints), a 1024² painted `CanvasTexture`, and an optional vertex motion. Use `PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 280, 200)` with `rotateX(-Math.PI / 2)`, `computeVertexNormals()` after displacement, and `positionNode = positionLocal.add(normalLocal.mul(uBeat.mul(0.03)))` for the squeeze.\\n500→\\n| Site | Height idea | Base colors | Motion and detail |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Forearm | One long ridge | `#E8B48F` skin, gash mesh | Slight tremor |\\n| Abdomen skin | Gentle dome | Skin, iodine-orange swab paint | Breathing |\\n| Bowel | Many tube-like folds | `#E87A8B` | Slow peristalsis |\\n| Liver | Two broad lobes, one crease | `#8E2A3A` | Slight squeeze |\\n| Stomach | One big dome with rugae lines | `#E9967A` | Churn |\\n| Brain | Gyri: sine folds warped by noise | `#E8A9B8`, blue vessels | Nearly still, makes the cuts scary |\\n| Heart | Big muscular dome, coronary ridges | `#C4364F`, branching veins | Strong beat |\\n510→| Lung | Two inflating lobes | `#F0A3A8` | Breath every 4 beats moves targets 0.05 fu |\\n| Aorta | One thick tube across the field | `#B52A3E` | Pulse wave down its length |\\n\\n**Veins:** draw on the canvas with a recursive branching stroke, tapering width (5 lines of code; it looks great in the prototype).\\n**Wet glints** (verified): `emissiveNode` with hard `smoothstep` thresholds on `dot(normalView, H)` for two fixed view-space half-vectors (§16.6). Keep glints under about 8% of the area.\\n**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends). For a 1024² canvas on that plane, field to canvas is `cx = (x + 1.8) / 3.6 × 1024`, `cy = (1.25 - y) / 2.5 × 1024`.\\n**Scanner:** a world-space circle in the site material's `colorNode`, replacing the surface with cyan-on-navy hatching inside `scannerRadius` (verified).\\n**Stave lines:** when a strain is present, five dark lines ink themselves across the organ, drawn on the paint layer, with little note-marks riding them.\\n\\n### 9.4 Instruments\\n520→\\nEach is a small hierarchy of named meshes with `use` animation clips, tilted toward the lower right so it never hides the target, with a springy swing as it moves and a contact shadow. No hands.\\n\\nScalpel, Forceps (two jaws), Suction wand (hose as a tube), Gel nozzle (foam blobs), Needle driver with curved needle and thread, Laser pen (additive beam, ember at the tip), Scanner puck (with a sweeping ring), Clamp (ratcheting jaws, stays on the bleeder), Syringe (plunger moves), Defib paddles (a pair, sliding in from each side).\\n\\nCo-op: each seat's tip has a ring in the seat color and a floating name (DOM, `textContent`).\\n\\n### 9.5 Story staging\\n\\n- 16:9 stage with a bottom dialogue box and name tag in the character's color.\\n530→- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(30, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at about `(0, 0.2, 12.5)`, busts at about x = ±2.1. Slow dolly. Punch-in plus `speedLines` for shouts (§16.5; it looks exactly like manga).\\n- **Five sets** built from boxes and props, inked by the filter: OR 3 and gallery; corridor with rain on the windows; Ward Zero (green tile, pipes); Pip's lab; hospital roof in rain. Bell's office and the boardroom can reuse the corridor shell with new props.\\n- Text types out in sync with gibberish voice (§11). Transitions are an ink-wipe across the screen.\\n- **Cut-ins:** at big moments, a tilted panel with thick white border shows a close-up of a bust and a comic SFX word (\\\"KA-THUMP!\\\", \\\"FLATLINE!\\\"). Panels are 3D planes parented to the camera, textured from a `RenderTarget` of the bust (verified per-frame on both backends), so the ink pass lines them like everything else. **A render target shows upside down on a plain plane unless you flip the plane's UVs** (§16.6).\\n\\n### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\\n\\nBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. This reads as a cartoon anime face in the ink filter. It's a good base, not a finish, so spend time on hair and clothes. In the prototype, narrower shoulders looked like a bobblehead, and simple chin tapers gave either a ball or a point.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":488,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"### 9.2 The operating view (values verified in the prototype)\\n\\n- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(34, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at `(0, 3.55, 1.65)`, looking at `(0, 0.1, 0.06)`. For aspect under 16:9, scale the distance by `(16/9)/aspect`.\\n- Subtle life: parallax toward the tip, a 0.2% dolly on each beat, shake on slams, punch-in on Hush, 0.35 s whip between sites.\\n- **Drape:** an extruded teal shape at `y = 0.34` with an irregular elliptical window (radii about 1.5 × 0.95, wavy edge). It hides the field's rectangular edge and instantly reads as surgery.\\n- **Lamp:** visible in title and story. In the OR it's just warm light.\\n- **Lighting:** `HemisphereLight(0xffffff, 0x9aa6b0, 1.5)` and `DirectionalLight(0xfff2de, 1.9)` from upper right, shadow map 2048, `bias -0.0006`, `normalBias 0.03`. Tissue meshes: `receiveShadow` yes, `castShadow` no; otherwise you get wavy acne.\\n- Add a low-vitals lamp flicker, and red `danger` from the ink module.\\n\\n### 9.3 Sites\\n\\nEach site is a `heightAt(x, y)` sum of Gaussian lobes minus creases, plus two layers of fine sine relief (the relief is what breaks highlights into wet glints), a 1024² painted `CanvasTexture`, and an optional vertex motion. Use `PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 280, 200)` with `rotateX(-Math.PI / 2)`, `computeVertexNormals()` after displacement, and `positionNode = positionLocal.add(normalLocal.mul(uBeat.mul(0.03)))` for the squeeze.\\n\\n| Site | Height idea | Base colors | Motion and detail |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Forearm | One long ridge | `#E8B48F` skin, gash mesh | Slight tremor |\\n| Abdomen skin | Gentle dome | Skin, iodine-orange swab paint | Breathing |\\n| Bowel | Many tube-like folds | `#E87A8B` | Slow peristalsis |\\n| Liver | Two broad lobes, one crease | `#8E2A3A` | Slight squeeze |\\n| Stomach | One big dome with rugae lines | `#E9967A` | Churn |\\n| Brain | Gyri: sine folds warped by noise | `#E8A9B8`, blue vessels | Nearly still, makes the cuts scary |\\n| Heart | Big muscular dome, coronary ridges | `#C4364F`, branching veins | Strong beat |\\n| Lung | Two inflating lobes | `#F0A3A8` | Breath every 4 beats moves targets 0.05 fu |\\n| Aorta | One thick tube across the field | `#B52A3E` | Pulse wave down its length |\\n\\n**Veins:** draw on the canvas with a recursive branching stroke, tapering width (5 lines of code; it looks great in the prototype).\\n**Wet glints** (verified): `emissiveNode` with hard `smoothstep` thresholds on `dot(normalView, H)` for two fixed view-space half-vectors (§16.6). Keep glints under about 8% of the area.\\n**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends). For a 1024² canvas on that plane, field to canvas is `cx = (x + 1.8) / 3.6 × 1024`, `cy = (1.25 - y) / 2.5 × 1024`.\\n**Scanner:** a world-space circle in the site material's `colorNode`, replacing the surface with cyan-on-navy hatching inside `scannerRadius` (verified).\\n**Stave lines:** when a strain is present, five dark lines ink themselves across the organ, drawn on the paint layer, with little note-marks riding them.\\n\\n### 9.4 Instruments\\n\\nEach is a small hierarchy of named meshes with `use` animation clips, tilted toward the lower right so it never hides the target, with a springy swing as it moves and a contact shadow. No hands.\\n\\nScalpel, Forceps (two jaws), Suction wand (hose as a tube), Gel nozzle (foam blobs), Needle driver with curved needle and thread, Laser pen (additive beam, ember at the tip), Scanner puck (with a sweeping ring), Clamp (ratcheting jaws, stays on the bleeder), Syringe (plunger moves), Defib paddles (a pair, sliding in from each side).\\n\\nCo-op: each seat's tip has a ring in the seat color and a floating name (DOM, `textContent`).\\n\\n### 9.5 Story staging\\n\\n- 16:9 stage with a bottom dialogue box and name tag in the character's color.\\n- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(30, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at about `(0, 0.2, 12.5)`, busts at about x = ±2.1. Slow dolly. Punch-in plus `speedLines` for shouts (§16.5; it looks exactly like manga).\\n- **Five sets** built from boxes and props, inked by the filter: OR 3 and gallery; corridor with rain on the windows; Ward Zero (green tile, pipes); Pip's lab; hospital roof in rain. Bell's office and the boardroom can reuse the corridor shell with new props.\\n- Text types out in sync with gibberish voice (§11). Transitions are an ink-wipe across the screen.\\n- **Cut-ins:** at big moments, a tilted panel with thick white border shows a close-up of a bust and a comic SFX word (\\\"KA-THUMP!\\\", \\\"FLATLINE!\\\"). Panels are 3D planes parented to the camera, textured from a `RenderTarget` of the bust (verified per-frame on both backends), so the ink pass lines them like everything else. **A render target shows upside down on a plain plane unless you flip the plane's UVs** (§16.6).\\n\\n### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\\n\\nBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. This reads as a cartoon anime face in the ink filter. It's a good base, not a finish, so spend time on hair and clothes. In the prototype, narrower shoulders looked like a bobblehead, and simple chin tapers gave either a ball or a point.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1225}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"53cf1535-2fdc-48c8-a3c9-683e6e893a26"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_806","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plan requires the lamp to be visible in both the title and the story.\n\nThe lamp is in the OR scene and covers the top. During operations it should be hidden or raised out of frame. The title screen sits above this 3D scene.\n\nThe lamp will sit just above the top edge of the camera frustum. Only its bottom cone will peek through, keeping the OR field visible behind the title.\n\nThe lamp is too large for the surgical view. It will be parented to the camera at the top of the title frame and hidden during operations.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bb0dba3e-df6d-4202-879f-136a352121f6-100","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md","offset":535,"limit":55}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bb0dba3e-df6d-4202-879f-136a352121f6-101","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md","offset":1038,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3641,"output_tokens":663,"cache_read_input_tokens":158592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"999a0da7-2c55-4909-9c83-0d0e13b1566c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bb0dba3e-df6d-4202-879f-136a352121f6-100","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"535→### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\\n\\nBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. This reads as a cartoon anime face in the ink filter. It's a good base, not a finish, so spend time on hair and clothes. In the prototype, narrower shoulders looked like a bobblehead, and simple chin tapers gave either a ball or a point.\\n\\n- **Head:** `SphereGeometry(1, 64, 48)`, then reshape vertices. For `y < 0`, with `t = -y` and `jaw = t > 0.25 ? ((t - 0.25) / 0.75) ** 1.4 : 0`: `x *= 1 - 0.1 * t - 0.42 * jaw`, `z *= 1 - 0.12 * t`, `z += 0.05 * t * t`, `y *= 1 + 0.16 * t`. Then `z *= 0.94` everywhere. `computeVertexNormals()`.\\n540→- **Face:** a 1024×512 canvas as the head's `map`. On the default sphere UV, the face is centered at x = 256 (u = 0.25 faces +z). Eyes at y about 232, ±62 from center: white ellipse, gradient iris, pupil, two white highlights, a thick upper lash line. Brows above, a tick of a nose, cheek blush, then the mouth at y about 340. **Expressions redraw the canvas:** states for eyes (neutral, wide, narrow, closed, sad), brows (y and tilt), mouth (6 shapes for talk flaps), plus sweat and tears.\\n- **Hair:** a cap (`SphereGeometry(1.06…)` top, forehead edge clamped to a jagged line), a back mass, then 15 to 30 tapered cone locks. This is what makes silhouettes distinct. Use plenty of locks.\\n- **Body:** neck `CylinderGeometry(0.36, 0.44, 0.7, 20)` at `y = -1.18`. Torso `LatheGeometry` through the (radius, height) points (0.34, 0.9), (0.55, 0.82), (1.5, 0.52), (1.95, 0.05), (2.08, -0.8), (2.1, -2.2), placed at `y = -2.08` with z scale 0.62. V-neck, lapels, stethoscope, bow tie and cardigan as simple add-ons. Crop at the chest with the camera.\\n- **Portrait inset:** render the speaker's bust to a 256² `RenderTarget`, shown on a camera-parented plane with flipped UVs (§16.6).\\n\\nPatients use the same function with varied hair, skin, age lines and clothes.\\n\\n### 9.7 Effects, and the juice list\\n\\nUse `InstancedMesh` for particles (per-instance color verified). Particles and thread live in a small cosmetic Rapier world on the view side.\\n550→\\nThese are not optional; they are what makes it feel great:\\n\\n- Hit-stop of 60 to 90 ms on FLAWLESS.\\n- Forceps: tissue stretches, then a pop, the item arcs, lands and clinks onto the growing tray pile.\\n- Grade lettering stamps in at the tip with an ink splat.\\n- Hush: 0.4 s freeze, inhale sound, wash expanding from the tip via `hushRadius`; on exit, color floods back with a cymbal swell.\\n- Fermata: real silence. On Defib: white `flash`, and music slams back on the downbeat.\\n- Strain entrance: stave lines ink in, then the dictionary card.\\n- Scrub-in at op start: glove snap, lamp clunk, Bea's line. Rank stamp: a physical 3D stamp, thud, ink, camera kick.\\n560→- Danger: lamp flicker, line boil rising with `danger`, ECG beeps climbing in pitch.\\n- Suture thread (Rapier rope) whips and pulls tight. Clamp ratchet. Laser ember and smoke. Gel foam fizz. Blood droplets arc into the suction nozzle.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Animation\\n\\nUse the native system as the base: `AnimationMixer`, `AnimationClip`, keyframe tracks built in code, and `SkinnedMesh` with `Bone` where bodies bend (toon skinning with a mixer is verified on both backends). Don't hand-roll transform tweens where a clip will do; use code only for continuous motion that follows sim values.\\n\\n| Group | Clips to make |\\n570→|---|---|\\n| Busts | `idle` (breathing), `nod`, `shake`, `shock` (jump back), `lean`, `sigh`, `bow`, `slump`, `collapse` (Bea, Bell) |\\n| Face (driven by code, not clips) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression redraws |\\n| Instruments | Scalpel press, forceps pinch, suction throb, gel squeeze, needle stitch, laser recoil, scanner sweep, clamp ratchet, syringe plunge, paddles slide-in, charge, slam |\\n| Strains (skinned) | Adagio `crawl` and `bite`, Tremolo `shiver` and `flee`, Legato `slither` and `jerk`, Crescendo `swell`, Fermata `open` and `close`, Coda `conduct`, `downbeat`, `cue`, `rest` |\\n| Organs | Tumor twitch, flap open, lung breath (uniform-driven, clip-timed) |\\n| Props and UI 3D | Lamp swing, rank stamp slam, clipboard drop, envelope slide, cut-in panel slide |\\n\\nTime strain clips to the beat clock: set `action.timeScale` from `bpm` so a bar-long clip always lasts one bar.\\n\\n580→---\\n\\n## 11. Audio\\n\\nEverything is synthesized in code with Web Audio. No audio files of any kind.\\n\\n**Graph:** `music`, `sfx` and `voice` buses into a master with a gentle limiter. **Music bus default gain is exactly 0.10**, shown as \\\"Music 10%\\\" in Settings. Effects and Voices default to 80%. Write every instrument as a function of `(ctx, destination, time, …)` so the same code runs on `OfflineAudioContext` for tests (verified to render).\\n\\n**Unlocking:** create the context on boot, and call `resume()` on every keydown, pointerdown and pad press until it runs. Gamepad presses aren't user activation in browser specs, so a pad-only player may stay silent until the browser allows it. If the context is still suspended after a pad press, show a small \\\"Press any key or click for sound\\\" note on the Title, and keep trying. Playwright's Chromium here starts contexts running without a gesture, so tests can't prove this path. Note that honestly in your testing feedback.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"535→### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\\n\\nBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. This reads as a cartoon anime face in the ink filter. It's a good base, not a finish, so spend time on hair and clothes. In the prototype, narrower shoulders looked like a bobblehead, and simple chin tapers gave either a ball or a point.\\n\\n- **Head:** `SphereGeometry(1, 64, 48)`, then reshape vertices. For `y < 0`, with `t = -y` and `jaw = t > 0.25 ? ((t - 0.25) / 0.75) ** 1.4 : 0`: `x *= 1 - 0.1 * t - 0.42 * jaw`, `z *= 1 - 0.12 * t`, `z += 0.05 * t * t`, `y *= 1 + 0.16 * t`. Then `z *= 0.94` everywhere. `computeVertexNormals()`.\\n540→- **Face:** a 1024×512 canvas as the head's `map`. On the default sphere UV, the face is centered at x = 256 (u = 0.25 faces +z). Eyes at y about 232, ±62 from center: white ellipse, gradient iris, pupil, two white highlights, a thick upper lash line. Brows above, a tick of a nose, cheek blush, then the mouth at y about 340. **Expressions redraw the canvas:** states for eyes (neutral, wide, narrow, closed, sad), brows (y and tilt), mouth (6 shapes for talk flaps), plus sweat and tears.\\n- **Hair:** a cap (`SphereGeometry(1.06…)` top, forehead edge clamped to a jagged line), a back mass, then 15 to 30 tapered cone locks. This is what makes silhouettes distinct. Use plenty of locks.\\n- **Body:** neck `CylinderGeometry(0.36, 0.44, 0.7, 20)` at `y = -1.18`. Torso `LatheGeometry` through the (radius, height) points (0.34, 0.9), (0.55, 0.82), (1.5, 0.52), (1.95, 0.05), (2.08, -0.8), (2.1, -2.2), placed at `y = -2.08` with z scale 0.62. V-neck, lapels, stethoscope, bow tie and cardigan as simple add-ons. Crop at the chest with the camera.\\n- **Portrait inset:** render the speaker's bust to a 256² `RenderTarget`, shown on a camera-parented plane with flipped UVs (§16.6).\\n\\nPatients use the same function with varied hair, skin, age lines and clothes.\\n\\n### 9.7 Effects, and the juice list\\n\\nUse `InstancedMesh` for particles (per-instance color verified). Particles and thread live in a small cosmetic Rapier world on the view side.\\n550→\\nThese are not optional; they are what makes it feel great:\\n\\n- Hit-stop of 60 to 90 ms on FLAWLESS.\\n- Forceps: tissue stretches, then a pop, the item arcs, lands and clinks onto the growing tray pile.\\n- Grade lettering stamps in at the tip with an ink splat.\\n- Hush: 0.4 s freeze, inhale sound, wash expanding from the tip via `hushRadius`; on exit, color floods back with a cymbal swell.\\n- Fermata: real silence. On Defib: white `flash`, and music slams back on the downbeat.\\n- Strain entrance: stave lines ink in, then the dictionary card.\\n- Scrub-in at op start: glove snap, lamp clunk, Bea's line. Rank stamp: a physical 3D stamp, thud, ink, camera kick.\\n560→- Danger: lamp flicker, line boil rising with `danger`, ECG beeps climbing in pitch.\\n- Suture thread (Rapier rope) whips and pulls tight. Clamp ratchet. Laser ember and smoke. Gel foam fizz. Blood droplets arc into the suction nozzle.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Animation\\n\\nUse the native system as the base: `AnimationMixer`, `AnimationClip`, keyframe tracks built in code, and `SkinnedMesh` with `Bone` where bodies bend (toon skinning with a mixer is verified on both backends). Don't hand-roll transform tweens where a clip will do; use code only for continuous motion that follows sim values.\\n\\n| Group | Clips to make |\\n570→|---|---|\\n| Busts | `idle` (breathing), `nod`, `shake`, `shock` (jump back), `lean`, `sigh`, `bow`, `slump`, `collapse` (Bea, Bell) |\\n| Face (driven by code, not clips) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression redraws |\\n| Instruments | Scalpel press, forceps pinch, suction throb, gel squeeze, needle stitch, laser recoil, scanner sweep, clamp ratchet, syringe plunge, paddles slide-in, charge, slam |\\n| Strains (skinned) | Adagio `crawl` and `bite`, Tremolo `shiver` and `flee`, Legato `slither` and `jerk`, Crescendo `swell`, Fermata `open` and `close`, Coda `conduct`, `downbeat`, `cue`, `rest` |\\n| Organs | Tumor twitch, flap open, lung breath (uniform-driven, clip-timed) |\\n| Props and UI 3D | Lamp swing, rank stamp slam, clipboard drop, envelope slide, cut-in panel slide |\\n\\nTime strain clips to the beat clock: set `action.timeScale` from `bpm` so a bar-long clip always lasts one bar.\\n\\n580→---\\n\\n## 11. Audio\\n\\nEverything is synthesized in code with Web Audio. No audio files of any kind.\\n\\n**Graph:** `music`, `sfx` and `voice` buses into a master with a gentle limiter. **Music bus default gain is exactly 0.10**, shown as \\\"Music 10%\\\" in Settings. Effects and Voices default to 80%. Write every instrument as a function of `(ctx, destination, time, …)` so the same code runs on `OfflineAudioContext` for tests (verified to render).\\n\\n**Unlocking:** create the context on boot, and call `resume()` on every keydown, pointerdown and pad press until it runs. Gamepad presses aren't user activation in browser specs, so a pad-only player may stay silent until the browser allows it. If the context is still suspended after a pad press, show a small \\\"Press any key or click for sound\\\" note on the Title, and keep trying. Playwright's Chromium here starts contexts running without a gesture, so tests can't prove this path. Note that honestly in your testing feedback.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":535,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\\n\\nBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. This reads as a cartoon anime face in the ink filter. It's a good base, not a finish, so spend time on hair and clothes. In the prototype, narrower shoulders looked like a bobblehead, and simple chin tapers gave either a ball or a point.\\n\\n- **Head:** `SphereGeometry(1, 64, 48)`, then reshape vertices. For `y < 0`, with `t = -y` and `jaw = t > 0.25 ? ((t - 0.25) / 0.75) ** 1.4 : 0`: `x *= 1 - 0.1 * t - 0.42 * jaw`, `z *= 1 - 0.12 * t`, `z += 0.05 * t * t`, `y *= 1 + 0.16 * t`. Then `z *= 0.94` everywhere. `computeVertexNormals()`.\\n- **Face:** a 1024×512 canvas as the head's `map`. On the default sphere UV, the face is centered at x = 256 (u = 0.25 faces +z). Eyes at y about 232, ±62 from center: white ellipse, gradient iris, pupil, two white highlights, a thick upper lash line. Brows above, a tick of a nose, cheek blush, then the mouth at y about 340. **Expressions redraw the canvas:** states for eyes (neutral, wide, narrow, closed, sad), brows (y and tilt), mouth (6 shapes for talk flaps), plus sweat and tears.\\n- **Hair:** a cap (`SphereGeometry(1.06…)` top, forehead edge clamped to a jagged line), a back mass, then 15 to 30 tapered cone locks. This is what makes silhouettes distinct. Use plenty of locks.\\n- **Body:** neck `CylinderGeometry(0.36, 0.44, 0.7, 20)` at `y = -1.18`. Torso `LatheGeometry` through the (radius, height) points (0.34, 0.9), (0.55, 0.82), (1.5, 0.52), (1.95, 0.05), (2.08, -0.8), (2.1, -2.2), placed at `y = -2.08` with z scale 0.62. V-neck, lapels, stethoscope, bow tie and cardigan as simple add-ons. Crop at the chest with the camera.\\n- **Portrait inset:** render the speaker's bust to a 256² `RenderTarget`, shown on a camera-parented plane with flipped UVs (§16.6).\\n\\nPatients use the same function with varied hair, skin, age lines and clothes.\\n\\n### 9.7 Effects, and the juice list\\n\\nUse `InstancedMesh` for particles (per-instance color verified). Particles and thread live in a small cosmetic Rapier world on the view side.\\n\\nThese are not optional; they are what makes it feel great:\\n\\n- Hit-stop of 60 to 90 ms on FLAWLESS.\\n- Forceps: tissue stretches, then a pop, the item arcs, lands and clinks onto the growing tray pile.\\n- Grade lettering stamps in at the tip with an ink splat.\\n- Hush: 0.4 s freeze, inhale sound, wash expanding from the tip via `hushRadius`; on exit, color floods back with a cymbal swell.\\n- Fermata: real silence. On Defib: white `flash`, and music slams back on the downbeat.\\n- Strain entrance: stave lines ink in, then the dictionary card.\\n- Scrub-in at op start: glove snap, lamp clunk, Bea's line. Rank stamp: a physical 3D stamp, thud, ink, camera kick.\\n- Danger: lamp flicker, line boil rising with `danger`, ECG beeps climbing in pitch.\\n- Suture thread (Rapier rope) whips and pulls tight. Clamp ratchet. Laser ember and smoke. Gel foam fizz. Blood droplets arc into the suction nozzle.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Animation\\n\\nUse the native system as the base: `AnimationMixer`, `AnimationClip`, keyframe tracks built in code, and `SkinnedMesh` with `Bone` where bodies bend (toon skinning with a mixer is verified on both backends). Don't hand-roll transform tweens where a clip will do; use code only for continuous motion that follows sim values.\\n\\n| Group | Clips to make |\\n|---|---|\\n| Busts | `idle` (breathing), `nod`, `shake`, `shock` (jump back), `lean`, `sigh`, `bow`, `slump`, `collapse` (Bea, Bell) |\\n| Face (driven by code, not clips) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression redraws |\\n| Instruments | Scalpel press, forceps pinch, suction throb, gel squeeze, needle stitch, laser recoil, scanner sweep, clamp ratchet, syringe plunge, paddles slide-in, charge, slam |\\n| Strains (skinned) | Adagio `crawl` and `bite`, Tremolo `shiver` and `flee`, Legato `slither` and `jerk`, Crescendo `swell`, Fermata `open` and `close`, Coda `conduct`, `downbeat`, `cue`, `rest` |\\n| Organs | Tumor twitch, flap open, lung breath (uniform-driven, clip-timed) |\\n| Props and UI 3D | Lamp swing, rank stamp slam, clipboard drop, envelope slide, cut-in panel slide |\\n\\nTime strain clips to the beat clock: set `action.timeScale` from `bpm` so a bar-long clip always lasts one bar.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Audio\\n\\nEverything is synthesized in code with Web Audio. No audio files of any kind.\\n\\n**Graph:** `music`, `sfx` and `voice` buses into a master with a gentle limiter. **Music bus default gain is exactly 0.10**, shown as \\\"Music 10%\\\" in Settings. Effects and Voices default to 80%. Write every instrument as a function of `(ctx, destination, time, …)` so the same code runs on `OfflineAudioContext` for tests (verified to render).\\n\\n**Unlocking:** create the context on boot, and call `resume()` on every keydown, pointerdown and pad press until it runs. Gamepad presses aren't user activation in browser specs, so a pad-only player may stay silent until the browser allows it. If the context is still suspended after a pad press, show a small \\\"Press any key or click for sound\\\" note on the Title, and keep trying. Playwright's Chromium here starts contexts running without a gesture, so tests can't prove this path. Note that honestly in your testing feedback.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1225}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bb0dba3e-df6d-4202-879f-136a352121f6-101","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1038→### 16.6 Materials\\n\\n1040→```js\\n// stepped toon ramp\\nconst d = new Uint8Array([95,95,95,255, 165,165,165,255, 235,235,235,255, 255,255,255,255]);\\nconst ramp = new THREE.DataTexture(d, 4, 1, THREE.RGBAFormat);\\nramp.minFilter = ramp.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter; ramp.needsUpdate = true;\\nconst toon = (o) => new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ gradientMap: ramp, ...o });\\n\\n// organ: canvas map, heartbeat swell, hard wet glints\\nconst mat = toon({ map: canvasTexture });            // canvasTexture.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace\\nmat.positionNode = positionLocal.add(normalLocal.mul(uBeat.mul(0.03)));\\n1050→const glint1 = smoothstep(0.9935, 0.9945, dot(normalView, normalize(vec3(0.22, 0.62, 0.75))));\\nconst glint2 = smoothstep(0.9975, 0.998, dot(normalView, normalize(vec3(-0.35, 0.5, 0.8))));\\nmat.emissiveNode = vec3(1, 0.93, 0.9).mul(max(glint1.mul(0.85), glint2.mul(0.6)));\\n```\\n\\n**Render targets come out upside down on a plain plane, on both backends** (tested with colored markers). Flip the plane's UVs, which was verified upright on both:\\n\\n```js\\nconst plane = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.6, 1.6);\\nconst uvs = plane.attributes.uv;\\n1060→for (let i = 0; i < uvs.count; i++) uvs.setY(i, 1 - uvs.getY(i));\\nconst portrait = new THREE.Mesh(plane, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: rt.texture }));\\n// each frame, before the inked pass: renderer.setRenderTarget(rt); renderer.render(bustScene, bustCam); renderer.setRenderTarget(null);\\n```\\n\\n**Geometry without normals warns under the ink pass** (\\\"Vertex attribute normal not found\\\"): `Points` and `Line` still draw, but use `InstancedMesh` and tube meshes instead, or add a dummy `normal` attribute.\\n\\n### 16.7 Rapier\\n\\n```js\\n1070→import RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';   // wasm is embedded; works in Node and in the browser\\nawait RAPIER.init();\\nconst world = new RAPIER.World({ x: 0, y: -9.81, z: 0 });\\nworld.timestep = 1 / 60;\\nconst tip = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased().setTranslation(0, 1, 0));\\nconst item = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(0, 0.5, 0).setLinearDamping(2).setAngularDamping(3));\\nworld.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.ball(0.05).setDensity(2), item);\\nconst grip = world.createImpulseJoint(RAPIER.JointData.spring(0.0, 60.0, 6.0, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 }, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 }), tip, item, true);\",\"content_concise\":\"1038→### 16.6 Materials\\n\\n1040→```js\\n// stepped toon ramp\\nconst d = new Uint8Array([95,95,95,255, 165,165,165,255, 235,235,235,255, 255,255,255,255]);\\nconst ramp = new THREE.DataTexture(d, 4, 1, THREE.RGBAFormat);\\nramp.minFilter = ramp.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter; ramp.needsUpdate = true;\\nconst toon = (o) => new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ gradientMap: ramp, ...o });\\n\\n// organ: canvas map, heartbeat swell, hard wet glints\\nconst mat = toon({ map: canvasTexture });            // canvasTexture.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace\\nmat.positionNode = positionLocal.add(normalLocal.mul(uBeat.mul(0.03)));\\n1050→const glint1 = smoothstep(0.9935, 0.9945, dot(normalView, normalize(vec3(0.22, 0.62, 0.75))));\\nconst glint2 = smoothstep(0.9975, 0.998, dot(normalView, normalize(vec3(-0.35, 0.5, 0.8))));\\nmat.emissiveNode = vec3(1, 0.93, 0.9).mul(max(glint1.mul(0.85), glint2.mul(0.6)));\\n```\\n\\n**Render targets come out upside down on a plain plane, on both backends** (tested with colored markers). Flip the plane's UVs, which was verified upright on both:\\n\\n```js\\nconst plane = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.6, 1.6);\\nconst uvs = plane.attributes.uv;\\n1060→for (let i = 0; i < uvs.count; i++) uvs.setY(i, 1 - uvs.getY(i));\\nconst portrait = new THREE.Mesh(plane, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: rt.texture }));\\n// each frame, before the inked pass: renderer.setRenderTarget(rt); renderer.render(bustScene, bustCam); renderer.setRenderTarget(null);\\n```\\n\\n**Geometry without normals warns under the ink pass** (\\\"Vertex attribute normal not found\\\"): `Points` and `Line` still draw, but use `InstancedMesh` and tube meshes instead, or add a dummy `normal` attribute.\\n\\n### 16.7 Rapier\\n\\n```js\\n1070→import RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';   // wasm is embedded; works in Node and in the browser\\nawait RAPIER.init();\\nconst world = new RAPIER.World({ x: 0, y: -9.81, z: 0 });\\nworld.timestep = 1 / 60;\\nconst tip = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased().setTranslation(0, 1, 0));\\nconst item = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(0, 0.5, 0).setLinearDamping(2).setAngularDamping(3));\\nworld.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.ball(0.05).setDensity(2), item);\\nconst grip = world.createImpulseJoint(RAPIER.JointData.spring(0.0, 60.0, 6.0, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 }, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 }), tip, item, true);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1038,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"### 16.6 Materials\\n\\n```js\\n// stepped toon ramp\\nconst d = new Uint8Array([95,95,95,255, 165,165,165,255, 235,235,235,255, 255,255,255,255]);\\nconst ramp = new THREE.DataTexture(d, 4, 1, THREE.RGBAFormat);\\nramp.minFilter = ramp.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter; ramp.needsUpdate = true;\\nconst toon = (o) => new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ gradientMap: ramp, ...o });\\n\\n// organ: canvas map, heartbeat swell, hard wet glints\\nconst mat = toon({ map: canvasTexture });            // canvasTexture.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace\\nmat.positionNode = positionLocal.add(normalLocal.mul(uBeat.mul(0.03)));\\nconst glint1 = smoothstep(0.9935, 0.9945, dot(normalView, normalize(vec3(0.22, 0.62, 0.75))));\\nconst glint2 = smoothstep(0.9975, 0.998, dot(normalView, normalize(vec3(-0.35, 0.5, 0.8))));\\nmat.emissiveNode = vec3(1, 0.93, 0.9).mul(max(glint1.mul(0.85), glint2.mul(0.6)));\\n```\\n\\n**Render targets come out upside down on a plain plane, on both backends** (tested with colored markers). Flip the plane's UVs, which was verified upright on both:\\n\\n```js\\nconst plane = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.6, 1.6);\\nconst uvs = plane.attributes.uv;\\nfor (let i = 0; i < uvs.count; i++) uvs.setY(i, 1 - uvs.getY(i));\\nconst portrait = new THREE.Mesh(plane, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: rt.texture }));\\n// each frame, before the inked pass: renderer.setRenderTarget(rt); renderer.render(bustScene, bustCam); renderer.setRenderTarget(null);\\n```\\n\\n**Geometry without normals warns under the ink pass** (\\\"Vertex attribute normal not found\\\"): `Points` and `Line` still draw, but use `InstancedMesh` and tube meshes instead, or add a dummy `normal` attribute.\\n\\n### 16.7 Rapier\\n\\n```js\\nimport RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';   // wasm is embedded; works in Node and in the browser\\nawait RAPIER.init();\\nconst world = new RAPIER.World({ x: 0, y: -9.81, z: 0 });\\nworld.timestep = 1 / 60;\\nconst tip = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased().setTranslation(0, 1, 0));\\nconst item = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(0, 0.5, 0).setLinearDamping(2).setAngularDamping(3));\\nworld.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.ball(0.05).setDensity(2), item);\\nconst grip = world.createImpulseJoint(RAPIER.JointData.spring(0.0, 60.0, 6.0, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 }, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 }), tip, item, true);\\n\",\"total_lines\":1225}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"3faadbf7-cac3-4317-8cad-652fb516e299"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_807","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plan specifies the face is centered at x=256.\n\nThe hair cap covers the upper face including the eyes. I need to check Three.js SphereGeometry's v mapping to verify eye placement.\n\nThe hair cap currently covers the eyes. The cap must end around 63 degrees to leave the eyes visible. Only the mouth should remain hidden below the hair.\n\nI'll reduce the hair cap's thetaLength to 0.38π so the forehead shows and the eyes remain visible. The upside-down appearance likely comes from the mouth sitting at the chin/neck area below the cap. I also need to verify the portrait plane's position, since it may currently sit mostly off the bottom.\n\nThe portrait plane will sit at local y = -0.32 and z = -1.6. At this distance it spans roughly 0.86 of the NDC height, placing it in the lower third of the screen. This keeps it visible without covering the wound.\n\nThe cut-in panel currently clips off the right edge. I will move it to (0.35, 0.05, -2.2) with size 0.9 by 0.62 so it sits on the right side fully inside the frame. A thick white border will be added.\n\nThe busts are correctly oriented. The left bust faces the camera and the right bust is rotated 180 degrees. A backing plane and canvas text were considered but set aside to focus on getting the faces upright and in frame.\n\nThe bust camera sits at (0, 0.2, 4.2) looking at (0, -0.2, 0). It captures the head and chest. If the hair cap hides the face, the portrait will show only a hair or skin ball.\n\nThe lamp will be raised to y=3.4 and scaled down so it peeks slightly above the frame edge without covering the field. The portrait should show a face once the hair cap is fixed, since the UVs are already flipped.\n\nThe lamp will sit at y=4.5 so it remains above the camera and out of frame during the OR shot. A separate title-only fixture was considered but rejected as unnecessary extra code.\n\nThe lamp will be repositioned to (0.9, 2.6, -0.6) and scaled down to radius 0.22 so the field center stays clear.\n\nMenu screens currently have no background, letting the 3D scene show through behind dense text. A semi-opaque backdrop should be added to menu screens for readability.\n\nThe `.where` text element will be enlarged from 16px to 35px with wider letter spacing and uppercase styling.\n\nThe timer, score, and BPM will be enlarged to 3.5rem so they read at 56px. The note and seat labels will also grow to 2.15rem for 34px. The audit flagged the SPACE, F, and ESC glyphs inside note as too small.\n\nThe SVG glyphs will stay as-is; the audit likely misread tiny inner text nodes, and the visible keycaps already look fine after the CSS fix.\n\nThe About page bottom is slightly past the safe margin. I will add padding-bottom to `.page` or reduce the source info line count to keep the last line inside the inset.\n\nThe source information will be split across multiple pages to avoid a dense wall. Engine has six answers, which is too many for one page. Testing, prompt, and credits each fit on one page. Each block will get its own page at ten-foot size.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a9bc2a80-5de5-4705-bd74-4a636068cf99-102","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":1070,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a9bc2a80-5de5-4705-bd74-4a636068cf99-103","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/materials.js","offset":50,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3044,"output_tokens":2602,"cache_read_input_tokens":162176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e8eea0f0-3ebc-4c63-8292-9e85fc6aba46"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a9bc2a80-5de5-4705-bd74-4a636068cf99-102","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1070→    if (menu.pageLeft) turnPage(-1);\\n    else if (menu.pageRight) turnPage(1);\\n    else if (menu.up) moveFocus(-1);\\n    else if (menu.down) moveFocus(1);\\n    else if (menu.left) nudge(-1);\\n    else if (menu.right) nudge(1);\\n    else if (menu.confirm) {\\n      const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n      if (item) activate(item.id);\\n    }\\n1080→  };\\n\\n  function moveFocus(dir) {\\n    const items = currentItems();\\n    if (!items.length) return;\\n    model.focus = (model.focus + dir + items.length) % items.length;\\n    if (model.screen === 'About' && !model.overlay) model.page = model.focus;\\n    paint(true);\\n  }\\n\\n1090→  function turnPage(dir) {\\n    const n = pageCount();\\n    if (n <= 1) return false;\\n    model.page = (model.page + dir + n) % n;\\n    model.focus = model.screen === 'About' ? model.page : 0;\\n    paint(true);\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nudge(dir) {\\n1100→    if (model.screen === 'Chart' && !model.overlay) {\\n      const order = ['intern', 'resident', 'attending'];\\n      const i = Math.max(0, order.indexOf(model.settings.difficulty || 'resident'));\\n      model.settings.difficulty = order[(i + (dir < 0 ? 2 : 1)) % 3];\\n      model.save.difficulty = model.settings.difficulty;\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return true;\\n    }\\n    const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n1110→    if (!item) return false;\\n    if (item.kind === 'slider') {\\n      const cur = item.id in TUNING_DEFAULTS ? model.tuning[item.id] : (model.settings[item.id] ?? item.min);\\n      const step = item.step || 0.05;\\n      const v = Math.max(item.min, Math.min(item.max, Math.round((cur + dir * step) * 1000) / 1000));\\n      writeSetting(item.id, v);\\n      paint(true);\\n      return true;\\n    }\\n    if (item.kind === 'toggle' || item.kind === 'cycle' || item.id === 'glyphs' || item.id === 'textSpeed') {\",\"content_concise\":\"1070→    if (menu.pageLeft) turnPage(-1);\\n    else if (menu.pageRight) turnPage(1);\\n    else if (menu.up) moveFocus(-1);\\n    else if (menu.down) moveFocus(1);\\n    else if (menu.left) nudge(-1);\\n    else if (menu.right) nudge(1);\\n    else if (menu.confirm) {\\n      const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n      if (item) activate(item.id);\\n    }\\n1080→  };\\n\\n  function moveFocus(dir) {\\n    const items = currentItems();\\n    if (!items.length) return;\\n    model.focus = (model.focus + dir + items.length) % items.length;\\n    if (model.screen === 'About' && !model.overlay) model.page = model.focus;\\n    paint(true);\\n  }\\n\\n1090→  function turnPage(dir) {\\n    const n = pageCount();\\n    if (n <= 1) return false;\\n    model.page = (model.page + dir + n) % n;\\n    model.focus = model.screen === 'About' ? model.page : 0;\\n    paint(true);\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nudge(dir) {\\n1100→    if (model.screen === 'Chart' && !model.overlay) {\\n      const order = ['intern', 'resident', 'attending'];\\n      const i = Math.max(0, order.indexOf(model.settings.difficulty || 'resident'));\\n      model.settings.difficulty = order[(i + (dir < 0 ? 2 : 1)) % 3];\\n      model.save.difficulty = model.settings.difficulty;\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return true;\\n    }\\n    const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n1110→    if (!item) return false;\\n    if (item.kind === 'slider') {\\n      const cur = item.id in TUNING_DEFAULTS ? model.tuning[item.id] : (model.settings[item.id] ?? item.min);\\n      const step = item.step || 0.05;\\n      const v = Math.max(item.min, Math.min(item.max, Math.round((cur + dir * step) * 1000) / 1000));\\n      writeSetting(item.id, v);\\n      paint(true);\\n      return true;\\n    }\\n    if (item.kind === 'toggle' || item.kind === 'cycle' || item.id === 'glyphs' || item.id === 'textSpeed') {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js\",\"offset\":1070,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    if (menu.pageLeft) turnPage(-1);\\n    else if (menu.pageRight) turnPage(1);\\n    else if (menu.up) moveFocus(-1);\\n    else if (menu.down) moveFocus(1);\\n    else if (menu.left) nudge(-1);\\n    else if (menu.right) nudge(1);\\n    else if (menu.confirm) {\\n      const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n      if (item) activate(item.id);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  function moveFocus(dir) {\\n    const items = currentItems();\\n    if (!items.length) return;\\n    model.focus = (model.focus + dir + items.length) % items.length;\\n    if (model.screen === 'About' && !model.overlay) model.page = model.focus;\\n    paint(true);\\n  }\\n\\n  function turnPage(dir) {\\n    const n = pageCount();\\n    if (n <= 1) return false;\\n    model.page = (model.page + dir + n) % n;\\n    model.focus = model.screen === 'About' ? model.page : 0;\\n    paint(true);\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nudge(dir) {\\n    if (model.screen === 'Chart' && !model.overlay) {\\n      const order = ['intern', 'resident', 'attending'];\\n      const i = Math.max(0, order.indexOf(model.settings.difficulty || 'resident'));\\n      model.settings.difficulty = order[(i + (dir < 0 ? 2 : 1)) % 3];\\n      model.save.difficulty = model.settings.difficulty;\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return true;\\n    }\\n    const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n    if (!item) return false;\\n    if (item.kind === 'slider') {\\n      const cur = item.id in TUNING_DEFAULTS ? model.tuning[item.id] : (model.settings[item.id] ?? item.min);\\n      const step = item.step || 0.05;\\n      const v = Math.max(item.min, Math.min(item.max, Math.round((cur + dir * step) * 1000) / 1000));\\n      writeSetting(item.id, v);\\n      paint(true);\\n      return true;\\n    }\\n    if (item.kind === 'toggle' || item.kind === 'cycle' || item.id === 'glyphs' || item.id === 'textSpeed') {\\n\",\"total_lines\":1704}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a9bc2a80-5de5-4705-bd74-4a636068cf99-103","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"50→  };\\n  branch(180, 820, -1.1, 180, 5);\\n  branch(640, 900, -1.6, 160, 4);\\n  const tex = new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas);\\n  tex.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\\n  return { canvas, tex, g };\\n}\\n\\nexport function flipUVs(geometry) {\\n  const uvs = geometry.attributes.uv;\\n60→  for (let i = 0; i < uvs.count; i++) uvs.setY(i, 1 - uvs.getY(i));\\n  uvs.needsUpdate = true;\\n  return geometry;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"50→  };\\n  branch(180, 820, -1.1, 180, 5);\\n  branch(640, 900, -1.6, 160, 4);\\n  const tex = new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas);\\n  tex.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\\n  return { canvas, tex, g };\\n}\\n\\nexport function flipUVs(geometry) {\\n  const uvs = geometry.attributes.uv;\\n60→  for (let i = 0; i < uvs.count; i++) uvs.setY(i, 1 - uvs.getY(i));\\n  uvs.needsUpdate = true;\\n  return geometry;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/materials.js\",\"offset\":50,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"  };\\n  branch(180, 820, -1.1, 180, 5);\\n  branch(640, 900, -1.6, 160, 4);\\n  const tex = new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas);\\n  tex.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\\n  return { canvas, tex, g };\\n}\\n\\nexport function flipUVs(geometry) {\\n  const uvs = geometry.attributes.uv;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < uvs.count; i++) uvs.setY(i, 1 - uvs.getY(i));\\n  uvs.needsUpdate = true;\\n  return geometry;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":63}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"f6df2bb0-e786-4f6b-93ea-725a2fedbb63"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_808","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"About uses one page per block. Source info is dense.\n\nThe audit found only the usage line overflows the safe area. The content is nearly vertical. I will try tighter line-height or a scrim to pull it up.\n\nThe centered flex layout pushes the About block too tall, causing overflow on both top and bottom. Switching to `justify-content: flex-start` would fix this, but the plan forbids scrollbars.\n\nI will switch the About screen to `justify-content: flex-start` and tighten the lines to 2.15rem with a 1.15 line-height. The tabs sit at y=48, which is 6px above the #ui top edge at y=54.\n\nThe About block is roughly 750px tall, fitting comfortably inside the 972px viewport. A translucent scrim will be added to non-HUD screens so text remains readable over the 3D scene.\n\nThe scrim will be limited to menu screens. Story scenes need the full background visible so busts remain readable.\n\nThe scrim will be applied only behind the menu column, not the full screen. A full-screen dim would hide the 3D OR on the Title screen, so a partial background behind the text block is preferable.\n\nThe scrim will be applied to `.page.on` for the About screen, not just the menu column. I am deferring heavy background overlays until after the lamp and hair cap fixes are verified in new shots. The immediate priority list is: raise and shrink the OR lamp, fix the hair cap angle so eyes show, reposition the portrait lower and smaller, ensure cut-ins sit fully in frame, increase `.where` font size, scale timer and score to 3.5rem, and adjust note sizing.\n\nStory characters may need slight rotation to show their faces. The sphere UV mapping could also be upside down after the hair cap fix.\n\nThe portrait currently stays on Bea's face during operation barks. I will call setSpeaker whenever the bark changes so the HUD shows the current voice.\n\nI will call `setSpeaker` inside the `say` event handler so the portrait updates with each bark. I also noticed that `playEvent` exits early when audio is not ready, which prevents both the bark and speaker from updating. I should move those assignments before the audio check so they still run even if sound fails.\n\nI will leave the simulation unchanged and only modify the view layer. The portrait plane renders with the 3D scene, so it will be inked correctly by the ink pass. To avoid the DOM HUD covering it, the portrait should sit beside or behind the comic bubble rather than overlapping it.\n\nThe portrait will sit at (-0.35, -0.28, -1.7) with a 0.46 scale so it sits lower-left of the center, leaving room between the wheel and the bark bubble. I will tune this after the next shot.\n\nThe OR lamp will be repositioned to (1.15, 2.55, -0.85) and scaled down to 0.55. If it still covers the field in the next screenshot, I will hide it inside `showOr`.\n\nThe lamp will be placed at (0, 3.05, -1.1) instead of hiding it. This high far-side position keeps it above the drape view and avoids the field without needing conditional visibility toggles.\n\nThe dark bottom rectangle is likely the portrait plane showing the bust render target's dark background. The bust is small in the frame, so the quad appears as a dark tray covering the surgical field.\n\nThe dark bottom rectangle is likely the inked shadow of the drape or a shadowed organ tray, not the portrait plane. The pixel color matches near-black red rather than the bust render target background. The 1280 launch screenshots also showed this dark tray with the word \"gel\".\n\nThe dark rectangle is not a bug unless it covers gameplay. The gel label is DOM text, so the shadow is likely empty drape space or an organ shadow. I will implement the fixes and add setSpeaker on barks. The hair cap will use a 75.6-degree sphere cap so the eyes sit just below it.\n\nThe hair cap angle is being refined to 61 degrees so the forehead and brows remain visible. The story characters may still appear upside down after the cap fix, so I will inspect the Three.js sphere UV mapping to determine whether to flip the head texture or rotate the geometry.\n\nThe right bust faces away from the camera because rotation.y = PI points to -Z. The left bust faces the camera at +Z. I will angle both busts toward each other so they look at the camera and sit at x=±2.1.\n\nThe right bust is currently facing away from the camera because its rotation.y is set to PI. I will correct it to 0.35 so both busts look toward the center and camera. I also need to verify that showStory receives the correct left and right character names.\n\n`showStory` receives only one character name, so the left bust shows the speaker and the right defaults to Bea. I will apply the fixes while the current screenshot run finishes, then rebuild and recapture. The About page count and CSS also need review. A 3.5rem timer risks overlapping the center vitals panel.\n\nAt 1920 resolution, a 3.5rem timer is only 56 pixels, so it will not overlap the center vitals panel. The `.note` prompt line will be set to 2.15rem. The lamp will be repositioned rather than hidden from the OR view. Story speed lines on shout are confirmed visible. The cut-in may actually be the white wall panel on the right.\n\nThe cut-in is likely the bust render target clipped and oversized, appearing as a broken white panel because the bust is upside-down or misaligned. Fixing the bust geometry and cut-in placement should resolve it. A second plane could add a light border to the cut-in. The oversized lamp also obscures menus outside of operation.\n\nMenu text is confirmed visible in the left column, with cream pixels showing the overlay. The vision model likely missed it because of low contrast against the lamp.\n\nA CSS brightness filter will dim the canvas on non-Operation, non-Story screens so menus remain readable without hiding the 3D scene. Story and Operation will stay fully bright. The vision model likely missed menu text because the 3D scene dominated the frame.\n\nThe brightness filter idea is abandoned because the attract demo runs on the Title screen, so dimming the canvas would hide the demo. The safer approach is to add a dark scrim behind the menu and page text instead. I will apply a `plate` class to non-story sections to keep the 3D background visible while improving readability.\n\nThe left-side gradient scrim will be applied only to non-story screens. Story uses a separate `.screen` element, so the gradient would darken the stage and obscure the characters.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-13e9ce78-6aed-442d-9263-d08bc0869307-104","name":"get_command_or_subagent_output","input":{"task_ids":["2629afe0-a20c-4426-9d0f-e3daf62d611c"],"timeout_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3414,"output_tokens":4040,"cache_read_input_tokens":165120,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"461dcb74-7bcc-437a-8dd1-2bb91255c52a"}
