{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_809","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The capture succeeded for almost all shots. It failed on the session card because the iframe was not ready.\n\nI will inspect op-calm, story, hush, and strain-adagio to verify the lamp and strain visibility. The BPM \"72\" at y=323 is mid-upper screen, not top HUD.\n\nThe BPM at y=323 sits inside the `.ecg-line` div nested below `.vitals`. The top timer is at y=92. This explains why the BPM is mid-screen while the vitals remain higher.\n\nThe BPM at y=323 conflicts with the HUD grid layout. The first row should place it near 161px, not 323px. This suggests the \"72\" text node may not actually be the BPM counter.\n\nThe flex layout should not wrap, so the center column is not pushed down by text size. A duplicate \"72\" in the 3D scene is unlikely.\n\nThe audit confirms the BPM is 2.4rem, or 38px. The vitals readout sits near the top of the pale shape, while the BPM text appears in the middle-right of the field. This confirms a layout bug: the center HUD stack is either too tall or the BPM has dropped into the game area.\n\nThe \"72\" text is only 256 pixels wide, which is far too large for a single digit. This means the `p.timer` element itself is stretching horizontally as a block, and its parent center div is likely expanding to accommodate it. The `.ecg-line` div is only 0.4rem tall, so the canvas or animation inside it may be forcing that parent to grow unexpectedly.\n\nThe `.ecg-line` div also carries the `#ecg` ID, so its height is set to 3.2rem rather than 0.4rem. That still does not explain why the BPM sits at y=323. The vitals box may be taller than expected because of large font size and line-height. The x=1051 coordinate suggests the center column is centered horizontally, while the parent container likely has significant margin pushing the BPM downward.\n\nI will crop the screenshot with ImageMagick to inspect the HUD layout more closely. The BPM is right-aligned inside a wide flex column, so it sits on the right edge of the center block and appears in the game field rather than nesting tightly under the vitals.\n\nI will crop the op-calm top and center HUD to inspect the layout. The script failed before the session card, so I will fix the visual bugs first and then recapture the title screen, settings, and session card with longer waits. I will also check whether the creature is visible under the lamp in strain-adagio.\n\nThe plan now includes six specific visual fixes. The lamp should sit inside the operative window or remain as warm light. The bust hair cap needs shortening so the eyes show and the right bust faces the camera. The portrait plane should move to bottom center, shrink, and set the speaker on bark. The cut-in must be fully framed with a pale border. CSS font sizes need adjustment: `.where` at 2.2rem, `.timer` and `.score` at 3.5rem, `.note` and `.seat` at 2.15rem, the about screen at `flex-start`, and menus need a scrim. Most importantly, the center HUD column must become a tight stack so the BPM counter sits directly under the vitals instead of dropping into the game field.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ecbf1c06-e42f-4834-97d7-152a0da12710-105","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"magick \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots/op-calm.png\" -resize 960x540 \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots/preview-calm.jpg\" && magick \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots/story-shout.png\" -resize 960x540 \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots/preview-story.jpg\" && magick \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/