{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a1778943-864a-452b-ae11-8a87f7b3f497-112","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/jpeg\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a1778943-864a-452b-ae11-8a87f7b3f497-113","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/jpeg\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a1778943-864a-452b-ae11-8a87f7b3f497-114","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/jpeg\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a1778943-864a-452b-ae11-8a87f7b3f497-115","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/jpeg\"}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"736b7cfc-5553-4e44-9a43-65e9d98a4ebf"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_813","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The face crop is very informative.\n\nThe left character's eyes are completely obscured by the teal hair cap. The blush and mouth remain in correct orientation.\n\nThe right character is facing the wrong way. Its rotation must be fixed.\n\nThe lamp shade has vertical striations from normal discontinuities on its low-poly cone. It looks like a giant chin or shade covering the surgical field. It needs to be moved out of the OR view.\n\nThe lamp shade might actually be the portrait plane showing a close-up of the top of a head. The curved bottom edge could be the cone's bottom cap.\n\nThe portrait plane sits at the top of the view, not the bottom. The camera's local -Y should be up, so this placement is unexpected. The geometry size and flipUVs are being checked.\n\nThe portrait plane faces the camera's back side. The default material culls back faces, so the plane might be invisible unless the WebGPU node material is double-sided.\n\nThe portrait plane faces the camera, so it is visible. The giant shape at the top is the lamp cone at y=2.2.\n\nThe lamp cone is only 0.45 units in radius, so it should not fill the top of the frame. The camera sits at depth 1.83, which makes the visible portion unexpectedly large. A careful recompute with a script is needed to verify the exact screen size.\n\nThe lamp cone spans roughly 40% of the screen height. It will be hidden during operations and kept only for title and story scenes.\n\nThe lamp will be repositioned to the far side of the room at (0, 1.6, -1.8) with a smaller radius of 0.22. This keeps it visible in title and menu scenes while preventing it from becoming a large covering blob in the operating room view.\n\nThe lamp will be hidden during operations and placed at (0, 2.9, -0.2) with a 0.35 scale. This keeps it as a small cap near the top edge without covering the surgical field.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2b41ced2-93f3-42bf-a2eb-ac33a717e9c7-116","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node << 'JS'\nfunction project(lx, ly, lz, scale=1) {\n  const C = [0, 3.55, 1.65];\n  const T = [0, 0.1, 0.06];\n  const Fraw = [T[0]-C[0], T[1]-C[1], T[2]-C[2]];\n  const fl = Math.hypot(...Fraw);\n  const F = Fraw.map(v => v/fl);\n  const up = [0,1,0];\n  // right = normalize(cross(F, up))? three.js lookAt: z = normalize(eye-target) = -F\n  // matrix: x = normalize(cross(up, z)) where z is camera forward in world which is -look\n  const zaxis = Fraw.map(v => -v/fl); // camera local +Z points backward? three camera looks down -Z, so world direction of local -Z is F (look)\n  // local +Z world dir = -F\n  const z = [-F[0], -F[1], -F[2]];\n  // x = normalize(cross(up, z))\n  let x = [up[1]*z[2]-up[2]*z[1], up[2]*z[0]-up[0]*z[2], up[0]*z[1]-up[1]*z[0]];\n  const xl = Math.hypot(...x); x = x.map(v=>v/xl);\n  // y = cross(z, x)\n  const y = [z[1]*x[2]-z[2]*x[1], z[2]*x[0]-z[0]*x[2], z[0]*x[1]-z[1]*x[0]];\n  const V = [lx-C[0], ly-C[1], lz-C[2]];\n  // camera local: x right, y up, z backward. depth toward look = -dot(V, z) = dot(V, F)\n  const depth = V[0]*F[0]+V[1]*F[1]+V[2]*F[2];\n  const sx = V[0]*x[0]+V[1]*x[1]+V[2]*x[2];\n  const sy = V[0]*y[0]+V[1]*y[1]+V[2]*y[2];\n  const tan = Math.tan(17*Math.PI/180);\n  const hh = depth * tan;\n  const hw = hh * 16/9;\n  const r = 0.45 * scale;\n  return { depth: +depth.toFixed(2), ndcY: +(sy/hh).toFixed(2), ndcX: +(sx/hw).toFixed(2), radY: +(r/hh).toFixed(2), sy: +sy.toFixed(2), hh: +hh.toFixed(2) };\n}\nfor (const p of [[0,2.2,0.2,1],[0,3.1,-0.4,0.45],[0,2.7,-1.2,0.4],[1.2,2.4,-1.5,0.35],[0,1.8,-2.2,0.5]]) {\n  console.log(JSON.stringify(p), project(...p));\n}\nJS","description":"Project lamp positions into the OR view"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2584,"output_tokens":2252,"cache_read_input_tokens":186240,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"76996332-cd33-44bd-b6d0-596990832717"}
