{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-089c714f-9517-4b09-8d9a-cddd026ec451-121","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tfor ( let ix = 0; ix <= widthSegments; ix ++ ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tconst u = ix / widthSegments;\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// vertex\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertex.x = - radius * Math.cos( phiStart + u * phiLength ) * Math.sin( thetaStart + v * thetaLength );\\n100→\\t\\t\\t\\tvertex.y = radius * Math.cos( thetaStart + v * thetaLength );\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertex.z = radius * Math.sin( phiStart + u * phiLength ) * Math.sin( thetaStart + v * thetaLength );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertices.push( vertex.x, vertex.y, vertex.z );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// normal\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnormal.copy( vertex ).normalize();\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnormals.push( normal.x, normal.y, normal.z );\\n\\n110→\\t\\t\\t\\t// uv\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tuvs.push( u + uOffset, 1 - v );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tverticesRow.push( index ++ );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tgrid.push( verticesRow );\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"90→\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tfor ( let ix = 0; ix <= widthSegments; ix ++ ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tconst u = ix / widthSegments;\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// vertex\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertex.x = - radius * Math.cos( phiStart + u * phiLength ) * Math.sin( thetaStart + v * thetaLength );\\n100→\\t\\t\\t\\tvertex.y = radius * Math.cos( thetaStart + v * thetaLength );\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertex.z = radius * Math.sin( phiStart + u * phiLength ) * Math.sin( thetaStart + v * thetaLength );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertices.push( vertex.x, vertex.y, vertex.z );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// normal\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnormal.copy( vertex ).normalize();\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnormals.push( normal.x, normal.y, normal.z );\\n\\n110→\\t\\t\\t\\t// uv\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tuvs.push( u + uOffset, 1 - v );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tverticesRow.push( index ++ );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tgrid.push( verticesRow );\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/node_modules/three/src/geometries/SphereGeometry.js\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tfor ( let ix = 0; ix <= widthSegments; ix ++ ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tconst u = ix / widthSegments;\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// vertex\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertex.x = - radius * Math.cos( phiStart + u * phiLength ) * Math.sin( thetaStart + v * thetaLength );\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertex.y = radius * Math.cos( thetaStart + v * thetaLength );\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertex.z = radius * Math.sin( phiStart + u * phiLength ) * Math.sin( thetaStart + v * thetaLength );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tvertices.push( vertex.x, vertex.y, vertex.z );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// normal\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnormal.copy( vertex ).normalize();\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tnormals.push( normal.x, normal.y, normal.z );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// uv\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tuvs.push( u + uOffset, 1 - v );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tverticesRow.push( index ++ );\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tgrid.push( verticesRow );\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":174}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"30decd8f-f37d-491e-8fd9-f0fe6f736ee0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_819","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Mapping UV coordinates for a sphere. V equals iy divided by heightSegments. Theta equals v times PI, with zero at the north pole and PI at the south.\n\nCanvas y=0 maps to the north pole. Eyes at canvas y=232/512 yield uv.y=0.547, v=0.453, and theta≈81.5° from north. The cap spans 99°.\n\nThe mouth sits at 119°, below the 99° cap. The crop confirms the face is upright and the eyes are hidden under the hair. The cap should end around 61° to cover the forehead while keeping the eyes clear. Brows at 69° will remain visible. Locks placed near y=0.15 might also obscure the face.\n\nLocks are not the main problem. The crop shows a clean cap edge.\n\nThe face sits at +Z with u=0.25. The left bust should rotate to -0.35 and the right bust to 0.35 so both face the camera.\n\nPortrait will show the speaker when bark audio plays and move into frame. CSS font sizes are being set for where, timer, score, note, and seat elements. The about section will receive a class and flex-start justification.\n\nThe about section will use `class=\"screen about-fit\"` with `justify-content: flex-start` and a 0.5rem gap. This keeps content inside the existing 5% UI margin instead of overflowing. A new `.about-line` class sets line-height to 1.2.\n\nBPM at y=323 is dropping into the field area while vitals 100 stays near the top. The center div layout likely has a sizing issue, perhaps from an oversized ECG element pushing the BPM downward.\n\nThe 200px gap between vitals and BPM cannot be explained by the 51px ECG element. The center column may be stretching via alignment, or a tall sibling could be pushing the BPM downward. There is also a suspicion that two elements might both display the text \"72\".\n\nThe BPM text is confirmed to be the element at y=323. The `.hud` grid layout and `.hud-top` row height are being examined as possible causes for the downward shift, but the objective wraps to one line and the vitals block does not explain the 323px gap.\n\nThe ECG element is ruled out as the cause of the gap. `.hud-top` uses flexbox rather than grid, and flex items default to `align-items: flex-start`, so the `ecg-line` background stretching cannot be forcing the BPM downward.\n\nThe BPM text sits at y=323, which matches its visual position in the crop-lamp image. The vitals \"100\" and BPM \"72\" are not stacked tightly; they appear as separate elements in the field.\n\nThe vitals \"100\" and BPM \"72\" share nearly the same x-coordinate in the crop. The vitals element is wide with centered text, so its glyphs sit near the center of a box that starts higher than the BPM field.\n\nThe center HUD will be tightened with flexbox and a 0.15rem gap. Vitals, timer, and score will use 3.5rem font size with line-height set to 1. The ECG height will be reduced to 2.2rem. If the BPM still drops, the ECG is the culprit. A tool hint at y=956 overlaps the bottom edge because the .note element is only 32px.\n\nThe bottom-right prompt is fully visible. The main-menu.png crop shows an operation HUD with overlapping text, contradicting the audit's claim that it was a menu. This suggests the wrong file was cropped or the image was overwritten.\n\nThe audit found zero issues because the DOM was still the main menu when it ran. The screenshot captured the operation HUD instead. A step or paint must have changed the DOM between those two moments. The screenshot does not advance the simulation, but a running animation frame loop could still update the scene.\n\nThe screenshot waits for fonts and paint. During that wait, the attract timer can expire and trigger mountAttract. The HUD paints before the pixels are captured. This explains why the audit saw the menu but the crop shows the operation HUD.\n\nThe capture script samples the DOM before Playwright begins its screenshot. The 1.8-second wait plus the screenshot's own font and paint delays push the idle timer past ten seconds, so attract mode starts during the capture itself. The logged state therefore records the menu while the final image shows the operation HUD.\n\nThe About screenshot is likely genuine. The audit flagged the usage line, confirming the DOM was still the About screen when sampled. The 3D head shows through behind the text. The main menu screenshot was captured after attract mode had already replaced it with the operation HUD.\n\nThe title, main menu, and settings screenshots need recapturing with attract mode suppressed. Since lastInput is not exposed on the API, a non-navigating key press or a mousemove could reset the idle timer before the next screenshot.\n\nThe recapture plan is to press Shift or a harmless key immediately before each screenshot so the idle timer resets, then step once and capture with a short timeout. This keeps the wait under ten seconds and prevents attract mode from stealing the frame. The title shot will exit attract mode first. After fixing the code issues, the project will be rebuilt and all screenshots recaptured.\n\nOperation screenshots are valid because attract mode only triggers on Title, Main Menu, Free Play, and Touch notice. The settings screenshot landed on Lobby instead of Settings, which means one down arrow was lost. The first ArrowDown may have been consumed as an exit-attract input while the main menu screenshot was running.\n\nThe recapture script will press Escape to exit attract mode, step once, and then navigate by checking focusId. Code fixes and CSS are being implemented now, followed by a rebuild and recapture. The speaker portrait will be positioned so it appears during bark audio.\n\nThe `playEvent` function must not return early before setting the speaker portrait and bark state. Hair cap, bust rotations, lamp scale, and cut-in group transforms are being adjusted. A new `hud-mid` class will tighten the center HUD. The about section will use `justify-content: flex-start`.\n\nThe ECG element will be sized at 2.4rem by 14rem. Objective text on the lamp will receive a text-shadow to improve contrast once the lamp moves. The right character's back-of-head rotation is being corrected. The story where font is also being addressed.\n\nThe story-shout cut-in was a badly framed head panel clipped by the right edge. Repositioning it should reveal a proper face panel.\n\nNarration uses teal hair and pale skin, matching the crop exactly. The right character is default Bea with brown hair turned away. After the rotation fix both faces will be visible.\n\nThe initial bust is Bea, so setSpeaker may need to be called during operations.\n\nThe speaker portrait will default to Bea for barks. Preview and crop files will be deleted from the folder so only the final evidence set remains. The browser suite must be rebuilt and rerun because HTML and CSS changes affect the shipped page, though it is long at eighty tests.\n\nThe hub suite is slow and likely unnecessary. It checks the rebuilt HTML, but the session JavaScript behavior is unchanged. The playEvent change only affects the director, and setSpeaker is view-only. Only the browser suite needs rerunning.\n\nThe browser suite will be rerun after visual confirmation to update browser.log, since the old log no longer matches the rebuilt HTML. The launch check may also need rerunning because the prompt layout changed.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The 1080p shots show three real problems: the surgical lamp covers the field, character eyes sit under the hair, and the other bust faces away. Key numbers and the scene label are also under the ten-foot size. I’ll fix those and shoot again."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-547c1cf3-9294-49ba-ab14-9bdffb8e479f-122","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js","old_string":"  const lamp = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.ConeGeometry(0.45, 0.3, 16), toon({ color: '#f4efe4' }));\n  lamp.position.set(0, 2.2, 0.2);\n  lamp.name = 'lamp';","new_string":"  const lamp = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.ConeGeometry(0.45, 0.3, 16), toon({ color: '#f4efe4' }));\n  // High and small: warm light only. A lower cone fills the top of the 34° view.\n  lamp.position.set(0, 2.55, -0.15);\n  lamp.scale.setScalar(0.28);\n  lamp.name = 'lamp';"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-547c1cf3-9294-49ba-ab14-9bdffb8e479f-123","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js","old_string":"  const portraitGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(0.7, 0.7));\n  const portrait = new THREE.Mesh(portraitGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\n  portrait.position.set(0, -0.55, -1.4);\n  camera.add(portrait);\n  scene.add(camera);\n\n  const cutGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.1, 0.7));\n  const cutin = new THREE.Mesh(cutGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\n  cutin.position.set(0.7, 0.25, -1.6);\n  cutin.rotation.z = -0.12;\n  cutin.visible = false;\n  camera.add(cutin);","new_string":"  const portraitGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(0.42, 0.42));\n  const portrait = new THREE.Mesh(portraitGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\n  portrait.position.set(-0.15, -0.32, -1.65);\n  camera.add(portrait);\n  scene.add(camera);\n\n  const cutGroup = new THREE.Group();\n  const cutFrame = new THREE.Mesh(\n    new THREE.PlaneGeometry(0.98, 0.68),\n    new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color: '#f4efe4' }),\n  );\n  cutFrame.position.z = -0.02;\n  const cutGeo = flipUVs(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(0.86, 0.56));\n  const cutin = new THREE.Mesh(cutGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: bustRT.texture }));\n  cutGroup.add(cutFrame, cutin);\n  cutGroup.position.set(0.52, 0.08, -2.4);\n  cutGroup.rotation.z = -0.08;\n  cutGroup.visible = false;\n  camera.add(cutGroup);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-547c1cf3-9294-49ba-ab14-9bdffb8e479f-124","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js","old_string":"    busts.left.position.set(-2.1, -0.4, 0);\n    busts.right.position.set(2.1, -0.4, 0);\n    busts.right.rotation.y = Math.PI;","new_string":"    busts.left.position.set(-2.1, -0.4, 0);\n    busts.right.position.set(2.1, -0.4, 0);\n    // Face texture looks down local +Z. Angle inward so both faces meet the camera.\n    busts.left.rotation.y = -0.4;\n    busts.right.rotation.y = 0.4;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-547c1cf3-9294-49ba-ab14-9bdffb8e479f-125","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js","old_string":"  function shout(on) {\n    cutin.visible = !!on;\n    if (ink && on) ink.u.speedLines.value = 1;\n  }","new_string":"  function shout(on) {\n    cutGroup.visible = !!on;\n    if (ink && on) ink.u.speedLines.value = 1;\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-547c1cf3-9294-49ba-ab14-9bdffb8e479f-126","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/bust.js","old_string":"  const cap = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(1.06, 32, 16, 0, Math.PI * 2, 0, Math.PI * 0.55), toon({ color: look.hair }));","new_string":"  // Stop above the eyes. 0.55π buried the irises under the cap.\n  const cap = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(1.06, 32, 16, 0, Math.P