,119,32,40,194,167,49,57,41,46,32,67,111,112,121,32,116,111,32,116,104,101,32,114,111,111,116,32,102,105,108,101,46,32,79,110,101,32,108,97,115,116,32,102,117,108,108,32,116,101,115,116,32,114,117,110,46,10,49,49,54,57,58,42,42,65,98,111,117,116,32,38,32,67,114,101,100,105,116,115,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,46,42,42,32,89,111,117,114,32,98,114,105,101,102,32,108,105,115,116,115,32,102,111,117,114,32,98,108,111,99,107,115,32,116,104,97,116,32,109,117,115,116,32,97,112,112,101,97,114,32,98,111,116,104,32,105,110,32,121,111,117,114,32,99,104,97,116,32,114,101,112,108,121,32,97,110,100,32,111,110,32,116,104,105,115,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,58,32,83,111,117,114,99,101,32,73,110,102,111,114,109,97,116,105,111,110,44,32,84,101,115,116,105,110,103,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,44,32,69,110,103,105,110,101,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,44,32,80,114,111,109,112,116,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,46,32,71,105,118,101,32,101,97,99,104,32,98,108,111,99,107,32,105,116,115,32,111,119,110,32,112,97,103,101,115,32,97,116,32,116,101,110,45,102,111,111,116,32,115,105,122,101,44,32,97,32,102,101,119,32,115,104,111,114,116,32,97,110,115,119,101,114,115,32,112,101,114,32,112,97,103,101,44,32,109,111,118,101,100,32,116,104,114,111,117,103,104,32,119,105,116,104,32,76,49,47,82,49,32,111,114,32,81,47,69,44,32,110,101,118,101,114,32,97,32,100,101,110,115,101,32,119,97,108,108,46,32,65,100,100,32,97,32,99,114,101,100,105,116,115,32,112,97,103,101,58,32,116,104,101,32,109,111,100,101,108,32,108,105,110,101,32,102,114,111,109,32,121,111,117,114,32,98,114,105,101,102,44,32,84,104,114,101,101,46,106,115,44,32,82,97,112,105,101,114,44,32,66,97,110,103,101,114,115,32,97,110,100,32,66,97,114,108,111,119,32,67,111,110,100,101,110,115,101,100,32,40,79,70,76,41,44,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,114,101,110,100,101,114,101,114,32,105,110,32,117,115,101,32,116,104,105,115,32,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,46,10,49,50,48,56,58,124,32,72,101,97,100,108,101,115,115,32,116,101,115,116,115,44,32,111,110,101,32,99,111,109,109,97,110,100,44,32,102,97,105,108,117,114,101,115,32,97,110,100,32,97,32,99,111,117,110,116,44,32,97,32,102,117,108,108,32,115,99,114,105,112,116,101,100,32,112,108,97,121,116,104,114,111,117,103,104,44,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,115,104,111,116,115,32,111,110,108,121,32,119,104,101,110,32,110,101,101,100,101,100,44,32,110,111,32,114,101,118,105,101,119,32,115,117,98,97,103,101,110,116,115,32,124,32,194,167,49,55,32,124,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":21,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"**Perspective:** first-person surgeon's-eye view of a 3D operative field, from a fixed, tilted camera (§9.2). Story scenes are staged third-person two-shots of 3D character busts.\"},{\"line_number\":378,\"content\":\"**Lint:** a test fails if any Bea line contains \\\"good\\\" outside S16. In Op 5 Bea still calls the barks and trades shots with Ines. In Op 6 Ines interjects over comms. In Op 7 every bark comes from Pip reading the notebook.\"},{\"line_number\":423,\"content\":\"### 8.4 Ten-foot rules (tests can't judge these; check at 1920×1080)\"},{\"line_number\":716,\"content\":\"The host's copy runs the only `Sim`, including Rapier. Everyone else renders snapshots. The host's view reads the sim directly; a client reads its decoded state, with entities and other seats interpolated 100 to 150 ms behind. **Your own tip is always local and instant**, and tool sounds and cosmetic trails start locally. Grades and results come from the host.\"},{\"line_number\":728,\"content\":\"Keep each copy to at most 16 messages/s (the limit is 20, burst 40) with one token-bucket `send()` wrapper that sheds `s` and `i` first. **Any console line starting `[AIHub]` fails the hub's check**, including rate and size warnings, and `finish` called from a non-host. Drop snapshots older than the newest applied. Clients send `i` even when idle, as the harness needs traffic both ways.\"},{\"line_number\":742,\"content\":\"    else if (from === info.host) view?.applySnapshot(data);\"},{\"line_number\":755,\"content\":\"      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\"},{\"line_number\":792,\"content\":\"These are all reproduced in §17: it plays shared worlds at 2, 3 and 4 players at 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss, with a player leaving; `scenario=host-leave`; `scenario=server` at 2 players. It checks the client is exactly one unmodified copy (SHA-256, §16.2). Then, on its own: opens the page, presses Enter, Space, Enter, Space, checks that nothing threw, `AIHub.active` is false, `Math.random` is untouched, and the screenshot isn't blank.\"},{\"line_number\":810,\"content\":\"                        tools/*.js, strains/*.js, ops-runner.js, snapshot.js, bot.js\"},{\"line_number\":825,\"content\":\"The view reconciles meshes against `state` by entity id, and turns `events` into particles, paint, sounds and barks. It runs from `sim.state` in solo and couch play, and from decoded snapshots on a hub client: the same code either way. That single decision makes the Node tests, the bot, attract mode, the server copy and co-op all cheap.\"},{\"line_number\":879,\"content\":\"All run here on 2026-11-04: Chromium 153 under Playwright 1.63.0, Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. A skeleton with this stack (a toon scene, Rapier on the host, its own card, snapshots at 10/s with a 1/s keyframe, input at 12/s) passed the hub's harness on WebGPU at 2 players, 4 players on a bad network with one leaving, host-leave and server scenarios. The 4-player run also passed without WebGPU, on the WebGL2 fallback. The skeleton's scene was small: your real game will take longer in these runs, so allow for it.\"},{\"line_number\":928,\"content\":\"**Use these five flags.** Your brief's machine notes list a shorter set (`--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`). On this computer, those alone **lose the device right after the first frame** (console: \\\"A valid external Instance reference no longer exists\\\"), which is why a screenshot comes out blank. With the hub's flags, frames draw, `page.screenshot` works, and pixel readback works:\"},{\"line_number\":1036,\"content\":\"Tune `line`, thresholds and colors to taste at 1920×1080. If you add outline-worthy color edges (a stripe on one surface), remember the filter only sees depth and normal breaks, so paint them dark.\"},{\"line_number\":1109,\"content\":\"- Snapshot round-trip: decoded state contains everything the view reads. The `s` message stays under 1,100 bytes at the busiest moment of Grand Rounds with 4 seats.\"},{\"line_number\":1118,\"content\":\"- Boots on `webgpu` with flags and `webgl2` without; no page errors on either; screenshot not blank (PNG well above a blank page's size). WebKit boots.\"},{\"line_number\":1141,\"content\":\"Wait for `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]` (allow 300 s), and require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` and **no console line starting `[AIHub]`**. Use a 1280×860 viewport. Run all five with the §16.3 flags, and the 4-player run once more without them (WebGL2). Then **on its own:** load the page, wait 2.5 s, press Enter, Space, Enter, Space with 500 ms gaps, wait 2 s; require no page errors, `AIHub.active === false`, `AIHub.seeded !== true`, and a non-blank screenshot.\"},{\"line_number\":1143,\"content\":\"**Screenshots, only for what scripts can't judge.** At 1920×1080: Title, Main Menu, one story scene with a shout, Operation at a calm moment, Operation in danger, Hush, each strain once, Report, Settings, About, session card. Add one HUD portrait and one cut-in: faces must be upright. Look for: text legibility from ten feet, ink quality, overlaps. Fix what you see.\"},{\"line_number\":1158,\"content\":\"8. **Multiplayer.** Snapshots, couch lobby, session, card. All hub runs pass.\"},{\"line_number\":1159,\"content\":\"9. **Final pass.** Calibrate `parScore`. Screenshot review. Write `docs/AUTHORING.md`. Fill in About and the exit interview (§19). Copy to the root file. One last full test run.\"},{\"line_number\":1169,\"content\":\"**About & Credits screen.** Your brief lists four blocks that must appear both in your chat reply and on this screen: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback. Give each block its own pages at ten-foot size, a few short answers per page, moved through with L1/R1 or Q/E, never a dense wall. Add a credits page: the model line from your brief, Three.js, Rapier, Bangers and Barlow Condensed (OFL), and the renderer in use this session.\"},{\"line_number\":1208,\"content\":\"| Headless tests, one command, failures and a count, a full scripted playthrough, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | §17 |\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"99a9bab2-df2a-462d-86e2-cf25131f3822"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_824","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The first step is to rebuild the HTML.\n\nshots.mjs needs several fixes. Reset lastInput before screenshots to avoid stale input. Capture the title immediately instead of waiting 1800ms. Navigate to settings by looping until focusId matches. Poll the iframe until screen equals 'Card'. Close the browser and server in catch blocks. The 1800ms delay caused an attract race condition where idle time could exceed 10 seconds during slow WebGPU screenshots.\n\nA Shift key or mousemove will reset lastInput immediately before each menu screenshot. The exact input event that triggers this reset still needs verification. test.step is required for the simulation to process input, but checkAttract runs on every animation frame regardless.\n\nA screenshot longer than ten seconds could still trigger attract mid-capture and corrupt the menu image. WebGL might be faster than WebGPU for shots, though the plan requires WebGPU evidence. Disabling attract during shots would require a test hook or game code change. Poking input repeatedly during a long screenshot is impractical.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2ab35922-1889-4e41-b3ca-d90045213b07-9","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function checkAttract|lastInput|attract\\.on|blockMenu","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2ab35922-1889-4e41-b3ca-d90045213b07-10","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Verification plan|## 17|Screenshots","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9448,"output_to