{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_825","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking the checkAttract function and rAF loop to see if lastInput can be accessed from page evaluate before screenshot.\n\nlastInput is not exposed via state(). I will fire a mousemove event to trigger the handler that sets it. Screenshot times are roughly 20 seconds each.\n\nA race condition exists where attract mode could start during the screenshot wait and paint over the menu. The screenshot is a blocking CDP call, so it is unclear whether the page's animation loop continues running in JavaScript during that time.\n\nPage JavaScript continues running during Playwright screenshots. Injecting a mousemove from the Node side is impossible while the screenshot is in progress.\n\nTwo fixes are being weighed:\n- Temporarily lengthen the attract timeout in source for test mode.\n- In test mode, trigger attract only from test.step and not from the rAF loop.\n\nDisabling rAF checkAttract in test mode would break tests that expect attract after exactly 10000 ms wall clock. The next idea is to use WebGL for screenshots to reduce capture time, though layout and ink filter differences remain a concern.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6b25dcf-2cbb-4c5e-afce-41bee8543630-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":130,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6b25dcf-2cbb-4c5e-afce-41bee8543630-12","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":800,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6b25dcf-2cbb-4c5e-afce-41bee8543630-13","name"