{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_837","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The lamp is positioned above the NDC y=1 boundary.\n\nThe lamp is completely off-screen. It needs to be lowered and moved closer to the camera's view of the field.\n\nThe old lamp sits at y=2.2 with scale 1 and radius 0.45. Its bottom edge is at y=2.05. I am testing lower positions to find a sliver in NDC y between 0.85 and 0.98.\n\nScanning y from 1.2 to 2.2 at scale 1 and smaller scales to find a bottom edge between NDC 0.82 and 0.98.\n\nThe portrait corners span the lower-left of the operative field, so it would be too large for a HUD bust. It might overlap the wound.\n\nThe portrait would overlap the organ at field center. I will shrink it and move it to a corner, likely bottom-left or bottom-right.\n\nThe portrait plane is 43% of the screen height at distance 1.65. That is why it spans 0.83 NDC units. Shrinking the geometry or moving it farther from the camera would make it smaller.\n\nAn 18% screen-height portrait at distance 1.65 yields a NDC span of about 0.37. The safe bottom-left corner is near NDC x -0.72 and y -0.62, with a 0.28-unit span. World half-width and half-height are roughly 0.896 and 0.504.\n\nLocal coordinates for the bottom-left HUD portrait are x = -0.672 and y = -0.312. The 0.16 plane fits cleanly inside the view volume. It will sit behind the tool wheel, which occupies the bottom-left DOM edge.\n\nThe bottom-left corner is already occupied by the DOM tool wheel. A portrait there would sit behind it. The lower portion of the screen might overlap the bark or wheel. An upper area near the wound center could be crowded with vitals. A small portrait just above the bark, left of center, below the wound might avoid overlap.\n\nThe portrait will be a camera child so it stays screen-fixed. A small 0.18 plane at z=-1.65, x=-0.62, y=-0.28 should fit in the lower-left gap. The story camera cut-in spans the right half of the frame and may cover the right bust.\n\nThe cut-in currently covers the right bust and much of the center. This would hide both faces, which violates the \"both faces visible\" rule. I will move it to a corner instead, likely upper-right, and make it smaller. The story camera half-height at distance 2.4 is about 0.643.\n\nThe cut-in will sit in the upper-right corner at local x = 0.71 and y = 0.35, sized 0.55 by 0.38. Its right edge lands just past the right bust center at ndc x = 0.38, keeping it clear of both faces.\n\nThe cut-in panel will sit at local x = 0.849, y = 0.35, sized 0.44 by 0.38. Its left edge lands at ndc x = 0.55, safely past the right bust center at 0.521.\n\nThe cut-in panel clears the right bust at ndc x = 0.935. Its upper edge sits safely above the heads, which span y from -0.48 to 0.12. I will enlarge it slightly to an ndc height of 0.36, giving a local geometry height of about 0.38.\n\nThe cut-in panel will use a 0.50 by 0.32 frame and a 0.42 by 0.24 picture, placed at local x = 0.78, y = 0.38, z = -2.4. The lamp cone will be lowered so its bottom rim sits just above the wound at NDC y = 0.92.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-44edd212-6e90-4de8-8e93-b5226226e7f1-35","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Title|function paint","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-44edd212-6e90-4de8-8e93-b5226226e7f1-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":1280,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":733,"output_tokens":3045,"cache_read_input_tokens":88320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null