{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_849","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Mouse frames on the Operation screen are positioned absolutely from the pointer.\n\nA mouse poke during Operation would slam the tip to a corner. The device stays 'mouse' after pointerdown until a keydown. I will press a harmless key before operation shots to reset it to 'keyboard'.\n\nShift keydown during Operation resets the device to keyboard without pausing. The frame steady state correctly returns to false after the keyup. If pointerdown was sent alone, it may linger; switching to keyboard mode prevents it from triggering use.\n\nI will dispatch pointerup to clear the lingering pointer state. The keep-awake interval must be stopped before pressing Shift to restore keyboard mode. Menu navigation is unaffected because the pointer at 4,4 sits outside the inset UI area and cannot activate a button. A pointerdown during attract mode exits that screen.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e8689f00-7f3b-4afb-a286-d79571b4e4ba-55","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"focusId","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2371,"output_tokens":603,"cache_read_input_tokens":107008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"92b92af1-193d-44f2-881e-92e2044fbcf0"}
