ice.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"AI Hub protocol and harness, engine prototypes on this computer, and the plan's notes on the source.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The sim suite (51 checks) and the hub harness (23 checks) caught the issues that would have shipped. The browser suite (80 checks) caught UI timing: attract was swallowing the next confirm, and a reload was dropping screens the playthrough had already opened.\\\",\\n    \\\"A few were critical: a story line that failed the Bea lint, snapshot traffic that could trip the hub rate warning, and a ready() call that the client ignores if it happens before welcome.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the Normal bot playthrough with the 45 to 75 percent clear-time band. It kept the operations honest.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was staring at a single still of the title. Behavior checks found the breaks. A picture did not.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"MeshToonNodeMaterial plus the ink graph is a complete look from primitives, and the hub client is small enough to read.\\\",\\n    \\\"WebGPU on this machine needs five browser flags or the device dies after one frame. Rapier must be initialized before the first world, and ready() is a no-op until the welcome arrives.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation sim, the bot, and the snapshot codec. The engine draws and hears. It does not know surgery.\\\",\\n    \\\"Software WebGPU is slow enough that a test has to drive the sim with step and warp, and four inked views in one harness is a memory tightrope.\\\",\\n    \\\"Nothing in the engine source. The operative rules live in this game.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to boot SwiftShader WebGPU without a private flag recipe, and a ready() that queues until welcome instead of vanishing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about feel: ten-foot type, one patient, four surgeons, and a story that knows when to be quiet.\\\",\\n    \\\"Two WebGPU flag lists disagree. The shorter one draws a blank here. The plan's five flags are the ones that work.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a sloppy four-surgeon coda inside the rules without moving the Normal scores, then proving the hub harness on software WebGPU.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say once, in the prompt, which browser flags this computer actually needs.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"credits\\\": [\\n    \\\"xAI grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh, via Grok CLI\\\",\\n    \\\"Three.js r180\\\",\\n    \\\"Rapier 0.19.3\\\",\\n    \\\"Bangers and Barlow Condensed, SIL Open Font License\\\",\\n    \\\"AI Hub session client 1.4.0\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":46}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"7f112a98-846b-44d9-a102-2f87ce950b50"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_857","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"sourceInformation contains 15 fields.\n\nsourceInformation overflows because 15 entries at 2.2rem line height wrap to roughly 1300px, exceeding the 972px limit. I will paginate it into chunks of about four entries and split long feedback lines across pages. The current page model uses model.page for both tab indexing and focus, so adding subpages would complicate Q/E and tab navigation. I will flatten the about section into a list of slides with headIndex, label, and lines, letting model.page index them directly while keeping tabs jump to the first slide of each block.\n\nThe current About screen code ties model.page directly to model.focus and the tab index. Because Q/E navigation and pageCount both rely on that same value, adding subpages would break focus tracking. I need to separate the slide index from the focus index before paginating.\n\nI will keep model.page as the block index and add model.aboutSlice for subpages within each block. Q/E will advance slices first, wrapping back to the start of the same block, then move to the next block. Tabs will switch blocks directly. This lets me build a flat slides array while preserving both navigation methods.\n\nThe current About template uses model.page as the tab index to highlight the active head and render the body. If model.page becomes a slide index, that mapping breaks: there is no tab for slide 7, so nothing gets highlighted and the wrong content may appear. I need to decouple the slide index from the tab index before flattening the section.\n\nI am writing the `aboutSlides()` helper to build the flattened slide array. It splits each block into pages of up to four lines, tracking part and total counts per slide.\n\nThe helper now handles credits, renderer info, object blocks, and arrays. sourceInformation pages will hold four entries each; other blocks get two. A full page should fit at roughly 520 pixels. Feedback lines remain long and may wrap.\n\nTwo feedback lines per page should still fit, since a 200-character line wraps to about three lines at this font size. I am now updating pageCount and the About template to use the flattened slides array.\n\nThe About template now wraps the slide index and maps tabs to their first slide. Because `btn` highlights via `model.focus`, and that focus value will be a slide index rather than a block index, the active tab must be highlighted by class instead of by focus.\n\nThe About template now highlights the active tab by adding an `on` class directly to the button, bypassing the focus index. The `activate('about:N')` handler still works because N is the first slide index of that block. I also verified that `turnPage` and the arrow-down logic remain compatible with this flattened slide model.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b7aa567-45c7-44e6-a3e0-41b79825e96b-65","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":980,"limit":130}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1175,"output_tokens":1728,"cache_read_input_tokens":116480,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"56fdac42-e317-42d5-b543-bbd1f2af0415"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6b7aa567-45c7-44e6-a3e0-41b79825e96b-65","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"980→      model.overlay = null;\\n      setScreen('Operation');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'quit') {\\n      model.overlay = null;\\n      freeSim();\\n      setScreen('Main Menu');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n990→    if (id === 'dev') {\\n      if (model.mode === 'session') return;\\n      setOverlay('dev');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'back-settings' || id === 'back') {\\n      closeSettings();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id.startsWith('about:')) {\\n1000→      model.page = Number(id.slice(6)) || 0;\\n      model.focus = model.page;\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id.startsWith('site:')) {\\n      const sim = model.sim;\\n      if (!sim) return;\\n      const idx = sim.op.sites.findIndex((s) => s.id === id.slice(5));\\n      if (idx >= 0) sim.setSite(sim.seats[0], idx);\\n1010→      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'glyphs') {\\n      model.settings.glyphs = model.settings.glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'playstation' : 'xbox';\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'rumble' || id === 'swapSticks' || id === 'shake' || id === 'boil') {\\n1020→      model.settings[id] = !model.settings[id];\\n      if (id === 'boil') model.view?.setBoil?.(!!model.settings.boil);\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'fullscreen') {\\n      model.settings.fullscreen = !model.settings.fullscreen;\\n      const node = document.documentElement;\\n      if (model.settings.fullscreen) node.requestFullscreen?.().catch(() => {});\\n1030→      else document.exitFullscreen?.().catch(() => {});\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'textSpeed') {\\n      model.settings.textSpeed = model.settings.textSpeed >= 4 ? 1 : model.settings.textSpeed * 2;\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n1040→    }\\n    if (DEV_IDS.includes(id) || id === 'reset-page' || id === 'reset-all' || id === 'jump') {\\n      const page = devPages()[model.page] || [];\\n      const found = page.find((item) => item.id === id);\\n      runDev(model, id, found?.keys);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function openSettings() {\\n1050→    if (model.mode === 'session') {\\n      model.sessionPause = true;\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    model.returnTo = { screen: model.screen, overlay: model.overlay };\\n    model.page = 0;\\n    setScreen('Settings');\\n  }\\n\\n1060→  function closeSettings() {\\n    if (model.mode === 'session') {\\n      model.sessionPause = false;\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const ret = model.returnTo;\\n    model.returnTo = null;\\n    if (!ret) {\\n      setScreen('Main Menu');\\n1070→      return;\\n    }\\n    setScreen(ret.screen);\\n    if (ret.overlay) setOverlay(ret.overlay);\\n  }\\n  model.applySettings = (sample) => {\\n    const menu = sample?.menu || {};\\n    if (menu.pageLeft) turnPage(-1);\\n    else if (menu.pageRight) turnPage(1);\\n    else if (menu.up) moveFocus(-1);\\n1080→    else if (menu.down) moveFocus(1);\\n    else if (menu.left) nudge(-1);\\n    else if (menu.right) nudge(1);\\n    else if (menu.confirm) {\\n      const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n      if (item) activate(item.id);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  function moveFocus(dir) {\\n1090→    const items = currentItems();\\n    if (!items.length) return;\\n    model.focus = (model.focus + dir + items.length) % items.length;\\n    if (model.screen === 'About' && !model.overlay) model.page = model.focus;\\n    paint(true);\\n  }\\n\\n  function turnPage(dir) {\\n    const n = pageCount();\\n    if (n <= 1) return false;\\n1100→    model.page = (model.page + dir + n) % n;\\n    model.focus = model.screen === 'About' ? model.page : 0;\\n    paint(true);\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nudge(dir) {\\n    if (model.screen === 'Chart' && !model.overlay) {\\n      const order = ['intern', 'resident', 'attending'];\\n      const i = Math.max(0, order.indexOf(model.settings.difficulty || 'resident'));\",\"content_concise\":\"980→      model.overlay = null;\\n      setScreen('Operation');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'quit') {\\n      model.overlay = null;\\n      freeSim();\\n      setScreen('Main Menu');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n990→    if (id === 'dev') {\\n      if (model.mode === 'session') return;\\n      setOverlay('dev');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'back-settings' || id === 'back') {\\n      closeSettings();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id.startsWith('about:')) {\\n1000→      model.page = Number(id.slice(6)) || 0;\\n      model.focus = model.page;\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id.startsWith('site:')) {\\n      const sim = model.sim;\\n      if (!sim) return;\\n      const idx = sim.op.sites.findIndex((s) => s.id === id.slice(5));\\n      if (idx >= 0) sim.setSite(sim.seats[0], idx);\\n1010→      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'glyphs') {\\n      model.settings.glyphs = model.settings.glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'playstation' : 'xbox';\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'rumble' || id === 'swapSticks' || id === 'shake' || id === 'boil') {\\n1020→      model.settings[id] = !model.settings[id];\\n      if (id === 'boil') model.view?.setBoil?.(!!model.settings.boil);\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'fullscreen') {\\n      model.settings.fullscreen = !model.settings.fullscreen;\\n      const node = document.documentElement;\\n      if (model.settings.fullscreen) node.requestFullscreen?.().catch(() => {});\\n1030→      else document.exitFullscreen?.().catch(() => {});\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'textSpeed') {\\n      model.settings.textSpeed = model.settings.textSpeed >= 4 ? 1 : model.settings.textSpeed * 2;\\n      persist();\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n1040→    }\\n    if (DEV_IDS.includes(id) || id === 'reset-page' || id === 'reset-all' || id === 'jump') {\\n      const page = devPages()[model.page] || [];\\n      const found = page.find((item) => item.id === id);\\n      runDev(model, id, found?.keys);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function openSettings() {\\n1050→    if (model.mode === 'session') {\\n      model.sessionPause = true;\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    model.returnTo = { screen: model.screen, overlay: model.overlay };\\n    model.page = 0;\\n    setScreen('Settings');\\n  }\\n\\n1060→  function closeSettings() {\\n    if (model.mode === 'session') {\\n      model.sessionPause = false;\\n      paint(true);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const ret = model.returnTo;\\n    model.returnTo = null;\\n    if (!ret) {\\n      setScreen('Main Menu');\\n1070→      return;\\n    }\\n    setScreen(ret.screen);\\n    if (ret.overlay) setOverlay(ret.overlay);\\n  }\\n  model.applySettings = (sample) => {\\n    const menu = sample?.menu || {};\\n    if (menu.pageLeft) turnPage(-1);\\n    else if (menu.pageRight) turnPage(1);\\n    else if (menu.up) moveFocus(-1);\\n1080→    else if (menu.down) moveFocus(1);\\n    else if (menu.left) nudge(-1);\\n    else if (menu.right) nudge(1);\\n    else if (menu.confirm) {\\n      const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n      if (item) activate(item.id);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  function moveFocus(dir) {\\n1090→    const items = currentItems();\\n    if (!items.length) return;\\n    model.focus = (model.focus + dir + items.length) % items.length;\\n    if (model.screen === 'About' && !model.overlay) model.page = model.focus;\\n    paint(true);\\n  }\\n\\n  function turnPage(dir) {\\n    const n = pageCount();\\n    if (n <= 1) return false;\\n1100→    model.page = (mo