{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_867","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"About sets page 0 is complete. Now building.\n\nBuilding from the dev folder. Shots will run next and may take over ten minutes. The browser suite must wait until shots finish. The build updates tests/hub/site/game.html.\n\nThe shot script's Playwright evaluation is safe. The title button is large enough for a corner click. The attract exit path uses the correct pointer event.\n\nThe shot script's pointer events dispatch directly on the window node. They never hit-test or target the start button, so the attract exit path is fully isolated.\n\nThe keep-awake pointerup fires on the window node, so it cannot trigger activate or exit attract. The 1.5-second interval keeps lastInput fresh during screenshots and runs in the page JavaScript during CDP capture.\n\nI will check tools/build.mjs to confirm the output path. After building, I will verify the HTML file size changed and contains the lamp position string.\n\nFor the shots job, I will redirect output to a log file and use a monitor that wakes only on \"done\", \"Error\", or \"exit\". This avoids being woken by every progress line.\n\nThe shots script will run in the background with output redirected to a log file. I will poll that log every thirty seconds and only print actionable events like an exit code or stack trace. I will wait for the process to finish before examining the generated images.\n\nShots should take about seven to eight minutes, so a fifteen-minute block is safe. I will wait for them to finish before proceeding. I could write the launch script while they run.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-be40ac52-3465-4d6f-bb37-568b8e90aa1c-82","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230\" && node tools/build.mjs","description":"Rebuild the single-file game HTML"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":346,"output_tokens":1147,"cache_read_input_tokens":132736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"dab8c614-b3ea-4c1d-a543-3cbdd4066e5b"}
