{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_874","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Visual progress looks good. I am now identifying issues.\n\nThe pagination logic is too strict. Any line over 140 characters forces the entire block to size 1, so short fields like dates are isolated on their own pages. The fix is to chunk by estimated wrapped lines instead of checking individual line lengths.\n\nThe new chunking function estimates each line's visual cost as `Math.max(1, Math.ceil(length / 90))`. It accumulates lines until the running total reaches four, then starts a new slide. Short fields like date and genre will group together on one page, while longer entries like tech will sit alone.\n\nThe About slide will be sparse because the current run is in progress. I will fix the chunking logic after it finishes and recapture only about.png. This is not a blocker for the remaining shots.\n\nBPM 72 is sitting too low in the wound field instead of tucking under vitals. The ECG element may still be oversized, or the center column might be stretching despite flex-start alignment. I am also checking whether the bpm paragraph is actually inside hud-mid in the built file.\n\nThe CSS gap is only 0.15rem and the ECG line is 0.4rem, so BPM 72 should sit immediately under the horizontal line. The image description may have overstated the distance. I am now examining the actual rendered layout to verify.\n\nThe BPM 72 is actually positioned correctly. It sits in the upper half of the oval, above the glass shards, grouped with vitals and ECG. The perceived gap is likely just the large font size and dark background. No recapture is needed.\n\nI will crop the saved PNG with ImageMagick to verify the exact vertical positions of 100 and 72. The portrait is upright and readable, with hair spikes forming a sunburst around the head. Story faces are both turned toward the camera with visible eyes and hair caps above them.\n\nThe cut-in frame is excellent. It shows an upright pale face with a cream border, speed lines, large dialogue, and the room lamp visible.\n\nThe tool hint sits at the bottom center without overlapping the wound. The prompt remains fully visible.\n\nThe ECG line is now thin as intended. The operating room field is clear and the glass shards are visible.\n\nThe calm operating room still shows heavy radial speed lines. The `shout()` function sets the ink filter's speedLines value to 1 when activated but never resets it to 0 when deactivated. Because `present()` calls `shout(false)` at the start of the operation, the uniform stays stuck at 1 and produces the unwanted ink effect.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b96bba2f-a2e5-4c1b-9c9a-665aa0ffd1ec-95","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"speedLines","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5079,"output_tokens":1576,"cache_read_input_tokens":142464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"a10ed6cb-e909-4952-8df4-c8507634e5e4"}
