f20-44de-46bd-904b-370924dfd662"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_875","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A decay issue was found in `sync()`.\n\nThe decay is intentional. Speed lines fade by 1/60 per frame after a shout burst. The calm shot was captured mid-fade because it followed a shout. Zeroing speed lines when leaving the story or stepping more frames before the calm shot would fix this.\n\nStepping 70 frames before the calm and strain shots will let the speed lines decay to zero. This is preferable to adding a test hook in `go()` because it avoids advancing the simulation. The glass phase should remain unaffected.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1f59c02d-031b-4984-87dc-ab533b22430b-96","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js","offset":300,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1990,"output_tokens":509,"cache_read_input_tokens":147456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"66ce717e-2536-4461-90c9-49f5cfe276ba"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1f59c02d-031b-4984-87dc-ab533b22430b-96","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"300→      rig = new THREE.Group();\\n      const ring = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.TorusGeometry(0.08, 0.012, 6, 12), toon({ color: seat.color || '#e8443a' }));\\n      ring.rotation.x = Math.PI / 2;\\n      rig.add(ring);\\n      for (const k of tools) {\\n        const m = toolMesh(k);\\n        m.visible = k === (seat.tool || 'gel');\\n        rig.add(m);\\n      }\\n      or.add(rig);\\n310→      tips.set(seat.id, rig);\\n    }\\n    return rig;\\n  }\\n\\n  function sync(state, dt = 0.016) {\\n    if (!state) return;\\n    const organId = state.organ || state.siteOrgan || 'forearm';\\n    if (organ.userData.organ !== organId) {\\n      organ.userData.organ = organId;\\n320→      setOrgan(organId);\\n      organ.userData.organ = organId;\\n    }\\n    const beat = state.beatPhase || 0;\\n    if (organ.userData.beat) organ.userData.beat.value = Math.sin(beat * Math.PI * 2) * 0.5 + 0.5;\\n    mixer.update(dt);\\n    const danger = state.vitals != null ? Math.max(0, (40 - state.vitals) / 40) : 0;\\n    if (ink) {\\n      ink.u.danger.value = danger * boil;\\n      ink.u.hushRadius.value = state.hush ? Math.min(1.8, (state.hushT || 0.4) * 2) : 0;\\n330→      ink.u.flash.value = Math.max(0, (ink.u.flash.value || 0) - dt * 2);\\n      ink.u.speedLines.value = Math.max(0, (ink.u.speedLines.value || 0) - dt);\\n    }\\n    const seen = new Set();\\n    for (const seat of state.seats || []) {\\n      if (seat.out) continue;\\n      const rig = ensureTip(seat);\\n      const p = fieldToWorld(seat.x, seat.y, 0.16);\\n      rig.position.lerp(p, 0.65);\\n      rig.rotation.z = -0.4;\",\"content_concise\":\"300→      rig = new THREE.Group();\\n      const ring = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.TorusGeometry(0.08, 0.012, 6, 12), toon({ color: seat.color || '#e8443a' }));\\n      ring.rotation.x = Math.PI / 2;\\n      rig.add(ring);\\n      for (const k of tools) {\\n        const m = toolMesh(k);\\n        m.visible = k === (seat.tool || 'gel');\\n        rig.add(m);\\n      }\\n      or.add(rig);\\n310→      tips.set(seat.id, rig);\\n    }\\n    return rig;\\n  }\\n\\n  function sync(state, dt = 0.016) {\\n    if (!state) return;\\n    const organId = state.organ || state.siteOrgan || 'forearm';\\n    if (organ.userData.organ !== organId) {\\n      organ.userData.organ = organId;\\n320→      setOrgan(organId);\\n      organ.userData.organ = organId;\\n    }\\n    const beat = state.beatPhase || 0;\\n    if (organ.userData.beat) organ.userData.beat.value = Math.sin(beat * Math.PI * 2) * 0.5 + 0.5;\\n    mixer.update(dt);\\n    const danger = state.vitals != null ? Math.max(0, (40 - state.vitals) / 40) : 0;\\n    if (ink) {\\n      ink.u.danger.value = danger * boil;\\n      ink.u.hushRadius.value = state.hush ? Math.min(1.8, (state.hushT || 0.4) * 2) : 0;\\n330→      ink.u.flash.value = Math.max(0, (ink.u.flash.value || 0) - dt * 2);\\n      ink.u.speedLines.value = Math.max(0, (ink.u.speedLines.value || 0) - dt);\\n    }\\n    const seen = new Set();\\n    for (const seat of state.seats || []) {\\n      if (seat.out) continue;\\n      const rig = ensureTip(seat);\\n      const p = fieldToWorld(seat.x, seat.y, 0.16);\\n      rig.position.lerp(p, 0.65);\\n      rig.rotation.z = -0.4;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js\",\"offset\":300,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"      rig = new THREE.Group();\\n      const ring = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.TorusGeometry(0.08, 0.012, 6, 12), toon({ color: seat.color || '#e8443a' }));\\n      ring.rotation.x = Math.PI / 2;\\n      rig.add(ring);\\n      for (const k of tools) {\\n        const m = toolMesh(k);\\n        m.visible = k === (seat.tool || 'gel');\\n        rig.add(m);\\n      }\\n      or.add(rig);\\n      tips.set(seat.id, rig);\\n    }\\n    return rig;\\n  }\\n\\n  function sync(state, dt = 0.016) {\\n    if (!state) return;\\n    const organId = state.organ || state.siteOrgan || 'forearm';\\n    if (organ.userData.organ !== organId) {\\n      organ.userData.organ = organId;\\n      setOrgan(organId);\\n      organ.userData.organ = organId;\\n    }\\n    const beat = state.beatPhase || 0;\\n    if (organ.userData.beat) organ.userData.beat.value = Math.sin(beat * Math.PI * 2) * 0.5 + 0.5;\\n    mixer.update(dt);\\n    const danger = state.vitals != null ? Math.max(0, (40 - state.vitals) / 40) : 0;\\n    if (ink) {\\n      ink.u.danger.value = danger * boil;\\n      ink.u.hushRadius.value = state.hush ? Math.min(1.8, (state.hushT || 0.4) * 2) : 0;\\n      ink.u.flash.value = Math.max(0, (ink.u.flash.value || 0) - dt * 2);\\n      ink.u.speedLines.value = Math.max(0, (ink.u.speedLines.value || 0) - dt);\\n    }\\n    const seen = new Set();\\n    for (const seat of state.seats || []) {\\n      if (seat.out) continue;\\n      const rig = ensureTip(seat);\\n      const p = fieldToWorld(seat.x, seat.y, 0.16);\\n      rig.position.lerp(p, 0.65);\\n      rig.rotation.z = -0.4;\\n\",\"total_lines\":489}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6a80b14d-f09f-4985-a4fb-9a4167558005"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_876","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The sync function is called from draw when a simulation is active.\n\nIn test mode, draw() still runs every animation frame even when warp is zero. Sync therefore decays speedLines by 1/60 each frame. Software WebGPU renders at roughly 260–410 ms per frame, so the decay happens across several screenshots.\n\nThe slow decay leaves speedLines near 0.83 across the first few frames, which explains the heavy rays. Because render dt is much smaller than sim dt, the one-second fade lasts roughly eighteen seconds of wall-clock time and the rays stick too long. The fix is to either zero speedLines immediately when leaving the shout or decay based on a timestamp.\n\nDecaying by a fixed dt of 1/60 per frame is too slow. At three frames per second, one second of visual fade takes twenty seconds of wall-clock time. The decay should instead use the real frame delta or a fixed fraction that fades within a few frames.\n\nDecaying by 8% per frame would clear the rays in about twelve frames, but that is still too slow for the calm shot. The better approach is to zero speedLines immediately when leaving the shout via `shout(false)`, letting decay handle only the tail during the active frame. The `shout` function is being updated to toggle cutGroup visibility.\n\nThe `shout` function will set `ink.u.speedLines.value` to 1 when turning on and 0 when turning off. During a shout line, `present()` resets the value to 1 every story frame, so the rays stay bright; leaving the line zeros them immediately. When operation starts, `present` calls `shout(false)` once to clear them before sync begins decaying from zero. The current shot run will still show speed lines early in operations.\n\nThe calm, portrait, and early strain shots will be recaptured after the speedLines fix. Later shots in this run may still show lingering lines if decay is too slow.\n\nThe current run will continue through card, hush, danger, and strains. Hush and danger are meant to look dramatic, so speed lines on danger might be acceptable.\n\nNext steps include fixing the about chunking, checking BPM spacing with a crop, and inspecting the portrait crop. The bust RT camera likely cuts off the head at the chin.\n\nThe about page will be reorganized to pack fields by cost rather than splitting every source field onto its own page. The first source page will group three or four short fields together instead of showing only the date. A magick crop of the op-calm center-top region is planned while waiting, and the settings and cut-in sections will be checked quickly. It is also necessary to verify whether 72 overlaps the objective.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2ae5f5e0-6535-4b35-a245-44e6717e64ac-97","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots\"\nmagick \"$SCRATCH/op-calm.png\" -crop 520x640+700+0 +repage \"$SCRATCH/crop-hud.png\"\nmagick \"$SCRATCH/story-shout.png\" -crop 700x500+150+350 +repage \"$SCRATCH/crop-faces2.png\"\nmagick \"$SCRATCH/hud-portrait.png\" -crop 280x320+40+620 +repage \"$SCRATCH/crop-bust.png\"\necho ok","description":"Crop HUD, faces, and portrait for inspection"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1117,"output_tokens":1383,"cache_read_input_tokens":149376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"14adb4a8-b372-4892-98a4-afcd36725c63"}
