{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_877","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-57ccff7b-22b9-4e3f-abb3-8610e9012ce5-98","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots/crop-hud.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-57ccff7b-22b9-4e3f-abb3-8610e9012ce5-99","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots/crop-faces2.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-57ccff7b-22b9-4e3f-abb3-8610e9012ce5-100","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots/crop-bust.png"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1491,"output_tokens":225,"cache_read_input_tokens":150400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e7016c48-b758-46dc-b287-3ac264797600"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-57ccff7b-22b9-4e3f-abb3-8610e9012ce5-98","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/png\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-57ccff7b-22b9-4e3f-abb3-8610e9012ce5-99","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/png\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-57ccff7b-22b9-4e3f-abb3-8610e9012ce5-100","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/png\"}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"fa7de7fc-b4ff-4dd0-b847-e1f74e34486c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_878","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The HUD crop confirms 72 sits well below the ECG line, not a tight stack.\n\nThe 100 and 72 are separated by roughly 150–200 pixels, not a 0.15rem gap. The HTML places the timer inside a separate `.hud-mid` div below the ECG line, and `.hud-top` uses flexbox with `justify-content: space-between`.\n\nThe `.hud-mid` container uses `flex-direction: column` with a 0.15rem gap. The large gap likely stems from the ECG line being unusually tall, a duplicate 72 rendered elsewhere, or the parent grid row stretching the flex column.\n\nThe `.hud-mid` container has no height or stretch rules, so it should stay tight. The 0.15rem gap likely comes from the ECG line itself being taller than expected, perhaps from a lingering `height: 2.2rem` rule in the built CSS.\n\nA 2.2rem ECG line would only add about 35 pixels of height, which is too small to explain the large gap. The crop also shows the 100 and 72 sitting on the right side of the frame, not centered under the line as expected.\n\nThe 100 and 72 are likely right-aligned within the center column, which explains their position on the right side of the crop. The vertical gap is roughly 7.5rem, far larger than the intended 0.15rem. There is no margin on `.timer`.\n\nThe browser default paragraph margin is the culprit. `.timer` uses `font-size: 3.5rem`, so its 1em top and bottom margins equal roughly 56 pixels each. Those margins stack between the vitals text, the ECG line, and the BPM timer to create the ~118 pixel gap. The fix is to zero out paragraph margins.\n\nThe fix will zero out default margins on `.vitals`, `.timer`, `.score`, `.bpm`, `.obj`, `.note`, `.bark`, and `.who`. The objective text already looked fine, but the note element may also need clearing to prevent HUD overlap. The current shot run is still capturing operations with the gap.\n\nThe current run will finish first to preserve story, title, menu, and strain shots. Then I will fix margins, speed lines, and about packing, rebuild, and recapture only the affected operations and about shots. Speed lines will be zeroed when shouting ends. About sizing logic also needs adjustment. Portrait looks correct with eyes, mouth, and upright positioning above the wheel.\n\nThe face crop looks clean with eyes, brows, mouth, and cap in place. The earlier \"spikes\" are ink speed lines crossing the face rather than hair locks. Speed lines should remain during shouts and be cleared otherwise.\n\nThe audit reports zero issues because the numbers stay inside the safe area. The overlap with the wound is a visual problem that only manual review catches.\n\nI will edit the source CSS now while the browser run continues, then rebuild after the process exits to avoid conflicts. I will also set `shout(false)` to zero so the story shot clears speed lines immediately. I have started rewriting the about slides packing logic.\n\nThe about slides packing logic now groups lines by page cost. Each line’s weight equals its length divided by 80, rounded up to at least one. A page holds lines until the running total reaches five; then it starts a new page. For example, date, source, plan, and genre fit on the first page, while perspective begins the next.\n\nThe about page now fits roughly three lines per slide, so the note reads 1 / 6. I will zero paragraph margins and apply the fixes now, then wait for the shot run to finish before rebuilding. I can also check settings.png since that shot likely already captured.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6ff48780-50a0-4aa3-90e3-10e8caf7906f-101","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/ui/ui.css","old_string":".obj { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; max-width: 36rem; }\n.hud-mid { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 0.15rem; }\n.vitals, .timer, .score, .bpm { font-size: 3.5rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; text-align: center; }","new_string":".obj { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; max-width: 36rem; margin: 0; }\n.hud-mid { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 0.15rem; }\n.vitals, .timer, .score, .bpm { font-size: 3.5rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; text-align: center; margin: 0; }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6ff48780-50a0-4aa3-90e3-10e8caf7906f-102","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/view/renderer.js","old_string":"  function shout(on) {\n    cutGroup.visible = !!on;\n    if (ink && on) ink.u.speedLines.value = 1;\n  }","new_string":"  function shout(on) {\n    cutGroup.visible = !!on;\n    if (ink) ink.u.speedLines.value = on ? 1 : 0;\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6ff48780-50a0-4aa3-90e3-10e8caf7906f-103","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","old_string":"      const size = lines.some((line) => line.length > 140) ? 1 : 3;\n      const count = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(lines.length / size));\n      for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n        slides.push({ head: key, label, lines: lines.slice(i * size, (i + 1) * size), part: i + 1, parts: count });\n      }","new_string":"      const groups = [];\n      let cur = [];\n      let cost = 0;\n      for (const line of lines) {\n        const weight = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(line.length / 80));\n        if (cur.length && cost + weight > 5) {\n          groups.push(cur);\n          cur = [];\n          cost = 0;\n        }\n        cur.push(line);\n        cost += weight;\n      }\n      if (cur.length || !groups.length) groups.push(cur);\n      groups.forEach((chunk, i) => {\n        slides.push({ head: key, label, lines: chunk, part: i + 1, parts: groups.length });\n      });"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1421,"output_tokens":2776,"cache_read_input_tokens":151808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d132df10-7fb2-4d4c-8678-ad19248662de"}
