{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1bb95d24-7ab0-4662-8c9f-ccb8b47d1ad3-122","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1625→  const api = {\\n    state,\\n    audio,\\n    devRun(id, arg) { return runDev(model, id, arg); },\\n  };\\n1630→  if (model.test) {\\n    api.test = {\\n      step(n) {\\n        const count = Math.max(0, n | 0);\\n        for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) stepOnce();\\n      },\\n      warp(n) { model.warp = n | 0; },\\n      input(frame) { model.override = frame || null; },\\n      bot(on, opts) {\\n        model.botOn = !!on;\\n1640→        if (opts) model.botOpts = opts;\\n      },\\n      skipTo(op, phase) {\\n        model.flow = model.flow || 'free';\\n        model.opId = op;\\n        freeSim();\\n        model.sim = new Sim({\\n          op, seed: 1, physics: false, tuning: model.tuning,\\n          difficulty: model.settings.difficulty || 'resident', players: 1,\\n        });\\n1650→        if (phase) model.sim.skipTo(phase);\\n        model.resultShown = false;\\n        model.overlay = null;\\n        setScreen('Operation');\\n      },\\n      hash() { return model.sim ? model.sim.hash() : ''; },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  let raf = 0;\\n1660→  let timer = 0;\\n  function draw() {\\n    if (model.mode === 'session' || !model.view || model.norender || model.painting) return;\\n    model.painting = true;\\n    try {\\n      if (model.sim && (model.attract.on || model.screen === 'Operation')) {\\n        model.view.showOr?.();\\n        model.view.sync(decorateState(model.sim.state), 1 / 60);\\n      } else if (model.screen === 'Story') present();\\n    } catch { /* draw again next frame */ }\\n1670→    const drawn = model.view.render?.();\\n    if (drawn?.then) drawn.then(() => { model.painting = false; }, () => { model.painting = false; });\\n    else model.painting = false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function loop() {\\n    raf = requestAnimationFrame(loop);\\n    if (model.mode === 'session') return;\\n    checkAttract();\\n    if (model.test && !(model.warp > 0)) {\\n1680→      /* scripted steps own the sim */\\n    } else {\\n      const n = model.warp > 0 ? model.warp : 1;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) stepOnce();\\n    }\\n    draw();\\n  }\\n\\n  function wantsTouch() {\\n    const mq = window.matchMedia?.('(any-pointer: fine)');\\n1690→    if (!mq) return false;\\n    return mq.matches === false && !model.input.seenPad;\\n  }\\n\\n  async function bootView() {\",\"content_concise\":\"1625→  const api = {\\n    state,\\n    audio,\\n    devRun(id, arg) { return runDev(model, id, arg); },\\n  };\\n1630→  if (model.test) {\\n    api.test = {\\n      step(n) {\\n        const count = Math.max(0, n | 0);\\n        for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) stepOnce();\\n      },\\n      warp(n) { model.warp = n | 0; },\\n      input(frame) { model.override = frame || null; },\\n      bot(on, opts) {\\n        model.botOn = !!on;\\n1640→        if (opts) model.botOpts = opts;\\n      },\\n      skipTo(op, phase) {\\n        model.flow = model.flow || 'free';\\n        model.opId = op;\\n        freeSim();\\n        model.sim = new Sim({\\n          op, seed: 1, physics: false, tuning: model.tuning,\\n          difficulty: model.settings.difficulty || 'resident', players: 1,\\n        });\\n1650→        if (phase) model.sim.skipTo(phase);\\n        model.resultShown = false;\\n        model.overlay = null;\\n        setScreen('Operation');\\n      },\\n      hash() { return model.sim ? model.sim.hash() : ''; },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  let raf = 0;\\n1660→  let timer = 0;\\n  function draw() {\\n    if (model.mode === 'session' || !model.view || model.norender || model.painting) return;\\n    model.painting = true;\\n    try {\\n      if (model.sim && (model.attract.on || model.screen === 'Operation')) {\\n        model.view.showOr?.();\\n        model.view.sync(decorateState(model.sim.state), 1 / 60);\\n      } else if (model.screen === 'Story') present();\\n    } catch { /* draw again next frame */ }\\n1670→    const drawn = model.view.render?.();\\n    if (drawn?.then) drawn.then(() => { model.painting = false; }, () => { model.painting = false; });\\n    else model.painting = false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function loop() {\\n    raf = requestAnimationFrame(loop);\\n    if (model.mode === 'session') return;\\n    checkAttract();\\n    if (model.test && !(model.warp > 0)) {\\n1680→      /* scripted steps own the sim */\\n    } else {\\n      const n = model.warp > 0 ? model.warp : 1;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) stepOnce();\\n    }\\n    draw();\\n  }\\n\\n  function wantsTouch() {\\n    const mq = window.matchMedia?.('(any-pointer: fine)');\\n1690→    if (!mq) return false;\\n    return mq.matches === false && !model.input.seenPad;\\n  }\\n\\n  async function bootView() {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js\",\"offset\":1625,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"  const api = {\\n    state,\\n    audio,\\n    devRun(id, arg) { return runDev(model, id, arg); },\\n  };\\n  if (model.test) {\\n    api.test = {\\n      step(n) {\\n        const count = Math.max(0, n | 0);\\n        for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) stepOnce();\\n      },\\n      warp(n) { model.warp = n | 0; },\\n      input(frame) { model.override = frame || null; },\\n      bot(on, opts) {\\n        model.botOn = !!on;\\n        if (opts) model.botOpts = opts;\\n      },\\n      skipTo(op, phase) {\\n        model.flow = model.flow || 'free';\\n        model.opId = op;\\n        freeSim();\\n        model.sim = new Sim({\\n          op, seed: 1, physics: false, tuning: model.tuning,\\n          difficulty: model.settings.difficulty || 'resident', players: 1,\\n        });\\n        if (phase) model.sim.skipTo(phase);\\n        model.resultShown = false;\\n        model.overlay = null;\\n        setScreen('Operation');\\n      },\\n      hash() { return model.sim ? model.sim.hash() : ''; },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  let raf = 0;\\n  let timer = 0;\\n  function draw() {\\n    if (model.mode === 'session' || !model.view || model.norender || model.painting) return;\\n    model.painting = true;\\n    try {\\n      if (model.sim && (model.attract.on || model.screen === 'Operation')) {\\n        model.view.showOr?.();\\n        model.view.sync(decorateState(model.sim.state), 1 / 60);\\n      } else if (model.screen === 'Story') present();\\n    } catch { /* draw again next frame */ }\\n    const drawn = model.view.render?.();\\n    if (drawn?.then) drawn.then(() => { model.painting = false; }, () => { model.painting = false; });\\n    else model.painting = false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function loop() {\\n    raf = requestAnimationFrame(loop);\\n    if (model.mode === 'session') return;\\n    checkAttract();\\n    if (model.test && !(model.warp > 0)) {\\n      /* scripted steps own the sim */\\n    } else {\\n      const n = model.warp > 0 ? model.warp : 1;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) stepOnce();\\n    }\\n    draw();\\n  }\\n\\n  function wantsTouch() {\\n    const mq = window.matchMedia?.('(any-pointer: fine)');\\n    if (!mq) return false;\\n    return mq.matches === false && !model.input.seenPad;\\n  }\\n\\n  async function bootView() {\\n\",\"total_lines\":1749}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"680b4795-f66c-4b2c-aa56-43855fa5a32e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_888","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"In test mode, rAF only calls draw(), not stepOnce.\n\nHUD numbers freeze because paint/patchLive only runs during setScreen. After a screen change, stepOnce updates the simulation but never repaints the HUD, so vitals stay stuck at their last painted value while the vignette updates correctly. This may also affect play mode.\n\nReal play is equally broken. The main loop and stepOnce never call paint, so HUD vitals stay frozen during operations. They only update when the paint signature changes, such as a phase or bark shift.\n\nBrowser tests likely passed because they read vitals from state rather than the DOM. The fix is to call patchLive() from draw() during Operation screens so HUD numbers stay current.\n\npatchLive() is cheap enough to call every frame. It skips when an async render is already in flight, so the HUD will update on the next frame instead. The danger screenshot will then capture the correct vitals after the fix. One remaining question is whether patchLive is safe if the UI nodes are missing.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f43b1a30-3b23-43fe-8f3f-254f2bb08a3c-123","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"paint\\(|patchLive|syncFromSim","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/session.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":909,"output_tokens":753,"cache_read_input_tokens":169088,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"8aeb8ec0-431f-4d20-9ee6-8d0d30b8becf"}
