tes=3417771 issues=0\\nmain-menu.png screen=Main Menu phase=null vitals= attract=false bytes=3427015 issues=0\\nopened Settings focus music\\nsettings.png screen=Settings phase=null vitals= attract=false bytes=3446988 issues=0\\nafter settings back Main Menu focus story\\nopened About\\nabout.png screen=About phase=null vitals= attract=false bytes=3488236 issues=0\\nstory line NARRATION The beeps land on the bar line. The silhouette bows.\\nstory-shout.png screen=Story phase=null vitals= attract=false bytes=3187267 issues=0\\ncut-in.png screen=Story phase=null vitals= attract=false bytes=3177101 issues=0\\ngo broken-glass glass -> Operation glass vitals=100\\nop-calm.png screen=Operation phase=glass vitals=100 attract=false bytes=3283333 issues=0\\nhud-portrait.png screen=Operation phase=glass vitals=100 attract=false bytes=3283525 issues=0\\nhush.png screen=Operation phase=glass vitals=100 attract=false bytes=2075379 issues=0\\ngo broken-glass glass -> Operation glass vitals=100\\npage.evaluate: Target crashed \\n    at main (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots.mjs:205:29) {\\n  log: [],\\n  name: \\u001b[32m'Error'\\u001b[39m\\n}\\nEXIT:1\\n\",\"total_lines\":26}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e2dd3602-a5e9-4c78-9136-0012c5172775"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_901","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The target crashed during the danger evaluation. An out-of-memory error from software WebGPU caused it, as the summary had warned.\n\nThe crash stems from the danger loop calling paint(false) every step. That triggers up to 1000 DOM rebuilds and WebGPU renders in one evaluate. The previous run had already cleared danger.\n\nTwo fixes are being weighed. Batch paints at the end of each loop instead of every step. Or break the danger loop into chunks with short pauses so the browser can garbage-collect between steps.\n\nBark text is part of the signature. If bleeders bark every step, the HUD rebuilds 1000 times while the 3D scene runs. That likely caused the OOM. patchLive already skips full rebuilds when the signature matches. The game should still update bark via patchLive instead of forcing a full innerHTML rebuild.\n\nThe danger loop will be fixed by inserting `await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 0))` after each 20-step batch. This yields control to the browser between steps so the renderer can catch up and garbage-collect. It trades a little speed for stability.\n\nYielding between steps might not prevent the crash. If memory stays high, earlyoom could still kill the process.\n\nThe real problem is the loop length. Four bleeders drain vitals at roughly four per second, plus pools. Dropping from one hundred to twenty-one vitals takes about nine hundred to twelve hundred frames. That is why the loop runs one thousand steps.\n\nReducing the step count is a better fix than yielding.\n\nThe danger loop will be split into forty thirty-step chunks. Each chunk runs inside its own evaluate call with a pause between them. This lets the browser settle memory between steps instead of running one giant synchronous loop.\n\nThe danger loop is now forty thirty-step chunks, totaling 1200 steps. Each evaluate returns so the browser can paint and garbage-collect between steps.\n\nThe crash left later shots stale from the previous run. The new build already overwrote op-calm, portrait, hush, about, title, and story. Danger, strains, report, and card still hold old data.\n\nThe danger screenshot still shows vitals at one hundred. To avoid repeating the first two minutes, a RESUME=ops flag will be added so the script boots straight to operations and skips menus. The danger loop will also be made safe in shots.mjs.\n\nSkipping the menu shots is not worth the extra flag. The whole script will be rerun so every screenshot comes from one build. The hush capture looks good. A leftover browser process must be killed before relaunch.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-34ea8279-dbfb-4b69-8d61-f9ed925a7585-138","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots.mjs","old_string":"  await go('broken-glass', 'glass');\n  const danger = await page.evaluate(() => {\n    const g = window.__game;\n    g.devRun('freeze');\n    for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) g.devRun('bleeder');\n    let last = g.state();\n    for (let n = 0; n < 50; n++) {\n      g.test.step(20);\n      last = g.state();\n      if (last.vitals < 22 || last.screen !== 'Operation') break;\n    }\n    return { screen: last.screen, vitals: last.vitals, phase: last.phase };\n  });\n  say('danger ' + JSON.stringify(danger));","new_string":"  await go('broken-glass', 'glass');\n  await page.evaluate(() => {\n    const g = window.__game;\n    g.devRun('freeze');\n    for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) g.devRun('bleeder');\n  });\n  let danger = { screen: '', vitals: 100, phase: '' };\n  for (let n = 0; n < 40; n++) {\n    danger = await page.evaluate(() => {\n      window.__game.test.step(30);\n      const last = window.__game.state();\n      return { screen: last.screen, vitals: last.vitals, phase: last.phase };\n    });\n    if (danger.vitals < 22 || danger.screen !== 'Operation') break;\n  }\n  say('danger ' + JSON.stringify(danger));"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-34ea8279-dbfb-4b69-8d61-f9ed925a7585-139","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"pgrep -af 'shots.mjs|playwright_chromiumdev_profile' | grep -E 'x8f49b6|shots.mjs' | head -5 || echo 'clear'","description":"Confirm the crashed screenshot browser exited"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1060,"output_tokens":1857,"cache_read_input_tokens":181888,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6327bb9d-5c32-459d-a118-80d3de78ea21"}
