1,111,117,114,32,98,114,105,101,102,44,32,84,104,114,101,101,46,106,115,44,32,82,97,112,105,101,114,44,32,66,97,110,103,101,114,115,32,97,110,100,32,66,97,114,108,111,119,32,67,111,110,100,101,110,115,101,100,32,40,79,70,76,41,44,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,114,101,110,100,101,114,101,114,32,105,110,32,117,115,101,32,116,104,105,115,32,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,46,10,49,50,48,56,58,124,32,72,101,97,100,108,101,115,115,32,116,101,115,116,115,44,32,111,110,101,32,99,111,109,109,97,110,100,44,32,102,97,105,108,117,114,101,115,32,97,110,100,32,97,32,99,111,117,110,116,44,32,97,32,102,117,108,108,32,115,99,114,105,112,116,101,100,32,112,108,97,121,116,104,114,111,117,103,104,44,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,115,104,111,116,115,32,111,110,108,121,32,119,104,101,110,32,110,101,101,100,101,100,44,32,110,111,32,114,101,118,105,101,119,32,115,117,98,97,103,101,110,116,115,32,124,32,194,167,49,55,32,124,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":18,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"**Perspective:** first-person surgeon's-eye view of a 3D operative field, from a fixed, tilted camera (§9.2). Story scenes are staged third-person two-shots of 3D character busts.\"},{\"line_number\":378,\"content\":\"**Lint:** a test fails if any Bea line contains \\\"good\\\" outside S16. In Op 5 Bea still calls the barks and trades shots with Ines. In Op 6 Ines interjects over comms. In Op 7 every bark comes from Pip reading the notebook.\"},{\"line_number\":423,\"content\":\"### 8.4 Ten-foot rules (tests can't judge these; check at 1920×1080)\"},{\"line_number\":432,\"content\":\"The field fills the center, and the HUD holds the edges. At 1080p the drape window leaves about 100 px clear at the top and 190 px at the bottom, so keep the ECG band shallow and let the portrait use the bottom.\"},{\"line_number\":440,\"content\":\"| Bottom center | The current voice's portrait (live 3D bust, §9.6; Bea, Pip in Op 7) and the bark in a comic bubble |\"},{\"line_number\":442,\"content\":\"| Bottom center, above portrait | Site tabs (only with more than one site), with an alarm icon when another site is in trouble |\"},{\"line_number\":716,\"content\":\"The host's copy runs the only `Sim`, including Rapier. Everyone else renders snapshots. The host's view reads the sim directly; a client reads its decoded state, with entities and other seats interpolated 100 to 150 ms behind. **Your own tip is always local and instant**, and tool sounds and cosmetic trails start locally. Grades and results come from the host.\"},{\"line_number\":728,\"content\":\"Keep each copy to at most 16 messages/s (the limit is 20, burst 40) with one token-bucket `send()` wrapper that sheds `s` and `i` first. **Any console line starting `[AIHub]` fails the hub's check**, including rate and size warnings, and `finish` called from a non-host. Drop snapshots older than the newest applied. Clients send `i` even when idle, as the harness needs traffic both ways.\"},{\"line_number\":755,\"content\":\"      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\"},{\"line_number\":825,\"content\":\"The view reconciles meshes against `state` by entity id, and turns `events` into particles, paint, sounds and barks. It runs from `sim.state` in solo and couch play, and from decoded snapshots on a hub client: the same code either way. That single decision makes the Node tests, the bot, attract mode, the server copy and co-op all cheap.\"},{\"line_number\":879,\"content\":\"All run here on 2026-11-04: Chromium 153 under Playwright 1.63.0, Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. A skeleton with this stack (a toon scene, Rapier on the host, its own card, snapshots at 10/s with a 1/s keyframe, input at 12/s) passed the hub's harness on WebGPU at 2 players, 4 players on a bad network with one leaving, host-leave and server scenarios. The 4-player run also passed without WebGPU, on the WebGL2 fallback. The skeleton's scene was small: your real game will take longer in these runs, so allow for it.\"},{\"line_number\":1036,\"content\":\"Tune `line`, thresholds and colors to taste at 1920×1080. If you add outline-worthy color edges (a stripe on one surface), remember the filter only sees depth and normal breaks, so paint them dark.\"},{\"line_number\":1061,\"content\":\"const portrait = new THREE.Mesh(plane, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: rt.texture }));\"},{\"line_number\":1128,\"content\":\"- **Full UI playthrough** with `?test=1&norender=1`, the bot and `warp`: New Game through every scene and operation to the credits, using real menu inputs. `state().reached` contains Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report and Credits roll. Other tests here cover Fail, Free Play, Lobby, Settings, About and Touch notice; the hub suite covers the session card.\"},{\"line_number\":1143,\"content\":\"**Screenshots, only for what scripts can't judge.** At 1920×1080: Title, Main Menu, one story scene with a shout, Operation at a calm moment, Operation in danger, Hush, each strain once, Report, Settings, About, session card. Add one HUD portrait and one cut-in: faces must be upright. Look for: text legibility from ten feet, ink quality, overlaps. Fix what you see.\"},{\"line_number\":1158,\"content\":\"8. **Multiplayer.** Snapshots, couch lobby, session, card. All hub runs pass.\"},{\"line_number\":1169,\"content\":\"**About & Credits screen.** Your brief lists four blocks that must appear both in your chat reply and on this screen: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback. Give each block its own pages at ten-foot size, a few short answers per page, moved through with L1/R1 or Q/E, never a dense wall. Add a credits page: the model line from your brief, Three.js, Rapier, Bangers and Barlow Condensed (OFL), and the renderer in use this session.\"},{\"line_number\":1208,\"content\":\"| Headless tests, one command, failures and a count, a full scripted playthrough, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | §17 |\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6bd275f1-c9bf-40c9-b464-efbefe45d329-16","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,56,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,46,103,114,111,107,47,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,115,47,37,50,70,104,111,109,101,37,50,70,109,105,99,104,97,37,50,70,100,101,118,37,50,70,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,37,50,70,114,117,110,115,37,50,70,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,37,50,70,119,111,114,107,47,48,49,97,49,97,97,53,54,45,54,50,51,49,45,55,99,102,48,45,97,54,54,54,45,100,102,53,102,98,98,48,57,48,55,49,48,47,103,111,97,108,47,112,108,97,110,46,109,100,10,49,51,58,52,46,32,80,108,97,121,97,98,108,101,32,112,114,101,115,101,110,116,97,116,105,111,110,44,32,105,110,112,117,116,44,32,97,110,100,32,115,104,101,108,108,46,32,84,104,101,32,115,104,105,112,112,101,100,32,112,97,103,101,32,98,111,111,116,115,32,97,32,84,104,114,101,101,46,106,115,32,114,49,56,48,32,115,99,101,110,101,32,119,105,116,104,32,99,101,108,45,115,104,97,100,101,100,47,116,111,111,110,32,109,97,116,101,114,105,97,108,115,44,32,116,104,101,32,105,110,107,47,104,97,108,102,116,111,110,101,32,102,105,108,116