9,104,32,99,104,101,99,107,46,10,53,48,58,45,32,83,111,102,116,119,97,114,101,32,87,101,98,71,80,85,32,105,115,32,126,50,54,48,226,128,147,52,49,48,32,109,115,47,102,114,97,109,101,32,97,110,100,32,101,97,114,108,121,111,111,109,32,107,105,108,108,115,32,101,120,116,114,97,32,98,114,111,119,115,101,114,115,46,32,72,117,98,32,114,117,110,115,32,109,97,121,32,110,101,101,100,32,116,104,101,32,102,117,108,108,32,51,48,48,32,115,32,98,117,100,103,101,116,46,32,82,117,110,32,111,110,101,32,98,114,111,119,115,101,114,46,32,73,102,32,116,104,101,32,104,97,114,110,101,115,115,32,112,114,111,99,101,115,115,32,105,116,115,101,108,102,32,99,97,110,110,111,116,32,115,116,97,114,116,44,32,99,97,112,116,117,114,101,32,116,104,97,116,32,108,111,103,59,32,100,111,32,110,111,116,32,115,117,98,115,116,105,116,117,116,101,32,97,32,109,111,99,107,101,100,32,104,117,98,32,114,101,115,117,108,116,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":8,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"4. Playable presentation, input, and shell. The shipped page boots a Three.js r180 scene with cel-shaded/toon materials, the ink/halftone filter, code-built organs, instruments, and strains, and Rapier-backed pulls, on WebGPU under PLAN §16.3’s five flags and on WebGL2 without them, with zero page errors. The render surface’s drawing size equals the requested size and is substantially filled (not a blank or a few pixels). Pad (standard mapping), keyboard, and mouse drive the same screens: tip, eight-way wheel, analog use, hover-moves-focus, prompts follow the last device (`data-prompt-set`; PlayStation glyphs default, Xbox via Settings). All music, effects, and Animalese/Simlish voices are synthesized (no audio files); music-bus gain defaults to 0.10. Touch-only (`(any-pointer: fine)` false and no pad) shows exactly “Controller or keyboard required” plus a tappable Settings button, no touch controls, and attract mode still runs. Attract mode starts after 10 s of wall-clock idle on Titl [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"2. gating: Browser suite (`node tests/run-all.mjs browser`) drives the shipped page, including `?test=1` hooks that call into the real sim, and asserts criterion 4: WebGPU boot with the five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, WebGL2 boot without them, WebKit boot, zero page errors, non-blank shots, pad/mouse/key input (full right stick for 1 s moves the tip by `tipSpeed` ±5%), prompt set and Xbox glyphs, dev-mode slider changes the sim and reset restores defaults, attract at 10 s ±1 s and exit without a save, Pixel 7 and iPhone 15 profiles show the exact touch notice and a working Settings tap, OfflineAudioContext output is non-silent for every track, effect, and voice, music gain 0.10, no audio-file references, save survives reload, About fields and `#about-data` parse, two stub pads score in couch play, UI playthrough `state().reached` contains Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Opera [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"4. gating: Launch the real root HTML twice, from `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1` (bind `127.0.0.1` on an OS-picked port; confirm `window.__game` exists before trusting the page). Use the five flags above. Each run: zero page errors; canvas drawing buffer equals the requested size; painted fraction is high (a blank or speck fails — do not treat a successful blank readback as a missing tool); a driven input (stub pad or mouse) changes the on-screen tip or HUD, visible in a second capture. Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch.log` and rely on steps 1–3; a started browser that returns an empty buffer is a failure to fix.\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"Follow PLAN.md for rules and content; the layout there is guidance so the sim stays testable, not a reason to reject an equivalent structure. Keep the operation sim pure (JSON state, seeded RNG, fixed 1/60, Rapier in field space) so Node tests and the bot drive it with no browser. Let the view, audio, and DOM reconcile that state or a decoded snapshot, never own the rules. Build operations, strains, and scenes as data. Ship one command that runs sim, then browser, then hub, and prints only failures and a count. Inline the browser bundle so `file://` works. Use the five WebGPU flags from PLAN §16.3, not the shorter set in TASK.md. One browser at a time. Stop only processes this work started, by PID.\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"- [x] Calibrate `parScore`, write the authoring note, fill About and `exit-interview.json`, copy the HTML to the root name, and save sim, browser, hub, and two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\"},{\"line_number\":49,\"content\":\"- TASK.md’s shorter WebGPU flags drop the device after the first frame on this machine; PLAN §16.3’s five flags are the ones that draw. A blank readback with those five flags is an app bug, not an excuse to skip the launch check.\"},{\"line_number\":50,\"content\":\"- Software WebGPU is ~260–410 ms/frame and earlyoom kills extra browsers. Hub runs may need the full 300 s budget. Run one browser. If the harness process itself cannot start, capture that log; do not substitute a mocked hub result.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"385c339c-2306-4b9e-9c23-5c0cb362f94f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_927","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A clear fix has been identified. PLAN 8 will be reviewed next.\n\nThe 3D portrait shows through the session card overlay. The fix is to call setPortrait in syncFromSim based on screen state. This hides the portrait on the card and keeps it visible during operations.\n\nNeed to check ui.css overlay and screen backgrounds. The portrait may overlap settings buttons during operation pause if the overlay doesn't fully cover the lower left. Cut-in during session is operation-only.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fa199265-c959-466c-af08-e6a0283c31f3-17","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"present\\(","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fa199265-c959-466c-af08-e6a0283c31f3-18","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/bundled/skills/long-running-background-tasks/SKILL.md","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fa199265-c959-466c-af08-e6a0283c31f3-19","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"card|session-card|harness","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/shots.mjs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5402,"output_tokens":553,"cache_read_input_tokens":44544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"0385f4d5-21a6-4b86-abe6-17eef2e27129"}
