16,101,112,83,116,114,97,105,110,115,96,46,32,82,101,97,100,32,96,115,105,109,46,116,117,110,105,110,103,96,32,102,111,114,32,104,105,116,32,112,111,105,110,116,115,44,32,115,112,101,101,100,44,32,97,110,100,32,100,97,109,97,103,101,46,32,68,111,32,110,111,116,32,99,97,108,108,32,96,77,97,116,104,46,114,97,110,100,111,109,96,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":16,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/bridge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":283,\"content\":\"export function createLocalNetwork({ latency = 0, jitter = 0, loss = 0, random = Math.random, clock = globalThis } = {}) {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/round.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":48,\"content\":\" * Math.random and every copy starts the same: read from the game's own tag,\"},{\"line_number\":50,\"content\":\" * (ids it makes from Math.random must differ between its copies), so it keeps one.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/browser/suite.mjs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":81,\"content\":\"    if (rel.startsWith('src/sim') && text.includes('Math.random')) check('no Math.random in sim', false, rel);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":792,\"content\":\"These are all reproduced in §17: it plays shared worlds at 2, 3 and 4 players at 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss, with a player leaving; `scenario=host-leave`; `scenario=server` at 2 players. It checks the client is exactly one unmodified copy (SHA-256, §16.2). Then, on its own: opens the page, presses Enter, Space, Enter, Space, checks that nothing threw, `AIHub.active` is false, `Math.random` is untouched, and the screenshot isn't blank.\"},{\"line_number\":827,\"content\":\"- All randomness in the sim comes from a seeded generator passed in. `Math.random` is banned from `src/sim` by a test.\"},{\"line_number\":1129,\"content\":\"- Packaging: one file, no external script or font URLs, exactly one pristine client (§16.2), hub tags match the §14.6 regex form, no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder` or `stub` in `src/` (search your own source, not the output: the engines' bundled code can contain those words), no `Math.random` in `src/sim`, title string only in `identity.js`.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/sim/rules.mjs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":273,\"content\":\"  pass('no Math.random in sim', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":277,\"content\":\"      if (text.includes('Math.random')) return path.relative(root, file);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tools/vendor/session.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":38,\"content\":\"    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\"},{\"line_number\":115,\"content\":\"  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\"},{\"line_number\":117,\"content\":\"  var realRandom = Math.random;\"},{\"line_number\":120,\"content\":\"    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\"},{\"line_number\":149,\"content\":\"   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\"},{\"line_number\":155,\"content\":\"    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/docs/AUTHORING.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":54,\"content\":\"2. Handle that `kind` in `src/sim/strains.js`, inside `stepStrains`. Read `sim.tuning` for hit points, speed, and damage. Do not call `Math.random`.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-920cf244-79be-427b-be64-2d83ba8ecdf8-51","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:12:30\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical action (arcade operation game) with a visual-novel story\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"First-person surgeon's-eye 3D operative field; staged third-person story scenes\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js r180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback), TSL ink post-filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2; hub session client 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Comic-book medical drama: cel-shaded toon materials, ink outline filter, manga tone, all geometry made in code\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Three.js AnimationMixer with code-built clips, skinned strains, procedural follow-through\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"All synthesized in code: step-sequenced music, procedural effects, Animalese-style gibberish voices; music at 10% by default\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players; couch co-op on its own\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim suite 51 checks, Playwright browser suite 80 checks on Chromium and WebKit, hub harness 23 checks. No physical controller, no second human, no real iOS device.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"AI Hub protocol and harness, engine prototypes on this computer, and the plan's notes on the source.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"The sim suite (51 checks) and the hub harness (23 checks) caught the issues that would have shipped. The browser suite (80 checks) caught UI timing: attract was swallowing the next confirm, and a reload was dropping screens the playthrough had already opened.\\\",\\n    \\\"A few were critical: a story line that failed the Bea lint, snapshot traffic that could trip the hub rate warning, and a ready() call that the client ignores if it happens before welcome.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the Normal bot playthrough with the 45 to 75 percent clear-time band. It kept the operations honest.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was staring at a single still of the title. Behavior checks found the breaks. A picture did not.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"MeshToonNodeMaterial plus the ink graph is a complete look from primitives, and the hub client is small enough to read.\\\",\\n    \\\"WebGPU on this machine needs five browser flags or the device dies after one frame. Rapier must be initialized before the first world, and ready() is a no-op until the welcome arrives.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation sim, the bot, and the snapshot codec. The engine draws and hears. It does not know surgery.\\\",\\n    \\\"Software WebGPU is slow enough that a test has to drive the sim with step and warp, and four inked views in one harness is a memory tightrope.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Nothing in the engine source. The operative rules live in this game.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to boot SwiftShader WebGPU without a private flag recipe, and a ready() that queues until welcome instead of vanishing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan is specific about feel: ten-foot type, one patient, four surgeons, and a story that knows when to be quiet.\\\",\\n    \\\"Two WebGPU flag lists disagree. The shorter one draws a blank here. The plan's five flags are the ones that work.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping a sloppy four-surgeon coda inside the rules without moving the Normal scores, then proving the hub harness on software WebGPU.\\\",\\n    \\\"Say once, in the prompt, which browser flags this computer actually needs.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"credits\\\": [\\n40→    \\\"xAI grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh, via Grok CLI\\\",\\n    \\\"Three.js r180\\\",\\n    \\\"Rapier 0.19.3\\\",\\n    \\\"Bangers and Barlow Condensed, SIL Open Font License\\\",\\n    \\\"AI Hub session client 1.4.0\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:12:30\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical action (arcade operation game) with a visual-novel story\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"First-person surgeon's-eye 3D operative field; staged third-person story scenes\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js r180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback), TSL ink post-filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2; hub session client 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Comic-book medical drama: cel-shaded toon materials, ink outline filter, manga tone, all geometry made in code\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Three.js AnimationMixer with code-built clips, skinned strains, procedural follow-through\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"All synthesized in code: step-sequenced music, procedural effects, Animalese-style gibberish voices; music at 10% by default\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players; couch co-op on its own\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim suite 51 checks, Playwright browser suite 80 checks on Chromium and WebKit, hub harness 23 checks. No physical controller, no second human, no real iOS device.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"AI Hub protocol and harness, engine prototypes on this computer, and the plan's notes on the source.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"The sim suite (51 checks) and the hub harness (23 checks) caught the issues that would have shipped. The browser suite (80 checks) caught UI timing: attract was swallowing the next confirm, and a reload was dropping screens the playthrough had already opened.\\\",\\n    \\\"A few were critical: a story line that failed the Bea lint, snapshot traffic that could trip the hub rate warning, and a ready() call that the client ignores if it happens before welcome.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the Normal bot playthrough with the 45 to 75 percent clear-time band. It kept the operations honest.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was staring at a single still of the title. Behavior checks found the breaks. A picture did not.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"MeshToonNodeMaterial plus the ink graph is a complete look from primitives, and the hub client is small enough to read.\\\",\\n    \\\"WebGPU on this machine needs five browser flags or the device dies after one frame. Rapier must be initialized before the first world, and ready() is a no-op until the welcome arrives.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation sim, the bot, and the snapshot codec. The engine draws and hears. It does not know surgery.\\\",\\n    \\\"Software WebGPU is slow enough that a test has to drive the sim with step and warp, and four inked views in one harness is a memory tightrope.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Nothing in the engine source. The operative rules live in this game.\\\",\\n    \\\"A supported way to boot Swi