{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-41a9eef9-2a37-4925-a9d3-b0373b14bc83-98","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Progress\\n\\nThe title was chosen with `crypto.randomInt` from 50 candidates and stored only in `src/config/identity.js` inside the dev folder. No other source file may contain that string.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Dev folder, package, vendored AI Hub session client 1.4.0, and the single-file build.\\n- Headless sim, operations, bot, and sim suite: 0 failed, 51 passed.\\n- View, audio, menus, save, attract, dev mode, couch, and hub session.\\n10→- The operative portrait shows during an operation and stays off the session card. The card countdown sits with the seat list.\\n- Browser suite: 0 failed, 80 passed. Hub harness: 0 failed, 23 passed. Two WebGPU launches of the root page agree.\\n- Authoring note, About data, exit interview, and 1920×1080 shots of the title, menus, story, operation, strains, report, and session card.\\n\\n## Now\\n\\n- Hand-in is in this folder.\\n\\n## Next\\n\\n20→- Nothing further on this machine.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Progress\\n\\nThe title was chosen with `crypto.randomInt` from 50 candidates and stored only in `src/config/identity.js` inside the dev folder. No other source file may contain that string.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Dev folder, package, vendored AI Hub session client 1.4.0, and the single-file build.\\n- Headless sim, operations, bot, and sim suite: 0 failed, 51 passed.\\n- View, audio, menus, save, attract, dev mode, couch, and hub session.\\n10→- The operative portrait shows during an operation and stays off the session card. The card countdown sits with the seat list.\\n- Browser suite: 0 failed, 80 passed. Hub harness: 0 failed, 23 passed. Two WebGPU launches of the root page agree.\\n- Authoring note, About data, exit interview, and 1920×1080 shots of the title, menus, story, operation, strains, report, and session card.\\n\\n## Now\\n\\n- Hand-in is in this folder.\\n\\n## Next\\n\\n20→- Nothing further on this machine.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Progress\\n\\nThe title was chosen with `crypto.randomInt` from 50 candidates and stored only in `src/config/identity.js` inside the dev folder. No other source file may contain that string.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Dev folder, package, vendored AI Hub session client 1.4.0, and the single-file build.\\n- Headless sim, operations, bot, and sim suite: 0 failed, 51 passed.\\n- View, audio, menus, save, attract, dev mode, couch, and hub session.\\n- The operative portrait shows during an operation and stays off the session card. The card countdown sits with the seat list.\\n- Browser suite: 0 failed, 80 passed. Hub harness: 0 failed, 23 passed. Two WebGPU launches of the root page agree.\\n- Authoring note, About data, exit interview, and 1920×1080 shots of the title, menus, story, operation, strains, report, and session card.\\n\\n## Now\\n\\n- Hand-in is in this folder.\\n\\n## Next\\n\\n- Nothing further on this machine.\\n\",\"total_lines\":20}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-41a9eef9-2a37-4925-a9d3-b0373b14bc83-99","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [completed] gap: Read goal plan, STAGE, TASK, and current hand-in to find the remaining gap\\n- [completed] fix: Hide HUD portrait except during Operation/attract\\n- [completed] verify: Rebuild, recapture session card, re-run browser suite and two launches\\n- [completed] shots: Session card recaptured: Ready and More Time are clear\\n- [completed] handin: Update PROGRESS.md without the title string; confirm hand-in files\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Read goal plan, STAGE, TASK, and current hand-in to find the remaining gap\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Hide HUD portrait except during Operation/attract\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Rebuild, recapture session card, re-run browser suite and two launches\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Session card recaptured: Ready and More Time are clear\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Update PROGRESS.md without the title string; confirm hand-in files\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"gap\":{\"content\":\"Read goal plan, STAGE, TASK, and current hand-in to find the remaining gap\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"fix\":{\"content\":\"Hide HUD portrait except during Operation/attract\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"verify\":{\"content\":\"Rebuild, recapture session card, re-run browser suite and two launches\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"shots\":{\"content\":\"Session card recaptured: Ready and More Time are clear\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"handin\":{\"content\":\"Update PROGRESS.md without the title string; confirm hand-in files\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}}}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d2755b3a-e4da-4548-a37a-77d161b3a74f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_973","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The reply needs four \"about\" blocks.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The hand-in is in this folder. The session card no longer paints the operative portrait over Ready and More Time, and the countdown sits with the seat list.\n\nThe rebuilt page matches in the dev folder, the root HTML, and the hub copy. The sim suite is 0 failed, 51 passed. The browser suite is 0 failed, 80 passed. The hub harness is 0 failed, 23 passed. Both WebGPU launches of the root page agree: the canvas is 1280×720, the tip moves, and about two-thirds of the frame is painted. The new 1920×1080 session card shows the buttons clear of the bust.\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-04 23:12:30\n- Source: Trauma Center: Second Opinion\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: Surgical action (arcade operation game) with a visual-novel story\n- Perspective: First-person surgeon's-eye 3D operative field; staged third-person story scenes\n- Tech: Three.js r180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback), TSL ink post-filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2; hub session client 1.4.0\n- Art Direction: Comic-book medical drama: cel-shaded toon materials, ink outline filter, manga tone, all geometry made in code\n- Animation: Three.js AnimationMixer with code-built clips, skinned strains, procedural follow-through\n- Audio: All synthesized in code: step-sequenced music, procedural effects, Animalese-style gibberish voices; music at 10% by default\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players; couch co-op on its own\n- Testing: Headless sim suite 51 checks, Playwright browser suite 80 checks on Chromium and WebKit, hub harness 23 checks. No physical controller, no second human, no real iOS device.\n- Research: AI Hub protocol and harness, engine prototypes on this computer, and the plan's notes on the source.\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\n- Usage: added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- The sim suite (51 checks) and the hub harness (23 checks) caught the issues that would have shipped. The browser suite (80 checks) caught UI timing: attract was swallowing the next confirm, and a reload was dropping screens the playthrough had already opened.\n- A few were critical: a story line that failed the Bea lint, snapshot traffic that could trip the hub rate warning, and a ready() call that the client ignores if it happens before welcome.\n- The most helpful test was the Normal bot playthrough with the 45 to 75 percent clear-time band. It kept the operations honest.\n- The least helpful test was staring at a single still of the title. Behavior checks found the breaks. A picture did not.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- MeshToonNodeMaterial plus the ink graph is a complete look from primitives, and the hub client is small enough to read.\n- WebGPU on this machine needs five browser flags or the device dies after one frame. Rapier must be initialized before the first world, and ready() is a no-op until the welcome arrives.\n- The operation sim, the bot, and the snapshot codec. The engine draws and hears. It does not know surgery.\n- Software WebGPU is slow enough that a test has to drive the sim with step and warp, and four inked views in one harness is a memory tightrope.\n- Nothing in the engine source. The operative rules live in this game.\n- A supported way to boot SwiftShader WebGPU without a private flag recipe, and a ready() that queues until welcome instead of vanishing.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- The plan is specific about feel: ten-foot type, one patient, four surgeons, and a story that knows when to be quiet.\n- Two WebGPU flag lists disagree. The shorter one draws a blank here. The plan's five flags are the ones that work.\n- Keeping a sloppy four-surgeon coda inside the rules without moving the Normal scores, then proving the hub harness on software WebGPU.\n- Say once, in the prompt, which browser flags this computer actually needs."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":588,"output_tokens":994,"cache_read_input_tokens":131200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"d5007345-a5b3-468d-a66c-72d9eb53530c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_974","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will act as an adversarial verifier.\n\nI will read STAGE.md, PLAN.md, and TASK.md. I will audit the evidence to verify the work against the objective. Then I will write the verdict files.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll audit the hand-in against STAGE.md, PLAN.md, and TASK.md, starting with the contract and the implementer's captured evidence."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a7489ee6-54b6-4dd4-a158-c7fb615f49d4-0","name":"list_dir","input":{"target_directory":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a7489ee6-54b6-4dd4-a158-c7fb615f49d4-1","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/STAGE.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a7489ee6-54b6-4dd4-a158-c7fb615f49d4-2","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/TASK.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a7489ee6-54b6-4dd4-a158-c7fb615f49d4-3","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6%2Fwork/01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":22159,"output_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":1792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6bbba489-7a56-4955-91a9-1ee28f121342"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a7489ee6-54b6-4dd4-a158-c7fb615f49d4-0","content":"{\"type\":\"ListDir\",\"Content\":{\"content\":\"- /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer/\\n  - boss8.txt\\n  - bots-sweep.txt\\n  - bots.mjs\\n  - browser.log\\n  - card-shot.mjs\\n  - coda-n7.json\\n  - coda-n8.json\\n  - coda-normal.json\\n  - coda-normal3.json\\n  - coda-normal4.json\\n  - coda-normal5.json\\n  - coda-normal6.json\\n  - coda-normal7.json\\n  - coda-normal8.json\\n  - coda-normal9.json\\n  - coda-s7.json\\n  - coda-sloppy.json\\n  - coda-sloppy2.json\\n  - coda-sloppy3.json\\n  - coda-sloppy5.json\\n  - coda-sloppy6.json\\n  - coda-sloppy7.json\\n  - coda-sloppy8.json\\n  - coda-sloppy9.json\\n  - coda-trace4.txt\\n  - coda-trace8.txt\\n  - coda-trace9.txt\\n  - dbg-circle.mjs\\n  - dbg-coda.mjs\\n  - dbg-phases.mjs\\n  - dbg-ring.mjs\\n  - dbg-vmin.mjs\\n  - dbg.mjs\\n  - dbg2.mjs\\n  - dbg3.mjs\\n  - dump-chain.mjs\\n  - gr2.json\\n  - hub.log\\n  - launch-1.png\\n  - launch-2.png\\n  - launch.log\\n  - launch.mjs\\n  - legato-normal2.json\\n  - legato-sloppy.json\\n  - legato-sloppy2.json\\n  - legato-sloppy6.json\\n  - miss.mjs\\n  - one.mjs\\n  - package.log\\n  - phases.mjs\\n  - project.mjs\\n  - shots-run.log\\n  - shots.mjs\\n  - shots/\\n    - about.png\\n    - card-shot.log\\n    - cut-in.png\\n    - hud-portrait.png\\n    - hush.png\\n    - main-menu.png\\n    - op-calm.png\\n    - op-danger.png\\n    - report.png\\n    - session-card.png\\n    - settings.png\\n    - shots.log\\n    - story-shout.png\\n    - strain-adagio.png\\n    - strain-coda.png\\n    - strain-crescendo.png\\n    - strain-fermata.png\\n    - strain-legato.png\\n    - strain-staccato.png\\n    - strain-tremolo.png\\n    - title.png\\n  - sim.log\\n  - smoke-menu.mjs\\n  - smoke.mjs\\n  - snap.mjs\\n  - trace-boss.mjs\\n  - trace-chain.mjs\\n  - trace-recap.mjs\",\"absolute_root_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a7489ee6-54b6-4dd4-a158-c7fb615f49d4-1","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/STAGE.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a7489ee6-54b6-4dd4-a158-c7fb615f49d4-2","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→SOURCE: Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\n\\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\\n\\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\\n\\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\\n\\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\\n10→\\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\\n\\nTech Stack: Use Three.js R180, WEBGPU, use a stylized cel-shaded / ink filter, rapier 0.19.3 for physics, Web Audio, Gamepad API; The rest of the tech stack is yours to choose.\\n\\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\\n\\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\\n\\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\\n20→\\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\\n\\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\\n\\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\\n\\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n30→Effort: Spend effort however you see fit.\\n\\n## This computer\\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\\n\\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\\n40→  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \\\"Target closed\\\", \\\"page crashed\\\" or \\\"browser has been closed\\\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\\n\\n### What this computer doesn't have\\n\\n50→No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\\n\\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\\n\\n### Sharing this computer\\n60→\\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\\n\\n70→Scope\\n\\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\\n\\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\\n\\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\\n\\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\\n\\n80→Narrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\\n\\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\\n\\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\\n\\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\\n\\n## Done\\n90→No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 23:12:30\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n100→- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n110→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\