{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_984","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug exists in the countdown logic.\n\nThe outer condition `clock >= 0` makes the inner `clock < 0` branches unreachable. Because AIHub.time() returns negative values during countdown, the 3-2-1 screen never renders.\n\nThe countdown display also renders raw milliseconds instead of seconds.\n\nThe countdown is a required visible feature per PLAN §14.4. The unreachable code is a real defect, not a placeholder.\n\nI am checking the card left unit against the harness implementation to confirm the raw milliseconds bug.\n\nThe card `left` value is confirmed to be milliseconds. The harness passes this raw value through the bridge, and the game renders it as-is. The screenshot shows 6166, confirming the bug. I am now weighing whether the real hub also sends milliseconds or if the harness is the source of the error.\n\nThe deduplication logic only resends the card state when the ceiled seconds change. The game still receives raw millisecond values each time. A value of 6166 is inconsistent with this behavior, so the raw unit bug is confirmed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1086538e-8f79-4033-883d-6a0e338a5fe8-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"countN|Countdown","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1086538e-8f79-4033-883d-6a0e338a5fe8-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/session.js","offset":1,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2169,"output_tokens":1415,"cache_read_input_tokens":70528,"cache_creation_input