{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_990","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The countdown timer is set to 3000 milliseconds. The hub sends the start signal for 3000ms in the future.\n\nThe countdown makes `AIHub.time()` negative during the 3-second window. The card handler only switches the screen to Card when time is exactly `-Infinity`. Because the value is negative, the screen stays on Card instead of transitioning.\n\nThe Countdown screen is never shown. The operation starts at the correct time, but the 3-2-1 visual countdown is missing.\n\nThe missing countdown is a core defect. PLAN.md explicitly requires it. The Countdown screen is dead code caused by an inverted condition. This is a textbook bug.\n\nThe card seconds display is also wrong. It shows 6166 ms instead of roughly 6 or 7. The screenshot confirms this.\n\nThe countdown sits between the seat list and the controls. The Ready and More Time buttons are below. The agent's claim that the bust does not obscure the buttons appears true.\n\nThe hub suite passed.\n\nThe countdown is not a separate acceptance criterion, but it is required by PLAN.md. Refuting the two card bugs is correct and specific. I will not add tuning deviations because the suites passed and §17 allows tuning until invariants hold. I am also checking whether the hub README documents the card `left` field as seconds.\n\nThe harness is the official test harness from the repository. It sends card `left` in milliseconds. The game displays this raw value without converting it to seconds. This confirms the display bug. A bridge comment and tickCard logic both indicate the protocol value is in milliseconds.\n\nThe host pump guard and 0.05 dt cap are safe. The simulation can catch up within the 16 ms wall-clock window.\n\nThe missing countdown and card seconds are not tested. The hub suite does not assert the displayed digits. A test should be added to drive the real card path and prevent regression.\n\nThe 6166 value is confirmed to be the raw card `left` field. No division by 1000 exists elsewhere in the code. I am now checking strain rules for more severe gameplay bugs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9373d2a3-d5f7-489e-baee-78ead7551864-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"vitals = 48|vitals = 35|drain.*1|crash|hush","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src","glob":"*.js","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9373d2a3-d5f7-489e-baee-78ead7551864-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/round.js","offset":310,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2003,"output_tokens":1645,"cache_read_input_tokens":80896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"65fb45a4-e48d-4c88-9752-501685bff016"}
