ode\":0,\"match_count\":14,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":12,\"content\":\"  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\"},{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\"},{\"line_number\":29,\"content\":\"  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"  #log { overflow: auto; font: 12px/1.35 ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"    <section id=\\\"checks\\\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\\\"checklist\\\"><li class=\\\"hint\\\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\"},{\"line_number\":72,\"content\":\"const auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\"},{\"line_number\":77,\"content\":\"const SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\"},{\"line_number\":181,\"content\":\"  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\"},{\"line_number\":211,\"content\":\"    frame.allow = 'fullscreen; autoplay; gamepad; pointer-lock';\"},{\"line_number\":258,\"content\":\"    if (!auto && performance.now() >= state.splashUntil) return releaseRound(state);\"},{\"line_number\":302,\"content\":\"  if (!auto && players.every((c) => ready.has(c.key))) return releaseRound(state);\"},{\"line_number\":377,\"content\":\" * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\"},{\"line_number\":544,\"content\":\"if (auto) conformance();\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"e70aa69a-efd3-4bd6-859e-60e0079d0625"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1003","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test must drive the real hub card.\n\nThe test must read the DOM directly. It should assert that visible seconds match ceil(left/1000) and that the countdown shows 3, 2, or 1 before the operation starts. The `left` value can be read from the game model or the harness.\n\nExposing `card.left` in `state()` lets the test compare DOM text directly against the game's own value. This avoids hardcoding and keeps the test driving the shipped code.\n\nAdding `cardLeft` and `countN` to `state()` is the chosen approach. The test will compare DOM text directly against these values. Exact state key checks are a concern.\n\nThe test must not start past the countdown. It should load the harness, wait for the card to appear naturally, read the DOM, then click Ready to begin the 3000ms countdown. The pump runs every 16ms, so the digits 3, 2, and 1 should be visible before the Operation screen appears.\n\nThe test will run in the hub suite as a new `cardCountdown` function in `tests/hub/suite.mjs`. It uses WebGL mode for speed and a single player to keep the extra ~15 second run manageable.\n\nThe hub suite already serves the site, so the new test can run alongside the existing heavy runs. After editing source files, a rebuild is required because the test reads the built `game.html`. The implementation adds `Math.max(0, Math.ceil(model.card.left / 1000))` to the card text in `director.js`.\n\nThe card text element will receive a `data-live` attribute so the test can target it precisely. The session.js clock logic is being updated to prevent negative clock values from triggering the countdown when the screen is already Operation, Round over, or Countdown.\n\nThe session.js clock logic is being simplified. It now distinguishes between negative clocks and finite positive clocks to control when the screen switches from Card to Countdown or Operation.\n\nThe session.js clock logic is being finalized. Negative clocks switch the screen from Card to Countdown and set countN. Positive finite clocks switch the screen from Card or Countdown to Operation and clear countN. Screens like Round over or session pause will not be reset incorrectly.\n\nThe test will read both the DOM and state. It targets `.card .vitals` text and reads `cardLeft` from `state()`. The `cardCountdown` function is being drafted in the hub suite with a headless Chromium browser.\n\nThe test navigates to the WebGL harness with one player. It waits for the game frame to report a Card screen before reading the DOM.\n\nThe test extracts the card text and `cardLeft` from the game state. It asserts the displayed seconds is a positive integer between 1 and 20 and matches `Math.max(0, Math.ceil(card.left / 1000))`. After passing this check it will click Ready inside the game frame.\n\nThe test clicks the Ready button inside the game frame. It then polls the iframe for 8 seconds, reading the `.screen .big` digit and current screen state each cycle. The assertion expects the screen to reach Countdown and display 1, 2, or 3.\n\nThe test polls the iframe for 8 seconds, breaking when it sees a 1, 2, or 3 digit. It then waits for the Operation screen to confirm the countdown completes before the operation begins.\n\nThe test will close the browser in a finally block. Clicking Ready inside the iframe should work because pointer-events are auto. Pressing Enter is an alternative since the harness handles synthetic keys.\n\nThe test will click the real Ready button in the DOM rather than press Enter. For a single player, that click triggers `answer('ready')`, which releases the round and starts the 3000ms countdown. The game pump switches screens once the clock becomes negative finite. A 50ms polling interval should catch the 3-2-1 digits before the Operation screen appears.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6b5a58a-c35f-4c31-8b37-635f6fe8a932-118","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/session.js","offset":100,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6b5a58a-c35f-4c31-8b37-635f6fe8a932-119","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function activate|id === 'ready'|answer\\(","glob":"**/src/app/director.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6b5a58a-c35f-4c31-8b37-635f6fe8a932-120","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html","offset":1,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3540,"output_tokens":2751,"cache_read_input_tokens":145920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"796f392c-a448-480a-a9f3-9307933b4365"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d6b5a58a-c35f-4c31-8b37-635f6fe8a932-118","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→\\n  function finish(forceWon) {\\n    if (!info.isHost || finished || ended) return;\\n    finished = true;\\n    const out = outcome(model, info, left);\\n    if (typeof forceWon === 'boolean') out.won = forceWon && out.won;\\n    try { AIHub.finish(out); } catch { /* host only; the client warns if misused */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  AIHub.on('card', (card) => {\\n110→    model.card = card || model.card;\\n    if (AIHub.time() === -Infinity) model.screen = 'Card';\\n    model.paint?.();\\n  });\\n  AIHub.on('start', () => {\\n    model.started = true;\\n  });\\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\\n    if (!data || ended) return;\\n    if (data.t === 'i' || data.t === 'a') {\\n120→      if (!model.sim || from === AIHub.me) return;\\n      const cur = cmds.get(from) || { source: 'abs', x: 0, y: 0, use: 0, tool: 'gel' };\\n      if (data.t === 'i') {\\n        cur.source = 'abs';\\n        cur.x = data.x;\\n        cur.y = data.y;\\n        if (data.tool) cur.tool = data.tool;\\n        cur.use = data.use || 0;\\n        cur.steady = !!data.steady;\\n      } else {\\n130→        if (data.syringe) cur.syringe = true;\\n        if (data.special) cur.special = true;\\n        if (data.alt) cur.alt = true;\\n        if (data.swap) cur.swap = true;\\n        if (data.siteDelta) cur.siteDelta = data.siteDelta;\\n        if (Number.isInteger(data.site)) cur.site = data.site;\\n      }\\n      cmds.set(from, cur);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n140→    if (from !== info.host) return;\\n    if (data.t === 'k') {\\n      const dec = decodeKeyframe(data);\\n      if (!base || dec.tick == null || base.tick == null || dec.tick >= base.tick) base = dec;\\n    } else if (data.t === 's' && base) {\\n      base = applyUnreliable(base, data);\\n    } else if (data.t === 'e' && data.ev) {\\n      model.remoteEvents = data.ev;\\n    }\\n    model.netState = base;\\n150→  });\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\\n    left.add(id);\\n    try { model.sim?.leave(id); } catch { /* already gone */ }\\n  });\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => {\\n    if (model.sim?.complete) finish(true);\\n    else finish(false);\\n  });\\n  AIHub.on('end', () => {\\n160→    ended = true;\\n    model.screen = 'Round over';\\n    try { model.audio?.ctx?.suspend?.(); } catch { /* already suspended */ }\\n    model.paint?.();\\n  });\\n\\n  AIHub.ready();\\n\\n  const boot = (async () => {\\n    if (info.isHost) {\",\"content_concise\":\"100→\\n  function finish(forceWon) {\\n    if (!info.isHost || finished || ended) return;\\n    finished = true;\\n    const out = outcome(model, info, left);\\n    if (typeof forceWon === 'boolean') out.won = forceWon && out.won;\\n    try { AIHub.finish(out); } catch { /* host only; the client warns if misused */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  AIHub.on('card', (card) => {\\n110→    model.card = card || model.card;\\n    if (AIHub.time() === -Infinity) model.screen = 'Card';\\n    model.paint?.();\\n  });\\n  AIHub.on('start', () => {\\n    model.started = true;\\n  });\\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\\n    if (!data || ended) return;\\n    if (data.t === 'i' || data.t === 'a') {\\n120→      if (!model.sim || from === AIHub.me) return;\\n      const cur = cmds.get(from) || { source: 'abs', x: 0, y: 0, use: 0, tool: 'gel' };\\n      if (data.t === 'i') {\\n        cur.source = 'abs';\\n        cur.x = data.x;\\n        cur.y = data.y;\\n        if (data.tool) cur.tool = data.tool;\\n        cur.use = data.use || 0;\\n        cur.steady = !!data.steady;\\n      } else {\\n130→        if (data.syringe) cur.syringe = true;\\n        if (data.special) cur.special = true;\\n        if (data.alt) cur.alt = true;\\n        if (data.swap) cur.swap = true;\\n        if (data.siteDelta) cur.siteDelta = data.siteDelta;\\n        if (Number.isInteger(data.site)) cur.site 