{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1005","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A potential bug was spotted: the card handler only resets the screen to Card when time equals -Infinity.\n\nThe pump updates countN every frame, so paint rebuilds only when the digit changes. Screen transitions trigger paint correctly because the signal changes. The screen is set before paint in each tick.\n\nChecking when goAt is set. It happens on release(), which occurs after all players are ready, so AIHub.time() becomes negative and the pump switches to Countdown with countN = 3.\n\nThere is a concern about calling ready() before welcome, since session.js triggers it immediately at runSession start. A prior bug suggests ready() may need to be called again after welcome.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-08eceb2c-161c-4bfd-ac6d-78f1f9455ff8-123","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"card:\\s*true|connect\\(","glob":"**/src/**/*.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2025,"output_tokens":409,"cache_read_input_tokens":154880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"3b3058b6-6562-4284-8703-0dc6e03c8069"}
