{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1006","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The connect card is active. The harness will send card events.\n\nChecking splash timing. A 10-second splash window may end before the game boots. If boot takes longer than 10 seconds, the card could be missed. In non-auto mode, releaseRound fires automatically once the splash timer expires.\n\nBoot time was roughly 4 seconds in the prior test. The harness will use WebGL with one player to keep things fast. The test waits for the Card screen and a vitals number, timing out at 15 seconds. If the splash timer expires first, the test fails. The paint function displays ceil(card.left/1000) seconds.\n\nThe displayed countdown digit will be read from the `.big` element. The card screen uses `.logo` instead, so the two states won't conflict. The test can verify `state().screen === 'Countdown'` and the digit text. I'm also considering whether to update the paint signature.\n\nThe paint signature already includes countN, so repeated identical values won't trigger unnecessary redraws. Setting model.screen to Countdown every frame while the clock is negative is harmless. A late card event arriving during countdown could still cause issues.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4672c4fb-f2dc-413a-9139-d3de611eda7c-124","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/round.js","offset":470,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4672c4fb-f2dc-413a-9139-d3de611eda7c-125","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tools/vendor/session.js","offset":200,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1210,"output_tokens":858,"cache_read_input_tokens":156800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"3c099f63-36b3-4518-84b2-e2c202c258db"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4672c4fb-f2dc-413a-9139-d3de611eda7c-124","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"470→    status();\\n    settle();\\n  }\\n\\n  const sitOut = (test) => () => {\\n    if (phase !== 'loading') return;\\n    for (const s of copies) if (test(s) && !s.out) markOut(s, 'not-ready');\\n    status();\\n    settle();\\n  };\\n480→\\n  function startRound() {\\n    // A gated round waits on the hub's splash, however long it holds: only\\n    // release() starts the clock on the games that are still loading.\\n    if (!gate) {\\n      later(t.helloMs, sitOut((s) => !s.hello));\\n      later(t.readyMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\\n    }\\n    status();\\n  }\\n490→\\n  /** The splash is over: start as soon as every game has loaded, and wait loadGraceMs at most for the slow ones. */\\n  function release() {\\n    if (released || phase !== 'loading') return;\\n    released = true;\\n    later(t.loadGraceMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\\n    status();\\n    settle();\\n  }\\n\\n500→  startRound();\\n\\n  return {\\n    receive,\\n    leave,\\n    release,\\n    /** Call time now, as the cap would: the host pressed \\\"End round\\\". */\\n    timeUp() {\\n      if (phase === 'countdown' || phase === 'playing') timeUp();\\n    },\\n510→    /** A player's progress score, as the hub's scoreboard saw it (parallel and ghost). */\\n    progress(id, score) {\\n      const seat = seats[id];\\n      if (seat && !seat.out && !seat.result && Number.isFinite(score) && phase !== 'ended') seat.progress = score;\\n    },\\n    /** End the round now: the session ended, or the host skipped this game. */\\n    abort(reason = 'skipped') {\\n      finishVoid(reason, reason === 'session-ended' ? 'session-ended' : 'void');\\n    },\\n    get phase() {\",\"content_concise\":\"470→    status();\\n    settle();\\n  }\\n\\n  const sitOut = (test) => () => {\\n    if (phase !== 'loading') return;\\n    for (const s of copies) if (test(s) && !s.out) markOut(s, 'not-ready');\\n    status();\\n    settle();\\n  };\\n480→\\n  function startRound() {\\n    // A gated round waits on the hub's splash, however long it holds: only\\n    // release() starts the clock on the games that are still loading.\\n    if (!gate) {\\n      later(t.helloMs, sitOut((s) => !s.hello));\\n      later(t.readyMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\\n    }\\n    status();\\n  }\\n490→\\n  /** The splash is over: start as soon as every game has loaded, and wait loadGraceMs at most for the slow ones. */\\n  function release() {\\n    if (released || phase !== 'loading') return;\\n    released = true;\\n    later(t.loadGraceMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\\n    status();\\n    settle();\\n  }\\n\\n500→  startRound();\\n\\n  return {\\n    receive,\\n    leave,\\n    release,\\n    /** Call time now, as the cap would: the host pressed \\\"End round\\\". */\\n    timeUp() {\\n      if (phase === 'countdown' || phase === 'playing') timeUp();\\n    },\\n510→    /** A player's progress score, as the hub's scoreboard saw it (parallel and ghost). */\\n    progress(id, score) {\\n      const seat = seats[id];\\n      if (seat && !seat.out && !seat.result && Number.isFinite(score) && phase !== 'ended') seat.progress = score;\\n    },\\n    /** End the round now: the session ended, or the host skipped this game. */\\n    abort(reason = 'skipped') {\\n      finishVoid(reason, reason === 'session-ended' ? 'session-ended' : 'void');\\n    },\\n    get phase() {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/round.js\",\"offset\":470,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    status();\\n    settle();\\n  }\\n\\n  const sitOut = (test) => () => {\\n    if (phase !== 'loading') return;\\n    for (const s of copies) if (test(s) && !s.out) markOut(s, 'not-ready');\\n    status();\\n    settle();\\n  };\\n\\n  function startRound() {\\n    // A gated round waits on the hub's splash, however long it holds: only\\n    // release() starts the clock on the games that are still loading.\\n    if (!gate) {\\n      later(t.helloMs, sitOut((s) => !s.hello));\\n      later(t.readyMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\\n    }\\n    status();\\n  }\\n\\n  /** The splash is over: start as soon as every game has loaded, and wait loadGraceMs at most for the slow ones. */\\n  function release() {\\n    if (released || phase !== 'loading') return;\\n    released = true;\\n    later(t.loadGraceMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\\n    status();\\n    settle();\\n  }\\n\\n  startRound();\\n\\n  return {\\n    receive,\\n    leave,\\n    release,\\n    /** Call time now, as the cap would: the host pressed \\\"End round\\\". */\\n    timeUp() {\\n      if (phase === 'countdown' || phase === 'playing') timeUp();\\n    },\\n    /** A player's progress score, as the hub's scoreboard saw it (parallel and ghost). */\\n    progress(id, score) {\\n      const seat = seats[id];\\n      if (seat && !seat.out && !seat.result && Number.isFinite(score) && phase !== 'ended') seat.progress = score;\\n    },\\n    /** End the round now: the session ended, or the host skipped this game. */\\n    abort(reason = 'skipped') {\\n      finishVoid(reason, reason === 'session-ended' ? 'session-ended' : 'void');\\n    },\\n    get phase() {\\n\",\"total_lines\":533}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4672c4fb-f2dc-413a-9139-d3de611eda7c-125","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"200→  function post(type, fields) {\\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\\n    try {\\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n210→  function emit(type, args) {\\n    var list = handler