104-231230__x8f49b6/work/exit-interview.json\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim suite 51 checks, Playwright browser suite 80 checks on Chromium and WebKit, hub harness 23 checks. No physical controller, no second human, no real iOS device.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"    \\\"The sim suite (51 checks) and the hub harness (23 checks) caught the issues that would have shipped. The browser suite (80 checks) caught UI timing: attract was swallowing the next confirm, and a reload was dropping screens the playthrough had already opened.\\\",\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"5430eecb-9715-4285-a0c1-b301c5516634"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1012","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will update the counts once the new hub total is known.\n\nExit-interview and about.json must stay in sync. The testing feedback will reflect the new count. Director paint handles countdown DOM updates correctly. Setting the screen to Countdown inside the pump also sets the body dataset. The 3.5rem vitals font size is fine for small numbers.\n\nAdding `data-live` attributes to the seconds element and countdown paragraph for stable test queries. Replacing the dead branch in session.js clock block. The existing negative-clock guard remains unchanged.\n\nPortrait stays hidden during countdown because syncFromSim only turns it on for the Operation screen. Performance impact from repeated sync calls is acceptable. The countdown number renders directly in the DOM. I am also checking whether Math.ceil handles negative clock values correctly.\n\nA negative clock delay could push the countdown above 3 seconds. The test only accepts 1, 2, or 3. This edge case must be handled.\n\nThe client countdown starts at the computed `in` value, so the first observed second should be 3. Slow polling may cause the test to see 2 or 1 instead. I will not clamp the count to 3 unless the harness specifically requires it.\n\nThe countdown formula will be `Math.max(1, Math.ceil(-clock/1000))`, matching the old code. The test will record the displayed digit and confirm the operation follows. I will add a `hubTests` counting helper and check if the browser suite needs this test too.\n\nThe countdown test will live only in the hub suite. I will rebuild and run just the card test first to iterate quickly, then run the full hub suite for the official proof.\n\nI will add the countdown test to the hub suite. To avoid running all six WebGPU tests, I will export `cardFlow` from `suite.mjs` and call it directly in a small verification script.\n\nI will recapture session-card.png after the fix so the verifier sees the correct countdown. I also need to update PROGRESS and the four about blocks if their counts changed, since TASK.md requires them in the chat reply.\n\nThe paint signature includes raw card.left so the DOM updates correctly when the displayed digit changes. I will check director.js line 1578 and session.js line 282 before editing.\n\nThe test must read the card seconds before clicking Ready, since the Ready button disappears when the screen becomes Countdown. If the splash auto-releases before the click, the countdown should still begin without a manual click. I will read the card quickly after it appears and click immediately to avoid race conditions.\n\nThe countdown test will wait for the Card screen, read the vitals seconds, click Ready if needed, poll for the countdown digit before the operation, and then wait for the operation. If the splash auto-releases before the click, answer() returns early because goAt is already set; this is acceptable. Session calls ready() after the welcome message but before the view boots, so the card appears at the right time.\n\nA `count` class will mark the countdown digit for stable test queries. The countdown paint can use a simple textContent update since the digit changes only once per second. I am now applying the code edits.\n\nThe test will target the iframe directly with Playwright's frameLocator to avoid matching the parent page. The Ready button sits inside that iframe, so a direct locator click is simpler than navigating through the page. Parent page errors might not catch errors thrown inside the game iframe, so I will also listen for page errors on the iframe itself.\n\nI will attach the iframe error listener after navigation. The about counts will be updated to the new total before the official hub run so the shipped page matches, but the card test does not depend on that text.\n\nThe browser suite is not needed for this change because it exercises standalone mode rather than the session path. The hub test already covers the card countdown.\n\nI will re-run the browser suite and hub suite to satisfy the plan's verification step. The countdown fix is session-only, so standalone launches remain unchanged.\n\nLaunches are gating steps and the HTML bytes changed, so they will be re-run after the hub suite. Sim and package remain untouched.\n\nI will add one short comment to session.js explaining that AIHub.time() is negative during the countdown and -Infinity before the hub starts it. No other code changes are needed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9b86650c-cca0-4b89-a068-fb7fb0892cd0-132","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"left","glob":"**/README*"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1613,"output_tokens":3086,"cache_read_input_tokens":162816,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"37ed7220-241d-448d-a300-e0ff19b16c42"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9b86650c-cca0-4b89-a068-fb7fb0892cd0-132","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"cd80a1ba-9950-43c7-99cb-14ac9704713b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1013","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The harness is the authority. I will implement now.\n\nChecking paint signature timing. The displayed number may lag by up to 250ms because the display updates when the second changes, not continuously. It will match the rounded-down value from the received timestamp.\n\nThe card countdown will update from the stored left on each paint. The card event updates model.card.left. Between events the number stays fixed. This keeps the DOM consistent with the game state. I will add cardCountdown to suite.mjs and hubTests. I will also add a way to run just that test.\n\nI will embed the card countdown test inside hubTests to avoid double-serving. I am also adding a quick-run helper at the bottom of suite.mjs.\n\nI will export only `cardCountdown` from suite.mjs. The scratch runner will import it and serve its own tiny static server to run the test.\n\nThe test will use the existing Playwright Chromium import. It targets a node with `data-live=\"card\"` and trims whitespace from its text content. The iframe click should work because no harness overlay blocks it. The game boot may take up to 20 seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The hub sends `card.left` in milliseconds, and the 3-2-1 only runs while `AIHub.time()` is negative. Both paths were treating that clock as if it had already started."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5379749d-ee3c-4882-a063-4a77a317065a-133","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","old_string":"    const secs = document.createElement('p');\n    secs.className = 'vitals';\n    if (model.card?.left != null) secs.textContent = String(Math.max(0, Math.ceil(model.card.left)));","new_string":"    const secs = document.createElement('p');\n    secs.className = 'vitals';\n    secs.dataset.live = 'card';\n    if (model.card?.left != null) secs.textContent = String(Math.max(0, Math.ceil(model.card.left / 1000)));"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5379749d-ee3c-4882-a063-4a77a317065a-134","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","old_string":"    if (model.mode === 'session' && model.screen === 'Countdown') {\n      ui.innerHTML = `<section class=\"screen\"><p class=\"big\">${esc(model.countN || '')}</p></section>`;\n      return;\n    }","new_string":"    if (model.mode === 'session' && model.screen === 'Countdown') {\n      ui.innerHTML = `<section class=\"screen\"><p class=\"big\" data-live=\"count\">${esc(model.countN || '')}</p></section>`;\n      return;\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5379749d-ee3c-4882-a063-4a77a317065a-135","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","old_string":"      reached: [...model.reached],\n    };","new_string":"      reached: [...model.reached],\n      cardLeft: model.card?.left ?? null,\n      countN: model.countN || 0,\n    };"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5379749d-ee3c-4882-a063-4a77a317065a-136","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/session.js","old_string":"    if (clock >= 0 && clock < 1e12) {\n      if (model.screen === 'Card' || model.screen === 'Countdown') {\n        model.screen = clock < 0 ? 'Countdown' : 'Operation';\n        if (model.screen === 'Operation') model.reached.add('Operation');\n      }\n      model.countN = clock < 0 ? Math.max(1, Math.ceil(-clock / 1000)) : 0;\n    }","new_string":"    // time() is -Infinity on the card, negative through the 3-2-1, and only then >= 0.\n    if (Number.isFinite(clock) && clock < 0) {\n      if (model.screen === 'Card' || model.screen === 'Countdown') model.screen = 'Countdown';\n      model.countN = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(-clock / 1000));\n    } else if (clock >= 0 && clock < 1e12) {\n      if (model.screen === 'Card' || model.screen === 'Countdown') {\n        model.screen = 'Operation';\n        model.reached.add('Operation');\n      }\n      model.countN = 0;\n    }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3228,"output_tokens":1849,"cache_read_input_tokens":164352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"6f4285e2-5493-432d-8e26-471bed5966ad"}
