{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1041","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The screenshot now displays \"6\" instead of \"6166\".\n\nThe seconds fix is visually confirmed. The code divides card time by 1000 in director.js and shows countdown digits when the clock is finite and negative in session.js. The test now checks card seconds, countdown digits, and page errors. Hub logs show 26 passed tests versus 23 before. The test's honesty is being questioned.\n\nThe test is honest. It reads the real DOM and compares the displayed card time to the raw hub milliseconds divided by 1000. A hardcoded \"6\" would fail if the actual cardLeft value falls outside the 5001–6000 millisecond window.\n\nThe splash starts at 10 seconds, so the first rendered card time should be 9 or 10. A hardcoded 6 would fail immediately.\n\nThe countdown test requires the screen to read Countdown, then display a digit of 1, 2, or 3, and finally reach Operation. Skipping the countdown would leave the digit empty and cause failure.\n\nA race condition is unlikely because the code explicitly keeps the Countdown state active for the full 3000 milliseconds while the clock is negative.\n\nThe test repeatedly clicks the ready button while polling for Countdown or Operation. This verifies that clicking ready actually starts the countdown.\n\nThe test also dispatches an Enter key event. The harness auto-releases the card after ten seconds if the ready click fails to register. The total wait time covers this fallback. The hub suite passed all 26 checks.\n\nThe log is from this round and not stale. The implementer's evidence is the primary source, so the 26-pass result is accepted as genuine.\n\nThe countdown formula `Math.max(1, Math.ceil(-clock / 1000))` risks showing a fourth digit when the clock is slightly negative. The plan specifies a 3-2-1 countdown, so this edge case needs fixing.\n\nA brief fourth digit is harmless because the test only requires 1, 2, or 3. The screen state transitions correctly from Card to Countdown. The critical unknown is whether model.paint() actually re-renders the Countdown state during the pump cycle, or if a signature skip leaves the card stuck.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-37d277d9-d58d-438c-a729-14faa927b3fc-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js","offset":1320,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-37d277d9-d58d-438c-a729-14faa927b3fc-64","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pointerup|data-item|answer\\('ready'\\)|keydown","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3331,"output_tokens":1387,"cache_read_input_tokens":113408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"53c6fc33-0a4d-464e-a26b-1b5446f018c4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-37d277d9-d58d-438c-a729-14faa927b3fc-63","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1320→      }\\n      if ((menu.left || pend.left) && nudge(-1)) return;\\n      if ((menu.right || pend.right) && nudge(1)) return;\\n      const padUp = sample.seats.some((s) => s.edges?.up);\\n      const padDown = sample.seats.some((s) => s.edges?.down);\\n      if (menu.up || pend.up || (padUp && !inPlay)) moveFocus(-1);\\n      else if (menu.down || pend.down || (padDown && !inPlay)) moveFocus(1);\\n      else if (inPlay && padDown) askBea();\\n      const inMenu = !!model.overlay || !!model.sessionPause || model.screen !== 'Operation';\\n      const padConfirm = sample.seats.some((s) => s.edges?.confirm);\\n1330→      const confirm = menu.confirm || pend.confirm || (padConfirm && inMenu);\\n      if (confirm && inMenu) {\\n        const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n        if (item) activate(item.id);\\n      } else if ((menu.back || pend.back) && !inPlay) {\\n        if (model.screen === 'Settings') closeSettings();\\n        else if (model.screen !== 'Title' && model.screen !== 'Main Menu' && model.screen !== 'Touch notice') {\\n          const prev = model.stack.pop();\\n          setScreen(prev || 'Main Menu');\\n        }\\n1340→      }\\n      tickAudio();\\n    } finally {\\n      busy = false;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function btn(item, index) {\\n    const on = index === model.focus ? ' on' : '';\\n    const pick = item.id === model.consultChoice ? ' pick' : '';\\n1350→    const slider = item.kind === 'slider'\\n      ? `<input type=\\\"range\\\" data-slider=\\\"${esc(item.id)}\\\" min=\\\"${item.min}\\\" max=\\\"${item.max}\\\" step=\\\"${item.step || 0.01}\\\" value=\\\"${item.id in TUNING_DEFAULTS ? model.tuning[item.id] : (model.settings[item.id] ?? item.min)}\\\">`\\n      : '';\\n    return `<button class=\\\"item${on}${pick}\\\" data-item=\\\"${esc(item.id)}\\\" type=\\\"button\\\"><span data-readout=\\\"${esc(item.id)}\\\">${esc(item.label)}</span>${slider}</button>`;\\n  }\\n\\n  function menuBlock(title, items, extra = '') {\\n    model.focus = Math.max(0, Math.min(model.focus, Math.max(0, items.length - 1)));\\n    return `<section class=\\\"screen\\\"><h1 class=\\\"logo\\\">${esc(title)}</h1>${extra}<div class=\\\"menu\\\">${items.map(btn).join('')}</div></section>`;\\n  }\\n1360→\\n  function paint(force) {\\n    const ui = model.ui;\\n    if (!ui) return;\\n    const sig = [\\n      model.screen, model.overlay, model.storyMode, model.line, model.focus, model.page,\\n      model.attract.on ? model.attract.opIndex : '', model.sessionPause, model.countN,\\n      model.card ? (model.card.ready || []).join(',') : '',\\n      model.opId, model.sceneId, model.nogfxNotice, model.consultChoice, model.settings.difficulty,\\n      model.settings.glyphs, [...model.joined].join(','), model.sim?.phase?.id || '', model.sim?.over || '',\\n1370→      model.bark?.text || '', model.flow, model.doctor || '',\\n    ].join('|');\\n    document.body.dataset.screen = model.attract.on ? (model.attract.from || model.screen) : model.screen;\\n    if (!force && sig === model.paintSig) {\\n      patchLive();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    model.paintSig = sig;\\n    const boot = document.getElementById('boot');\\n    const app = document.getElementById('app');\\n1380→    if (boot) boot.hidden = model.screen !== 'Boot';\\n    if (app) app.hidden = model.screen === 'Boot';\\n    if (model.nogfxNotice) {\\n      ui.innerHTML = `<section class=\\\"screen nogfx\\\"><p>This room cannot draw. A browser with graphics can open the chart. Your progress is still here.</p>${btn({ id: 'nogfx-ok', label: 'Continue' }, 0)}</section>`;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (model.mode === 'session' && model.screen === 'Card') {\\n      paintCard(ui);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n1390→    if (model.mode === 'session' && model.screen === 'Countdown') {\\n      ui.innerHTML = `<section class=\\\"screen\\\"><p class=\\\"big\\\" data-live=\\\"count\\\">${esc(model.countN || '')}</p></section>`;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (model.screen === 'Round over') {\\n      ui.innerHTML = '<section class=\\\"screen\\\"><h1 class=\\\"big\\\">Round over</h1><p class=\\\"note\\\">The table is clear.</p></section>';\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (model.attract.on) {\\n      ui.innerHTML = `${hudHtml()}<p class=\\\"demo\\\">DEMO</p><p class=\\\"press\\\">Press any button</p>${model.attract.from === 'Touch notice' ? touchHtml() : ''}`;\\n1400→      return;\\n    }\\n    if (model.sessionPause) {\\n      ui.innerHTML = `${hudHtml()}<div class=\\\"overlay\\\">${menuBlock('Settings', settingsItems(), pageDots())}</div>`;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (model.overlay === 'pause') {\\n      ui.innerHTML = `<div class=\\\"overlay\\\">${menuBlock('Paused', pauseItems())}</div>`;\\n      return;\\n    }\",\"content_concise\":\"1320→      }\\n      if ((menu.left || pend.left) && nudge(-1)) return;\\n      if ((menu.right || pend.right) && nudge(1)) return;\\n      const padUp = sample.seats.some((s) => s.edges?.up);\\n      const padDown = sample.seats.some((s) => s.edges?.down);\\n      if (menu.up || pend.up || (padUp && !inPlay)) moveFocus(-1);\\n      else if (menu.down || pend.down || (padDown && !inPlay)) moveFocus(1);\\n      else if (inPlay && padDown) askBea();\\n      const inMenu = !!model.overlay || !!model.sessionPause || model.screen !== 'Operation';\\n      const padConfirm = sample.seats.some((s) => s.edges?.confirm);\\n1330→      const confirm = menu.confirm || pend.confirm || (padConfirm && inMenu);\\n      if (confirm && inMenu) {\\n        const item = currentItems()[model.focus];\\n        if (item) activate(item.id);\\n      } else if ((menu.back || pend.back) && !inPlay) {\\n        if (model.screen === 'Settings') closeSettings();\\n        else if (model.screen !== 'Title' && model.screen !== 'Main Menu' && model.screen !== 'Touch notice') {\\n          const prev = model.stack.pop();\\n          setScreen(prev || 'Main Menu');\\n        }\\n1340→      }\\n      tickAudio();\\n    } finally {\\n      busy = false;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function btn(item, index) {\\n    const on = index === model.focus ? ' on' : '';\\n    const pick = item.id === model.consultChoice ? ' pick' : '';\\n1350→    const slider = item.kind === 'slider'\\n      ? `<input type=\\\"range\\\" data-slider=\\\"${esc(item.id)}\\\" min=\\\"${item.min}\\\" max=\\\"${item.max}\\\" step=\\\"${item.step || 0.01}\\\" value=\\\"${item.id in TUNING_DEFAULTS ? model.tuning[item.id] : (model.settings[item.id] ?? item.min)}\\\">`\\n      : '';\\n    return `<button class=\\\"item${on}${pick}\\\" data-item=\\\"${esc(item.id)}\\\" type=\\\"button\\\"><span data-readout=\\\"${esc(item.id)}\\\">${esc(item.label)}</span>${slider}</button>`;\\n  }\\n\\n  function menuBlock(title, items, extra = '') {\\n    model.focus = Math.max(0, Math.min(model.focus, Math.max(0, items.length - 1)));\\n    return `<section class=\\\"screen\\\"><h1 class=\\\"logo\\\">${esc(title)}</h1>${extra}<div class=\\\"menu\\\">${items.map(btn).join('')}</div></section>`;\\n  }\\n1360→\\n  function paint(force) {\\n    const ui = model.ui;\\n    if (!ui) return;\\n    const sig = [\\n      model.screen, model.overlay, model.storyMode, model.line, model.focus, model.page,\\n      model.attract.on ? model.attract.opIndex : '', model.sessionPause, model.countN,\\n      model.card ? (model.card.ready || []).join(',') : '',\\n      model.opId, model.sceneId, model.nogfxNotice, model.consultChoice, model.settings.difficulty,\\n      model.settings.glyphs, [...model.joined].join(','), model.sim?.phase?.id || '', model.sim?.over || '',\\n1370→      model.bark?.text || '', model.flow, model.doctor || '',\\n    ].join('|');\\n    document.body.dataset.screen = model.attract.on ? (model.attract.from || model.screen) : model.screen;\\n    if (!force && si