{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1042","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The paint signature includes countN. When that value changes, the full paint runs and updates the countdown DOM.\n\nThe card signature excludes card.left, so the seconds display updates via patchLive() instead. I still need to verify whether pointerup on the button triggers answer('ready').\n\nsession.js listens for confirm edges from input poll rather than raw pointer events. If the test's pointerup bypasses the input system, ready may not fire until the 10-second splash timeout. The hub log shows the test passed anyway. The harness timing accounts for page load, card wait, clicking, and the splash delay.\n\nThe test can pass via the auto-release countdown even if the click is a no-op. This still validates the countdown path. I should verify pointer handling for Ready button clicks, though the harness previously passed with synthetic keys. I need to check how keys are read.\n\ndirector.js line 161 triggers `answer('ready')` on enter, space, or spacebar. I need to confirm whether the session key handler listens on the window and if a KeyboardEvent dispatched directly on the iframe contentWindow reaches it.\n\nA KeyboardEvent dispatched directly on the window target may not reach document-level listeners. This suggests the synthetic key might not actually trigger the Ready button, and the test could be passing only because of the auto-release countdown. The test is not theater: it reads real DOM from the live game, so it would fail if the seconds are not divided or the countdown screen never appears.\n\nThe countdown display logic is sound. A countN of zero would render empty, but the countdown never reaches zero. The ceiling calculation rounds negative clock values upward, so a slight delay past the intended second still shows the correct digit. The test accepts 1-3, which covers this edge case.\n\nThe test passed, so the bundled game.html must contain the fix. I will grep the built files for a distinctive string to confirm the division logic is present.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-00de8321-0d60-4dd1-be80-4c34b37acf53-65","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"data-live=.count|card.left / 1000|Number.isFinite\\(clock\\) && clock < 0","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work","glob":"*.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-00de8321-0d60-4dd1-be80-4c34b37acf53-66","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pointerup|pointerdown|activate\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/src/app/director.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3123,"output_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":116736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"f64f2518-da8c-417f-b6cc-db1ad22bdfef"}
