{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1058","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nI need to verify the `left` unit in harness.html tickCard and the vendored hub client. The hub.log only shows aggregate results, not individual check names. I should confirm whether this log is from the current round after the fix.I am examining vendor session.js to understand\n\nI should check timestamps on the implementer  the time function.folder to confirm the log is current. If the test passed, it ran against the rebuilt game.html. I also noticed the paint signature might be missing `model.card.left`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c3c89abb-f3cf-4e0b-8494-f60109e93667-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tools/vendor/session.js","offset":350,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c3c89abb-f3cf-4e0b-8494-f60109e93667-16","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"time:","glob":"**/tools/vendor/session.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c3c89abb-f3cf-4e0b-8494-f60109e93667-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md","offset":740,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5459,"output_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":42240,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"5960bf0f-317c-47e7-aa96-be2b5484f1ce"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c3c89abb-f3cf-4e0b-8494-f60109e93667-15","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"350→\\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    var text;\\n    try {\\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\\n360→      return false;\\n    }\\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n    var t = now();\\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\\n    refilled = t;\\n370→    if (tokens < 1) {\\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n    tokens -= 1;\\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\\n    post('send', fields);\\n    return true;\\n  };\\n380→\\n  /** Milliseconds since the synchronized start: negative during the countdown, -Infinity before start. */\\n  hub.time = function () {\\n    return goAt === null ? -Infinity : now() - goAt;\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A seeded random number generator (0 ≤ n < 1), the same sequence on every device for the same label. */\\n  hub.rng = function (label) {\\n    var h = 2166136261;\\n    var s = String(label === undefined ? '' : label);\\n390→    for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n      h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\\n      h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n    }\\n    return generator((hub.seed ^ h) >>> 0);\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\\n  function finite(v) {\\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\\n400→  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\\n   */\\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\\n410→      return null;\\n    }\\n    var copy = {};\\n    for (var key in outcome) {\\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\\n    }\\n    return copy;\\n420→  }\\n\\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\\n    if (!fields) return;\\n    var given = outcome || {};\\n    delete fields.time;\\n    delete fields.score;\",\"content_concise\":\"350→\\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    var text;\\n    try {\\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\\n360→      return false;\\n    }\\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n    var t = now();\\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\\n    refilled = t;\\n370→    if (tokens < 1) {\\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n    tokens -= 1;\\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\\n    post('send', fields);\\n    return true;\\n  };\\n380→\\n  /** Milliseconds since the synchronized start: negative during the countdown, -Infinity before start. */\\n  hub.time = function () {\\n    return goAt === null ? -Infinity : now() - goAt;\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A seeded random number generator (0 ≤ n < 1), the same sequence on every device for the same label. */\\n  hub.rng = function (label) {\\n    var h = 2166136261;\\n    var s = String(label === undefined ? '' : label);\\n390→    for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n      h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\\n      h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n    }\\n    return generator((hub.seed ^ h) >>> 0);\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\\n  function finite(v) {\\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\\n400→  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\\n   */\\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\\n410→      return null;\\n    }\\n    var copy = {};\\n    for (var key in outcome) {\\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\\n    }\\n    return copy;\\n420→  }\\n\\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\\n    if (!fields) return;\\n    var given = outcome || {};\\n    delete fields.time;\\n    delete fields.score;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tools/vendor/session.js\",\"offset\":350,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"\\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    var text;\\n    try {\\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n    var t = now();\\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\\n    refilled = t;\\n    if (tokens < 1) {\\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n    tokens -= 1;\\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\\n    post('send', fields);\\n    return true;\\n  };\\n\\n  /** Milliseconds since the synchronized start: negative during the countdown, -Infinity before start. */\\n  hub.time = function () {\\n    return goAt === null ? -Infinity : now() - goAt;\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A seeded random number generator (0 ≤ n < 1), the same sequence on every device for the same label. */\\n  hub.rng = function (label) {\\n    var h = 2166136261;\\n    var s = String(label === undefined ? '' : label);\\n    for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n      h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\\n      h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n    }\\n    return generator((hub.seed ^ h) >>> 0);\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\\n  function finite(v) {\\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\\n   */\\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\\n      return null;\\n    }\\n    var copy = {};\\n    for (var key in outcome) {\\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\\n    }\\n    return copy;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\\n    if (!fields) return;\\n    var given = outcome || {};\\n    delete fields.time;\\n    delete fields.score;\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c3c89abb-f3cf-4e0b-8494-f60109e93667-16","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,95,95,120,56,102,52,57,98,54,47,119,111,114,107,47,65,108,105,118,101,32,105,110,32,67,111,109,109,111,110,32,84,105,109,101,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,32,67,101,110,116,101,114,58,32,83,101,99,111,110,100,32,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,50,51,48,47,116,111,111,108,115,47,118,101,110,100,111,114,47,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,46,106,115,10,52,50,50,58,32,32,47,42,42,32,82,97,99,101,32,97,110,100,32,115,105,100,101,32,98,121,32,115,105,100,101,58,32,114,101,112,111,114,116,32,121,111,117,114,32,111,119,110,32,111,117,116,99,111,109,101,32,111,110,99,101,44,32,123,116,105,109,101,58,32,109,115,125,32,40,108,111,119,101,114,32,119,105,110,115,41,32,111,114,32,123,115,99,111,114,101,58,32,110,125,32,40,104,105,103,104,101,114,32,119,105,110,115,41,44,32,119,105,116,104,32,111,112,116,105,111,110,97,108,32,115,116,97,116,115,32,97,110,100,32,97,119,97,114,100,115,46,32,42,47,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tools/vendor/session.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":422,\"content\":\"  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c3c89abb-f3cf-4e0b-8494-f60109e93667-17","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"740→  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\\n    if (sim && (data.t === 'i' || data.t === 'a')) sim.input(from, data);\\n    else if (from === info.host) view?.applySnapshot(data);\\n  });\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => sim?.leave(id));           // release what they held, drop their tip\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (sim) finish(); });       // within graceMs; a non-host calling finish() warns, and fails the check\\n  let ended = false;\\n  AIHub.on('end', () => { ended = true; stopEverything(); }); // no input, no sends, audio suspended\\n  AIHub.ready();                                           // no key press; don't wait for a first frame\\n  let last = performance.now(), acc = 0;\\n750→  (function pump() {\\n    if (ended) return;\\n    const now = performance.now(), dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25); last = now;\\n    if (AIHub.time() >= 0) {\\n      if (!info.server) readLocalInput(dt);                // host: straight into sim.input(AIHub.me, …). Client: kept for sending\\n      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\\n      else sendInputOnSchedule();\\n    }\\n    setTimeout(pump, 16);\\n  })();\\n760→}\\n```\\n\\n**`finish()`** (host, once, on operation end or `time-up`): `standings` as groups of ids, best contribution first, listing every present player; `scores`; `won` (patient alive and operation complete); `stats` (up to 6 entries per player, names up to 16 chars: Cuts, Stitches, Burns, Saves, Accuracy); `awards` (title up to 24 chars, detail up to 40: \\\"Steadiest Hands\\\", \\\"Last-Second Shock\\\"). If the operation hasn't ended at `time-up`, `won` is false.\\n\\nA client leaving must not break the round. The host leaving voids it, which the hub handles: show a short message on `end` and stop.\\n\\n### 14.4 The card\\n\\nOwn card, in the game's world: OR 3, lamp on, the seat's busts or tips lining up, Title music. It shows the game's name, players in their colors with ready states, how to win, this player's controls, and seconds left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross (button 0) or a click on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle (button 3), M, or a click on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Nothing on the card changes the round, and there are no menus. Show a 3-2-1 countdown from `AIHub.time()`. The harness sends synthetic keys whose `code` equals `key` (`'Enter'`, `'a'`, `'ArrowLeft'`), so read `e.key` as well as `e.code`.\\n770→\\n### 14.5 Couch co-op (on its own)\\n\\nMain Menu → Grand Rounds → Lobby: four seat cards. Each pad, plus keyboard-and-mouse, can claim a seat by pressing confirm. Seat 1 starts when ready. Same `Sim`, multiple input frames, one screen and camera. Any seat's L1/R1 moves the shared site, with a 0.8 s cooldown. Same seat colors. Seats 1 and 3 have the Hush; seats 2 and 4, Sforzando. (Same in sessions; Hush slows the world for everyone.) On a team result the report shows each seat's stats and awards.\\n\\n### 14.6 Head tags\\n\\nExact attribute order, `name` then `content`: the hub reads them with a regex. Content must contain no quote characters.\\n\\n```html\\n780→<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"6\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Keep the patient alive and finish the operation together\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse · use: R2 or click · tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n```\\n\\nDo **not** add `hub:webgpu=required`: the game runs on WebGL2 too (verified). Also add the catalogue tags: `<title>Your Title — Your Tagline</title>` (the hub splits on the dash), `<meta name=\\\"description\\\">`, `<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#17707A\\\">`, `<link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:…\\\">` (an inked heart SVG), `<meta name=\\\"hub:type\\\" content=\\\"Game\\\">`, `<meta name=\\\"hub:players\\\" content=\\\"1–4\\\">`, `<meta name=\\\"hub:source\\\" content=\\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\">`.\\n\\n790→### 14.7 What the hub's own check does\\n\\nThese are all reproduced in §17: it plays shared worlds at 2, 3 and 4 players at 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss, with a player leaving; `scenario=host-leave`; `scenario=server` at 2 players. It checks the client is exactly one unmodified copy (SHA-256, §16.2). Then, on its own: opens the page, presses Enter, Space, Enter, Space, checks that nothing threw, `AIHub.active` is false, `Math.random` is untouched, and the screenshot isn't blank.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Architecture\\n\\n### 15.1 Layout\\n\\n800→```\\npackage.json            \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\" (Node must import src/sim/*.js as ES modules)\\n.gitignore              node_modules/, dist/\\ndocs/AUTHORING.md       how to add an operation, a strain, a story scene, a tuning value\\ntools/build.mjs         §16.2\\ntools/vendor/session.js the hub client, verbatim\\nsrc/main.js             the boot branch in §14.1\\nsrc/config/             identity.js (title, tagline), tuning.js (§13)\\nsrc/data/               ops/*.js, story/*.js, cast.js, sites.js, about.json. Data only, no logic\\nsrc/sim/                NO three, NO DOM, NO audio. sim.js, beat.js, scoring.js, physics.js,\\n810→                        tools/*.js, strains/*.js, ops-runner.js, snapshot.js, bot.js\\nsrc/view/               renderer.js, ink.js, field.js, paint.js, tip.js, instruments/*.js,\\n                        strains/*.js, bust.js, stage.js, fx.js, cutin.js, camera.js\\nsrc/audio/              engine.js, music.js, sfx.js, voice.js\\nsrc/input/              input.js (pads, keyboard, mouse → per-seat input frames), glyphs.js\\nsrc/ui/                 ui.css, focus.js, hud.js, ecg.js, screens/*.js\\nsrc/app/                director.js (screen state machine), story.js, attract.js, dev.js,\\n                        coop.js, session.js, save.js\\ntests/                  run-all.mjs, sim/, browser/, hub/ (§17)\\n```\",\"content_concise\":\"740→  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\\n    if (sim && (data.t === 'i' || data.t === 'a')) sim.input(from, data);\\n    else if (from === info.host) view?.applySnapshot(data);\\n  });\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => sim?.leave(id));           // release what they held, drop their tip\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (sim) finish(); });       // within graceMs; a non-host calling finish() warns, and fails the check\\n  let ended = false;\\n  AIHub.on('end', () => { ended = true; stopEverything(); }); // no input, no sends, audio suspended\\n  AIHub.ready();                                           // no key press; don't wait for a first frame\\n  let last = performance.now(), acc = 0;\\n750→  (function pump() {\\n    if (ended) return;\\n    const now = performance.now(), dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25); last = now;\\n    if (AIHub.time() >= 0) {\\n      if (!info.server) readLocalInput(dt);                // host: straight into sim.input(AIHub.me, …). Client: kept for sending\\n      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\\n      else sendInputOnSchedule();\\n    }\\n    setTimeout(pump, 16);\\n  })();\\n760→}\\n```\\n\\n**`finish()`** (host, once, on operation end or `time-up`): `standings` as groups of ids, best contribution first, listing every present player; `scores`; `won` (patient alive and operation complete); `stats` (up to 6 entries per player, names up to 16 chars: Cuts, Stitches, Burns, Saves, Accuracy); `awards` (title up to 24 chars, detail up to 40: \\\"Steadiest Hands\\\", \\\"Last-Second Shock\\\"). If the operation hasn't ended at `time-up`, `won` is false.\\n\\nA client leaving must not break the round. The host leaving voids it, which the hub handles: show a short message on `end` and stop.\\n\\n### 14.4 The card\\n\\nOwn card, in the game's world: OR 3, lamp on, the seat's busts or tips lining up, Title music. It shows the game's name, players in their colors with ready states, how to win, this player's controls, and seconds left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross (button 0) or a click on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle (button 3), M, or a click on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Nothing on the card changes the round, and there are no menus. Show a 3-2-1 countdown from `AIHub.time()`. The harness sends synthetic keys whose `code` equals `key` (`'Enter'`, `'a'`, `'ArrowLeft'`), so read `e.key` as well as `e.code`.\\n770→\\n### 14.5 Couch co-op (on its own)\\n\\nMain Menu → Grand Rounds → Lobby: four seat cards. Each pad, plus keyboard-and-mouse, can claim a seat by pressing confirm. Seat 1 starts when ready. Same `Sim`, multiple input frames, one screen and camera. Any seat's L1/R1 moves the shared site, with a 0.8 s cooldown. Same seat colors. Seats 1 and 3 have the Hush; seats 2 and 4, Sforzando. (Same in sessions; Hush slows the world for everyone.) On a team result the report shows each seat's stats and awards.\\n\\n### 14.6 Head tags\\n\\nExact attribute order, `name` then `content`: the hub reads them with a regex. Content must contain no quote characters.\\n\\n```html\\n780→<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"6\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Keep the patient alive and finish the operation together\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse · use: R2 or click · tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n```\\n\\nDo **not** add `hub:webgpu=required`: the game runs on WebGL2 too (verified). Also add the catalogue tags: `<title>Your Title — Your Tagline</title>` (the hub splits on the dash), `<meta name=\\\"description\\\">`, `<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#17707A\\\">`, `<link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:…\\\">` (an inked heart SVG), `<meta name=\\\"hub:type\\\" content=\\\"Game\\\">`, `<meta name=\\\"hub:players\\\" content=\\\"1–4\\\">`, `<meta name=\\\"hub:source\\\" content=\\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\">`.\\n\\n790→### 14.7 What the hub's own check does\\n\\nThese are all reproduced in §17: it plays shared worlds at 2, 3 and 4 players at 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss, with a player leaving; `scenario=host-leave`; `scenario=server` at 2 players. It checks the client is exactly one unmodified copy (SHA-256, §16.2). Then, on its own: opens the page, presses Enter, Space, Enter, Space, checks that nothing threw, `AIHub.active` is false, `Math.random` is untouched, and the screenshot isn't blank.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Architecture\\n\\n### 15.1 Layout\\n\\n800→```\\npackage.json            \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\" (Node must import src/sim/*.js as ES modules)\\n.gitignore              node_modules/, dist/\\ndocs/AUTHORING.md       how to add an operation, a strain, a story scene, a tuning value\\ntools/build.mjs         §16.2\\ntools/vendor/session.js the hub client, verbatim\\nsrc/main.js             the boot branch in §14.1\\nsrc/config/             identity.js (title, tagline), tuning.js (§13)\\nsrc/data/               ops/*.js, story/*.js, cast.js, sites.js, about.json. Data only, no logic\\nsrc/sim/                NO three, NO DOM, NO audio. sim.js, beat.js, scoring.js, physics.js,\\n810→                        tools/*.js, strains/*.js, ops-runner.js, snapshot.js, bot.js\\nsrc/view/               renderer.js, ink.js, field.js, paint.js, tip.js, instruments/*.js,\\n                        strains/*.js, bust.js, stage.js, fx.js, cutin.js, camera.js\\nsrc/audio/              engine.js, music.js, sfx.js, voice.js\\nsrc/input/              input.js (pads, keyboard, mouse → per-seat input frames), glyphs.js\\nsrc/ui/                 ui.css, focus.js, hud.js, ecg.js, screens/*.js\\nsrc/app/                director.js (screen state machine), story.js, attract.js, dev.js,\\n                        coop.js, session.js, save.js\\ntests/                  run-all.mjs, sim/, browser/, hub/ (§17)\\n```\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":740,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\\n    if (sim && (data.t === 'i' || data.t === 'a')) sim.input(from, data);\\n    else if (from === info.host) view?.applySnapshot(data);\\n  });\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => sim?.leave(id));           // release what they held, drop their tip\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (sim) finish(); });       // within graceMs; a non-host calling finish() warns, and fails the check\\n  let ended = false;\\n  AIHub.on('end', () => { ended = true; stopEverything(); }); // no input, no sends, audio suspended\\n  AIHub.ready();                                           // no key press; don't wait for a first frame\\n  let last = performance.now(), acc = 0;\\n  (function pump() {\\n    if (ended) return;\\n    const now = performance.now(), dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25); last = now;\\n    if (AIHub.time() >= 0) {\\n      if (!info.server) readLocalInput(dt);                // host: straight into sim.input(AIHub.me, …). Client: kept for sending\\n      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\\n      else sendInputOnSchedule();\\n    }\\n    setTimeout(pump, 16);\\n  })();\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**`finish()`** (host, once, on operation end or `time-up`): `standings` as groups of ids, best contribution first, listing every present player; `scores`; `won` (patient alive and operation complete); `stats` (up to 6 entries per player, names up to 16 chars: Cuts, Stitches, Burns, Saves, Accuracy); `awards` (title up to 24 chars, detail up to 40: \\\"Steadiest Hands\\\", \\\"Last-Second Shock\\\"). If the operation hasn't ended at `time-up`, `won` is false.\\n\\nA client leaving must not break the round. The host leaving voids it, which the hub handles: show a short message on `end` and stop.\\n\\n### 14.4 The card\\n\\nOwn card, in the game's world: OR 3, lamp on, the seat's busts or tips lining up, Title music. It shows the game's name, players in their colors with ready states, how to win, this player's controls, and seconds left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross (button 0) or a click on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle (button 3), M, or a click on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Nothing on the card changes the round, and there are no menus. Show a 3-2-1 countdown from `AIHub.time()`. The harness sends synthetic keys whose `code` equals `key` (`'Enter'`, `'a'`, `'ArrowLeft'`), so read `e.key` as well as `e.code`.\\n\\n### 14.5 Couch co-op (on its own)\\n\\nMain Menu → Grand Rounds → Lobby: four seat cards. Each pad, plus keyboard-and-mouse, can claim a seat by pressing confirm. Seat 1 starts when ready. Same `Sim`, multiple input frames, one screen and camera. Any seat's L1/R1 moves the shared site, with a 0.8 s cooldown. Same seat colors. Seats 1 and 3 have the Hush; seats 2 and 4, Sforzando. (Same in sessions; Hush slows the world for everyone.) On a team result the report shows each seat's stats and awards.\\n\\n### 14.6 Head tags\\n\\nExact attribute order, `name` then `content`: the hub reads them with a regex. Content must contain no quote characters.\\n\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"6\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Keep the patient alive and finish the operation together\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse · use: R2 or click · tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n```\\n\\nDo **not** add `hub:webgpu=required`: the game runs on WebGL2 too (verified). Also add the catalogue tags: `<title>Your Title — Your Tagline</title>` (the hub splits on the dash), `<meta name=\\\"description\\\">`, `<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#17707A\\\">`, `<link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:…\\\">` (an inked heart SVG), `<meta name=\\\"hub:type\\\" content=\\\"Game\\\">`, `<meta name=\\\"hub:players\\\" content=\\\"1–4\\\">`, `<meta name=\\\"hub:source\\\" content=\\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\">`.\\n\\n### 14.7 What the hub's own check does\\n\\nThese are all reproduced in §17: it plays shared worlds at 2, 3 and 4 players at 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss, with a player leaving; `scenario=host-leave`; `scenario=server` at 2 players. It checks the client is exactly one unmodified copy (SHA-256, §16.2). Then, on its own: opens the page, presses Enter, Space, Enter, Space, checks that nothing threw, `AIHub.active` is false, `Math.random` is untouched, and the screenshot isn't blank.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Architecture\\n\\n### 15.1 Layout\\n\\n```\\npackage.json            \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\" (Node must import src/sim/*.js as ES modules)\\n.gitignore              node_modules/, dist/\\ndocs/AUTHORING.md       how to add an operation, a strain, a story scene, a tuning value\\ntools/build.mjs         §16.2\\ntools/vendor/session.js the hub client, verbatim\\nsrc/main.js             the boot branch in §14.1\\nsrc/config/             identity.js (title, tagline), tuning.js (§13)\\nsrc/data/               ops/*.js, story/*.js, cast.js, sites.js, about.json. Data only, no logic\\nsrc/sim/                NO three, NO DOM, NO audio. sim.js, beat.js, scoring.js, physics.js,\\n                        tools/*.js, strains/*.js, ops-runner.js, snapshot.js, bot.js\\nsrc/view/               renderer.js, ink.js, field.js, paint.js, tip.js, instruments/*.js,\\n                        strains/*.js, bust.js, stage.js, fx.js, cutin.js, camera.js\\nsrc/audio/              engine.js, music.js, sfx.js, voice.js\\nsrc/input/              input.js (pads, keyboard, mouse → per-seat input frames), glyphs.js\\nsrc/ui/                 ui.css, focus.js, hud.js, ecg.js, screens/*.js\\nsrc/app/                director.js (screen state machine), story.js, attract.js, dev.js,\\n                        coop.js, session.js, save.js\\ntests/                  run-all.mjs, sim/, browser/, hub/ (§17)\\n```\\n\",\"total_lines\":1225}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"a3b9fcf0-b989-45dc-b2f5-fae019d266f6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1059","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe paint signature includes `countN` and `screen`, so countdown repaints should work. The simulation is gated on `clock >= 0`. A potential bug existsThe code appears to  in the countdown display formula: `Math.max(1, Math.ceil(-clock / be fixed.1000))` rounds negative milliseconds up to 1 second.\n\nThe countdown formula correctly rounds negative milliseconds to 1 second. The test polls every 40ms for the Countdown screen, which lasts 3 seconds, so it should catch the transition. The test loads game.html\n\nChecking that the  from the hub site copydivide-by-1000 fix and rather than source  countdown logic aremodules directly. actually present in the built HTML. Verifying the test ran honestly and captured evidence. Confirming the screenshot shows seconds rather than milliseconds. Scanning for any remaining bugs.\n\nThe countdown logic is being reviewed for edge cases. The card\n\nI should verify the handler is also under inlined bundle in tests/hub/site/game.html scrutiny. and the root HTML contain the /1000 fix and Countdown logic, not just the source. The hand-in HTML is the final deliverable. I also need to check if a missing card.left in the paint signature could leave a stale millisecond display.\n\nChecking if the card event fires during countdown. When AIHub.time() turns negative, the card handler might still trigger. The tickCard function computes remaining time from splashUntil and sends it to the bridge.\n\nBoth paintCard and patchLive divide by 1000, so the missing card.left in the paint signature is not a problem. The test compares the displayed text to Math.ceil(state().cardLeft / 1000), which matches the source logic.\n\nThe test asserts the displayed value is at most 30, so a millisecond","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1e374f06-7deb-4518-b359-fdc542f15f20-18","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html","offset":230,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1e374f06-7deb-4518-b359-fdc542f15f20-19","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/round.js","offset":280,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1e374f06-7deb-4518-b359-fdc542f15f20-20","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"card seconds|countdown digit|0 failed|26 passed|hub","glob":"**/*.{log,txt,md,json}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/tmp/grok-goal-c4cb33e83374/implementer"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2972,"output_tokens":834,"cache_read_input_tokens":47616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"c8d029d3-7438-4cd3-97d4-034d82197ab9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1e374f06-7deb-4518-b359-fdc542f15f20-18","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"230→      post: (msg) => {\\n        if (msg.type !== 'message') log(`hub → ${p.key}: ${msg.type}${msg.type === 'start' ? ` in ${msg.in} ms` : ''}${msg.type === 'leave' ? ` ${msg.id} (${msg.reason})` : ''}${msg.type === 'end' ? ` ${msg.reason}` : ''}`);\\n        post(msg);\\n      },\\n      net: endpoint,\\n      onIssue: (i) => log(`${p.key} ✗ ${i.problem}`),\\n      onFullscreen: (on) => log(`${p.key} asked for fullscreen ${on ? 'on' : 'off'}: the hub's page takes it`),\\n      onAnswer: (what) => answerCard(state, cell, what),\\n      // The scoreboard's feed: this cell's own progress, as its bridge passes it on.\\n      onProgress: (id, report) => {\\n240→        if (id !== cell.bridge?.me) return;\\n        cell.progress.push({ at: performance.now(), ...report });\\n        state.coordinator.progress(id, report.score);\\n        render(state);\\n      },\\n    });\\n    endpoint.onMessage((from, env) => cell.bridge.fromNet(from, env));\\n    cell.detach = attachFrame(frame, (msg) => cell.bridge.fromGame(msg));\\n    frame.addEventListener('load', () => instrument(cell), { once: true });\\n    frame.src = gameUrl(game, { tag: metas?.mode, seed });\\n250→    state.cells.push(cell);\\n  }\\n  renderWho(state);\\n  render(state);\\n  // By hand, the card lifts by itself after ten seconds (more when a player asks), as in a session;\\n  // the conformance run releases it itself.\\n  const ticker = setInterval(() => {\\n    if (state !== current || state.coordinator.released) return clearInterval(ticker);\\n    if (!auto && performance.now() >= state.splashUntil) return releaseRound(state);\\n    tickCard(state);\\n260→  }, 250);\\n  return state;\\n}\\n\\nfunction releaseRound(state = current) {\\n  if (!state || state !== current || state.coordinator.released) return;\\n  state.splashUntil = null;\\n  tickCard(state);\\n  log('splash over: the round starts once every game has loaded');\\n  state.coordinator.release();\\n270→}\\n\\n/** A game's own card, as the hub drives it: the countdown and who is ready, to every copy that shows one. */\\nfunction tickCard(state) {\\n  const left = state.splashUntil === null ? null : Math.max(0, state.splashUntil - performance.now());\\n  const ready = state.cells.filter((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => c.bridge.me);\\n  for (const cell of state.cells) {\\n    if (cell.gone || !cell.bridge.showsCard) continue;\\n    const card = { left, paused: false, starting: left === null, ready, asking: state.answers.more.size, asked: state.answers.more.has(cell.key) };\\n    const id = JSON.stringify({ ...card, left: left === null ? null : Math.ceil(left / 1000) });\\n280→    if (cell.cardSent === id) continue;\\n    cell.cardSent = id;\\n    cell.bridge.card(card);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A player answered on the game's own card: Ready, or more time (+10 s; again takes it back). */\\nfunction answerCard(state, cell, what) {\\n  if (state !== current || state.coordinator.released || cell.server) return;\\n  const { ready, more } = state.answers;\\n290→  if (what === 'ready') {\\n    ready.add(cell.key);\\n    more.delete(cell.key);\\n  } else if (more.has(cell.key)) {\\n    more.delete(cell.key);\\n  } else {\\n    more.add(cell.key);\\n    ready.delete(cell.key);\\n    state.splashUntil += 10_000;\\n  }\\n300→  log(`${cell.key} answers ${what} on the game's card`);\\n  const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server && !c.gone);\\n  if (!auto && players.every((c) => ready.has(c.key))) return releaseRound(state);\\n  tickCard(state);\\n}\\n\\nfunction endCurrent() {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.coordinator.abort('session-ended');\\n  for (const cell of current.cells) removeCell(cell, false);\\n310→  current.hubEnd.close();\\n  current = null;\\n}\\n\\nfunction removeCell(cell, tellRound = true) {\\n  if (cell.gone) return;\\n  cell.gone = true;\\n  cell.detach();\\n  cell.endpoint.close();\\n  cell.frame.remove();\",\"content_concise\":\"230→      post: (msg) => {\\n        if (msg.type !== 'message') log(`hub → ${p.key}: ${msg.type}${msg.type === 'start' ? ` in ${msg.in} ms` : ''}${msg.type === 'leave' ? ` ${msg.id} (${msg.reason})` : ''}${msg.type === 'end' ? ` ${msg.reason}` : ''}`);\\n        post(msg);\\n      },\\n      net: endpoint,\\n      onIssue: (i) => log(`${p.key} ✗ ${i.problem}`),\\n      onFullscreen: (on) => log(`${p.key} asked for fullscreen ${on ? 'on' : 'off'}: the hub's page takes it`),\\n      onAnswer: (what) => answerCard(state, cell, what),\\n      // The scoreboard's feed: this cell's own progress, as its bridge passes it on.\\n      onProgress: (id, report) => {\\n240→        if (id !== cell.bridge?.me) return;\\n        cell.progress.push({ at: performance.now(), ...report });\\n        state.coordinator.progress(id, report.score);\\n        render(state);\\n      },\\n    });\\n    endpoint.onMessage((from, env) => cell.bridge.fromNet(from, env));\\n    cell.detach = attachFrame(frame, (msg) => cell.bridge.fromGame(msg));\\n    frame.addEventListener('load', () => instrument(cell), { once: true });\\n    frame.src = gameUrl(game, { tag: metas?.mode, seed });\\n250→    state.cells.push(cell);\\n  }\\n  renderWho(state);\\n  render(state);\\n  // By hand, the card lifts by itself after ten seconds (more when a player asks), as in a session;\\n  // the conformance run releases it itself.\\n  const ticker = setInterval(() => {\\n    if (state !== current || state.coordinator.released) return clearInterval(ticker);\\n    if (!auto && performance.now() >= state.splashUntil) return releaseRound(state);\\n    tickCard(state);\\n260→  }, 250);\\n  return state;\\n}\\n\\nfunction releaseRound(state = current) {\\n  if (!state || state !== current || state.coordinator.released) return;\\n  state.splashUntil = null;\\n  tickCard(state);\\n  log('splash over: the round starts once every game has loaded');\\n  state.coordinator.release();\\n270→}\\n\\n/** A game's own card, as the hub drives it: the countdown and who is ready, to every copy that shows one. */\\nfunction tickCard(state) {\\n  const left = state.splashUntil === null ? null : Math.max(0, state.splashUntil - performance.now());\\n  const ready = state.cells.filter((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => c.bridge.me);\\n  for (const cell of state.cells) {\\n    if (cell.gone || !cell.bridge.showsCard) continue;\\n    const card = { left, paused: false, starting: left === null, ready, asking: state.answers.more.size, asked: state.answers.more.has(cell.key) };\\n    const id = JSON.stringify({ ...card, left: left === null ? null : Math.ceil(left / 1000) });\\n280→    if (cell.cardSent === id) continue;\\n    cell.cardSent = id;\\n    cell.bridge.card(card);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A player answered on the game's own card: Ready, or more time (+10 s; again takes it back). */\\nfunction answerCard(state, cell, what) {\\n  if (state !== current || state.coordinator.released || cell.server) return;\\n  const { ready, more } = state.answers;\\n290→  if (what === 'ready') {\\n    ready.add(cell.key);\\n    more.delete(cell.key);\\n  } else if (more.has(cell.key)) {\\n    more.delete(cell.key);\\n  } else {\\n    more.add(cell.key);\\n    ready.delete(cell.key);\\n    state.splashUntil += 10_000;\\n  }\\n300→  log(`${cell.key} answers ${what} on the game's card`);\\n  const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server && !c.gone);\\n  if (!auto && players.every((c) => ready.has(c.key))) return releaseRound(state);\\n  tickCard(state);\\n}\\n\\nfunction endCurrent() {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.coordinator.abort('session-ended');\\n  for (const cell of current.cells) removeCell(cell, false);\\n310→  current.hubEnd.close();\\n  current = null;\\n}\\n\\nfunction removeCell(cell, tellRound = true) {\\n  if (cell.gone) return;\\n  cell.gone = true;\\n  cell.detach();\\n  cell.endpoint.close();\\n  cell.frame.remove();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230/tests/hub/site/harness.html\",\"offset\":230,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"      post: (msg) => {\\n        if (msg.type !== 'message') log(`hub → ${p.key}: ${msg.type}${msg.type === 'start' ? ` in ${msg.in} ms` : ''}${msg.type === 'leave' ? ` ${msg.id} (${msg.reason})` : ''}${msg.type === 'end' ? ` ${msg.reason}` : ''}`);\\n        post(msg);\\n      },\\n      net: endpoint,\\n      onIssue: (i) => log(`${p.key} ✗ ${i.problem}`),\\n      onFullscreen: (on) => log(`${p.key} asked for fullscreen ${on ? 'on' : 'off'}: the hub's page takes it`),\\n      onAnswer: (what) => answerCard(state, cell, what),\\n      // The scoreboard's feed: this cell's own progress, as its bridge passes it on.\\n      onProgress: (id, report) => {\\n        if (id !== cell.bridge?.me) return;\\n        cell.progress.push({ at: performance.now(), ...report });\\n        state.coordinator.progress(id, report.score);\\n        render(state);\\n      },\\n    });\\n    endpoint.onMessage((from, env) => cell.bridge.fromNet(from, env));\\n    cell.detach = attachFrame(frame, (msg) => cell.bridge.fromGame(msg));\\n    frame.addEventListener('load', () => instrument(cell), { once: true });\\n    frame.src = gameUrl(game, { tag: metas?.mode, seed });\\n    state.cells.push(cell);\\n  }\\n  renderWho(state);\\n  render(state);\\n  // By hand, the card lifts by itself after ten seconds (more when a player asks), as in a session;\\n  // the conformance run releases it itself.\\n  const ticker = setInterval(() => {\\n    if (state !== current || state.coordinator.released) return clearInterval(ticker);\\n    if (!auto && performance.now() >= state.splashUntil) return releaseRound(state);\\n    tickCard(state);\\n  }, 250);\