17,115,101,115,32,116,104,101,32,107,101,121,115,32,80,67,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,115,32,101,120,112,101,99,116,32,102,111,114,32,116,104,101,32,103,101,110,114,101,46,32,84,104,101,32,109,111,117,115,101,32,97,105,109,115,44,32,108,111,111,107,115,44,32,97,110,100,32,99,108,105,99,107,115,32,109,101,110,117,32,105,116,101,109,115,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,105,110,103,115,32,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,119,111,114,108,100,32,40,104,111,118,101,114,32,109,111,118,101,115,32,116,104,101,32,102,111,99,117,115,41,32,119,104,101,114,101,118,101,114,32,116,104,101,32,103,101,110,114,101,32,117,115,101,115,32,105,116,46,32,79,110,45,115,99,114,101,101,110,32,112,114,111,109,112,116,115,32,102,111,108,108,111,119,32,116,104,101,32,105,110,112,117,116,32,117,115,101,100,32,108,97,115,116,58,32,80,108,97,121,83,116,97,116,105,111,110,32,103,108,121,112,104,115,32,102,111,114,32,116,104,101,32,99,111,110,116,114,111,108,108,101,114,32,40,119,105,116,104,32,97,32,83,101,116,116,105,110,103,115,32,111,112,116,105,111,110,32,116,111,32,115,104,111,119,32,88,98,111,120,32,103,108,121,112,104,115,44,32,65,32,66,32,88,32,89,44,32,105,110,115,116,101,97,100,41,44,32,107,101,121,115,32,97,110,100,32,109,111,117,115,101,32,98,117,116,116,111,110,115,32,102,111,114,32,107,101,121,98,111,97,114,100,32,97,110,100,32,109,111,117,115,101,46,10,56,55,58,84,111,117,99,104,45,111,110,108,121,32,100,101,118,105,99,101,115,58,32,110,111,32,116,111,117,99,104,32,99,111,110,116,114,111,108,115,59,32,115,104,111,119,32,34,67,111,110,116,114,111,108,108,101,114,32,111,114,32,107,101,121,98,111,97,114,100,32,114,101,113,117,105,114,101,100,34,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,115,101,116,116,105,110,103,115,32,98,117,116,116,111,110,46,32,76,101,116,32,116,104,101,32,97,116,116,114,97,99,116,32,109,111,100,101,32,114,117,110,46,10,49,50,52,58,32,32,32,32,34,99,111,110,116,114,111,108,115,34,58,32,34,116,104,101,32,99,111,110,116,114,111,108,115,44,32,105,110,32,111,110,101,32,108,105,110,101,34,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":30,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"You are building this game from this document, without its author. Your brief comes first; this plan turns the brief's open choices into decisions. Where the plan is silent, choose whatever serves the pillars in §1. Don't stop to ask.\"},{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\"- **Contents:** §1 the game · §2 world and cast · §3 core rules · §4 tools · §5 strains · §6 operations · §7 story · §8 controls and screens · §9 art · §10 animation · §11 audio · §12 attract mode · §13 dev mode · §14 multiplayer · §15 architecture · §16 verified recipes and traps · §17 testing · §18 build order · §19 About screen, exit interview, catalogue · §20 brief coverage checklist\"},{\"line_number\":124,\"content\":\"- **Aim assist (pad and keyboard only):** near an active guide, and when the Use input is held on a cut or stitch, pull the tip toward the nearest guide point: `tip += (nearest - tip) × aimAssist × dt × 12`, within 0.12 fu.\"},{\"line_number\":294,\"content\":\"2. **Wave 1:** 8 notes from 3 open holes.\"},{\"line_number\":323,\"content\":\"2. **Development (lung, breathing field):** Tremolo and a Legato chain. Bleeders open back at the heart: site-switch alarm, teaching L1/R1.\"},{\"line_number\":355,\"content\":\"| S5 | Before Op 3 | Pip's pathology lab | Envelope: sheet music addressed to \\\"The Surgeon on Call\\\". Pip plays it on a keyboard: \\\"It's a heartbeat…\\\" Ambulance: a cellist |\"},{\"line_number\":384,\"content\":\"### 8.1 Operating controls\"},{\"line_number\":386,\"content\":\"Design order: DualSense, then keyboard and mouse, then the Xbox glyph option. Same game, same screens.\"},{\"line_number\":392,\"content\":\"| Use (analog) | R2 (Cross = full) | RT (A) | LMB (J or Enter on keyboard only) |\"},{\"line_number\":409,\"content\":\"### 8.2 Menu controls\"},{\"line_number\":417,\"content\":\"- **Pad, PlayStation (default):** drawn SVG shapes for ✕ ○ □ △ in their usual colors; L1/R1/L2/R2 pills; stick icons.\"},{\"line_number\":421,\"content\":\"Device switching: any key press means keyboard; mouse movement over 4 px or a click means mouse; a pad button or stick past deadzone means pad. Set `data-prompt-set` on `<html>` so tests can read it. Poll pads every frame; don't rely on `gamepadconnected`.\"},{\"line_number\":460,\"content\":\"| Settings | Three pages. **Audio:** Music (default 10%), Effects, Voices. **Controls:** Glyphs (PlayStation/Xbox), Rumble, Aim Assist, Swap Sticks, Tip Speed. **Display:** Fullscreen, Screen Shake, Line Boil, Text Speed |\"},{\"line_number\":465,\"content\":\"**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches === false` and no pad seen. Don't use `navigator.maxTouchPoints`: it reported 0 on the WebKit iPhone and iPad profiles here. Show **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"** and a **Settings** button, and no touch controls of any kind. Settings must work by tap on this path. Attract mode still starts after 10 s idle, behind the notice, and a tap returns to it. A key press or pad press leaves the notice for the normal Title.\"},{\"line_number\":769,\"content\":\"Own card, in the game's world: OR 3, lamp on, the seat's busts or tips lining up, Title music. It shows the game's name, players in their colors with ready states, how to win, this player's controls, and seconds left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross (button 0) or a click on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle (button 3), M, or a click on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Nothing on the card changes the round, and there are no menus. Show a 3-2-1 countdown from `AIHub.time()`. The harness sends synthetic keys whose `code` equals `key` (`'Enter'`, `'a'`, `'ArrowLeft'`), so read `e.key` as well as `e.code`.\"},{\"line_number\":773,\"content\":\"Main Menu → Grand Rounds → Lobby: four seat cards. Each pad, plus keyboard-and-mouse, can claim a seat by pressing confirm. Seat 1 starts when ready. Same `Sim`, multiple input frames, one screen and camera. Any seat's L1/R1 moves the shared site, with a 0.8 s cooldown. Same seat colors. Seats 1 and 3 have the Hush; seats 2 and 4, Sforzando. (Same in sessions; Hush slows the world for everyone.) On a team result the report shows each seat's stats and awards.\"},{\"line_number\":803,\"content\":\"docs/AUTHORING.md       how to add an operation, a strain, a story scene, a tuning value\"},{\"line_number\":814,\"content\":\"src/input/              input.js (pads, keyboard, mouse → per-seat input frames), glyphs.js\"},{\"line_number\":893,\"content\":\"The recipe below produced a working single file on `file://` with fonts loaded, `$&` and `</script>` intact, and the client hash right. Bundle size with both engines: about 3 MB.\"},{\"line_number\":1119,\"content\":\"- Input: pad stub moves the tip the right distance (full right stick for 1 s = `tipSpeed` ±5%), R2 analog reaches the sim, left-stick flick picks the right tool; mouse is absolute and hover moves menu focus; click activates; keys 1 to 8 work; keyboard-only WASD works.\"},{\"line_number\":1123,\"content\":\"- Touch: Pixel 7 (Chromium) and iPhone 15 (WebKit) profiles show the exact text and a working Settings button by tap, no controls, attract still runs; a pad press leaves the notice.\"},{\"line_number\":1187,\"content\":\"**Exit interview file.** Write it exactly as your brief specifies, and check it parses. For the `aiHub` block: `type` Game; `genre` Simulation; `source` Trauma Center: Second Opinion; `series` Trauma Center; `players` 1–4; `controls` \\\"Right stick or mouse to aim, left stick or 1-8 for tools, R2 or left click to use\\\"; `tags` `[\\\"3d\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"sci-fi\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]`. `name`, `tagline` and `description` are yours.\"},{\"line_number\":1214,\"content\":\"| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover moves focus; prompts follow last input; PlayStation glyphs with Xbox option; no dense screens | §8 |\"},{\"line_number\":1215,\"content\":\"| Touch-only: no touch controls, exact notice text, Settings button, attract runs | §8.6 |\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/TASK.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"},{\"line_number\":39,\"content\":\"  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\"},{\"line_number\":83,\"content\":\"Design the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\"},{\"line_number\":87,\"content\":\"Touch-only devices: no touch controls; show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\"},{\"line_number\":124,\"content\":\"    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5302ab8f-7008-4898-aa0f-e392a0960884-4","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231230__x8f49b6/work/STAGE.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"a127ffe3-3e72-4391-aa36-4c1b298e4a57"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1085","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The delivered artifact is a self-contained browser game HTML file titled \"Alive in Common Time\". It is a surgical simulation inspired by Trauma Center: Second Opinion.\n\nOpen the HTML file directly in a browser. Aim with the right stick or mouse. Select tools with the left stick or keys 1–8. Activate tools with R2 or left click.\n\nThe exact filename is `Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230.html`. Open it from a local file or `http://127.0.0.1`. WebGPU requires an `http://` origin.\n\nXbox controller glyphs are available in Settings. Story or Free Play starts from the title screen. Touch-only devices show a controller requirement prompt.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"**Alive in Common Time** is a self-contained browser surgical sim for 1–4 players, a playful riff on Trauma Center: Second Opinion.\n\n- Open `Alive in Common Time-Trauma Center: Second Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231230.html` in a browser via `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1`.\n- Aim with the right stick or mouse, pick tools with the left stick or keys 1–8, and use R2 or left click.\n- Start Story or Free Play from the title screen. PlayStation glyphs are the default; switch to Xbox in Settings."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2769,"output_tokens":1916,"cache_read_input_tokens":16128,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa56-6231-7cf0-a666-df5fbb090710","uuid":"499948d4-76be-4959-8121-1c8c5da5b407"}
